('anki-card-1755152505619-13', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Sentence A. Monosodium glutamate is found in seaweeds.
Sentence B. MSG is a food seasoning that enhances the flavor of dishes.', 'Both sentences are correct', 'MSG was discovered in 1908 by Japanese chemist Kikunae Ikeda who studied a traditional Japanese broth (dashi) made from kombu, a type of edible kelp/seaweed.

He extracted glutamic acid crystals from the seaweed broth and realized they created a savory, delicious taste he named umami.

He combined this glutamate with sodium to create monosodium glutamate (MSG) because it dissolved easily and tasted best.

It is used as a seasoning because it enhances umami and intensifies savory flavor.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T15:57:57.961Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:57:57.961Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:57:57.961Z"'::jsonb),
