('anki-card-1755152654716-18', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Sentence A. Bacteria alone can be used as a coagulant in cheese.
Sentence B. Bacteria causes holes in swiss cheese.', 'Sentence B is correct', 'Primarily, Rennet or acids: Milk is turned into solid curds and liquid whey using rennet (an enzyme) or acids like vinegar or lemon juice, rather than bacteria alone.

Lactic acid bacteria: Starter cultures of bacteria are added to milk to consume lactose and produce lactic acid, which helps with acidification and flavor. This acid environment prepares the milk, but coagulation itself relies on rennet or direct acidifiers

Certain cultures also produce gases that create the characteristic holes in Swiss-type cheeses.

The holes in Swiss cheese are created by carbon dioxide gas released during fermentation by the bacterium Propionibacterium freudenreichii.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:49:41.176Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:49:41.176Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:49:41.176Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755152686217-19', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Sentence A. In pinipig, the ability to gelatinize is increased.
Sentence B. This is due to the breakdown of starches into dextrins during the process of making pinipig.', 'Sentence B is correct', 'Pinipig – parboiled waxy rice; pounded, winnowed, and toasted

Toasting = example of dextrinization

When pinipig (pounded young glutinous rice) undergoes dextrinization, the long-chain starch molecules (amylose and amylopectin) are chemically broken down into shorter, smaller carbohydrate fragments called dextrins. 

In dry-heat cooking, e.g. toasting, starch is partly degraded to dextrins that have less ability to swell and gelatinize. Because gelatinization requires intact, long-chain starch granules to swell, burst, and trap water into a thick, cohesive network, the fragmented structure of dextrinized starch prevents this from happening.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:52:02.200Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:52:02.200Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:52:02.200Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755152839408-20', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Sentence A. Amount of salt must be reduced if fine iodized salt will be used to replace rock salt.
Sentence B. Fine iodized salt is saltier than rock salt.', 'Both sentences are correct', 'Fine iodized salt packs more densely than coarse rock salt, so substituting it volume-for-volume may require reducing the amount. 

The perceived difference is related mainly to crystal size and packing rather than iodine itself.

Fine salt can taste saltier than rock salt by volume because the tiny grains pack tightly into a spoon, meaning you get more actual salt than the same spoonful of chunky rock salt.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:47:28.142Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:47:28.142Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:47:28.142Z"'::jsonb),
