Sentence B. The separation of mayonnaise may be caused by too much addition of oil.', 'Both sentences are correct', 'A broken mayonnaise can often be re-emulsified by starting with an emulsifier such as egg yolk (has lecithin) and slowly incorporating the broken mixture. 

Adding oil too rapidly or in excessive amounts can overwhelm the emulsion and cause separation.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T15:10:06.709Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:10:06.709Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:10:06.900Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755153216241-34', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Sentence A. Scorching in milk is mainly due to accumulation of lactalbumin at the bottom and side of pan.
Sentence B. Use of double boiler may prevent scorching.', 'Both sentences are correct', 'Scorching – caused by overheating the serum proteins (lactalbumin) that precipitate; stirring once in a double boiler or low heat during cooking minimizes scorching.

A double boiler provides gentler, indirect heating and reduces the risk of scorching.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T15:05:27.931Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:05:27.931Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:05:27.931Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755153246373-35', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Sentence A. Lactase is the most common enzyme used in cheese production.
Sentence B. Casein is first to coagulate upon application of heat.', 'Both sentences are incorrect', 'Rennet, whose active enzyme is chymosin, is the traditional coagulant used in many cheeses, not lactase. 

Casein is not simply the first component to coagulate from ordinary heating alone under all conditions.

Protein coagulation starts at sixty-five (65)C with lactalbumin as the first to be denatured; casein needs higher temperature to coagulate.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:46:52.591Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:46:52.591Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:46:52.591Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755153278002-36', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Sentence A. Pasteurized milk can be stored at room temperature.
Sentence B. In pasteurization, pathogenic microorganisms are destroyed.', 'Sentence B is correct', 'Sentence A is incorrect because pasteurized milk still requires refrigeration. 

Sentence B is correct because pasteurization is designed to destroy pathogenic microorganisms and reduce spoilage organisms, although it does not sterilize the product.

Pasteurization – the process of heating food to a certain temperature and holding it at that temperature until most of the possible pathogens present in food are destroyed or killed. Used for products that are heat-sensitive like milk and fruit juices.

Sterilization – the process by which food is rendered completely free of microorganisms, which could be injurious to the health of man. Use temperatures higher than that in pasteurization. A “commercially sterile” product is not completely free of microorganisms but has killed all but the more resistant bacterial (thermophilic) spores and conditions in the container are not conducive for the growth of the bacterial spores.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T12:57:41.409Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T12:57:41.409Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T12:57:41.625Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755153301536-37', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Sentence A. Agglomerated dried milk is soluble in cold water.
Sentence B. This is due to the hygroscopic property of dried milk.', 'Sentence A is correct', 'Agglomerated milk powder is an "instant" milk powder made by clustering fine spray-dried milk particles into larger, porous granules. 

Water penetrates the porous clusters rapidly, allowing the powder to dissolve instantly without clumping.

Sentence A is correct because agglomerated dried milk is designed to disperse and dissolve more readily in water, including cold water. 

Sentence B is incorrect because this improved reconstitution is mainly due to agglomeration (spray drying followed by other processes) and increased particle structure, not simply to hygroscopicity.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:49:16.248Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:49:16.248Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:49:16.248Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755153326502-38', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Sentence A. Bran is prone to rancidity.
Sentence B. Polished and whole corn kernels store longer than unpolished ones.', 'Both sentences are correct', 'Whole grain and undermilled cereals deteriorate more rapidly because of the presence of the bran and germ than refined or undermilled; oxidative rancidity attacks the unsaturated fats in the germ and bran; they should not be kept in storage too long unless refrigerated.

Removing or protecting outer layers and reducing exposure to damaging conditions can improve storage stability of cereal grains.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T15:37:07.135Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:37:07.135Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:37:07.135Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755153351934-39', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Sentence A. Hydrogenation prevents oxidative rancidity.
Sentence B. Oxidative rancidity is more prone in oils with higher saturated fatty acids.', 'Sentence A is correct', 'Sentence A is correct because hydrogenation reduces the number of double bonds and can improve resistance to oxidative rancidity. 

Sentence B is incorrect because highly unsaturated fats are generally more prone to oxidation than saturated fats.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T15:51:40.808Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:51:40.808Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:51:40.808Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755153376331-40', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Sentence A. Polished rice cooks longer than unpolished rice.
Sentence B. This is due to the fact that polished rice contains more starch.', 'Both sentences are incorrect', 'Unpolished rice generally requires longer cooking because the bran layer and intact structure slow water penetration. 

• Sentence A is incorrect: Polished rice (white rice) actually cooks much faster than unpolished rice (brown or red rice). Polished rice usually takes about 15 to 20 minutes to cook, whereas unpolished rice takes 40 to 45 minutes. This is because unpolished rice retains its tough, fibrous outer bran layer, which slows down water absorption and requires a longer time to soften.
• Sentence B is incorrect: Since the premise of Sentence A is completely backward, the explanation in Sentence B is also fundamentally incorrect. While milling and polishing do increase the percentage of starch by weight (by stripping away the fiber-rich bran and nutrient-dense germ), it makes the grain cook faster, not longer, because the water can instantly penetrate the exposed starch.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:50:42.813Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:50:42.813Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:50:42.813Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755153398747-41', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Sentence A. Breads from sweet potato, corn or cassava are crumbly.
Sentence B. Sweet potato, corn or cassava flours do not contain gluten', 'Both sentences are correct', 'Flours from sweet potato, corn, and cassava lack gluten-forming proteins, so breads containing large amounts of these flours tend to have a more crumbly structure.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T12:55:26.235Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T12:55:26.235Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T12:55:26.235Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755153423680-42', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Sentence A. Fish has less extractives than red meats.
Sentence B. Fish is commonly eaten with salt, seasoning, and sauces.', 'Both sentences are correct', 'Fish generally contains fewer extractives than red meat, contributing to its milder flavor. Salt, seasonings, and sauces are therefore commonly used to enhance fish dishes.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:40:57.731Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:40:57.731Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:40:57.731Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755153445731-43', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Sentence A. Barbeque from loin is less tender and less flavourful than belly.
Sentence B. Belly is more exercise than loin.', 'Both sentences are correct', 'Barbeque made from pork loin is naturally more tender in initial structure than pork belly, but it has less flavor and a much higher risk of drying out. 

Pork belly is usually more flavorful and succulent than loin because it contains more fat and connective tissue. 

The belly muscles are generally subjected to more activity than the relatively tender loin muscles.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T13:19:49.589Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:19:49.589Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:19:49.778Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755153469063-44', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Sentence A. During rigor mortis, actomyosin dissociates due to lack of energy.
Sentence B. Rigor mortis is the stiffening of muscle.', 'Sentence B is correct', 'Sentence A is incorrect because rigor mortis involves the formation and persistence of actomyosin cross-bridges when ATP is depleted. Actomyosin does not dissociate because of lack of energy. 

Sentence B is correct because rigor mortis is the postmortem stiffening of muscle.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:13:45.939Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:13:45.939Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:13:45.939Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755153491577-45', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Sentence A. Papain is a proteolytic enzyme found in papaya.
Sentence B. Papain tenderizes meat by changing gelatin to collagen', 'Sentence A is correct', 'Sentence A is correct because papain is a proteolytic enzyme from papaya. 

Sentence B is incorrect because papain tenderizes meat by hydrolyzing proteins and elastin at high temperatures. It does not change gelatin into collagen.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T15:52:49.008Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:52:49.008Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:52:49.008Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755153511960-46', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Sentence A. Fish cooks faster than meat.
Sentence B. This is because fish has less glycogen than meat thus making the muscle less tough.', 'Sentence A is correct', 'Sentence A is correct because fish generally cooks faster than red meat due to its delicate muscle structure and lower connective tissue content. 

Sentence B is incorrect because the main reason is not lower glycogen content but the structure and composition of fish muscle. Fish has less connective tissues.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:43:21.928Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:43:21.928Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:43:21.928Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755153546090-47', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Sentence A. Less tender cuts of meat usually contain more connective tissue.
Sentence B. Elastin hydrolyzes during moist heat cooking.', 'Sentence A is correct', 'Sentence A is correct because less tender cuts usually contain more connective tissue. 

Sentence B is incorrect because collagen can be converted to gelatin during moist heating, whereas elastin is much more heat resistant and does not readily tenderize.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T15:04:47.848Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:04:47.848Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:04:47.848Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755153569590-48', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Sentence A. Starch high in amylose will gel while starch high in amylopectin does not gel.
Sentence B. Taro flour, which has a considerable amount of amylopectin, can be used in noodle making.', 'Both sentences are correct', 'Sentence A is correct because amylose has a linear structure that forms strong hydrogen bonds upon cooling, creating a firm gel network.

Amylopectin has a heavily branched structure that provides high viscosity when hot, but it does not form a strong gel on its own. 

Sentence B is correct because taro flour contains high levels of amylopectin and provides the necessary cohesive, viscous paste properties useful in certain food applications, including specific types of noodles and binding.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T15:29:08.506Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:29:08.506Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:29:08.506Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755153616321-49', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Sentence A. Baking soda may be substituted for baking powder.
Sentence B. Baking soda also contains an acid ingredient.', 'Both sentences are incorrect', 'Sentence A is incorrect because baking soda can replace baking powder if sufficient acid is also supplied. 

Sentence B is incorrect because baking soda is alkaline and does not itself contain an acid ingredient.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:50:21.941Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:50:21.941Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:50:21.941Z"'::jsonb)
