('anki-card-1755153674885-50', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Flat yellow noodles made from wheat flour, lye, salt, and water', 'Miki', 'Miki is a flat yellow noodle made from wheat flour, water, salt, and alkaline ingredients such as lye water. 

Bihon is rice vermicelli, sotanghon is usually mung-bean starch vermicelli, and canton refers to another style of wheat noodle.', '["Bihon","Sotanghon","Miki","Canton"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T11:47:55.789Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T11:47:55.789Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T11:47:55.959Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755153717166-51', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'A coddled egg is one which has been:', 'cooked in water after it has stopped boiling', 'A coddled egg is gently cooked by residual heat after the water has been brought to a boil, producing a softly set egg. 

Prolonged boiling produces a harder-cooked egg rather than a coddled egg.', '["cooked in water after it has stopped boiling","cooked in boiling water for 10-12 minutes","cooked slowly in boiling water for 20 minutes","boiled for 5 minutes in a covered pot"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:34:09.722Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:34:09.722Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:34:09.722Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755153747380-52', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Raw starch flavor is caused by:', 'Lumping', 'A raw starch flavor results when a starch mixture form lumps that could be due to inadequate stirring or cooking. Formation of lumps can cause uneven hydration and gelatinization.

When starch hits hot liquid without proper separation, the outside of a clump gelatinizes instantly.

This outer sticky layer blocks liquid from reaching the inner starch. The trapped center remains ungelatinized, leaving a distinct raw flour or starch taste in the final dish.', '["Lumping","incorrect measurements of ingredients","vigorous stirring","inadequate stirring"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T13:28:08.065Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:28:08.065Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:28:08.065Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755153781964-53', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Vacuum-packed meats are ____ in color', 'Dark brown', 'This color change occurs because the meat is sealed without oxygen. Meat needs oxygen to maintain its bright red color (which creates a protein called oxymyoglobin). 

When you open the vacuum package and expose the meat to the air for about 15 to 30 minutes, it will "bloom" and turn back to its normal bright red color.', '["Red","Dark brown","Pink","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:49:35.384Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:49:35.384Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:49:35.384Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755153817096-54', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Yambean is the same as:', 'Both a and b', 'Yambean is another name for jicama, known in the Philippines as singkamas. 

Therefore, both A and B refer to the same root crop.', '["Jicama","Singkamas","Both a and b","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T11:40:31.417Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T11:40:31.417Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T11:40:31.595Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755153847160-55', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'An alkaline ingredient used as a leavening.', 'Baking soda', 'Baking soda is sodium bicarbonate, an alkaline leavening ingredient that releases carbon dioxide when it reacts with an acid and moisture.

Cream of tartar and vinegar are acidic, while fruit juice may be acidic but is not the standard alkaline leavener.', '["Cream of tartar","Baking soda","Vinegar","Fruit juice"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:18:34.036Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:18:34.036Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:18:34.036Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755153894658-56', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'One gallon of ice cream is equivalent to how many pints?', '8', 'In standard liquid volume measurements used in food service and kitchen management, one gallon is equivalent to 8 pints.

Quick Volume Conversion Chart:

• 1 Gallon = 4 Quarts
• 1 Gallon = 8 Pints
• 1 Gallon = 16 Cups
• 1 Gallon = 128 Fluid Ounces', '["8","16","4","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:46:39.183Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:46:39.183Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:46:39.183Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755153936074-57', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Lechon Kawali is best made from this pork cut', 'Liempo', 'Lechon kawali is best made from liempo or pork belly because its layers of meat and fat produce the characteristic rich, crisp, and succulent result.

Lomo and pigue are leaner cuts, while ribs are less suitable for the usual preparation.', '["Lomo","Liempo","Pigue","Tadyang"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T11:39:43.524Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T11:39:43.524Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T11:39:43.524Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755153969272-58', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Semolina flour is made from', 'Durum wheat', 'Semolina is a coarse flour made from durum wheat and is commonly used for pasta and some other wheat products.', '["Cassava starch","Rootcrop starch","Durum wheat","Millet"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T12:11:28.234Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T12:11:28.234Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T12:11:28.234Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154022951-59', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Clostridium botulinum can be completely destroyed only at', 'at 121ºC', 'Commercial sterilization of low-acid canned foods requires temperatures around 121°C under pressure to destroy highly heat-resistant spores such as those of Clostridium botulinum. 

Boiling at 100°C is insufficient for this purpose.', '["very high pH","at 121ºC","very alkaline condition","at 100ºC"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:51:03.414Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:51:03.414Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:51:03.414Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154062399-60', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Weeping out of liquid from gelatinized starch during prolonged storage', 'syneresis', 'Syneresis is the weeping or separation of liquid from a starch or gel network during storage. 

Retrogradation is a broader starch reassociation process that can contribute to syneresis.', '["retrogradation","syneresis","gelatinization","gelation"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T13:26:56.281Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:26:56.281Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:26:56.281Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154121648-61', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Proportion of liquid and flour in order to make soft dough', '1 part liquid: 3 parts flour', 'In culinary arts and baking science, mixtures are categorized as either batters or doughs based on their ratio of liquid to flour.

• Pour Batter (1:1 Ratio): Equal parts liquid and flour (e.g., pancakes, crepes, waffles).
• Drop Batter (1:2 Ratio): One part liquid to two parts flour. It is too thick to pour but drops easily from a spoon (e.g., muffins, drop biscuits).
• Soft Dough (1:3 Ratio): One part liquid to three parts flour. It is thick enough to be handled, kneaded, and rolled out on a floured surface while remaining pliable (e.g., rolled biscuits, scones, yeast breads).
• Stiff Dough (1:4 to 1:8 Ratio): Very low hydration, resulting in a firm, dense consistency that is easily sliced or shaped (e.g., pie crusts, sugar cookies, noodles).', '["1 part liquid: 1 part flour","1 part liquid: 2 parts flour","1 part liquid: 3 parts flour","1 part liquid: 4 parts flour"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:47:07.123Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:47:07.123Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:47:07.123Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154155644-62', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Rice that is high in amylopectin.', 'Waxy', 'Rice starch consists of two types of molecules: amylose and amylopectin.

Ordinary rice contains both amylose (around 15–30%) and amylopectin. Waxy rice (also commonly known as glutinous rice or sticky rice), however, contains almost 100% amylopectin and virtually 0% amylose.

Amylopectin is responsible for the sticky, gelatinous, and chewy texture of rice when cooked. This makes waxy rice the essential ingredient for traditional Filipino rice cakes (kakanin) like biko, suman, and sapin-sapin.

• Pre-gelatinized: Rice that has been precooked and dried so that it cooks much faster or can dissolve in cold water (often used in instant baby food or porridge).
• Parboiled: Rice that has been partially boiled in its husk before milling. This process drives nutrients from the husk into the grain, making it less sticky and more nutritious than regular white rice.
• Ordinary: Regular non-glutinous table rice (like Jasmine or Sinandomeng). It contains higher levels of amylose, which allows the grains to separate easily when cooked.', '["Ordinary","Waxy","Parboiled","pre-gelatinized"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:50:45.046Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:50:45.046Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:50:45.046Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154190893-63', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Kimchi is a', 'Fermented product', 'Kimchi is produced through controlled lactic acid fermentation. Pickling may involve acidification, but kimchi is specifically recognized as a fermented vegetable product.

Fermentation gives its characteristic flavor.', '["Pickled product","Fermented product","Cured product","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T13:21:30.706Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:21:30.706Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:21:30.706Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154242092-64', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'In curing, the desirable pink color is due to:', 'nitrosomyoglobin', 'The desirable cured-meat pink color is associated with nitrosomyoglobin, formed when nitric oxide reacts with myoglobin during curing and heating.

• Hemoglobin: The oxygen-transporting protein found in the blood. While it contains iron and binds oxygen similarly to myoglobin, most blood is removed during slaughter, meaning it plays a minor role in meat color compared to myoglobin.
• Oxymyoglobin: The compound formed when fresh myoglobin is exposed to oxygen (like fresh beef sitting on a counter). It gives fresh, raw red meat its bright, cherry-red color, but it turns brown quickly when cooked or exposed to heat.
• Metmyoglobin: The oxidized form of myoglobin that occurs when meat is exposed to oxygen for a prolonged period or stored improperly. It turns the iron into a ferric state (Fe³⁺), resulting in an unappealing brownish-gray color (commonly seen on the surface of old ground beef).', '["nitrosomyoglobin","hemoglobin","oxymyoglobin","metmyoglobin"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:11:18.780Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:11:18.780Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:11:18.780Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154272858-65', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Heat is transferred in lechon in spit by:', 'radiation', 'Lechon cooked on a spit receives substantial heat by radiation from the fire or hot coals, while conduction and convection play secondary roles depending on the setup.', '["radiation","conduction","convection","microwave"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T13:37:53.167Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:37:53.167Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:37:53.167Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154321471-66', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Process of allowing meat to stand at low temperature for a few weeks is:', 'Aging', 'Aging is the controlled holding of meat at low temperature to allow postmortem enzymatic changes that improve tenderness and flavor. 

Curing is a preservation process using salt and related agents.', '["Curing","Aging","Preservation","Tenderization"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T15:51:56.777Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:51:56.777Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:51:56.777Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154344669-67', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Fat is used as edible spreads and shortening due to:', 'plasticity property', 'Plasticity is the ability of fat to be spread or molded while remaining semi-solid, making it useful in spreads and shortening.

• Softening property: Softening is a physical transition state near a melting point, not the technical property that defines mechanical moldability or spreadability.
• Viscosity property: Viscosity applies specifically to liquid fluids (their resistance to flow). Shortenings and spreads are evaluated as semi-solids or plastic solids, not free-flowing fluids.
• Greasy property: While fats feel greasy to the touch, this is a physical texture description rather than a functional engineering property used to manufacture baking ingredients or table spreads.', '["plasticity property","softening property","viscosity property","greasy property"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T15:08:02.798Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:08:02.798Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:08:02.798Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154378551-68', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Toasted flour (as in polvoron) is sweeter because of the formation of', 'dextrin', 'Heating flour causes dextrinization, producing dextrins that contribute a sweeter taste and browned flavor.', '["monosaccharides","dextrin","HCFS","gluten"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T13:14:21.808Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:14:21.808Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:14:21.808Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154409049-69', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Microorganism used to make tempeh', 'Rhizopus', 'Tempeh is a traditional Indonesian soy product made by a natural culturing and controlled fermentation process.

It specifically uses a wild mold or starter culture belonging to the genus Rhizopus—most commonly Rhizopus oligosporus or Rhizopus oryzae.

As the mold grows, its white filaments (hyphae) bind the soybeans together into a compact, solid cake that is rich in protein and fiber.

• Penicillium roqueforti: A blue mold fungus used in the production of blue cheeses (like Roquefort, Gorgonzola, and Stilton) to create its distinct flavor and blue veins.
• Aspergillus niger: A black mold fungus commonly used in food science to industrially produce citric acid and various commercial food enzymes, but not used for fermenting tempeh.', '["Rhizopus","Aspergillus niger","Penicillium roqueforti","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T15:23:46.235Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:23:46.235Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:23:46.235Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154436566-70', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Type of microorganism that will grow in orange marmalade', 'Osmophilic', 'Orange marmalade has a high sugar content, which creates an environment with low water activity. This condition is most favorable for osmophilic microorganisms.

Osmophilic microorganisms thrive in environments with high osmotic pressure, such as those with high concentrations of sugar. Therefore, the type of microorganism that will grow in orange marmalade is osmophilic.

Halophilic organisms thrive in high salt concentrations, xerophilic organisms are adapted to survive in extremely dry environments, and thermophilic organisms flourish in high-temperature conditions.', '["Halophilic","Thermophilic","Xerophilic","Osmophilic"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T13:27:17.205Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:27:17.205Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:27:17.205Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154465397-71', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Pasteurization is applied in processing foods that are generally', 'acidic', 'Pasteurization is generally used for acidic or acid foods because their acidity limits the growth of many dangerous spore-formers. 

Low-acid foods usually require more severe thermal processing.', '["salty","acidic","basic","spicy"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T11:48:55.767Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T11:48:55.767Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T11:48:55.767Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154490145-72', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Unfrozen water exists in all frozen food items because:', 'bound water cannot be frozen', 'Some water remains unfrozen because bound water is associated with food components and has reduced mobility and a lower freezing point.', '["bound water cannot be frozen","lowwater activity","high water activity","high water content"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:44:08.929Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:44:08.929Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:44:08.929Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154520944-73', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Principle of food preservation involved in ube jam processing is:', 'prevention from microbial decomposition', 'Ube jam is preserved mainly by preventing microbial decomposition through concentration of sugar and heat treatment, which lower water availability and reduce microbial survival.', '["prevention from physical damage","prevention from microbial decomposition","prevention from self-decomposition","prevention from biochemical decomposition"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T13:11:12.667Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:11:12.667Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:11:12.857Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154553259-74', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Deterioration that is formed when unwrapped or uncovered food items are stored in low temperature.', 'freezer burn', 'When food items are left unwrapped or uncovered in a low-temperature environment (specifically a freezer), the cold, dry air continuously pulls moisture out from the surface of the food. This leads to sublimation (where ice crystals turn directly into water vapor), leaving behind dehydrated, dry, and spongy pockets on the food''s surface.

• Case hardening: A structural defect that occurs during high-temperature drying or dehydration. If the heat is turned up too high too quickly, the outer surface of the food dries out and forms a hard, impermeable crust, trapping moisture inside and preventing proper preservation.
• Oxidative rancidity: The chemical breakdown of fats and oils caused by exposure to oxygen, resulting in an off-odor and unpleasant flavor. While open freezing accelerates oxygen exposure, freezer burn is the direct, visible physical deterioration that forms on uncovered foods.
• Putrefaction: The biological decomposition of proteins by anaerobic bacteria, resulting in foul odors. This happens in warm or improper storage conditions, as freezing temperatures typically halt or drastically slow down putrefactive bacterial growth.', '["oxidative rancidity","case hardening","freezer burn","Putrefaction"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T15:09:11.888Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:09:11.888Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:09:11.888Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154581258-75', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Group of microorganisms that are more likely to grow on the surface of dried squid packed in polyethylene bags', 'mold', 'Dried squid has significantly reduced moisture content and available water. 

Most bacteria require a high water activity (typically above 0.91) to grow. 

Yeasts generally need an Aw 0.80 or above. 

Conversely, xerophilic (dry-loving) molds can actively grow in environments with a water activity as low as 0.60 to 0.70.', '["mold","Bacteria","yeasts","Algae"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:46:59.644Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:46:59.644Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:46:59.644Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154667237-76', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'The amount of alcohol produced when making wines and beer depends primarily on', 'amount of fermentable carbohydrates', 'The amount of alcohol produced depends primarily on the amount of substrate or fermentable carbohydrate available for microorganisms to convert into ethanol.', '["kind of microorganisms present","amount of oxygen present","amount of fermentable carbohydrates","amount of salt"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T11:24:19.763Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T11:24:19.763Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T11:24:19.763Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154710584-77', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Which heats faster when microwaved', 'water', 'Water heats efficiently in a microwave because its polar molecules interact strongly with microwave energy. 

Water molecules have a positive end and a negative end, making them act like tiny magnets (dipoles). The microwave generates an electric field that changes direction billions of times every second.

Water molecules twist and flip back and forth to line up with this shifting field. This rapid movement causes the molecules to bump into each other, creating heat through friction. 

Glass and many dry solids absorb less, while butter behaves differently because of its composition.', '["water","glass","solids","butter"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:28:44.587Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:28:44.587Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:28:44.587Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154738334-78', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Used to limit the migration of moisture into the product.', 'Packaging', 'Packaging can act as a moisture barrier and limit the migration of moisture into or out of a food product. 

Heating, freezing, and drying change the product but do not primarily provide a barrier.', '["Heating","Drying","Freezing","Packaging"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:09:09.129Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:09:09.129Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:09:09.310Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154770449-79', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Process of ensuring that a number of factors are in place and will prevent growth of microorganisms', 'Hurdle concept', 'The hurdle concept combines several preservation factors so that microorganisms cannot grow even when any single factor alone may be insufficient.

It uses two or more intelligent preservation factors called "hurdles" so microorganisms cannot survive or multiply. Each hurdle disturbs the internal balance, or homeostasis, of the microbial cells.

Mild individual treatments work together to achieve a powerful result without damaging the food''s taste or nutrition.', '["Hurdle concept","Modified atmosphere packaging","Vacuumpack","Radura"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:45:09.547Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:45:09.547Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:45:09.547Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154795332-80', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'International symbol indicating food is irradiated', 'Radura', 'The Radura is the international symbol used to indicate that a food product has been treated with ionizing radiation (irradiated). It features a distinctive green icon of a stylized plant inside a broken circle, which symbolizes a safe protective shield.

• Hurdle concept: A highly influential food preservation strategy that applies a combination of multiple sub-lethal preservative factors or barriers (like adjusting temperature, pH, water activity, and competitive flora simultaneously) to completely inhibit microbial growth instead of relying on a single intense sterilization method.
• Vacuum pack: A packaging method where air is entirely drawn out and evacuated from a non-permeable pouch before sealing. This creates an anaerobic interior that prevents the growth of standard spoilage-causing aerobic bacteria and molds.
• Modified atmosphere packaging (MAP): A food preservation technique that replaces the ambient air inside a package with a precise, pre-calculated gas blend (usually varying combinations of nitrogen, carbon dioxide, and oxygen) to drastically slow down chemical respiration and extend the product''s natural shelf-life.', '["Hurdle concept","Modified atmosphere packaging","Vacuum pack","Radura"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T13:35:43.905Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:35:43.905Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:35:44.093Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154823165-81', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Intrinsic factors that have the capacity to either stimulate or retard the growth of microorganisms in food', 'pH, redox potential, water activity and antimicrobial substances', 'Intrinsic factors are properties inherent in the food itself.

These are:
• pH
• Moisture
• Redox potential
• Nutrient Content
• Antimicrobial constituents
• Biological structures', '["Temperature, relative humidity, pH and water activity","Redox potential, atmosphere, relative humidity and antimicrobial substances","Relative humidity, atmosphere and temperature","pH, redox potential, water activity and antimicrobial substances"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:46:00.399Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:46:00.399Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:46:00.399Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154859812-82', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'BSE or mad cow disease involves:', 'Prions', 'Bovine Spongiform Encephalopathy (BSE), commonly known as mad cow disease, is caused by an abnormal, infectious type of protein called a prion.

Prions are not alive like bacteria, viruses, or parasites; they are misfolded proteins. When they enter the body, they induce normal proteins in the brain and central nervous system to also misfold.

This causes a progressive, fatal neurological degeneration that leaves the brain looking like a sponge (spongiform). In humans, consuming meat contaminated with BSE prions can lead to Variant Creutzfeldt-Jakob Disease (vCJD), which is also fatal. Prions are extremely resilient and cannot be destroyed by normal cooking, freezing, or standard chemical disinfection.

• Virus: Infectious agents made of genetic material (DNA or RNA) inside a protein coat (e.g., Rabies, Foot-and-Mouth disease). BSE does not contain any genetic material.
• Bacteria: Single-celled living microorganisms (e.g., Salmonella, Anthrax). They can be killed with antibiotics or heat, whereas prions cannot.
• Parasites: Organisms that live on or inside a host and feed off it (e.g., Tapeworms, Trichinella in pork).', '["Virus","Prions","Bacteria","Parasites"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:35:34.774Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:35:34.774Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:35:34.774Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154884843-83', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Consumer Act of the Philippines', 'RA 7394', 'Enacted in 1992, Republic Act No. 7394, otherwise known as the Consumer Act of the Philippines, is the country''s primary legal framework dedicated to protecting consumer welfare, promoting general health and safety standards, and enforcing fair business practices.

• PD 856: This is the Code on Sanitation of the Philippines, which focuses on public health, waste management, and sanitation standards for institutions and establishments.
• RA 3720: This is the Food, Drug, and Cosmetic Act, a legacy law enacted in 1963 to ensure the safety and purity of foods, drugs, and cosmetics (later amended by RA 9711 to create the modern Food and Drug Administration).
• PD 704: This is the Fisheries Decree of 1975, which focuses on the conservation, development, and utilization of fishery and aquatic resources.', '["RA 7394","PD 704","RA 3720","PD 856"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T13:02:16.297Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:02:16.297Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:02:16.297Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154965807-84', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Code on Sanitation of the Philippines', 'PD 856', 'Presidential Decree No. 856, issued in 1975, is officially known as the Code on Sanitation of the Philippines. It sets the health and sanitation standards for food establishments, water supply, industrial hygiene, and public places in the country.

• RA 7394: The Consumer Act of the Philippines
• PD 704: The Fisheries Decree of 1975
• RA 3720: The Food, Drug, and Cosmetic Act', '["RA 7394","PD 704","RA 3720","PD 856"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T13:36:53.334Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:36:53.334Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:55:37.306Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755154986605-85', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Appropriate packaging material for liquid items which require high temperature processing', 'Tetra Pak', 'Tetrapack (Tetra Pak): This multi-layered carton packaging is specifically engineered for liquid items (such as milk, juices, and soups) that undergo aseptic or high-temperature processing (such as Ultra-High Temperature or UHT pasteurization and retort sterilization).

It provides a sterile environment, strong barrier protection against light and oxygen, and structural integrity under heat. 

• Saran: A plastic wrap (polyvinylidene chloride) mostly used for moisture/odor barriers or food covering, but not suitable for structural liquid packaging during high-temperature processing.
• Glassine: A smooth, translucent paper that is grease-resistant. It is used for dry goods, interleaving, or bakery items but cannot hold liquids or withstand extreme liquid processing temperatures. 
• Plioform (or Pliofilm): A rubber hydrochloride plastic film primarily used for wrapping moisture-sensitive items like meats, but not built for high-temperature liquid sterilization.', '["Saran","Plioform","Glassine","Tetra Pak"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T13:31:02.242Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:31:02.242Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:31:02.424Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755155023620-86', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Certification that a food safety management system is in place', 'ISO 22000', 'ISO 22000 is the correct answer because it specifically defines the international requirements for a Food Safety Management System (FSMS). 

• Good Manufacturing Practices (GMP): Operational guidelines and baseline conditions for safe food processing facilities, rather than an overarching management system certification.
• Good Agricultural Practices (GAP): Principles for safe and sustainable farming practices at the primary production level.
• CODEX Alimentarius: A collection of international standards, guidelines, and codes of practice adopted by the FAO/WHO, rather than a certifiable management system itself.', '["Good Manufacturing practices","ISO 22000","Good Agricultural practices","CODEX Alimentarius"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:49:09.925Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:49:09.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:49:09.925Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755155086001-87', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Which of the following microorganisms produce heat stable enterotoxin', 'Staphylococcus aureus', 'Staphylococcus aureus produces enterotoxins that resist high heat and can cause food poisoning even after the food is cooked.

• Aspergillus flavus produces aflatoxins (mycotoxins), not enterotoxins.
• Clostridium perfringens produces an enterotoxin in the gut during sporulation, but it is not typically classified as a pre-formed heat-stable food toxin in the same manner.
• Clostridium botulinum produces a neurotoxin that is heat-labile (destroyed by boiling).', '["Staphylococcus aureus","Clostridium perfringens","Clostridium botulinum","Aspergillus flavus"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:47:58.321Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:47:58.321Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:47:58.321Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755155117317-88', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'The cooling process behind storing food in earthen wares or clay pots.', 'evaporative cooling', 'Clay pots (traditionally known as palayok or banga in the Philippines) are made from porous earthenware clay.

When water or moist food is placed inside the pot, a small amount of moisture seeps through the tiny microscopic pores of the clay to the outer surface of the vessel.

As warm air passes over the outside of the pot, it causes this surface moisture to evaporate. In physics, evaporation requires heat energy. The water molecules absorb heat from the clay pot and the food inside it to transform into vapor, leaving the remaining contents significantly cooler than the surrounding ambient temperature.', '["chilling","evaporative cooling","refrigeration","slow cooling"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:24:51.455Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:24:51.455Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:24:51.455Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755155140832-89', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Syrup used for freezing delicate flavored fruits.', 'Thin', 'In food preservation and freezing science, a thin syrup (low sugar-to-water concentration, usually around 20% to 30% sugar) is intentionally used for mild or delicate-flavored fruits like melons, grapefruits, and pineapples.

A higher sugar concentration (like heavy or very heavy syrup) would completely overpower and mask the natural, subtle flavors of these fruits. A thin pack provides just enough sugar density to protect the cell structure, retain the fruit''s shape, and block oxygen from causing discoloration, all without ruining its delicate taste.

• Heavy: Contains a much higher sugar-to-water concentration (around 40% to 50% sugar). It is reserved for strong-flavored, highly acidic, or very sour fruits (like sour cherries or plums) that can stand up to heavy sweetness.
• Moderate (Medium): A standard mid-range syrup option (around 30% to 40% sugar) used for everyday fruits with balanced flavors like peaches, pears, and apples.
• Dry: Refers to the "dry sugar pack" method where dry granulated sugar is sprinkled directly onto juicy fruits (like strawberries) to draw out their natural juices to form their own syrup. This is not a liquid syrup classification used for delicate whole or sliced fruits.', '["Thin","Heavy","Moderate","Dry"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:51:06.298Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:51:06.298Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:51:06.298Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755155169598-90', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Factor affecting the size of ice crystals in food', 'rate of freezing', 'The rate of freezing strongly affects ice-crystal size: rapid freezing forms many small crystals, while slow freezing allows larger crystals to develop.', '["quantity of bound water","type of food","rate of freezing","presence of enzymes in food"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T13:27:35.833Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:27:35.833Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:27:35.833Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755155200813-91', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'The canning process at high altitude must be:', 'lengthened because boiling point gets lower', 'At higher altitudes, atmospheric pressure is lower and water boils at a lower temperature, so thermal processing time must be lengthened to achieve the required lethality.', '["lengthened because boiling point gets lower","lengthened because relative humidity gets lower","shortened because boiling point gets higher","shortened because relative humidity gets higher"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T11:40:08.468Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T11:40:08.468Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T11:40:08.468Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755155253442-92', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'The desired salt concentration of the medium in the production of burong mangga is:', '5 to 15%', 'Burong mangga is prepared using a salt concentration within the keyed 5–15% range to support the desired preservation and fermentation conditions.

In the lactic acid fermentation process of making burong mangga (fermented green mangoes), salt serves to draw out moisture and nutrients via osmosis. This creates a favorable environment for beneficial lactic acid bacteria while suppressing the growth of spoilage-causing organisms.

A brine concentration within 5% to 15% (most typically maintained around 5% to 10% or a 40° salometer reading during active fermentation) ensures proper preservation and texture without completely arresting microbial activity. 

When concentration below 5%, proteolytic or spoilage bacteria may cause the mangoes to become mushy and foul-smelling. 

When concentration is higher than 15% to 20% without gradual adjustments, and the fermentation slows down dramatically or stops entirely.', '["4 to 15%","15 to 20%","5 to 15%","0 to 5%"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:22:29.700Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:22:29.700Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:22:29.700Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755155281574-93', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Deterioration of canned items due to undercooling that results to growth of thermophilic microorganisms', 'Flat sours', 'Flat sour spoilage occurs when thermophilic microorganisms grow and produce acid without gas, often associated with inadequate cooling or storage conditions.

• Springer: A can where one flat end bulges outward, but if you press it down with your finger, the opposite end pops out instead.
• Hydrogen swell: A chemical defect caused by internal corrosion where the acid in the food reacts with the tinplate lining of the can, generating hydrogen gas that physically swells the can.
• Flipper: A can that appears completely normal and flat on both ends, but when struck or brought down hard against a flat table surface, one end flips or bulges outward due to internal vacuum loss.', '["Flipper","Hydrogen swell","Springer","Flat sours"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T13:47:31.913Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:47:31.913Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:47:31.913Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755155315058-94', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Best temperature for drying.', '140-145ºF', 'In food dehydration, 140°F or 60°C is widely recognized as the optimum standard temperature. If the temperature is too high, the outside of the food cooks and hardens (“case hardening”), which traps moisture inside and leads to molding. 

This temperature range is also high enough to safely drive out moisture quickly before spoilage micro-organisms can replicate, but low enough to avoid cooking the food. 

Consider also:
• Air Flow
• Time
• Nature of food', '["100-115ºF","120-125ºF","130-135ºF","140-145ºF"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:45:16.051Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:45:16.051Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:45:16.051Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755155337690-95', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Food additive used to prevent both enzymatic and non-enzymatic discoloration', 'Sulfur dioxide', 'Sulfur Dioxide inhibits the action of polyphenol oxidase (PPO), the enzyme responsible for turning cut or bruised fruits and vegetables brown.

It reacts also with carbonyl intermediates in the Maillard reaction, stopping the chemical processes that cause heat- or storage-induced discoloration in processed foods. 

• Sodium Nitrites / Potassium Nitrates: These are primarily used as curing agents and antimicrobials in processed meat products (like bacon and hot dogs) to lock in a stable pink color and prevent bacterial growth. They do not address general enzymatic or non-enzymatic plant discoloration. 
• Benzoic Acid: This is used as an antimicrobial preservative to inhibit the growth of mold, yeast, and bacteria in highly acidic environments like juices and carbonated drinks.', '["Sodiumnitrites","Sulfur dioxide","Potassium nitrates","Benzoic acids"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T13:03:57.965Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:03:57.965Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:03:57.965Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755155368470-96', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Processed cheese is predominantly made with', 'None of the above', 'Processed cheese is predominantly made with natural cheese, typically accounting for about 50–60% of its composition).

Water, dairy solids, emulsifying salts, and sometimes vegetable oils or fats make up the remaining portion.

Milk: While derived from milk originally via the natural cheese base, processed cheese is blended from finished cheese rather than fluid milk.', '["Milk","Vegetable oil","Water","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:49:31.857Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:49:31.857Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:49:31.857Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755155396153-97', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Sugar concentrate made from crushed fruit pulp used to flavor the popular suman from Leyte with chocolate is', 'Jam', 'Jam is a concentrated fruit product made from crushed or pulped fruit and sugar, making it suitable as a flavoring concentrate.

Jelly is made from clear fruit juice strained out after boiling, containing no pulp pieces.

Preserves contain whole fruits or large, uniform pieces of fruit cooked in a thick syrup

Food gels are semi-solid, viscoelastic structures made by trapping liquids within a network of proteins, starches, or gums.', '["Jam","Jelly","Gel","Preserve"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T14:53:57.965Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T14:53:57.965Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T14:53:57.965Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755155421868-98', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Precipitating agent of pectin causing it to form network of the jelly', 'Sugar', 'Sugar acts as the precipitating agent that draws water away from the pectin molecules, allowing them to bond and form the network of the gel.

It attracts and holds water, breaking the pectin-water equilibrium and forcing the pectin chains to link together.

• Acid: Neutralizes the negative charges on pectin molecules so they do not repel each other, assisting the set.
• High heat activates the gelling properties of pectin so it can form a molecular web that traps the remaining liquid and thickens the jam. The ideal setting temperature for homemade jam is  around 220°F (105°C) at sea level, but may vary depending on type of fruit used.
• Water naturally exists inside fruit cells and acts as the liquid medium where sugar and natural pectin dissolve.', '["Acid","Heat","water","Sugar"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:17:48.343Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:17:48.343Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:17:48.343Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755155454901-99', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'The process of jelly making involves boiling fruit to:', 'extract pectin, obtain maximum juice and extract flavor', 'Boiling fruit in jelly making helps extract pectin and juice and develop the characteristic flavor of the finished jelly.', '["hydrolyze pectic acid, dissolve the fruit pulp and extract color","extract pectin, obtain maximum juice and extract flavor","dissolve the pectic acid, extract the sugar and flavor","volatize the aroma, extract pulp and hydrolyze the protopectin"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T15:22:17.130Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:22:17.130Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:22:17.130Z"'::jsonb)
