('anki-card-1755157217084-150', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Management by Objective implies the need to have', 'Clearly defined key result areas and time', 'Management by Objectives (MBO) is a strategic management model that aims to improve organizational performance by aligning employee goals with the overall objectives of the company. It fundamentally relies on setting specific, measurable targets (Key Result Areas) within a designated timeframe so that progress can be tracked objectively.', '["A good manager","Clear organizational chart","Clearly defined key result areas and time","Adequate staff"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T15:29:45.196Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:29:45.196Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:29:45.377Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157249083-151', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'The principle of “span of supervision” recognizes that:', 'There is a limit to a person’s capacity to supervise effectively', 'Span of supervision recognizes that there is a practical limit to the number of subordinates one person can supervise effectively.', '["The more subordinates under one supervisor the better","The less subordinates, the better","The supervisor should be near the subordinates at all times","There is a limit to a person’s capacity to supervise effectively"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T12:51:17.957Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T12:51:17.957Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T12:51:18.129Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157271446-152', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Most government hospitals purchase food by:', 'Bid buying', 'Government hospitals commonly use bid buying or competitive bidding to promote transparency and obtain acceptable terms under procurement rules.', '["Negotiated buying","Bid buying","Future contract","Blank check"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:51:09.038Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:51:09.038Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:51:09.038Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157298212-153', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Example of fringe benefit', 'Christmas bonus', 'A fringe benefit is any form of extra compensation provided by an employer to an employee supplemental to their regular basic salary or wages. They are designed to improve job satisfaction, motivation, and employee retention.

While regular pay covers your standard work hours, monetary perks like a Christmas bonus, profit sharing, gym memberships, or rice allowances are classic examples of fringe or de minimis benefits. Under Philippine labor and tax laws, discretionary year-end bonuses and small-value perks given for employee wellness or holiday celebrations fall directly into this category.', '["Promotion","Christmas bonus","Dayoff","Holiday off"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T15:47:19.545Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:47:19.545Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:47:19.545Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157338677-154', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'All newly hired employees should be given:', 'Orientation', 'Orientation introduces newly hired employees to the organization, policies, workplace, and basic expectations before or at the start of employment.', '["Orientation","Pre-service training","IQ test","Medical check-up"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T11:25:53.291Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T11:25:53.291Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T11:25:53.478Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157368975-155', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'A No.2 can of fruit juice contains', '2 ¼ cups', 'In standard Food Service and Institutional Management measurements, a No. 2 can has the following characteristics:
• Weight/Volume: Approximately 20 ounces (1 lb 4 oz)
• Volume in Cups: Approximately 2 ½ cups (2.5 cups)
• Average Servings: Offers about 5 servings of 4 ounces each.

Other Common Can Sizes for Comparison:

• No. 1 can: Contains about 1⅓ cups
• No. 2 ½ can: Contains about 3 ½ cups
• No. 3 can: Contains about 4 to 5 ¾ cups (often used for single-strength juices)
• No. 10 can: Contains about 12 to 13 cups (the massive institutional standard can)', '["1 cup","2 ¼ cups","1 gallon","2 gallons"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:46:47.559Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:46:47.559Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:46:47.559Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157398191-156', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Appropriate storage temperature for ripe fruits (except bananas).', '50ºF', '50ºF (approx. 10ºC) falls perfectly into the "cool storage" range (40–55°F) used to slow down the respiration and ripening process of many ripe, perishable fruits without causing chilling injuries or freezing.

20ºF is well below freezing and would destroy the cellular structure of the fruit, ruining its texture.

50ºC (122ºF) is extremely hot and would cook the fruit, leading to rapid decay.

Room temperature accelerates spoiling and rot once a fruit is already fully ripe.', '["20ºF","50ºF","50ºC","Roomtemperature"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:14:39.429Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:14:39.429Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:14:39.429Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157426791-157', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Minimum internal cooking temperature of pork chop', '145ºF', 'According to the USDA Safe Minimum Internal Temperature Chart, fresh whole muscle cuts of pork—including pork chops, pork roasts, and pork loins—must be cooked to a minimum internal temperature of 145°F (63°C).

To safely hit this baseline, you must also allow the meat to rest for at least 3 minutes after removing it from the heat source. During this resting period, the internal temperature remains constant or continues to rise slightly, destroying harmful foodborne pathogens while keeping the meat juicy and tender.

• 155ºF: This is the standard minimum internal cooking temperature for ground meats (such as ground pork, ground beef, or sausage) under regulatory food safety frameworks like ServSafe. Ground meats require a higher temperature because the grinding process distributes surface bacteria throughout the meat.
• 165ºF: This is the required safety threshold for all poultry (chicken, turkey, duck), stuffed meats, and reheated leftovers.
• 170ºF: This is an older, outdated standard for pork. Cooking modern, lean pork to 170°F results in a dry, tough, and overcooked piece of meat.', '["170ºF","155ºF","165ºF","145ºF"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:43:53.960Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:43:53.960Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:43:53.960Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157455488-158', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Minimum internal cooking temperature of salmon', '145ºF', 'Salmon: 145°F (63°C) or cook until the flesh is opaque and flakes easily with a fork.

• 165ºF: The safe baseline for all poultry (chicken, turkey) and leftovers.
• 155ºF: The standard food safety threshold often taught for ground meats (like pork or beef) under regional food codes before the general public safety chart rounds it to 160°F.
• 170ºF: The internal temperature indicator for completely well-done beef or game meat.', '["170ºF","155ºF","165ºF","145ºF"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T12:50:33.914Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T12:50:33.914Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T12:50:33.914Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157482805-159', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Minimum internal cooking temperature of eggs', '160ºF', 'Eggs: 160°F (71°C) for combined dishes like casseroles or quiches; for whole, fried, or scrambled eggs, cook until both the white and the yolk are firm.', '["140ºF","150ºF","160ºF","170ºF"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T11:27:09.128Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T11:27:09.128Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T11:27:09.128Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157511652-160', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'The total raw food cost of a recipe yielding 50 serving portions is ₱200. To keep raw food costs at 40%, the selling price per portion should be:', '₱10.00', 'Food cost per serving is ₱200 ÷ 50 = ₱4. 

If ₱4 represents 40% of selling price, selling price = ₱4 ÷ 0.40 = ₱10.', '["₱4.00","₱8.00","₱10.00","₱80.00"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:08:31.658Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:08:31.658Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:08:31.658Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157539636-161', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'This equipment is useful when food production and service areas are on separate floors.', 'Dumbwaiter', 'A dumbwaiter is a small, specialized freight elevator or lift system designed to transport food, dishes, and kitchen supplies vertically between multiple floors of a building.

In hospitality, hospitals, and multi-story restaurant settings, the main food production kitchen is often located in the basement or ground floor, while the service or dining areas are located on upper levels. A dumbwaiter allows hot meals to be quickly and safely dispatched to service stations on separate floors without relying on staff manually carrying heavy trays up and down stairs or taking up passenger elevators.

• Hood: A kitchen exhaust ventilation canopy positioned directly above cooking equipment to remove steam, smoke, heat, and airborne grease.
• Doilies: Small, decorative, ornamental mats made of paper, lace, or fabric used in food presentation (such as being placed on a saucer beneath a coffee cup or a dessert bowl).
• Bain-marie: A specialized water bath system or hot well table used to hold, warm, or gently cook hot foods at a stable temperature in production or buffet service lines. It does not move food across different floors.', '["Doilies","Hood","Bainmarie","Dumbwaiter"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:02:32.933Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:02:32.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:02:32.933Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157563117-162', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Basis for recruiting personnel', 'Job description', 'Job description – an organized list of duties, skills and responsibilities required in a specific position. This should be written for every position and should be reviewed and updated periodically.', '["Job description","Performance rating scale","Procedure manual","Organizational chart"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:46:55.406Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:46:55.406Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:46:55.406Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157618497-163', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'In the satellite food production system,', 'Food procurement and pre-preparation are
 centralized, but final preparation and service
 are decentralized', 'All bulk food procurement, inventory storage, and primary pre-preparation (and often major cooking) are handled entirely at a single, heavily equipped central facility.

The prepared or semi-prepared menu items are then systematically transported to separate, remote satellite units (such as individual schools, hospitals, or smaller branches). These decentralized satellite sites handle the final preparation (like rethermalizing or portioning) and immediate service to the consumers.', '["Food procurement and pre-preparation are\n centralized, but final preparation and service\n are decentralized","All the centers are decentralized","Food is prepared and then frozen until needed","Food procurement and pre-preparation are centralized, but final preparation and service are decentralized"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T15:04:18.736Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:04:18.736Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:04:18.736Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157651329-164', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'When fish fillet is on the menu, you need fish that will be:', 'deboned and sliced', 'Fish fillets should be boneless and cut into appropriate portions or slices because a fillet is a boneless section of fish flesh.', '["served whole","deboned and sliced","flaked","stuffed"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T13:38:52.070Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:38:52.070Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:38:52.070Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157675278-165', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Paella Negra gets its black color from:', 'Squid ink', 'Paella Negra (also known as Arroz Negro in Spain) gets its signature deep black color and distinct savory, umami flavor from squid ink (or cuttlefish ink), which is incorporated directly into the cooking liquid while the rice simmers.

• Bile: This bitter fluid produced by the liver is used in specific traditional dishes (like the Filipino beef soup papaitan) to add a bitter flavor profile and a greenish tint, not a rich black color.
• Pirurutong: A native heirloom variety of sticky, deep purple-to-black rice commonly used in the Philippines to make traditional desserts like puto bumbong. It is not used in traditional paella.
• Black rice: While natural black rice grains exist (like forbidden rice), classic Paella Negra is made using standard white medium-grain rice (like Bomba or Arborio) that is stained black during the cooking process using the ink.', '["Squid ink","Bile","Black rice","Pirurutong"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T11:46:17.226Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T11:46:17.226Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T11:46:17.226Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157701142-166', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Bacteria commonly found in shellfish from contaminated water that can cause gastroenteritis or primary septicemia among patients with cirrhosis or diabetes.', 'Vibrio vulnificus', 'Vibrio vulnificus is a halophilic (salt-loving), Gram-negative bacterium naturally found in warm coastal and brackish waters. It frequently contaminates filter-feeding shellfish like oysters and clams.

While it can cause mild gastroenteritis in healthy individuals, it poses an extreme danger to individuals with underlying health conditions—especially liver cirrhosis, chronic liver disease, or diabetes.

In these high-risk patients, eating contaminated raw/undercooked seafood can allow the bacteria to cross the intestinal wall into the bloodstream. This triggers primary septicemia (blood poisoning), which progresses rapidly into septic shock, severe blistering skin lesions (hemorrhagic bullae), and multiorgan failure. It carries a staggering mortality rate of over 50%.

• Listeria monocytogenes: Known for contaminating deli meats, unpasteurized milk, and soft cheeses. While it causes severe illness in pregnant women, newborns, and immunocompromised individuals (listeriosis), it is not a hallmark cause of primary shellfish-borne septicemia in cirrhotic patients.
• Shigella spp: A bacterium primarily transmitted via the fecal-oral route through contaminated food or water. It causes bacillary dysentery (severe diarrhea with blood/mucus) but does not typically present as marine-acquired septicemia.
• Hepatitis A: A virus (not a bacterium) that can be contracted from shellfish harvested from sewage-polluted waters. It causes acute liver inflammation (infectious hepatitis) rather than bacterial gastroenteritis or rapid septic shock.', '["Vibrio vulnificus","Shigella spp","Hepatitis A","Listeria monocytogenes"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T15:27:44.104Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:27:44.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:27:44.104Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157725941-167', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'A savory pie with a predominant egg filling.', 'Quiche', 'A quiche is a French savory pie consisting of a pastry crust filled with savory custard, cheese, meats, seafood, or vegetables.

The defining characteristic of a quiche is its predominant egg and cream filling, which bakes into a rich, custard-like texture.

• Omelet: A dish made from beaten eggs fried with butter or oil in a frying pan, usually folded around a filling. It does not have a pie crust.
• Egg tart: A sweet pastry crust filled with a sugary egg custard, popular in Portuguese, English, and Hong Kong cuisines. It is a dessert, not a savory pie.', '["Egg tart","Quiche","Omelet","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:42:41.210Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:42:41.210Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:42:41.210Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157748441-168', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Spore-forming bacteria that grows without oxygen and can produce a deadly toxin when food is time-temperature abused.', 'Clostridium botulinum', 'Clostridium botulinum is a notorious spore-forming bacterium. Its spores can survive extreme environmental conditions, including normal cooking temperatures.

It is strictly anaerobic, meaning it thrives and multiplies only in environments devoid of oxygen—such as improperly home-canned foods, vacuum-packed foods, garlic-in-oil mixtures, or tightly wrapped baked potatoes.

When contaminated food is time-temperature abused, the spores germinate into active bacteria and produce a highly lethal neurotoxin. Ingesting even a microscopic amount of this toxin causes botulism, a severe foodborne illness that leads to muscle paralysis and can be fatal if respiratory muscles fail.

• Salmonella spp: A non-spore-forming, facultative anaerobic bacterium commonly found in poultry and eggs. It causes an infection rather than a pre-formed deadly neurotoxin.
• Listeria monocytogenes: A non-spore-forming bacterium that can grow in cold environments (like refrigerators). It is an aerobe/facultative anaerobe commonly linked to unpasteurized dairy and deli meats.
• Bacillus cereus: While this is a spore-forming bacterium linked to time-temperature abuse (classically found in fried rice), it is a facultative anaerobe (grows with or without oxygen) and its toxins cause vomiting or diarrhea, but are rarely lethal compared to botulinum neurotoxins.', '["Clostridium botulinum","Salmonella spp","Listeria monocytogenes","Bacillus cereus"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:50:59.661Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:50:59.661Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:50:59.661Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157769508-169', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'The following are yogurt variations or dishes with yogurt EXCEPT:', 'Hummus', 'Hummus is a popular Middle Eastern dip or spread. It is fundamentally made from cooked, mashed chickpeas (garbanzo beans) blended with tahini (toasted ground sesame paste), olive oil, lemon juice, salt, and garlic. It does not traditionally contain any yogurt or dairy products.

• Kefir: A fermented milk drink very similar to a thin, pourable yogurt. It is made by inoculating cow, goat, or sheep milk with symbiotic colonies of bacteria and yeast known as "kefir grains."
• Tzatziki: A classic Greek yogurt sauce or dip. It is prepared by mixing salted strained yogurt (Greek yogurt) with grated cucumber, garlic, olive oil, and fresh herbs like dill or mint.
• Raita: A traditional South Asian (Indian) condiment. It consists of dahi (native yogurt) mixed with raw or cooked vegetables (like cucumber, onions, or tomatoes), fruits, and toasted spices like cumin and coriander.', '["Raita","Hummus","Kefir","Tsatziki"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:22:05.178Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:22:05.178Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:22:05.178Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157794272-170', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'When cost is not a problem, the best material for sinks is:', 'Stainless steel', 'Stainless steel is the preferred sink material when cost is not limiting because it is durable, corrosion-resistant, smooth, and easy to clean and sanitize.', '["Stainless steel","Japanese steel","Galvanized iron","Aluminum"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:44:06.316Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:44:06.316Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:44:06.316Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157825255-171', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Being non-flammable, asbestos is good for:', 'Roofing material', 'Asbestos was historically valued for non-flammability and heat resistance and was used in construction materials, but it is now recognized as a serious health hazard and should not be recommended for new applications.', '["Office furniture","Kitchen table tops","Roofing material","All of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T15:58:28.521Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:58:28.521Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T15:58:28.521Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157850971-172', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Bacteria found in the intestines of cattle that causes hemorrhagic colitis.', 'Shiga-toxin producing E. coli', 'Shiga toxin-producing Escherichia coli (STEC), most notably the E. coli O157:H7 strain, naturally and asymptomatically colonizes the intestines of healthy cattle and other ruminants. When humans consume food or water contaminated with bovine feces (such as undercooked ground beef or unpasteurized raw milk), the bacteria colonize the human large intestine and release potent Shiga toxins. These toxins cause severe vascular damage to the intestinal lining, resulting in acute hemorrhagic colitis (profuse, bloody diarrhea).

• Staphylococcus aureus: A major cause of food intoxication, but the bacteria reside primarily on human skin and nasal passages. It produces heat-stable enterotoxins that trigger rapid onset vomiting and abdominal cramps, not hemorrhagic colitis.
• Clostridium perfringens: While it can be found in animal intestines and causes common foodborne diarrhea, it is associated with meat products held at improper serving temperatures, resulting in watery diarrhea rather than hemorrhagic colitis. (Note: In veterinary medicine, it is linked to Hemorrhagic Bowel Syndrome in cattle itself, but not as the zoonotic agent causing human hemorrhagic colitis).
• Vibrio vulnificus: A marine bacterium found in warm coastal waters. It is contracted by eating raw shellfish (like oysters) or through open wound exposure to seawater, causing severe septicemia or necrotizing fasciitis, not cattle-borne colitis.', '["Shiga-toxin producing E. coli","Clostridium perfringens","Staphylococcus aureus","Vibrio vulnificus"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T14:58:47.664Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T14:58:47.664Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T14:58:47.664Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157873720-173', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Setting and clearing of dinner plates is done at the ______________.', 'Right of the guest', 'Dinner plates are conventionally set and cleared from the guest''s right in standard service procedures.', '["Right of the guest","Left of the guest","both a and b","none of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:11:48.270Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:11:48.270Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:11:48.270Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157930249-174', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'The government agency is mandated to ensure the safety of food supplies.', 'FDA', 'FDA (Food and Drug Administration): This agency is primary mandated to ensure the safety, efficacy, and quality of food supplies, drugs, cosmetics, and medical devices.

• DA (Department of Agriculture): While the DA is heavily involved in agriculture and food production, the regulatory enforcement of safety standards for processed and pre-packaged food supplies falls under the FDA.
• FNRI (Food and Nutrition Research Institute): Focuses on research, data collection, and nutritional science.
• NNC (National Nutrition Council): Serves as the policy-making and coordinating body for nutrition programs.', '["FNRI","NNC","FDA","DA"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:07:27.909Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:07:27.909Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:07:27.909Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755157972364-175', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Sanitizing food service utensils may be accomplished by', 'Both of the above', 'Sanitizing may be accomplished by approved hot-water immersion or approved chemical treatment, depending on the equipment and procedure.', '["Immersion in hot water","Chemical treatment","Both of the above","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T13:21:58.285Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:21:58.285Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:21:58.285Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755158000263-176', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Menu analysis is essential in determining:', 'All of the above', 'Menu analysis helps determine equipment needs, kitchen space, and the number and skills of workers; therefore all listed factors may be affected.', '["Type and number of equipment","Kitchen space requirements","Skills and number of workers","All of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:47:31.662Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:47:31.662Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:47:31.662Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755158026213-177', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Open market buying means', 'After a canvass, purchases are made from the vendor who offers the best terms', 'Open market buying is a flexible procurement method commonly used in food service and small businesses. 

Instead of locking into a long-term contract with a single supplier, the buyer "canvasses" (requests price quotes from) multiple vendors and places the order with whoever provides the best price, quality, and delivery terms for that specific purchase.', '["The buyer has to go to the market","After a canvass, purchases are made from the vendor who offers the best terms","Purchasing through a middle man","Purchasing from one source only"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T11:28:14.428Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T11:28:14.428Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T11:28:14.428Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755158072392-178', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'To avoid conflict in authority, all workers should:', 'Know to whom they are directly responsible', 'Unity of command requires each worker to know the person to whom they are directly responsible, helping avoid conflicting authority.', '["Know to whom they are directly responsible","Be directly responsible to the head of the department","Cooperate with each other","Be rotated in different sections"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:50:50.802Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:50:50.802Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:50:50.802Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755158107724-179', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Type of oven in which heat is generated from within the food', 'Microwave', 'Unlike traditional ovens that heat the air around the food, a microwave oven uses an electronic tube called a magnetron to produce electromagnetic waves (microwaves).

These waves pass directly into the food and are absorbed by water, fat, and sugar molecules. The microwaves cause these polar molecules to rotate rapidly billions of times per second.

This intense friction generates heat from within the food itself, which then spreads outward to cook the rest of the item. This is why microwaving is incredibly fast compared to surface-heating methods.

• Convection: An oven equipped with a fan and exhaust system that actively circulates hot air around the cavity, transferring heat to the food''s surface via currents.
• Quartz: An oven that uses quartz heating elements to emit infrared radiant heat, cooking the food from the outside in using light energy.
• Conventional: A standard radiant oven where stationary hot air rises from heating elements at the bottom or top of the appliance, slowly warming the exterior of the food.', '["Microwave","Conventional","Convection","Quartz"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:44:46.019Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:44:46.019Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:44:46.019Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755158146671-180', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'The following are under the danger zone EXCEPT:', '80ºC', 'The food temperature danger zone is the range between 40°F and 140°F (4°C and 60°C) where harmful bacteria multiply rapidly, doubling in number in as little as 20 minutes.', '["41ºF","120ºF","80ºC","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:44:57.605Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:44:57.605Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:44:57.605Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755158182737-181', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Concrete floors in a food service facility are:', 'Both of the above', 'Concrete floors are durable and suitable for areas such as storerooms and receiving areas, but they are hard and non-resilient, which can fatigue workers. 

Therefore both statements are correct.', '["Suitable for storerooms and receiving area","Not resilient and therefore fatiguing to workers","Both of the above","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:46:13.652Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:46:13.652Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:46:13.652Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755158200520-182', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Promotes team spirit of unity and harmony among employees', 'Principle of esprit de corps', 'According to Henri Fayol''s 14 Principles of Management, Esprit de Corps literally translates to "group spirit" or "team spirit". This principle dictates that organizations should actively strive to promote team spirit, mutual trust, unity, and harmony among employees to build a cooperative and highly productive work environment.

• Principle of unity of command: States that each employee should receive orders from, and report to, only one direct supervisor to prevent confusion and conflicting instructions.
• Principle of centralization: Refers to the degree to which decision-making authority is concentrated at the top levels of management versus being dispersed throughout the organization.
• Principle of unity of direction: States that organizational activities sharing the same objective must be directed by a single manager using a single, unified plan to ensure proper coordination.', '["Principle of unity of direction","Principle of unity of command","Principle of centralization","Principle of esprit de corps"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T13:59:33.538Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:59:33.538Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:59:33.735Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755158220967-183', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'The architectural plan of spaces on a floor of a building is called the:', 'Floor plan', 'A floor plan is a scaled, top-down diagram showing the arrangement of rooms, spaces, and structural features on a specific floor of a building.

A blueprint is a general reproduction or copy of any technical drawing.

A lay-out is a broader term for the overall arrangement of elements, not strictly the architectural drawing of a building floor.

Foodservice design refers specifically to commercial kitchen and dining facility planning.', '["Blueprint","Lay-out","Floor plan","Foodservice design"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:47:16.736Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:47:16.736Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:47:16.736Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755158245467-184', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'The principle that refers to the number of subordinates who report directly to a higher executive', 'Span of control', 'Span of control is the number of subordinates who report directly to a manager or higher executive.

• Departmentalization: The process of dividing an organization into distinct sections or departments based on functions, products, or geographic areas (e.g., separating a facility into a Kitchen Department, Purchasing Department, and Accounting Department).
• Unity of command: The management principle stating that each subordinate should receive orders from, and be accountable to, only one direct supervisor to prevent conflicting instructions.
• Delegation: The act of assigning authority, responsibility, and specific tasks from a higher-level manager down to a subordinate.', '["Span of control","Departmentalization","Unity of command","Delegation"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:44:02.386Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:44:02.386Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:44:02.386Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755158261668-185', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Budget that is used to determine if funds will be available when needed:', 'Cash', 'Cash Budget tracks expected cash inflows and outflows. Its primary purpose is to manage liquidity, allowing managers to forecast cash positions and ensure that enough cash is available when needed to meet immediate obligations like payroll or supplier bills. 

• Master Budget: This is a comprehensive, overarching financial plan that consolidates all individual functional budgets (including operating, capital, and financial budgets). 
• Operating Budget: This focuses on day-to-day revenue-generating activities, such as projected sales, production, and routine operating expenses. It does not measure actual cash timing.
• Capital Budget: This is a long-term plan dedicated to major asset investments, such as buying property, new machinery, or technology', '["Master","Operating","Capital","Cash"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:46:03.165Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:46:03.165Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:46:03.165Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755158296132-186', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Lenten observance among Roman Catholics prescribes abstinence from:', 'Meat', 'Roman Catholic Lenten abstinence traditionally prescribes abstaining from meat on designated days. Fish and other non-meat foods may be consumed.', '["Fish and shellfish","Vegetables","Meat","Fruits"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:23:06.952Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:23:06.952Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:23:06.952Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755158338597-187', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'The optimum working Tº is between:', '65-73ºF', 'The optimum working temperature for productivity and human comfort in an office environment is typically between 65–73ºF (18–23ºC).', '["60-71ºF","3-72ºF","65-73ºF","67-74ºF"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:51:37.026Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:51:37.026Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:51:37.026Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755158361461-188', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Pertains to a disciplined, data-driven approach and methodology for eliminating defects in any process from manufacturing to transactional and from product to service.', 'Six sigma', 'Six Sigma is a disciplined, data-driven method for eliminating defects and reducing variation in manufacturing, service, and transactional processes.

HACCP (Hazard Analysis Critical Control Point) focuses specifically on food safety risk management.

ISO 22000 is an international standard for food safety management systems.

TQM (Total Quality Management) is a broader organization-wide management approach to long-term success through customer satisfaction, rather than a specific statistical defect-reduction methodology like Six Sigma.', '["Six sigma","HACCP","ISO 22000","TQM"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:45:25.450Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:45:25.450Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:45:25.450Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755158384977-189', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Function of management involved in the development of formal structure through which work is defined, divided and coordinated to achieve goals.', 'Organizing', 'In management science (including Henri Fayol''s and Luther Gulick''s classic management frameworks), organizing is the process of building the formal structural framework of an organization.

It specifically involves arranging resources, defining roles, dividing tasks or labor into manageable departments, and establishing a hierarchy or chain of command so that workflows can be successfully coordinated to achieve organizational objectives.

• Planning: The foundational function that involves setting goals, projecting future scenarios, and mapping out the specific courses of action required to achieve them. It happens before structure is built.
• Coordinating: The function of harmonizing and unifying separate team efforts and workflows to ensure they run smoothly together. While related to structure, it is a component of directing or the output of a well-organized system rather than the function that develops the formal structural framework.
• Staffing: The process of recruiting, selecting, hiring, training, and maintaining the human resources needed to fill the positions established by the organizational structure.', '["Coordinating","Planning","Organizing","Staffing"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:48:11.310Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:48:11.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:48:11.310Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755158434275-190', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'The aim of work design is to:', 'increase productivity and employee satisfaction', 'Work design aims to develop jobs and methods that improve productivity and employee satisfaction while supporting efficient, safe work.', '["increase productivity and employee satisfaction","provide efficient and effective work methods","provide safe and healthy work environment","design a staff of fit people"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:45:53.595Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:45:53.595Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:45:53.595Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755158463108-191', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Information which is/are useful for time and motion studies:', 'all of the above', 'Job breakdowns, process charts, and flow charts can all provide information useful in time-and-motion studies.', '["job breakdown","process chart","flow chart","all of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T13:40:49.936Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:40:49.936Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:40:49.936Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755158487407-192', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Broiler is a term used to refer to', 'Chicken', 'Broiler is a market term for a young chicken suitable for broiling or similar dry-heat cooking.

• Young or middle-aged pork: Swine or pigs are categorized into culinary and market classes such as suckling pig (lechon de leche), boar, sow, or gilt. The term "broiler" is never applied to pork or any mammalian livestock.', '["Chicken","Young pork","Middle-aged pork","All of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T13:21:02.441Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:21:02.441Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:21:02.441Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755158518621-193', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'It is a special type of broiler used in foodservice that makes use of overhead infrared heating.', 'Salamander', 'A salamander is a specialized broiler that applies intense overhead infrared or radiant heat for browning, finishing, or broiling.

In professional kitchens and food service operations, it is primarily used for rapid top-browning, melting cheese (such as on French onion soup or lasagna), crisping meat fat, or lightly caramelizing sugar coatings without cooking the interior of the dish further.

• Rotisserie: A cooking appliance or attachment where meat (often whole chickens) is skewered on a spit and slowly rotated over or next to a heat source for even roasting.
• Bain-marie: A hot water bath system used in commercial food lines to hold cooked food at safe, warm serving temperatures. It does not cook, broil, or emit infrared heat.
• Microwave: An appliance that cooks food by using electromagnetic radiation waves to excite water molecules within the food, generating friction and volumetric heat rather than overhead radiant grilling.', '["Baine Marie","Rotisserie","Microwave","Salamander"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:20:54.340Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:20:54.340Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:20:54.340Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755158541819-194', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'It refers to a Vietnamese baguette sandwich.', 'Bahn mi', 'Bánh mì is the Vietnamese baguette sandwich.

Gỏi cuốn are fresh spring rolls, nước chấm is a dipping sauce, and phở is a noodle soup.', '["Bahn mi","Goi cuon","Nuoc cham","Pho"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:47:24.078Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:47:24.078Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:47:24.078Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755158566952-195', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Porto is a:', 'Wine', 'Vinho do Porto (commonly known simply as Porto or Port wine) is a Portuguese fortified wine produced exclusively in the Douro Valley in the northern provinces of Portugal.

It is called a fortified wine because a neutral grape spirit (known as aguardente, similar to brandy) is added during the fermentation process. This stops fermentation early, leaving residual sugar in the wine and boosting its alcohol content—usually to around 19% to 22% ABV.

It is typically a sweet, rich red wine served as a digestif or dessert wine, though it also comes in dry, semi-dry, and white varieties. It gets its name from the coastal city of Porto, where the wine is aged and shipped globally.

• Whiskey: A distilled alcoholic beverage made from fermented grain mash (such as barley, corn, rye, or wheat).
• Beer: An alcoholic beverage produced by brewing and fermenting starches, mainly derived from cereal grains—most commonly malted barley, though wheat, maize (corn), rice, and oats are also used.
• Brandy: A spirit produced by distilling wine or fermented fruit mash. While brandy (specifically a clear grape spirit) is added to Porto to stop its fermentation, Porto itself remains classified as a fortified wine rather than a distilled spirit like brandy.', '["Beer","Wine","Whiskey","Brandy"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:06:19.124Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:06:19.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:06:19.124Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755158589502-196', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'The following are liqueurs EXCEPT:', 'Grenadine', 'Kahlúa, crème de menthe, and Baileys are liqueurs. 

Grenadine is a sweet syrup used as a cocktail ingredient and is not itself a liqueur.', '["Kahlua","Grenadine","Crème de Menthe","Baileys"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T13:30:05.128Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:30:05.128Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:30:05.128Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755158613234-197', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'A flapjack refers to:', 'Pancake', '"Flapjack" is a traditional, centuries-old colloquial term used primarily in North America to refer to a pancake or griddle cake.

• Hash brown: Shredded or finely chopped potatoes that are pan-fried until golden brown.
• Shoe string potatoes: Extremely thin, finely cut strips of potato that are deep-fried until very crisp (similar to thin French fries).
• Popcorn: Puffed, heated corn kernels.', '["shoe string potatoes","popcorn","Pancake","hashbrown"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T13:37:40.391Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:37:40.391Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:37:40.391Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755158638198-198', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Taters refer to:', 'Potatoes', '"Taters" is a casual, colloquial slang term derived from the word "potatoes" (commonly used in phrases like tater tots or mashed taters).', '["Potatoes","Chips","Popcorn","Shrimp"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T11:48:34.376Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T11:48:34.376Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T11:48:34.376Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755158664465-199', NULL, 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Subs are:', 'all of the above', 'Subs are sandwiches also known as hoagies or heroes, depending on regional terminology. Therefore all the listed descriptions apply.', '["Hoagies","Heros","Sandwiches","all of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T13:41:02.922Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:41:02.922Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:34.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T13:41:03.104Z"'::jsonb)
