('anki-card-1758689821618-4', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'The building blocks of protein are amino acids. What reaction allows several amino acids to join together to form a protein? *', 'condensation reaction', 'condensation reaction', '["condensation reaction","evaporation reaction","hydrolysis","hydrogenation"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-01T10:57:36.231Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:57:36.231Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758689843299-5', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'The B vitamin that contains the mineral cobalt: *', 'B12', '', '["B6","B1","B2","B12"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-01T11:48:07.795Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:48:07.795Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:48:07.795Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758689861465-6', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Thiamin is essential in carbohydrate metabolism. A high carbohydrate diet will increase the need for vitamin B1. *', 'Both statements are correct.', 'Both statements are correct.', '["Only the first statement is correct.","Both statements are correct.","Only the second statement is correct.","Both statements are incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-01T10:29:15.472Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:29:15.472Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758689882280-7', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'It has the highest amount of linoleic acid: *', 'corn oil', '', '["corn oil","coconut oil","palm oil","olive oil"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T11:37:49.673Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:37:49.673Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:37:49.673Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758689902277-8', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'The science that investigates how the different nutrients influence the activities of genes: *', 'nutrigenomics', '', '["nutrigenetics","nutrigenomics","epigenetics","genomics"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-01T12:34:31.909Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T12:34:31.909Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T12:34:31.909Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758689917813-9', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'When using a Biuret’s test, which macromolecule/s will produce a positive reaction? *', 'protein', '', '["fat","all of the above","carbohydrate","protein"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T11:44:52.690Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:44:52.690Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:44:52.918Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758689977842-11', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'It is a precursor of serotonin: *', 'tryptophan', '', '["tryptophan","valine","methionine","phenylalanine"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T15:01:42.561Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T15:01:42.561Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T15:01:42.731Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690012224-13', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Glycemic effect of food refers to: *', 'both of the above', '', '["both of the above","how quickly blood glucose levels return to normal","how quickly glucose is absorbed after eating","none of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T10:41:34.465Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:41:34.465Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:41:34.465Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690030624-14', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'A period of relaxation when the heart fills with blood. *', 'diastole', '', '["systole","period of filling","diastole","isovolumic relaxation"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T11:03:47.907Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:03:47.907Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:03:48.127Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690047575-15', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'The largest, least dense lipoprotein that carries the greatest number of triglycerides. *', 'chylomicron', '', '["VLDL","chylomicron","HDL","LDL"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T10:51:16.182Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:51:16.182Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:51:16.423Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690063705-16', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'The body stores energy for future use in: *', 'triglycerides', 'Adipose tissue plays a fundamental role in maintaining long-term energy balance by storing concentrated energy in the form of triglycerides (fats).

Triglycerides provide a highly concentrated fuel source yielding 9 kcal/g, making them the most efficient and virtually unlimited way for the body to store excess calories for future energy needs.

• Proteins: While amino acids from proteins can be broken down for energy during late prolonged starvation, the primary physiological role of proteins is structural and functional (building tissues and machinery); they are not stored for the dedicated purpose of serving as an energy reserve.
• Acetyl CoA & Ketone bodies: These are intermediate metabolic molecules and transient byproducts of fuel breakdown. They are utilized immediately by tissues or converted further to produce ATP, but they cannot be stored by the body for future use.', '["acetyl CoA","proteins","triglycerides","ketone bodies"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2028-04-21T13:48:42.236Z","interval":529,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":9}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T13:48:42.236Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T13:48:42.236Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690082520-17', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'It is a part of CoA:', 'pantothenic acid', '', '["folate","biotin","thiamin","pantothenic acid"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-01T12:31:25.913Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T12:31:25.913Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T12:31:26.165Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690102387-18', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'The psychological desire to eat that accompanies the sight, smell, or thought of food is known as: *', 'appetite', 'appetite<span style="color: rgb(32, 33, 36);"> </span>', '["palatability","hunger","satiety","appetite"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T10:34:19.171Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:34:19.171Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690123237-19', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Fat-soluble vitamins involved in bone metabolism and development except: *', 'vitamin E', 'vitamin E<span style="color: rgb(32, 33, 36);"> </span>', '["vitamin A","vitamin K","vitamin D","vitamin E"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-01T11:03:21.218Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:03:21.218Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690142570-20', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'The normal blood glucose level for optimal body functioning: *', '80 – 120 mg/dL', '', '["70 – 150 mg/dL","90 – 110 mg/dL","80 – 120 mg/dL","60 – 90 mg/dL"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T10:19:25.825Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:19:25.825Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:19:25.825Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690158349-21', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'The vitamin most directly involved in protecting biomolecules from damage caused by oxidation is: *', 'E', 'Vitamin E (tocopherol) is recognized as the body''s primary fat-soluble antioxidant. Its most direct, essential physiological role is to protect lipids and other vulnerable biomolecules inside cell membranes from oxidative damage.

Free radicals break down cell structures by attacking polyunsaturated fatty acids in a destructive chain reaction called lipid peroxidation. Vitamin E sits directly within the lipid bilayer of cell membranes, sacrificing itself to neutralize these free radicals, which preserves the structural integrity of every cell in the body.

• C: While Vitamin C (ascorbic acid) is a powerful water-soluble antioxidant that works closely with Vitamin E (even recycling oxidized Vitamin E back to its active form), it also acts as a necessary co-factor for many non-antioxidant enzymatic reactions, such as collagen synthesis.
• A: While carotenoids (precursors to Vitamin A) have antioxidant properties, preformed Vitamin A (retinol) functions primarily in vision, cell differentiation, and immune health rather than acting as a general biomolecule antioxidant.
• B3: Vitamin B3 (niacin) forms the coenzymes NAD and NADP, which are essential for cellular respiration and energy transfer reactions rather than scavenging free radicals to stop oxidation.', '["A","E","B3","C"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 3, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-04T08:09:38.358Z","interval":6,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:09:38.358Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:09:38.682Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690174868-22', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'For the body to absorb pyridoxine, it must first be: *', 'dephosphorylated', 'dephosphorylated', '["dephosphorylated","deaminated","decarboxylated","phosphorylated"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T10:27:36.082Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:27:36.082Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690196349-23', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Linoleic acid is the parent amino acid of: *', 'arachidonic acid', 'arachidonic acid', '["docosahexaenoic acid","arachidonic acid","docosapentaenoic acid","eicosapentaenoic acid"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T10:36:53.203Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:36:53.203Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690228047-24', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Examples of derived lipids except: *', 'gangliosides', 'Gangliosides are categorized as compound (or complex) lipids rather than derived lipids. Specifically, they are complex glycosphingolipids composed of a fatty acid, a sphingosine backbone, and a complex oligosaccharide chain containing one or more residues of sialic acid.

Derived lipids are substances produced via the chemical hydrolysis of simple or compound lipids. They include free fatty acids, structural alcohols, hydrocarbons, fat-soluble vitamins, and sterols.

• Vitamin D: A fat-soluble vitamin. Because it is a secosteroid derivative generated from lipid precursors, it is classified under the derived lipids family.
• Cholesterol: The principal animal sterol. It lacks ester bonds but exhibits lipid-like properties and is a primary hydrolytic product/derivative of complex steroid pathways, placing it firmly in the derived lipid category.
• Ergosterol: A plant and fungal sterol (the biological precursor to vitamin D2). Like cholesterol, it is a non-saponifiable steroid molecule classified structurally as a derived lipid.', '["vitamin D","ergosterol","gangliosides","cholesterol"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, 'Gangliosides are structurally classified as compound lipids—specifically, they are a subtype of glycolipids.', '{"dueDate":"2029-11-24T13:50:00.032Z","interval":1111,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":10}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T13:50:00.032Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T13:50:00.032Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690245279-25', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Vitamins that help in cell division: *', 'folate & B12', 'Both folate (vitamin B9) and vitamin B12 (cobalamin) are essential coenzymes required for the synthesis of nucleic acids (DNA and RNA).

Before a cell can divide, it must perfectly replicate its entire DNA strands. Folate is a crucial building block for this replication process. Vitamin B12 acts as the mandatory key that unlocks folate, converting it into its active form inside the body.

If either vitamin is missing, cell division stalls. This is most visibly seen in fast-dividing tissues like bone marrow, where a lack of cell division leads to megaloblastic anemia (large, immature, undivided red blood cells).', '["folate & biotin","thiamin & riboflavin","niacin & B12","folate & B12"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-29T11:22:06.218Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T11:22:06.218Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T11:22:06.394Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690260679-26', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'The largest of the organelles within the cell is: *', 'nucleus', '', '["Golgi apparatus","nucleus","endoplasmic reticulum","mitochondrion"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-01T11:51:00.627Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:51:00.627Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:51:00.627Z"'::jsonb),
