('anki-card-1758690312847-29', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Canola oil is a source of ____ while corn oil is a source of ____. *', 'omega-3 PUFA; omega-6 PUFA', 'omega-3 PUFA; omega-6 PUFA', '["monounsaturad fat; omega-6 PUFA","omega-6 PUFA; omega-3 PUFA","omega-3 PUFA; omega-6 PUFA","omega-3 PUFA; monounsaturated fatty acid"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T11:47:54.649Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:47:54.649Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690333059-30', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'The combination of processes by which a living organism receives and utilizes the materials needed to maintain its functions and for the growth and renewal of its components. *', 'nutrition', '', '["metabolism","absorption","nutrition","digestion"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T12:08:54.027Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T12:08:54.027Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T12:08:54.233Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690355310-31', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Metabolic pathways of cholesterol except: *', 'energy production', 'energy production', '["energy production","hormone formation","secretion into bile","excretion into feces"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T14:13:13.194Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T14:13:13.194Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690370075-32', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Chronic alcoholism adversely affects the utilization of these fat-soluble vitamins: *', 'vitamins A & D', 'Vitamin A degradation: Chronic alcohol consumption induces the cytochrome P450 enzyme system (specifically CYP2E1) in the liver, which heavily accelerates the breakdown and depletion of retinol (Vitamin A) stores. Additionally, alcohol directly competes with Vitamin A for the metabolic enzymes alcohol dehydrogenase (ADH) and aldehyde dehydrogenase (ALDH).

Vitamin D malabsorption & impaired activation: Alcohol interferes with the liver''s ability to hydrolyze cholecalciferol into its active form. It also disrupts bile secretion and impairs the mucosal lining of the small intestine, leading to significant fat malabsorption that prevents fat-soluble vitamins like Vitamin D from being absorbed properly.

While chronic alcoholism can impact all fat-soluble vitamins (A, D, E, and K), vitamins A & D are the most clinically prominent and severely affected in terms of metabolic utilization, hepatic storage depletion, and target organ complications (e.g., night blindness and alcoholic bone disease/osteopenia).', '["vitamins A & E","vitamins D & E","vitamins D & K","vitamins A & D"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, 'The liver is the primary storage organ for Vitamin A and the critical site where Vitamin D undergoes its initial hydroxylation step (converting into 25-hydroxyvitamin D). Chronic alcohol consumption overburdens and damages liver cells, which severely disrupts the body''s ability to chemically activate, store, and utilize these two specific vitamins.', '{"dueDate":"2028-04-21T13:49:08.573Z","interval":529,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":9}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T13:49:08.573Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T13:49:08.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690386257-33', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Most of the energy required by the body is supplied by: *', 'glucose & fatty acid', 'glucose & fatty acid', '["glycerol & amino acid","proteins & fats","vitamins & minerals","glucose & fatty acid"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T11:04:41.169Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:04:41.169Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
