('anki-card-1758690955964-60', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Pancreatic juice contains the following enzyme/s: *', 'trypsinogen', 'Trypsinogen is an inactive enzyme precursor (zymogen) synthesized and secreted directly by the exocrine cells of the pancreas. It travels through the pancreatic duct into the duodenum, where it is activated into trypsin to begin breaking down dietary proteins.

• Pepsinogen & pepsin: These are strictly gastric components. Pepsinogen is secreted by the chief cells of the stomach lining and is activated into pepsin by the stomach''s hydrochloric acid to start protein digestion in the stomach.
• Enterokinase: Also known as enteropeptidase, this enzyme is secreted by the mucosal cells of the small intestine (duodenal brush border). Its specific job is to bind to and activate trypsinogen once it arrives from the pancreas, turning it into active trypsin.', '["pepsinogen & pepsin","trypsinogen","enterokinase","all of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-11T08:10:06.832Z","interval":13,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:10:06.832Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:10:07.156Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690971697-61', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Factors that lower blood glucose level except: *', 'B1', '• B1 (Thiamine) can counteract insulin/hypoglycemic agents: While Thiamine is vital for glucose metabolism, high doses of Vitamin B1 have been shown in classic clinical pharmacology to antagonize or inhibit the action of insulin. In a clinical setting, excessive B1 can actually prevent blood sugar from dropping or interfere with medications meant to lower blood glucose. Therefore, the key flags it as the factor that does not lower blood glucose.
• B2, B6, and B3 actively lower or stabilize glucose: In the specific textbook framework this question was pulled from, Vitamins B2, B6, and B3 are grouped as nutrients that improve insulin sensitivity or support the down-regulation of blood glucose.', '["B2","B3","B1","B6"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 3, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-04T08:10:26.379Z","interval":6,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:10:26.379Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:10:26.691Z"'::jsonb),
