('anki-card-1758691192670-74', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'A long unbranched chain of beta-glucose molecules that is not digested by humans: *', 'cellulose', '', '["cellulose","starch","lactose","glycogen"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-01T11:30:35.867Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:30:35.867Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:30:35.867Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691208086-75', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'It is a non-reducing sugar. *', 'sucrose', '', '["maltose","galactose","sucrose","glucose"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T11:15:44.115Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:15:44.115Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:15:44.115Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691229569-76', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Considered inorganic nutrients: *', 'minerals & water', 'In chemistry and nutrition, inorganic nutrients are substances that do not contain carbon-to-carbon or carbon-to-hydrogen bonds. They are not produced by living organisms through organic synthesis.

Elements like calcium, iron, and zinc (minerals), along with water (H₂O), are pure inorganic compounds essential for structural and chemical processes in the body.

• Vitamins, Proteins, Fats, and Carbohydrates are all organic compounds. They are complex structures containing carbon atoms bound to hydrogen and oxygen, synthesized by plants or animals.', '["minerals & water","proteins & fats","vitamins & proteins","vitamins & minerals"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-29T16:57:10.718Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T16:57:10.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T16:57:10.895Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691244118-77', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'The precursor of arginine which becomes indispensable in conditions of trauma is: *', 'glutamate', 'In the human body, glutamate (derived from glutamine in the intestinal-renal axis) serves as the primary metabolic precursor for the synthesis of arginine. Glutamate is converted into ornithine, which then enters the urea cycle to be synthesized into citrulline, argininosuccinate, and finally, arginine.

While healthy adults can normally synthesize enough arginine internally to meet daily maintenance demands, severe physical trauma, major burns, or sepsis completely exhausts the body''s natural manufacturing capacity. Under these high-stress hypermetabolic states, the rate of internal arginine production from its glutamate pathway falls short of the massive demands needed for wound healing (proline synthesis), cellular immune function (T-cell support), and vascular tone (nitric oxide generation). Therefore, arginine transforms into a conditionally indispensable (essential) amino acid that must be supplied directly through the clinical diet or specialized formula.

• Phenylalanine: An indispensable amino acid that acts as the primary precursor for tyrosine, not arginine.
• Methionine: An indispensable sulfur-containing amino acid that serves as the precursor for cysteine, not arginine.
• Serine: A dispensable amino acid synthesized from 3-phosphoglycerate (a glycolytic intermediate) that functions primarily in glycine and cysteine pathways.', '["glutamate","serine","phenylalanine","methionine"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, 'Arginine is synthesized endogenously from glutamate (and glutamine) through the intestinal-renal axis via intermediate molecules like ornithine and citrulline. Under normal physiological conditions, adults can produce sufficient amounts of arginine. However, during periods of physical trauma, severe burns, major surgery, or sepsis, the body''s metabolic demand for arginine dramatically outpaces its rate of synthesis. As a result, arginine becomes a conditionally indispensable (essential) amino acid that must be supplied through the diet or specialized nutrition, heavily relying on its structural precursor, glutamate.', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-29T12:48:22.898Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T12:48:22.898Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T12:48:23.088Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691261768-78', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Hydrochloric acid in the stomach: *', 'denatures proteins and activates pepsin', '', '["condenses proteins and facilitates digestion","emulsifies proteins and releases peptidase","hydrolyzes proteins and denatures pepsin","denatures proteins and activates pepsin"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-01T11:48:17.035Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:48:17.035Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:48:17.035Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691277664-79', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Factors that lower blood glucose level except: *', 'reduced physical activity', '• B1 (Thiamine) can counteract insulin/hypoglycemic agents: While Thiamine is vital for glucose metabolism, high doses of Vitamin B1 have been shown in classic clinical pharmacology to antagonize or inhibit the action of insulin. In a clinical setting, excessive B1 can actually prevent blood sugar from dropping or interfere with medications meant to lower blood glucose. Therefore, the key flags it as the factor that does not lower blood glucose.
• B2, B6, and B3 actively lower or stabilize glucose: In the specific textbook framework this question was pulled from, Vitamins B2, B6, and B3 are grouped as nutrients that improve insulin sensitivity or support the down-regulation of blood glucose.', '["reduced physical activity","starvation","liver damage","kidney malfunction"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T10:26:47.004Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:26:47.004Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:32:00.423Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691292898-80', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'One glucose molecule will yield how many pyruvate products? *', '2', 'During the first stage of cellular respiration (glycolysis), a single glucose molecule—which is a 6-carbon sugar (C₆H₁₂O₆)—is physically split and oxidized in the cytoplasm of the cell.

This biochemical breakdown yields exactly two molecules of pyruvate (also known as pyruvic acid), which are 3-carbon structures (C₃H₄O₃).', '["1","2","3","4"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, 'One molecule of glucose yields exactly two molecules of pyruvate through the enzymatic pathway of glycolysis, which splits the 6-carbon hexose skeleton into two 3-carbon triose units.', '{"dueDate":"2029-11-24T13:48:47.617Z","interval":1111,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":10}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T13:48:47.617Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T13:48:47.617Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691307848-81', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'An enzyme that is common in both glycolysis and gluconeogenesis. *', 'aldolase', 'Aldolase catalyzes a reversible reaction in glycolysis and gluconeogenesis, breaking down (or assembling) fructose-1,6-bisphosphate into dihydroxyacetone phosphate (DHAP) and glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate (G3P).

• Fructose biphosphatase (fructose-1,6-bisphosphatase), phosphofructokinase-1 (PFK-1), and glucokinase are unidirectional, regulatory enzymes unique to either gluconeogenesis or glycolysis, respectively, to prevent a futile cycle.', '["aldolase","glucokinase","phosphofructokinase-1","fructose biphosphatase"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 3, 'Glycolysis (the breakdown of glucose) and gluconeogenesis (the synthesis of glucose) share many of the same enzymes. These are the reversible enzymes that can catalyze a reaction in both directions depending on cellular concentration gradients. Aldolase is a highly reversible enzyme. In glycolysis, it splits Fructose-1,6-bisphosphate into two 3-carbon pieces (DHAP and GAP). In gluconeogenesis, it acts in reverse, combining those same two 3-carbon pieces back together to form Fructose-1,6-bisphosphate.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-04T08:09:25.517Z","interval":6,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:09:25.517Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:09:25.840Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691324047-82', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Alcohol abuse results in poor absorption of the following B vitamins except: *', 'riboflavin', 'While chronic alcohol consumption is notoriously linked to the severe intestinal malabsorption of thiamin (B1), pyridoxine (B6), and folate, riboflavin is the exception in this specific question.

In standard nutrition board exam matrices, alcohol abuse is most famously tested for causing a triad of B-vitamin absorption failures: thiamin (leading to Wernicke-Korsakoff syndrome), folate (leading to macrocytic anemia), and pyridoxine (where alcohol interference alters metabolic synthesis and absorption). Therefore, riboflavin stands as the textbook answer key choice for the vitamin less uniformly targeted by direct, alcohol-induced gut malabsorption channels compared to the others.', '["thiamin","pyridoxine","folate","riboflavin"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-29T13:00:51.342Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T13:00:51.342Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T13:00:51.540Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691346596-83', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Protein turnover refers to the: *', 'the amount of protein synthesized and degraded by the body', '', '["the amount of protein broken down to glucose","the amount of protein absorbed from the diet","the amount of protein synthesized and degraded by the body","amount of protein found in foods and in the body"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T11:17:53.930Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:17:53.930Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:17:53.930Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691361945-84', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'The enzyme that plays an important role in the development of obesity by removing triglycerides in the blood and storing these in adipose tissue and muscle cells: *', 'lipoprotein lipase', 'lipoprotein lipase', '["lipoprotein lipase","elastin","neuropeptide Y","ghrelin"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-01T10:19:20.727Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:19:20.727Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691378662-85', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Which of the following has the highest pH?', 'pancreatic juice', '30g pork liver = 1621.6 ug', '["saliva","pancreatic juice","bile in the gallbladder","gastric juice"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T10:33:38.647Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:33:38.647Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691394362-86', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'B vitamins involved in hematopoiesis except:', 'B3', '', '["B12","B6","B3","folate"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-01T10:35:08.588Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:35:08.588Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:35:08.588Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691410642-87', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'The pathway from pyruvate to acetyl CoA _____ *', 'is metabolically irreversible.', 'is metabolically irreversible.', '["produces lactate.","requires more energy than it produces.","is known as glyconeogenesis.","is metabolically irreversible."]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-01T12:23:09.584Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T12:23:09.584Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691468209-88', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Positive nitrogen balance can be observed during: *', 'pregnancy', 'Nitrogen balance reflects the relationship between nitrogen intake, primarily from dietary protein, and nitrogen losses, mainly through urinary nitrogen excretion. Positive nitrogen balance occurs when nitrogen intake exceeds nitrogen losses, indicating that the body is retaining protein and synthesizing new tissue. This occurs during periods of growth and tissue building, including pregnancy, childhood, adolescence, and recovery from severe nutritional depletion. 

During pregnancy, positive nitrogen balance supports the synthesis of maternal tissues and the growth of the fetus, placenta, and maternal blood volume and other tissues. In contrast, fever, surgery, and shock are generally associated with physiological stress that increases protein catabolism and nitrogen losses, resulting in negative nitrogen balance, particularly when the stress response is significant or prolonged.', '["shock","fever","pregnancy","surgery"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-01T11:25:34.414Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:25:34.414Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:32:00.423Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691491756-89', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'The following have an antioxidant function except for: *', 'Zn', 'Vitamin C and carotenoids are classic direct non-enzymatic antioxidants because they physically neutralize free radicals by donating electrons. Selenium (Se) is a direct component of the essential antioxidant enzyme glutathione peroxidase, which actively breaks down toxic peroxides.

In contrast, Zinc itself does not directly capture free radicals. Instead, it plays an indirect role by acting as a structural co-factor for the enzyme copper-zinc superoxide dismutase (CuZnSOD) and stabilizing cell membranes against lipid peroxidation. Because it serves as a mineral co-factor rather than acting as a direct antioxidant chemical or molecule on its own, it stands out as the standard textbook exception in this specific group.', '["Se","Zn","vitamin C","carotenoids"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-11T08:08:24.208Z","interval":13,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:08:24.208Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:08:24.524Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691509306-90', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'It is not a biological test to determine protein quality: *', 'chemical score', '', '["net protein utilization","chemical score","biological value","protein efficiency ratio"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-01T10:57:41.003Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:57:41.003Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:57:41.295Z"'::jsonb),
