('anki-card-1758691595086-95', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Vitamin C is the most unstable of all water-soluble vitamins. On the other hand, vitamin B3 is the most stable. *', 'Both statements are correct.', 'Both statements are correct.<span style="color: rgb(32, 33, 36);"> </span>', '["Both statements are incorrect","Only the first statement is correct.","Only the second statement is correct.","Both statements are correct."]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T10:31:11.204Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:31:11.204Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691610083-96', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'The formation of a disaccharide from 2 monosaccharides is known as: *', 'glycogenesis', 'glycogenesis<span style="color: rgb(32, 33, 36);"> </span>', '["dehydration","hydrolysis","condensation","glycogenesis"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T14:35:49.322Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T14:35:49.322Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691625750-97', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Blood leaving the gastrointestinal tract goes first to the: *', 'liver', '', '["kidneys","liver","pancreas","heart"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T11:50:08.679Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:50:08.679Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:50:08.679Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691644649-98', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'It is a branched-chain amino acid: *', 'isoleucin', 'Isoleucine is one of the three classic branched-chain amino acids (BCAAs), alongside leucine and valine. These amino acids are chemically distinguished by an aliphatic, non-linear side chain featuring a central branch point.

Unlike most other amino acids that are metabolized primarily in the liver, BCAAs are unique because they bypass initial liver breakdown and are taken up directly by skeletal muscle tissue. There, they serve as a critical substrate for energy production and play a major role in stimulating muscle protein synthesis during periods of recovery or metabolic stress.

• Alanine: A dispensable (non-essential) amino acid with a simple, straight-chain methyl side group. It is heavily involved in the glucose-alanine cycle to transport nitrogen from muscles to the liver.
• Lysine: An indispensable (essential) amino acid with a straight, basic hydrocarbon side chain ending in an amino group, not a branched-chain configuration.
• Glutamine: A conditionally indispensable amino acid with a straight-chain amide side group. It is the most abundant free amino acid in the human body, acting as a premier fuel source for rapidly dividing immune cells and enterocytes in the gut.', '["glutamine","alanine","lysine","isoleucin"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, 'There are only three BCAAs among the proteinogenic amino acids: leucine, isoleucine, and valine. All three are essential amino acids, meaning the body cannot synthesize them, and they must be obtained through the diet.', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-29T14:18:30.133Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T14:18:30.133Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T14:18:30.315Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691662116-99', NULL, 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'The increase in basal metabolism per degree Fahrenheit rise in body temperature. *', '7%', '', '["7%","10%","8%","5%"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T10:33:27.928Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:33:27.928Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:33:27.928Z"'::jsonb),
