('anki-card-1754747162368-48', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608654256-1786809564961', 'Which is TRUE about cell growth?', 'Hyperplasia is characterized by the increase in number of cells through cell division', 'Hyperplasia: This term is defined precisely as an increase in the absolute number of cells within a tissue or organ, driven directly by cellular proliferation and cell division (mitosis).

• Why Option B is incorrect: The definition given in option B is inverted. Hypertrophy is characterized by an increase in the physical size or volume of existing cells due to the accumulation of proteins and cellular components, not an increase in their number.', '["Hyperplasia is characterized by the increase in number of cells through cell division","Hypertrophy is characterized by the increase in number of cells through cell division","A and B are both TRUE","A and B are both FALSE"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T13:49:04.570Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T13:49:04.570Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.332Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T13:49:04.570Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754747302810-49', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608654256-1786809564961', 'The effortless expulsion of gastric contents caused by GI reflux in babies', 'Regurgitation', 'This question is lifted verbatim from local Philippine Community and Public Health Nutrition (CPHN) board exam references. In clinical and nutritional frameworks, specific terminology is used to define infant gastric movement:

Regurgitation: This is defined exactly as the effortless, non-forceful expulsion of gastric contents back up into the mouth due to gastrointestinal reflux. It happens casually (often called "posseting") because an infant''s lower esophageal sphincter (LES) is still physically immature and relaxed.

While "spitting up" is the casual, everyday phrase parents use for the action, Regurgitation is the formal, technical medical term required by local board exams and textbooks to fill this definition.

• Diarrhea: The frequent, abnormal passage of loose, watery, and unformed stools from the lower GI tract.
• Colic: Predictable, prolonged, and intense crying or fussiness in an otherwise healthy infant, often linked to severe gas or abdominal discomfort.
• Spitting-up-food: The colloquial description of the symptom, but it is not the prioritized medical term in professional test banks.', '["Colic","Spitting-up-food","Diarrhea","Regurgitation"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T14:26:18.658Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:26:18.658Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.332Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:26:18.658Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754880713876-0', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608681588-1790433140276-5f3w7', 'Which is true about physiological maturity?', 'Achieved when full genetic body size is attained', 'Achieved when full genetic body size is attained', '["Achieved when full genetic body size is attained","Achieved with continuous organ and tissue growth","All of the above","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-08-12T20:00:00.000Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.763Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754880779639-1', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608681588-1790433140276-5f3w7', 'Which is true about menopause among females:', 'A and B are both TRUE', 'Menopause is the permanent cessation of menstrual periods resulting from the natural biological aging of the female reproductive system:

• Statement A is TRUE: As a woman transitions into menopause, her ovaries dramatically reduce their secretion of the key female sex hormones, leading to severely decreased levels of estrogen and progesterone. This sharp hormonal decline is responsible for classic menopausal symptoms like hot flashes and night sweats.
• Statement B is TRUE: The root biological cause of this hormone drop is the natural depletion of the ovarian reserve. A woman is born with a finite number of primordial follicles. Over her reproductive lifespan, as more follicles undergo ovulation or atresia (shrinkage/cell death), the ovaries end up with a significantly lower number of viable ovarian follicles. Consequently, fewer follicles develop completely to ovulate and transform into a corpus luteum (the temporary structure responsible for secreting progesterone).', '["A result of decreased levels of estrogen and progesterone","A result of less number of ovarian follicles and corpora lutea","A and B are both TRUE","A and B are both FALSE"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-08-12T20:00:00.000Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.763Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:32:00.423Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754880843733-2', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608681588-1790433140276-5f3w7', 'Josh is obese. Upon plotting his weight on the growth chart, what is the direction of the curve?', 'Outside the upper reference line', 'Outside the upper reference line', '["Outside the lower reference line","Outside the upper reference line","Flat curve","Falling curve"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-08-12T20:00:00.000Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.763Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754880939247-3', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608681588-1790433140276-5f3w7', 'Which is true about brain growth and development in preschool age?', 'Brain size has reached 75% of its adult weight by age 2', 'At birth, the brain is 25% of its future adult size, and head circumference is about 14 inches (about 35 centimeters).

• By 1 year of age, the brain is 75% of its adult size. By 3 years of age, the brain is 80% of its adult size.
• By 7 years of age, the brain is 90% of its adult size (Gaber, 2019).', '["Brain size has reached 55% of its adult weight by age 2","Brain size has reached 75% of its adult weight by age 2","Brain size has reached 80% of its adult weight by age 2","Brain size has reached 90% of its adult weight by age 2"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-08-12T20:00:00.000Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.763Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:32:00.423Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754880994112-4', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608681588-1790433140276-5f3w7', 'Majority of the body protein is located in the ___.', 'Muscle', '', '["Muscle","Skeleton","Skin","Connective tissue"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-08-12T20:00:00.000Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.763Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754881035393-5', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608681588-1790433140276-5f3w7', 'This type of malnutrition is also known as dietary malnutrition.', 'Primary', '', '["Acute","Chronic","Primary","Secondary"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-08-12T20:00:00.000Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.763Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754881093275-6', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608681588-1790433140276-5f3w7', 'Marc''s height falls under the <-2SD. Thus, his height-for-age is classified as:', 'Stunted', '', '["Normal","Stunted","Tall","Wasted"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-08-12T20:00:00.000Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.763Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754881153055-7', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608681588-1790433140276-5f3w7', 'The process of physical development from child to adult and refers to the maturation of the body.', 'Puberty', 'Puberty is the biological process during which the body physically matures into an adult capable of reproduction, involving hormonal, physical, and sexual maturation. 

• Adolescence is the broader psychosocial and developmental life stage encompassing puberty but also including cognitive, emotional, and social development beyond just physical maturation. 
• Pubescence is a less standard/precise term sometimes used interchangeably but not the preferred technical term. 
• Maturity is too general and does not specifically denote the physical maturation process described.', '["Adolescence","Pubescence","Puberty","Maturity"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-08-12T20:00:00.000Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.763Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:32:00.423Z"'::jsonb),
