('anki-card-1758683965204-3', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'Another name for primary deficiency disease is: *', 'dietary deficiency disease', 'A primary deficiency is caused directly by an inadequate dietary intake of a nutrient from food sources.

• Iatrogenic malnutrition: Malnutrition inadvertently caused by medical treatment or hospitalization.
• Conditioned deficiency disease: Another term for secondary deficiency (caused by malabsorption or disease states rather than direct lack of food).', '["dietary deficiency disease","iatrogenic malnutrition","conditioned deficiency disease","none of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:42:58.914Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758683978654-4', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'The onset of nutritional diseases depends on: *', 'the level of nutrient reserves in the body', 'The time it takes for a nutritional deficiency disease to manifest clinically depends heavily on how large the body''s internal storage reserves of that specific nutrient are (e.g., Vitamin A or B12 liver stores take months or years to exhaust).

• Food likes/dislikes & amount of food intake: Influence intake, but the timeline of disease onset is governed by tissue reserves.', '["the level of nutrient reserves in the body","the individual’s food likes and dislikes","the amount of food intake","the body’s ability to fight diseases"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:43:09.617Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758683993786-5', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'The first stage in the development of a deficiency disease. *', 'nutritional inadequacy', 'The absolute earliest, initial stage in the development of any deficiency disease is dietary or systemic nutritional inadequacy, long before biochemical depletion or anatomical lesions appear.

• Tissue depletion / Functional changes / Anatomic lesions: Later sequential stages occurring progressively after initial inadequacy.', '["tissue depletion","nutritional inadequacy","functional changes","anatomic lesions"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:43:16.886Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684005803-6', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'Considered underlying causes of malnutrition: 1. inadequate food intake; 2. inadequate access to food in a household; 3. inadequate care given to children & women; 4. frequent diseases and illnesses *', '2 & 3', 'According to the UNICEF conceptual framework of malnutrition, these represent core underlying causes operating at the household level.

• Inadequate food intake & Frequent diseases/illnesses: Classified as immediate causes, not underlying causes.', '["1 & 4","2 & 3","1 & 2","1 & 3"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:43:24.564Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684027784-7', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'This hormone stimulates the thickness of the uterine wall during menstrual cycle. *', 'estrogen', 'Estrogen drives the proliferative phase of the uterine cycle, stimulating the thickening and vascularization of the endometrial uterine wall.

• Progesterone: Maintains the secretory endometrium post-ovulation.
• LH / FSH: Gonadotropic pituitary hormones regulating ovulation and follicular growth.', '["estrogen","progesterone","luteinizing hormone","follicle-stimulating hormone"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:44:40.413Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684100599-8', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'It is not a part of a prenatal nutrition assessment: *', 'evaluation of a 7-day food intake record', 'A prospective 7-day weighed food record is too burdensome and rarely utilized for routine prenatal screening, whereas short recalls, biomarker labs, and dietary/resource evaluations form standard prenatal assessment.', '["evaluation of biomarkers of nutritional status","evaluation of dietary intake","assessment of food preferences & resources","evaluation of a 7-day food intake record"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:44:46.682Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684115397-9', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'A placental hormone that supports fetal growth and development by increasing the availability of glucose and amino acids. *', 'human placental lactogen', 'Also known as human chorionic somatomammotropin, hPL alters maternal metabolic processes to ensure adequate glucose and amino acid availability for the developing fetus.

• hCG: Maintains the corpus luteum in early pregnancy.
• Progesterone: Relaxes smooth muscle and maintains uterine lining.', '["human chorionic gonadotropin","progesterone","human placental lactogen","human chorionic somatotropin"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:44:55.846Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684139530-10', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'Pregnancy is characterized by relaxation of gastrointestinal tract muscles that can lead to heartburn when the esophageal sphincter relaxes. This effect is due mainly to which hormone? *', 'progesterone', 'Elevated progesterone levels during pregnancy cause generalized smooth muscle relaxation throughout the gastrointestinal tract, leading to lower esophageal sphincter relaxation and heartburn (acid reflux).

• Estrogen / hCG / hCS: Play primary roles in endocrine regulation and placental growth rather than smooth muscle relaxation.', '["estrogen","progesterone","human chorionic gonadotropin","human chorionic somatotropin"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:45:03.030Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684177095-11', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'Except for ____, the nutrient needs of a pregnant woman can be met by consuming a well-balanced and adequate diet. *', 'iron', 'Due to massive maternal red blood cell expansion and fetal iron demands, dietary intake alone is universally insufficient to meet pregnancy iron needs, requiring routine medicinal iron-folate supplementation.

• Folate / Zinc / Calcium: While requirements increase, well-balanced diets can generally meet these needs more readily than iron without supplementation.', '["folate","iron","zinc","calcium"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:45:10.206Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684188311-12', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'Based on the PDRI, a pregnant woman would need an additional ____ kcal per day while a lactating woman would need an additional ____ kcal daily. *', '300; 500', 'According to Philippine Dietary Reference Intakes (PDRI), pregnant women require an additional 300 kcal/day, while lactating women require an additional 500 kcal/day to sustain milk production.', '["200; 400","300; 400","300; 500","300; 600"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:45:15.717Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684203476-13', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'The only fat-soluble vitamin that can lead to an increased risk to fetal abnormalities when consumed in excessive amounts. *', 'vitamin A', 'High doses of preformed Vitamin A (retinol) consumed during pregnancy are teratogenic and carry a high risk of causing severe fetal malformations and birth defects.', '["vitamin A","vitamin D","vitamin E","vitamin K"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:45:21.512Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684217108-14', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'Consumption of supplements that provide 60 mg or more of this mineral is not advised among pregnant women due to its ability to act as pro-oxidant resulting in the inflammation and damage of mitochondrial cells. *', 'iron', 'High supplemental doses of iron (60 mg/day or more) can act as a free-radical pro-oxidant in the gastrointestinal tract, causing cellular inflammation, oxidative stress, and mucosal damage.

• Iodine / Zinc / Calcium: Essential minerals without the same pro-oxidant cellular damage profile at standard supplementation levels.', '["iodine","zinc","calcium","iron"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:45:30.825Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684232842-15', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'Which of the following is a correct statement on the role of fats for infants? *', 'Infants require a higher percentage of their daily calories from fat compared to children and adults', 'Human breast milk derives roughly 50% of its calories from fat to support rapid infant brain development and high energy needs.', '["Fat restriction among infants born at term can be started when they reach 1year old.","Breast milk has a lower fat content compared to standard infant formulas.","Infants require a higher percentage of their daily calories from fat compared to children and adults","Healthy infants in their first year do not need long-chain fatty acids."]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:45:36.984Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684245208-16', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'Hormone that stimulates milk production. *', 'prolactin', 'Prolactin is the primary anterior pituitary hormone responsible for stimulating milk production (lactogenesis).

• Estrogen / Progesterone: Inhibit milk secretion during pregnancy.
• hPL: Placental hormone supporting fetal metabolism.', '["estrogen","progesterone","human placental lactogen","prolactin"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:45:43.915Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684257441-17', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'This is the best way to increase milk production: *', 'Remove milk from the breast and feed frequently.', 'Lactation is governed by supply and demand; frequent nursing and complete milk removal stimulate prolactin and maintain high milk volume.

• Reduce fat in diet / Use pump at start: Ineffective or counterproductive for optimizing breast milk supply.', '["Reduce fat in a nursing woman’s diet.","Remove milk from the breast and feed frequently.","Feed the infant at both breasts in a single feeding.","Use a pump to express milk at the beginning of a feeding."]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:45:52.545Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684270190-18', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'The two important predictors of an infant’s survival and future health: 1. birth weight; 2. length of gestation; 3. head circumference; d. length *', '1 & 2', 'These two parameters are universally recognized as the single most critical epidemiological predictors of neonatal survival, infant growth, and future health.

• Head circumference / Length: Important anthropometric indicators, but birth weight and gestational age dictate immediate neonatal viability.', '["1 & 2","2 & 3","1 & 4","2 & 3"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:46:00.808Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684285405-19', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'The screening tool that is recommended in assessing overweight, obesity, and underweight in young children is: *', 'body mass index-for-age percentile', 'According to WHO and pediatric growth standards, BMI-for-age percentile charts are the recommended screening tool to assess overweight, obesity, and underweight in children and adolescents.

• Actual weight-for-age: Measures underweight status, but fails to distinguish stunting from wasting or evaluate obesity.', '["actual weight in kg","weight-for-age percentile","body mass index-for-age percentile","actual body mass index"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:46:06.931Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684298605-20', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'It is considered a risk factor for low vitamin D status: *', 'dark skin pigmentation', 'Melanin in dark skin acts as a natural sunscreen, reducing the cutaneous synthesis of Vitamin D from ultraviolet-B sunlight and increasing risk of deficiency.

• Light skin pigmentation / High calcium intake: Do not act as primary risk factors for inadequate Vitamin D synthesis.', '["light skin pigmentation","dark skin pigmentation","low calcium intake","high calcium intake"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:46:13.314Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684310538-21', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'A vegan adolescent will most likely have these nutrients missing from their diets: *', 'vitamins B6, D, B12, iron, and calcium', 'Strict vegan diets eliminate all animal products, putting individuals—especially growing adolescents—at high risk for deficiencies in Vitamin B12 (found exclusively in animal sources), Vitamin D, iron, calcium, and vitamin B6.

• Vitamins A, E, folate: Abundant in plant-based diets.', '["vitamins B6, B2, E, zinc, and choline","vitamins A, D, E, folate, and iron","vitamins A, D, E, iron, and zinc","vitamins B6, D, B12, iron, and calcium"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:46:19.894Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684323189-22', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'According to the WHO, successful breastfeeding is ensured when: *', 'mothers start breastfeeding within 30 minutes after a normal delivery.', 'WHO and Unicef guidelines emphasize early initiation of breastfeeding within the first 30 minutes to 1 hour postpartum to ensure colostrum delivery and lactation success.', '["mothers start breastfeeding within 20 minutes after a normal delivery.","mothers start breastfeeding within 30 minutes after a normal delivery.","mothers start breastfeeding within 1 hour after a normal delivery.","mothers start breastfeeding within 2 hours after a normal delivery."]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:46:27.432Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684332853-23', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'The period characterized by an increase in the organism’s size through cell multiplication and cell size enlargement. *', 'growth', 'Growth is defined biologically as an increase in physical size resulting from cell multiplication (hyperplasia) and cell enlargement (hypertrophy).

• Development: Refers to functional maturation and skill acquisition.
• Organogenesis: Formation of organ systems during embryogenesis.', '["growth","development","organogenesis","differentiation"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:46:33.299Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684347985-24', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'A pregnant woman undergoes a sequence of physiological changes. The first stage involves: *', 'expansion of plasma volume', 'The earliest and most dramatic physiological sequence of maternal adaptation during pregnancy is the rapid expansion of plasma volume starting in the first trimester.

• Fetal weight gain: Occurs primarily in the late second and third trimesters.', '["accumulation of nutrient stores","expansion of plasma volume","an increase in placental weight","an increase in fetal weight"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:46:40.520Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684361403-25', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'For the elderly, nutrient requirements are either maintained at normal levels or increased except for: *', 'kilocalories', 'Due to progressive decreases in basal metabolic rate (BMR) and reductions in physical activity, total daily caloric energy requirements decline in the elderly, whereas protein, calcium, and micronutrient requirements remain elevated or maintained.', '["protein","iron","calcium","kilocalories"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:46:46.914Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684372552-26', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'Between the ages of 2 and 4 years: *', 'a child’s appetite tends to decrease.', 'Following the rapid infancy growth velocity, growth rate slows down between ages 2 and 4 years, resulting in a natural, physiological decrease in appetite and variable food intake ("picky eating" phase).', '["a child’s appetite increases enormously.","a child’s eating habits tend to stabilize.","a child’s appetite tends to decrease.","a child will generally try any new food that is offered."]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:46:52.253Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684384568-27', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'Which of the following groups of children are the most difficult to rehabilitate from severe protein energy malnutrition? *', 'preschoolers 1-3 years', 'Toddlers aged 1 to 3 years are the most difficult to rehabilitate from severe protein-energy malnutrition due to high nutrient demands for brain/motor development, frequent infectious illnesses, difficult weaning behaviors, and high rates of developmental stunting.', '["infants","preschoolers 1-3 years","preschoolers 4-6 years","school children"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:47:00.077Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684394452-28', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'Anabolic processes associated with pregnancy except: *', 'mobilization of nutrient stores', 'Pregnancy is predominantly an anabolic state characterized by building up tissue and storing nutrients (fat and glycogen) in early/mid-gestation to prepare for lactation; mobilization of maternal stores occurs primarily late or during lactation, making mobilization an exception to early anabolic processes.', '["increased blood volume due to developing fetus","mobilization of nutrient stores","building up glycogen stores","performing ability decreases"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:47:05.481Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684409650-29', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'The major fetal fuel is ____ while the major maternal fuel is ____. *', 'glucose; fat', 'The developing fetus relies almost exclusively on maternal glucose as its primary fuel source, while maternal metabolism shifts toward fatty acid oxidation (lipolysis) as the primary maternal fuel source to spare glucose for the fetus.', '["glucose; fat","fat; glucose","glucose; protein","protein; glucose"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:47:14.199Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684421132-30', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'Galactopoiesis means: *', 'milk production', 'Galactopoiesis refers specifically to the maintenance and sustained physiological production of milk once lactation has been established.

• Milk ejection: Governed by oxytocin (let-down reflex).', '["red blood cell formation","formation of galactose","milk production","milk ejection"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:47:20.513Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684431617-31', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'Epidemiology can be defined as the study of: *', 'the distribution and determinants of frequency of disease in humans', 'This is the standard, comprehensive epidemiological definition encompassing who gets the disease, where it occurs, why it happens, and how it spreads.', '["the etiology of disease in humans","the frequency of causes of death in humans","the determinants of frequency of disease in humans","the distribution and determinants of frequency of disease in humans"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:47:26.192Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684444115-32', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'Loss of teeth, anorexia, and inability to self-feed are some problems that: *', 'interfere with ingestion', 'Tooth loss, anorexia, and inability to self-feed prevent food from entering the mouth, directly interfering with the mechanical process of food ingestion.

• Nutrient absorption / Utilization: Occurs downstream in the gastrointestinal tract and metabolic pathways.', '["interfere with nutrient absorption","interfere with nutrient utilization","interfere with ingestion","increase nutrient requirement"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:47:46.138Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684458998-33', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'All of the following statements regarding screening for thyroid disease are true except: *', 'Neck palpation is an accurate method to detect thyroid disease.', 'Neck palpation has low sensitivity and specificity for early or minor thyroid pathologies, making it an inaccurate standalone screening method compared to sensitive TSH/thyroid hormone blood panels or ultrasound.', '["All neonates should be screened for congenital hypothyroidism.","Although women are at an increased risk for thyroid cancer, ultrasound screening examinations are recommended only for those women with symptoms.","Neck palpation is an accurate method to detect thyroid disease.","Serum levels of thyroid hormones characteristic of thyroid disease are often influenced by a variety of biological factors."]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:47:48.080Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684469064-34', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'Decreased levels of nutrients in body fluids may be assessed using the following nutrition assessment method/s: *', 'biochemical', 'Laboratory assays of blood, serum, or urine evaluate internal biochemical nutrient concentrations, detecting subclinical decreased levels of nutrients in body fluids before physical signs appear.

• Clinical: Relies on observable physical signs.', '["biochemical","clinical","both a & b","none of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:47:54.399Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684479496-35', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'The level of prevention being practiced when an individual engages in periodic follow-up and treatment to prevent relapses in certain diseases. *', 'tertiary prevention', 'Tertiary prevention focuses on managing established chronic diseases, conducting periodic follow-ups, rehabilitation, and preventing relapses or complications.

• Primary prevention: Prevents initial disease onset.
• Secondary prevention: Early screening and detection.', '["primary prevention","secondary prevention","tertiary prevention","none of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:48:02.623Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684488846-36', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'Rural health units, barangay health stations, and health centers are considered: *', 'primary level facilities of health services', 'Rural Health Units (RHUs), Barangay Health Stations (BHS), and local health centers serve as the first point of contact in the primary healthcare delivery system.

• Secondary / Tertiary: District/provincial hospitals and specialized medical centers.', '["primary level facilities of health services","secondary level facilities of health services","tertiary level facilities of health services","none of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:48:10.726Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684499030-37', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'The first immunization given to babies at birth or soon after birth is: *', 'tuberculosis', 'The BCG vaccine is administered to newborns at birth or immediately thereafter as the first routine immunization to prevent tuberculosis.

• DPT / Measles: Given at later scheduled intervals (6 weeks onwards and 9 months, respectively).', '["diphtheria, whooping cough, and tetanus (DPT)","measles","tuberculosis","none of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:48:18.745Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684510662-38', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'All are cultural influences that enable one to understand the local etiology of malnutrition except: *', 'mothers/caregivers have not completed their elementary education', 'Maternal educational attainment is a socioeconomic determinant of health, whereas the other options represent direct cultural beliefs and food taboos regarding disease etiology.', '["type and amount of complementary foods given to the child","giving milk to infants only and not to toddlers and young children","mothers/caregivers have not completed their elementary education","not giving solid food to a child with fever"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:48:28.302Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684527128-39', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'The initial stage of iron deficiency can be detected by: *', 'low serum ferritin', 'Serum ferritin reflects stored body iron; the very first initial stage of iron deficiency is the depletion of iron stores, which is detected sensitively by low serum ferritin.

• Hemoglobin drop / Low transferrin saturation: Occur in later stages when iron-deficient erythropoiesis and frank anemia develop.', '["low transferrin saturation","low serum ferritin","a drop in hemoglobin production","high levels of erythrocyte protoporphyrin"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:48:34.923Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684536176-40', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'It is not a reliable indicator of iron deficiency since its concentrations are increased by infection and inflammation: *', 'serum ferritin', 'Serum ferritin is an acute-phase reactant protein that increases markedly during infections, systemic inflammation, or tissue injury, making it an unreliable indicator of iron status during acute illness.

• Hemoglobin / Transferrin / Protoporphyrin: Respond differently or are utilized alongside specific inflammatory corrections.', '["serum ferritin","transferrin","hemoglobin","erythrocyte protoporphyrin"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:48:41.073Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684557926-41', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'Very frequent symptoms of iron deficiency anemia except: *', 'koilonychia', 'Koilonychia ("spooning" of the nails) is a classic, but late-stage chronic sign of severe iron-deficiency anemia, making it less frequent in early or mild iron deficiency compared to fatigue, headache, and dyspnea.', '["fatigue","headache","dyspnea","koilonychia"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:48:46.487Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684567808-42', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'A measurement of body stores of vitamin A indicating either a deficient or excessive status: *', 'serum retinol', 'Serum retinol is the standard biochemical measurement used to assess body reserves and circulating vitamin A status, reflecting both deficient and excessive states.

• Retinol binding protein: A carrier transport protein, whereas serum retinol measures the actual circulating vitamin level.
• Urinary excretion of vitamin A: Not a standard or reliable clinical indicator for assessing vitamin A stores.', '["retinol binding protein","serum retinol","urinary excretion of vitamin A","none of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:51:19.161Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684578694-43', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'It is a process of measuring the indicators of dietary status and nutrition-related health status to identify the possible occurrence, nature, and extent of impaired nutritional status. *', 'nutrition monitoring', 'Nutrition monitoring is the continuous process of measuring indicators of dietary and health status to track changes and identify the occurrence, nature, and extent of nutritional problems.

• Nutrition assessment: The diagnostic evaluation of an individual''s nutritional status.
• Nutrition surveillance: Continuous population-level tracking for public health policy action.
• Nutrition intervention: The therapeutic or programmatic action taken to solve a problem.', '["nutrition assessment","nutrition monitoring","nutrition surveillance","nutrition intervention"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:51:23.934Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684590008-44', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'A nutrition assessment system that is able to identify geographic areas and/or sub-population groups at-risk of chronic malnutrition. *', 'nutrition survey', 'A nutrition survey is a cross-sectional assessment system designed to identify geographic areas and vulnerable population groups at risk of chronic malnutrition.

• Nutrition screening: Focuses on identifying individuals rather than population geographic areas.
• Nutrition surveillance: Continuous ongoing monitoring rather than periodic cross-sectional survey snapshots.', '["nutrition screening","nutrition survey","nutrition surveillance","nutrition intervention"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:51:29.839Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684598625-45', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'A nutrition assessment system used to identify malnourished individuals who require intervention by comparing an individual’s measurements to cut-off points. *', 'nutrition screening', 'Nutrition screening is a rapid assessment process used in clinical or community settings to identify malnourished individuals who require immediate intervention by comparing measurements against established cut-offs.

• Nutrition survey: Population-level epidemiological assessment.
• Nutrition monitoring: Tracking ongoing program indicators over time.', '["nutrition survey","nutrition screening","nutrition surveillance","nutrition monitoring"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:51:38.886Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684606058-46', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'A sensitive index of current nutritional status which is not age-dependent for the first 10 years of life. *', 'weight-for-height', 'Weight-for-height is a sensitive index of current acute nutritional status (wasting) that is independent of age for the first 10 years of life.

• Height-for-age: Evaluates chronic stunting and is heavily age-dependent.
• Weight-for-age: Confounded by age and cannot distinguish stunting from wasting.', '["weight-for-age","height-for-age","MUAC-for-age","weight-for-height"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:51:45.182Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684614074-47', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'It is used to have a rapid diagnosis of PEM among children 1-4 years old. *', 'MUAC', 'Mid-Upper Arm Circumference (MUAC) is a rapid, simple anthropometric screening tool used to diagnose acute malnutrition and wasting among children aged 1 to 4 years, especially in emergency settings.

• Head circumference / Chest-head ratio: Specialized neonatal or infancy neurological assessment metrics.', '["MUAC","head circumference","chest/head circumference ratio","weight-for-age"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:51:49.026Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684621240-48', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'If MUAC is used to assess nutritional status, its cut-off for undernutrition is: *
a. 
b. 
c. d.', '<12.5 cm', 'The standard public health cut-off for moderate-to-severe undernutrition using MUAC screening in children is below 12.5 cm (with <11.5 cm indicating severe acute malnutrition).', '["<12.5 cm","serum retinol","Assessing the situation","coconut and corn oils"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:51:55.175Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684632023-49', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'An appropriate measurement of iron status that determines if iron stores have been depleted is: *', 'serum ferritin', 'Serum ferritin is the primary biochemical parameter that directly reflects and measures stored body iron levels, making it the most sensitive indicator for detecting depleted iron stores.

• Hemoglobin / Hematocrit: Functional indicators that drop only in late-stage iron deficiency anemia.
• Transferrin: Transport protein that increases during iron deficiency.', '["hemoglobin","hematocrit","serum ferritin","transferrin"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:51:59.466Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684641624-50', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'Anthropometric measurements that assess body size and growth except: *', 'MUAC', 'Mid-Upper Arm Circumference (MUAC) assesses both muscle mass and subcutaneous fat, serving as a screening indicator for acute wasting rather than a primary linear growth standard.

• Height / Weight / Head circumference: Standard linear and mass growth measurements.', '["height","weight","MUAC","head circumference"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:52:03.924Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684650757-51', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'Anthropometric measurements that determine body composition except: *', 'head circumference', 'Head circumference is a primary structural growth indicator used to monitor infant neurological development, whereas waist circumference, MUAC, and skinfolds specifically assess body fat composition.', '["waist circumference","MUAC","triceps skin fold","head circumference"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:52:08.450Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758684661506-52', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'The stage in planning when resources for nutrition programs and existing constraints are identified: *', 'Assessing the situation', 'Assessing the situation (situational analysis) is the foundational planning phase where available resources, institutional assets, and operational constraints are systematically identified.

• Setting objectives: Formulating targets based on identified gaps.
• Implementation and monitoring: Action and tracking phases.', '["Assessing the situation","Implementation and monitoring","Setting the objectives","none of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:52:13.746Z"'::jsonb)
