“Stop gap” ration is also called _____. *', 'Compact food ration', 'In immediate disaster response settings where cooking facilities are offline, emergency "stop gap" rations are distributed as ready-to-eat compact food rations.', '["Compact food ration","Dry ration","Wet ration","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:06:45.229Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758685275644-90', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'It provides for a Barangay Nutrition Scholar as a grassroot worker, *', 'PD 1569', 'Presidential Decree No. 1569 (enacted in 1978) formally established the Barangay Nutrition Scholar (BNS) Program, providing for the deployment, training, and allowance of volunteer grassroots workers tasked with delivering nutrition services at the barangay level.

• PD 491 (1974): Created the National Nutrition Council (NNC) as the highest policy-making body on nutrition, but did not specifically create the BNS grassroots worker program.
• PD 1286 (1977): The Nutrition and Dietetics Decree, which regulates the practice of the profession and sets hospital RND staffing requirements.
• PD 996 (1976): Made basic infant and child immunization compulsory.', '["PD 491","PD 1569","PD 1286","PD 996"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:42:10.252Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758685283775-91', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'A dietary assessment method that determines the overproduction of staple foods. *', 'food balance sheet', 'A Food Balance Sheet (FBS) is a macro-level national accounting tool that tracks total food supplies, production, and trade, indirectly revealing national food availability and potential overproduction or deficits.', '["food consumption survey","food balance sheet","food inventory","food account"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:05:59.181Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758685290959-92', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'The step in delivering community nutrition services which involves putting the plan into action. *', 'implementation', 'Implementation is the operational phase in community service delivery where strategic plans, budgets, and programs are actively put into action.', '["situational analysis","monitoring","implementation","planning"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:06:02.340Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758685299642-93', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'Two deficiencies often associated with PEM: 1. VAD; 2. IDA; 3. IDD; 4. Zn deficiency *', '1 & 2', 'Protein-energy malnutrition (PEM) frequently coexists synergistically with micronutrient deficiencies, most notably Vitamin A Deficiency (VAD) (1) and Iron Deficiency Anemia (IDA) (2).', '["1 & 2","2 & 3","2 & 4","3 & 4"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:06:07.199Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758685311809-94', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'Possible causes of vitamin A deficiency except: *', 'lack of fat intake to absorb the vitamin', '', '["lack of fat intake to absorb the vitamin","lack of enzyme to absorb the vitamin","rapid utilization of the vitamin","presence of infections such as measles"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758685320240-95', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'Malnutrition resulting from lack of food intake. *', 'primary malnutrition', 'Primary malnutrition is caused directly by an inadequate dietary intake of food and nutrients.

• Secondary malnutrition: Caused by malabsorption or underlying disease states.', '["chronic malnutrition","primary malnutrition","secondary malnutrition","acute malnutrition"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:06:17.468Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758685338291-96', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'People “in the know” about the community who can provide information about the target population. *', 'key informants', 'Key informants are respected community members "in the know" regarding local culture, habits, and population needs, serving as valuable resources for qualitative assessments.', '["key informants","social group","resource persons","focus group"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:06:28.150Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758685348991-97', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'A group of 5-12 people who are interdependent, sharing a set of norms, beliefs, and values or behavior. *', 'focus group', 'A focus group comprises a small, interdependent cohort of 5–12 individuals sharing similar backgrounds who participate in guided qualitative discussions.', '["focus group","control group","target group","social group"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:06:33.517Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758685358522-98', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'Target groups of Garantisadong Pambata: *', 'children 0-5 years', 'Garantisadong Pambata is a nationwide DOH child health campaign targeting children aged 0 to 5 years (under-five population) with integrated health and nutrition services.', '["children 0-6 years","children 1-3 years","children 1-5 years","children 0-5 years"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:06:49.596Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758685367721-99', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'Food products with Sangkap Pinoy Seal are fortified with: *', 'iron, vitamin A, iodine', 'Products bearing the government''s Sangkap Pinoy Seal are voluntarily fortified with the three mandatory national micronutrients: iron, vitamin A, and iodine.', '["iron, vitamin A, thiamin","vitamin C, iron, iodine","iron, vitamin A, iodine","vitamin C, vitamin A, iron"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.160Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:06:53.373Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758685421754-100', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'The first national nutrition survey was conducted in: *', '1978', 'The First National Nutrition Survey (NNS) in the Philippines was conducted in 1978 by the Food and Nutrition Research Institute (FNRI) to establish baseline health, anthropometric, and dietary data across the country.', '["1979","1982","1978","1976"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.008Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:42:26.153Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758685441519-101', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'The immunization given to infants to protect them from TB infection from other family members: *', 'BCG', 'BCG (Bacille Calmette-Guérin) vaccine is administered to infants at birth or shortly thereafter specifically to prevent severe forms of tuberculosis (such as TB meningitis).

• OPV (Oral Polio Vaccine): Protects against poliomyelitis.
• Measles: Protects against measles virus.
• DPT: Protects against diphtheria, pertussis, and tetanus.', '["BCG","OPV","measles","DPT"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.008Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:43:44.208Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758685449868-102', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608782087-1790433140508-zgaqi', 'The frequency of deworming recommended for children: *', '3 times a year', 'Standard public health deworming protocols for preschool- and school-age children in endemic areas recommend routine mass deworming every 4 months (3 times a year).', '["once a month","once a year","2 times a year","3 times a year"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.008Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T08:43:53.550Z"'::jsonb)
