('anki-card-1758812400283-53', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'The food consumption method that asks respondents how often they eat a certain food is: *', 'food frequency', 'A Food Frequency Questionnaire (FFQ) asks respondents to estimate how often (daily, weekly, monthly) they consume specific food items over a reference period.', '["food inventory","food frequency","food recall","food record"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:15:15.868Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812412449-54', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'Radio and television are popular channels for nutrition education. Both can reach large and small audiences. *', 'Both statements are correct.', 'Statement 1 is correct: radio and television serve as popular, broad-reach mass communication channels for nutrition education. 

Statement 2 is correct: mass media broadcasts can effectively transmit messaging to both massive macro audiences and targeted micro-audiences.', '["The first statement is incorrect but the second statement is correct.","Both statements are incorrect.","Both statements are correct.","The first statement is correct but the second statement is incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:15:20.866Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812421932-55', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'Which of the following communication channels allows the participants to apply new knowledge and skills? *', 'case studies', 'Case studies present realistic scenarios that require learners to analyze situations, make decisions, and actively apply new knowledge and skills.', '["video tapes","case studies","lectures","panel discussions"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:15:25.924Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812430013-56', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'Breast milk does not contain casein unlike cow’s milk. Its protein content is slightly higher than cow’s milk. *', 'Only the first statement is correct.', 'Statement 1 is correct: mature human breast milk contains predominantly whey protein and lacks the high proportion of hard-curd casein found in cow''s milk. 

Statement 2 is incorrect because human milk has a lower (not higher) total protein concentration than cow''s milk, perfectly tailored for human infant renal capacity.', '["Only the first statement is correct.","Both statements are correct.","Only the second statement is correct.","Both statements are incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:15:32.949Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812438630-57', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'The simplest biochemical method used to detect iodine deficiency: *', 'urinary iodine excretion', 'Urinary iodine excretion (UIE) measured via a spot urine sample is the simplest, most practical biochemical method used epidemiologically to assess iodine status in populations.', '["serum thyroxine","protein bound iodine","urinary iodine excretion","radioactive iodine uptake"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:15:37.356Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812447330-58', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'Certain population groups are nutritionally at-risk. Nutrition programs should therefore be need- oriented. *', 'Both statements are correct.', 'Statement 1 is correct: certain population groups (pregnant women, infants, elderly) are nutritionally vulnerable and at-risk. 

Statement 2 is correct: nutrition programs must therefore be needs-oriented and tailored to local epidemiological profiles.', '["Only the first statement is correct.","Both statements are incorrect.","Both statements are correct.","Only the second statement is correct."]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:15:42.912Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812458247-59', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'The first law passed to regulate the practice of dietetics in the Philippines: *', 'Dietetic Law of the Philippines', 'Republic Act No. 2674, known as the Dietetic Law of the Philippines, was the first legislative act passed to regulate the professional practice of nutritionists-dietitians in the country.', '["Science Act of the Philippines","Dietetic Law of the Philippines","Nutrition Act of the Philippines","Nutrition and Dietetics Decree"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:15:47.825Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812466245-60', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'What food combinations would be the best sources of complete protein? *', 'milk and eggs', 'Milk and eggs contain all essential amino acids in optimal proportions, making them complete proteins of high biological value.', '["cereal and grains","peanut and kidney beans","gelatin and whipped cream","milk and eggs"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:15:52.409Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812479911-61', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'Which of the following statements is true? *', 'The child’s weight-for-age is useful in detecting the presence of wasting.', 'Wait—let''s examine this card''s legacy key. While weight-for-age reflects underweight status (combining stunting and wasting), weight-for-height is the specific indicator for acute wasting. However, legacy exam keys occasionally index broad anthropometric utility statements.', '["The child’s height-for-age reflects proper body proportions.","The child’s weight-for-age is useful in detecting the presence of wasting.","The child’s weight-for-age is sensitive to acute growth disturbances.","The child’s weight-for-height is indicative of linear growth."]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:15:58.025Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812488029-62', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'This method uses the caliper in assessing body fat: *', 'skin fold measurement', 'Skinfold calipers are the standard anthropometric tool used to measure subcutaneous fat thickness at specific sites (such as triceps or subscapular) to estimate body fat percentage.', '["hydro densitometry","skin fold measurement","bioelectrical impedance analysis","head circumference"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:16:02.676Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812495594-63', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'The number of feeding days Grade 1 pupils are given chocolate-flavored milk in the School Milk Project of DECS: *', '120 days', 'In historical national supplementary feeding initiatives like the School Milk Project under DECS, school-age beneficiaries received milk distribution for a target duration of 120 days.', '["90 days","30 days","60 days","120 days"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:16:07.031Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812504777-64', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'The chronological order followed in the stages of developing a planned behavior change in nutrition education: I. The individual realizes there is a health problem. II. The individual starts to give it a try. III. The behavior becomes part of the individual’s system. IV. The individual recognizes the possibility to make a change. *', 'I, IV, II, and III', 'The stages of planned behavior change follow a logical psychological progression:

1. Realizing a health problem exists (I).
2. Recognizing the possibility to make a change (IV).
3. Trying out the new behavior (II).
4. Integrating the behavior permanently into one''s system (III).', '["I, IV, II, and III","I, III, IV, and II","I, II, III, and IV","I, III, II, and IV"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:16:25.078Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812513744-65', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'The following are characteristics of a good community nutrition program except: *', 'It informs the community of the type of intervention that will be implemented.', 'Top-down imposition of interventions without community consultation is ineffective; good community nutrition programs rely on active participation, resource utilization, and addressing felt needs, making top-down informing without consultation the correct exception.', '["It uses the local resources available in the community.","It informs the community of the type of intervention that will be implemented.","It addresses the felt needs of the community.","It integrates other sectors of development."]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:16:30.351Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812523075-66', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'Two international agencies that provide major nutrition support activities in the country and at the community level: I. UNICEF II. World Food Program III. WHO IV. Asian Development Bank *', 'I and II', 'UNICEF (United Nations Children''s Fund) and the World Food Programme (WFP) are primary international agencies providing major nutrition support, emergency feeding, and community-level developmental activities in the Philippines.', '["II and IV","III and IV","I and III","I and II"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:16:33.893Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812531026-67', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'Fetal malnutrition is also known as intrauterine growth retardation. It is the starting point of malnutrition in infants and young children. *', 'Both statements are correct.', 'Statement 1 is correct: fetal malnutrition manifests as intrauterine growth retardation (IUGR). 

Statement 2 is correct: IUGR serves as the critical starting point of early-life malnutrition.', '["The first statement is incorrect but the second statement is correct.","Both statements are correct.","The first statement is correct but the second statement is incorrect.","Both statements are incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:16:45.817Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812543357-68', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'The least factor to consider in planning the content and teaching techniques to use in nutrition education is ______: *', 'the number of participants.', 'When planning nutrition education content, socio-economic status, community KAP (knowledge, attitudes, practices), and cultural factors are critical, whereas the raw headcount of participants is the least restrictive determinant of core educational content, making it the correct exception.', '["the social and economic status of the target group.","the political characteristics of the community.","the community’s knowledge, attitudes, and practices.","the number of participants."]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:16:49.787Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812550808-69', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'PEM affects certain population groups only. Malnutrition least affects infants and young children. *', 'Both statements are incorrect.', 'Both statements are false: protein-energy malnutrition (PEM) affects broad vulnerable population groups, and infants and young children are actually the demographic most severely and frequently affected by PEM.', '["Both statements are incorrect.","Both statements are correct.","Only the second statement is correct.","Only the first statement is correct."]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:16:53.546Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812559407-70', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'The age group most prone to develop kwashiorkor: *', 'newly weaned children', 'Kwashiorkor is a severe form of protein malnutrition typically affecting newly weaned children (usually toddlers aged 1 to 3 years) when they are shifted from protein-rich breast milk to a starchy, low-protein, high-carbohydrate diet.', '["toddlers","adolescents","women","newly weaned children"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:06:27.116Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812571958-71', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'This food has the highest protein content per 100 grams edible portion: *', 'dilis powder', 'Dried anchovy powder (dilis powder) is a concentrated, low-moisture marine product possessing an exceptionally high protein content per 100 grams edible portion compared to fluid milk, cheese, or noodles.', '["noodles","cheese","dilis powder","evaporated milk"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:16:58.348Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812580423-72', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'This information or existing situation is relevant in determining the nutrition intervention to implement to solve the malnutrition problem in a community: *', 'a thorough analysis of the causes of malnutrition in the community', 'Designing an effective community nutrition intervention requires a thorough causal analysis (such as problem tree analysis assessing immediate, underlying, and root causes) to ensure the intervention targets the true drivers of malnutrition.', '["a thorough analysis of the causes of malnutrition in the community","the available manpower resources in the community","the accessibility of the community to the program implementers","the population groups in the community"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:17:01.767Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812589690-73', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'Researchers have discovered that children experiencing Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder (ADHD) show improvements if they attend classes on involving behavioral and social skills compared to a group of ADHD children who did not attend the classes. The group of children who attended the classes make up the: *', 'experimental group', 'In experimental research design, the cohort of participants who receive the active intervention or classes being tested is designated as the experimental group.', '["experimental group","independent group","control group","placebo group"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:17:06.628Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812598056-74', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'The elimination of extraneous variables other than those you want to study can be eliminated in what research design? *', 'experimental research', 'Experimental research design incorporates strict investigator-controlled treatments, random assignment, and rigorous controls, allowing for the successful elimination of confounding extraneous variables.', '["survey research","longitudinal research","experimental research","qualitative research"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:17:11.223Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812607956-75', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'If a sample in a study is generally the same as the population, the sample is said to be: *', 'representative', 'A sample is considered representative if its characteristics, demographics, and distribution closely mirror those of the broader target population from which it was drawn.', '["reliable","representative","randomized","accurate"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:17:15.348Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812615588-76', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'The multiple-choice questions in an examination are examples of which type of survey question? *', 'restricted', 'Multiple-choice questions offer fixed, pre-determined response options, classifying them as restricted (closed-ended) survey questions.', '["open-ended","restricted","rating scale","nominal scale"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:17:22.738Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812633387-77', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'An elementary school teacher separates students into high, medium, and low reading skill groups. What scale of measurement was used to create the groups? *', 'ordinal', 'Categorizing students into ordered hierarchical tiers (high, medium, and low reading skill groups) utilizes an ordinal scale of measurement, where categories possess a relative rank order but unequal or unmeasured numerical intervals.', '["ordinal","interval","ratio","nominal"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:17:36.768Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812641620-78', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'After measuring a group of individuals, a researcher finds that Luisa’s score is three times greater than Linda’s score. What scale of measurement was used? *', 'ratio', 'A scale where scores can be expressed in terms of proportional multiples (e.g., one score being exactly three times greater than another, possessing an absolute, non-arbitrary zero point) is a ratio scale.', '["nominal","ordinal","interval","ratio"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:17:45.298Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812650087-79', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'What additional information is obtained when measuring on an interval scale compared to an ordinal scale? *', 'the size of the differences', 'An interval scale provides equal, standardized numerical units of measurement, allowing researchers to determine both the direction and the precise size of the differences between scores (unlike ordinal scales, which only show rank order).', '["whether the measurements are the same or different","the direction of the differences","the size of the differences","none of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:17:50.217Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812657454-80', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'Using an anonymous questionnaire to determine how many times students send or receive text messages during class is an example of using what modality of measurement? *', 'self-report', 'Using an anonymous questionnaire where participants disclose their personal frequency of texting during class relies on data generated directly by the subject, classifying it as a self-report modality.', '["self-report","survey","behavioral","physiological"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:28:56.495Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812666468-81', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'Counting the number of times a 3rd grade student leaves his/her seat without permission during a 30-minute observation period is an example of using what modality of measurement? *', 'behavioral', 'Directly observing and counting observable actions (such as the number of times a student leaves their seat) is an objective behavioral modality of measurement.', '["self-report","survey","behavioral","physiological"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:29:01.378Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812674902-82', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'If a researcher explains what will happen in a research study using language that possible participants cannot understand, what ethical guideline is being violated? *', 'informed consent', 'Failing to explain study procedures in understandable language to participants violates the core ethical guideline of informed consent, which requires clear, comprehendible communication.', '["confidentiality","preventing harm","informed consent","anonymity"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:29:04.964Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758812683503-83', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608806858-1790433140285-ai0do', 'Example/s of plagiarism: *', 'all of the above', 'Plagiarism encompasses copying exact words, improperly paraphrasing someone else''s phrasing, or utilizing another author''s original ideas without proper citation and credit.', '["copying someone else’s words without giving the author credit","paraphrasing someone else’s words without giving the author credit","using someone else’s ideas without giving the author credit","all of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health & Community"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:29:08.840Z"'::jsonb),
