INSERT INTO public.flashcards (id, user_id, deck_id, front, back, rationale, options, tags, ndle_subject, difficulty, leitner_box, user_notes, sm2, last_reviewed_at, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
('card-1792144517142-ps1h1', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608929173-1790433142619-teu0e', 'An infant is physiologically ready for solid foods when:', 'All of the above', 'An infant becomes developmentally and physiologically ready to transition to solid foods (complementary feeding) around 6 months of age, marked by several key internal changes:
• Saliva is produced: Around 3 to 6 months, an infant’s salivary glands mature, significantly increasing saliva production. Saliva contains lubricants and enzymes that help moisten and break down solid textures.

• Gastric acidity increases: A newborn''s stomach has a relatively high pH (less acidic). As the infant approaches 6 months, gastric acid production increases, lowering the stomach pH to adult-like levels. This is necessary to properly digest complex proteins from solid foods and kill harmful foodborne pathogens.
• Enzymes for starch digestion are produced: During early infancy, levels of pancreatic amylase (the enzyme needed to digest complex starches) are very low. By 6 months of age, the secretion of these digestive enzymes matures significantly, allowing the infant''s GI tract to safely process and absorb starches from rice, cereals, and mashed root crops.', '["All of the above","Saliva is produced","Gastric acidity increases","Enzymes for starch digestion is produced"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-17T10:36:22.229Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:36:22.229Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T09:55:17.868Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:36:22.229Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1792145015213-bzxs1', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608929173-1790433142619-teu0e', 'Which is true about the basal metabolic of the elderly?', 'A and B are both FALSE', 'The basal metabolic rate (BMR) does decline with age, but it happens because of a decrease in the functional capacity of cells and a prominent loss of functioning lean muscle tissue (sarcopenia). It does not decline because cell capacity increases.

The decline in baseline metabolic needs is typically accompanied by an increase in body fat (adipose tissue) and a redistribution of fat toward the abdomen, rather than a decrease in body fat.', '["A and B are both FALSE","It declines with age because of the increase in the functional capacity of cells","The declined metabolic needs is accompanied by a decrease in body fat","A and B are both TRUE"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-17T10:36:29.110Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:36:29.110Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:03:36.002Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:36:29.110Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1792145072979-404ox', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608929173-1790433142619-teu0e', 'Psychological related factors resulting to malnutrition in elderly except:', 'Immobility', 'Immobility is a physical/biological factor: It refers to the physical inability to move around easily, which causes malnutrition by making it difficult for an elderly person to shop for groceries, lift heavy cooking utensils, or prepare meals independently.

The other options are psychological/social factors: Living alone (which leads to loneliness and isolation), depression, and anxiety are all mental, emotional, or psychological states that directly destroy an elderly person''s appetite, interest in food, and motivation to eat (a condition often called the "anorexia of aging").', '["Immobility","Living alone","Depression","Anxiety"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-17T10:36:35.677Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:36:35.677Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:04:36.137Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:36:35.677Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1792145133410-lknqx', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608929173-1790433142619-teu0e', 'Hyposmia is also know as:', 'Lowered sense of smell', 'Hyposmia is the official clinical term for a partially reduced or lowered ability to smell and detect odors. It is very common in older adults due to natural aging, as well as clinical conditions like chronic sinusitis, viral infections, or neurodegenerative changes.

• Decreased taste sensitivity: This is known as hypogeusia (whereas a complete loss of taste is ageusia).
• Loss of appetite: This is known clinically as anorexia (such as the anorexia of aging).
• Lowered thirst sensation: This is known as hypodipsia.', '["Lowered sense of smell","Decreased taste sensitivity","Loss of appetite","Lowered thirst sensation"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-17T10:36:48.366Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:36:48.366Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:05:34.069Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:36:48.366Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1792145308872-7k558', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608929173-1790433142619-teu0e', 'Which is true about menopause among females:', 'A and B are both TRUE', 'Menopause is the permanent cessation of menstrual periods resulting from the natural biological aging of the female reproductive system:

• Statement A is TRUE: As a woman transitions into menopause, her ovaries dramatically reduce their secretion of the key female sex hormones, leading to severely decreased levels of estrogen and progesterone. This sharp hormonal decline is responsible for classic menopausal symptoms like hot flashes and night sweats.
• Statement B is TRUE: The root biological cause of this hormone drop is the natural depletion of the ovarian reserve. A woman is born with a finite number of primordial follicles. Over her reproductive lifespan, as more follicles undergo ovulation or atresia (shrinkage/cell death), the ovaries end up with a significantly lower number of viable ovarian follicles. Consequently, fewer follicles develop completely to ovulate and transform into a corpus luteum (the temporary structure responsible for secreting progesterone).', '["A and B are both TRUE","A result of decreased levels of estrogen and progesterone","A result of less number of ovarian follicles and corpora lutea","A and B are both FALSE"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-17T10:36:59.927Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:36:59.927Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:08:29.336Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:36:59.927Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1792145374332-vvkhi', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608929173-1790433142619-teu0e', 'The breast milk that women produce in the first few days after delivery', 'Colostrum', 'Colostrum is the distinct, specialized form of breast milk produced by the mammary glands in late pregnancy and the first few days after delivery (typically days 1 to 4). It is a thick, yellowish fluid that is uniquely adapted to a newborn''s immediate needs:

It is highly concentrated with leukocytes and protective antibodies—especially Immunoglobulin A (IgA)—acting as the infant''s first natural vaccine.

It contains high levels of epidermal growth factors to help mature the infant''s gut lining, and acts as a mild laxative to assist the baby in passing meconium (the first stool).

• Mature milk: This thinner, bluish-white milk transitions in around day 10 to 15 postpartum, supplying the stable balance of water, carbohydrates, lipids, and proteins needed for long-term growth.
• Foremilk: This is the milk available at the beginning of a single feeding session, which is watery and high in lactose to satisfy the infant''s thirst.
• Hindmilk: This is the creamier milk released toward the end of a single feeding session, which is dense in fat and calories to promote satiety and weight gain.', '["Colostrum","Mature milk","Foremilk","Hindmilk"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-17T10:37:12.562Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:37:12.562Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:09:34.927Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:37:12.562Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1792145503463-fnle0', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608929173-1790433142619-teu0e', 'A multi-level tool for promoting and sustaining risk-reducing behavior change in individuals and communities by distributing tailored specific messages through a variety of channels.', 'Behavior Change Communication', 'Behavior Change Communication (BCC) is a strategic, multi-level framework designed to foster and maintain healthy, risk-reducing lifestyle habits within populations.

It systematically delivers tailored, highly specific messages designed to resonate with particular audiences. Rather than relying on a single approach, BCC distributes these messages across a variety of communication channels—including interpersonal counseling, group discussions, community media, and mass marketing campaigns.

While Nutrition Education is a component of this process, BCC focuses more broadly on the psychological and social drivers of action to shift actual behavior, moving beyond simply providing raw academic facts.', '["Behavior Change Communication","Nutrition Education","Learning Strategies","Health Promotion"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-17T10:37:17.906Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:37:17.906Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:11:44.166Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:37:17.906Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1792145652252-xfzat', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608929173-1790433142619-teu0e', 'Which is an example of interpersonal communication?', 'Nutrition counseling', 'Interpersonal communication refers to a face-to-face, interactive exchange of information between two or more people. In this context, nutrition counseling is the perfect example because it involves a direct, personalized, two-way dialogue between a healthcare professional (or nutrition worker) and an individual client or family. This layout allows for active listening, immediate feedback, and tailored advice.', '["Nutrition counseling","Mother''s class","Airing of nutrition messages in TV","Distribution of nutrition handouts"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-17T10:37:22.233Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:37:22.233Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:14:12.722Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:37:22.233Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1792145907870-itdps', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608929173-1790433142619-teu0e', 'Who is the chair of the National Nutrition Council Governing Board?', 'Department of Health', 'By law, under Presidential Decree No. 491 (The Nutrition Act of the Philippines) and subsequent executive updates, the Secretary of the Department of Health (DOH) serves as the official Chairperson of the National Nutrition Council (NNC) Governing Board.

The NNC is the country''s highest policy-making and coordinating body on nutrition. Its leadership structure consists of:
• Chairperson: Secretary of the Department of Health (DOH)
• Vice-Chairs:
	1. Secretary of the Department of Agriculture (DA)
	2. Secretary of the Department of the Interior and Local Government (DILG)

The board also includes the heads of several other departments (such as DepEd, DSWD, DTI, DOST, and DOLE) alongside representatives from the private sector to ensure a multi-sectoral approach to addressing malnutrition.', '["Department of Health","Department of Agriculture","Department of Education","Department of Interior and Local Government"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-17T10:37:31.656Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:37:31.656Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:18:28.393Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:37:31.656Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1792145946968-1bk4n', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608929173-1790433142619-teu0e', 'Which law specifies rules and regulations which contain standard procedures to be followed for rooming-in and breastfeeding in all private and government health institutions?', 'RA 7600', '', '["RA 7600","RA 8172","RA 8976","RA 10028"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-17T10:37:36.568Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:37:36.568Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:19:08.347Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:37:36.568Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1792145970153-bvwoz', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608929173-1790433142619-teu0e', 'Which law requires private enterprises as well as government agencies, including government-owned and controlled corporations, to put up lactation stations?', 'RA 10028', '', '["RA 10028","RA 7600","RA 8172","RA 8976"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-17T10:37:41.505Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:37:41.505Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:19:30.850Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:37:41.505Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1792145996585-1rs6n', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608929173-1790433142619-teu0e', 'What executive order regulates the marketing of infant milk formula, other milk products, foods and beverages, as well as feeding bottles and teats?', 'EO 51', '', '["EO 51","EO 41","EO 61","EO 71"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-17T10:37:45.300Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:37:45.300Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:19:57.360Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:37:45.300Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1792146059233-gfgva', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608929173-1790433142619-teu0e', 'What law strengthens the Barangay Nutrition Program by providing for a Barangay Nutrition Scholar in every barangay to assist in the coordination and implementation of nutrition programs, projects, and activities and the barangay level?', 'PD 1569', 'Signed on June 11, 1978, Presidential Decree No. 1569 is titled "Strengthening the Barangay Nutrition Program by providing for a Barangay Nutrition Scholar (BNS) in every barangay, providing funds therefor, and for other purposes."

It officially established the BNS program across the Philippines, mandating that every barangay should have a trained local volunteer (the BNS) responsible for:
• Monitoring the nutritional status of children through routine weighing (Operation Timbang Plus)
• Linking malnourished children and families to health and nutrition services
• Coordinating nutrition programs, projects, and activities directly at the grass-roots barangay level', '["PD 1569","PD 1596","PD 1659","PD 1695"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-17T10:38:01.908Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:38:01.908Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:20:59.881Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-16T10:38:02.089Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754280382829-0', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The tolerable upper intake level (UL) is the largest daily nutrient intake shown to harbor no adverse side effects to ___', 'A large majority of individual in a particular age or gender group', 'The reason the Tolerable Upper Intake Level (UL), or Upper Tolerable Limit, applies to a large majority (almost all) of individuals in a specific group but not absolutely everyone, is due to the inherent biological variability in the human population and the conservative methodology used to establish the UL.

Estimated Average Requirement (EAR), which is set at the median requirement covering only half of a group, not the UL. The UL is therefore a ceiling for safe habitual intake and not a recommended target intake.', '["Half the individuals in a particular age or gender group","A large majority of individual in a particular age or gender group","Everyone in a particular age or gender group","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-27T08:35:13.195Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:35:13.195Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:35:13.195Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754280527235-1', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Based on the Acceptable Macronutrient Distribution Ranges (AMDR), energy from fat as a percentage of total energy for adults should be within the range?', '15-30%', 'The correct range is 15-30% of total energy based on the Philippine Dietary Reference Intakes (PDRI) AMDR for fat in adults.

Carbohydrate: 55-75%
Protein: 10-15%
Fat: 15-30%', '["<10%","10-20%","15-30%","35-50%"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-27T14:43:51.984Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:43:51.984Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:43:51.984Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754280732361-2', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which one of the following statements is incorrect?', 'According to Pinggang Pinoy, meat, fish, and alternatives should comprise one-third of the plate', 'Answer should be 1/6 ~ 17%.', '["According to Pinggang Pinoy, half of our plate should be include fruits and vegetable","According to Pinggang Pinoy, meat, fish, and alternatives should comprise one-third of the plate","The statement \"Eat lots of fruits and vegetables\" is a food-based dietary guideline","The statement \"Eat less sodium-no more than 2g/day\" is not food-based dietary guideline"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-27T08:34:26.376Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:34:26.376Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:34:26.376Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754280875002-3', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Nutritional Deficiency is usually initiated by __?', 'Inadequate dietary intake of one or more nutrients', 'This is the 1st stage, based on schema of the development of nutritional deficiency. This stage precedes any measurable biochemical, functional, or clinical change in the body. Illness and low income are underlying or basic causes that may contribute to inadequate intake but are not themselves the initiating physiological event. 

The sequence generally progresses from dietary inadequacy to depleted tissue stores, then biochemical changes, and finally clinical signs.', '["Inadequate dietary intake of one or more nutrients","Illness","Low income","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-27T13:25:47.538Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:25:47.538Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:25:47.538Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754280958464-4', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Following the stages of developing nutrient deficiency, what is the appropriate method for the first stage?', 'Dietary', 'The correct answer is dietary assessment because the first stage of deficiency is inadequate dietary intake, and only dietary methods (recalls, records, FFQs) can directly capture what and how much a person is eating. 

• Anthropometry reflects later effects on body size and composition, appearing only after prolonged deficiency. 
• Clinical assessment detects obvious signs and symptoms, which appear latest in the sequence. 
• Biochemical assessment detects depleted nutrient stores or altered biomarkers, a stage that occurs after dietary inadequacy but before clinical signs. Matching the assessment method to the stage of deficiency ensures problems are caught as early as possible.', '["Anthropometry","Dietary","Clinical","Biochemical"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-27T09:41:22.108Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:41:22.108Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:41:22.108Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754281066276-5', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Include factors that influence health: biological, chemical, physical, social, cultural, economic, genetic, and behavioral', 'Determinants', 'Determinants is the standard epidemiological term for factors that influence the frequency and distribution of health-related states. 

• Distribution refers to how disease or health outcomes are spread across person, place, and time, not the causal factors themselves.
• "Health-related states and events" refers to the outcomes being studied, not their causes. 
• "Application" is unrelated to this definition.', '["Determinants","Distribution","Health-related states and events","Application"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-27T14:47:34.611Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:47:34.611Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:47:34.808Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754281368645-6', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The theoretical or conceptual framework for the research defines the boundaries of your problem; and is used to develop a perspective in which the factual and conceptual elements become interconnected into a logical structure of relationships. Which one of the following is false?', 'In formulating conceptual framework, you may look at the various theories upon which you can base your study', 'The false statement is D; in constructing a conceptual framework, the researcher draws upon related studies and existing theories, so the missing element is "related studies,"

• Choice A is true because both frameworks are built from facts and explanations grounded in existing knowledge of the problem. 
• Choice B is true because the theoretical framework specifically presents the theory underpinning the research problem. 
• Choice C is true because the conceptual framework maps out relationships among the specific concepts/variables under study.', '["Both theoretical and conceptual frameworks consist of facts and explanation which proceed from the understanding on the knowledge about a problem","Theoretical framework presents the theory from which your research problem was derived","In the conceptual framework you present the relationship between the specific concepts for study","In formulating conceptual framework, you may look at the various theories upon which you can base your study"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T13:35:29.583Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:35:29.583Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:35:29.583Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754281626685-7', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Research design should be accurate. This means:', 'Strive to be definite, precise, and exact', 'In research methodology and design, distinct terms specify the standard requirements for a study''s framework:

• Accurate: Means that the researcher must strive to be definite, precise, and exact with their parameters, measurements, and data representation to avoid errors.
• Objective: This corresponds to option A (Unbiased, unprejudiced, detached, impersonal). It ensures the findings are guided by empirical data rather than personal opinions or emotions.
• Analytical: This describes option B, focusing on breaking down complex subjects into their individual, fundamental parts to comprehend them comprehensively.', '["Unbiased, unprejudiced, detached, impersonal","There are relatively agreed-upon defined traits or boundaries which specify what kind of things or boundaries you study","Strive to be definite, precise, and exact","Concerned with the identification and study of the component parts or elements which make up the things which you study"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:48:12.080Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:48:12.080Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:48:12.080Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754281705048-8', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which type of objective is the most applicable if your study uses methodology research design?', 'To evaluate measuring instrument', 'In research methodology textbooks, a methodological research design (sometimes called methodological research) does not focus on investigating a substantive medical or social phenomenon itself. Instead, its primary purpose is the controlled development, testing, and validation of the research tools themselves.

The Goal of Methodological Design is to target the validation or evaluation of a measuring instrument, scale, survey tool, or clinical questionnaire to ensure it possesses high validity and reliability before it is deployed in field studies.

	• To explore relationship: Best fits a correlational or explanatory research design.
	• To make comparison between groups: Best fits an experimental, quasi-experimental, or comparative research design.
	• To describe population or certain phenomena: Best fits a classic descriptive or observational research design.', '["To evaluate measuring instrument","To describe population or certain phenomena","To explore relationship","To make comparison between groups"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:41:08.151Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:41:08.151Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:41:08.332Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754281889790-9', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'It is the study of assessment of diet and its relationship to disease etiology in the populations.', 'Nutritional epidemiology', 'Nutritional epidemiology specifically studies dietary patterns and nutrient intake in relation to disease occurrence at the population level.

• "Food and nutrition research" is a broader, generic term not specific to disease etiology. 
• "Food and nutrition epidemiology" and "food epidemiology" are not the standard, recognized terms used in the field.', '["Nutritional epidemiology","Food and nutrition research","Food and nutrition epidemiology","Food epidemiology"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:20:34.247Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:20:34.247Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:20:34.247Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754282064782-10', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The 3Rs are principle of good science designed by scientist to improve animal welfare and scientific accuracy. Which of the following means finding ways of making animals'' lives better in labs, this can include toys for animals or better training for technicians.', 'Refinement', 'Refinement - Minimize animal pain, suffering, and distress.

• Reduction - Use the minimum number of animals necessary.
• Replacement - Use non-animal methods where possible.
• Recognition - random word which start with letter R.', '["Reduction","Replacement","Refinement","Recognition"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:45:57.549Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:45:57.549Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:45:57.549Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754282189492-11', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'It is the practice of analyzing describing a complex phenomenon in terms of phenomena that are held to represent a single or more fundamental level, especially when this is a said to provide a sufficient explanation', 'Reductionism in research', 'Reductionism is a philosophical and scientific approach that breaks down complex systems or phenomena into their smaller, simpler, or more fundamental components. In research (especially in fields like nutritional biochemistry or physiology), it assumes that understanding these isolated, individual parts provides a sufficient explanation for the behavior of the entire system.

• Scientific Method: The systematic, step-by-step process of observing, forming a hypothesis, experimenting, and drawing conclusions to gather knowledge.
• Research Method: The specific tools, techniques, or procedures used to collect and analyze data (e.g., surveys, randomized controlled trials, or double-blind studies).
• Research Design: The overall structural blueprint or strategy chosen to integrate the different components of a study in a coherent and logical way (e.g., cross-sectional, cohort, or experimental design).', '["Research method","Reductionism in research","Scientific method","Research design"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:29:47.414Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:29:47.414Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:29:47.612Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754282328051-12', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'What is the over-all goal of nutritional epidemiology?', 'To contribute to the prevention of disease and the improvement of public health', 'The correct answer is to contribute to the prevention of disease and the improvement of public health, which represents the ultimate purpose (goal). Choices A, B, and D are all legitimate specific aims or objectives that serve this larger goal.

“Goal" (why it exists)
"Objectives" (what it specifically does to get there)', '["To monitor the food consumption, nutrient intake and nutritional status of a population","To assess  the strength of diet-disease associations","To contribute to the prevention of disease and the improvement of public health","To generate new hypothesis about diet and disease"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:21:41.118Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:21:41.118Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:21:41.118Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754282471562-13', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'What study design will you use to determine the relation of wealth status (rich, middle class) and fruit intake (in grams) per day.', 'Cross-sectional', 'Cross-sectional is the most applicable for determining the current, simple relationship between an exposure (wealth status) and outcome (fruit intake).

• Cohort - aim to determine the cause-and-effect relationship between an exposure and the development of a disease/outcome over a long period of time
• Case series - aims to provide a detailed description of a small number of patients (case series) or a single patient (case report) with an unusual or novel condition
• Case-control - aims to determine the past exposures that led to a rare disease/outcome', '["Cross-sectional","Cohort","Case series","Case control"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:16:09.664Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:16:09.664Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:16:10.010Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754282694468-14', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'What statistical test will you use in the study particularly if the data is normally distributed?

Study: to determine the relation of wealth status (rich, middle class) and fruit intake (in grams) per day', 'T-test', 'T-test - parametric test used to compare the means of exactly two groups. Since there are only two wealth statuses to compare fruit intake then this is the correct answer.

• ANOVA - parametric test used to compare the means of three or more groups.
• Chi-square test - used for categorical data
• Mann-Whitney - is a non-parametric test', '["T-test","ANOVA","Chi-square test","Mann-Whitney"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T13:59:38.426Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:59:38.426Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:59:38.426Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754282976955-15', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Refers to a phenomenon which is thought to occur when people observed during a research study temporarily change their behavior or performance', 'Hawthorne', 'Hawthorne effect occurs when participants change their behavior simply because they know they are being observed or studied.

• Ecological fallacy - Mistakenly applying conclusions drawn from group-level data (e.g., states, countries) to individuals within those groups.
• Systematic error - Consistent, non-random error that always biases measurements in the same direction (e.g., a poorly calibrated scale).
• Placebo effect - A positive or therapeutic effect that results from a participant''s expectation or belief in the treatment, rather than the treatment''s actual physiological mechanism.', '["Ecological facally","Systematic error","Hawthorne","Placebo effect"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T07:51:53.394Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:51:53.394Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:51:53.394Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754283151564-16', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'This means making up data, experiments, or other significant information in proposing, conducting, or reporting research', 'Fabrication', 'Fabrication is the act of making up data or results entirely and recording or reporting them as true.

• Falsification involves manipulating research materials, equipment, or processes, or changing/omitting data so that the research record does not accurately represent the actual work.
• Plagiarism is using another person''s ideas, processes, results, or words without giving them proper credit.', '["Falsification","Fabrication","Plagiarism","Intentional misconduct"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:17:18.282Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:17:18.282Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:17:18.282Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754283248926-17', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which of the following is not a nutritional exposure?', 'IQ score', 'IQ score functions as an outcome (dependent variable) not an exposure (independent variable/risk factor) in most nutrition research contexts. Physical activity, coffee intake, and reading food labels are all behaviors or exposures that can be investigated as potential predictors of a nutrition-related outcome.

Exposure is the cause or predictor (the independent variable or risk factor), which is the factor being investigated for its effect. Outcome is the effect or result (the dependent variable), which is the disease, event, or condition being studied.', '["Physical activity","Coffee intake","IQ score","Reading food labels"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:38:31.860Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:38:31.860Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:38:31.860Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754283503615-18', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Interpret the results of correlation between abdominal circumstances and HDL cholesterol level: r = 0.16, P = 0.002.', 'There is no correlation between abdominal circumference and HDL cholesterol level, and it is unlikely that our result is caused by play of chance', 'The correct interpretation is that there is essentially no meaningful correlation between abdominal circumference and HDL cholesterol, and the small effect that was found is unlikely to be due to chance.

r = 0.16 (Weak Positive Correlation). The value is close to zero, meaning the linear association is minor. The positive sign means that as abdominal circumference increases, HDL cholesterol tends to slightly increase as well.

p= 0.002 (Statistically Significant). Since p<0.05 (the common threshold), we reject the null hypothesis. The observed correlation of 0.16 is highly unlikely to have occurred by random chance.', '["There is a significant correlation between abdominal circumference and HDL cholesterol level","There is no correlation between abdominal circumference and HDL cholesterol level, and it is likely that our result is caused by play of chance","Abdominal circumference measurement may predict HDL cholesterol level","There is no correlation between abdominal circumference and HDL cholesterol level, and it is unlikely that our result is caused by play of chance"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:33:08.657Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:33:08.657Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:33:08.657Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754283703972-19', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which of the following is false?', 'The tests of significance enable the researcher to know for sure that the researcher''s analysis correct', 'In biostatistics and research methodology, statistical tests of significance can never provide absolute certainty or prove that an analysis or hypothesis is "correct" for sure.
• Hypothesis testing operates entirely on probability, measuring the strength of evidence against a null hypothesis.
• A statistically significant result (e.g., p < 0.05) simply means that the observed data or difference is highly unlikely to have occurred by pure random chance under the assumption that the null hypothesis is true. It always leaves open a margin of uncertainty.

• Option A is TRUE: Inferential statistics deal purely with mathematical probability, not certainty. There is always a non-zero risk that your conclusions are false positives or false negatives.
• Option B is TRUE: There is an inverse mathematical trade-off between the two types of errors. If a researcher strictly lowers the significance level (α, the probability of a Type I error) from 0.05 to 0.01, the standard for rejecting the null hypothesis becomes much harder to meet. This automatically increases the probability of committing a Type II error (β, missing a real effect).
• Option C is TRUE: Parametric tests (like the t-test or ANOVA) carry strict assumptions about data structure, requiring variables to be continuous and measured on an interval or ratio scale, alongside approximately normal distributions. Non-parametric tests are used for nominal or ordinal data.', '["The tests of significance deal with probability not certainty","The tests of significance enable the researcher to know for sure that the researcher''s analysis correct","Generally speaking, a parametic test of significance should be used when the data represent interval or ratio scale","As a researcher decreases the chances of committing a Type I error, the researcher increases the probability of committing a Type II error"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T14:09:40.532Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:09:40.532Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:09:40.532Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754283816051-20', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The first president of the Dietetic Association of the Philippines:', 'Presentation Perez', 'Presentation Perez - first president of the Dietetic Association of the Philippines.

• Preciosa Irma Florentin - established the first dietetic internship program in the Philippines; the first hospital-based Nutrition Clinic; and the first metabolic unit at the Philippine General Hospital (PGH) in 1952.
• Adelisa Ramos - first RND head of DOH Nutrition Service
• Tecla San Andres - first woman in the Philippines to top the Bar Examinations for law graduates', '["Presentation Perez","Preciosa Irma Florentin","Adelisa Ramos","Tecla San Andres"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T14:11:31.342Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:11:31.342Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:11:31.532Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754283970343-21', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A function of public health nutritionist which focuses on assisting the community to assesses the program’s success or failure by evaluating program activities.', 'Program Evaluator', 'Program Evaluator since this function specifically involves to evaluate whether a program met its objectives by systematically assessing its activities and results. 

• Program Assessor focuses on measurement and is a more common term in educational settings. 
• Program Organizer focuses on assembling resources and stakeholders before or during implementation. 
• Program Implementer focuses on carrying out planned activities, not evaluating them afterward.', '["Program Assessor","Program Organizer","Program Implementer","Program Evaluator"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T13:42:09.435Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:42:09.435Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:42:09.435Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754284110703-22', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'It refers to a set of processes and conditions by which food is produced, processed, and stored, marketed and distributed, and prepared and consumed for proper nutrition and good.', 'Food and Nutrition system', '• Food Security - the state of having reliable access to sufficient, affordable, nutritious food.
• Food Path - the entire set of activities from farm to fork (production, processing, distribution, consumption, and waste).
• Ecology of Food and Nutrition - the complex relationship between humans, food, and the natural, social, and cultural environment.', '["Food security","Food Path","Food and Nutrition system","Ecology of Food and Nutrition"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T07:39:59.046Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:39:59.046Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:39:59.046Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754284195300-23', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'It is an art and science of promoting health thru an organized effort of improving the food and nutrition system.', 'Public Health Nutrition', 'Public Health Nutrition – narrower definition; focused on food, diet, and nutrition issues within the population context.

• Community Nutrition – narrowest definition; focused on the local implementation and tailored needs of a smaller geographic or demographic area.
• Public Health – broadest definition; encompasses all health issues (infectious disease, injury, environment, etc.).', '["Community Nutrition","Public Health Nutrition","Public Health","All of the above"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:41:04.780Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:41:04.780Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:41:04.780Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754284281262-24', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A function of public health nutritionist which focuses on assisting the community in identification of their needs and help them realizing their nutrition and nutrition-related problems.', 'Assessor', 'Assessor centers on assessment by helping the community identify and recognize its own nutrition and nutrition-related problems as a first step in program planning. 

• Organizer focuses on mobilizing resources and stakeholder. 
• Implementer focuses on carrying out planned interventions. 
• Educator focuses on transmitting knowledge and skills.', '["Assessor","Organizer","Implementer","Educator"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:31:51.852Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:31:51.852Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:31:52.064Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754284408557-25', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The main role of public health nutritionist is ____', 'Nutrition program planner and manager', 'While a Registered Dietitian-Nutritionist (RDN) can work across various fields, public health nutrition focuses specifically on populations and communities rather than individual patients.

The primary responsibility of a public health nutritionist is macro-level intervention. This includes assessing the nutritional needs of a community, designing health promotion programs, securing resources, and managing large-scale implementation to reduce disease risks across a population.', '["Nutrition program planner and manager","Diet counselor","Foodservice manager","All of the above"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T14:48:45.185Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:48:45.185Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:48:45.185Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754284605583-26', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A function of public health nutritionist which focuses on financial management and organizing the personnel who are involve in nutrition program implementation.', 'Program Administrator', 'Program administrator manages the daily operations.

• Program planner - designs the program strategy
• Program organizer - assembles necessary resources
• Program implementer - delivers the program activities', '["Program planner","Program Organizer","Program Implementer","Program Administrator"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:05:56.025Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:05:56.025Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:05:56.210Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754284704226-27', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'When was the first nutrition survey released?', '1910', 'The first nutrition survey results were released in 1910 during the American Regime, which primarily focused on investigating beriberi and its links to eating polished white rice.', '["1910","1920","1930","1940"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:32:58.823Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:32:58.823Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:32:59.030Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754284794655-28', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Who was the first secretary of Department of Health and Welfare?', 'Dr. Jose Fabella', 'Dr. Jose Fabella is a Filipino physician and public health leader, known as the "Father of Public Health" in the Philippines. He served as the first Secretary of Health.

• Dr. Francisco O. Santos - A Filipino chemist and agricultural scientist, recognized as the "Father of Human Nutrition" in the Philippines.
• Dr. Juan Salcedo, Jr. - A prominent Filipino physician, researcher, and public health advocate; he led early efforts against Vitamin B1 deficiency and served as Secretary of Health and Chairman of the National Science Development Board.
• Dr. Coronado R. Pascual - A Filipino nutritionist and physician who served as the Director of the Food and Nutrition Research Institute (FNRI) formerly NI and was a key figure in Philippine national nutrition planning.', '["Dr. Jose Fabella","Dr. Francisco O. Santos","Dr. Juan Salcedo Jr.","Dr. Coronado R. Pascual"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:27:51.688Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:27:51.688Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:27:51.889Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754284940883-29', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Who was the first president of Philippine Association of Nutrition?', 'Dr. Francisco O. Santos', 'Dr. Francisco O. Santos is a Filipino chemist and agricultural scientist, recognized as the "Father of Human Nutrition" in the Philippines.

• Dr. Jose Fabella - A Filipino physician and public health leader, known as the "Father of Public Health" in the Philippines. He served as the first Secretary of Health.
• Dr. Juan Salcedo, Jr. - A prominent Filipino physician, researcher, and public health advocate; he led early efforts against Vitamin B1 deficiency and served as Secretary of Health and Chairman of the National Science Development Board.
• Dr. Coronado R. Pascual - A Filipino nutritionist and physician who served as the Director of the Food and Nutrition Research Institute (FNRI) formerly NI and was a key figure in Philippine national nutrition planning.', '["Dr. Jose Fabella","Dr. Francisco O. Santos","Dr. Juan Salcedo Jr.","Dr. Coronado R. Pascual"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T13:06:10.273Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:06:10.273Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:06:10.448Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754285118559-30', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The primary building substance of cell is:', 'Protein', 'Protein - structure & function: acts as enzymes to catalyze reactions, builds structural components, and performs transport/movement.

• Water: for solvent & medium: provides the environment for all chemical reactions (cytoplasm) and acts as a transport mechanism.
• Fats – for boundary & energy storage: primary component of the cell membrane (boundary) and long-term energy reserve.
• Carbohydrates – for immediate energy & recognition: the cell''s primary and immediate energy source, also used for cell-to-cell communication.', '["Water","Protein","Fat","Carbohydrates"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T07:37:40.860Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:37:40.860Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:37:40.860Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754285174821-31', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The lowest level of structural organization of the living human body', 'Chemical', 'To understand the structural hierarchy of the human body, scientists view it in six increasing levels of complexity, from smallest to largest:

1. Chemical Level (Lowest): This includes atoms (such as carbon, hydrogen, and oxygen) and molecules (like water, DNA, and glucose) that combine to form the basic building blocks of life.
2. Cellular Level: Molecules combine to form cells, which are the basic structural and functional units of an organism.
3. Tissue Level: Groups of similar cells join together to perform a highly specific function (e.g., epithelial, connective, muscular, or nervous tissue).
4. Organ Level: Different types of tissues join together to form recognizable structures with specific shapes and functions (e.g., the stomach, heart, or liver).
5. System Level: Related organs connect to form an organ system with a common function (e.g., the digestive or cardiovascular system).
6. Organismal Level (Highest): All structural parts of the human body working together to create a single, living individual.', '["Cellular","Tissue","Organ","Chemical"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:55:08.925Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:55:08.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:55:09.101Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754285284600-32', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A cell region acts as a selective barrier to the movement of substances into and out of the cell.', 'Plasma membrane', 'Plasma membrane - outer boundary; controls what enters and exits the cell

• Nucleus - control center; stores DNA/Genetic Instructions.
• Cytoplasm - jelly-like fluid; holds organelles; site of metabolism
• Ribosome - protein factory; synthesizes proteins from mRNA', '["Nucleus","Cytoplasm","Plasma membrane","Ribosome"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:42:29.447Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:42:29.447Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:42:29.447Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754285374496-33', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Age period characterized by rapid differentiation and establishment of system and organs:', 'Embryonic', 'The correct answer is embryonic period during which the basic body systems and organs rapidly differentiate and form (roughly weeks 3-8 of gestation). 

The early fetal period and late fetal period are characterized more by growth and maturation of already-formed structures rather than initial organ formation. 

The neonatal period refers to the first 28 days after birth, well after organogenesis is complete.', '["Embryonic","Early fetal","Late fetal","Neonatal"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T13:40:49.420Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:40:49.420Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:40:49.617Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754285497906-34', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which is TRUE about cell growth?', 'Hyperplasia is characterized by the increase in number of cells through cell division', 'Hyperplasia is characterized by an increase in the number of cells through cell division. Choice B is false because it describes hypertrophy is actually the increase in the SIZE of existing cells, not their number.', '["Hyperplasia is characterized by the increase in number of cells through cell division","Hypertrophy is characterized by the increase in number of cells through cell division","A and B are both TRUE","A and B are both FALSE"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:08:18.635Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:08:18.635Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:08:18.635Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754285595420-35', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which is TRUE about the purpose of the menstrual cycle?', 'A and B are both TRUE', 'The menstrual cycle serves to develop and release a mature ovum (ovulation) and to prepare the uterine lining (endometrium) for potential implantation.', '["To develop and release a mature ovum","To prepare the uterus lining","A and B are both TRUE","A and B are both FALSE"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:24:14.032Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:24:14.032Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:24:14.032Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754285719099-36', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'In the female hormonal system, the source of luteinizing hormone-releasing hormone or LHRH is:', 'Hypothalamus', 'Luteinizing Hormone-Releasing Hormone (LHRH) is simply an older, synonymous name for Gonadotropin-Releasing Hormone (GnRH).

Any hormone that has the phrase "releasing hormone" in its name (such as LHRH/GnRH, TRH, CRH, and GHRH) is manufactured and secreted by the specialized nerve cells of the Hypothalamus.

The hypothalamus secretes LHRH into tiny blood vessels that travel directly to the Anterior Pituitary Gland. There, it triggers the pituitary gland to produce and release Luteinizing Hormone (LH) and Follicle-Stimulating Hormone (FSH) into general blood circulation to act on the ovaries.

• Anterior pituitary gland - GH, TSH, ACTH, FSH, LH, PRL
• Posterior pituitary gland - ADH, OT
• Ovary - estrogen, progesterone, inhibin, androgen', '["Hypothalamus","Anterior pituitary gland","Posterior pituitary gland","Ovary"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T08:44:05.232Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:44:05.232Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:44:05.423Z"'::jsonb)
