('anki-card-1754285836026-37', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The placenta is formed for different purposes EXCEPT:', 'For production of nutrients and vitamins', 'The placenta serves as the physiological lifeline between the mother and the fetus, acting temporarily as the fetus''s lungs, kidneys, gut, and liver.

• Storage: The placenta dynamically stores nutrients like glycogen, iron, and specific fat-soluble vitamins during early pregnancy to ensure a steady, regulated supply is available for the developing fetus.
• Waste Removal: It efficiently clears fetal metabolic waste products (such as carbon dioxide, urea, and uric acid) from the fetal bloodstream and transfers them into the maternal blood for excretion.
• Supply Line: Its paramount baseline function is to transfer oxygen, water, glucose, amino acids, and essential vitamins from the maternal bloodstream into fetal circulation via the umbilical cord.

The placenta cannot synthesize or manufacture nutrients and vitamins from scratch. It relies entirely on drawing these essential substances from the mother''s circulation. It does produce hormones (such as hCG, progesterone, and estrogen), but not nutrients or vitamins.', '["To supply the fetus with nutrients and oxygen","For production of nutrients and vitamins","For storage of nutrients and vitamins","For removing of fetal waste products"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:39:22.668Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:39:22.668Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:39:22.850Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754285961769-38', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A hormone secreted by the placenta that stimulates the secretion of estrogen and progesterone.', 'Chorionic gonadotropin', '• Luteinizing hormone - Anterior Pituitary Gland - triggers ovulation in women and stimulates testosterone production in men.
• Placental lactogen - modifies the mother''s metabolism to facilitate energy supply to the fetus; also stimulates mammary gland development.
• Follicle-stimulating hormone - Anterior Pituitary Gland - stimulates the growth of ovarian follicles in women and sperm production in men.', '["Luteinizing hormone","Chorionic gonadotropin","Placental lactogen","Follicle-stimulating hormone"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:31:19.837Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:31:19.837Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:31:20.039Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754286048581-39', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The nutritional requirements are increased during pregnancy to:', 'A and B are both True', 'Increased nutrient needs during pregnancy serve to support the growing fetus and other maternal tissues (such as the placenta and expanded blood volume), as well as to build maternal reserves in preparation for delivery and the subsequent demands of lactation.', '["To meet the nutrient needs of the growth fetus, other maternal tissues","To build reserves in preparation of delivery and lactation","A and B are both True","A and B are both False"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:15:01.872Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:15:01.872Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:15:01.872Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754286153962-40', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Possible consequences of iodine deficiency during pregnancy:', 'Cretinism', 'While low birth weight, stillbirth, and miscarriage can all be caused or exacerbated by severe maternal iodine deficiency, Cretinism is the most definitive, classic textbook consequence specifically caused by fetal iodine deficiency and congenital hypothyroidism.

Cretinism is an irreversible condition characterized by severe mental retardation, deaf-mutism, short stature (dwarfism), and spastic diplegia. It is uniquely linked to profound maternal and fetal iodine deficiency during critical early periods of brain development.

While options A, B, and D are broader obstetric complications that can result from many different underlying medical and nutritional issues, cretinism stands out as the direct, hallmark clinical manifestation of severe iodine deficiency disorder (IDD) in a developing fetus.', '["Low birth weight","Stillbirth","Miscarriage","Cretinism"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:48:33.550Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:48:33.550Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:48:33.859Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754286249490-41', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The following are dietary management for morning sickness during pregnancy EXCEPT:', 'Citrus juice, water, milk coffee or tea if experiencing nausea', 'Citrus juice (high acidity), water (trigger the gag reflex), milk (aggravates nausea), coffee, or tea (can stimulate stomach acid secretion) if experiencing nausea.', '["Frequent small meals","Dry toast or crackers","Citrus juice, water, milk coffee or tea if experiencing nausea","Avoidance of foods with offensive odors"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T13:46:58.805Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:46:58.805Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:46:58.995Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754286303270-42', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'What is the process of milk synthesis and secretion of the mammary gland?', 'Lactogenesis', 'Lactogenesis is the initiation/start of milk production.

Lactation is the entire, ongoing process of milk production and secretion.', '["Lactation","Lactogenesis","All of the above","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:27:57.584Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:27:57.584Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:27:57.584Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754286354951-43', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The folllowing are hormones of lactation EXCEPT:', 'Insulin', 'Insulin is associated with glucose metabolism and diabetes.

• Prolactin - stimulates milk synthesis
• Estrogen - contributes to mammary gland development
• Oxytocin - triggers the milk ejection (let-down) reflex', '["Prolactin","Estrogen","Oxytocin","Insulin"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:40:02.661Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:40:02.661Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:40:02.661Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754286521345-44', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which of the following is NOT true about human milk composition?', 'The composition of human milk is dependent of the state of the mother''s nutrition', 'The composition of human milk is dependent of the state of the mother''s nutrition: not necessarily because the composition of human milk is not entirely dependent on the mother''s diet. Human milk is remarkably stable for macronutrients (protein, carbohydrate) but highly dependent for certain micronutrients and fatty acids.', '["The composition of human milk is dependent of the state of the mother''s nutrition","Composition of human milk varies from one human to another","Human milk consists of solution of protein, sugar, and salts","The human milk is a solution in which a variety of fatty compounds are suspended"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:25:48.043Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:25:48.043Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:25:48.043Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754286704585-45', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which is true about amino acids in human milk?', 'Rich in taurine', 'Human milk is rich in taurine, an amino acid important for infant brain and retinal development that is present in relatively high concentration compared to cow''s milk. Human milk is actually lower in methionine and higher in cysteine, relatively low in phenylalanine and tyrosine compared to other protein sources.', '["Rich in taurine","Higher in methionine and lower in cysteine","High in phenylalanine and tyrosine","All of the above"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T07:44:55.987Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:44:55.987Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:44:55.987Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754286743414-46', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The human milk has a high concentration of the following minerals EXCEPT:', 'Iron', 'In maternal and child nutrition, human milk is characterized as a poor source of total iron, containing a very low absolute concentration of the mineral (approximately 0.2 to 0.4 mg/L).

Despite its low concentration, healthy full-term infants do not typically require iron supplementation during the first 6 months of exclusive breastfeeding. This is because the iron present in breast milk is exceptionally bound to lactoferrin and paired with high lactose and vitamin C levels, allowing up to 50% of it to be absorbed by the infant''s gut (compared to only ~4% absorption from cow''s milk or standard infant formula).

Calcium, Potassium, and Phosphorus are major essential macrominerals found in much higher, structural quantities in human milk to directly drive infant bone mineralization, fluid balance, and cellular development.', '["Calcium","Potassium","Iron","Phosphorus"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:05:11.671Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:05:11.671Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:05:11.671Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754286829398-47', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'An anti-infectious factor in human milk that protects the integrity of the GIT epithelium?:', 'Prostaglandins', '• Bifidus factor - feeds beneficial Bifidobacterium (probiotic); promotes healthy gut flora.
• Lactoperoxidase - kills bacteria by catalyzing the production of hypothiocyanite (antimicrobial compound)
• Lactoferrin - binds and sequesters iron, depriving harmful bacteria (which need iron to grow) of a vital nutrient.', '["Bifidusfactor","Lactoperoxidase","Lactoferrin","Prostaglandins"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:50:31.267Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:50:31.267Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:50:31.267Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754286903425-48', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which of the following conditions lead to contraindication to breastfeeding?', 'Galactosemia', 'Galactosemia - the infant''s body cannot process the galactose, it rapidly builds up in the blood and tissues, becoming toxic.

Because lactose—the primary sugar in human breast milk—breaks down into glucose and galactose, breastfeeding a baby with this condition causes toxic levels of galactose to accumulate in their body.

If breast milk is not immediately replaced with a lactose-free formula, it can rapidly lead to life-threatening complications, including liver failure, severe brain damage, cataracts, and shock.', '["Multiple births","Galactosemia","Hemorrhagic disease of the newborn","Diarrhea"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:15:12.911Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:15:12.911Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:15:13.231Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754286997920-49', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A drug that should be given to nursing mothers because of it may cause metabolic acidosis and can cause rash.', 'Aspirin', 'Aspirin (salicylates) is famous in pediatric clinical pharmacology for causing mixed acid-base disorders. High-dose maternal ingestion has documented case studies causing metabolic acidosis in nursing infants due to renal accumulation of salicylic acid.

Salicylates also carry risks of antiplatelet-induced rashes/petechiae, hypersensitivity, and the theoretical risk of Reye’s syndrome if the infant encounters a viral illness.

• Clemastine - causes drowsiness, irritability, and may reduce milk supply
• Phenobarbital - causes significant sedation, lethargy, and central nervous system (CNS) depression.
• Primidone - causes severe sedation, feeding problems, and is metabolized into phenobarbital.', '["Aspirin","Clemastine","Phenobarbital","Primidone"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:35:06.354Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:35:06.354Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:35:06.354Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754287374505-50', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which is true about brain growth and development in preschool age?', 'Brain size has reached 75% of its adult weight by age 2', 'At birth, the brain is 25% of its future adult size, and head circumference is about 14 inches (about 35 centimeters).

• By 1 year of age, the brain is 75% of its adult size. By 3 years of age, the brain is 80% of its adult size.
• By 7 years of age, the brain is 90% of its adult size (Gaber, 2019).', '["Brain size has reached 55% of its adult weight by age 2","Brain size has reached 75% of its adult weight by age 2","Brain size has reached 80% of its adult weight by age 2","Brain size has reached 90% of its adult weight by age 2"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T13:17:17.239Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:17:17.239Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:17:17.426Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754287461501-51', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'This term refers to the child who is "not up to expectation in general health"', 'Failure to thrive', 'Failure to thrive refers to poor weight gain or size deviation post-natally.

• Low birth weight - birth weight less than 2,500 grams.
• Small for gestational age - birth weight below the 10th percentile for the baby''s age.
• Premature infant - born before 37 full weeks of gestation', '["Low birth weight","Small for gestational age","Failure to thrive","Premature infant"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T07:39:21.687Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:39:21.687Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:39:21.687Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754287547462-52', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Based on the general Management of Childhood Illness (IMC) color-coded triage system, what color indicates urgent hospital referral or admission?', 'Pink', 'In the World Health Organization''s (WHO) Integrated Management of Childhood Illness (IMCI) guidelines, a distinct three-color-coded triage system is used to quickly classify a child''s illness and guide treatment protocols:

• PINK (Severe Classification): Indicates urgent hospital referral or admission. A pink row or box on the clinical chart indicates that the child exhibits general danger signs or severe symptoms (such as severe pneumonia, severe dehydration, or severe acute malnutrition). Immediate pre-referral treatment (like a first dose of antibiotics) is given before urgent transfer.

• YELLOW (Specific Outpatient Treatment): Indicates that the child needs a specific medical treatment that can be managed at an outpatient health facility. Healthcare workers prescribe oral drugs and counsel the caregiver on how to administer them at home.

• GREEN (Supportive Home Care): Indicates that the child has no signs of severe illness or conditions requiring specific medical treatments. The caregiver is given simple advice on supportive home management, such as continuous feeding and fluids.', '["Green","Yellow","Red","Pink"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:12:04.838Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:12:04.838Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:12:04.838Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754287774370-53', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The following are normal food behaviors of preschool children EXCEPT:', 'Preference for sweet and spicy', 'Preschoolers typically show a preference for sweet and mild (not spicy) flavors, and an early preference for strongly spicy foods is not a typical, expected behavior at this age.', '["Erratic appetite","Unpredictable appetite","Food rituals are common","Preference for sweet and spicy"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T12:53:35.444Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T12:53:35.444Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T12:53:35.444Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754287936298-54', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'To meet the dietary allowances of the preschool children, the following are TRUE except:', 'A and B are both True', 'Providing varied meals in amounts sufficient to satisfy appetite and offering nutritious mid-morning and afternoon snacks especially for active children are both established, evidence-based strategies for meeting preschoolers'' nutrient needs given their small stomach capacity and high activity levels.', '["Provide meals with a variety of foods in amounts sufficient to satisfy the appetite","Offering nutritious snacks in the middle of the morning and afternoon, especially to active children","A and B are both True","A and B are both False"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:50:54.494Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:50:54.494Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:50:54.494Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754288027858-55', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'One of the typical nutritional problems among preschool children characterized by loss of subcutaneous fat and gross muscle wasting:', 'PEM', 'PEM – marasmus (wasting) and kwashiorkor (edema)

• Parasitism - presence of worm; can contribute to malnutrition
• Edema – fluid retention; different or opposite-appearing presentation of PEM
• Hyperkinesis - hyper-active; unrelated to wasting', '["Parasitism","PEM","Edema","Hyperkinesis"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T12:47:59.272Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T12:47:59.272Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T12:47:59.272Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754288112021-56', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The period shortly after a slow growth period when the weight and height gains are likely to be faster than expected for age and gender.', 'Catch-up Growth', 'Catch-up growth is the accelerated growth following a period of growth faltering, allowing a child to "catch up" toward their expected growth trajectory.

Growth spurt is the period of rapid growth (such as during adolescence) without necessarily following a preceding slow-growth or deficit period.', '["Growth Spurt","Catch-up Growth","All of the above","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:36:30.285Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:36:30.285Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:36:30.462Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754288206034-57', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The protein requirement of children is:', 'Relatively higher in relation to the body weight than those in adults', 'Children''s protein requirement is relatively higher in relation to body weight than that of adults, reflecting the additional protein needed to support rapid growth, tissue building, and development during childhood.', '["Relatively higher in relation to the body weight than those in adults","Relatively lower in relation to the body weight than those in adults","A and B are both True","A and B are both False"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:08:55.659Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:08:55.659Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:08:55.974Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754288317777-58', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The process of physical development from child to adult and refers to the maturation of the body.', 'Puberty', 'Puberty is the biological process during which the body physically matures into an adult capable of reproduction, involving hormonal, physical, and sexual maturation. 

• Adolescence is the broader psychosocial and developmental life stage encompassing puberty but also including cognitive, emotional, and social development beyond just physical maturation. 
• Pubescence is a less standard/precise term sometimes used interchangeably but not the preferred technical term. 
• Maturity is too general and does not specifically denote the physical maturation process described.', '["Adolescence","Pubescence","Puberty","Maturity"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:33:40.451Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:33:40.451Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:33:40.451Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754288387960-59', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which is NOT true about brain development during school age?', 'Rapid growth of brain and head', 'The correct answer is rapid growth of the brain and head, because by school age brain growth has actually slowed considerably and is nearing completion, having occurred most rapidly during infancy and early childhood. 

Slowing down of brain/head growth and brain growth being essentially complete by school age are both accurate descriptions of this developmental stage.', '["Rapid growth of brain and head","Slowing down of growth of brain and head","Brain growth is essential complete during school age","All of the above"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:11:00.100Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:11:00.100Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:11:00.100Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754288444972-60', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'All are feeding problems prevalent in preschool-age EXCEPT:', 'Meal skipping', 'Meal skipping is more common among school children and adolescents.', '["Food jags","Dawdling","Gagging","Meal skipping"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:07:52.686Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:07:52.686Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:07:52.686Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754288620847-61', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Psychological eating disorder that is also known as "George and Purge"', 'Bulimia nervosa', 'Bulimia nervosa - cycles of binging (overeating) followed by compensatory behaviors (e.g., purging, excessive exercise).

• Anorexia nervosa - restriction leading to dangerously low body weight due to fear of fatness.
• Binge eating - recurring episodes of uncontrolled eating (binging) without compensatory behaviors.
• Pica - persistent consumption of non-food items (e.g., dirt, paint, paper).', '["Anorexia nervosa","Bulimia nervosa","Binge eating","Pica"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:31:55.029Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:31:55.029Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:31:55.225Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754288670578-62', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'All are feeding problems prevalent in adolescence EXCEPT:', 'Gagging', 'Gagging is a feeding problem prevalent among preschool children.', '["Snacking","Non-traditional eating patterns","Gagging","Meal skipping"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:03:20.976Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:03:20.976Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:03:21.187Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754288759957-63', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The following are recommendations to address obesity during adolescence EXCEPT:', 'Psychotherapy', 'Psychotherapy - this recommendation is for other professional.', '["Increased physical activity and exercise","Dietary change","Food use retraining","Psychotherapy"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T08:43:50.069Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:43:50.069Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:43:50.261Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754288839154-64', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which is true about physiologic maturity?', 'Achieved when full genetic body size is attained', 'The correct answer is that physiologic maturity is achieved when full genetic body size (adult stature/proportions) is attained, marking the endpoint of the growth process. 

Choice B is incorrect because continuous organ and tissue growth is actually characteristic of the growing, immature state, not of maturity itself, which represents growth''s completion.', '["Achieved when full genetic body size is attained","Achieved with continuous organ and tissue growth","All of the above","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T14:42:21.355Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:42:21.355Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:42:21.355Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754288882537-65', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'It refers to the person''s unique pattern of living:', 'Lifestyle', 'Lifestyle - Total way of living

• Health - state of complete physical, mental, and social well-being
• Wellness - Active pursuit of optimal health through conscious choice
• Behavior - Individual actions or reactions', '["Health","Wellness","Lifestyle","Behavior"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T12:52:12.468Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T12:52:12.468Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T12:52:12.468Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754288973598-66', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'An approach to health and well-being which focuses on identiying risk factors and prevention to minimize risk.', 'Preventive approach', 'Preventive approach: This specific model focuses directly on screening populations, identifying underlying risk factors (such as high blood pressure, genetics, or poor diet), and introducing interventions to minimize those risks before a clinical disease develops.

• Traditional approach: Often referred to as the pathogenic or biomedical model, this approach is reactive. It focuses primarily on diagnosing and treating a disease after symptoms have already manifested.
• Wellness approach: This is a holistic approach that goes beyond risk minimization. It focuses on actively optimizing positive health, well-being, and lifestyle factors (such as self-actualization, fitness, and stress management) to help an individual thrive, rather than just preventing illness.', '["Traditional approach","Wellness approach","Preventive approach","Avoidance approach"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:18:21.430Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:18:21.430Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:18:21.430Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754289078410-67', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A branch of science dealing with psychological, social, economical, physiological, and medical aspects of aging.', 'Gerontology', 'Gerontology is the broad, multidisciplinary study of the aging process. It encompasses the biological, psychological, social, economic, physiological, and even political aspects of growing old.

• Geriatrics - Medical care of elderly people and their diseases
• Healthy ageing - Maintaining functional ability and well-being throughout later life.
• Nutrigenomics - How nutrients affect genes and gene expression', '["Geriatrics","Gerontology","Healthy ageing","Nutrigenomics"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:49:47.628Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:49:47.628Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:49:47.628Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754289140209-68', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'This theory of ageing attributes aging to chemical and mechanical exhaustion of cells', 'Wear-and-tear theory', 'Wear-and-tear theory - Mechanical Deterioration

• Clinker theory - Accumulated Waste
• Somatic mutation theory - DNA Damage Accumulation
• Cross-linkage theory - Molecular Rigidity/Stiffening', '["Clinker theory","Wear-and-tear theory","Somatic mutation theory","Cross-linkage theory"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T13:39:49.718Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:39:49.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:39:49.936Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754289229987-69', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A theory of aging where cells are inactivated or defective as a result of errors in DNA replication.', 'Somatic mutation theory', '• Genetic theory - Internal Clock/Programmed
• Wear-and-tear theory - External Damage/Breakdown
• Cross-linkage theory - Molecular Rigidity/Stiffening', '["Genetic theory","Wear-and-Tear theory","Somatic mutation theory","Cross-linkage theory"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:39:19.097Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:39:19.097Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:39:19.097Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754289356713-70', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which behavior change theory/model is best to use if the community members are interested to be involved in the nutrition programs because they believe that they will benefit to the program?', 'Theory of Planned Behavior', 'The correct answer is the Theory of Planned Behavior because the scenario describes both a personal attitude/belief about benefit (attitude toward the behavior) and social influence from friends (subjective norm), the two central constructs the theory uses to predict behavioral intention.

• Precaution Adoption Process Model - Process of adopting a new precaution.
• Health Belief Model - Beliefs about risk and effectiveness.
• Theory of Planned Behavior - Intentions predict behavior.
• Self-determination Theory - quality of motivation', '["Precaution Adoption Process Model","Health Belief Model","Theory of Planned Behavior","Self-determined Theory"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:29:04.784Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:29:04.784Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:29:04.978Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754289493907-71', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'In promotion of healthy lifestyle, which behavior change theory/model is best if the community members are eager to participate in Zumba sessions because they are fond of dancing.', 'Self-determination Theory', 'Self-Determination Theory focuses heavily on the distinction between intrinsic motivation (doing an activity because it is inherently enjoyable, interesting, or fun) and extrinsic motivation (doing an activity for an external reward or out of fear).
• The Core Clue: The question stem states that community members are eager to participate because they "are fond of dancing."
• This means their drive is entirely autonomous and intrinsically motivated. SDT is the premier framework for leveraging and sustaining health behaviors that align with a person''s natural passions, autonomy, and intrinsic joy.

• Precaution Adoption Process Model - Process of adopting a new precaution.
• Health Belief Model - Beliefs about risk and effectiveness.
• Theory of Planned Behavior - Intentions predict behavior.
• Self-determination Theory - quality of motivation', '["Precaution Adoption Process Model","Health Belief Model","Theory of Planned Behavior","Self-determination Theory"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:25:15.152Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:25:15.152Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:25:15.344Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754289543572-72', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which is an example of non-verbal communication?', 'Tone of voices', 'Tone of voice conveys meaning through vocal quality and inflection rather than through words themselves, making it a classic example of paralinguistic, non-verbal communication (body language, tone, facial expression). 

Maps, traffic signals, and reports are all forms of visual or written symbolic communication that convey explicit, standardized information.', '["Tone of voices","Maps","Traffic signals","Reports"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:05:19.197Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:05:19.197Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:05:19.197Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754289645617-73', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'In conducting mental feeding to daycare students, which nutrition education material is best to use?', 'Cartoons', 'Cartoons are colorful and engaging, appropriate for children.

• Diorama - formal
• Comics - individual
• Caricature - satirical or comic effect.', '["Diorama","Comics","Caricature","Cartoons"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:03:06.045Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:03:06.045Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:03:06.045Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754289712531-74', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'It is a process of enabling people to increase control over and improve their own health status.', 'Health promotion', 'Health promotion is enabling people to increase control over and improve their health (broad term).

• Nutrition education- Teaching knowledge and skills for making healthy food choices.
• Social mobilization - Rallying all sectors (communities, leaders) to achieve a health goal.
• Social networking - Using online platforms to connect individuals and groups (often for communication/sharing).', '["Nutrition education","Social mobilization","Health promotion","Social networking"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T13:36:31.141Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:36:31.141Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:36:31.141Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754289858328-75', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'It is a process by which a community identifies its needs or objectives, gives priority to them, develops confidence and will work at them, find resources to deal with them and extends and develops cooperative and collaborative attitude and practices in the community.', 'Community organizing', 'Community organizing is building permanent, local power structures to solve problems.

• Community mobilization - Rallying all existing resources to achieve a specific goal.
• Community participation - Involvement of members in planning and implementation of a project.
• Community empowerment - Gaining control by community members over the factors affecting their lives.', '["Community mobilization","Community organizing","Community participation","Community empowerment"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:07:55.697Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:07:55.697Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:07:55.697Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754289969155-76', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which of the following is an example of alliance building?', 'Convening the key persons that can contribute to the implementation of the program', 'The best answer is convening key persons who can contribute to program implementation, because alliance building specifically involves bringing together influential stakeholders to form a working partnership around a shared goal. 

While every item could be an answer, Letter D is the best because it includes the action and purpose.', '["Coordination to all stakeholders","Selecting interested stakeholders","Providing incentives to increase participation among stakeholders","Convening the key persons that can contribute to the implementation of the program"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:36:17.353Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:36:17.353Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:36:17.353Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754290008100-77', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which is an example of audio material?', 'Podcast', '• Video - audio visual
• Vodcast - audio visual
• Podcast - audio
• TV - audio-visual', '["Video","Vodcats","Podcast","TV"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:57:30.593Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:57:30.593Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:57:30.593Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754290070082-78', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Myers-Briggs Type indicator is an example of  ___.', 'Learning styles', 'While the Myers-Briggs Type Indicator (MBTI) is fundamentally a psychological tool designed to map personality profiles, it is heavily utilized in public health education, academic counseling, and workforce training to classify distinct learning styles.

The four primary dichotomies directly correlate with how individuals absorb, process, and retain new information:
• Extraversion (E) vs. Introversion (I): Dictates a preference for active, group-oriented learning versus reflective, independent study.
• Sensing (S) vs. Intuition (N): Reflects a preference for concrete facts and sequential learning versus abstract theories and imaginative concepts.
• Thinking (T) vs. Feeling (F): Influences whether a learner evaluates information using logical, objective analysis or personal, value-driven judgments.
• Judging (J) vs. Perceiving (P): Governs structural preferences, distinguishing those who thrive on rigid timelines and planned tasks from those who prefer spontaneous, open-ended environments.

• Behavior change theories - Transtheoretical Model (Stages of Change)
• Learning theories - Social Learning Theory (Bandura)
• Element of learning - Reinforcement', '["Behavior change theories","Learning styles","Learning theories","Element of learning"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:30:54.719Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:30:54.719Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:30:54.906Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754290157543-79', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'If you will design a nutrition education program for diabetic patients, what nutrition eduction method will you use?', 'Nutrition counselling', 'Nutrition counseling - because of individualized nutrition which is important for DM management', '["Nutrition counselling","Group discussion","Mass Media","Social marketing"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:21:08.151Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:21:08.151Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:21:08.328Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754290225424-80', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'What is an example of tertiary audience?', 'Religious leaders', 'Religious leaders are the tertiary audience since they may encounter the message; has a general interest or stake.

• Mothers of malnourished children - primary audience (directly receives and acts on the message)
• Barangay health workers - secondary (advises or influences the primary audience)
• Daycare workers - secondary (advises or influences the primary audience)', '["Mothers of malnourished children","Barangay health workers","Daycare workers","Religious leaders"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:43:21.413Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:43:21.413Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:43:21.717Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754290435866-81', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'International agreement signed at the First International Conference on Health Promotion, organized by the WHO. It is the first of its type to consider all determinants of health and not just the absence of the disease.', 'Ottawa charter', 'The Ottawa Charter for Health Promotion was presented and signed on November 21, 1986, at the World Health Organization''s (WHO) First International Conference on Health Promotion in Ottawa, Canada.

It historically expanded the definition of health by stating that it is not merely the objective of living or the absence of disease, but a positive concept and resource for everyday life emphasizing social, personal, and physical capacities.

The agreement shifted public health focus heavily toward the determinants of health, identifying fundamental prerequisites such as peace, shelter, education, food, income, a stable ecosystem, and sustainable resources.

• Zero Hunger Challenge - End hunger, malnutrition, and unsustainable food systems globally.
• Rome Declaration - Commitments to eliminate food insecurity and poverty (outcome of WFS).
• World Food Summit - Major UN conference aimed at eradicating hunger worldwide and ensuring food security', '["Zero Hunger challenge","Ottawa charter","Rome Declaration","World Food Summit"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T07:57:18.802Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:57:18.802Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:57:19.121Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754290513727-82', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'What is the element of learning that involves preparedness of a person to handle change in behavior?', 'Readiness', 'Readiness is the preparation or willingness (physical or mental) to learn or act, i.e., being motivated to study for an exam.

• Situation - stimulus or context that initiates a behavior, i.e. seeing a tempting dessert.
• Interpretation - meaning or understanding assigned to the situation; “That dessert is a reward" OR "That dessert is unhealthy."
• Reaction to thwarting - behavioral response to obstacles preventing goal achievement, i.e. getting angry when a recipe fails.', '["Situation","Interpretation","Reaction to thwarting","Readiness"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:21:44.110Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:21:44.110Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:21:44.313Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754290578474-83', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', '"I can exercise" in social psychological theory is an example of:', 'Self-efficacy', '• Subjective norm - "My friends think I should run this marathon."
• Goal intention - "I intend to lose 10 pounds."
• Facilitating condition - Having a nearby gym or readily available healthy food.', '["Subjective norm","Self-efficacy","Goal intention","Facilitating condition"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:41:36.199Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:41:36.199Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:41:36.199Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754290640908-84', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Something that would prevent an individual from carrying out a recommended response or action.', 'Barrier', 'Barrier is an obstacle or cost preventing the desired action.

• Threat - perceived severity and susceptibility to a health problem.
• Fear - emotional response to a perceived danger or threat.
• Intention - commitment or plan to perform a specific behavior.', '["Threat","Fear","Barrier","Intention"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T13:39:16.041Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:39:16.041Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:39:16.041Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754290725887-85', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which type of audience/s include/s individual or group whom you want to directly reach and influence with your messages?', 'Primary audience', 'Primary audience - group directly targeted and influenced by a nutrition education message.

Secondary audience – those who advise or influence the primary audience rather than being directly targeted themselves.

Tertiary audience - those with only a general interest or indirect connection to the message.', '["Primary audience","Secondary audience","Tertiary audience","All of the above"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 3, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-05T08:52:12.849Z","interval":7,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:52:12.849Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:52:13.045Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754290786615-86', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which is an authoritative teaching procedure?', 'Lecture', '• Symposium - conference
• Group discussion - dialogue
• Open forum - questioning', '["Symposium","Group discussion","Lecture","Open Forum"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:54:00.279Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:54:00.279Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.972Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:54:00.458Z"'::jsonb)
