('anki-card-1754292744393-111', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Under the mandatory food fortification program, cooking oil is fortified with:', 'Vit A', 'See RA 8976 (Philippine Food Fortification Act of 2000):

A. Vitamin A – oil, sugar
B. Iron – rice
C. Iodine - salt
D. Vitamin A and iron - wheat flour', '["Vit A","Iron","Iodine","Vit A and Iron"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:52:31.898Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:52:31.898Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:52:31.898Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754292812642-112', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which age group is the target in Operation Timbang Plus', '0-59 months', 'Operation Timbang (OPT) Plus is the regular child growth assessment of all children 0-59 months old conducted annually in all barangays in the country to identify and locate families with malnourished preschool children and determine the overall nutrition situation in the area. It also involves planning, follow-up, and data quality check.

See reference here: https://nnc.gov.ph/plans-and-programs/philippine-nutrition-surveillance-system-pnss/operation-timbang-plus-otp/', '["0-11 months","0-23 months","0-35 months","0-59 months"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T07:38:28.282Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:38:28.282Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:38:28.282Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754292867155-113', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Who is NOT a member of the Operation Timbang Plus team?', 'Mayor', 'The correct answer is the Mayor, who serves in a broader local governance and oversight role as chair of the local nutrition committee. BHW, BNS, and DCW are all members of the OPT Plus team.

See reference here: https://nnc.gov.ph/plans-and-programs/philippine-nutrition-surveillance-system-pnss/operation-timbang-plus-otp/', '["Barangay health worker","Barangay nutrition scholar","Day care worker","Mayor"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T14:46:41.641Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:46:41.641Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:46:41.641Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754292942302-114', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'This program involves the provision of pharmaceutical preparations of vitamins and minerals.', 'Micronutrient Supplementation', 'Micronutrient supplementation, defined specifically as providing vitamins and minerals in pharmaceutical form (such as capsules, syrups, or tablets) directly to individuals.

Food fortification instead adds nutrients to commonly consumed foods during processing. Livelihood assistance and food production are indirect, food-security-oriented interventions.', '["Food Fortification","Micronutrient Supplementation","Livelihood Assistance","Food Production"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:33:51.786Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:33:51.786Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:33:51.987Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754293049914-115', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'This relates to the process by which the nutritional quality of food crops is improved through agronomic practices, conventional plant breeding, or modern biotechnology.', 'Biofortification', 'The correct answer is biofortification, specifically defined by improving the nutrient content of crops themselves through agricultural or breeding methods (such as Golden Rice enriched with vitamin A precursor).

See reference here: https://www.who.int/tools/elena/bbc/biofortification', '["Mandatory fortification","Voluntary fortification","Biofortification","Food fortification"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T14:14:36.128Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:14:36.128Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:14:36.128Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754293131141-116', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', '____ is an information-sharing type of activity that provides nutrition information to 10-12 participating mothers who are seated in a circular position', 'Pabasa sa nutrisyon', 'Pabasa sa Nutrisyon (PSN) is an information-sharing nutrition education initiative developed by the Nutrition Center of the Philippines (NCP). It is traditionally formatted as a community course where small groups of around 10 to 12 target mothers or caregivers sit in a circular arrangement to comfortably read, learn from standard nutritional guidelines, and share personal child-rearing experiences.

• Nutribus - 1980’s Nutrition Education using a bus.
• TCP - Teacher Child Parent Approach - The Teacher-Child-Parent approach to nutrition is a collaborative strategy where teachers, parents, and other community members work together to promote and improve children''s nutrition through consistent education and support
• Kumare - (Kalusugan para Umunlad si Mare) is a maternal health program designed to improve the delivery of much-needed iron supplements to pregnant women. This approach increases the number of prenatal visits, the number of iron tablets consumed, and improved hemoglobin levels. The intervention is anchored on training and re-orientation of health workers by giving them more responsibility for the mothers in their catchment area.', '["Nutribus","Pabasa sa nutrisyon","TCP","Kumare"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:17:05.810Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:17:05.810Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:17:06.133Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754293198155-117', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which is a livelihood assistance program?', 'Lingap sa mahirap', 'Lingap sa Mahirap: A historical, comprehensive poverty alleviation fund introduced during the Estrada administration targeting the 100 poorest families in every province and city to deliver integrated social welfare packages.

• Tindahan Natin Program (TNP): This is a national government initiative implemented by the Department of Social Welfare and Development (DSWD). It serves as a livelihood assistance and job generation project alongside working as a targeted food price subsidy. It provides micro-financing and starter capital for low-income individuals, barangay councils, or community groups to set up small grocery stores (tindahan) that sell low-priced, quality food items like NFA rice and noodles.
• Ginintuang Masaganang Ani: An overarching agricultural modernization program run by the Department of Agriculture (DA) focused on boosting crop productivity, farm technology, and national food sufficiency.
• Sustansya para sa Masa: A multi-sectoral national movement launched to combat malnutrition through public food fortification strategies, such as adding Vitamin A to localized products.', '["Ginintuang masaganang ani","Lingap sa mahirap","Sustansya para sa masa","Tindahan natin"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:38:39.302Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:38:39.302Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:38:39.302Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754293288222-118', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'What is/are the priority foods source/s during the early emergency period?', 'Water and Calories', 'Water and calories are the two most immediately life-sustaining priorities in the very early phase of an emergency response. 

• Water alone is insufficient because caloric/energy needs are also urgently critical for survival. 
• Adding protein and further adding fat reflect priorities that become important slightly later, as the emergency response matures beyond the immediate survival phase into more complete dietary support.', '["Water","Water and Calories","Water, Calories, and Protein","Water, Calores, Protein, and Fat"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:01:23.598Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:01:23.598Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:01:23.598Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754293357865-119', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which CMAM component treats children with SAM with poor appetite or medical complications?', 'Inpatient care', 'Inpatient care, which is specifically designated within the Community-based Management of Acute Malnutrition (CMAM) framework for children with severe acute malnutrition (SAM) who present with poor appetite (failed appetite test) or medical complications requiring more intensive, facility-based treatment. 

• Outpatient care is instead used for SAM children who pass the appetite test and have no medical complications, allowing home-based management with ready-to-use therapeutic food.
• Home care and community care are not standard, formally defined CMAM components matching this specific clinical criterion.', '["Inpatient care","Outpatient care","Home care","Community care"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:58:35.422Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:58:35.422Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:58:35.607Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754293495908-120', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Characterized mainly by a program already prepared by a group external to a community or environment. It may also mean top-down approach which is characterized mainly by the formulation of a plan at a higher level (e.g. national level), for implementation at a lower level (e.g. municipality or barangay).', 'Pre-Determined planning', 'Pre-determined planning is defined as a top-down approach where plans are formulated at a higher level (e.g., national) for implementation at a lower level (e.g., barangay), without the community''s initial input into design. 

• Self-determined planning instead involves the community itself formulating its own plan. 
• Joint planning involves collaboration between external and community stakeholders together. 
• Strategic planning refers to a broader planning methodology focused on long-term goal-setting.', '["Self-Determined planning","Pre-Determined planning","Joint planning","Strategic planning"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T07:48:55.869Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:48:55.869Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:48:55.869Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754293672217-121', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The following are characteristics of nutrition-oriented development planning EXCEPT:', 'Malnutrition is merely a problem of food consumption and availability', 'Nutrition-oriented development planning explicitly recognizes malnutrition as a complex, multi-causal problem, not one reducible to just food consumption/availability alone. 

Nutrition being included as an objective integrated into development planning, diagnostic analysis used to identify causes, and nutrition actions applied across local/national and sectoral plans are all genuine, defining characteristics of this planning approach.', '["Malnutrition is merely a problem of food consumption and availability","Nutrition is included as an objective and integrated into development planning","Diagnostic analysis is used in identifying cause of malnutrition","Nutrition actions are applied in local and national levels; and in sectoral development plans"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:02:35.289Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:02:35.289Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:02:35.605Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754293803929-122', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Mechanism for planning, implementing, monitoring, evaluating, and coordinating the local plans of action for nutrition at the province, city/municipality, and barangay levels.', 'Local Nutrition Committees', 'Local Nutrition Committees (LNCs) serve as multi-function coordinating role across all local government levels in the Philippines, chaired by the respective local chief executive, and the basic functional unit of the nutrition program implementation and management.

See more here: https://nnc.gov.ph/mindanao-region/lnc-the-basic-functional-unit-of-the-nutrition-program/', '["Local Nutrition Committees","Local Nutrition Action Officers","Local Development Coordinators","Local Development Planning Team"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:29:34.922Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:29:34.922Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:29:35.140Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754293882457-123', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Local nutrition committees are chaired by the following local chief executives, EXCEPT:', 'Congressmen', 'Congressmen are national legislative officials, not local chief executives, and therefore do not chair Local Nutrition Committees. 

Barangay Captains, Mayors, and Governors are all local chief executives who chair LNCs at their respective barangay, city/municipal, and provincial levels.', '["Barangay Captains","Mayors","Governors","Congressmen"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:19:00.812Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:19:00.812Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:19:00.812Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754294137080-124', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Local nutrition action plans (LNAP) serves as the mechanism to achieve nutrition goals at the city/municipal/provincial level. It should be harmonized in the local development system and plans, EXCEPT:', 'Environmental Impact Assessment', 'Environmental Impact Assessment is a project-specific environmental review process, not one of the standard local development planning documents that the Local Nutrition Action Plan (LNAP) is meant to be harmonized with. 

The Comprehensive Land Use Plan, Executive Legislative Agenda, and Comprehensive Development Plan are all standard local government planning documents that the LNAP should align with to ensure nutrition is mainstreamed into broader development planning and budgeting processes.', '["Comprehensive Land Use Plan","Environmental Impact Assessment","Executive Legislative Agenda","Comprehensive Development Plan"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T08:20:34.639Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:20:34.639Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:20:34.962Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754294224925-125', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Focal persons for nutrition at the local levels are:', 'BNS, CNAO, MNAO, PNAO', 'Regional nutrition focal points/officers serve national/sub-national levels.

• BNS, CNAO, MNAO, PNAO, RNAO - national level
• BNS, CNAO, MNAO, PNAO, RNPC - national level
• BNS, CNPC, MNPC, PNPC, RNPC - national level', '["BNS, CNAO, MNAO, PNAO, RNAO","BNS, CNAO, MNAO, PNAO, RNPC","BNS, CPNC, MNPC, PNPC, RNPC","BNS, CNAO, MNAO, PNAO"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:24:00.428Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:24:00.428Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:24:00.428Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754294321520-126', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'In preparing for program planning and management, the first step is:', 'Identifications/mobilization of LNC or planning core group', 'Establishing the group responsible for leading the planning process is the necessary first step before any assessment, goal-setting, or plan preparation can occur. 

Assessment or diagnostic analysis, setting goals and objectives, and preparing the plan of operation are all important subsequent steps, but they require an organized planning group to already be in place to carry them out.', '["Assessment or Diagnostic Analysis","Setting of goals and objectives","Identifications/mobilization of LNC or planning core group","Preparation of plan of operation"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T13:42:57.936Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:42:57.936Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:42:58.141Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754294432383-127', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Re-planning is a necessary step in nutrition program planning and management. In doing so, the following are revisited:', 'All of the above', 'Re-planning revisits the nutrition situation, the goals and objectives, and the strategies for targeting and implementing interventions together. Re-planning is triggered by monitoring and evaluation findings that suggest the current approach needs adjustment, and effective re-planning requires reassessing the full planning cycle.', '["Nutrition situation","Goals and objectives","Strategies in targeting for and implementation of nutrition interventions","All of the above"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T12:53:08.968Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T12:53:08.968Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T12:53:08.968Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754294555427-128', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'In nutritional assessment, causes of malnutrition must be classified into immediate, underlying and basic causes. Food insecurity and poor child care are classified as:', 'Underlying causes', 'Underlying causes – contributing causes; food security, health services, practices

• Immediate causes – direct causes; food and care (individual level)
• Basic causes – societal; political, economic, education etc.
• Cross-cutting causes', '["Immediate causes","Underlying causes","Basic cause","Cross-cutting causes"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T14:10:36.759Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:10:36.759Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:10:36.759Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754294663254-129', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Key decisions for implementation of nutrition programs/projects/activities such as continue with or without modification; stop the implementation; replace with new interventiion are done in what phase/step of program management?', 'Re-planning', 'Re-planning is a specific decision types (continue, modify, stop, or replace an intervention) made once monitoring and evaluation data reveal how a program is performing. 

• Assessment and plan preparation occurs before implementation and does not involve adjusting an ongoing program. 
• Implementation is the execution phase itself. 
• Monitoring and evaluation generates the data that informs these decisions but is technically the data-gathering step preceding the actual re-planning decision-making.', '["Assessment and plan preparation","Implementation","Re-planning","Monitoring and Evaluation"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:35:03.365Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:35:03.365Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:35:03.583Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754294765749-130', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A method of delivering goods and/or services to a selected group of individuals or households rather than to every individual or household in the population.', 'Targeting', 'Targeting is defined as directing program benefits to a specifically selected subgroup rather than universally to the entire population. 

• Prioritizing of beneficiaries is a related but broader concept describing the ranking of need, not the delivery mechanism. 
• Sampling refers to a research/survey selection method, not a program service delivery approach. 
• Identification and selection of clients is part of the targeting process but does not capture the full definition of the delivery method as precisely as "targeting" does.', '["Prioritizing of beneficiaries","Sampling","Identification and selection of clients","Targeting"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T13:52:15.731Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:52:15.731Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:52:15.923Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754294871679-131', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Depends on decision-making structures at the community level to allocate program goods or services effectively according to the criteria as defined in the program objectives.', 'Community-based', 'Community-based uses local knowledge and consensus (e.g., councils) to select beneficiaries.

• Administrative - uses official records and pre-determined criteria (e.g., income data, public registries).
• Self-targeting - uses program design (e.g., low-quality food, hard labor requirement) to make the benefit unattractive', '["Administrative","Community-based","Self-targeting","Market-based"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T12:55:51.323Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T12:55:51.323Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T12:55:51.502Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754294999358-132', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'It is the regular and periodical follow-up of the implementation of planned activities and progress to determine whether steps in the strategy are followed and whether program objectives by phase or activity are attained as planned.', 'Monitoring', 'Monitoring is tracking progress and resource use against plans, usually ongoing and internal.

• Systematic Assessment of Progress (SAP) - structured, periodic check to see if short-term goals are being met and whether the project logic remains sound
• Evaluation - determining relevance, effectiveness, impact, and efficiency of the project, often periodic or end-of-cycle
• Sustainability - ensuring benefits continue after the program''s funding or external support ends', '["Monitoring","Systematic Assessment of Progress","Evaluation","Sustainability"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:52:22.872Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:52:22.872Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:52:22.872Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754295080469-133', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Information which is used to measure changes which occur during course of program it allows one to monitor the progress of the program or it is a measure of progress towards meeting a program''s objectives', 'Indicators', 'Indicators are specific, measurable values that show the status or progress toward a desired result or goal.

• Data - raw, unorganized facts and figures
• Records - stored, organized sets of data about a specific entity
• Criteria - standards or principles used to judge, classify, or make a decision (e.g., age, income level).', '["Data","Records","Criteria","Indicators"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:45:08.653Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:45:08.653Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:45:08.841Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754295192634-134', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'It refers to the changes in the condition of the target population which generally reflect the primary objectives of the project or program, e.g. percent improvement in the prevalence of stunting in the municipality.', 'Impact indicator', 'Impact indicator - measures long-term, ultimate changes in well-being or the environment (e.g., reduced mortality rates, national poverty reduction)

• Input indicator - measures resources put into a program (e.g., funds spent, staff hired)
• Output indicator - measures direct, tangible results of program activities (e.g., training sessions held, meals served)
• Outcome indicator - measures changes in behavior, knowledge, or condition achieved by the target group (e.g., improved hygiene practices, increased enrollment)', '["Input indicator","Output indicator","Outcome indicator","Impact indicator"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T08:37:21.574Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:37:21.574Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:37:21.766Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754295288077-135', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'It shows how inputs or resources invested in the project are transformed through a series of sequential processes into outputs; helpful in monitoring ongoing projects or activities.', 'Process evaluation', 'Process evaluation - assessing how the program was implemented and managed (efficiency, quality).

• Ex-ante evaluation - assessing potential before program starts (feasibility, relevance).
• Ex-post evaluation - assessing actual results/impact after program ends (overall success).
• Result evaluation - assessing what the program achieved (outcomes, effects, and impact).', '["Ex-ante evaluation","Ex-post evaluation","Process evaluation","Result evaluation"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T13:24:34.247Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:24:34.247Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:24:34.247Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754295389422-136', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'In process evaluation, the following questions will be addressed, EXCEPT:', 'What will be the result of this project?', 'The question "what will be the result of this project?" belongs to result evaluation, which focuses on outcomes and impact, not process evaluation, which focuses on implementation quality and efficiency.', '["Are we doing our job well?","What can we be improved upon in the project?","Are we spending resources properly?","What will be the result of this project?"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T14:55:54.648Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:55:54.648Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:55:54.842Z"'::jsonb)
