('anki-card-1755585768527-49', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609155594-1790433139836-6hvft', 'Milk which undergoes a mechanical process in order to break up fat globules and prevent them from coalescing is called:', 'Homogenized milk', 'Homogenization is a process where milk is forced through a fine filter under high pressure to break up the fat globules into smaller sizes. This process helps to distribute the fat evenly throughout the milk, preventing cream from rising to the top and creating a smoother texture.

• Skimmed milk refers to milk from which most of the fat has been removed
• Evaporated milk has had about 60% of its water content removed by evaporation
