Sentence B: Oxidative rancidity is more prone in oils with high saturated fatty acids.', 'Sentence A is correct', 'Hydrogenation can help in reducing oxidative rancidity by converting unsaturated fats, which are more prone to oxidation, into more stable saturated fats. This makes the statement correct to an extent since hydrogenated fats are less likely to undergo oxidative rancidity compared to their unsaturated counterparts.

This statement is incorrect because oxidative rancidity primarily affects oils high in unsaturated fatty acids, not saturated fatty acids. Saturated fats are more stable and less likely to oxidize.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-08-30T20:00:00.000Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.839Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:32:00.423Z"'::jsonb),
