('anki-card-1756168447789-9', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'The cost incurred by an operation that includes rent, depreciation, utlities, etc.', 'Operating cost', 'Operating or overhead costs are costs other than food and labor. This includes utilities, repairs and maintenance, cleaning materials, rent, depreciation, taxes, insurance, etc.', '["Operating cost","Labor cost","Fixed cost","Food cost"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-19T20:00:00.000Z","interval":49,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T16:35:55.131Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756168517884-10', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'It refers to all conditions and measures necessary to ensure safety and suitability of food at all stages of the food chain.', 'Food hygiene', 'Food hygiene comprises conditions and measures necessary for the production, processing, storage, and distribution of food designed to ensure a safe, sound, and wholesome product fit for human consumption.', '["Food hygiene","Food safety","Food sanitation","HACCP"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-16T20:00:00.000Z","interval":46,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T16:37:48.017Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756168564418-11', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'As business volume increases, variable cost will:', 'Increase', 'Variable costs cover COGS; the more you sell, COGS also increases and other costs tied up in production.', '["Increase","Decrease","Remain constant","No longer recorded"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","interval":45,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T16:36:54.645Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756168608799-12', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'Term in marketing that describes sales promotion:', 'Merchandising', 'Merchandising is the activity of promoting the sale of goods, especially by their presentation in retail outlets.', '["Merchandising","Branding","Benchmarking","None of the choices"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-22T20:00:00.000Z","interval":52,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T16:41:12.189Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756168658010-13', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'Food service system utilized in most coffee shops like Dunkin Donuts:', 'Assembly', 'Dunkin Donuts practices off premise food production and the food are usually just assembled, heated before service. This is a characteristic of assembly/serve foodserving system.', '["Assembly","Conventional","Commisary","Ready prepared"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","interval":51,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T16:41:27.514Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756168725144-14', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'If the actual cost of a whole cake is P500, having a yield of 10 slices, and selling price is P90 per slice, what is the food cost percentage?', '55.6%', '(500/(90*10))*100', '["55.6%","5.56%","18%","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-18T20:00:00.000Z","interval":48,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T16:36:14.929Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756168798590-15', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'Basic rules in integrated pest management:', 'All of the above', 'All of the above', '["Deny pest access to facility","Deny pests food, water, and hiding or nesting place","Work with licensed and registered pest control operator","All of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-16T20:00:00.000Z","interval":46,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756168871837-16', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'HACCP stands for:', 'Hazard Analysis Critical Control Point', '', '["Hazardous Action Critical Concepts Plan","Hazard Actions Cautious Controls Point","Hazard Analysis Control Center Plan","Hazard Analysis Critical Control Point"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-22T20:00:00.000Z","interval":52,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756168903852-17', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'The largest controllable cost incurred in a foodservice unit is:', 'Food', 'Food cost is the percentage of total sales spent onf food products. This usually ranges from 40-45% of all the costs and it under the control of the owner/manager.', '["Food","Labor","Operation","Utilities"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-21T20:00:00.000Z","interval":51,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T16:41:42.874Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756168980834-18', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'In terms of pricing, breakfast combo meals could be classified under this type of menu:', 'Table d''hote', 'The main difference between a la Carte and table d hote is that the à la Carte is a menu type having a wide variety of courses that are individually priced whereas the table d’hôte is a menu type usually with a set number of courses, all for a set price.', '["Table d''hote","Ala carte","Du jour","Semi-ala carte"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-19T20:00:00.000Z","interval":49,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T16:40:43.813Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756169030896-19', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'Considered the Father of Industrial Catering.', 'Robert Owen', 'In the 1800s, Robert Owen put up a kitchen and eating room for his workers starting the idea of employee meal subsidy thus he is referred to as the Father of Industrial Catering (Scotland).', '["Robert Owen","Escoffier","Boulanger","Alexis Soyer"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-20T20:00:00.000Z","interval":50,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T16:40:26.771Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756169070259-20', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'Areas wherein closely related task are done by a person or persons.', 'Work center', 'Work center is the basic unit in a layout. Thus, these are areas wherein closely related tasks are done by a person or persons.', '["Work center","Work area","Section","Layout"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:50:56.931Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:50:56.931Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:50:57.129Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756169123407-21', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'Which is not a factor choice of distribution system?', 'Consumer''s capacity to pay', 'In foodservice systems management, selecting the appropriate distribution and delivery system (the method of getting cooked food from the kitchen to the point of service) is an operational and architectural decision. It is dictated by structural, physical, and logistical factors within the establishment:

• Type of foodservice system: Whether an operation is Conventional, Commissary, Ready-Prepared, or Assembly/Serve directly dictates the assembly and distribution infrastructure required.
• Size and layout of the facility: A multi-story hospital or large campus requires decentralized distribution (e.g., using rethermalization carts or satellite pantries), whereas a compact single-room diner can use a simple centralized counter distribution system.
• Style of service: Self-service cafeterias, tray service, banquets, and vending machines each require distinct holding, temperature control, and physical transport distribution methods.

While the target consumer''s financial capacity heavily influences menu pricing, decor tiering, food service classifications, and ingredient sourcing, it does not mechanically alter or dictate the internal engineering or logistical choice of the physical distribution system inside the facility.', '["Type of foodservice system","Size and lay out of facility","Style of service","Consumer''s capacity to pay"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:52:15.043Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:52:15.043Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:52:15.043Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756169166923-22', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'Income less cost of good sold is known as the:', 'Gross profit', 'Gross Profit = Sales/Income - Cost of Goods Sold (COGS)

To arrive at Net Profit/Loss, the operating expenses and other applicable expenses (such as interest and taxes) are then deducted from the gross profit: Sales/Income – COGS = Gross Profit 

Gross Profit – Operating and Other Expenses = Net Profit/Loss', '["Gross profit","Net profit/loss","Food cost","Prime cost"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:52:47.839Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:52:47.839Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:52:47.839Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756169221053-23', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'System that identifies specific hazard and measures for their control to ensure the safety of food.', 'HACCP', 'HACCP stands for Hazard Analysis and Critical Control Points which is a systematic system that identifies specific hazards and measures for their control to ensure food safety. This focuses more on prevention rather than relying mainly on end-product testing.', '["HACCP","Codex","Food safety","GMP"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:52:54.953Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:52:54.953Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:52:54.953Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756169252803-24', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'Another name for family style of service.', 'Compromise', 'Family or compromise style of service is a compromise between the Russian and English styles; some foods are served directly from the kitchen on individual dishes and some are served at the table. It is best used in small groups, not more than eight.', '["Compromise","Continental","English","Apartment"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-01T20:00:00.000Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T16:42:29.819Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756170100698-25', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'Japanese style of management in which workers are seen as the key to increased productivity:', 'Theory Z', 'William Ouchi’s Theory Z makes certain assumptions about workers. One assumption is that they seek to build cooperative and intimate working relationships with their coworkers. In other words, employees have a strong desire for affiliation. Another assumption is that workers expect reciprocity and support from the company. 

According to Theory Z, people want to maintain a work-life balance, and they value a working environment in which things like family, culture, and traditions are considered to be just as important as the work itself. Under Theory Z management, not only do workers have a sense of cohesion with their fellow workers, they also develop a sense of order, discipline, and a moral obligation to work hard. 

Finally, Theory Z assumes that given the right management support, workers can be trusted to do their jobs to their utmost ability and look after for their own and others’ well-being.', '["Theory Z","Theory X","Theory Y","Total Quality Management"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-01T20:00:00.000Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T16:26:16.259Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756170155445-26', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'Breakdown of task into organized activity considering time and sequence of operation:', 'Work schedule', 'Work schedule – an outline of work to be performed, procedures to be used, and time schedule for a particular position. Workers may be scheduled successfully only after thorough analysis and study of the jobs to be done, the working conditions, and the probable efficiency of the employees.', '["Work schedule","Organizational chart","Daily Tally sheet","Evaluation sheet"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:53:17.371Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:53:17.371Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:53:17.371Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756170213857-27', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'A collection of data about the market and other factors. It is conducted to determine if the project is worth pursuing.', 'Feasibility study', 'A feasibility study is acollection of data about the market and other factors. It is conducted to determine if the project is worth pursuing. It includes: The Prospectus, Research on the proposed site, Design trends, Market research, Community growth, Competition in the area, Financial goals, and Standard Operating Procedures.', '["Feasibility study","Market survey","Market acceptability","Consumer demand survey"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:53:22.818Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:53:22.818Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:53:22.818Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756170251424-28', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'Simulation type of training:', 'vestibule', 'Vestibule training is one of the on-the-job training where technical staff is trained on how to use tools and machinery by creating a simulated workplace. This training is also termed as ''near the job training'' in which a simulated work setup is created near the main production plant.', '["vestibule","on-the-job","mentoring","apprenticeship"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:53:27.155Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:53:27.155Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:53:27.155Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756170514010-29', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'According to the Labor Code of the Philippines, service charge is to be distributed as follows:', '85% for all covered employees; 15% to management', 'Service charges and pooled tips – eighty-five percent (85%) equally shared by the employees, fifteen percent (15%) retained by the management.

Although recent:
Under Article 96 of the Labor Code of the Philippines (as amended by Republic Act No. 11360 and DOLE Department Order No. 242, Series of 2024), service charges collected by hotels, restaurants, and similar establishments are distributed as follows:
• 100% Full Distribution: All collected service charges must be distributed completely and equally among covered employees. Management can no longer retain a percentage.', '["85% for all covered employees; 15% to management","90% for all covered employees; 10% to management","Equal distribution among all employees including rank-and-file and management","10% for all rank-and-file employees; 90% to management"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:53:32.463Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:53:32.463Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:53:32.463Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756170564707-30', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'This refers to the amount of product that should be on hand at any given time.', 'Par stock', 'Par Stock – amount of product that should be on hand between one delivery and the next. This represents the ideal or standard operating quantity of an item that must be physically physically present in stock at any given time to fulfill normal customer demand between delivery cycles. When stock levels drop below this baseline figure, it automatically triggers a reorder to bring the inventory back up to par.

• Minimum stock: This is the absolute safety threshold or "buffer" limit below which inventory should never fall to avoid severe stockouts or operational emergencies.
• Ending stock: The actual physical quantity of product remaining on hand at the exact conclusion of an accounting or inventory reporting period.
• Perpetual inventory: A continuous tracking method or accounting ledger system that automatically registers adjustments to stock balances in real time as items are bought or sold.', '["Par stock","Perpetual inventory","Minimum stock","Ending stock"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:54:40.960Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:54:40.960Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:54:40.960Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756170621472-31', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'Theory of management that contains the doctrine of interdependecy and wholism.', 'Systems approach', 'Systems approach has a set of interdependent parts that work together to achieve a common goal. Interdependency is the key concept in systems theory.', '["Systems approach","Classical","Contingency","Human relations"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-01T20:00:00.000Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T16:31:08.456Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756170660369-32', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'The most practical type of storage in small stores is:', 'Reach-in chiller', 'Reach-in units are used to store food products at point-of-use or used in central storage units in small operations.', '["Reach-in chiller","Blast chiller","Walk-in chiller","Chest freezer"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-01T20:00:00.000Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T16:29:05.554Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756170753585-33', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'A set of waste management practices which aims to safely and effectively handle the municipal solid waste stream with the least adverse impact on human health and the environment.', 'Integrated Solid Waste Management', 'Integrated Solid Waste Management is a set of waste management practices which aims to safely and effectively handle the municipal solid waste stream with the least adverse impact on human health and the environment. 

• Republic Act No. 9003 “Ecological Solid Waste Management Act of 2000”. 
• Zero Waste Management Strategy - aims to achieve zero waste of resources; to eliminate solid waste, hazardous waste, emissions, toxic wastes and others; to eliminate waste at source and at all points down the production and supply chains rather than management of the wastes created in the process.', '["Integrated Solid Waste Management","RA No. 9003","Reuse, Reduce, Recycle","Zero Waste Management Strategy"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:58:28.225Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:58:28.225Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:58:28.225Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756170798113-34', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'An organized list of duties, skills, and responsibilities required in a specific position.', 'Job description', 'Job description is an organized list of duties, skills and responsibilities required in a specific position. This should be written for every position and should be reviewed and updated periodically.', '["Job description","Job analysis","Job specification","Job requirements"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:58:44.685Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:58:44.685Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:58:44.685Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756170847012-35', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'A detailed floor plan showing arrangement of equipment for accomplishing work according to logical sequence of operation.', 'layout', 'Layout – a detailed floor plan showing arrangement of equipment for accomplishing work according to logical sequence of operation. It refers to the process of arranging the physical facilities which includes a design drawn on paper to show structural components such as walls, windows, door, etc.', '["layout","floor plan","blueprint","work center"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:58:55.877Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:58:55.877Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:58:55.877Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756170963755-36', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'A line type of organization is applicable to a dietary department primarily because it:', 'shows the relationship of each position in the over-all plan and function of the department', 'In dietary department, lines of authority should be clearly drawn.', '["shows the relationship of each position in the over-all plan and function of the department","provides information on the number of employees required to do each job","justifies request for additional employees for each task or work","all of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:59:16.022Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:59:16.022Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:59:16.022Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756171025120-37', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'An inventory system when an item is allowed to deplete to safety level before new order is submitted to bring up level up to maximum.', 'Minimax', 'Minimax system means that an item is allowed to deplete to safety level before new order is submitted to bring up level up to maximum.

In foodservice inventory management, the Minimax system establishes two primary stock triggers for each item: a minimum safety level (the floor) and a maximum capacity level (the ceiling). Stock is deliberately allowed to deplete until it hits that lower safety margin. Once it reaches that precise reorder point, a fresh order is generated to purchase exactly enough supply to restore the inventory back up to its defined maximum limit.

• Partially blind method: This is a technique used during physical inventory receiving where the clerk is given an invoice or PO showing the item names but with some quantities blocked out, forcing them to do a blind, independent count.
• Economic order quantity (EOQ): This is a mathematical formula used to determine the absolute most cost-effective amount of inventory to order by perfectly balancing holding costs against ordering costs. It focuses on cost optimization rather than a strict minimum-to-maximum safety cutoff loop.
• Par stock: Unlike the fluctuating buffer of the minimax system, par stock requires a set, fixed total quantity of an item to be physically present on the shelves at any given time. Every single time a replenishment order is placed, a purchase is made to bring the stock right back up to that static "par" number.', '["Minimax","Par stock","Partially blind method","Economic order quantity"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T15:03:29.093Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:03:29.093Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:03:29.093Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756171114365-38', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'According to the Labor Code of the Philippines, night shift differential means:', 'Employee compensation not less than 10% of the regular wage per hour of work between 10pm-6am', '85% for all covered employees; 15% to management', '["Employee compensation not less than 5% of the regular wage per hour of work between 11pm-5am","Employee compensation not less than 5% of the regular wage per hour of work between 10pm-6am","Employee compensation not less than 10% of the regular wage per hour of work between 11pm-5am","Employee compensation not less than 10% of the regular wage per hour of work between 10pm-6am"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:59:22.908Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:59:22.908Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756171168347-39', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'Management philosophy combining principles of quality assurance, participative management, and quality work life:', 'Total Quality Management', 'TQM is a system of management based on the principle that every staff member must be committed to maintaining high standards of work in every aspect of a company''s operations towards attaining customer satisfaction.', '["Total Quality Management","Theory X","Theory Y","Theory Z"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-01T20:00:00.000Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T16:26:30.705Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756171213345-40', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'The third step in a three-stage hand-washing dishes is:', 'Sanitizing', 'There are three parts to hand-washing dishes: wash, rinse, and sanitize. In order to accomplish all three, your facility must have a three-compartment dishwashing sink. The sink must be clean and sanitized before beginning the washing process.', '["Sanitizing","Rinsing","Drying","Air-drying"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:59:53.455Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:59:53.455Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:59:53.455Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756171263809-41', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'Under PD 856, the minimum kitchen size for a 40 m² dining area is (m²):', '10', 'Rule: The kitchen area must be at least 1/4 (25%) of the total dining area, but it cannot fall below a baseline minimum of 9.30 m² (100 sq. ft.).

Calculated Kitchen Area = 40 m² x 0.25 = 10 m²', '["10","5","15","20"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:59:57.123Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:59:57.123Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:59:57.123Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756171319039-42', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'A way of thinking that there is always a better way to eliminate any uneconomical use of resources:', 'Work simplification', 'Work Simplification is the systematic use of common sense in the quest for better and easier methods of accomplishing the work.', '["Work simplification","Motion economy","Productivity","Efficiency Performance"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T15:03:41.572Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:03:41.572Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:03:41.572Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756171408600-43', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'An unpaid form of promotion in which satisfied customers tell other people how much a product or service is favored.', 'Word-of-mouth', 'Word-of-mouth (WOM) marketing relies entirely on authentic human recommendations. It is completely unpaid because it happens naturally when satisfied customers organically share their positive experiences, reviews, or favorite products with friends, family, or colleagues.', '["Social media advertising","Personal selling","Radio commercials","Word-of-mouth"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T15:04:17.014Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:04:17.014Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:04:17.014Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756171451617-44', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'The main bases for space allocation:', 'Menu', 'Menu serves as the basis for physical factors like equipment, kitchen space, layout and sanitation.', '["Menu","Type of equipment material","Quantity of equipment","Manpower"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T15:04:21.514Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:04:21.514Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:04:21.514Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756171503981-45', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'German global online food delivery marketplace that allows customers to directly order meals online or via mobile.', 'Foodpanda', 'Foodpanda is an online food and grocery delivery platform brand owned by Delivery Hero, which is headquartered in Berlin, Germany and operates with 20 brands in about 50 countries across four continents. The Foodpanda brand, currently used in Asia, Bulgaria and Romania, was acquired by Delivery Hero in December 2016.

• Honestbee was an online grocery and food delivery service based in Singapore.
• Munchpunch is a food discovery and restaurant directory website based in the Philippines.
• AmazonFresh is a grocery delivery service owned by the American tech giant Amazon.', '["Foodpanda","Honestbee","Munchpunch","Foodpanda"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T15:04:30.510Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:04:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:04:30.510Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756171567728-46', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'Decision-making guides that are written to ensure that all actions taken by organization members are consistent with the organization''s strategy and objectives.', 'Policies', 'In organizational management and foodservice planning, policies function as comprehensive, high-level decision-making guides. Rather than telling employees exactly what to do step-by-step, they establish a reliable boundaries framework. This ensures that every independent decision or action made by staff members stays completely aligned with the company’s broad strategy, vision, and core objectives.

• Rules: These are strict, specific, and inflexible directives that dictate exactly what must or must not be done in a given situation (e.g., "No smoking in the kitchen"). They leave zero room for individual decision-making or managerial discretion.
• Operating plans: These are short-term, detailed tactical blueprints that outline specific tasks, timelines, schedules, and budgets to execute operations over a precise period (such as weekly or monthly outputs).
• Standing plans: This is a broad, overarching category of plans designed to be used repeatedly for recurring organizational activities. Standing plans include policies, procedures, and rules collectively, making it too broad of a classification to serve as the definition for a targeted decision-making guide.', '["Rules","Standing plans","Policies","Operating plans"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T15:05:26.186Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:05:26.186Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:05:26.186Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756171695272-47', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'A function of management that involves developing in broad outline the activities required to accomplish the objectives of the organization and the most effective ways of doing so. It is a continuous process and requires that management be diligent in conducting periodic reviews of all plans to ensure that they are still appropriate as conditions change.', 'Planning', 'In management theory, planning is universally recognized as the foundational function that involves determining the organization''s goals and charting out a broad outline of activities and strategies to achieve them.

Because business and environmental conditions constantly shift, planning cannot be a one-time task. It requires an ongoing, continuous process where managers regularly review, adjust, and adapt their roadmaps to ensure the organization stays on track.

• Marketing: The function focused on identifying, anticipating, and satisfying customer needs through product design, pricing, promotion, and distribution.
• Finance: The function responsible for managing the organization''s monetary resources, budgeting, and capital allocations.
• Operations: The function that deals with the daily execution, transformation of inputs into outputs, and physical manufacturing or service delivery processes.', '["Marketing","Finance","Planning","Operations"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T15:01:27.109Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:01:27.109Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:01:27.319Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756171777003-48', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'The main goal of staff orientation program:', 'communicate information and create response to the company and the job', 'Staff orientation is done to help recently hired staff in adjusting to their new employer. It gives staff members the fundamental organizational knowledge and serves as a venue for the employees to solicit responses about their new team, division, and job within the firm.', '["communicate information and create response to the company and the job","establish a system of discipline and rewards for the staff","establish training plan and method for evaluation progress","assess the reaction of other workers to the new worker"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-01T20:00:00.000Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T16:31:48.352Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756171830367-49', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'In foodservice facilities and layout, supporting services include the following, except:', 'None of the above', 'It includes all plus an area for steam hose use to wash and sanitize carts, etc.', '["None of the above","Office","Janitor''s closet/storage","Trash and waste storage"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T15:02:15.456Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:02:15.456Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:02:15.456Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757640435609-0', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609193199-1790433139825-f6c4y', 'Papain is used as:', 'Meat tenderizer', 'Papain is a proteolytic enzyme extracted from raw papaya latex that breaks down tough muscle collagen and connective tissue fibers, making it widely used commercially as a natural meat tenderizer.

• Stabilizer / Flavoring / In candy making: Papain does not function primarily as a gelling stabilizer, synthetic flavoring, or confectionery agent.', '["Stabilizer","Flavoring","In candy making","Meat tenderizer"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.234Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T05:15:50.840Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757640472665-1', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609193199-1790433139825-f6c4y', 'A carcinogenic mold present in nuts and grains:', 'Aflatoxin', 'Aflatoxin is a potent carcinogenic mycotoxin produced by molds (Aspergillus flavus and Aspergillus parasiticus) that commonly contaminate improperly stored nuts, grains, corn, and peanuts in humid tropical conditions.

• Salmonella: A pathogenic bacterium causing foodborne bacterial infection.
• Antitoxin: An antibody neutralizing specific bacterial toxins.
• Solanine: A natural toxic glycoalkaloid found in green potatoes and nightshades.', '["Aflatoxin","Salmonella","Antitoxin","Solanine"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.234Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T05:15:57.000Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757640529246-2', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609193199-1790433139825-f6c4y', '_____ is a local alcoholic beverage made from coconut sap while ______ is a fermented alcoholic beverage made from
sugar cane.', 'Tuba and Basi', 'In traditional Filipino beverages, tuba is the native alcoholic sap harvested from coconut palms (coconut toddy), while basi is the traditional fermented alcoholic beverage produced from sugarcane juice.

• Lambanog and Basi: Lambanog is distilled coconut liquor, whereas tuba is the fermented sap.
• Basi and Mirin / Mirin and Lambanog: Incorrect regional beverage pairings.', '["Lambanog and Basi","Tuba and Basi","Basi and Mirin","Mirin and Lambanog"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.234Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T05:16:03.483Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757640554843-3', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609193199-1790433139825-f6c4y', 'Chief source of commercial gelatin:', 'Hide stock and bones', 'Commercial gelatin is a translucent, colorless protein derived primarily by the thermal partial hydrolysis of collagen extracted from animal connective tissues, specifically hide stock and bones.

• Tissues / Muscles: Contain muscle proteins (myosin and actin), but commercial gelatin extraction relies on collagen-rich hides and bones.
• Seaweeds: Yield hydrocolloids like agar-agar and carrageenan, not animal gelatin.', '["Tissues","Muscles","Hide stock and bones","Seaweeds"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.234Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T05:16:10.162Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757640576443-4', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609193199-1790433139825-f6c4y', 'Spore-former food intoxication agent:', 'Staphylococcus aureus', 'Staphylococcus aureus is a leading bacterial cause of food intoxication (producing heat-stable enterotoxins), though it is not a traditional spore-former (unlike Clostridium botulinum or Bacillus cereus). However, in this specific board exam test bank key, Staphylococcus aureus is paired under toxin-mediated illness questions. (Note: Clostridium botulinum is the classic spore-forming intoxicator, but we match the exact test bank key).', '["Staphylococcus aureus","Clostridium botulinum","Shigella sonnei","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.234Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T05:16:19.974Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757640599243-5', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609193199-1790433139825-f6c4y', '_____ is a type of microorganism that can thrive in fruit juices', 'Acidophile', 'Acidophiles are acid-loving microorganisms that can thrive and multiply in low-pH, highly acidic environments such as citrus fruits, fruit juices, and pickled products.

• Alkaliphile: Organisms thriving in high alkaline (high pH) environments.
• Osmophile: Microorganisms adapted to environments with high osmotic pressure (high sugar concentrations).
• Halophile: Salt-loving microorganisms thriving in high salinity conditions.', '["Alkaliphile","Acidophile","Osmophile","Halophile"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.234Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T05:16:25.193Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757640624356-6', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609193199-1790433139825-f6c4y', 'The antioxidant Lycopene is normally present in high amounts in:', 'Dried tomatoes per 100 g', 'Lycopene is a potent carotenoid antioxidant. When tomatoes are dehydrated into dried tomatoes, water is removed, concentrating all nutrients and phytochemicals so that the lycopene content per 100 grams is dramatically higher than in fresh or standard cooked tomatoes.

• Fresh tomatoes per 100 g: Contain high water content, diluting per-100g nutrient concentration.
• Cooked tomatoes per 100 g: Cooking concentrates lycopene compared to raw, but dried tomatoes represent maximum moisture removal.
• Watermelon per 100 g: Contains lycopene, but at significantly lower concentrations than sun-dried tomatoes.', '["Dried tomatoes per 100 g","Fresh tomatoes per 100 g","Cooked tomatoes per 100 g","Watermelon per 100 g"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.234Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T05:16:31.225Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757640653889-7', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609193199-1790433139825-f6c4y', 'The following are intrinsic factors in food spoilage except for:', 'Temperature', 'Intrinsic factors influencing food spoilage are internal characteristics inherent to the food item itself—such as moisture content (aw), pH, nutrient composition, and antimicrobial constituents. Temperature is an external environmental parameter, classifying it as an extrinsic factor, making temperature the correct exception.

• Moisture content: An intrinsic physical factor affecting microbial growth.
• pH: An intrinsic chemical factor determining acidity levels.
• Available nutrients: Intrinsic nutritional composition supporting microbial metabolism.', '["Moisture content","Temperature","pH","available nutrients"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.234Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T05:16:37.280Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757640679072-8', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609193199-1790433139825-f6c4y', 'Creaming is a process involved in making:', 'Butter cake', 'Creaming is the foundational mixing method used in butter cake production, where solid fat (butter or shortening) and granulated sugar are beaten together vigorously to incorporate tiny air pockets for leavening.

• Pie crust: Utilizes the cutting-in method (incorporating cold solid fat into flour), not creaming.
• Sponge cake: Relies on whipped whole eggs or separated whipped egg whites (foam method), not fat creaming.', '["Pie crust","Butter cake","Sponge cake","All"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.234Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T05:16:43.885Z"'::jsonb)
