('anki-card-1758784001952-42', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'The best environment for storing herbs and spices is: *', 'a cool, dry place', 'Herbs and spices contain volatile aromatic essential oils that degrade rapidly when exposed to heat, light, and moisture; they should be stored in a cool, dry place in airtight containers.', '["moist place","a warm, bright place","a cool, dry place","a hot, moist place"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:54:25.928Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784009600-43', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Dehydration method most suitable for the production of instant coffee powder: *', 'spray dryer', 'Spray drying atomizes liquid coffee extract into a hot drying chamber, instantly evaporating moisture and producing fine, soluble instant coffee powder.', '["cabinet dryer","tunnel dryer","drum dryer","spray dryer"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:54:29.910Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784022116-44', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'The rancidity which results from the exposure of fat to oxygen is called: *', 'oxidative rancidity', 'Oxidative rancidity occurs when unsaturated fatty acids react with atmospheric oxygen via free radical mechanisms, producing off-flavors, peroxides, and aldehydes.

• Hydrolytic rancidity: Caused by enzymatic cleavage (lipases) releasing free fatty acids.', '["regular rancidity","hydrolytic rancidity","oxidative rancidity","flavor rancidity"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:54:34.139Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784032766-45', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Which of the following is not true about pH? *', 'It affects sourness of food.', '', '["It affects sourness of food.","It influences growth of microorganisms.","It controls many biological and chemical reactions.","It affects color brightness and stability of pigments of fruits and vegetables."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784042166-46', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'The best temperature for beating egg whites into a stable foam is: *', 'room temperature', 'Whipping egg whites into a stable, high-volume foam is best achieved at room temperature because lower surface tension allows proteins to denature and trap air more rapidly than cold refrigerator temperatures.', '["very high temperature","room temperature","lukewarm temperature","refrigerator temperature"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:54:40.349Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784052115-47', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Cross-contamination occurs when: *', 'microorganisms transfer from one food or surface to another.', 'Cross-contamination is defined as the physical transfer of harmful microorganisms or allergens from one food item, utensil, or surface to another (typically from raw foods to ready-to-eat foods).', '["delivered food is not stored immediately.","growth of microorganisms is not arrested quickly.","microorganisms transfer from one food or surface to another.","a customer experiences allergic reactions."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:54:44.036Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784061113-48', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Proper handwashing involves rubbing hands together: *', 'for at least 20 seconds', 'According to handwashing guidelines established by public health agencies (WHO/CDC), proper handwashing requires vigorously rubbing soapy hands together for at least 20 seconds.', '["for at least 15 seconds","for at least 20 seconds","until they appear clean","until nails are clean"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:54:47.113Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784070764-49', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Store raw food: *', 'below cooked and ready-to-eat food', 'To prevent cross-contamination from raw meat juices dripping downward, raw foods must always be stored on refrigerator shelves below cooked and ready-to-eat foods.', '["above cooked and ready-to-eat food","on the same shelf as cooked and ready-to-eat food","below cooked and ready-to-eat food","behind cooked and ready-to-eat food"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:54:51.057Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784099827-50', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'What is the % overrun of an ice cream with an initial ice cream mixture of 160ml and has a final yield of 280 ml? *', '75%', 'To calculate ice cream overrun percentage:

Formula = [(Final Volume − Initial Mix Volume) ÷ Initial Mix Volume] × 100. 
Given values: Initial mix = 160 ml; Final yield = 280 ml. 
Calculation = [(280 − 160) ÷ 160] × 100 = (120 ÷ 160) × 100 = 75%.', '["175%","43%","57%","75%"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:55:25.265Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784111078-51', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'A person diagnosed with this pathogen should be excluded from working in a foodservice establishment: *', 'Salmonella typhi', 'Salmonella typhi is the systemic pathogen responsible for typhoid fever; food handlers diagnosed with typhoid fever must be strictly excluded from working in foodservice establishments to prevent transmission.', '["amoeba","Anisakis simplex","Salmonella typhi","Trichinella spiralis"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:49:48.428Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784120662-52', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'A way of preventing lumps in starch cooking is to initially disperse starch in melted fat forming a _____. *', 'Roux', 'A roux is prepared by cooking equal parts flour and fat together to coat starch granules in lipid, which separates them and prevents lump formation when hot liquids are added.', '["Beurre manie","Slurry","Roux","Paste"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:55:29.895Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784130762-53', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'A safe and acceptable way to thaw a pack of frozen marinated chicken is: *', 'gradual thawing under refrigeration', 'Gradual thawing under refrigeration (4°C or below) is the safest, most approved foodservice method because it keeps perishable foods out of the "temperature danger zone" while thawing safely.', '["rapid thawing in boiling water","gradual thawing under refrigeration","gradual thawing at room temperature","gradual thawing under hot running water"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:55:34.219Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784138495-54', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Which of the following cuts of beef is best for cooking Sinigang? *', 'brisket', 'The brisket is a tougher, heavily exercised cut of beef containing abundant collagen connective tissue that breaks down during slow, moist-heat simmering, making it suitable for savory soups like sinigang.', '["chuck","picnic","brisket","rib loin"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:55:37.561Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784149210-55', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'What can precipitate the casein protein in milk? *', 'rennet', 'Rennet (containing the enzyme chymosin) specifically hydrolyzes and cleaves kappa-casein in milk, causing the destabilization and precipitation of casein protein to form solid curds during cheesemaking.', '["heat","rennet","alkaline","salt"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:55:41.205Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784157696-56', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'The process involved in removing unsaturations in fatty acids to make the fat stable. *', 'hydrogenation', 'Hydrogenation is the chemical process of reacting liquid unsaturated fatty acids with hydrogen gas under high pressure and temperature in the presence of a catalyst to saturate double bonds, stabilizing the fat into a solid or semi-solid state.', '["winterization","hydrogenation","halogenization","saponification"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:55:44.567Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784167974-57', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'When Mg++ is replaced by H+ in the chlorophyll structure, this compound is produced: *', 'pheophytin', 'When green plant tissue is heated or exposed to acid, the magnesium ion (Mg²⁺) in the center of the chlorophyll molecule is displaced by hydrogen ions (H⁺), converting bright green chlorophyll into olive-brown pheophytin.', '["chlorophyllin","porphyrin","chlorophyllase","pheophytin"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:56:38.708Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784177460-58', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'The enzyme that mediates browning reactions in fruits and vegetables. *', 'phenolase', 'Phenolase (polyphenol oxidase) is the copper-containing enzyme responsible for catalyzing the oxidation of phenolic compounds into dark melanin pigments during enzymatic browning in cut fruits and vegetables.', '["phenolase","pectinase","melanase","oxidase"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:56:42.749Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784184625-59', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'The form of pectic substance predominantly present in under ripened fruits. *', 'protopectin', 'Protopectin is the water-insoluble, highly methylated pectic substance predominantly present in firm, hard, under-ripened fruits, which progressively hydrolyzes into water-soluble pectin as fruits ripen.', '["pectinic acid","pectic acid","protopectin","prepectinic acid"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:56:46.922Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784193874-60', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'The compound responsible for the characteristic green coloration of uncooked crustaceans. *', 'ovoverdine', 'Ovoverdine is the carotenoid-protein complex composed of astaxanthin bound to a protein, responsible for the characteristic dark green or blue-green coloration of raw, unheated crustaceans (such as lobsters and crabs).', '["astaxanthin","bilirubin","ovoverdine","chlorophyllin"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:56:50.052Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784206008-61', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'The local term for taro: *', 'gabi', 'Gabi is the local Filipino term for taro (Colocasia esculenta), a starchy tuber grown for its edible corms and leaves.', '["ubi","gabi","uraro","kamote"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:56:54.830Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784214673-62', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'A storage form of phosphorus found in cereals and root crops which binds with minerals like Ca, Fe,and Zn making these minerals unavailable for utilization. *', 'phytate', 'Phytate (phytic acid) is the primary storage form of phosphorus found in the bran of cereal grains and root crops; it acts as an antinutrient by binding strongly with divalent minerals like calcium, iron, and zinc, reducing their bioavailability.', '["trypsin","linamarin","phytate","fiber"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:56:58.669Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784223156-63', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'During cooking or processing, the glycosidic bonds joining glucose molecules of starch are broken. This process is called: *', 'hydrolysis', 'Hydrolysis is the chemical reaction where glycosidic bonds joining glucose molecules in starch polymers are cleaved by water molecules in the presence of heat, acid, or enzymes (breaking starch into smaller dextrins and sugars).', '["dextrinization","syneresis","retrogradation","hydrolysis"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:57:02.275Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784231624-64', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'The function of starch in soups or gravies. *', 'as a thickener', 'Starch functions primarily as a thickening agent in liquid foods like soups, sauces, and gravies by gelatinizing and swelling to trap free water molecules, increasing viscosity.', '["as colloidal stabilizer","as a thickener","as a flavor carrier","as moisture retainer"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:57:05.885Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784248540-65', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'It is also called cellophane noodles or bean threads being made from mungbean flour. *', 'sotanghon', 'Sotanghon refers to thin, translucent glass noodles or cellophane noodles traditionally manufactured from mung bean starch flour.', '["sotanghon","canton","miswa","bihon"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:57:09.329Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784263889-66', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'In jellies and jams, sugar functions as a: *', 'preserving agent', 'In high concentrations (typically 65%+ soluble solids), sugar acts as a powerful preserving agent in jams and jellies by creating high osmotic pressure that draws water out of microbial cells, preventing spoilage.', '["sweetening agent","colorant and flavoring agent","texture modifier","preserving agent"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:57:13.039Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784272339-67', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'A seaweed used to process monosodium glutamate. *', 'kelp', 'Kelp (a large brown seaweed/macroalgae) is naturally rich in glutamates and serves as a commercial raw source utilized in the industrial extraction and production of monosodium glutamate (MSG) and seasoning agents.', '["agar","carrageenan","kelp","gelatin"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:57:17.979Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784282171-68', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Equivalent of 1 brick of butter in cups. *', '1 cup', 'Standard baking and culinary measurement equivalencies state that 1 standard "brick" or block of butter equals exactly 8 tablespoons, which is equivalent to 1 cup (or 2 sticks where 1 stick = 1/2 cup).', '["1 cup","2 cups","3 cups","½ cup"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:57:21.191Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784290855-69', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Flour mixture products leavened by chemical agents such as baking soda and baking powder. *', 'quick breads', 'Quick breads are flour-based baked goods leavened rapidly by chemical leavening agents (baking soda and baking powder) or steam rather than slow biological yeast fermentation.', '["quick breads","yeast breads","cream puff","pie"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:58:40.781Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784299687-70', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Which of the following sugars will crystallize most readily? *', 'lactose', 'Lactose (milk sugar) crystallizes most readily and rapidly out of solution compared to sucrose, glucose, or fructose, which is why improper candy-making or ice cream storage can lead to a sandy, gritty texture caused by coarse lactose crystal formation.', '["sucrose","glucose","fructose","lactose"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:58:46.392Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784308203-71', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'In sugar cookery, fats such as butter and cream function as: *', 'interfering agents', 'In sugar cookery and confectionery, fats (such as butter and cream) function as interfering agents that physically interrupt and slow down the rapid crystallization of sugar molecules, ensuring smooth textures in fudges and caramels.', '["interfering agents","crystallizing agents","stabilizers","emulsifiers"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:58:50.384Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758784318653-72', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'In coffee brewing, prolonged contact of coffee grounds with boiling water results in: *', 'a bitter taste due to too much tannin extraction', 'Prolonged contact of coffee grounds with boiling water extracts excess bitter tannins and undesirable phenolic compounds, resulting in an unpalatably bitter, harsh beverage.', '["a maximal blending of flavors","a bitter taste due to too much tannin extraction","dissolution of coffee grounds","a bland taste due to volatilization"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.352Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:58:53.961Z"'::jsonb),
