('anki-card-1758785425700-142', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'What is the % sales mix of an ice cream sundae that sold 300 units in a day when 656 desserts were sold? *', '45.73%', 'To calculate sales mix percentage:

Formula =  (Units Sold for Specific Item÷Total Category Units Sold)>100.

Given values: Sundaes sold = 300 units; Total desserts sold = 656 units.

Calculation =  (300÷656)×100=45.73%.', '["40%","45.73%","43.72%","54.73%"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:04:54.445Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785435002-143', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'According to the Sanitation Code of the Philippines, how much space should be provided for the kitchen? *', '¼ of dining area space', 'According to the Sanitation Code of the Philippines (PD 856), food establishment regulations recommend that kitchen and food preparation space allocation should be approximately one-fourth (1/4) of the customer dining area space.', '["½ of dining area space","¼ of dining area space","2/3 of dining area space","same amount of space as the dining area"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:05:00.314Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785447484-144', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'A technique in a wage program that translates relative job worth into money values. *', 'job pricing', 'Job pricing is the compensation technique in wage administration that translates the relative job worth determined via job evaluation into concrete monetary salary scales.', '["job evaluation","job pricing","Cost of Living Allowance (COLA)","job grading"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:05:05.329Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785455267-145', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Considered the foundation of Human Resource Management. *', 'job analysis', 'Job analysis is the systematic, foundational HR process of gathering data, tasks, duties, and requirements to build job descriptions and specifications.', '["job analysis","job evaluation","training","organization"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:05:09.768Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785462467-146', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'A test which determines quality standards to be set for commodities that involves coming up with the best count, weight, or quantity of fruits and vegetables. *', 'raw food test', 'A raw food test (yield test / butchering test) determines the standard quality, trim loss, edible portion yield, and purchase specifications for raw commodities like fresh fruits and vegetables.', '["butchering test","raw food test","canned good test","cooking test"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:05:13.823Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785470549-147', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'It is a term used to refer to equipment that are manufactured according to the buyer’s specifications. *', 'custom built equipment', 'Custom built equipment refers to specialized machinery and fixtures manufactured precisely according to a buyer''s unique architectural and operational specifications.

• Stock equipment: Standard catalog-manufactured equipment.', '["stock equipment","commercial equipment","custom built equipment","foodservice equipment"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:05:19.477Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785480200-148', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'A government agency that settles labor disputes. *', 'National Labor Relations Commission', 'The National Labor Relations Commission (NLRC) is the government quasi-judicial agency mandated to arbitrate and settle formal labor disputes, strikes, and employer-employee grievances in the Philippines.', '["Employee Compensation Commission","National Labor Relations Commission","Court of Appeals","Dept. of Trade and Industry"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:05:22.664Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785488430-149', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'A form of positive reinforcement which aims to provide guidance or advice to an erring employee. *', 'counseling', 'Counseling is a form of positive behavioral reinforcement and coaching used by supervisors to provide constructive guidance, feedback, and advice to an erring employee.', '["disciplining","a pat in the back","counseling","performance appraisal"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:05:26.553Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785496865-150', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Work stoppage that happens at the instigation of the employer. *', 'lock out', 'A lock-out is a temporary work stoppage or denial of employment initiated by the employer during a labor dispute (as opposed to a strike initiated by employees).', '["strike","lock out","stalemate in negotiation","collective bargaining"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:05:30.137Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785503882-151', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'The temperature of Chicken Joy was checked to see if its critical limit of 1800F was met. Which HACCP principle was applied? *', 'Monitoring', 'Checking and measuring temperature against established critical limits during food preparation is the core definition of monitoring in a HACCP system.

• Verification: Activities (other than monitoring) that validate the HACCP plan.
• Record keeping: Documenting the monitored data.
• Hazard analysis: Identifying biological, chemical, or physical hazards.', '["Verification","Monitoring","Record keeping","Hazard analysis"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:07:46.928Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785512347-152', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Which of the following is not a principle of good organization? *', 'commitment to excellence', '"Commitment to excellence" is a general corporate mission or value statement, whereas the established classical principles of good organization include division of labor, unity of command, and esprit de corps.

• Division of labor / Esprit de corps / Unity of command: Core classical management and organizational principles.', '["departmentalization/division of labor","esprit de corps","unity of command","commitment to excellence"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:07:54.355Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785520763-153', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Refers to the basic unit of a layout. *', 'work centers', 'A work center is the basic physical and functional unit of a kitchen layout where specific equipment and tasks are grouped together.', '["work design","work centers","work flow","flow chart"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:07:59.316Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785529146-154', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'The most sanitary type of food equipment. *', 'stainless steel', 'Stainless steel is the premier material for commercial foodservice equipment because it is non-porous, corrosion-resistant, durable, and exceptionally sanitary.

• Copper / Aluminum: Prone to chemical reactivity or pitting.', '["copper","aluminum","porcelain","stainless steel"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:08:09.534Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785564962-155', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Which of the following is an ideal material flow? *', 'receiving to storage to pre-preparation', 'An ideal material and operational flow follows a logical forward progression from receiving to storage, pre-preparation, production, and service, preventing cross-contamination.', '["receiving to storage to cooking","cooking to assembly to plating","storage to pre-preparation to assembly","receiving to storage to pre-preparation"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:08:16.244Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785574927-156', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Worktable heights for standing tasks are: *', '36 – 41 inches', 'Standard ergonomic guidelines specify that worktable heights for tasks performed while standing should be between 36 and 41 inches depending on the operator''s height and task type.', '["30 – 35 inches","30 – 40 inches","36 – 41 inches","28 – 30 inches"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:08:23.449Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785591693-157', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Worktable heights for sitting tasks are: *', '28 – 30 inches', 'Ergonomic seating standards dictate that worktable heights for seated tasks should be lower, ranging between 28 and 30 inches.', '["30 – 35inches","30 – 40 inches","36 – 41 inches","28 – 30 inches"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:08:28.418Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785605643-158', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'The ideal height of the highest shelf should be: *', '6 inches', 'Sanitation regulations mandate that the highest storage shelf and stacked items must maintain adequate clearance from ceilings and lighting fixtures (typically maintaining safe vertical margins), while floor clearance requires at least 6 inches.', '["5 inches","10 inches","6 inches","8 inches"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:08:49.058Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785616027-159', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Space allocation for sanitation should consider the following except: *', 'volume of detergents needed', 'Space allocation for sanitation facilities considers the physical space required for cleaning personnel, dishwashing methods, and tool/chemical storage, whereas the specific chemical volume needed is an operational consumable inventory rather than a structural space-planning determinant.', '["number of cleaning personnel","volume of detergents needed","method of dishwashing","storage area for cleaning equipment, tools, and agents"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:08:53.369Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785635458-160', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Contamination will likely occur when: *', 'an employee walks in the kitchen in a crisscross pattern', 'Crisscrossing pathways in a kitchen layout increase traffic congestion and cross-contamination risks between clean and soiled workflows.', '["an employee walks from clean to dirty area","an employee walks in the kitchen in a crisscross pattern","an employee brings more than what he can bring","an employee passes through the stations"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:08:57.030Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785643026-161', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Key players in facilities planning design except: *', 'store manager', 'Facilities planning and design teams typically involve architects, builders, engineers, and investors, whereas store managers execute operations rather than serving as primary design engineers.', '["store manager","builder","investors","architect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:09:00.558Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785660608-162', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Considered basic work centers in the facility except: *', 'receiving area', 'Receiving is an intake and holding dock rather than a basic internal food production or processing work center (which includes pre-preparation, cooking, and housekeeping/sanitation).', '["pre-preparation of meats, vegetables, and fruits","cooking area","receiving area","housekeeping – pan washing, dishwashing, sanitation"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:09:05.550Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785673057-163', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'The main determinant of space allocation is the: *', 'type of menu', 'The menu is the single most important document and main determinant dictating equipment requirements, operational steps, and spatial space allocation in a foodservice facility.', '["type of service","type of menu","number of employees","type of construction materials"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:09:09.647Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785681224-164', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'It consists of a group of related work centers: *', 'section', 'A section in facility layout terminology consists of a coordinated group of related work centers operating together.', '["layout","floor plan","section","work area"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:09:14.944Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785692556-165', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'The number of tablespoons in a Scoop #16: *', '4', 'A Scoop #16 holds a capacity of 1/16 of a gallon, which equates to 2 ounces or exactly 4 level tablespoons of food portioning volume.', '["5 ½","4","3","2 2/3"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:48:56.287Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785702422-166', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'The section of a feasibility study that describes the company’s product, how it is made, and the facility where the produce will be produced. *', 'technical section', 'The technical section of a feasibility study details the engineering specifications, manufacturing processes, required equipment, raw materials, and facility layout where the product will be produced.', '["marketing section","executive summary","technical section","none of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:09:20.098Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785713204-167', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'He proposed the 14 principles of management. *', 'Henri Fayol', 'Henri Fayol proposed the classic 14 principles of management under administrative management theory.

• Max Weber: Proposed bureaucratic theory.
• Henry Gantt: Developed the Gantt chart scheduling tool.', '["Max Weber","Henry Gantt","Lilian Gilbreth","Henri Fayol"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:09:26.032Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785723638-168', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'How many servings will you have for 1 gallon of ice cream using Scoop No. 4? *', '32', 'To calculate the yield from a gallon of ice cream using Scoop No. 4:

1 gallon = 4 quarts = 128 fluid ounces.

Scoop No. 4 holds 1/4 of a quart (or 8 fluid ounces / 1 cup per scoop).

Calculation = 128 oz ÷ 4 oz (or 4 quarts × 8 scoops per quart) = 32 servings.', '["24","40","32","36"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:09:36.637Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785732871-169', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'How many 2 ½ cans of evaporated milk are there in 1 case? *', '24', 'Standard commercial cases of No. 2 ½ canned goods (such as evaporated milk) contain exactly 24 cans per case.', '["12","24","36","38"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:09:41.764Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785744421-170', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Information which may be obtained from a market research except: *', 'approximate expenses', 'Market research focuses externally on customer demographics, spending habits, and market demand/sales potential, whereas internal cost accounting determines approximate expenses.', '["approximate sales","average spending of the customer","information about the target customers","approximate expenses"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:09:45.944Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785752887-171', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'This tool serves as the blueprint of the restaurant’s operations.', 'business plan', 'A business plan serves as the overarching structural blueprint and strategic roadmap of a restaurant''s financial, operational, and marketing goals.', '["feasibility study","business plan","technical research","floor plan"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:09:49.382Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785762902-172', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Part of the business plan that provides the approximate capital needed to run the restaurant operations. *', 'technical section', 'The technical and operational section of a business plan outlines production methods, facility layout, equipment needs, and approximate capital requirements needed to launch operations.', '["market section","technical section","financial section","capital section"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:09:52.259Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785771936-173', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'The provision of ramps and railings is mandated by this law: *', 'Accessibility Law', 'Batas Pambansa Blg. 344 (The Accessibility Law) mandates the provision of architectural structural modifications such as ramps, railings, and accessible facilities for disabled persons.', '["Building Code of the Philippines","Sanitation Code of the Philippines","Accessibility Law","Magna Carta for Disabled Persons"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:09:57.339Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785787485-174', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'The Temperature Danger Zone is between: *', '4°C (40°F) and 60°C (140°F)', 'The Temperature Danger Zone—the critical thermal range where pathogenic bacteria multiply rapidly in food—spans between 4°C (40°F) and 60°C (140°F).', '["-18.0°C (0°F) and 4.4°C (40°F)","0°C (32°F) and 4.4°C (40°F)","4°C (40°F) and 60°C (140°F)","60.0°C (140°F) and 74°C (165°F)"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:10:01.808Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785796935-175', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Nutritionist-Dietitians are guided to act ethically by PD 1289. This act is also called the Nutritionist-Dietitian Code of Ethics. *', 'Only the second sentence is correct.', '', '["Only the first sentence is correct.","Only the second sentence is correct.","Both sentences are correct.","Both sentences are incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785806635-176', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Decentralization is one of the principles of organization. This complements another principle which is delegation. *', 'Both sentences are correct.', 'Statement 1 is correct: decentralization of authority disperses decision-making. 

Statement 2 is correct: decentralization complements and relies directly on the principle of delegation.', '["Only the first sentence is correct.","Only the second sentence is correct.","Both sentences are correct.","Both sentences are incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:10:22.345Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785816550-177', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Classical Management Theory generated the principles of good organization. Systems theory emphasizes interrelationships between organizational components. *', 'Both sentences are correct.', 'Statement 1 is correct: classical management theory generated structural principles of organization. 

Statement 2 is correct: systems theory highlights dynamic interrelationships across organizational components.', '["Only the first sentence is correct.","Only the second sentence is correct.","Both sentences are correct.","Both sentences are incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:10:30.501Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785829033-178', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Decision-making in foodservice operations can be complicated without theories. Using the systems theory, a manager projecting sales should consider sales performance in the past. *', 'Both sentences are correct.', 'Statement 1 is correct: decision-making requires administrative theories as conceptual frameworks. 

Statement 2 is correct: systems theory dictates that managers use historical sales feedback when forecasting future sales.', '["Only the first sentence is correct.","Only the second sentence is correct.","Both sentences are correct.","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:10:38.861Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785839350-179', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Proper receiving of food should involve checking of: *', 'temperature', 'Proper receiving protocols for perishable foods mandate physically inspecting delivery trucks and checking internal food item temperatures using calibrated thermometers.', '["packaging","appearance","temperature","nutritional information"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:10:43.411Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785847732-180', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Which of the following teaching methods promote employees’ involvement and facilitate their learning? *', 'question and answer, role plays, and behavior modeling', 'Interactive training techniques like Q&A sessions, role-playing, and behavioral modeling actively engage employees and promote active experiential learning.', '["small discussion groups with a report back to the larger group","case studies, with questions to answer","question and answer, role plays, and behavior modeling","let the group lead the way and decide the training methods for themselves"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:10:46.800Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785855964-181', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'The most probable cause of foodborne illness is: *', 'a virus', 'Viral pathogens (such as Norovirus and Hepatitis A) transmitted via poor hygiene are among the most common leading causes of foodborne illness outbreaks.', '["an employee eating during snack hours","poor personal hygiene","a virus","due to the use of toothpicks"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:10:50.683Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785866066-182', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'The HACCP started in what commercial product? *', 'low acid canned food', 'The HACCP system was originally pioneered and developed in the early 1970s by Pillsbury alongside NASA specifically for ensuring the absolute safety of space foods, starting with commercial low-acid canned foods.', '["seafood for export","low acid canned food","canned pineapple","crackers"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:10:53.978Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785873696-183', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'HACCP will help: *', 'reduce costs of analyses', 'HACCP shifts quality control from end-product testing to proactive, preventative process monitoring, which significantly reduces the high costs associated with continuous microbiological end-product testing and analyses.', '["solve sensory attributes","establish market","determine pricing","reduce costs of analyses"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:10:57.661Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785882316-184', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Potatoes and carrots are blanched before drying in order to: *', 'prevent Maillard reaction', 'Blanching root vegetables like potatoes and carrots prior to drying inactivates polyphenol oxidases and leaches out excess reducing sugars, preventing unwanted Maillard browning and caramelization during dehydration.', '["avoid caramelization","prevent Maillard reaction","prevent enzymatic browning","avoid hydrolytic and oxidative rancidity"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:11:01.591Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785890864-185', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Why is salt added to flour mixtures? *', 'to produce a firm dough', 'Salt strengthens gluten protein networks, controls yeast fermentation rates, and helps produce a cohesive, firm dough structure in baking.', '["to produce a sticky dough","to produce a firm dough","to inhibit yeast activity","to increase fermentation"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:11:05.929Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785900962-186', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'The main difference between RA 2674 and PD 1286 is that _____: *', 'there is no difference between the two laws.', '', '["those taking the Licensure Examination must be 21 years of age.","no Licensure Examination is required.","dietetic internship is replaced by practical trainings integrated in the curriculum.","there is no difference between the two laws."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785910643-187', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'The following foods are stored in the dry storage: I. canned goods III. eggs and dairy products II. potatoes and tubers IV. cooked foods *', 'I & II', 'Dry storage is appropriate for non-perishable canned goods (I) and root crops like potatoes and tubers (II) stored at cool ambient temperatures. Eggs, dairy, and cooked foods require refrigeration.', '["II & IV","I & II","I & III","III & IV"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:11:11.099Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785918930-188', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'The practical size of can for institutional preparation and cooking is: *', 'No. 2 ½', 'In institutional quantity food preparation, the No. 2 ½ can (holding roughly 3.5 cups / 27-28 oz) is recognized as the standard practical size for catering and quantity recipes.', '["No. 2","No. 303","No. 2 ½","No. 10"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:11:15.051Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785927813-189', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'This foodservice system that would have a problem in food safety: *', 'commissary', 'Commissary foodservice systems involve large-scale centralized production followed by bulk transport, holding, and reheating across remote satellite service sites, presenting inherent critical control point risks in temperature maintenance and food safety.', '["ready-prepared","assembly serve","commissary","conventional"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:11:20.102Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785938847-190', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'The type of material used for floors has an impact on efficiency. The recommended material for floor is quarry tile. *', 'Both statements are correct.', 'Statement 1 is correct: flooring material directly impacts operational safety, cleaning ease, and staff fatigue. 

Statement 2 is correct: quarry tile is widely recommended as an ideal heavy-duty kitchen flooring material due to its slip-resistance, durability, and non-porosity.', '["First statement is correct.","Second statement is correct.","Both statements are correct.","Both statements are incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:11:28.590Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758785947145-191', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609268127-1790433136748-a3r8j', 'Taste panels are important in evaluating food samples using different scientific objective tests. Males can detect sweetness better than females. *', 'Both statements are incorrect.', '', '["Both statements are correct.","Only the first statement is correct.","Both statements are incorrect.","Only the second statement is correct."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb)
