('anki-card-1758815042787-33', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'Substances used to preserve food by lowering the pH: *', 'vinegar and citric acid', 'Vinegar and citric acid lower food pH, creating an acidic environment that inhibits microbial spoilage and acts as a natural preservative.', '["vinegar and citric acid","salt and sugar","baking powder and soda","smoke and irradiation"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:29:51.255Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815052604-34', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'Sodium hydroxide is locally known as “apog”. It is used to facilitate the peeling of fruits such as tomato, guava, and others. *', 'The first statement is incorrect but the second statement is correct.', 'Statement 1 is incorrect because sodium hydroxide is locally known as "sosa" or caustic soda, whereas "apog" refers to calcium hydroxide (slaked lime). 

Statement 2 is correct: alkaline solutions like apog are traditionally used in food processing to facilitate fruit skin peeling (such as for tomatoes and guavas).', '["Both statements are correct.","Both statements are incorrect.","The first statement is incorrect but the second statement is correct.","The first statement is correct but the second statement is incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:29:58.031Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815061703-35', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'Miswa is a thread-like noodle made from rice and wheat flour. It can be cooked instantly. *', 'The first statement is incorrect but the second statement is correct.', 'Miswa (or meesua) is a very thin, thread-like salted wheat flour noodle (not rice flour) that cooks almost instantly in boiling water or hot broth.

• The first statement is incorrect: Miswa is made from wheat flour, not rice flour (which is used for bihon or rice sticks).
• The second statement is correct: Due to its extremely thin strands, it cooks instantaneously when added to boiling liquids.', '["The first statement is incorrect but the second statement is correct.","The first statement is correct but the second statement is incorrect.","Both statements are correct.","Both statements are incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:31:05.040Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815070684-36', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'Which of the following statements is true” *', 'As fruits ripen, sugar content increases.', 'During the natural ripening process of climacteric and non-climacteric fruits, complex carbohydrates (like starch) are enzymatically hydrolyzed into simple sugars, causing sugar content and sweetness to increase significantly while acidity typically declines.', '["As fruits ripen, sugar content remains the same.","As fruits ripen, sugar content increases.","As fruits ripen, sugar content decreases.","As fruits ripen, acidity increases."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:31:12.903Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815078218-37', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'Taste panels usually consist of at least ____ individuals. *', '5', 'Standard sensory evaluation protocols and consumer preference testing require a minimum sensory panel size of at least 5 trained or semi-trained individuals (though larger panels of 10 to 20+ are common for robust statistical validity).', '["5","7","10","3"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:31:17.199Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815109851-38', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'A research design that collects data from a group of customers at a single point in time. *', 'cross-sectional', 'A cross-sectional research design collects observational data from a target population or group of customers at a single, specific point in time without long-term tracking.

• Longitudinal: Collects data from the same subjects repeatedly over an extended period.
• Cohort: Follows a specific cohort forward or backward through time.
• Time series: Evaluates multiple data points across sequential time intervals.', '["longitudinal","cohort","time series","cross-sectional"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:31:23.234Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815118834-39', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'It is not the Pilipino translation: *', 'Cowpea is abitsuelas', 'Abitsuelas is the local Tagalog term for string beans, kidney beans, or common snap beans, whereas cowpea is locally known as paayap, making this statement the correct mismatch (exception).

• Chickpea is garbanzos: Correct translation.
• Mungbean is mongo: Correct translation.
• Soybean is utaw: Correct translation.', '["Cowpea is abitsuelas","Chickpea is garbanzos","Mungbean is mongo","Soybean is utaw"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:31:31.559Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815127167-40', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'The cut of pork that is best for cooking sinigang. *', 'picnic', 'The picnic shoulder cut (kasim or picnic shoulder) contains a balanced amount of lean meat, connective tissue, and fat, making it ideal for slow-simmered local savory soup dishes like sinigang.

• Tenderloin: Extremely tender and lean, best for quick-cooking, dry-heat preparations (stewing causes it to dry out).
• Leg: Lean cut better suited for roasting or ham preparation.', '["picnic","tenderloin","leg","rib loin"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:31:38.685Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815134982-41', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'An example of a subjective food evaluation test: *', 'creating a taste panel', 'Creating a human sensory taste (evaluation) panel is a subjective (sensory) food evaluation test relying on human sensory organs (taste, smell, texture).

• Measuring weight / Spectrophotometer / Measuring volume: Objective physical or chemical instrumental tests.', '["creating a taste panel","measuring weight of food","measuring volume","using a spectrophotometer"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:29:03.697Z"'::jsonb)
