('anki-card-1758815152314-42', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'Food preservation is treating food by any method such as drying or smoking. It is done to kill the microorganisms present in food. *', 'The first statement is correct but the second statement is incorrect.', 'Food preservation methods (such as drying, salting, canning, or smoking) are designed to inhibit, control, or reduce microbial growth and enzyme activity, but they do not universally or completely "kill" all microorganisms present in food.

• The first statement is correct: Preservation encompasses techniques like drying or smoking.
• The second statement is incorrect: Preservation inhibits spoilage and pathogens rather than serving as a guaranteed sterilization technique to kill all microorganisms.', '["Both statements are incorrect.","The first statement is incorrect but the second statement is correct.","Both statements are correct.","The first statement is correct but the second statement is incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:31:44.330Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815162415-43', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'he term referring to goat meat: *', 'chevon', 'Chevon is the standardized culinary and meat science term for the meat harvested from goats.

• Venison: Meat from deer.
• Mutton: Meat from adult sheep.
• Veal: Meat from calves.', '["chevon","venison","mutton","veal"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:31:48.103Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815194930-44', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'Which ingredient differentiates Sinuam from Tinola? *', 'unripe papaya', 'Sinuam and tinola are both traditional Filipino ginger-based broths (soup dishes), but sinuam distinctively incorporates shredded or sliced green (unripe) papaya and native ginger paste, whereas traditional tinola typically utilizes chayote or green papaya wedges with ginger and chili leaves.

• Pepper leaves: Used in both tinola and sinuam.', '["chicken","pork","unripe papaya","pepper leaves"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:32:03.658Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815203544-45', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'Despite efforts to eliminate spoilage organisms during canning, sometimes canned foods spoil. This may be due to: *', 'all of the above', 'Even with advanced industrial canning technology, commercial canned foods can occasionally spoil due to pre-processing raw material spoilage, under-processing (insufficient thermal lethality), or post-processing container leakage where contaminated cooling water enters through defective can seams.', '["spoilage before canning","under processing during canning","leakage of contaminated water through can seams during cooking","all of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:32:08.951Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815212431-46', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'This involves development of new products by making a genetic modification in a living organism. *', 'biotechnology', 'Biotechnology encompasses advanced scientific techniques involving genetic modification, gene splicing, and recombinant DNA technology applied to living organisms to create novel food products or crops.

• Epigenetics: The study of cellular gene expression changes without altering underlying DNA sequence.', '["food technology","epigenetics","biotechnology","genetics"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:32:14.972Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815220762-47', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'A symbiotic relationship beneficial to both associates: *', 'mutualism', 'Mutualism is a biological symbiotic relationship where both interacting species derive mutually beneficial fitness outcomes.

• Commensalism: One organism benefits while the other is unaffected.
• Parasitism: One organism benefits at the expense of the host.', '["mutualism","commensalism","parasitism","opportunism"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:32:21.530Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815231827-48', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'The ratio of liquid to flour in popover batters: *', '1', 'Popovers are quick breads characterized by a fluid, high-liquid batter (equal parts flour and liquid by volume, yielding a 1:1 ratio) that creates steam to puff the pastry during baking.', '["1","3","2","4"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:32:32.699Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815240711-49', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'Why does commercial ice cream have more body than homemade ice cream? *', 'stabilizers are used', 'Commercial ice cream incorporates food stabilizers (such as gums, carrageenan, or gelatin) to bind free water molecules, prevent large ice crystal formation, and impart a smooth, uniform "body" and texture.

• Homemade ice cream: Often lacks commercial stabilizers, resulting in faster coarse ice crystal formation.', '["larger batches are made","high-technology equipment is used","secret recipes are used","stabilizers are used"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:32:37.323Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815247727-50', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'Deionized water is basically purified water without _____. *', 'minerals', 'Deionized water is treated via ion-exchange resins specifically to strip out dissolved mineral ions (such as calcium, magnesium, and sodium), yielding purified water devoid of minerals.', '["color","minerals","carbonation","steam"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:32:41.520Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815256627-51', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'It determines whether coffee is classified as light, medium or dark roast. *', 'roasting time', 'Roasting time (and thermal profile progression) governs the degree of caramelization and Maillard browning reactions, determining whether coffee beans are classified as light, medium, or dark roast.

• Grinding level: Determines particle size for brewing extraction, not the roast profile.', '["grinding level","roasting time","roasting temperature","decaffeination"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:32:47.940Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815265543-52', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'These are chemical compounds in green tea which act as antioxidants and may have anticarcinogenic properties: *', 'phenols', 'Green tea contains abundant polyphenolic compounds (such as catechins and flavonoids) that function as powerful biological antioxidants and possess potential anticarcinogenic properties.

• Tannins: Bitter astringent compounds, but polyphenolic phenols are the specific antioxidant agents highlighted.', '["phenols","phospholipids","pyroles","tannins"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:32:53.360Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815275924-53', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'A sensory phenomenon characterized by a dry, puckery feeling in the mouth: *', 'astringency', 'Astringency is a tactile oral sensory phenomenon characterized by a dry, puckery, drawing sensation in the mouth caused by the precipitation of salivary proteins by tannins or polyphenols.

• Tartness: A taste sensation driven by organic acids.', '["tartness","fizz","astringency","bitterness"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:32:57.227Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815282976-54', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'The sticky, moist texture of breads resulting from contamination by Bacillus mesentericus bacteria. *', 'rope', 'Rope is a classic bacterial spoilage defect in bread caused by Bacillus mesentericus spores surviving baking, resulting in a sticky, moist, stringy texture accompanied by a fruity odor.', '["roux","rope","flaking","none of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:33:01.534Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815291957-55', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'One cup gives ____ fluid ounces; _____ tablespoons; _____ teaspoons. *', '8; 16; 48', 'Standard kitchen measurement equivalencies state that 1 standard US cup equals exactly 8 fluid ounces, 16 tablespoons, and 48 teaspoons.', '["8; 14; 48","8; 16; 48","6; 16; 48","8; 12; 48"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:33:04.782Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815299057-56', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'Type of cheese usually used for pizza making. *', 'mozzarella', 'Mozzarella cheese possesses high moisture, excellent meltability, and optimal stretch characteristics, making it the classic cheese utilized worldwide for pizza making.

• Parmesan: Hard, aged grating cheese.
• Blue/bleu cheese: Semi-soft, pungent, crumbly cheese.', '["Edam","mozzarella","parmesan","blue/bleu cheese"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:33:08.844Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815306857-57', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'A mechanical process that breaks up fat globules in milk into smaller globules that do not clump together. *', 'homogenization', 'Homogenization is a mechanical high-pressure process that forces milk through minute valves, breaking large fat globules down into tiny, stable micro-globules that do not separate or clump together.

• Pasteurization: Thermal destruction of pathogens.', '["homogenization","pasteurization","toning","emulsification"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:33:13.034Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815315574-58', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'The cheese made from soy milk. *', 'tofu', 'Tofu (bean curd) is a soft, cheese-like food product manufactured by coagulating soy milk and pressing the resulting curds.

• Tempeh: A fermented whole soybean cake from Indonesia.', '["feta","tofu","tempeh","Gouda"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:33:17.036Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815325040-59', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'The formation of tiny syrup droplets on the surface of a baked meringue: *', 'beading', 'Beading refers to the formation of amber-colored syrup droplets on the surface of a baked meringue, typically caused by overbaking or und حل (undissolved sugar).

• Weeping: Syneresis or moisture pooling underneath the meringue.', '["weeping","crystallizing","binding","beading"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:27:34.999Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815333689-60', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'Artichoke and broccoli are classified as: *', 'flowers', 'Artichokes and broccoli represent immature floral buds harvested and consumed as culinary vegetables belonging to the flower classification.', '["fruits","flowers","stems & shoots","bulbs"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:46:07.399Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815341938-61', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'Fatty deposits within muscles of meat which contribute to its flavor and juiciness: *', 'marbling', 'Marbling refers to the fine, white flecks and intra-muscular deposits of fat distributed within meat muscles, which melt during cooking to enhance flavor, tenderness, and juiciness.

• Subcutaneous fat: Fat layer deposited directly underneath the skin.', '["subcutaneous fat","fatty acids","larding","marbling"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:33:21.913Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815350605-62', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'The effect of acid on the anthocyanin of red cabbage, changing its to ____: *', 'reddish hue', 'Anthocyanin pigments found in red cabbage are water-soluble flavonoids that shift to a bright pink or reddish hue in the presence of an acidic medium.

• Bluish/violet hue: Occurs in neutral or alkaline (basic) environments.', '["reddish hue","bluish hue","yellowish hue","violet hue"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:33:25.804Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815358738-63', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'The process of removing fat crystals so that oil remains liquid at refrigerated temperature: *', 'winterizing', 'Winterizing is an industrial food processing technique that chills edible oils and filters out high-melting-point saturated fat crystals so that the oil remains clear and liquid at refrigerated temperatures.

• Hydrogenation: Converts liquid oils into semi-solid fats by adding hydrogen.', '["hydrogenation","refining","winterizing","clarifying"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:33:32.269Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815367422-64', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'Compounds added to fats and oils which help prevent the development of rancidity: *', 'antioxidants', 'Antioxidants (such as BHA, BHT, tocopherols, and propyl gallate) are chemical compounds added to fats and oils to scavenge free radicals and prevent oxidative rancidity.', '["antioxidants","fatty acids","phytochemicals","emulsifiers"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:33:36.832Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815375904-65', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', '____ is the acid ingredient and _____ the alkaline ingredient used as components of leavening: *', 'cream of tartar; baking soda', 'Chemical leavening systems rely on an acid component (cream of tartar / potassium bitartrate) reacting with an alkaline component (baking soda / sodium bicarbonate) in the presence of moisture to release carbon dioxide gas.', '["cream of tartar; baking soda","baking soda; cream of tartar","baking powder; cream of tartar","cream of tartar; baking powder"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:33:40.331Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815387403-66', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'The emulsifying agent present in egg yolk: *', 'lecithin', 'Lecithin is a natural phospholipid found abundantly in egg yolk that acts as a powerful emulsifying agent, stabilizing oil-in-water emulsions like mayonnaise.

• Fat: General lipid class, not the specific emulsifier.
• Albumin: Major egg white protein, not the primary yolk emulsifier.
• Avidin: Egg white protein that binds biotin.', '["fat","albumin","avidin","lecithin"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:25:20.833Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815402470-67', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'The protein in milk which does not form a curd: *', 'whey', 'Whey is the liquid fraction of milk containing soluble proteins (such as lactalbumin and lactoglobulin) that remain dissolved and do not form a coagulated curd during acid or rennet precipitation.

• Casein: The primary milk protein that precipitates to form curds.
• Albumin / Ovalbumin: Egg proteins.', '["casein","albumin","whey","ovalbumin"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:25:32.486Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815409902-68', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'Poultry products are a likely source of infection by: *', 'Salmonella sp.', 'Poultry products and eggs are well-documented primary vehicles for Salmonella species infections.

• Staphylococcus aureus: Commonly associated with food handlers and protein-rich foods handled manually.
• Vibrio cholerae: Associated with contaminated water and raw seafood/shellfish.
• Clostridium perfringens: Associated with improperly cooled meats and gravies.', '["Staphylococcus aureus","Salmonella sp.","Vibrio cholera","Clostridium perfringens"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:25:40.986Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815424452-69', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'Plasmodium, the causative agent for Malaria, is classified as a/an: *', 'sporozoa', 'Plasmodium species (the protozoan parasites responsible for causing malaria) belong to the phylum Apicomplexa, classified under sporozoa (protozoa characterized by spore-forming life cycle stages).', '["amoeba","flagellates","ciliates","sporozoa"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:33:45.742Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815434568-70', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'A type of illness that arises from a chemical hazard: *', 'Monosodium glutamate poisoning', 'Monosodium glutamate (MSG) poisoning (or "Chinese Restaurant Syndrome") is a classic adverse reaction arising from a chemical food additive (chemical hazard).

• Trichinosis / Shigellosis: Biological hazards caused by parasitic worms and bacteria.', '["Trichinosis","Monosodium glutamate poisoning","Shigellosis","Mushroom poisoning"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:33:51.561Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815442284-71', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'A technique used as a pre-treatment of fruits and vegetables to deactivate enzymes early in the preparation stages for processing is: *', 'blanching', 'Blanching is a thermal pre-treatment where fruits or vegetables are briefly immersed in boiling water or steam to inactivate polyphenol oxidase and other spoilage enzymes prior to freezing, canning, or drying.', '["washing","blanching","lye peeling","scalding"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:33:55.788Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815450801-72', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'During frozen storage, what causes cell membranes to rupture? *', 'ice crystals', 'During slow or fluctuating frozen storage, water molecules form large ice crystals that puncture delicate cellular walls and membranes, causing cell collapse and textural softening upon thawing.', '["ice crystals","salting out","coagulation","denaturation"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:33:58.916Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815461864-73', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'A Philippine vegetable dish containing a wide assortment of vegetables, shrimps, pork, and sotanghon. *', 'laksa', 'Laksa is a savory noodle soup dish featuring a rich broth, a variety of vegetables, shrimp, pork, and vermicelli/sotanghon noodles.

• Pinakbet / Dinengdeng / Laing: Traditional indigenous Filipino vegetable dishes without sotanghon and shrimp/pork noodle soup combinations.', '["pinakbet","dinengdeng","laksa","laing"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:34:02.834Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815470081-74', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'A phenolic substance responsible for enzymatic browning in fruits and vegetables: *', 'cathecolase', 'Polyphenol oxidase (often referred to historically in culinary contexts as cathecolase or tyrosinase) is the copper-containing enzyme responsible for catalyzing enzymatic browning reactions in cut fruits and vegetables.

• Bromelin: A proteolytic enzyme found in pineapples.', '["cathecolase","bromelin","tannin","astaxanthin"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:34:07.338Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815477983-75', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'It is considered a stiff dough: *', 'pie crust', 'Pie pastry dough contains a high proportion of solid fat cut into flour with minimal liquid, classifying it as a stiff, laminated pastry dough.

• Cream puff / Yeast roll / Pound cake: Batter or soft dough formulations.', '["pie crust","cream puff","yeast roll","pound cake"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:34:13.879Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815488499-76', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'Vegetables cooked incorrectly lose their flavor. In cooking beans or carrots, it is least advisable to: *', 'cook them in an uncovered kettle', 'Cooking green vegetables (like beans or carrots) in an uncovered kettle allows volatile organic acids to escape, but leaving the pot uncovered for prolonged periods exposes plant pigments and nutrients to oxidative degradation, making it the least advisable practice among steam/pressure options.', '["cook them in a steamer","boil them in a small amount of water","cook them in an uncovered kettle","cook them in a pressure cooker"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:34:18.390Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815496648-77', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'Chief source of commercial gelatin: *', 'hide stock & bones', 'Commercial gelatin is derived primarily from the hydrolysis of collagen extracted from animal connective tissues, hide stock, and bones.

• Seaweeds: Source of agar-agar and carrageenan, not animal gelatin.', '["seaweeds","muscles","tissues","hide stock & bones"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:34:25.522Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815515379-78', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'A leavening agent which gives a disagreeable taste and a yellow color in baked products. *', 'baking soda', 'Excessive baking soda (sodium bicarbonate) used alone without sufficient acid leaves an unpleasant soapy, bitter, alkaline taste and imparts a yellowish chemical discoloration in baked goods.', '["baking powder","cream of tartar","sour milk","baking soda"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:34:29.538Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815523997-79', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'The change in the physical appearance of eggs when fried is an example of: *', 'coagulation', 'Cooking an egg transforms liquid egg proteins from a fluid sol state into a firm, set gel/solid state via heat-induced protein denaturation and coagulation.', '["denaturation","syneresis","coagulation","osmosis"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:34:33.203Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815543513-80', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'It measures the level of liking of foods. *', 'hedonic scale', 'A hedonic scale (ranging from "extremely like" to "extremely dislike") is the standard subjective sensory evaluation tool used to measure consumers'' degree of liking for food products.

• Descriptive / Discriminative tests: Measure specific sensory attributes or differences without rating personal preference.', '["hedonic scale","affective method","descriptive test","discriminative test"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:34:37.319Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815551761-81', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'The best way to measure dimensions of a regularly-shaped food. *', 'a & c only', 'The dimensions of regularly-shaped food products are accurately measured using precision tools like a micrometer (for thickness/small dimensions) and a standard ruler.', '["micrometer","sieve","ruler","a & c only"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:46:45.349Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815562477-82', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'Considered sensory difference tests: *', 'b & c only', 'Sensory difference tests determine whether discernible differences exist between food samples; paired comparison tests (b) and triangle tests (c) are standard difference methods. Paired preference tests measure subjective liking, not difference.', '["paired preference test","paired comparison test","triangle test","b & c only"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:46:51.992Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815569812-83', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'Consumer tests may be conducted with: *', 'both a & b', 'Consumer acceptance tests require large, untrained panels to determine general market preference, successfully executed with sample sizes ranging from moderate panels (24+ panelists) up to large consumer groups (200+ panelists).', '["at least 24 panelists","200 or more panelists","both a & b","none of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:46:57.182Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815577595-84', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'At the freezing point and below it, microorganisms become dormant because: *', 'b & c only', 'At freezing temperatures and below, microorganisms are rendered dormant because available free water is locked up as ice (lack of available moisture) and cellular enzymatic metabolic rates are drastically retarded.', '["cells die","of lack of available moisture","enzymatic activities are retarded","b & c only"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:47:02.372Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815585944-85', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'he systematic study of food spoilage caused by bacteria, yeast, or molds to food is known as: *', 'food microbiology', 'Food microbiology is the systematic scientific study of how microorganisms (bacteria, yeasts, and molds) interact with food, causing spoilage, fermentation, or foodborne illness.', '["food microbiology","food bacteriology","food parasitology","food preservation"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:47:06.730Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815594343-86', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'Freeze-drying is a process of dehydration which largely utilizes the principle of: *', 'sublimation', 'Freeze-drying (lyophilization) dehydrates foods by freezing them and placing them under a vacuum, allowing ice crystals to transition directly from a solid state into water vapor via sublimation.', '["refrigeration","sublimation","osmosis","evaporation"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:47:10.103Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815602158-87', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'Can cause ascariasis: *', 'helminthes', 'Ascariasis is a parasitic infection caused by Ascaris lumbricoides, which belongs to the parasitic roundworm group known as helminthes.', '["helminthes","slime molds","protozoa","water molds"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:47:14.762Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815615908-88', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'The end products of fermentation depend upon the following factors except: *', 'moisture content of the raw material', 'The end products of microbial fermentation depend primarily on the nature of the substrate, the specific microbial strains present, and environmental factors like temperature and pH, whereas raw material moisture content is not the defining determinant of fermentation pathway metabolites.', '["nature of the food","types of microorganisms present","environmental factors affecting microbial activity","moisture content of the raw material"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:25:50.367Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815623642-89', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'Which of the following is not an intrinsic factor in food spoilage? *', 'temperature', 'Temperature is an extrinsic environmental factor governing microbial growth, whereas pH, moisture content, and available nutrients are intrinsic factors inherent to the food itself.

• pH / Moisture content / Available nutrients: Intrinsic factors.', '["pH","moisture content","available nutrients","temperature"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:25:55.598Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815631457-90', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'At high temperatures, the rate of enzyme action decreases because the increased heat: *', 'alters the active site of the enzyme', 'Excessive thermal heat denatures protein enzyme structures, permanently altering the spatial geometry of their active binding sites and halting catalytic activity.', '["changes the pH of the system","alters the active site of the enzyme","neutralizes the acids and bases in the system","increases the concentration of the enzyme"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:46:11.675Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758815644891-91', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'It does not occur as the egg ages: *', 'acidity increases', 'As an egg ages, internal carbon dioxide gas escapes through the porous eggshell, causing internal pH to rise (become more alkaline, not acidic).

• Air cell enlarges / Water evaporates / Water enters yolk: Normal structural changes during egg aging.', '["the air cell enlarges","acidity increases","water evaporates","water enters the yolk"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:46:17.317Z"'::jsonb)
