('anki-card-1758816586912-178', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'All are tools for effective quantity food production except: *', 'food inventory', 'A food inventory is an accounting and stock control record used to track stock levels, whereas production schedules, standardized menus, and established food standards are direct operational tools for quantity food production.', '["production schedule","menu","food standards","food inventory"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.872Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:42:54.602Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758816595112-179', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'This information is not included in a standardized recipe: *', 'cost per serving portion', 'A standardized recipe provides precise ingredient weights, preparation instructions, cooking methods, portion sizes, and yield numbers. Cost per serving portion is dynamic and fluctuates with market prices, making it a financial management output rather than a static fixture of the recipe itself.', '["cooking methods and utensils to use","portion size","cost per serving portion","number of servings to cook"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.872Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:43:23.926Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758816608127-180', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'This foodservice system requires customers to line-up for hot and cold foods and a server gives their choices: *', 'cafeteria', 'A cafeteria foodservice system requires customers to form a line moving past a service counter where hot and cold foods are displayed, and attendants portion or serve their selections.

• Buffet: Customers serve themselves freely from a central display table.
• Bar / Drive-in: Counter beverage or car-side service models.', '["bar","cafeteria","buffet","drive-in restaurant"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.872Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:43:28.738Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758816618160-181', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'What will you do if a large number of your clientele became ill and food poisoning is suspected? *', 'Get samples of food served during the past 24 hours for laboratory analysis.', 'When food poisoning is suspected, the immediate epidemiological and sanitary priority is to secure and collect leftover food samples from the meals served over the past 24 hours for microbiological and toxicological laboratory analysis to identify the causative agent.

• Inspect storeroom expiry dates / Obtain 24-hour intake history / Check food handlers: Important secondary epidemiological investigations, but gathering physical food samples for immediate lab testing is the critical first diagnostic step.', '["Inspect the content of the food storeroom to determine the expiry date of all canned goods.","Obtain the food intake history of clients for the past 24 hours.","Get samples of food served during the past 24 hours for laboratory analysis.","Check all food personnel for the presence of upper respiratory infections or cut on hands."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.872Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:43:38.507Z"'::jsonb),
