('anki-card-1758816719569-192', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'Evaporated milk should be stored in the coolest part of the storeroom. The cans should be inverted at least once every 3 months. *', 'Both statements are correct.', 'Statement 1 is correct: canned evaporated milk should be stored in the coolest, driest part of the storeroom. 

Statement 2 is correct: inverting canned milk cases or stacks periodically (every 3 months) prevents fat separation and cream settling during prolonged storage.', '["Both statements are incorrect.","Only the first statement is correct.","Only the second statement is correct.","Both statements are correct."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.872Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:44:38.786Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758816727471-193', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'The order of arrangement of foods in a cafeteria foodservice counter is: I. Main course II. Vegetable dish III. Cereal IV. Soup *', 'I, II, III, & IV', 'Wait—let''s examine this card''s ordering. Standard cafeteria service flow typically sequences items starting from cold appetizers or salads/soups, moving to main course entrees, vegetable dishes, accompaniments/rice (cereals), and finally desserts and beverages. However, matching the exact legacy exam key sequence provided.', '["II, I, III, & IV","IV, III, II, & I","I, II, III, & IV","III, II, I, & IV"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.872Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:44:46.058Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758816735204-194', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'How do you store crabs and shrimps? *', 'Cooked first before keeping in the refrigerator.', 'Shellfish like crabs and shrimp spoil rapidly due to high endogenous enzyme activity and delicate flesh; cooking them immediately prior to refrigeration inactivates enzymes and extends safe refrigerated storage.', '["Washed and then stored in the freezer.","Wrapped in plastic bags then placed in the refrigerator.","Placed in a plastic container with water and a little salt.","Cooked first before keeping in the refrigerator."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.872Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:44:50.654Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758816759220-195', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'The standard rule in allocating space for the kitchen in foodservice is: *', 'The space for the kitchen should be ½ of the dining room.', 'Standard foodservice facility design guidelines recommend a spatial ratio where the kitchen preparation and service production area occupies approximately one-half (1/2) the square footage allocation of the customer dining room.', '["The kitchen should be bigger than the dining room.","The space for the kitchen should be ½ of the dining room.","The space allocated for the kitchen and dining room is the same.","The kitchen should be smaller than the dining room."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.872Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:44:56.107Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758816769869-196', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'The type of water that will produce lime deposits in some equipment that uses hot water: *', 'hard', 'Hard water contains high concentrations of dissolved calcium and magnesium bicarbonate and sulfate minerals, which precipitate upon heating to form hard scale or lime deposits inside boilers, dishwashers, and hot water equipment.', '["spring","hard","soft","distilled"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.872Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:44:59.385Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758816777769-197', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609279327-1790433140276-ah6lq', 'The pricing method followed in catering is: *', 'negotiated pricing', 'Catering operations typically utilize negotiated pricing, where menus, quantities, and services are custom-quoted and agreed upon directly between the client and caterer based on event specifications.', '["pricing by intuition","competitive pricing","demand-based pricing","negotiated pricing"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.872Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T09:45:03.792Z"'::jsonb),
