• Reduction: This involves simmering or boiling a liquid (such as stock, wine, or sauce) to evaporate water and concentrate the flavors. This process thickens the liquid and intensifies its taste, resulting in a richer sauce or liquid base for dishes.
• Concasse: This term refers to a method of preparing tomatoes by blanching, peeling, and chopping them into small pieces. The technique is often used to create a base for sauces or as a fresh ingredient in various dishes.', '["Reduction","Concasse","Deglazing","Dredging"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:15:36.967Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:15:36.967Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:15:36.967Z"'::jsonb),
