('anki-card-1756219110668-58', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Also known as Piyanggang, this is a dish from Tausug people of Mindanao, made with chicken or fish marinated in spices and burnt coconut, then grilled or stewed.', 'Piarun', '• Tiula Itum: A traditional Tausug dish from the Sulu Archipelago in the southern Philippines. Its distinctive black color comes from the use of burned or charred coconut meat, which is combined with spices such as ginger and turmeric to create a flavorful and aromatic soup.

