('anki-card-1756221141873-85', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'In cooking fibrous fruits like langka or beans in sugar syrup, tough product is obtained if:', 'sugar is added too early', 'Adding sugar too early in the cooking process can toughen fibrous fruits because it can cause the cell walls of the fruit to harden before they have a chance to soften sufficiently. This can lead to a chewy or tough texture instead of the desired tender consistency.

• Adding sugar too late might result in a less integrated flavor or less effective syrup concentration but generally doesn’t cause toughness. The texture issues are more related to when the sugar is added relative to the cooking time.
• Brown sugar can add a different flavor and color due to the presence of molasses, but it doesn’t usually make the product tougher. The toughness is more influenced by the timing of sugar addition.
• Stirring the syrup while cooking is generally done to ensure even cooking and to prevent burning.', '["sugar is added too early","sugar is added too late","brown sugar is used","the syrup is stirred while cooking"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:00:51.372Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:00:51.372Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:00:51.372Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756265644860-86', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'It assumes that employees are self-motivated, enjoy work, and seek responsibility. This theory suggests that workers are motivated by intrinsic factors and can be creative and productive if given the right environment.', 'Theory Y', '', '["Theory X","Scientific Approach","Human Relation Approach","Theory Y"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:52:18.893Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:52:18.893Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:52:18.893Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756265803723-87', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Refers to specific knowledge and expertise in a particular field or industry, important for lower levels of management, they become less critical.', 'Technical skill', 'Technical skill refers to specific knowledge and expertise in a particular field or industry. While technical skills are important for lower levels of management, they become less critical at the top level where managers focus more on overseeing and directing rather than performing technical tasks.

• Conceptual skill: Involves the ability to think strategically, understand complex situations, and develop innovative solutions. Top-level managers need strong conceptual skills to envision the organization’s future direction, set goals, and formulate strategic plans.
• Human skill: Also known as interpersonal or people skills, human skills involve the ability to work effectively with others, motivate and lead teams, and build relationships. These skills are important at all levels of management but are particularly crucial for middle managers who directly supervise employees.
• Administrative skill: Involves the ability to manage tasks, processes, and resources efficiently. It includes planning, organizing, coordinating, and controlling activities within the organization. Administrative skills are essential for all levels of management but are typically more operational in nature compared to conceptual skills.', '["Conceptual skill","Technical skill","Human skill","Administrative skill"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T12:59:44.947Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T12:59:44.947Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T12:59:44.947Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756265890283-88', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Also known as interpersonal or people skills, involves the ability to work effectively with others, motivate and lead teams, and build relationship. These skills are important at all levels of management but are particularly crucial for middle managers who directly supervice employees.', 'Human skill', 'Conceptual skill: Involves the ability to think strategically, understand complex situations, and develop innovative solutions. Top-level managers need strong conceptual skills to envision the organization’s future direction, set goals, and formulate strategic plans.

Technical skill: Refers to specific knowledge and expertise in a particular field or industry. While technical skills are important for lower levels of management, they become less critical at the top level where managers focus more on overseeing and directing rather than performing technical tasks.

Administrative skill: Involves the ability to manage tasks, processes, and resources efficiently. It includes planning, organizing, coordinating, and controlling activities within the organization. Administrative skills are essential for all levels of management but are typically more operational in nature compared to conceptual skills.', '["Conceptual skill","Technical skill","Human skill","Administrative skill"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:17:29.035Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:17:29.035Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:17:29.035Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756265955730-89', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Involves the ability to manage tasks, processes, and resources efficiently. Includes planning, organizing, coordinating, and controlling activities within the organization.', 'Administrative skill', 'Administrative skill', '["Conceptual skill","Technical skill","Human skill","Administrative skill"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:29:47.783Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:29:47.783Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756266112957-90', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Also known as a safety stock system, this approach involves maintaining an additional quantity of stock to protect against variations in demand or supply delays.', 'Buffer system', '', '["FIFO","Min-Max system","Par stock system","Buffer system"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T12:55:36.627Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T12:55:36.627Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T12:55:36.689Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756266370760-91', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Dishes are often prepared and partially cooked in the kitchen, but the final preparation and plating might be done at the table. It involves more elaborate and formal presentation.', 'French service', '', '["Russian service","American service","French service","Blue plate"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:28:33.269Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:28:33.269Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:28:33.269Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756266451739-92', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'All foods are prepared and portioned in the kitchen and arranged on serving platters. Food is then served to individual plates using cutlery. This method is characterized by its efficiency and the fact that all food is portioned and plated in the kitchen before being brought to the table.', 'Russian service', 'In Russian table service (also known as "platter service" or "service à la russe"), dishes are brought to the table already portioned and arranged on serving platters or dishes. These platters are placed in front of the guests, and they serve themselves using utensils provided. This style allows for a more elegant presentation and individualized servings.

• French Service: In French service, dishes are often prepared and partially cooked in the kitchen, but the final preparation and plating might be done at the table. It involves more elaborate and formal presentation.
• American Service: In American service, the food is completely prepared, portioned, and individually plated directly in the kitchen by the kitchen staff.
• Blue Plate: This term often refers to a type of casual dining service or a meal served on a blue plate, but it is not a specific style of table service.', '["Russian service","American service","French service","Blue plate"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:15:27.827Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:15:27.827Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T16:49:39.834Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756266555836-93', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'A mixture of spiced, herbs, and sometimes salt that is applied to the surface of meat to add flavor. It it not a curing salt but is used primarily for seasoning.', 'rub', 'A rub is a blend of dry spices, herbs, sugars, and salts applied generously to the exterior surface of meat before it is cooked (often smoked, grilled, or roasted).

Its main purpose is to season the meat, enhance flavor, and form a flavorful crust or "bark" on the surface during the cooking process.

Unlike curing agents (such as Prague powder), it does not act as a chemical preservative or color fixative for long-term meat preservation.', '["Prague powder","rub","kosher salt","fleur de sel"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:15:48.184Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:15:48.184Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:15:48.184Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756266610685-94', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'A coarse-grained salt commonly used in cooking and for meat. It it not typically used for curing but is favored for its clean flavor and ability to draw out moisture from foods.', 'kosher salt', 'Kosher salt gets its name from the traditional Jewish process of koshering meats (drawing blood out). Its coarse, flaky crystal structure lacks additives like iodine, yielding a very clean flavor.

Chefs prefer its tactile, large grains for even seasoning. Its specific surface structure makes it highly effective at drawing out surface moisture from meats via osmosis during dry-brining.

While it is widely used in daily cooking, it is distinct from specialized curing salts like Prague powder (which contains sodium nitrite to preserve meats and prevent bacterial growth)', '["Prague powder","rub","kosher salt","fleur de sel"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T12:53:57.964Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T12:53:57.964Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T12:53:57.964Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756266662098-95', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'A type of sea salt harvested from the surface of salt ponds. It is prized for its delicate flavor and texture and is often used as finishing salt, but is not used for curing.', 'fleur de sel', 'Fleur de sel (literally "flower of salt" in French) forms as a thin, fragile crystalline crust on the surface of salt ponds as seawater evaporates under specific sun and wind conditions.

It is meticulously hand-harvested by skimming the water''s surface before the crystals sink.

Because it is expensive, labor-intensive, and possesses a delicate texture and complex mineral flavor, it is strictly used as a finishing salt to elevate dishes immediately before serving. It is never wasted in cooking processes like boiling water or curing meats.', '["Prague powder","rub","kosher salt","fleur de sel"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:16:13.036Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:16:13.036Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:16:13.036Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791987542463-pxfml', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Salted fish roe especially of sturgeon or cod.', 'caviar', 'Caviar is a delicacy consisting of salt-cured fish roe (eggs), typically from sturgeon fish, although the term can also be used for roe from other fish species such as cod. It is known for its distinctive flavor, often described as briny and buttery, and is commonly served as a garnish or spread on dishes.

• Anchovies: Small, salted fish commonly used as a flavoring ingredient in various dishes.
• Scampi: A type of lobster or shrimp-like crustacean.
• Bagoong: Fermented fish or shrimp paste used in Filipino cuisine.', '["caviar","anchovies","scampi","bagoong"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:48:30.374Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:48:30.374Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:19:03.465Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:48:30.498Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791987608325-q3bzb', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Milk which undergoes a mechanical process in order to break up fat globules and prevent them from coalescing is called:', 'homogenized milk', 'Homogenization is a process where milk is forced through a fine filter under high pressure to break up the fat globules into smaller sizes. This process helps to distribute the fat evenly throughout the milk, preventing cream from rising to the top and creating a smoother texture.

• Skimmed milk refers to milk from which most of the fat has been removed
• Evaporated milk has had about 60% of its water content removed by evaporation
• Powdered milk is milk that has been dehydrated to form a powder', '["homogenized milk","skimmed milk","evaporated milk","powdered milk"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:48:34.945Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:48:34.945Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:20:09.391Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:48:35.065Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791987652129-ma143', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', '“Suahe” and “puti” are specifications for', 'shrimps', 'Suahe typically refers to a type of shrimp known as “white shrimp” in English. It’s a common term used in Filipino cuisine to describe certain varieties of shrimp.

Puti means “white” in Filipino and is used to describe the color of the shrimp, often referring to shrimp that are light or white in color.', '["shrimps","crabs","clams","fish"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:48:42.038Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:48:42.038Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:20:52.953Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:48:42.170Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791987897597-85x6s', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Effect of acid on chlorophyll', 'Changes green to olive green', 'The addition of acid turns chlorophyll into greenish gray (pheophytin a) or to brownish green or olive drab color (pheophytin b), in which Mg is replaced by hydrogen.

The addition of baking soda forms chlorophyllin, which has a bright green color.

• Effect of Acid: Olive green
• Effect of Alkali: Intensifies green color
• Effect of Prolonged Cooking: Olive green
• Solubility in Water: Slight', '["Changes green to olive green","Disintegration","Intensifies green color","No effect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:48:50.918Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:48:50.918Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:24:59.101Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:48:51.040Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791987960795-br9xc', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Type of microorganism that will grow in orange marmalade.', 'Osmophilic', 'Orange marmalade has a high sugar content, which creates an environment with low water activity. This condition is most favorable for osmophilic microorganisms. Osmophilic microorganisms thrive in environments with high osmotic pressure, such as those with high concentrations of sugar.

Therefore, the type of microorganism that will grow in orange marmalade is osmophilic.

• Halophilic organisms thrive in high salt concentrations
• Xerophilic organisms are adapted to survive in extremely dry environments
• Thermophilic organisms flourish in high-temperature conditions', '["Osmophilic","Halophilic","Xerophilic","Thermophilic"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:49:01.205Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:49:01.205Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:26:01.764Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:49:01.328Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791988008065-us5e5', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'The pigment responsible for the white color of fruits and vegetables', 'Anthoxanthin', 'Anthoxanthins are a group of water-soluble pigments that give fruits and vegetables their white or cream color. They are often present in foods such as cauliflower, potatoes, onions, and turnips. Anthoxanthins are colorless in acidic conditions and turn yellowish or white in alkaline conditions.

• Chlorophyll: Gives green color to plants and vegetables.
• Anthocyanin: Responsible for red, purple, and blue colors in fruits and vegetables.
• Carotenoid: Responsible for orange, yellow, and some red colors in fruits and vegetables.', '["Anthoxanthin","Chlorophyll","Anthocyanin","Carotenoid"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:49:07.053Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:49:07.053Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:26:48.901Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:49:07.179Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791988055748-nllm3', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'A process that causes drying and hardening of cooked starch', 'retrogradation', 'Retrogradation is the process where gelatinized starch molecules, upon cooling, undergo re-association and realignment, resulting in the firming or hardening of the starch. This is often observed in foods like bread and starchy foods that have been cooked and then cooled.

• Gelation: The process in which a gel forms when heated and then cools, resulting in a semi-solid structure.
• Caramelization: The browning and breakdown of sugars under high heat, resulting in the formation of a characteristic caramel flavor and color.
• Gelatinization: The process in which starch granules absorb water and swell when heated in the presence of water, resulting in the thickening of a liquid.', '["retrogradation","gelation","caramelization","gelatinization"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:49:12.667Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:49:12.667Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:27:36.804Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:49:12.790Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791988105626-bhxid', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'The Father of Canning is:', 'Nicholas Appert', 'Nicholas Appert, a French chef and confectioner, is credited with developing the method of preserving food by sealing it in sterilized containers. His work in the late 18th and early 19th centuries led to the discovery that food could be preserved by heat treatment to kill bacteria and other microorganisms, thereby preventing spoilage.

• Louis Appert, often confused with Nicholas Appert, was actually his son who helped to commercialize and refine his father’s methods.
• Louis Pasteur, on the other hand, made significant contributions to microbiology and food preservation techniques, particularly pasteurization, which involves heating liquids to kill pathogens and extend shelf life. However, he is not directly associated with canning.', '["Nicholas Appert","Louis Appert","Louis Pasteur","Nicholas Pasteur"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:49:21.133Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:49:21.133Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:28:26.498Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:49:21.257Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791988169917-tt741', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Food in its raw state, minus that which is discarded (bones, fat, skins, and/or seeds):', 'Edible portion (EP)', 'The edible portion of food refers to the part of the food item that is consumed after preparation, excluding any inedible or non-consumable parts like bones, peels, seeds, or other undesirable parts.', '["Edible portion (EP)","As purchased (AP)","Percentage Yield","Raw food weight"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:49:24.998Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:49:24.998Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:29:31.285Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:49:25.126Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791988230739-61d9z', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Heat transfer which involves the progressive transfer of heat from the source to the pan to the food is called:', 'conduction', 'Conduction is the process by which heat energy is transferred through direct contact between materials of different temperatures. In cooking, this occurs when the heat from a stove burner or other heat source is conducted through the metal pan and then to the food being cooked.

• Convection: Convection involves the transfer of heat through a fluid (liquid or gas) by the circulation of currents. In cooking, this occurs when heat is transferred by the movement of air or liquid, such as in a convection oven or boiling water.
• Radiation involves the transfer of heat through electromagnetic waves. In cooking, this can occur through infrared radiation from a broiler or microwave radiation in a microwave oven.', '["conduction","convection","radiation","combination of convection and reduction"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:49:33.683Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:49:33.683Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:30:31.798Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:49:33.803Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791988286085-qt42q', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Sentence A. In traditional ice cream making, salt is added to ice in the “garapinyera” during the freezing of ice cream mixture.
Sentence B. The addition of salt to ice prevents the melting of ice, thus ensuring quick freezing.', 'Sentence A is correct.', 'Sentence A is correct. In traditional ice cream making, particularly in the use of an ice cream maker like the ‘garapinyera,’ salt is added to ice to lower the freezing point of the ice, which helps in freezing the ice cream mixture.

Statement B is incorrect. The addition of salt to ice actually causes the ice to melt at a lower temperature. The process of melting absorbs heat from the surrounding environment (in this case, the ice cream mixture), which helps to freeze the ice cream more quickly. Salt lowers the freezing point of water, which allows the ice to absorb more heat as it melts, leading to a more effective freezing process.

When you add salt to ice, it lowers the freezing point of the water (a process known as freezing point depression). Normally, ice melts and freezes at 0°C (32°F), but when salt is added, the melting point drops below this temperature. As a result, the ice melts because the surrounding temperature is above the new, lower freezing point.

However, as the ice melts, it absorbs heat from its surroundings (an endothermic process), which creates a colder environment. This is why the salted ice can freeze the ice cream mixture faster, even though it actually causes the ice to melt more quickly.', '["Sentence A is correct.","Sentence B is correct.","Both sentences are correct.","Both sentences are incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:49:50.473Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:49:50.473Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:31:26.877Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:49:50.595Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791988324184-ty7fk', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'A cake is done if:', 'an inserted knife comes out clean', 'When baking a cake, one common method to check for doneness is to insert a clean knife or toothpick into the center of the cake. If it comes out clean, with no batter sticking to it (a few crumbs are usually okay), then the cake is baked through and is done.', '["an inserted knife comes out clean","the mixture coats the inserted knife","the crust attains a golden brown color","the crust attains a dark brown color"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:49:54.261Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:49:54.261Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:32:04.995Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:49:54.381Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791988370926-2if2r', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Sentence A. During rigor mortis, actomyosin dissociates to actin and myosin resulting in tough meat.
Sentence B. Rigor mortis is the stiffening of muscle.', 'Sentence B is correct.', '“During rigor mortis, actomyosin dissociates to actin and myosin resulting in tough meat.”

This statement is incorrect. During rigor mortis, actomyosin, a complex formed by actin and myosin, is what actually causes muscle stiffening. The dissociation of actomyosin into actin and myosin happens after rigor mortis, during the resolution phase when the muscle starts to soften again.

“Rigor mortis is the stiffening of muscle.”

This statement is correct. Rigor mortis is the post-mortem stiffening of muscles due to chemical changes in the muscle fibers, primarily the formation of actomyosin as ATP is depleted.', '["Sentence B is correct.","Sentence A is correct.","Both sentences are correct.","Both sentences are incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:49:57.755Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:49:57.755Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:32:52.203Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:49:57.875Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791988427878-sit5h', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'In curing, the desirable pink color is due to', 'nitrosomyoglobin', 'Nitrosomyoglobin is formed when myoglobin (a protein in meat) reacts with nitric oxide (NO) during curing or processing. It is responsible for the stable pink color in cured meats like ham or bacon.

• Hemoglobin: A protein in red blood cells that carries oxygen, but it is not directly responsible for the pink color in cured meat.
• Oxymyoglobin: A pigment in meat that gives it a bright red color when freshly cut and exposed to oxygen.
• Metmyoglobin: A brown pigment that forms when oxymyoglobin loses its oxygen molecule, causing meat to appear brown rather than pink.', '["nitrosomyoglobin","hemoglobin","oxymyoglobin","metmyoglobin"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:50:01.015Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:01.015Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:33:49.737Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:01.138Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791988477335-pnwe5', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Sentence A. Shortening impedes gluten development by hydrolysis.
Sentence B. Impeding gluten development would result in flaky products.', 'Sentence B is correct.', 'Hydrolysis is a chemical process in which a compound is broken down by reacting with water.

Sentence A is incorrect. Shortening (typically fats like butter or vegetable shortening) does not impede gluten development by hydrolysis. Instead, fats in dough or batter interfere with gluten formation by coating the gluten proteins and preventing them from forming strong bonds. This interference is not due to hydrolysis but rather to physical interactions.

Sentence B is correct. When gluten development is limited, the resulting dough has less elasticity and structure, producing a tender, flaky texture. This is particularly desirable in products such as pie crust, pastry crust, biscuits

Flakiness in baked goods like pastries is typically achieved by creating layers of fat and dough, such as in laminated doughs or pie crusts, not by impeding gluten development.', '["Sentence B is correct.","Sentence A is correct.","Both sentences are correct.","Both sentences are incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:50:11.345Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:11.345Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:34:38.391Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:11.464Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791988515641-tikhz', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Used to limit the migration of moisture into the product', 'packaging', 'To limit the migration of moisture into a product, the most effective method among the options provided is packaging. Proper packaging can create a barrier that prevents external moisture from entering the product, thereby preserving its quality and shelf life.

Heating, freezing, and drying are processes that can alter the moisture content of the product itself but do not prevent external moisture migration as effectively as proper packaging does.', '["packaging","heating","freezing","drying"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:50:14.699Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:14.699Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:35:16.618Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:14.825Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791988546062-hcwru', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Pasteurization is applied in processing foods that are generally:', 'acidic', 'Pasteurization is a process of heat treatment that aims to reduce the microbial load in food products without significantly affecting their taste or nutritional value. It is commonly used for acidic foods such as fruit juices, dairy products (like milk and yogurt), and certain sauces. The heat treatment destroys harmful bacteria and extends the shelf life of the product, making it safer for consumption.', '["acidic","salty","basic","spicy"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:50:18.038Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:18.038Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:35:47.340Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:18.156Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791988601014-pctkj', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Sentence A. In native cheese making, milk may be coagulated with the enzyme rennet.
Sentence B. In native cheese making, vinegar may be used to curdle the milk.', 'Both sentences are correct.', '“In native cheese making, milk may be coagulated with the enzyme rennet.”

This statement is correct. Rennet, which contains the enzyme chymosin, is commonly used in cheese making to coagulate milk, causing it to separate into curds and whey.

“In native cheese making, vinegar may be used to curdle the milk.”

This statement is correct. Vinegar, an acidic substance, can be used to curdle milk by lowering its pH, which causes the proteins in the milk to coagulate and form curds.', '["Both sentences are correct.","Sentence A is correct.","Sentence B is correct.","Both sentences are incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:50:22.619Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:22.619Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:36:42.472Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:22.745Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791988650675-78y3f', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'French word that means “everything in place”', 'Mise en place', '“Mise en place” is a culinary term that refers to the preparation and organization of ingredients and equipment before cooking. It involves arranging everything needed for cooking in an orderly and accessible manner to ensure efficiency and smooth workflow in the kitchen.

• Mirepoix: A mixture of diced vegetables (typically onions, carrots, and celery) used as a flavor base in cooking.
• Mise en poix: This term does not exist in culinary terminology.', '["Mise en place","Mirepoix","Mise en poix","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:50:25.909Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:25.909Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:37:31.498Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:26.036Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791988724876-lavm4', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'The increase in loaf volume during baking is called:', 'oven spring', 'The increase in loaf volume during baking is called oven spring. This phenomenon occurs when the dough rapidly expands in the oven due to the heat, which causes the gases trapped in the dough to expand and the yeast to produce more gas before it is killed by the heat.

• Bloat refers to excessive expansion of dough due to over-fermentation
• Loaf blow-up occurs when the dough rises too quickly, often leading to an uneven texture 
• Proofing is the controlled process of allowing dough to rise before baking to develop flavor and texture', '["oven spring","bloat","loaf blow-up","proofing"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:50:28.668Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:28.668Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:38:45.771Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:28.791Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791988781299-g1edd', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Foodborne illness caused by a neurotoxin found in food.', 'Botulism', 'Botulism is the foodborne illness caused by a neurotoxin produced by the bacterium Clostridium botulinum. This toxin affects the nervous system and can cause severe symptoms, including muscle weakness, difficulty swallowing, and respiratory failure. Proper food preservation and canning techniques are crucial to preventing botulism.

• Salmonellosis: Caused by the bacterium Salmonella. It leads to symptoms such as diarrhea, abdominal cramps, fever, and vomiting. Common sources include raw or undercooked eggs, meat, and unpasteurized dairy products.
• Listeriosis: Caused by the bacterium Listeria monocytogenes. It can cause symptoms like fever, muscle aches, and gastrointestinal issues. It is particularly dangerous for pregnant women, newborns, the elderly, and immunocompromised individuals. Common sources include unpasteurized dairy products, ready-to-eat meats, and contaminated produce.
• Yersiniosis: Caused by the bacterium Yersinia enterocolitica. It leads to symptoms like abdominal pain, diarrhea (often bloody), and fever. It is commonly associated with undercooked pork products, unpasteurized milk, and contaminated water.', '["Botulism","Salmonellosis","Listeriosis","Yersiniosis"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:50:35.652Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:35.652Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:39:42.493Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:35.770Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791988825944-28wbb', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'A process of checking the interior quality of eggs', 'candling', 'Candling involves passing an egg over a bright light source to examine its interior. This process helps to assess the quality of the egg, including the size of the air cell, the condition of the yolk, and the presence of any defects or abnormalities inside the shell.

• Grading is the process of evaluating eggs based on their quality, size, and appearance. This includes factors like the freshness, cleanliness, and strength of the eggshell, but it does not specifically focus on checking the interior quality.
• Sorting refers to the process of organizing eggs by size or grade, but it does not specifically assess the interior quality of the eggs.', '["candling","grading","sorting","none of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:50:38.290Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:38.290Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:40:26.767Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:38.404Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791988892923-hjgwx', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Salad dressing made of mayonnaise, chopped capers, and gherkins:', 'tartar', 'Tartar is a sauce traditionally made with mayonnaise or aioli, chopped pickles (gherkins or capers), and sometimes additional herbs or spices.

• Ranch: A creamy dressing typically made with buttermilk or sour cream, mayonnaise, and various herbs and spices.
• Thousand Island: A dressing that typically includes mayonnaise, ketchup or tomato paste, and sweet pickle relish, among other ingredients.
• Aioli: A Mediterranean sauce made with garlic, olive oil, and often egg yolks, similar to mayonnaise but with a garlic flavor.', '["tartar","ranch","thousand island","aioli"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:50:43.859Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:43.859Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:41:34.157Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:43.979Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791988943475-2yosa', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Sentence A. Crustacean releases the pigment astaxanthin which gives its orange color when cooked.
Sentence B. This is due to the breakdown of the ovoverdine-asthaxanthin complex during cooking.', 'Both sentences are correct.', 'Color change in crustaceans from natural dark blue green color to an attractive orange color is due to the release of an orange pigment astaxanthin from ovoverdine, a protein, when heated.', '["Both sentences are correct.","Sentence A is correct.","Sentence B is correct.","Both sentences are incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:50:47.851Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:47.851Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:42:24.567Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:47.971Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791988994524-02094', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Egg noodles made from flour, duck eggs, salt, and soda', 'pancit canton', 'Pancit canton is a type of egg noodle commonly used in Filipino cuisine. It is characterized by its yellow color due to the addition of duck eggs and its slightly chewy texture. The ingredients listed (flour, duck eggs, salt, and soda) are consistent with those used in making pancit canton.

• Sotanghon noodles, also known as cellophane or glass noodles, are made from mung bean starch. They are transparent when cooked and are not made from flour, duck eggs, salt, or soda.
• Miswa noodles are thin, salted wheat noodles often used in soups.
• Instant noodles are pre-cooked, While they can be made from wheat flour, they do not typically include duck eggs and soda in their preparation.', '["pancit canton","sotanghon","miswa","instant noodles"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:50:50.508Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:50.508Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:43:15.434Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:50.629Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791989034468-6mxhm', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Sentence A. Hydrogenation prevents oxidative rancidity.
Sentence B. Oxidative rancidity is more prone in oils with high saturated fatty acids', 'Sentence A is correct.', 'Hydrogenation can help in reducing oxidative rancidity by converting unsaturated fats, which are more prone to oxidation, into more stable saturated fats. This makes the statement correct to an extent since hydrogenated fats are less likely to undergo oxidative rancidity compared to their unsaturated counterparts.

This statement is incorrect because oxidative rancidity primarily affects oils high in unsaturated fatty acids, not saturated fatty acids. Saturated fats are more stable and less likely to oxidize.', '["Sentence A is correct.","Sentence B is correct.","Both sentences are correct.","Both sentences are incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:50:55.162Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:55.162Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:43:55.665Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:55.279Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791989076614-6kvqh', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'A dark purple-colored rice used in Puto Bumbong:', 'Pirurutong', 'Pirurutong rice is a type of glutinous rice that has a distinct purple hue due to its natural pigmentation. It is traditionally used in Filipino cuisine, particularly in dishes like Puto Bumbong, which is a type of steamed rice cake typically served during Christmas season in the Philippines. The purple color of Pirurutong adds a unique visual appeal and subtle flavor to the dish.

• Pinipig: Rice grains that are pounded flat and used in various Filipino desserts.
• Wagwag: A term sometimes used for dried, pounded rice.
• Gindara: A type of fish (sablefish or black cod), not rice.', '["Pirurutong","Pinipig","Wagwag","Gindara"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:50:58.002Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:58.002Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:44:37.730Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:50:58.117Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791989124347-lz2ow', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Genus with species capable of oxidizing ethanol to acetic acid', 'Acetobacter', 'Acetobacter is a genus of acetic acid bacteria known for its ability to convert ethanol into acetic acid through the process of oxidation. This characteristic is utilized in the production of vinegar.

• Lactococcus is a genus of bacteria that plays a crucial role in dairy fermentation processes. These bacteria are lactic acid bacteria, meaning they convert lactose (milk sugar) into lactic acid. This acidification process is essential in the production of various dairy products, such as cheese, buttermilk, and sour cream, as it helps to develop the flavor, texture, and preservation of these foods.

• Escherichia is a genus of bacteria that includes several species, with Escherichia coli (commonly known as E. coli) being the most well-known. E. coli is a diverse group of bacteria found in the intestines of humans and animals. While many strains of E. coli are harmless and play a role in maintaining gut health, some strains can cause foodborne illnesses, leading to symptoms like diarrhea, abdominal pain, and, in severe cases, kidney failure.

• Saccharomyces is a genus of yeast that is widely used in baking, brewing, and fermentation processes. The most well-known species is Saccharomyces cerevisiae, commonly referred to as baker’s yeast or brewer’s yeast.', '["Acetobacter","Escherichia","Lactococcus","Saccharomyces"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:51:02.312Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:51:02.312Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:45:25.161Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:51:02.433Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791989184120-ioz7j', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Strong flavoured vegetables like cabbage and radish should be cooked in an uncovered cooking vessel to', 'allow volatilization of sulfur compounds', 'Cabbage and radish contain sulfur compounds that can impart a strong odor when cooked. Cooking these vegetables uncovered allows the sulfur compounds to volatilize and escape into the air, reducing their strong odor and improving the overall flavor of the dish.', '["allow volatilization of sulfur compounds","retain best flavor","attain best texture","conserve nutrients"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:51:06.227Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:51:06.227Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:46:25.684Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:51:06.356Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791989243806-4f6yq', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'If the current yield of a recipe is 8 servings and the desired yield is 20 servings, what is the recipe conversion factor?', '2.5', 'Conversion factor = Desired yield/Current
= 20 servings / 8 servings
= 2.5', '["2.5","2","3","4"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:51:08.936Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:51:08.936Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:47:24.682Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:51:09.063Z"'::jsonb),
('card-1791989294177-6r2n9', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Element of the foodservice system that refers to the resources needed to be able to achieve the objectives of the organization', 'Input', 'In the context of a foodservice system, “input” refers to the resources such as ingredients, equipment, labor, and facilities that are necessary to produce and deliver food and services to customers. These resources are essential for the functioning of the foodservice operation and for meeting its goals and objectives.

Input refers to the resources (such as ingredients, equipment, labor, and capital) that are necessary for the foodservice system to operate and meet its goals. Inputs are essential for the production and delivery of food services.

• Control involves managing and regulating the process to ensure that the desired outcomes are achieved.
• Thruput (often referred to as “throughput”) refers to the amount of output or production that flows through a system in a given time period.
• Feedback is information about the outcome or performance of the system that can be used to make adjustments and improvements.', '["Input","Control","Thruput","Feedback"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, 'Foods and Food Service Systems', 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:51:13.805Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:51:13.805Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:48:15.476Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:51:13.930Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757930738284-0', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609398838-1790433146200-hye2o', 'What would be the appropriate weight gain of a person who consumes an excess of 500kcal daily for a month?*', '4 lbs', 'A surplus of approximately 3,500 kcal is required to gain one pound of body weight. Consuming an excess of 500 kcal daily for 30 days results in a total surplus of 15,000 kcal (500 x 30). Dividing 15,000 kcal by 3,500 kcal/lb yields approximately 4.28 pounds, which aligns with the test key of 4 lbs.', '["0.5 lb","2 lbs","3 lbs","4 lbs"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.883Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T03:12:01.609Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757930750482-1', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609398838-1790433146200-hye2o', 'What is considered to be a healthy rate of weight loss for most overweight people on a long-term basis?*', '0.5-1 lb/week', 'Public health and clinical dietetics guidelines recommend a gradual, sustainable weight loss rate of 0.5 to 1 pound per week for overweight individuals to ensure fat loss while preserving lean muscle mass and metabolic health.', '["0.5-1 lb/week","3 lbs/week","5 lbs/week","7-8 lbs/week"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.883Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T03:12:06.859Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757930765982-2', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609398838-1790433146200-hye2o', 'Which of the following describes the process of thermogenesis?*', 'Generation of heat', 'Thermogenesis refers specifically to the metabolic generation of heat by the body to maintain core body temperature, expend energy, and regulate adaptive thermic responses.

• Burning of fat: Describes lipid oxidation (lipolysis), which can fuel thermogenesis but is not the definition of the term itself.
• Synthesis of fat: Describes lipogenesis (anabolic fat storage).
• Generation of water: Refers to metabolic water production during oxidative phosphorylation.', '["Burning of fat","Synthesis of fat","Generation of heat","Generation of water"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.883Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T03:12:14.077Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757930778897-3', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609398838-1790433146200-hye2o', 'Which of the following is a feature of the basal metabolic rate?*', 'Pregnancy increases BMR', 'Basal Metabolic Rate (BMR) increases significantly during pregnancy due to the metabolic demands of supporting fetal growth, increased maternal tissue mass, and elevated cardiac workload.', '["Fever decreases BMR","Fasting increases BMR","Pregnancy increases BMR","Females have higher BMR than males"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.883Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T03:12:24.350Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757930792346-4', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609398838-1790433146200-hye2o', 'If a dancer and a typist are the same height and have the exact same body build, the dancer will be heavier because she has*', 'more muscle mass', 'Muscle tissue is significantly denser and heavier than adipose tissue. If a dancer and a typist have identical height and body frames but the dancer is heavier, it is because she possesses more muscle mass from rigorous physical conditioning.', '["more body fat","stronger bones","stronger muscles","more muscle mass"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.883Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T03:12:29.986Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757930806313-5', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609398838-1790433146200-hye2o', 'What is the approximate value for the thermic effect of a 2,500 kcal diet?*', '250 kcal', 'The thermic effect of food (TEF)—also known as dietary-induced thermogenesis—accounts for approximately 10% of total daily energy expenditure. For a 2,500 kcal diet, TEF is roughly 250 kcal (2,500 x 0.10).', '["25 kcal","250 kcal","400 kcal","500 kcal"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.883Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T03:12:35.291Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757930820129-6', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609398838-1790433146200-hye2o', 'What is the approximate basal metabolism of a 110 lb woman?*', '1080 kcal/day', 'Using standard rapid estimation formulas for basal energy expenditure (roughly 22 kcal per kg for women or empirical baseline estimates based on body weight), a 110 lb (approx. 50 kg) woman has a basal metabolism of roughly 1,080 kcal/day (50 kg x 22 kcal/kg = 1,100 kcal, closely approximating the 1,080 kcal key).', '["850 kcal/day","960kcal/day","1080 kcal/day","1240 kcal/day"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.883Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T03:12:42.116Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757930836212-7', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609398838-1790433146200-hye2o', 'Which of the following is a feature of the BMI?*', 'It correlates with disease risks.', 'Body Mass Index (BMI) is a standardized screening tool because epidemiological data demonstrates that abnormal BMI values (both underweight and overweight/obesity) correlate strongly with increased morbidity and chronic disease risks.', '["It correlates with disease risks.","It decreases by 1 unit for every 10 years of life.","It provides an estimate of the fat level of the body.","It is defined as the person’s height divided by the square of the weight."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.883Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T03:12:46.663Z"'::jsonb)
