[Image: Varenne (François Pierre de La)]D. Francois Pierre La Varenne', 'Auguste Escoffier
[Image: Georges Auguste Escoffier''s culinary legacy]

❌ Marie Antoine Carême: Known for codifying French haute cuisine, defining the early mother sauces, and creating elaborate pastry centerpieces (pièces montées).
❌ Anthelme Brillat-Savarin: A famous French lawyer and politician who became one of the world''s most celebrated epicures and food philosophers (famous for the quote, "Tell me what you eat, and I will tell you what you are").
❌ François Pierre La Varenne: A 17th-century chef who broke away from heavily spiced medieval cooking, wrote Le Cuisinier François, and laid the foundational roots for early modern French cuisine.', 'Auguste Escoffier', '["Auguste Escoffier\n<img alt=\"Georges Auguste Escoffier''s culinary legacy\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" width=\"134\">\n\n❌ Marie Antoine Carême: Known for codifying French haute cuisine, defining the early mother sauces, and creating elaborate pastry centerpieces (pièces montées).\n❌ Anthelme Brillat-Savarin: A famous French lawyer and politician who became one of the world''s most celebrated epicures and food philosophers (famous for the quote, \"Tell me what you eat, and I will tell you what you are\").\n❌ François Pierre La Varenne: A 17th-century chef who broke away from heavily spiced medieval cooking, wrote Le Cuisinier François, and laid the foundational roots for early modern French cuisine.","garde manger","controlling food cost for employees’ meals","To clean the storeroom"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:35:40.426Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-10T01:05:29.228Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879008500-0', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why is steaming preferred over boiling for cooking green vegetables when the goal is to maximize nutrient retention?', 'Steaming prevents loss of water-soluble vitamins into the cooking liquid.', 'Steaming cooks green vegetables using hot water vapor rather than direct immersion. Because the food does not come into direct contact with a large body of cooking water, leaching of water-soluble vitamins (such as Vitamin C and B-complex vitamins) is minimized, resulting in higher nutrient retention compared to boiling.', '["Steaming maintains a higher cooking temperature.","Boiling enhances the flavor through leaching.","Steaming prevents loss of water-soluble vitamins into the cooking liquid.","Boiling preserves more enzymes needed for digestion"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:22:38.366Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:22:38.366Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:36:41.357Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879033895-1', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'A food technologist is designing a process to minimize enzymatic browning in freshly sliced apples while enhancing flavor and color during baking. Which of the following best explains why applying heat serves this dual purpose?', 'Heat inactivates enzymes responsible for enzymatic browning and initiates Maillard browning, contributing to color and flavor.', 'Applying heat to apples during baking performs two distinct culinary and chemical functions: it denatures and inactivates polyphenol oxidase (the enzyme responsible for enzymatic browning), stopping undesirable discoloration, while also driving the non-enzymatic Maillard reaction between reducing sugars and amino acids to enhance color and flavor.', '["Heat promotes Maillard browning and accelerates the activity of polyphenol oxidase, increasing overall browning.","Heat inactivates enzymes responsible for enzymatic browning and initiates Maillard browning, contributing to color and flavor.","Enzymatic browning occurs at high temperatures, while Maillard browning is prevented by heat due to sugar caramelization.","Heating encourages enzymatic browning through protein denaturation and prevents the Maillard reaction by breaking down amino acids."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:34:39.995Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:34:39.995Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:36:45.698Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879054795-2', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which of the following best explains why kneading is essential for proper gluten development in yeast-leavened dough?', 'Kneading aligns gluten strands, forming an elastic network that traps gas.', 'Kneading stretches and manipulates yeast-leavened dough, which aligns the water-insoluble proteins gliadin and glutenin to form a cohesive, elastic gluten network capable of trapping carbon dioxide produced by yeast fermentation, allowing the bread to rise.', '["Kneading warms the dough, accelerating yeast fermentation.","Kneading introduces more flour, which strengthens the dough.","Kneading aligns gluten strands, forming an elastic network that traps gas.","Kneading dissolves gluten proteins to form a smoother texture."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:22:51.119Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:22:51.119Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:37:01.308Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879076047-3', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which of the following best explains why a starch-thickened sauce becomes watery when subjected to excessive heat for a prolonged period?', 'Excessive heat disrupts starch micelles, leading to a breakdown of the gel structure and resulting in a watery consistency.', 'Prolonged heating and excessive high temperatures beyond gelatinization cause swollen starch granules to rupture completely, fragmenting the starch chains (micelles) and destroying the viscous gel network, which causes the sauce to thin out and become watery.', '["Gelatinization causes starch granules to swell and burst, increasing the viscosity of the mixture.","Dextrinization enhances the thickening power of starch by breaking it into smaller chains.","Excessive heat disrupts starch micelles, leading to a breakdown of the gel structure and resulting in a watery consistency.","Higher temperatures always increase the thickening ability of starch due to continuous gelatinization."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:33:05.393Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:33:05.393Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:37:06.018Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879096026-4', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why should acidic ingredients like tomato juice or molasses be added only after beans have become tender during cooking?', 'Acids toughen cellulose, delaying softening and prolonging cooking time', 'Acids make the cell wall components (such as hemicellulose and pectic substances bound with cellulose) more resistant to softening. Adding acidic ingredients too early in bean preparation firms the plant tissues, significantly prolonging the cooking time required for softening.', '["Acids increase the rate of gelatinization, softening beans too quickly","Acids neutralize the beans’ natural flavor and aroma","Acids toughen cellulose, delaying softening and prolonging cooking time","Acids remove pigments that affect color and texture of beans"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:25:32.896Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:25:32.896Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:37:10.826Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879115026-5', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why is open kettle cooking recommended when preparing strong-flavored vegetables such as cabbage or radish?', 'It allows sulfur compounds to escape, reducing strong odors and flavors', 'Cruciferous and strong-flavored vegetables (like cabbage, cauliflower, and radishes) contain volatile sulfur compounds. Cooking them uncovered (open kettle method) allows these pungent sulfur gases to vaporize and escape into the air rather than concentrating in the cooking water.', '["It prevents oxidation of nutrients by limiting air exposure","It allows sulfur compounds to escape, reducing strong odors and flavors","It retains more chlorophyll for greener appearance","It speeds up cooking by increasing pressure inside the pot"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:31:15.936Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:31:15.936Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:37:14.590Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879132791-6', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why does cooking beans in hard water take longer compared to soft water?', 'Calcium and magnesium ions in hard water form insoluble salts with pectin, slowing the softening.', 'Hard water contains high concentrations of dissolved multivalent cations, specifically calcium and magnesium. These ions cross-link with pectic substances in plant cell walls to form insoluble salts (pectates), binding the tissues tightly together and preventing the beans from softening.', '["The minerals in hard water enhance bean flavor but reduce the temperature.","Calcium and magnesium ions in hard water form insoluble salts with pectin, slowing the softening.","Hard water contains fewer electrolytes needed for heat transfer.","Beans absorb less water in hard water due to its higher boiling point"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:35:22.631Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:35:22.631Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:37:18.908Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879152691-7', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why is it advisable to add acidic ingredients (like vinegar or calamansi) at the end of cooking green vegetables such as kangkong in dishes like sinigang?', 'Acids promote the formation of pheophytin, causing a dull or olive green color if added early.', 'Chlorophyll, the green pigment in vegetables like kangkong, is sensitive to acids. When acids are introduced in the presence of heat, the central magnesium ion in the chlorophyll molecule is replaced by hydrogen ions, converting it into pheophytin, which exhibits an unappealing dull olive-brown color.', '["Acids enhance the texture of vegetables by making them firmer.","Acids speed up the cooking process by increasing the temperature.","Acids preserve chlorophyll, maintaining the bright green color of vegetables.","Acids promote the formation of pheophytin, causing a dull or olive green color if added early."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:29:41.931Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:29:41.931Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:37:23.210Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879167656-8', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Tough cuts of red meat are best prepared using moist-heat methods because they:', 'Have high amounts of connective tissue that require longer cooking to soften.', 'Tough cuts of meat come from heavily exercised muscles containing high amounts of durable connective tissue (collagen and elastin). Moist-heat cooking methods use sustained, gentle heat and moisture to slowly hydrolyze tough collagen into soluble gelatin, rendering the meat tender.', '["Are low in protein and fat.","Have high amounts of connective tissue that require longer cooking to soften.","Easily disintegrate in dry heat.","Contain more water-soluble vitamins."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:28:01.859Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:28:01.859Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:37:28.031Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879185721-9', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Searing red meat before braising enhances flavor by:', 'Promoting Maillard browning reactions on the surface.', 'Searing meat exposes its surface amino acids and reducing sugars to high dry heat, triggering Maillard browning reactions that create complex savory flavor compounds and a rich crust.', '["Boiling away surface bacteria.","Sealing in internal moisture.","Promoting Maillard browning reactions on the surface.","Breaking down muscle fibers instantly."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:41:28.683Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:41:28.683Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:37:33.123Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879201153-10', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Tough cuts of red meat are best prepared using moist-heat methods because they:', 'Have high amounts of connective tissue that require longer cooking to soften.', 'Connective tissues (primarily collagen) require prolonged thermal exposure in the presence of moisture to break down successfully, which is why tough cuts necessitate moist-heat cookery.', '["Are low in protein and fat.","Have high amounts of connective tissue that require longer cooking to soften.","Easily disintegrate in dry heat.","Contain more water-soluble vitamins"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:30:03.865Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:30:03.865Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:37:37.154Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879218903-11', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Grilling is most suitable for tender cuts of red meat because it:', 'Uses high, direct heat to quickly sear the exterior.', 'Grilling applies intense, direct radiant heat to the surface of tender cuts of meat, rapidly cooking the exterior while keeping the interior juicy.', '["Requires minimal fat content.","Cooks meat through internal steam.","Prevents any protein denaturation.","Uses high, direct heat to quickly sear the exterior."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T15:06:19.268Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T15:06:19.268Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:37:41.009Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879239403-12', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Braising improves the tenderness of red meat by:', 'Slowly cooking the meat in a small amount of liquid.', 'Braising is a combination cooking method where meat is first seared and then covered and slowly simmered over low heat in a small quantity of cooking liquid, softening tough connective tissues.', '["Slowly cooking the meat in a small amount of liquid.","Steaming the meat at high pressure.","Applying intense dry heat directly.","Charring the outer surface at high temperature."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:27:09.296Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:27:09.296Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:37:44.974Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879268902-13', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which cooking method uses radiant heat from above and is ideal for melting fat and creating a crust on meats like pork chops or steaks?', 'Broiling', 'Broiling is a dry-heat cooking method utilizing direct radiant heat from an overhead heat source, ideal for browning surfaces and melting fats on steaks and chops.', '["Boiling","Broiling","Steaming","Roasting"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T15:05:42.643Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T15:05:42.643Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:45:35.235Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879283984-14', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'What combination cooking method begins by searing meat, then simmering it in a small amount of liquid, ideal for tough pork or beef cuts?', 'Braising', 'Braising combines initial high-heat browning (searing) followed by slow cooking in a covered pot with a small amount of liquid, making it ideal for breaking down tough cuts.', '["Broiling","Braising","Poaching","Deep frying"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:32:12.425Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:32:12.425Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:37:52.157Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879305799-15', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'When a tough cut of meat like beef brisket is cooked in liquid over low heat for a long period, the method used is:', 'Stewing', 'Stewing involves completely submerging bite-sized or whole tough cuts of meat in liquid and simmering them gently over low heat for an extended period.', '["Roasting","Steaming","Stewing","Sautéing"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:20:23.208Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:20:23.208Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:37:55.692Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879320564-16', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which cooking method is most suitable for tender cuts of meat, such as pork loin or beef sirloin, to preserve juiciness and flavor?', 'Grilling', 'Grilling uses dry, direct heat and is well-suited for tender, premium cuts of meat because they cook quickly without requiring long breakdown periods.', '["Boiling","Grilling","Braising","Stewing"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:24:29.786Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:24:29.786Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:37:59.079Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879336715-17', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'The meat cut likely to be most tender comes from the least exercised part of the animal.', 'Tenderloin', 'The tenderloin is located along the spine in a lightly exercised area, making it the most tender cut of meat on the animal.', '["Neck","Chuck","Tenderloin","Shank"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:20:02.781Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:20:02.781Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:38:02.920Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879351648-18', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'A variety of meat considered rich in iron and used in both Western and Asian cuisines is:', 'Tripe', 'Tripe refers to the edible muscular lining of a ruminant''s stomach chambers; it is exceptionally rich in iron and widely incorporated into both Western stews and traditional Asian dishes.', '["Tripe","Sirloin","Drumstick","Rump"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:29:24.562Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:29:24.562Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:38:07.443Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879370447-19', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which of the following requires moist-heat cooking?', 'Back and legs, because they are less tender due to frequent use', 'Avian muscles in the legs, thighs, and back are subjected to continuous weight-bearing and movement, accumulating more collagen and connective tissue, which requires moist-heat preparation.', '["Breast, because it has the most muscle activity","Thigh, because it is a lean and rarely used part","Back and legs, because they are less tender due to frequent use","Wings, because they are fatty and tender"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:38:00.810Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:38:00.810Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:38:11.860Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879387963-20', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Crustaceans such as crabs and lobsters change color from dark green or blue to bright orange-red when cooked because:', 'Heat causes protein-bound pigments like astaxanthin to be released.', 'Crustaceans store their natural reddish-orange carotenoid pigment (astaxanthin) bound to carrier proteins (crustacyanin) inside their shells, which masks the color with green/blue tones. When cooked, heat denatures these proteins, releasing free astaxanthin and turning the shell bright orange-red.', '["Their shells are exposed to steam, which softens pigments.","The muscle tissues absorb heat and change hue.","Heat causes protein-bound pigments like astaxanthin to be released.","Oxygen from boiling water reacts with shell minerals."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:29:58.882Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:29:58.882Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:38:15.696Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879407661-21', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Trimethylamine oxide (TMAO), naturally present in fish muscle, is converted into trimethylamine (TMA), producing a stale fish odor, due to the action of the enzyme:', 'Trimethylamine oxidase (TMAOase)', 'Post-mortem spoilage in marine fish involves endogenous enzymes or bacterial activity (such as trimethylamine oxidase) that reduce trimethylamine oxide (TMAO) into volatile trimethylamine (TMA), generating the characteristic fishy odor.', '["Lipase","Protease","Trimethylamine oxidase (TMAOase)","Catalase"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:33:38.066Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:33:38.066Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:38:22.770Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879425595-22', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Fish cooks faster than chicken, pork, or beef because it contains:', 'Less connective tissue and no elastin', 'Fish muscle fibers (myotomes) are very short and separated by delicate sheets of connective tissue (myocommata) containing virtually no tough elastin, allowing fish to cook significantly faster than land mammals.', '["More connective tissue and dense muscle fibers","Tougher myofibrillar proteins","Less connective tissue and no elastin","Higher amounts of saturated fat"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:36:12.138Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:36:12.138Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:38:25.856Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879440375-23', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which cooking method is most appropriate for lean fish with delicate muscle structure and minimal connective tissue?', 'Poaching', 'Poaching is a gentle moist-heat method utilizing low liquid temperatures (sub-simmering), making it ideal for preserving the delicate structural integrity of lean fish.', '["Braising","Stewing","Grilling","Poaching"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:35:11.806Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:35:11.806Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:38:31.026Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879459292-24', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why are duck eggs generally preferred over chicken eggs for salt curing, such as in the preparation of salted eggs?', 'Because duck eggs have a higher fat content in the yolk, resulting in a richer texture and flavor after curing.', 'Duck eggs possess a significantly higher proportion of lipids and fat density in their yolks compared to chicken eggs. During the salting and curing process, this elevated fat content contributes to a richer mouthfeel, denser texture, and superior flavor profile.', '["Because duck eggs have a thicker shell that absorbs salt faster.","Because duck eggs have a higher fat content in the yolk, resulting in a richer texture and flavor after curing.","Because duck eggs are smaller and cure more evenly in brine solutions.","Because duck eggs contain less water, allowing the salt to concentrate better in the yolk."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T15:04:50.686Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T15:04:50.686Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:38:37.077Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879475459-25', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why does overheating eggs beyond 70°C typically result in a tough and rubbery texture?', 'Because the egg proteins coagulate excessively, squeezing out water and forming a tight network.', 'Egg proteins begin to set at around 60°C to 70°C. When heated beyond optimal temperatures, egg proteins undergo excessive cross-linking and coagulation, tightening the protein matrix so severely that trapped moisture is forced out, yielding a dry, tough, and rubbery texture.', '["Because the yolk fats evaporate, leaving behind only dense proteins.","Because the egg proteins coagulate excessively, squeezing out water and forming a tight network.","Because the sugar in the egg caramelizes, hardening the mixture.","Because the egg white becomes diluted at high temperatures, making it less flexible."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:38:34.029Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:38:34.029Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:38:42.292Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879492275-26', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'In baked goods such as cakes and custards, how do eggs function as structural and textural agents?', 'Eggs coagulate during heating, helping form structure and a tender, fluffy texture.', 'In baking, egg proteins undergo thermal coagulation, providing essential structural rigidity while trapping air to ensure a light, tender crumb.', '["Eggs contribute moisture only and do not affect texture or structure.","Eggs prevent browning, keeping the product pale and soft.","Eggs break down starches, making the product denser and chewier.","Eggs coagulate during heating, helping form structure and a tender, fluffy texture."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:39:23.214Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:39:23.214Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:38:46.710Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879516657-27', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why are eggs considered excellent emulsifying agents in food preparation such as in mayonnaise or cake batters?', 'Because the whole egg forms foams that naturally keep mixtures stable.', '', '["Because egg whites contain proteins that prevent oil and water from separating.","Because egg yolks contain lecithin, which stabilizes emulsions by binding fat and water.","Because eggs are high in fat, which dissolves both oil and water easily.","Because the whole egg forms foams that naturally keep mixtures stable."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T15:06:30.603Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T15:06:30.603Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T15:06:30.603Z"'::jsonb)
