('anki-card-1756880567459-78', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'You are preparing a dry rub for grilling meat. Which of the following ingredient combinations contributes best to flavor penetration and surface browning?', 'Garlic powder, onion powder, brown sugar', 'Dry rubs containing aromatic powders and brown sugar caramelize effectively under dry heat, creating a rich exterior crust and carrying aromatic flavor compounds into meat surfaces.', '["Garlic powder, onion powder, brown sugar","Salt, black pepper, lemon juice, vinegar","Soy sauce, sesame oil, ginger, honey","Salt, black pepper, lemon juice, olive oil"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:26:41.628Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:26:41.628Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:44:39.897Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880582224-79', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why is salt often used first in marinating meat, even when acidic ingredients like vinegar or citrus juice are also present?', 'It helps seasonings penetrate by breaking down the protein structure', 'Salt draws out surface moisture and partially dissolves muscle proteins (myofibrillar solubilization), allowing dissolved seasonings and flavors to penetrate deeper into the meat tissue during marination.', '["It enhances sweetness","It tenderizes proteins chemically","It draws moisture out to dehydrate meat","It helps seasonings penetrate by breaking down the protein structure"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T15:06:07.061Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T15:06:07.061Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:44:43.155Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880602889-80', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why is an acid rinse effective in preventing browning of peeled fruits and vegetables?', 'It lowers pH, slowing down enzymatic activity', 'Polyphenol oxidase (the enzyme responsible for enzymatic browning in cut produce) operates poorly in acidic environments. Applying an acid rinse lowers pH and inhibits this enzymatic activity.', '["It removes surface moisture that causes browning","It inhibits oxygen penetration by tightening cell walls","It lowers pH, slowing down enzymatic activity","It denatures surface proteins preventing browning"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:31:24.556Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:31:24.556Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:44:47.637Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880617905-81', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'What is the primary functional reason for basting during roasting?', 'It adds moisture and prevents surface drying', 'Basting physically coats roasting meats with pan juices or fats, replenishing surface moisture lost to dry oven heat and preventing surface desiccation.', '["It prevents microbial growth on the surface","It caramelizes sugars for deeper browning","It adds moisture and prevents surface drying","It enhances the speed of protein coagulation"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:30:54.222Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:30:54.222Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:44:50.929Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880633339-82', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why is blanching used before freezing vegetables like broccoli or green beans?', 'To inactivate enzymes that cause spoilage', 'Blanching applies brief heat to vegetables prior to freezing to destroy endogenous plant enzymes (such as lipoxygenase and peroxidase) that cause off-flavors, nutrient loss, and color degradation during storage.', '["To inactivate enzymes that cause spoilage","To cook them halfway before final use","To improve their color by increasing chlorophyll","To reduce their carbohydrate content during long-term storage."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:20:40.292Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:20:40.292Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:44:54.530Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880648154-83', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'During caramelization, which chemical change primarily contributes to the flavor development?', 'Thermal degradation of sugar molecules', 'Caramelization is the non-enzymatic pyrolytic thermal degradation of sugar molecules occurring at high temperatures, producing complex aromatic caramel compounds and rich brown colors.', '["Protein denaturation","Lipid oxidation","Maillard reaction","Thermal degradation of sugar molecules"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T15:04:43.042Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T15:04:43.042Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:45:42.903Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880665120-84', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'What is the primary reason clarified butter (drawn butter) is preferred for high-heat cooking like sautéing or frying?', 'It has a higher smoke point due to removed milk solids', 'Clarified butter (ghee) has had water and milk solids removed. Because milk solids burn and smoke at relatively low temperatures, removing them raises the smoke point significantly for high-heat cooking.', '["It is less expensive than regular butter","It contains more saturated fat","It has a higher smoke point due to removed milk solids","It is thicker and coats foods better"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:23:00.939Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:23:00.939Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:44:59.738Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880677868-85', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which seasoning would be most appropriate to reduce bitterness in a vegetable stir-fry without masking the natural flavors?', 'Sugar', 'Sugar serves as a natural flavor balancer that counters bitterness in savory and stir-fry preparations.', '["Soy sauce","Vinegar","Sugar","Salt"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:20:52.337Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:20:52.337Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:45:06.286Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880691187-86', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'A recipe calls for 2 liters of broth. You only have a standard US measuring cup on hand. Approximately how many full cups will you need to measure out 2 liters of broth?', '9 cups', 'Standard liquid volume conversion dictates that 1 US cup equals 8 fluid ounces (roughly 240 mL). Two liters (2,000 mL) divided by 240 mL per cup equals approximately 8.33 cups, which rounds to 8 cups in standard culinary math.', '["6 cups","8 cups","9 cups","12 cups"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:39:40.581Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:39:40.581Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:45:49.018Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880706602-87', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'You are preparing a recipe that requires 1.5 pounds of flour, but your kitchen scale only measures in grams. Approximately how many grams of flour should you use?', '680 grams', 'Conversion factor: 1 pound equals approximately 453.59 grams. Therefore, 1.5 pounds multiplied by 453.59 g equals roughly 680.38 grams (680 grams).', '["500 grams","680 grams","750 grams","900 grams"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:37:04.205Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:37:04.205Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:45:54.170Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880723734-88', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why does deep-frying cook food faster than baking at the same temperature (e.g., 180°C or 350°F)?', 'Oil has a higher heat transfer coefficient than air', 'Deep-frying cooks food much faster than baking because hot cooking oil transfers thermal energy to the food via convection and conduction with a vastly higher heat transfer coefficient than oven air.', '["Oil conducts heat more slowly than air","Oil radiates heat more intensely than air","Oil has a higher heat transfer coefficient than air","Air circulates more efficiently than oil"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:35:04.263Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:35:04.263Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:45:58.566Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880757350-89', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'In which cooking method does radiation play the dominant role in transferring heat directly to the surface of the food?', 'Broiling', 'Broiling applies direct infrared radiant heat waves traveling through the air directly to the top surface of the food.', '["Simmering","Broiling","Steaming","Braising"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T15:05:31.202Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T15:05:31.202Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:46:04.074Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880772314-90', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why is moist-heat cooking generally preferred for tough cuts of meat like beef brisket or pork shoulder?', 'It breaks down connective tissues into gelatin through slow, wet cooking', 'Moist-heat cooking uses steady, low heat and liquid to slowly hydrolyze tough collagen fibers into soluble gelatin, softening tough cuts of meat.', '["It enhances the Maillard reaction for better browning","It breaks down connective tissues into gelatin through slow, wet cooking","It retains less moisture, making meat easier to shred","It crisps the outer surface for added texture"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:39:00.821Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:39:00.821Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:45:10.309Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880789065-91', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which of the following best explains the distinction between spices and herbs in culinary use?', 'Herbs are primarily leafy and used fresh or dried; spices come from other plant parts like seeds and bark', 'Culinary definitions distinguish herbs (fresh or dried leafy plant parts) from spices (derived from non-leafy parts such as bark, roots, buds, seeds, or fruits).', '["Spices are always stronger in flavor and must be used in larger quantities","Herbs are derived from dried roots while spices come from stems","Herbs are primarily leafy and used fresh or dried; spices come from other plant parts like seeds and bark","There is no clear difference; both terms are interchangeable in recipes"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:27:44.022Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:27:44.022Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:45:16.546Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880807713-92', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why is pork belly barbecue generally more tender and juicy than tenderloin barbecue, even though tenderloin is a leaner and more tender cut?', 'Pork belly has higher fat content that melts during cooking, adding moisture and flavor', 'Pork belly possesses rich interlaced layers of fat that render during high-heat grilling, bathing the muscle fibers in melted fat to keep the cut exceptionally tender and juicy compared to lean tenderloin.', '["Pork belly has less connective tissue, making it easier to cook","Tenderloin retains more moisture due to its low fat content","Pork belly has higher fat content that melts during cooking, adding moisture and flavor","Tenderloin absorbs more marinade, making it taste richer and juicier"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:24:57.628Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:24:57.628Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:45:21.390Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880824131-93', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'What is the best way to stabilize whipped cream for longer storage?', 'Add cornstarch', 'Stabilizing whipped cream for extended display requires a stabilizer like a small amount of gelatin, powdered sugar, or cornstarch, which absorbs free moisture and reinforces the fat-bubble foam walls.', '["Add cornstarch","Use skim milk","Increase whipping speed","Avoid chilling"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:23:22.544Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:23:22.544Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:45:25.425Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880843929-94', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which of the following best distinguishes oxidative rancidity from hydrolytic rancidity?', 'It produces ketones and aldehydes through fat oxidation.', 'Oxidative rancidity is a chemical degradation process where unsaturated fatty acids react with atmospheric oxygen via free-radical mechanisms, yielding foul-smelling volatile ketones, aldehydes, and peroxides.', '["It occurs only in saturated fats.","It involves water breaking down triglycerides.","It produces ketones and aldehydes through fat oxidation.","It is prevented by heat processing and enzyme destruction."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T15:06:13.501Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T15:06:13.501Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:45:29.693Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880856311-95', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which type of sugar is obtained by the hydrolysis of sucrose in the presence of acid or invertase?', 'Invert sugar', 'Invert sugar is produced through the hydrolysis of sucrose (table sugar) into its constituent monosaccharides, glucose and fructose, in the presence of an acid catalyst or the enzyme invertase.', '["Confectioner’s sugar","Invert sugar","Powdered sugar","Muscovado"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:29:34.189Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:29:34.189Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:36:53.913Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880897509-96', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Bihod is identified in Filipino markets as fresh fish roe and is locally referred to in Ilocano as:', 'Bogi', 'In local Filipino nomenclature, particularly within Ilocano dialects, fresh fish roe is commonly referred to as bogi (also widely known in Tagalog markets as bihod).', '["Aligi","Bogi","Tinapa","Tuyo"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:33:45.175Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:33:45.175Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T12:36:57.864Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928512767-0', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Meal management involves application of aesthetic qualities as well as scientific principles




True




False', 'True', 'Meal management is a multifaceted discipline that strictly requires the application of both aesthetic and scientific principles to be successful.

• Scientific Principles: This involves the application of nutrition (ensuring meals meet dietary and physiological requirements), food science and chemistry (understanding how ingredients react to heat, acids, and bases), food safety and sanitation (temperature control, preventing cross-contamination), and resource management (food costing, yield calculations).

• Aesthetic Qualities: This involves the sensory and psychological aspects of dining. A well-managed meal must appeal to the senses through a balance of colors, textures, flavors, shapes, and temperatures, as well as proper table setting and presentation (etiquette, centerpieces, appropriate tableware).

A meal can be scientifically nutritious and safe, but if it lacks aesthetic appeal, it will fail to satisfy the clientele. Conversely, a visually stunning meal that lacks nutritional balance or violates food safety protocols is equally poorly managed.', '["True","False","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:27:05.595Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:27:05.595Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T11:53:55.710Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928522448-1', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Socio-economic and cultural factors need not be considered in serving quality meals.



True




False', 'False', 'Socio-economic and cultural factors must be heavily considered when planning, preparing, and serving quality meals.

Socio-economic factors: These determine the budget, food cost allowances, and the purchasing power of your target clientele. A meal can only be considered a "quality meal" for a specific operation if it is financially viable to produce and affordable for the customers to buy.

Cultural factors: These dictate food habits, flavor preferences, and strict religious dietary laws (e.g., Halal for Muslims, Kosher for Jewish clients). You could prepare a perfectly cooked pork dish with the highest culinary standards, but if your clientele''s culture forbids pork, the meal is unacceptable and will result in plate waste and dissatisfaction. Clientele satisfaction is the ultimate measure of meal quality.', '["False","True","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:14:17.349Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:14:17.349Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:13:21.616Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928537698-2', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Organoleptic quality refers to palatability factors of food such as flavor, texture, and appearance.



True




False', 'True', '"Organoleptic" properties refer to all the characteristics of food that are experienced through the human senses—sight, smell, taste, and touch (mouthfeel). Therefore, organoleptic quality directly dictates a food''s palatability (how agreeable or pleasant it is to eat) by evaluating its flavor, texture, aroma, color, and overall appearance. In food service and sensory evaluation, achieving high organoleptic quality is essential for clientele satisfaction.', '["True","False","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:20:09.610Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:20:09.610Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:13:58.825Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928549597-3', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Menu serves as the primary control of the food service operation.



True




False', 'True', 'In food service management, the menu is considered the absolute "blueprint" or primary control tool of the entire operation. Every single managerial decision stems directly from what is written on the menu. It dictates:

• Purchasing: What ingredients to buy and how much to spend (food cost).
• Production: What cooking methods will be used.
• Staffing: What level of culinary skill is required (labor cost).
• Equipment & Layout: What types of ovens, stoves, or prep tables are needed in the kitchen layout.
• Clientele Satisfaction: How well the facility meets the nutritional and cultural needs of its target market.', '["True","False","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:14:59.937Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:14:59.937Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:14:42.081Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928564931-4', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Menu planning refers to listing down specific food for a meal.



True




False', 'True', 'Answer: True', '["True","False","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:02:33.094Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:02:33.094Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928578928-5', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'A la Carte menu is a static menu.



True




False', 'False', '"A la carte" and "static" refer to two completely different categories of menu planning.

• A la carte refers to the pricing structure where every single food and beverage item is priced and ordered separately (the opposite is Table d''hôte or a set menu).
• Static refers to the frequency of change, meaning the exact same menu items are offered every single day (the opposite is a cycle or single-use menu).', '["False","3, 4, 2, 1","salad fork","do not allow food to stand too long before serving"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:14:53.501Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:14:53.501Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:17:23.586Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928589146-6', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Cycle Menu is a non-selective menu.



True




False', 'True', 'Answer: True', '["True","False","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:02:38.880Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:02:38.880Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928600994-7', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Table d’ Hote offers selection in some courses.



True




