('anki-card-1757928616412-8', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Menu planning applies the principles of five M’s of management.



True




False', 'True', 'Menu planning heavily applies the principles of the Five M''s of Management, as the menu is the primary control that dictates how an operation utilizes all of its resources:

• Men (Labor/Staffing): The menu determines the number of personnel needed and the level of culinary skill required to cook the food.
• Money (Budget/Finance): The menu dictates the food cost, labor cost, and the required selling prices to maintain a balanced budget.
• Materials (Ingredients): The menu dictates exactly what raw foods and supplies need to be purchased and kept in inventory.
• Machines (Equipment): The menu dictates what type of kitchen equipment (ovens, fryers, mixers) is necessary to prepare the dishes.
• Methods (Procedures): The menu determines the cooking techniques, standardized recipes, and the overall workflow of the kitchen.', '["True","False","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:02:53.182Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:02:53.182Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:18:24.552Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928636293-9', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'An ideal method of evaluating food quality is using both sensory and objective evaluation.



True




False', 'True', 'In food science and food service management, the most ideal and comprehensive way to evaluate food quality is by combining both sensory and objective methods.

• Sensory evaluation: Uses human panels to judge palatability, preferences, and organoleptic traits (taste, aroma, mouthfeel, appearance). While essential for determining if a customer will actually eat the food, it is highly subjective.
• Objective evaluation: Uses laboratory equipment and physical/chemical tests (e.g., measuring viscosity, pH levels, or using a penetrometer for tenderness). This provides highly accurate, reproducible, and standardized data.

Using them together ensures that a food product is both scientifically consistent/safe (objective) and highly appealing to the target clientele (sensory).', '["True","False","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:02:59.300Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:02:59.300Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:18:54.768Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928647775-10', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Foods produced in tropical countries normally differ from countries with winter.



True




False', 'True', 'Climate and geography are the primary determinants of agricultural production and food availability.

Tropical countries (like the Philippines) have hot, humid climates that allow for year-round farming of specific crops like rice, coconuts, sugarcane, and tropical fruits (mangoes, bananas).

Countries with winters (temperate zones) have distinct growing seasons and produce crops suited for colder weather, such as wheat, apples, and hearty root vegetables. Furthermore, the presence of a winter season historically forced these cultures to develop specific food preservation techniques (like heavy canning, curing, and root cellaring) to survive the months when agricultural production completely halts. Therefore, both the raw foods produced and the resulting culinary traditions differ significantly.', '["True","False","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:12:52.056Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:12:52.056Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:19:42.131Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928663174-11', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Immigrants have more influence on the cuisine of the country where they migrate rather than the country influencing their way of eating. 



True




False', 'True', 'Answer: True', '["True","False","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:15:41.002Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:15:41.002Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928679109-12', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Dietary patterns of most individuals are dynamic and often changing.



True




False', 'True', 'Dietary patterns are highly dynamic and continually evolve throughout an individual''s lifetime. They are not static because they are constantly influenced by shifting factors such as transitioning through different life stages (e.g., childhood, pregnancy, older adulthood), changes in socio-economic status, geographical relocation (dietary acculturation), environmental food availability, and the development of health conditions that require medical nutrition therapy (MNT).', '["True","False","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:33:54.523Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:33:54.523Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:20:36.358Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928702074-13', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'The type of eating pattern of an individual is usually influenced  by knowledge of nutrition



True




False', 'False', 'In public health nutrition and behavioral science, it is a well-established principle that knowledge does not equal behavior.

While knowledge of nutrition is a factor, an individual''s daily eating pattern is primarily and much more strongly influenced by socio-economic status (budget/affordability), cultural background, taste preferences, convenience, and food availability. Many people possess adequate nutrition knowledge but do not apply it due to these stronger environmental and economic barriers.', '["False","True","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:04:56.637Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:04:56.637Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:20:57.960Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928715339-14', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Climate and topography affects the availability of food in a certain region.



True




False', 'True', 'Climate (weather patterns, temperature, and rainfall) and topography (physical features of the land like elevation, terrain, and soil quality) are the primary natural determinants of agricultural production.

Climate dictates what types of crops can survive and thrive (e.g., tropical heat and heavy rains are required for rice paddies, whereas temperate climates are needed for wheat).

Topography determines if the land is actually usable for agriculture. For example, flat plains are ideal for large-scale farming, mountainous regions may require terracing or are better suited for grazing livestock, and coastal regions provide access to seafood. Together, these geographical factors directly dictate the natural food supply and availability within any given region.', '["True","False","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:19:57.253Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:19:57.253Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:21:18.976Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928732739-15', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'In placing the table appointments on the table, one must keep in mind what is convenient and comfortable for the diner.




True




False', 'True', 'The fundamental principle behind all table setting rules and etiquette is the comfort and convenience of the diner. The specific placement of table appointments—such as arranging flatware from the outside in based on the order of courses, or placing the beverage glass on the upper right for easy reach—is designed entirely to make the dining experience ergonomic, logical, and effortless for the guest.', '["True","False","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:14:34.316Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:14:34.316Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:21:37.783Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928749038-16', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Napkins are placed on the right side of the cover to make it easier for the diner to unfold the napkin.




True



False', 'True', 'In standard table setting and meal management, the napkin is traditionally placed on the left side of the cover (to the left of the forks) or directly in the center of the service plate.

It is not placed on the right side because the right side is reserved for the knives, spoons, and glassware. Placing the napkin on the left allows the diner to easily reach for it with their left hand and place it on their lap without awkwardly reaching across their plate or navigating over the sharp edges of the knives.', '["True","False","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:31:40.425Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:31:40.425Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:22:25.458Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928758570-17', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'When placemats are used, napkins may be placed partly on the table.



True




False', 'True', 'Answer: True', '["True","False","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:06:56.502Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:06:56.502Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928771953-18', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'When only fork is required and no other flatwares are laid, the fork is placed on the right side of the cover/plate.



True




False', 'True', 'While forks are traditionally placed on the left side of the plate when a knife is present (because the knife is held in the dominant right hand and the fork in the left), the rule changes if the fork is the only piece of flatware required for the meal. In this case, the fork is placed on the right side of the cover. This is based on the core principle of diner convenience, allowing the majority of right-handed diners to easily pick up their single primary utensil with their dominant hand.', '["True","False","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:33:13.082Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:33:13.082Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:23:41.129Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928787069-19', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Knives are laid with the cutting edges facing the right.



True




False', 'False', 'In standard table setting etiquette, knives are placed on the right side of the plate, but the cutting edge (the blade) must always face inward, towards the plate (which means facing the left).

Historically and practically, this is a rule of safety and politeness. Facing the sharp edge of the blade outward toward the person sitting next to you is considered an aggressive or hostile gesture. Therefore, the blade is always turned inward to signify a peaceful dining environment.', '["False","True","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:19:20.811Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:19:20.811Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:24:00.738Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928801051-20', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Spoons are laid on the left side of the cover with bowls up.


True




False', 'False', 'In standard table setting, spoons are always placed on the right side of the cover (to the right of the knives). While it is true that they are laid with the bowls facing up, placing them on the left side is incorrect, as the left side is specifically reserved for the forks (and the napkin).', '["False","True","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:04:01.506Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:04:01.506Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:24:34.884Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928810952-21', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Serving flatwares should be left on the food on the platter.



True




False', 'False', 'In meal management and table service etiquette, serving flatwares (such as serving spoons or tongs) should be placed on the side of the platter or serving dish, beside the food.

They must never be left resting directly on the food itself. Doing so is both messy and unsanitary, as it increases the risk of the handles—which have been touched by people''s hands—slipping into or coming into direct contact with the food, compromising food safety and presentation for the next diner.', '["False","True","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:09:30.778Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:09:30.778Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:27:11.356Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928823732-22', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Dinnerplates are placed turned up in the middle of the cover.



True




False', 'True', 'In standard table setting and meal management, the dinner plate (or service plate) serves as the exact center of the "cover" (the individual diner''s place setting). It is placed right-side up (turned up) directly in the middle, typically about one inch from the edge of the table. It acts as the focal point around which all other flatware, glassware, and table appointments are arranged. Plates are never placed upside down in standard formal or informal service etiquette.', '["True","False","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:20:01.550Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:20:01.550Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:27:31.439Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928835617-23', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'When both bread and butter and salad plates are required, salad plate should be placed on the right side of the cover.



True




False', 'False', 'In standard table setting etiquette, the right side of the cover is strictly reserved for beverages (glassware, teacups, and saucers) along with knives and spoons.

When both a bread and butter plate and a salad plate are used simultaneously, they are both placed on the left side of the cover. The bread and butter plate is positioned at the top left (above the forks), and the salad plate is placed to the lower left of the forks (or just below the bread plate).', '["False","True","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:15:47.029Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:15:47.029Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:27:50.316Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928853000-24', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Flatwares should be laid in the order of service.





True




False', 'False', 'Answer: False', '["False","True","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:22:40.591Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:22:40.591Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928888732-25', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Coasters are used for stemmed glasses only.



True




False', 'False', 'Coasters are used to protect the table surface from heat or moisture (such as condensation or "sweat" from cold beverages). Therefore, they are used for any type of beverage container that might damage the table, and are actually most commonly used for unstemmed glasses (like tumblers, highballs, or water glasses) and hot mugs. They are absolutely not restricted to stemmed glasses only.', '["False","True","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:28:44.388Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:28:44.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:28:21.991Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928900548-26', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'When using candle as centerpiece, flames should be below eye level.



True




False', 'False', 'In formal table setting and meal management etiquette, candle flames should be above or below eye level, not strictly below.

The fundamental rule for any centerpiece is that it must not obstruct the guests'' line of sight or cause discomfort. If a candle flame is exactly at eye level, it creates a harsh glare that shines directly into the diners'' eyes, making it difficult for them to see and converse with the person sitting across from them. To prevent this, you should use either tall taper candles (so the flame is well above eye level) or short votive candles/tea lights (so the flame is well below eye level). Stating that they must strictly be below eye level is incorrect.', '["False","True","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:03:48.700Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:03:48.700Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:29:03.186Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928912681-27', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'The cover must consist of all types of flatwares.



True




False', 'False', 'A "cover" (the individual place setting for one diner) should only consist of the specific flatware required for the actual menu being served. It is considered poor etiquette and highly impractical to place "all types" of flatware on the table. Placing unnecessary utensils that will not be used clutters the dining space, confuses the diner, and violates the core principle of keeping the table setting convenient and comfortable.', '["False","True","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:30:20.760Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:30:20.760Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:29:40.892Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928925864-28', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Because of its beauty, value, and durability, sterling silver has been described as the “heirloom of tomorrow”



True




False', 'True', 'In meal management and the study of table appointments, sterling silver (an alloy of 92.5% pure silver and 7.5% copper for added strength) is widely considered the premier material for fine flatware. Because the addition of copper provides the durability needed to withstand years of use without losing the inherent beauty and intrinsic financial value of the precious metal, sterling silver sets are traditionally passed down through generations within families. Therefore, it is commonly referred to in textbooks and the industry as the "heirloom of tomorrow."', '["True","False","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:28:35.181Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:28:35.181Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:31:13.348Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928935895-29', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'When flowers are used as centerpiece, the height must be below eye level.



True




False', 'True', 'In standard meal management and table etiquette, the primary rule for any centerpiece is that it must not obstruct the sightlines or hinder conversation between guests sitting across the table from one another.

Therefore, when using flowers, the arrangement should be kept low (typically under 12 to 14 inches in height) so that it remains strictly below eye level. If a floral arrangement is placed directly at eye level, it acts as a physical and visual barrier, forcing diners to lean awkwardly to see and speak to each other, which violates the core principle of diner comfort. (Note: In large-scale formal banquets or weddings, very tall centerpieces elevated on thin stands are sometimes used so the flowers are entirely above eye level, but for standard table settings, keeping them below eye level is the universal rule).', '["True","False","Maybe","Depends"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:13:11.909Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:13:11.909Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:33:15.445Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929009541-30', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Maintenance of aesthetic and sanitary quality is another important goal in meal preparation. In order to achieve this, the following may be considered:
(1) practice FIRST IN, FIRST OUT for foods that are refrigerated or frozen
(2) use proper techniques of preparation as in the use of varied sizes and shapes in cutting fruits and vegetables
(3) buy the right cut of meat or the right type of fish for the dish in mind
(4) use correct temperature for specific procedure like frying, baking, roasting, and the like', 'All except 3', '', '["1 and 2","3 and 4","1 and 4","All except 3"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:24:24.811Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:24:24.811Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:24:24.811Z"'::jsonb)
