INSERT INTO public.flashcards (id, user_id, deck_id, front, back, rationale, options, tags, ndle_subject, difficulty, leitner_box, user_notes, sm2, last_reviewed_at, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
('anki-card-1757929054141-31', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Which of the following affects the sensory evaluation of food quality?
(1) color combination
(2) color of the plate
(3) religious practices', '1 & 2 only', 'Sensory evaluation is a scientific discipline used to evoke, measure, analyze, and interpret human reactions to the characteristics of food as they are perceived by the five senses: sight, smell, taste, touch, and hearing.

(1) Color combination and (2) Color of the plate directly affect the visual sense. Sight is the first sense used when evaluating food. The color contrast of the food components and how they stand out against the plate heavily influence flavor expectations, perceived freshness, and overall aesthetic quality.

(3) Religious practices dictate food acceptability and dietary choices (e.g., eating Kosher or Halal), but they do not change the actual organoleptic (sensory) properties of the food itself. A person''s religion dictates whether they will eat a food, not how their taste buds and eyes physically evaluate its quality.', '["1 & 3 only","1 & 2 only","all are correct","2 & 3 only"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:14:47.674Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:14:47.674Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:38:00.097Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929074105-32', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'What is the order in planning a cycle menu?
(1) plan the menu for breakfast
(2) plan the accompaniments, soup, and dessert
(3) plan the main course of the most important meal of the day
(4) plan the main course of the other meal', '3, 4, 2, 1', 'In standard institutional foodservice management, menu planning follows a strict top-down sequence based on cost and center-of-the-plate importance:

• First (3): Always plan the main course (entrée) of the most important meal of the day. The main dish is the most expensive item and dictates the theme, budget, and nutritional core of the day.

• Second (4): Plan the main course of the other meal(s). Doing this next ensures you do not repeat ingredients (e.g., avoiding chicken for both lunch and dinner) and helps balance the daily food cost.

• Third (2): Plan the accompaniments (starches, vegetables), soups, and desserts. These are chosen specifically to complement the main courses in flavor, texture, and color.

• Fourth (1): Plan breakfast last. Breakfast menus are generally standard, highly repetitive, less expensive, and easiest to fit into whatever daily budget remains.', '["1, 3, 4, 2","3, 4, 2, 1","3, 2, 1, 4","1, 3, 2, 4"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T05:17:14.620Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:17:14.620Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:17:14.620Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929087923-33', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Foods or portions of food served at a particular time of the day.', 'meal', 'In meal management and nutrition, a meal is defined as the specific food or portions of food served and consumed at a particular, designated time of the day (e.g., breakfast, lunch, or dinner).

• Menu: This is the physical list or the overall plan of the dishes available or to be served. It is the concept or the outline, not the actual physical food being eaten at that moment.
• Course: This refers to a specific, separate part of a meal that is served at one time (e.g., an appetizer course, a soup course, or a dessert course). A meal is often made up of multiple courses, making "course" only a subdivision of the answer.', '["menu","meal","course","none of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:33:42.217Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:33:42.217Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:39:39.988Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929102422-34', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Foods are priced individually and cooked as ordered.', 'a la carte', 'In foodservice and menu planning, an à la carte (French for "by the card") menu lists every food and beverage item separately, with its own individual price. Because items are selected and ordered individually by the diner, they are typically cooked to order rather than prepared in massive batches ahead of time.

• Selective menu: This refers to a menu that offers choices within categories (common in hospitals or cafeteria settings), but it does not define the pricing structure or cooking method.
• Table d'' hote: As established previously, this offers a complete, multi-course meal for one fixed, total price.
• California menu: This refers to a specific style of menu where breakfast, lunch, and dinner items are all available at any time of the day, regardless of how they are priced.', '["selective menu","table d’ hote","a la carte","California menu"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:21:28.787Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:21:28.787Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T11:55:03.389Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929124904-35', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Which of the following influence one’s choice of food?', 'all of the above', 'A person''s choice of food is complex and determined by a combination of physical, mental, and sociocultural factors:

• Topography (and climate): These physical factors determine agricultural production and what foods are locally grown, readily available, and affordable in a specific region. You can only choose to eat what is accessible to you.
• Psychological factors: Individual moods, stress levels, emotions, and personal associations (such as "comfort foods" tied to childhood memories) heavily drive what a person craves and ultimately chooses to consume.
• Education: A person''s level of knowledge regarding nutrition, health benefits, food safety, and dietary guidelines directly influences their cognitive decisions when selecting food, often steering them toward or away from certain dietary patterns.', '["topography","psychological factors","education","all of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:17:13.411Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:17:13.411Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:40:24.449Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929136170-36', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'In relation to food, palatability is', 'relative acceptance', 'In food science and sensory evaluation, palatability refers to the degree to which a food is agreeable or acceptable to the palate. It is a subjective measure of the hedonic reward (pleasure) provided by food, based on sensory properties like taste, aroma, texture, and appearance. Therefore, it is best defined as the "relative acceptance" of a food item by an individual or target demographic.', '["hunger","dislike","eating habits","relative acceptance"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:22:14.276Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:22:14.276Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T11:57:08.628Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929151736-37', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Dietary patterns of most individuals are', 'dynamic and often changing', 'Dietary patterns are not rigid; they continually evolve throughout a person''s lifespan.

While core cultural food habits established in childhood provide a foundation, an individual''s diet is dynamic because it constantly adapts to changes in age, health status, income, geographical location (acculturation), and shifts in lifestyle.', '["inherited","very stable","dynamic and often changing","not affected by technology"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:13:19.756Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:13:19.756Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:41:00.287Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929177901-38', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'A cuisine is a', 'style or manner of cooking or preparing food.', 'In culinary and food service terminology, a "cuisine" (derived from the French word for kitchen) specifically refers to a distinctive style, method, or manner of cooking and food preparation. It is usually characterized by specific ingredients, regional techniques, and cultural traditions (e.g., Filipino cuisine, Mediterranean cuisine, or French cuisine).

• Group of customs or characteristics: This is too broad and defines a "culture" or "tradition" in general, not specifically food.
• Diet pattern limited to foods of plant origin: This defines a vegetarian or vegan diet.
• Desire or craving for food in general: This is the physiological and psychological definition of "appetite."', '["group of customs or characteristics","diet pattern limited to foods of plant origin.","style or manner of cooking or preparing food.","desire or craving for food in general"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:03:42.815Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:03:42.815Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:41:49.133Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929193634-39', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'The type of eating pattern developed by an individual is usually NOT influenced by', 'enzymatic reactions', 'Eating patterns are behavioral habits shaped by external, environmental, and cognitive factors.

Economics, availability of food, and knowledge of nutrition (Options A, C, and D) are primary determinants of what a person chooses to buy and eat. They dictate affordability, physical access, and conscious dietary choices.

Enzymatic reactions (Option B), on the other hand, are involuntary biochemical processes. While they occur inside the body to digest food, or within the food itself to cause ripening or spoilage, they do not dictate the behavioral choices or cultural habits that form an individual''s eating pattern.', '["economics","enzymatic reactions","availability of food","knowledge of nutrition"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:31:55.791Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:31:55.791Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:42:16.171Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929206966-40', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Many members of the Jewish faith observe', 'Kashruth dietary laws', 'Members of the Jewish faith observe Kashruth (also spelled Kashrut), which is the body of Jewish religious laws concerning what foods can and cannot be eaten, as well as how those foods must be prepared and consumed. Food that satisfies the requirements of Jewish law is called Kosher.

• Halal food laws: These are the dietary laws observed by members of the Islamic faith.
• Adventist recommendations: These refer to the dietary guidelines of the Seventh-day Adventist Church, which strongly promote a vegetarian diet and abstaining from alcohol and caffeine.
• Vegetarian guidelines: While some Jewish individuals may choose to be vegetarian, vegetarianism itself is not a religious dietary law of the Jewish faith. Kashruth allows the consumption of certain meats (like beef and poultry) provided they are slaughtered and prepared according to strict ritual laws.', '["Kashruth dietary laws","Halal food laws","Vegetarian guidelines","Adventist recommendation"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:07:45.422Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:07:45.422Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:42:53.181Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929220033-41', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Members of the Jewish and Islamic faiths usually do not consume', 'Pork', 'Both the Jewish and Islamic faiths strictly prohibit the consumption of pork.

Under Jewish dietary laws (Kashruth), for a land animal to be considered Kosher, it must have cloven hooves and chew its cud. While pigs have cloven hooves, they do not chew their cud, making them unclean and forbidden.

Similarly, under Islamic dietary laws (Halal), the Quran explicitly categorizes swine (pork) as haram (forbidden). Both faiths allow the consumption of beef, chicken, and fish, provided they are prepared and slaughtered according to their respective religious guidelines.', '["Beef","Pork","Chicken","Fish"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:27:39.525Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:27:39.525Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:43:12.416Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929237982-42', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'What foods are most likely to be consumed by vegetarians following a vegan diet?', 'grains, fruits, and vegetables', 'A vegan diet is the strictest form of vegetarianism. Vegans consume exclusively plant-based foods and entirely exclude all animal flesh (meat, poultry, fish/seafood) as well as all animal-derived products (dairy, eggs, and often honey).

• Fish, fruits, and vegetables: This describes a pescatarian diet. Vegans do not eat fish.
• Chicken, grains, and vegetables: This includes poultry, which is excluded from all vegetarian diets.
• Eggs, grains, and vegetables: This describes an ovo-vegetarian diet. While ovo-vegetarians consume eggs, vegans strictly avoid them.', '["fish, fruits, and vegetables","grains, fruits, and vegetables","chicken, grains, and vegetables","eggs, grains, and vegetables"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:12:45.789Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:12:45.789Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:44:57.833Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929252730-43', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Food practices are influenced by the following, except:', 'none of the above', 'Food practices are heavily influenced by all of the options listed, meaning there is no exception among them:

• Immigrants bring their native cuisines, ingredients, and cooking techniques to new regions, leading to the introduction and blending of food cultures (acculturation).
• Traders from different countries historically introduced new spices, crops, and culinary methods across borders (e.g., the global spread of tomatoes, chilies, and spices through trade routes like the Galleon Trade).
• Religion directly dictates dietary laws, fasting practices, and food prohibitions (such as Halal in Islam or Kosher in Judaism).', '["immigrants","traders from different countries","religion","none of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:16:11.195Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:16:11.195Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:46:32.482Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929266514-44', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'The following factors affect the availability of food in a certain region, except:', 'religion', 'Religion is a cultural and social factor that dictates food acceptability or consumption (what people are allowed or choose to eat, like avoiding pork or beef), but it does not dictate the physical capacity of the land to produce food.

Climate, agricultural practices, and topography (the physical features of the land) are all environmental and technical factors that directly dictate food availability—meaning what crops can physically be grown, harvested, and supplied in a specific geographic region.', '["climate","topography","religion","agricultural practices"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:39:49.103Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:39:49.103Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:39:49.103Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929285347-45', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'The staff may attempt to produce the superb dishes listed in the menu but are likely to produce them to the required standard if they are not well trained or there are not sufficient staff. What options does the management has to solve the problem?
(1) change the items on the menu
(2) change the concept
(3) employ sufficient staff
(4) buy prepared foods', '1 and 3', '', '["2 only","1 and 3","3 only","All of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T04:35:54.805Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T04:35:54.805Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T04:35:54.805Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929298111-46', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Balance must be kept between costs and selling price. To help ensure this balance, which of the following may be done by the management of a not so high class establishment?
(1) have uniform price scheme
(2) do not include items that are over elaborate
(3) appropriate quality of raw materials for the establishment must be purchased
(4) cut the selling price of the main item and increasing the price of the other items', 'All except 1', '', '["3 only","1 and 4","1 and 2","All except 1"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T04:33:58.003Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T04:33:58.003Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T04:33:58.003Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929312994-47', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'A Grill restaurant with a cowboy motif will do away with the normal terms of food choices. Which of the following may be included in the menu?', 'Rodeo Pork Chops with Barbeque Sauce', 'In menu planning, the terminology, descriptions, and food selections must strongly align with the restaurant''s overall concept and theme to create a cohesive dining experience.

A cowboy-themed grill restaurant would naturally utilize Western, ranch, or rustic terminology. The word "Rodeo" directly fits the cowboy motif, and grilled pork chops with barbecue sauce are classic Western-style grill fare.', '["Sizzling Steamed Salmon","Stuffed Squid","Rodeo Pork Chops with Barbeque Sauce","Smoked Lamb Chops in Spiced Honey Sauce"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:17:08.153Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:17:08.153Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:47:59.721Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929326361-48', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'The goal of minimizing food cost and waste in meal preparation may be achieved through several procedures and techniques. These include:', 'Buy the right cut of meat or the type of fish for the dish in mind', 'Buy the right cut of meat or the type of fish for the dish in mind', '["Cook vegetables just enough to retain desired texture and color","Not throwing away soaking water, marinade, and cooking water","Using proper temperature and shortest cooking time possible","Buy the right cut of meat or the type of fish for the dish in mind"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:07:34.599Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:07:34.599Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929339428-49', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'In order to provide good nutrition in meal preparation, certain procedure in preparation must be practiced. The following may be applied except one.', 'do not allow food to stand too long before serving', 'do not allow food to stand too long before serving', '["do not throw away soaking water, marinade, and even cooking water","consider food preferences of the family","use proper cooking temperature and shortest cooking time possible","do not allow food to stand too long before serving"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:37:46.982Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:37:46.982Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929355648-50', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'To be a success, planning the menu must first of all regarded as a  marketing exercise. This exercise needs to be carried out in conjunction with certain important rules, like:
(1) it should complement the establishment’s image
(2) it must create consumer interest and stimulate appetite
(3) it should help produce the required profit
(4) it must meet consumer requirement', 'all of the above', 'Viewing the menu as a marketing exercise means recognizing it as the primary sales and merchandising tool of the restaurant. To be successful, menu planning must accomplish all four of these interconnected goals:

(1) It should complement the establishment''s image: The menu''s physical design, typography, language, and the actual dishes offered must seamlessly align with the restaurant''s brand, theme, and level of service (e.g., a fine-dining establishment needs a sophisticated menu presentation).

(2) It must create consumer interest and stimulate appetite: Through effective merchandising techniques like appetizing descriptions and strategic layout, the menu must entice the customer to order and potentially upsell them to higher-margin items.

(3) It should help produce the required profit: Through careful menu engineering, recipe costing, and strategic pricing, the menu is the central tool used to achieve the business''s target food cost percentage and overall financial goals.

(4) It must meet consumer requirement: A menu will fail if it does not offer what the target market actually wants. It must cater to the preferences, dietary needs, and price expectations of the specific demographic the restaurant serves.', '["1 and 3","2 and 3","3 only","all of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:10:41.089Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:10:41.089Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:49:55.168Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929383257-51', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'In order to carry out the above rules, the following should be considered in menu planning:
(1) clientele satisfaction
(2) balance in flavor, texture, color, shape, and method of preparation
(3) psychological factors
(4) environmental condition', 'all of the above except 4', 'all of the above except 4', '["2 and 3","1 and 4","all of the above","all of the above except 4"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T05:06:11.721Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:06:11.721Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929399958-52', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Considering the reasons for eating, what will finally be eaten is influenced by several factors:', 'psychological factors', 'psychological factors', '["food habits of the family","psychological factors","facilities available for preparation","all of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:41:21.249Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:41:21.249Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929417638-53', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Which of the following can save money?
(1)   Invest on special tools and equipment even if they are expensive
(2)   Use convenience food
(3)   Using right type of cookware
(4)   Dovetail activities', 'All of the above', 'All of the above', '["All of the above","(2) only","All except (1)","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T05:28:57.903Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":1.9,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:28:57.903Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929436689-54', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Why a person eats is a result of multi-factors.  These include:', 'all of the above', 'The reasons why a person eats, as well as what and how they eat, are shaped by a complex interplay of multiple factors:

• Family: Dietary habits are established early in life. Family traditions, cultural background, and the types of food regularly served at home build the foundation for a person''s food preferences and eating behaviors.

• Psychological: Emotions, mood, stress, and mental well-being heavily dictate food intake. People often eat for comfort, out of boredom, or as a coping mechanism (emotional eating), which goes beyond basic physiological hunger.

• Socio-economic: A person''s income, education level, occupation, and social environment directly dictate their purchasing power, access to certain foods (e.g., fresh produce vs. fast food), and nutritional knowledge.', '["family","psychological","socio-economic","all of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:16:18.218Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:16:18.218Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:51:38.970Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929451887-55', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'What meat will you buy for sautéed vegetables?', 'pork casim', 'Pork casim (shoulder) has an excellent balance of lean meat and fat. In Filipino cooking, sautéed vegetables (ginisa) rely on the rendered fat from the meat (sahog) to flavor the dish, and the marbling in casim keeps the small pieces of meat tender.

Beef tenderloin (A) is the most expensive and leanest cut of beef, best reserved for steaks; using it for basic vegetable sautéing is not economical. Pork loin (B) is very lean and dries out quickly when chopped into small pieces and sautéed.', '["beef tenderloin","pork casim","pork loin","Clinical option 4"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T04:31:20.322Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T04:31:20.322Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T04:31:20.322Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929465920-56', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'You are going to cook sweet & sour pork, and  the recipe calls for ½ cup pineapple chunks. What  will you buy?', 'canned pineapple chunks', 'In meal management and food procurement, purchasing decisions must be driven by the exact yield needed, labor time, and waste minimization.

Since the recipe requires only a very small amount (½ cup), buying a fresh whole or peeled pineapple (Options A and B) is highly inefficient. It would result in over-purchasing, excess yield that might go to waste if not utilized in another menu item, and unnecessary preparation labor.

Furthermore, canned pineapple chunks are the most practical and cost-effective choice for this specific dish because sweet and sour pork recipes traditionally utilize the leftover packing juice or syrup from the can as a primary ingredient for the sweet and sour sauce. This perfectly aligns with the food service goal of maximizing utility and minimizing waste.', '["fresh whole pineapple","peeled fresh pineapple from the market","canned pineapple chunks","any of the choices"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:16:02.965Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:16:02.965Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:52:20.197Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929487270-57', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Which is cheaper to buy if you will cook chicken tinola?', 'whole chicken', 'Buying a whole, intact chicken is almost always the cheapest option per kilo because you are not paying for the butcher''s labor to chop, separate, or package specific parts. You can easily cut it up yourself at home for the tinola, and using the whole bird (including the back and bones) creates a much richer, more flavorful broth.

Pre-cut whole chicken (D) costs slightly more per kilo due to the added labor of the butcher chopping it for you. Chicken breast (C) is generally the most expensive premium cut of the chicken (and is less ideal for soups since white meat dries out easily and lacks bones for a good broth). Chicken legs (B), while flavorful for tinola, carry a higher price tag per kilo than a whole chicken because they have been specially butchered and separated.', '["pre-cut whole chicken","whole chicken","chicken breast","chicken legs"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T04:32:21.997Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T04:32:21.997Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T04:32:21.997Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929502051-58', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'If you are to plan a menu for a special occasion wherein you do not know the composition guests, which of the following combination would you consider?', 'beef, poultry, fish, green salad', 'When planning a menu for a diverse or unknown group of guests, the fundamental rule is to maximize acceptability by avoiding universally common religious and cultural dietary prohibitions while providing a wide variety of choices.

• A and C both contain pork. Pork is strictly prohibited in major global religions, specifically Islam (Halal) and Judaism (Kashruth). Including it when guest demographics are unknown is a high-risk choice that can easily alienate guests.
• D (fish, poultry, sautéed vegetables) is a very safe combination, but it lacks the variety expected for a "special occasion."

Option B is the standard catering and banquet strategy for unknown groups. It eliminates the most common taboo (pork) and provides a comprehensive spread of protein classifications: a red meat (beef), a white meat (poultry), and seafood (fish). If a guest cannot eat beef (e.g., Hindus) or chooses to avoid red meat, they still have two other prominent protein options. The green salad provides a fresh, universally acceptable accompaniment that can also cater to vegetarian guests.', '["pork, seafoods, chicken, salad","beef, poultry, fish, green salad","beef, pork, seafoods, salad","fish, poultry, sautéed vegetables"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:09:19.644Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:09:19.644Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:53:47.638Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929515550-59', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'How many days can you keep cottage cheese in a refrigerator at 38°F?', 'one month', '', '["one week","two days","three days","one month"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T05:08:15.701Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:08:15.701Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:08:15.701Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929529016-60', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'The meat of a young cow is:', 'light red', 'In food science and meat grading, the color of raw meat is primarily determined by the concentration of myoglobin (the oxygen-binding protein in muscle). As an animal ages, it uses its muscles more, causing myoglobin levels to increase and the meat to become progressively darker.

Here is how the color of bovine (cattle) meat changes according to the animal''s age:

• Veal (young calf): Meat from a very young milk-fed calf (typically under 3–5 months) has very little myoglobin and is pink to grayish-pink.
• Calf (older calf): Meat from calves up to 8 months old begins to darken slightly to a grayish red.
• Young Beef (young cow, heifer, or steer): Meat from young, mature cattle (typically 1 to 2.5 years old) has the ideal, highly desired light red to bright cherry-red color.
• Mature Beef (old cow): Meat from older cattle (or draft animals like carabaos) has a high myoglobin concentration, making the meat dark, reddish brown or dark red.', '["dark, reddish brown","light red","grayish red","pink"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:38:11.897Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:38:11.897Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T10:55:49.008Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929541601-61', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Four pronged, shorter and broader', 'salad fork', 'In traditional table setting, a salad fork is easily identified because it is specifically designed to be shorter and broader than a standard dinner fork. It typically has four prongs (tines), with the tines being wider and flatter—and often the leftmost tine is extra thick—to provide leverage for cutting through lettuce leaves and scooping up vegetables without needing a knife.

The dinner fork (B) is the longest and standard-sized fork on the table. The dessert fork (A) is also shorter, but it is typically narrower and often only has three prongs. A fish fork (C) is also wider, but it is distinctly recognized by a deep notch on the side to help separate fish flesh from the bones, rather than just being "shorter and broader."', '["fish fork","salad fork","dinner fork","dessert fork"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T05:20:32.215Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:20:32.215Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:20:32.215Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929553016-62', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'A twelve inch plate used as underliner in formal dinner', 'place plate', '', '["dinner plate","salad plate","place plate","service plate"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:20:41.265Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:20:41.265Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:20:41.265Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929571681-63', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Small piece of material placed on top of tablecloth', 'top cloth', 'In meal management, a top cloth (also known as a slip cloth) is specifically defined as a smaller piece of cloth placed over the main tablecloth. Its purpose is to protect the primary tablecloth from spills and stains, lessening the need to wash the large, heavy tablecloth frequently.

A runner (B) is a long, narrow strip of cloth placed down the center of the table for decoration. A placemat (C) is placed under an individual diner''s specific place setting. Doilies (D) are small, ornamental (usually lace or paper) mats placed under centerpieces, teacups, or bowls primarily for decoration.', '["top cloth","placemat","runner","doilies"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T04:28:33.225Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T04:28:33.225Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T04:28:33.225Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929583748-64', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Heavy pad of material placed underneath the table covering.', 'silence cloth', 'A silence cloth (also known as a molleton or table pad) is a thick, heavy piece of fabric placed directly on the bare table underneath the main tablecloth. Its primary purposes are to muffle the sound of clanking plates and silverware, protect the wooden table surface from heat and scratches, and give the tablecloth a smoother, more elegant drape.

The table cloth (A) is the main decorative covering placed over the silence cloth. The top cloth (B) is a smaller cloth placed on top of the main tablecloth to catch spills. A runner (C) is a long, narrow strip of fabric placed across the center of the table purely for decoration.', '["table cloth","top cloth","silence cloth","runner"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T05:09:11.094Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:09:11.094Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:09:11.094Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929600012-65', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'When only fork is required and no other flatwares are laid:', 'the fork is placed on the right side of the cover/plate.', 'In standard meal management and table-setting etiquette, the general rule is that forks are placed on the left side of the plate, while knives and spoons go on the right.

However, there is a specific exception: when a fork is the only piece of flatware required for a meal or a course (such as a dessert or a simple pasta dish), it is placed on the right side of the plate.

The reasoning behind this rule is pure ergonomics and convenience. Since the majority of diners are right-handed, placing the solo utensil on the right side allows them to pick it up directly with their dominant hand without having to reach across the cover or awkwardly switch hands.', '["the fork is placed on the right side of the cover/plate.","the fork is placed on the left side of the plate","the fork is served with the course"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:31:31.220Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:31:31.220Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T11:30:59.576Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929612962-66', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'When using candle as centerpiece:', 'flames should be above eye level', 'In traditional meal management and formal table setting etiquette, if taper candles or candelabras are used, they must be tall enough so that the flames are above eye level when the guests are seated. This ensures that the glaring light of the flame does not shine directly into the diners'' eyes, and the candles do not obstruct the line of sight for conversation across the table.', '["flames should be below eye level","flames should be eye level","flames should be above eye level","the candle should not be lighted"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T05:07:25.180Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:07:25.180Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:07:25.180Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929629145-67', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Which of the following is not correct?
(1) knives are laid with the sharp edge facing right
(2) cup and saucer are placed on the lower right side of the cover
(3) bread and butter plate is placed above the forks
(4) spoon is laid on the table with the bowl turned down', '1 & 4', 'Statement (1) is INCORRECT: While knives are placed on the right side of the dinner plate, the sharp cutting edge must always face inward (to the left) towards the plate. Having the blade face outward (to the right) is a breach of etiquette.

Statement (4) is INCORRECT: Spoons are placed to the right of the knife with the bowl facing up, not down. (Note: While traditional French setting places forks and spoons face down to display engraved family crests on the back of the handles, standard international and Philippine meal management dictates bowls and tines face up).

• Why 2 and 3 are correct: The bread and butter plate is always placed on the upper left side of the cover (directly above the forks). The cup and saucer are placed on the right side, outside the spoons.', '["2 & 3","1 & 4","1 & 2","none of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T05:27:53.107Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:27:53.107Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:27:53.107Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929643961-68', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'When both bread and butter and salad plates are required, salad plate should be placed:', 'on the left side of the bread and butter plate', 'In formal and standard table setting (meal management), the left side of the cover is designated for plates, while the right side is reserved for glassware and cups.

The Bread and Butter (B&B) plate is the anchor for the upper left corner. It is always placed just above the tines of the forks.

The Salad plate, when served alongside the main meal (rather than as a separate course placed in the center), also belongs on the left side. To prevent crowding the forks or the dinner plate, the salad plate is traditionally placed to the lower left of the forks, which positions it directly to the left of the bread and butter plate (or slightly below it, depending on the table''s space constraints).', '["on the right side of the cover","on the left side of the bread and butter plate","in the middle of the cover","on top of the dinner plate"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:32:46.635Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:32:46.635Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T11:32:49.028Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929662561-69', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'No pork and pork products', 'SEVENTH DAY ADVENTIST', '', '["JEWISH","MORMONS","MUSLIMS","SEVENTH DAY ADVENTIST"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T05:28:53.978Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":1.9,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:28:53.978Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:28:53.978Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929697493-70', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'No animal products allowed for 40 days before Christmas and Easter', 'GREEK ORTHODOX', 'The Greek Orthodox Church (and Eastern Orthodox Christianity in general) observes strict fasting periods as a spiritual discipline to purify the body and mind. The two most prominent fasting periods are the Nativity Fast (40 days before Christmas) and Great Lent (40 days before Easter). During these strict fasting days, the faithful are required to abstain from all animal products—including meat, poultry, dairy, and eggs—essentially adhering to a vegan diet (and often restricting fish, olive oil, and wine on specific days).', '["JEWISH","MORMONS","MUSLIMS","GREEK ORTHODOX"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:17:20.450Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:17:20.450Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T11:33:21.798Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929713625-71', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'No food containing blood', 'SEVENTH DAY ADVENTIST', '', '["JEWISH","MORMONS","MUSLIMS","SEVENTH DAY ADVENTIST"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T05:28:41.968Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:28:41.968Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:28:41.968Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929727326-72', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Fasting is observed starting from dawn through dusk', 'MUSLIMS', 'In the Islamic faith, fasting (Sawm) is one of the Five Pillars of Islam. The most prominent fasting period occurs during the holy month of Ramadan, where Muslims are required to completely abstain from all food, water, and other beverages from dawn (Fajr) through dusk/sunset (Maghrib).

• Jewish: Major Jewish fasting days, such as Yom Kippur and Tisha B''Av, are observed from sundown to sundown, lasting for approximately 25 hours, rather than strictly dawn to dusk.
• Mormons: Members of the Latter-day Saint movement typically observe "Fast Sunday" once a month, which involves fasting for 24 hours (usually skipping two consecutive meals), not a daily dawn-to-dusk schedule.
• Seventh Day Adventist: While they have strict dietary guidelines (promoting vegetarianism and abstaining from alcohol and caffeine), a mandatory dawn-to-dusk fasting period is not a central tenet of their faith. Their time-specific observance is the Sabbath, which runs from Friday sunset to Saturday sunset.', '["JEWISH","MORMONS","MUSLIMS","SEVENTH DAY ADVENTIST"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:10:47.070Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:10:47.070Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T11:34:11.913Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929740106-73', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'No shellfish, alcoholic and caffeine containing beverages', 'MORMONS', '', '["JEWISH","MORMONS","MUSLIMS","SEVENTH DAY ADVENTIST"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:10:10.551Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:10:10.551Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:10:10.551Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929756388-74', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Foods are inspected by rabbi.', 'JEWISH', 'In the Jewish faith, foods that are prepared in accordance with strict dietary laws (Kosher) must be supervised and inspected by a Rabbi (or a designated Mashgiach under a Rabbi''s authority) to certify that all ingredients, slaughtering methods, and food handling practices strictly adhere to Kashrut.

Muslims (B) have their food inspected and certified for Halal compliance by an Imam or authorized Islamic certifying body. Mormons (C) and Seventh-Day Adventists (D) follow dietary guidelines (like avoiding alcohol/coffee or eating vegetarian), but their foods do not require formal religious inspection or certification by clergy to be eaten.', '["JEWISH","MORMONS","MUSLIMS","SEVENTH DAY ADVENTIST"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T05:28:12.408Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:28:12.408Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:28:12.408Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929770206-75', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Strictly observe “halal”', 'MUSLIMS', 'Members of the Islamic faith strictly observe Halal dietary laws. In Arabic, "halal" translates to "permissible" or "lawful," designating foods and beverages that are allowed under Islamic jurisprudence (the Quran). This includes specific guidelines for the humane slaughter of animals (Dhabiha) and strictly prohibits the consumption of haram (forbidden) items, most notably pork and alcohol.

• Jewish: The Jewish faith observes Kashruth (Kosher) dietary laws, not Halal.
• Mormons: The Latter-day Saints follow the "Word of Wisdom," which focuses on abstaining from alcohol, tobacco, and hot drinks (coffee and tea), rather than Halal guidelines.
• Seventh Day Adventist: While they have strict dietary guidelines that include abstaining from "unclean" meats (like pork and shellfish) based on biblical texts, as well as avoiding alcohol and caffeine, they do not follow Islamic Halal laws.', '["JEWISH","MORMONS","MUSLIMS","SEVENTH DAY ADVENTIST"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:13:48.928Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:13:48.928Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T11:38:14.657Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929783354-76', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Foods prepared are referred to as “KOSHER FOODS”', 'JEWISH', '"Kosher" is the specific term used to describe foods that comply with the strict dietary laws of Judaism (Kashrut), which dictate what animals can be eaten, how they must be slaughtered, and the strict separation of meat and dairy.

Foods prepared according to Muslim (B) dietary laws are called Halal. Seventh-Day Adventists (C) follow biblical clean/unclean meat laws and heavily promote vegetarianism, but do not use the term "Kosher" for their food preparation. Mormons (D) follow the "Word of Wisdom" (banning alcohol, coffee, and tea) but do not have Kosher preparation rules.', '["JEWISH","MORMONS","MUSLIMS","SEVENTH DAY ADVENTIST"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T05:27:59.988Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:27:59.988Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:27:59.988Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929801272-77', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'No meat broth', 'SEVENTH DAY ADVENTIST', 'The Seventh-day Adventist Church strongly advocates for a vegetarian lifestyle. The majority of devout followers practice a lacto-ovo vegetarian diet, which means they consume dairy and eggs but completely abstain from all meat, poultry, and fish. Because they do not consume animal flesh, all by-products derived from meat—including meat broths, stocks, gravies, and meat extractives—are also strictly avoided.

• Jewish: Jewish dietary laws (Kashruth) do not prohibit meat broth, provided the broth is made from a Kosher animal that was slaughtered correctly, and the broth is not consumed with or cooked alongside dairy products.
• Mormons: The Latter-day Saint "Word of Wisdom" advises that meat be eaten sparingly, but it does not forbid the consumption of meat or meat broths.
• Muslims: Islamic dietary laws (Halal) permit meat broth as long as it is made from Halal-certified meat and does not contain any pork derivatives or alcohol.', '["JEWISH","MORMONS","MUSLIMS","SEVENTH DAY ADVENTIST"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:14:27.153Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:14:27.153Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T11:39:54.425Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929816368-78', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Meat or poultry in combination with dairy products', 'JEWISH', 'Under Jewish dietary laws (Kashruth), it is strictly prohibited to consume, cook, or even derive benefit from meat or poultry in combination with dairy products. This fundamental rule is derived from the biblical commandment not to "boil a kid in its mother''s milk."

Because of this, Kosher-observant individuals will not eat dishes like cheeseburgers or chicken with a cream sauce. They also maintain completely separate sets of cookware, plates, and utensils for meat (fleishig) and dairy (milchig) to prevent cross-contamination, and they observe a mandatory waiting period between consuming meat and dairy.', '["JEWISH","MORMONS","MUSLIMS","SEVENTH DAY ADVENTIST"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T01:09:49.190Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T01:09:49.190Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T11:40:39.311Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929829867-79', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Order and Balance', 'Indonesian', '', '["Korean","Indonesian","Japanese","Chinese"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T05:28:34.676Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:28:34.676Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:28:34.676Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757929846585-80', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783609425474-1790433136742-1d3n3', 'Colorful, aromatic, & delicious', 'Chinese', 'In traditional Chinese culinary philosophy, the absolute golden standard for a perfect dish is that it must possess three essential characteristics: excellent color/appearance (色 - sè), aroma/smell (香 - xiāng), and taste/flavor (味 - wèi). In culinary textbooks and board exams, this traditional triad is directly translated as "colorful, aromatic, and delicious."

Japanese (D) cuisine prioritizes "order and balance" and preserving the raw, natural state of the ingredients. Korean (C) cuisine is heavily defined by fermentation (like kimchi) and an array of side dishes (banchan). Indonesian (B) cuisine is defined by its complex, pounded spice pastes (bumbu) rather than this specific three-word aesthetic philosophy.', '["Korean","Indonesian","Japanese","Chinese"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-09T05:14:39.886Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:14:39.886Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.198Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T05:14:39.886Z"'::jsonb)
