('anki-card-1756369060943-3', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'Manufacturers bile for fat emulsification.', 'Liver', 'Production: The liver makes bile every day.
Storage: The gallbladder only stores and concentrates the bile until your body needs it.', '["Liver","Pancreas","Gallbladder","Stomach"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2737-07-28T13:49:57.829Z","interval":259583,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":14}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T13:49:57.829Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T13:49:57.829Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756369113122-4', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'What is the most common, simplest fatty in foods?', 'Stearic and acetic acid', '🟢 Stearic acid is one of the most common long-chain saturated fatty acids found in everyday foods, appearing abundantly in both animal fats (like beef and butter) and plant fats (like cocoa butter).

🟢 Acetic acid is the simplest possible fatty acid because it contains only two carbon atoms (C2), making it the shortest and smallest carboxylic acid classified in this group.', '["Stearic and acetic acid","Acetic and stearic acid","Butyric and acetic acid","Butyric and stearic acid"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-01-07T14:06:25.869Z","interval":73,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:06:25.869Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:06:25.869Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756369158853-5', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'The difference between nitrogen intake and nitrogen excretion:', 'Nitrogen balance', 'At nitrogen equilibrium: N intake = N output; at positive nitrogen balance: N intake > N output; at negative nitrogen balance: N output > N intake.', '["Nitrogen balance","Protein digestibility","Amino acid score","Biologic value"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-01-14T14:12:27.035Z","interval":80,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:12:27.035Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:12:27.132Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756369203653-6', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'Transport form of lipid in blood which is associated with high cholesterol levels:', 'LDL', '❌ VLDL (Very-Low-Density Lipoprotein): Transports mainly endogenous triglycerides (not primarily cholesterol) from the liver to adipose and muscle tissue.
❌ IDL (Intermediate-Density Lipoprotein): Short-lived transitional remnant formed during the degradation of VLDL into LDL; not the primary clinical marker for elevated blood cholesterol.', '["LDL","VLDL","HDL","IDL"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2029-07-13T08:09:28.852Z","interval":988,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":7}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:09:28.852Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:09:29.188Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756369233283-7', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'Key metabolic carbohydrate:', 'Glucose', 'Glucose, also called blood sugar is the body’s major fuel to provide energy. It attaches to other sugars to form disaccharides and complex carbohydrates.', '["Glucose","Galactose","Fructose","Sucrose"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-12-30T14:10:27.039Z","interval":65,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:10:27.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:10:27.134Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756369313480-8', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'A measure of protein quality wherein the content of essential amino acids in food is divided by the amino acid requirements for each group.', 'Amino acid score', 'The amino acid score (also known as the chemical score) is a laboratory-based method used to evaluate protein quality. This measurement of the content of essential amino acids contribute to the nutrition value of a protein.

It is determined mathematically by taking the amount of each essential amino acid in a food protein and dividing it by the corresponding amino acid requirement of a standard reference profile (typically tailored to specific age groups like infants or preschool children):

Amino Acid Score = (mg of essential amino acid in 1 g of test protein / mg of essential amino acid in 1 g of reference protein) x 100

The lowest score among the essential amino acids identifies the limiting amino acid, which determines the overall quality of that specific protein source.

• Protein digestibility: A measure of the percentage of nitrogen in food that is absorbed by the digestive tract based on the difference between dietary intake and fecal excretion.
• Biologic value (BV): A measure of protein quality that calculates the percentage of absorbed nitrogen that is actually retained by the body for growth and maintenance. It requires tracking both fecal and urinary nitrogen in living subjects.
• Protein efficiency ratio (PER): A biological assay that evaluates protein quality by tracking the physical weight gain of growing animal subjects divided by their specific protein intake over a test period.', '["Amino acid score","Protein efficiency ratio","Biologic value","Protein digestibility"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2029-09-04T13:49:16.400Z","interval":1030,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":9}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T13:49:16.400Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T13:49:16.400Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756369357728-9', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'A class of carbohydrates that is also called functional foods:', 'Oligosaccharides', 'Functional foods are foods or food components that offer health benefits beyond basic nutrition (like simple energy provision).

Certain non-digestible oligosaccharides—such as Fructo-oligosaccharides (FOS) and Galacto-oligosaccharides (GOS)—act directly as prebiotics.

Instead of being broken down into simple sugars for immediate energy in the upper digestive tract, they pass into the large intestine where they feed and promote the growth of beneficial gut bacteria (Probiotics). This enhances gut health, microflora balance, and immune function, classifying them firmly as a class of carbohydrates used as functional foods.', '["Sucrose","Oligosaccharides","Fructose","Glucose"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2029-10-28T08:09:31.216Z","interval":1095,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":7}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:09:31.216Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:09:31.548Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756369437607-10', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'Oat bran, legumes, guar, pectins in fruits and vegetables are example of what?', 'Insoluble fibers', 'Insoluble fibers', '["Soluble fibers","Insoluble fibers","Crude fiber","Non-essential amino acids"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-01-04T14:09:13.502Z","interval":70,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:09:13.502Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756369508870-11', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'Nutrients are absorbed through:
I. Simple diffusion
II. Active transport
III. Facilitated diffusion
IV. Pinocytosis', 'All of the above', 'Simple diffusion - Water and small lipids cross into intestinal cells freely;
Facilitated diffusion - water soluble vitamins need a specific carrier to transport them from one side of the cell membrane to the other;
Active transport - glucose and amino acids move against a concentration gradient, which requires energy;
Pinocytosis, a form of endocytosis, in which material enters a cell through its membrane and is incorporated in vesicles for digestion.', '["All of the above","I and III only","I, II, and III","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-01-09T14:05:04.438Z","interval":75,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:05:04.438Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:05:04.438Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756369612332-12', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'These are purely ketogenic amino acids:', 'Leucine and Lysine', 'Leucine and Lysine are purely ketogenic amino acids that can be catabolized to form ketone bodies and yield acetyl CoA or acetoacetate.', '["Leucine and Lysine","Leucine and Lysine","Cysteine and Arginine","Leucine and Alanine"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-01-02T14:09:19.586Z","interval":68,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:09:19.586Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:09:19.586Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756369662180-13', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'All of the following slows or prolongs gastric emptying except:', 'Motilin', 'Motilin is released during the fasting state to stimulate the migrating motor complex (MMC), which “accelerate gastric emptying.”

🔴 Cholecystokinin (CCK): Released in response to fats and proteins in the duodenum, which “slows down the emptying of the stomach.”
🔴 Glucagon-like peptide-1 (GLP-1): Acts as an incretin hormone that also “slows gastric emptying in healthy subjects, obese subjects, type 2 diabetic patients, and critically ill subjects.”', '["Motilin","Cholecystokinin","GLP-1","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2862-06-27T13:48:57.188Z","interval":305208,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":13}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T13:48:57.188Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T13:48:57.188Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756369716013-14', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'Which is not considered as a complimentary protein meal?', 'Bread with jam', 'Complementary proteins combine two foods with different missing amino acids to make a complete protein. Bread with jam only provides carbohydrates and sugar. Jam contains no protein, so it cannot complete or complement the protein in bread.

🔴 a. Rice and mongo: grain (rice) and a legume (mung beans) 
🔴 b. Macaroni with cheese: wheat pasta with cheese
🔴 d. Pizza with salami: grain crust with meat and cheese', '["Bread with jam","Rice and Mongo","Macaroni with cheese","Bread with jam"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-12-30T14:07:14.440Z","interval":65,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:07:14.440Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:07:14.440Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756369780309-15', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'The protein splitting enzymes of the pancreas:', 'Carboxypeptidase and trypsin', 'Both are enzymes produced by the pancreas that break down proteins.

• Pancreatic lipase breaks down fats, not proteins.
• Pancreatic amylase breaks down carbohydrates (starches), not proteins.', '["Carboxypeptidase and trypsin","Carboxypeptidase and pancreatic lipase","Pancreatic lipase and pancreatic amylase","Carboxypeptidase and pancreatic amylase"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-12-30T14:12:06.470Z","interval":65,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:12:06.470Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:12:06.564Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756369854523-16', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'Limiting amino acid in rice:', 'Lysine', 'Lysine, the main limiting essential amino acid in cereals, restricts the absorption and utilization of other amino acids and proteins, which leads to nutrient deficiency.', '["Lysine","Tryptophan","Methionine","Tyrosine"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2033-10-22T08:09:52.990Z","interval":2550,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":8}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:09:52.990Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:09:53.305Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756369897553-17', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'The era when the essentiality of vitamins where established.', 'Biological era', 'Biological Era (1900 – 1955) focused on the “discovery and understanding of vitamins and their role in health.”

• a. Naturalistic Era: People believed food contained a single universal nutrient and relied on philosophy rather than chemical science to explain health.
• b. Chemical-Analytical Era: Scientists used early chemistry to discover and measure macronutrients (carbohydrates, proteins, and fats) but did not yet know vitamins existed.
• d. Cellular-Molecular Era: Modern researchers use advanced biotechnology to study how nutrients interact with human genes, DNA, and microscopic cellular pathways.', '["Biological era","Naturalistic","Chemical-Analytical","Cellular-Molecular Era"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-12-30T14:11:13.999Z","interval":65,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:11:13.999Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:11:13.999Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756369946967-18', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'A protein derivative that has been widely acclaimed to be non-toxic as a sugar substitute:', 'Aspartame', '', '["Fructose","Dextrose","Galactose","Aspartame"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-12-28T14:09:46.073Z","interval":63,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:09:46.073Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:09:46.073Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756370050416-19', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'What is the fate of excess intake of dietary protein?', 'After absorption, the extra amino acids will be rapidly degraded', 'Unlike carbohydrates and fats, the body does not have a specialized storage depot for excess amino acids or dietary protein. After dietary protein is digested and absorbed, amino acids enter the body''s amino acid pool and are used for protein synthesis and other metabolic functions. When amino acid availability exceeds the body''s immediate needs for protein synthesis and other required compounds, the excess amino acids are deaminated. Their nitrogen is converted primarily to urea in the liver and excreted in the urine, while their carbon skeletons can be used for energy or converted into glucose, ketone bodies, or other metabolites. 

Therefore, consuming more protein than needed does not result in the body storing the extra protein as protein for later use. The body continually regulates amino acid metabolism according to physiological needs. Excess energy from protein can ultimately contribute to energy storage as body fat if overall energy intake exceeds expenditure, but this occurs after amino acid catabolism, not through storage of excess dietary protein as a protein reserve.', '["After absorption, the liver will store the extra amino acids","After absorption, the extra amino acids will be rapidly degraded","Digestion will be decreased by 30-60% resulting in less absorption","After absorption, extra protein will by synthesized and stored for use when protein intake returns to normal"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-01-14T14:05:11.856Z","interval":80,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:05:11.856Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:32:00.423Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756370126892-20', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'As essential fatty acid derived from plant oils such as corn oil:', 'Linoleic acid', 'Corn oil is an excellent source of essential fatty acids, which typically exceed 60% of its total composition, with the main contribution of linoleic acid (C18:2).', '["Linoleic acid","Palmitic acid","Linolenic acid","Arachidonic acid"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-01-09T14:08:58.957Z","interval":75,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:08:58.957Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:08:58.957Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756370171373-21', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'Energy content of monosacharrides:', '4kcal/gram', '', '["2kcal/gram","4kcal/gram","6kcal/gram","9kcal/gram"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-12-30T08:07:26.267Z","interval":65,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T08:07:26.267Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T08:07:26.365Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756370211555-22', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'Hormone which stimulates the contraction of gallbladder to secrete bile:', 'Cholecystokinin', '🔴 a. Lipase: Lipase is not a hormone; it is a digestive enzyme primarily produced by the pancreas that works alongside bile to chemically break down lipids (fats) into fatty acids and glycerol.
🔴 b. Insulin: This is a metabolic hormone secreted by the beta cells of the pancreas. Its primary role is to regulate blood glucose levels by helping cells absorb glucose.
🔴 d. Cholecalciferol: This is the chemical name for Vitamin D3.', '["Cholecystokinin","Lipase","Insulin","Cholecalciferol"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-01-04T14:06:36.637Z","interval":70,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:06:36.637Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:06:36.637Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756370238121-23', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'A major component of gastric juice:', 'HCI', 'Hydrochloric acid secretion is responsible for the strong acidic condition of the stomach. With such an acidic environment, ingested proteins are denaturized thus, facilitating their digestion.', '["HCI","HCI","Amylase","Hormones"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-01-14T14:05:17.002Z","interval":80,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:05:17.002Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:05:17.002Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756370311035-24', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'Fats and carbohydrates are called protein sparing due to which of the following factors?', 'Their presence reduces the need of utilizing proteins for energy', 'Their presence reduces the need of utilizing proteins for energy', '["They comprise the major portions of diets","The body does not need protein if fats and carbohydrates are present","Their presence reduces the need of utilizing proteins for energy","They prevent storage of proteins"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-12-30T14:06:53.027Z","interval":65,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:06:53.027Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756370385317-25', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'A measure of protein quality which is determined as the percentage of nitrogen in the food and feces of subjects on a diet: containing a test protein.', 'Protein digestibility', 'Protein digestibility (specifically apparent or true digestibility) measures how well a protein source can be broken down and absorbed by the digestive tract.

It is calculated by finding the percentage of nitrogen consumed in the food that does not appear in the feces, revealing how much of that test protein was actually taken up into the body:

Protein Digestibility (%) = [(Nitrogen in Food - Nitrogen in Feces) / Nitrogen in Food] x 100

• Amino acid score: A chemical/laboratory measure that compares the amino acid profile of a test protein against a standard reference protein; it does not utilize living subjects or fecal analysis.
• Protein efficiency ratio (PER): A measure of protein quality based on the weight gain of growing animal subjects divided by their intake of a particular food protein during a specific period.
• Nitrogen balance: Measures the total influx of nitrogen versus total efflux. While it accounts for feces, it relies heavily on measuring urinary nitrogen to determine whether the body is retaining or losing overall protein mass.', '["Amino acid score","Protein efficiency ratio","Protein digestibility","Nitrogen balance"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2737-07-28T13:49:53.789Z","interval":259583,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":14}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T13:49:53.789Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T13:49:53.789Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756370426762-26', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'The interior of the intestinal tract is called __', 'Lumen', 'The actual open, interior space inside a tubular structure like the intestines where food and fluids pass.

🔴 Ileum: The final section of the small intestine.
🔴 Mucosa: The innermost tissue layer that surrounds the lumen.
🔴 Lining: A general term for the membrane covering the internal surface.', '["Lumen","Ileum","Mucosa","Lining"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-01-15T06:17:41.327Z","interval":80,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T06:17:41.327Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T06:17:41.422Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756370475760-27', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'A contemporary topic in Nutrition dealing with the nutritional problems arising as a result of medical treatment.', 'Latrogenic malnutrition', '', '["Sport nutrition","Food labeling","Space exploration","Latrogenic malnutrition"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-01-12T14:04:37.121Z","interval":78,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:04:37.121Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:04:37.121Z"'::jsonb),
