('anki-card-1756370556405-29', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'Disaccharides is an example of:', 'Simplex carbohydrates', '', '["Simplex carbohydrates","Starch","Glycogen","Fiber"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-01-04T14:11:20.530Z","interval":70,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:11:20.530Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:11:20.530Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756370606671-30', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'An impairment of health resulting from a dietary, excess, or imbalance of nutrients.', 'Malnutrition', '', '["Undernutrition","Malnutrition","Overnutrition","Nutrient deficiency"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-01-09T14:03:51.738Z","interval":75,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:03:51.738Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:03:51.738Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756370643251-31', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'The form in which lipids are transported in the blood after digestion:', 'Chylomicrons', 'Chylomicrons has the highest lipid content, lowest density, composed of TGs, synthesized in the intestinal wall and acted as transport TG in the blood and after a meal; cleared form the blood through the action of lipoprotein lipase.

🔴 Micelles: Tiny droplets that help move fatty acids to the intestinal wall, but they do not travel in the blood.
🔴 Bile salts: Chemicals made by the liver that break large fat drops into smaller ones during digestion.
🔴 Fatty acids: The individual building blocks of fats, which are reassembled into triglycerides inside cells before entering chylomicrons.', '["Chylomicrons","Micelles","Fatty acids","Bile salts"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-01-08T06:16:24.305Z","interval":73,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T06:16:24.305Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T06:16:24.402Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756370682937-32', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'Enzyme responsible for the breakdown of cooked starch to dextrin:', 'Amylase', 'Amylase produced by the pancreas enters the small intestine to assist in digestion by hydrolyzing complex carbohydrates.', '["Amylase","Lipase","Chymotrypsin","Trypsin"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-01-02T08:05:34.272Z","interval":68,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T08:05:34.272Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T08:05:34.370Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756370732781-33', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'The following are Behavioral and Human Arts with established relation with the field of Nutrition except:', 'Chemistry', '', '["Language","History","Chemistry","Sociology"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-01-03T06:17:15.574Z","interval":68,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T06:17:15.574Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T06:17:15.665Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756370785980-34', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'An important function of bile in digestion:', 'Fat emulsification', 'Bile salts are emulsifying agents; they disperse fats and form water-soluble micelles, which solubilize the products of fat digestion.', '["Fat emulsification","Fat hydrolysis","Fat emulsification","Fat absorption"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-01-04T14:07:49.698Z","interval":70,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:07:49.698Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:07:49.698Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756370811360-35', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'It stores bile until needed:', 'Gallbladder', 'The gallbladder acts like a small storage pouch or holding tank. It collects and concentrates bile between meals.

When you eat (especially foods high in fat), hormones trigger the gallbladder to contract, squeezing the stored bile through the bile ducts and into the small intestine to break down fats.', '["Liver","Pancreas","Gallbladder","Stomach"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2030-03-02T08:08:21.456Z","interval":1220,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":7}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:08:21.456Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:08:21.764Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756370867741-36', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'It prevents the reflux of small intestine contents to the stomach:', 'Pyloric sphincter', 'Acts as a barrier to prevent the backward flow (reflux) of small intestine con tents—which contain bile and pancreatic enzymes—back into the stomach.

❌ a. Upper esophageal sphincter: Controls the passage of food into the feeding tube while preventing air from entering the gastrointestinal tract.
❌ c. Lower esophageal sphincter: Regulates food entering the stomach while specifically preventing stomach acid and contents from refluxing upward into the esophagus.
❌ d. Cardiac sphincter: This is simply another name for the lower esophageal sphincter.', '["Pyloric sphincter","Upper esophageal sphincter","Pyloric sphincter","Cardiac sphincter"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-12-30T08:05:57.079Z","interval":65,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T08:05:57.079Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T08:05:57.185Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756370930288-37', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'The following are physiological actions of dietary fiber except:', 'Improves mineral absorption', 'Dietary fiber—particularly when paired with food components like phytates, oxalates, and tannins found in high-fiber plant foods—actually binds to essential minerals (such as iron, zinc, calcium, and magnesium) in the intestinal tract. This binding action makes the minerals insoluble and decreases or hinders their absorption rather than improving it.', '["Increases bile acid excretion","Improves glucose tolerance","Decreases stool transit time","Improves mineral absorption"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2033-05-05T13:48:51.863Z","interval":2369,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":10}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T13:48:51.863Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T13:48:51.863Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756370975587-38', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'The complex formed when bile salts combine with lipid material to facilitate digestion.', 'Micelle', 'Micelles are aggregated lipids formed from bile salts to help the transport and absorption of fat-soluble vitamins and digestive products of lipids in the human body.', '["Micelle","Chylomicron","Micelle","HDL"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-01-07T14:10:58.997Z","interval":73,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:10:58.997Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:10:58.997Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756371019402-39', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'Which molecule provides the immediate source of energy for muscle contraction?', 'ATP', 'Adenosine triphosphate (ATP) is the immediate source of energy used to power muscle contractions.

Inside muscle fibers, ATP binds directly to myosin heads. The subsequent hydrolysis of ATP into ADP (adenosine diphosphate) and an inorganic phosphate molecule (Pi) releases immediate chemical energy. This energy powers the myosin "power stroke," sliding the muscle filaments past each other to cause a physical contraction. ATP is also required to disconnect the cross-bridges and pump calcium back into storage.

• Lactic acid: A metabolic byproduct created during anaerobic glycolysis. It is not an energy source for contractions and can contribute to muscle fatigue if it accumulates heavily.
• Glycogen: The storage form of carbohydrates inside liver and muscle cells. While it acts as a premier reservoir of energy, it must first undergo glycogenolysis and glycolysis to generate ATP molecules before the muscles can utilize it.
• Fructose: A simple monosaccharide (fruit sugar) that must travel to the liver to be metabolized and fed into central energy pathways to generate ATP; it cannot be directly used by myosin heads.', '["Lactic acid","ATP","Glycogen","Fructose"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2687-04-18T13:49:03.017Z","interval":241220,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":14}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T13:49:03.017Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T13:49:03.017Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756371062016-40', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'The breakdown of triglycerides into fatty acids and glycerol:', 'Lipolysis', '*breakdown - hydrolysis

Lipolysis is also known as TAG degradation.', '["Lipolysis","Glycolysis","Lipogenesis","Beta oxidation"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-01-07T14:06:46.506Z","interval":73,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:06:46.506Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:06:46.506Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756371134828-41', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'Carbohydrate derivative which serves as a detoxifying agent in the liver:', 'Heparin', '❌ Ribose is a 5-carbon sugar used for RNA and ATP; has no detoxifying role.
❌ Pentose is a broad chemical class of 5-carbon monosaccharides; not a specific liver derivative.
❌ Maltose is a simple glucose disaccharide; broken down solely for energy.', '["Heparin","Ribose","Maltose","Pentose"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-01-12T14:05:35.980Z","interval":78,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:05:35.980Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:05:35.980Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756371203559-42', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'All of these are essential amino acids for adults EXCEPT:
I. Arginine
II. Glutamine
III. Lysine
IV. Leucine', 'I and II', '🟢 Arginine (I) is conditionally essential. Adults can make enough of it on their own, though growing children need it in their diet.
🟢 Glutamine (II) is a non-essential amino acid. Your body creates it in sufficient amounts under normal conditions.', '["I and II","II only","III only","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2030-01-16T08:08:44.220Z","interval":1175,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":7}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:08:44.220Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:08:44.541Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756371255890-43', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'An era in the field of Nutrition characterized by food taboos, magical power and medicinal value of food.', 'Naturalistic', '', '["Naturalistic","Chemical-analytical","Biological","Cellular-molecular"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-01-07T14:12:21.985Z","interval":73,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:12:21.985Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:12:22.078Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756371306506-44', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'The wavelike action causing relaxation and contraction of the muscles of the GI tract.', 'Peristalsis', '🔴 Digestion: The process of breaking down food into small nutrients.
🔴 Segmentation: Back-and-forth mixing of food in the intestine.
🔴 Excretion: The removal of waste products from the body.', '["Peristalsis","Digestion","Segmentation","Excretion"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-01-14T14:07:40.144Z","interval":80,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:07:40.144Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:07:40.144Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756371351636-45', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'The one animal polysaccharide that is not present in foods but is generally stored in the liver and muscle:', 'Glycogen', 'Glycogen is the storage form of carbohydrates in animals.', '["Glycogen","Lignin","Polymer","Lecithin"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-01-09T14:07:04.790Z","interval":75,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:07:04.790Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:07:04.790Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756371392250-46', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'Protein splitting enzyme secreted by the gastric glands and the stomach.', 'Pepsin', 'Pepsin is the main protein-digesting enzyme in the stomach. It is secreted by the gastric glands in an inactive form called pepsinogen. Pepsin cleaves proteins to smaller polypeptides and some free amino acids.', '["Pepsin","Rennin","Gastric lipase","Trypsin"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2034-04-28T08:09:40.815Z","interval":2738,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":8}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:09:40.815Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:09:41.137Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756371441848-47', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'Fatty acids present in animal fats are said to be:', 'Saturated fatty acids', 'In animals, the carbon atoms in the fatty acids are saturated with hydrogen atoms. This allows them to lie straight, and the molecules will pack neatly into a solid arrangement.', '["Saturated fatty acids","Containing hundreds of double bonds","Linoleic acid","Unsaturated fatty acids"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2029-09-26T08:08:04.949Z","interval":1063,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":7}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:08:04.949Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:08:05.271Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756371479365-48', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'The transport form of lipid which is associated with low cholesterol level is:', 'HDL', 'High-Density Lipoprotein (HDL) is famously referred to as "good cholesterol." It acts as a specialized scavenger vessel in the bloodstream.

Its primary physiological function is to gather excess, circulating cholesterol from peripheral tissues and blood vessel walls and transport it back to the liver. The liver then processes, breaks down, and safe-clears this lipid burden out of the body.

Because HDL acts directly to clear away excess fats, higher circulating levels of functional HDL are structurally associated with lower overall peripheral tissue cholesterol levels and a reduced risk of plaque build-up (atherosclerosis).

• LDL (Low-Density Lipoprotein): Acts as the primary transporter that delivers cholesterol to the cells and arteries. High levels of LDL are strongly associated with high peripheral cholesterol and heart disease risk.
• VLDL (Very Low-Density Lipoprotein): Primarily carries newly made triglycerides from the liver out to body tissues.
• IDL (Intermediate-Density Lipoprotein): A short-lived transition state formed as VLDL drops off its triglycerides and degrades into LDL.', '["VLDL","LDL","HDL","IDL"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2034-02-07T08:08:29.859Z","interval":2658,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":8}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:08:29.859Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:08:30.182Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756371543409-49', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'Obtained from food because the body cannot synthesize it in sufficient quantities to meet physiological needs.', 'Essential nutrients', 'Essential nutrients', '["Nutrients","Food","Essential nutrients","Non-essential nutrients"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-12-30T14:03:41.240Z","interval":65,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-26T14:03:41.240Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788372240959-50', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'Which of the following is an essential fatty acid?', 'Linoleic acid', 'Linoleic acid is an omega-6 polyunsaturated fatty acid. It is classified as "essential" because the human body lacks the desaturase enzymes required to insert a chemical double bond beyond the carbon-9 position of a fatty acid chain. Because your body cannot synthesize it from scratch, it must be consumed directly through your diet (such as from vegetable oils, nuts, and seeds).

❌ Palmitic acid: Saturated 16-carbon fatty acid synthesized endogenously by fatty acid synthase.
❌ Stearic acid: Saturated 18-carbon fatty acid readily produced in the body from palmitic acid elongation.
❌ Oleic acid: Monounsaturated omega-9 fatty acid synthesized endogenously via Δ9 desaturase.', '["Linoleic acid","Palmitic acid","Stearic acid","Oleic acid"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 3, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-04T15:17:09.130Z","interval":8,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:17:09.130Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:17:09.222Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788372300280-51', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'Which of the following is an example of soluble dietary fiber?', 'Pectin', 'Pectin is a structural polysaccharide found in the cell walls of fruits and vegetables (such as apples, citrus fruits, and carrots). It is highly water-soluble and absorbs water in the gastrointestinal tract to form a viscous, gel-like substance. This gelation slows down digestion, delays gastric emptying, stabilizes blood sugar levels, and binds to bile acids to help lower LDL cholesterol.

❌ Cellulose: Insoluble structural plant polysaccharide; adds fecal bulk without dissolving or gelling.
❌ Lignin: Insoluble, non-carbohydrate complex polymer (polyphenolic); remains completely intact throughout the GI tract.
❌ Chitin: Insoluble structural polysaccharide found in fungal walls and arthropod exoskeletons; non-gel-forming.', '["Pectin","Cellulose","Chitin","Lignin"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 3, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-04T15:15:36.076Z","interval":8,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:15:36.076Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:15:36.175Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788372355219-52', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'Which carbohydrate-related compound is important in hepatic conjugation reactions that help detoxify certain substances?', 'Glucuronic acid', 'Glucuronic acid (a sugar acid derived from glucose oxidation) is the essential component in glucuronidation, one of the most important Phase II detoxification pathways in the liver (hepatic system).

During this process:
1. An enzyme transfers glucuronic acid onto toxic, hydrophobic (fat-soluble) substances like bilirubin, steroid hormones, and various drugs/toxins.
2. This attachment significantly increases the molecule''s water solubility.
3. The newly conjugated, non-toxic compound can then be safely excreted from the body via bile or urine.', '["Ribose","Glucuronic acid","Lactose","Maltose"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 3, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-04T15:16:29.553Z","interval":8,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:16:29.553Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:16:29.646Z"'::jsonb)
