('anki-card-1788372517885-53', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'Which class of carbohydrates includes prebiotic compounds such as fructooligosaccharides?', 'Oligosaccharides', 'Oligosaccharides of various origins have been used as pharmacological supplements, food ingredients, in processed food to aid weight control, to regulation of glucose control for diabetic patients and reducing serum lipid levels in hyperlipidemics and other some acute and chronic diseases.', '["Oligosaccharides","Monosaccharides","Oligosaccharides","Disaccharides"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 3, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-04T15:14:01.497Z","interval":8,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:14:01.497Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:14:01.592Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788372560281-54', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'Sugar alcohols are produced primarily by the:', 'Reduction of sugars', 'Sugar alcohols (also called polyols) are formed when the reactive carbonyl group—specifically the aldehyde or ketone group—of a sugar molecule is reduced to a hydroxyl group.

During this reduction process, hydrogen is added to the sugar molecule. This converts the open-chain form of a sugar into a non-reducing polyol that lacks any functional carbonyl groups.

Examples of Sugar Reductions:

• Glucose reduces to form Sorbitol (D-glucitol)
• Mannose reduces to form Mannitol
• Xylose reduces to form Xylitol
• Galactose reduces to form Galactitol', '["Oxidation of fatty acids","Reduction of sugars","Hydrolysis of proteins","Oxidation of amino acids"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 3, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-04T15:14:50.039Z","interval":8,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:14:50.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:14:50.137Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788372591830-55', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'Which of the following is an example of complementary plant proteins?', 'Rice and mungo', 'Complementary proteins are two or more incomplete plant-based protein sources that, when eaten together, balance out each other''s missing amino acids to create a complete protein profile containing all nine essential amino acids.

The classic formula for this is pairing a grain with a legume:
• Rice (Grain): Is low in the essential amino acid lysine but high in methionine.
• Mungo / Mung Bean (Legume): Is high in lysine but low in methionine.

When you consume them together (a staple combination in Filipino and various Asian cultures), they perfectly offset each other''s deficits.', '["Rice and fish","Chicken and egg","Rice and mungo","Milk and cheese"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 3, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-04T15:17:59.073Z","interval":8,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:17:59.073Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:17:59.170Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788372625366-56', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610383500-1790433139830-giedk', 'Which artificial sweetener is a methyl ester of a dipeptide composed of aspartic acid and phenylalanine?', 'Aspartame', 'Aspartame is 160 to 220 times sweeter than sucrose that is noncariogenic and has limited glycemic response.', '["Aspartame","Sucralose","Saccharin","Acesulfame potassium"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 3, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-04T15:13:50.933Z","interval":8,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:13:50.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.744Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:13:51.029Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756551655927-0', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Also known as Vitamin H.', 'Biotin', 'Vitamin H is another name for biotin, which is also known as vitamin B7. The "H" comes from the German words "Haar und Haut," which mean hair and skin. It helps maintain healthy hair, skin, and nails.

Biotin is also known as Vitamin B7, Coenzyme R, Bios I, and anti-egg white injury factor.', '["Biotin","Riboflavin","Anti-vitamins","Carnitine"]'::jsonb, '["a.","Biotin"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:26:16.233Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:26:16.233Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:26:16.233Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756551715126-1', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'All of the following are functions of cobalamin EXCEPT:', 'antioxidant', 'Cobalamin (Vitamin B12) does not primarily function as a direct antioxidant in the body, unlike Vitamins C or E.', '["antioxidant","co-factors","healthy nerves (myelin sheath)"]'::jsonb, '["a.","Biotin"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:51:10.918Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:51:10.918Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:51:11.204Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756551746109-2', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'It enhances iron absorption.', 'Vit C', 'Vitamin C facilitates iron absorption by forming a chelate with ferric iron at acid pH that remains soluble at the alkaline pH of the duodenum.', '["Vit C","Vit A","Vit B","Vit D"]'::jsonb, '["a.","Biotin"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:58:26.999Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:58:26.999Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:58:26.999Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756551796538-3', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Deficiency of this micronutrient is associated with scurvy.', 'Vit C', 'Consumption of 100 mg of Vitamin C per day can increase the total body pool to a level of 1.2-2.0 g that is sufficient to protect the body from scurvy for 90 days.', '["Vit C","Vit A","Vit B","Vit K"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:40:38.638Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:40:38.638Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:40:38.638Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756551835622-4', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Anti-hemorrhagic factor.', 'Vit K', 'Blood clotting action of Vitamin K may cause hemorrhage.', '["Vit K","Vit A","Vit D","Vit E"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:27:03.946Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:27:03.946Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:27:03.946Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756551901850-5', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Chemical precursors of vitamins that are converted within the body to active vitamins.', 'Provitamins', 'Provitamins are inactive substances that the body can convert into active vitamins through normal metabolic processes. A classic example is beta-carotene, which the human body converts into active Vitamin A in the intestinal wall.

• Tetrahydrofolate is already an active, coenzyme form of Vitamin B9 (folate), rather than a precursor.
• Anti-vitamins are chemical compounds that inhibit the absorption or metabolic actions of vitamins.', '["Provitamins","Anti-vitamins","Previtamins","Tertrahydrofolate"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:45:09.756Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:45:09.756Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:45:09.756Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756551957214-6', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'The energy-releasing process by which large molecules are broken down to form smaller molecules is:', 'Catabolism', 'Catabolism is the branch of metabolism specifically responsible for breaking down complex, large molecules (such as carbohydrates, proteins, and lipids) into smaller, simpler units. This degradation process releases energy, which cells capture and store primarily in the form of ATP.

• Anabolism is the exact opposite; it uses energy to build large molecules from smaller ones.
• Metabolism is the overarching term that combines both catabolism and anabolism.
• Glycolysis is a specific metabolic pathway that breaks down glucose, meaning it is an example of a catabolic process rather than the general definition.', '["Anabolism","Catabolism","Metabolism","Glycolysis"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:31:30.513Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:31:30.513Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:31:30.888Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756552004928-7', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'A 6-carbon vitamin compound closely related to the monosaccharide glucose.', 'Vit B6', 'Vitamin B6 (specifically its vitamer Pyridoxine) is a 6-carbon compound (chemical formula: C₈H₁₁NO₃) containing a pyridine ring with six ring carbons. It has key structural similarities and functional relationships with glucose metabolism (e.g., serving as an essential cofactor for glycogen phosphorylase to break down glycogen into glucose units).

• Note on Vitamin C: While Vitamin C (Ascorbic acid) is the classic 6-carbon vitamin structurally derived directly from and most closely resembling the monosaccharide glucose (C₆H₈O₆), it is not listed among the given options. Among the choices provided, Vitamin B6 matches the 6-carbon molecular framework constraint.
• Vitamin B12 is an extremely large, complex organometallic compound containing dozens of carbons and a cobalt core.
• Vitamins D₂ and D₃ are large Secosteroid structural variants containing over 27 carbons.', '["Vit B6","Vit B12","Vit D2","Vit D3"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:48:09.719Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:48:09.719Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:48:10.055Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756552070759-8', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'A B-vitamin in pyruvate dehydrogenase, and enzyme that converts pyruvate to acetyl co-A.', 'B1', 'Vitamin B1 or thiamin is a coenzyme of pyruvate dehydrogenase complex that catalyze the conversion of pyruvate to acetyl-coA.', '["B1","B5","B2","B3"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:26:41.726Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:26:41.726Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:26:41.726Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756552139689-9', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Which of the following is NOT considered a micromineral?', 'Chlorine', 'Chlorine is a macronutrient mineral present in amounts greater than 5g.

Chlorine is classified as a macromineral (major mineral). Macrominerals are required by the body in large quantities (greater than 100 mg per day), alongside calcium, sodium, and potassium. Therefore, it is not a micromineral.

• Copper, Zinc, and Iron: Both of these are classic examples of essential microminerals (trace minerals) required by the body in very small quantities.', '["Chlorine","Iron","Copper","Zinc"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-03-03T08:08:49.573Z","interval":125,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":7}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:08:49.573Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:08:49.913Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756552165821-10', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Helps maintain normal blood sugar level.', 'Chromium', 'Chromium is a trace mineral that helps the body use insulin properly. It makes insulin more effective at moving sugar (glucose) from your blood into your cells for energy.', '["Chromium","Iron","Selenium","Copper"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:26:58.785Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:26:58.785Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:26:58.785Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756552204303-11', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'This micronutrient is deficient for those with rachitic rosary.', 'Vit D', 'Rachitic rosary is the swelling or beading at the costochondral junctions where the ribs meet the cartilage, looking like a string of beads on the chest. It is a classic physical sign of Rickets, caused by a lack of Vitamin D, which stops proper bone hardening.', '["Vit D","Calcium","Phosphorus","Vit D"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:28:59.849Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:28:59.849Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:29:00.263Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756552292868-12', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Its anti-vitamin is isonicotinic acid hydrazide used in the treatment of tuberculosis.', 'Vit B6', 'Isoniazid inhibits pyridoxine phosphokinase, which is responsible for maintaining the active form of vitamin B6. Isonicotinic acid hydrazide is known to increase vitamin B6 requirements.', '["Vit B6","Vit B1","Vit B6","Vit B12"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:36:09.939Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:36:09.939Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:36:09.939Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756552358165-13', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Its coenzymes FAD and FMN participate in oxidation-reduction reactions due to their ability to accept and transfer H atoms.', 'Riboflavin', 'Riboflavin (Vitamin B2) is the precursor for FAD (Flavin Adenine Dinucleotide) and FMN (Flavin Mononucleotide).

Riboflavin, the primary redox active component of flavin, is involved in many redox processes in biogeochemical systems. The flavin ring in these coenzymes can reversibly accept and transfer two hydrogen atoms (electrons and protons), switching between oxidized and reduced states (e.g., FAD  FADH₂).', '["Riboflavin","Thiamin","Riboflavin","Niacin"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:37:27.602Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:37:27.602Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:37:27.602Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756552395996-14', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Anti-beriberi factor.', 'Thiamin', 'Beri-beri is the result of thiamin deficiency. Thiamin (Vitamin B1) is historically designated as the anti-beriberi factor because its clinical discovery directly stemmed from searching for a cure for beriberi.

Beriberi is a severe deficiency disease caused by a lack of Thiamin, presenting as either dry beriberi (neurological damage, muscle wasting) or wet beriberi (cardiovascular failure, edema).

• Niacin (B3) is the anti-pellagra factor, while Riboflavin (B2) deficiency causes ariboflavinosis (cheilosis, glossitis).', '["Thiamin","Thiamin","Riboflavin","B4"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:54:58.734Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:54:58.734Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:54:59.010Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756552487008-15', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'The following are functions of sodium, except:', 'Participates in detoxification reactions', 'Sodium also maintains the normal pH value of extracellular fluids but does not participate in detoxification reactions.', '["Participates in detoxification reactions","Maintenance of normal extracellular fluid balance.","Absorption of glucose and in the transport of other nutrients"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:39:37.462Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:39:37.462Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:39:37.462Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756552537088-16', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'A vitamin synthesized in the liver from the amino acid tryptophan.', 'Niacin', 'Also known as vitamin B3, niacin is unique among water-soluble vitamins because the body does not rely solely on dietary intake. The liver can directly synthesize niacin from the essential amino acid tryptophan via the kynurenine pathway. 1 mg of niacin can be synthesized from the ingestion of 60 mg of tryptophan.', '["Niacin","Thiamin","Riboflavin","Niacin"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:50:50.353Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:50:50.353Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:50:50.353Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756552594054-17', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Deficiency of this micronutrient is associated with bleeding associated with delayed blood clotting.', 'Vitamin K', 'Vitamin K is well-known as the "clotting vitamin". It functions as an essential cofactor for the enzyme that activates crucial blood coagulation factors (Factors II, VII, IX, and X) in the liver.

A deficiency in Vitamin K means these clotting factors cannot be properly synthesized, directly causing delayed blood clotting, prolonged prothrombin time, and an increased risk of bruising or bleeding (hemorrhage).

• While a Vitamin C deficiency (scurvy) can cause fragile blood vessels and bleeding gums, it does not directly impair the chemical coagulation cascade like Vitamin K does.', '["Iron","Vit C","Choline","Vitamin K"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:33:23.738Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:33:23.738Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:33:23.738Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756552631168-18', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'It is considered both a vitamin and a hormone.', 'Vit D', 'As a vitamin: You can get it from food or supplements because your body needs it to stay healthy.

As a hormone: Your body can also make it in your skin when the sun shines on it. It travels through your blood to tell other parts of your body, like your bones and intestines, to absorb calcium.', '["Vit D","Vit A","Vit D","Vit E"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:51:16.681Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:51:16.681Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:51:16.982Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756552679683-19', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'The following are antioxidant vitamin EXCEPT:', 'Vitamin K', 'Vitamin K is primarily required for blood coagulation (clotting) and bone metabolism, but it does not serve as a major antioxidant.

• Vitamins A, C, and E (often remembered by the acronym ACE) are the primary nutrient antioxidants. They protect cells from damage by neutralizing free radicals.', '["Vitamin A","Vitamin C","Vitamin E","Vitamin K"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:32:33.619Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:32:33.619Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:32:33.900Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756552785278-20', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'A component of coenzyme A, a carrier of acetyl groups.', 'Pantothenic acid', 'Pantothenate is vitamin B5 and is the key precursor for the biosynthesis of CoA, a universal and essential cofactor involved in a myriad of metabolic reactions, including the synthesis of phospholipids, the synthesis and degradation of fatty acids, and the operation of the TCA cycle.', '["Pantothenic acid","Biotin","Provitamin","Thiamin"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:40:57.333Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:40:57.333Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:40:57.622Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756552822876-21', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'It is known as anti-hemolytic vitamin.', 'Vitamin E', 'Vitamin E is historically recognized as the anti-hemolytic vitamin because it protects the cell membranes of red blood cells (erythrocytes) from oxidative damage caused by free radicals. Without adequate Vitamin E, the lipid bilayer undergoes lipid peroxidation, making the cells fragile and causing them to rupture easily (hemolytic anemia).

• Vitamin K is the anti-hemorrhagic vitamin (prevents bleeding/hemorrhage), which is a common point of confusion.
• Folic acid deficiency leads to megaloblastic anemia, not hemolytic anemia.', '["Folic acid","Biotin","Vitamin K","Vitamin E"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:52:15.015Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:52:15.015Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:52:15.360Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756552945319-22', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Vitamins known to lower the levels of homocysteine in the blood, a byproduct of methionine metabolism and a known risk factor to heart disease.', 'Vit B2, B6, B12', 'Vitamin B2 (Riboflavin): Serves as a key cofactor for the methylenetetrahydrofolate reductase (MTHFR) enzyme. This enzyme generates the active folate necessary to drive the remethylation of homocysteine.

Vitamin B6 (Pyridoxine): Acts as a cofactor for cystathionine β-synthase (CBS), driving the transsulfuration pathway that converts homocysteine into cysteine.

Vitamin B12 (Cobalamin): Functions as a critical cofactor for methionine synthase, an enzyme that remethylates homocysteine back into methionine.', '["Vit B2, B6, B12","Vit B2, B5, B9","Vit B3, B5, B7","Vit B3, B7, B12"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:34:23.895Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:34:23.895Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:34:24.383Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756553029383-23', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'It is the pressure exerted by plasma proteins and keeps the fluid inside the blood.', 'Oncotic pressure', 'Oncotic pressure is a colloid pressure that occurs at the venular end of the blood capillaries that prevents fluid from leaving and helps removing metabolic wastes from the tissues.', '["Oncotic pressure","Hydrostatic pressure","Oncotic pressure","Osmotic pressure"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:34:42.637Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:34:42.637Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:34:43.010Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756553140810-24', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Its other name is pteroylglutamic acid; also citrovocum factor, lactobacillus casei factor, Vitamin M, and Factor U.', 'Folic acid', 'Other names of folic acid is folate, folacin, citrovorum factor, lactobacillus casei factor, Vitamin M, Vitamin B and Factor U.', '["Folic acid","Iron","Folic acid","Niacin"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:29:19.882Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:29:19.882Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:29:20.369Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756553198559-25', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'A mineral involved taste perception, sperm production, immune function, and is also proven to cure diarrhea among children.', 'Zinc', 'Zinc plays an indispensable role in taste perception (as a structural component of gustin/carbonic anhydrase VI), sperm production and male fertility, and immune system function (mediating T-cell development and macrophage function).

Crucially, clinical trials and healthcare bodies like the WHO explicitly recognize and recommend short-term zinc supplementation as an effective treatment to reduce the severity and duration of diarrhea among children.

• The other listed minerals (Selenium, Magnesium, and Manganese) are vital micronutrients but do not fit this specific, clinically proven combination of functions—particularly the specific therapeutic use for pediatric diarrhea.', '["Selenium","Magnesium","Manganese","Zinc"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:50:38.479Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:50:38.479Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:50:38.479Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756553241240-26', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Anti-pernicious anemia factor.', 'Vit B12', 'Vitamin B12 participates in the normal development and maturation of RBCs.', '["Vit B12","Vit B1","Vit B6","Vit B9"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:29:10.864Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:29:10.864Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:29:11.420Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756553304953-27', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Component of PLP.', 'Vit B6', 'Pyridoxal 5′-phosphate (PLP) is the active, functional form of Vitamin B6 in the body. Vitamin B6 can be converted to the coenzyme PLP that transfers amino groups from amino acid to make nonessential amino acids.', '["Vit B6","Vit B1","Vit B6","Vit B12"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:58:13.023Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:58:13.023Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:58:13.023Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756553346036-28', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'High intake of this mineral decreases the absorption of copper.', 'Iron', 'High dietary intake or supplementation of iron can competitively inhibit the intestinal absorption of copper (sharing pathways like DMT1 and CTR1).

Excessive iron levels can lead to a reduction in copper status and potentially cause copper deficiency.', '["Iron","Folic acid","Niacin","Zinc"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:28:47.667Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:28:47.667Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:28:47.979Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756553398617-29', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Involved in biosynthesis of collagen.', 'Vit C', 'Vitamin C plays a critical role in the maintenance of a normal mature collagen network by preventing the auto-inactivation of lysyl and prolyl hydroxylase, two key enzymes in collagen biosynthesis.', '["Vit C","Vit A","Vit B","Vit D"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:36:24.930Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:36:24.930Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:36:24.930Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756553436564-30', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'It is considered antioxidative mineral.', 'Selenium', 'Selenium is a cofactor of the antioxidant exam glutathione peroxidase, making it an antioxidant mineral.', '["Selenium","Iron","Zinc","Selenium"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:31:42.970Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:31:42.970Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:31:43.267Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756553479312-31', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'All are sulfur-containing vitamin EXCEPT:', 'B5', 'Among the choices provided, Vitamin B5 (Pantothenic acid) is the only one whose chemical structure does not inherently contain a sulfur atom.

• Vitamin B1 (Thiamine): Contains a thiazole ring, which explicitly features a sulfur atom joined with nitrogen.
• Vitamin B7 (Biotin): Features a tetrahydrothiophene ring system, which structurally contains a sulfur atom.
• Vitamin B5 (Pantothenic acid): Formed from the combination of pantoic acid and beta-alanine. It contains carbon, hydrogen, nitrogen, and oxygen, but no sulfur. (Note: While it binds to Coenzyme A—which has a sulfur-containing thiol group—to function in the body, the vitamin molecule itself does not contain sulfur).', '["B1","B5","B7","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-09-07T08:10:34.973Z","interval":313,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":8}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:10:34.973Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:10:35.299Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756553527761-32', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Erythrocyte maturation factor.', 'Vit B12', 'Vitamin B12 is critical to normal DNA synthesis, which in turn affects erythrocyte maturation.', '["Vit B12","Vit B1","Vit B6","Vit B9"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-03-03T08:10:21.595Z","interval":125,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":7}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:10:21.595Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:10:21.900Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756553635340-33', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Coenzyme form of folate (complete name).', '5-methyltetrahydrofolate', 'It also serves as the methyl-group donor in the remethylation of homocysteine to methionine.', '["5-methyltetrahydrofolate","S-adenosyl methionine","Homocysteine","7-dehydrocholesterol"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:42:26.977Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:42:26.977Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:42:26.977Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756553674704-34', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'It is the key enzyme in the regulation of glycolysis.', 'Phosphofructokinase', 'Phosphofructokinase catalyzes the ATP-dependent phosphorylation to convert fructose-6-phosphate into fructose 1,6-bisphosphate and ADP, it is one of the key regulatory steps of glycolysis.', '["Phosphofructokinase","Phosphofructokinase","NADPH","NAD"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-09-07T08:10:16.635Z","interval":313,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":8}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:10:16.635Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:10:16.965Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756553738168-35', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Characterized by microcytic, hypochromic anemia:', 'Both a and b', 'Most common nutritional cause: Iron deficiency', '["Both a and b","Iron deficiency","B6 deficiency","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:42:51.822Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:42:51.822Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:42:51.822Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756553831314-36', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', '__ is the form of Vit K found in animal products while __ is the form of Vit K in plants.', 'Menaquione, Phylloquione', 'Menaquinone (Vitamin K2) is primarily of bacterial origin and is the main form of Vitamin K found in animal products (such as meat, dairy, and eggs) and fermented foods.

Phylloquinone (Vitamin K1) is synthesized directly by plants and is found abundantly in green leafy vegetables.', '["Phylloquione, Menaquione","Menaquione, Phylloquione","Phylloquione, Phylloquione","Menaquione, Menaquione"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:58:07.552Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:58:07.552Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:58:07.552Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756553894911-37', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Deficiency of this micronutrient is associated with anencephaly.', 'Folic acid', 'Folate deficiency is highly associated with the risk of neural tube defects in growing fetus, malformation of the brain or lack of brain and skull (anencephaly) and spinal cord that result in disability or death.', '["Folic acid","Cobalamin","Biotin","Provitamins"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:49:26.998Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:49:26.998Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:49:27.560Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756553962627-38', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'The first symptom of Vitamin A deficiency affecting vision.', 'Nyctalopia', 'Nyctalopia is also called as night blindness. Manifestations of Vitamin A deficiency include eye defects including nyctalopia as the first symptom affecting vision.', '["Nyctalopia","Conjunctivitis","Corneal Xerosis","Nyctalopia"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:25:54.302Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:25:54.302Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:25:54.302Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756554024954-39', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Deficiency of this vitamin is associated with alopecia or baldness.', 'Biotin', 'Alopecia is linked with deficiency in biotin (Vitamin B7)', '["Biotin","Riboflavin","Pantothenic acid","Folate"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:27:23.844Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:27:23.844Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:27:24.150Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756554155165-40', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', '__ is the most abundant cation outside the cell while __ is the most abundant anion inside the cell.', 'Sodium, Phosphate', 'Sodium (Na⁺) is the principal, most abundant cation (positively charged ion) found in the extracellular fluid. It plays a dominant role in regulating osmotic pressure, fluid balance, and blood volume.

While Potassium (K⁺) is the most abundant cation inside the cell, Phosphate (primarily as HPO₄²⁻) is the most abundant anion (negatively charged ion) inside the intracellular fluid. It is vital for cellular energy production (ATP synthesis), DNA/RNA structure, and functioning as an intracellular acid-base buffer.

🔴 Chloride: most abundant ''anion outside'' the cell
🔴 Potassium: most abundant ''cation inside'' the cell', '["Sodium, Phosphate","Sodium, Chloride","Potassium, Chloride","Potassium, Phosphate"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-03-03T08:08:11.231Z","interval":125,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":8}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:08:11.231Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:08:11.540Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756554202246-41', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'A pellagra-preventive (P-P) factor.', 'Niacin', 'Severe niacin deficiency could lead to Pellagra, which is characterized by dementia, diarrhea, dermatitis, and death.', '["Niacin","Thiamin","Riboflavin","Niacin"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:49:35.033Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:49:35.033Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:49:35.471Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756554246293-42', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Component of enzyme that is involved in purine metabolism.', 'Molybdenum', 'Molybdenum is a cofactor for aldehyde oxidase, which participates in metabolism of purines.', '["Molybdenum","Manganese","Molybdenum","Copper"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-03-03T08:08:53.268Z","interval":125,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":8}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:08:53.268Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:08:53.586Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756554307908-43', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Vit D activation to 1,25 dihydroxycholecalciferol takes place in __.', 'Kidney', 'Activation of Vitamin D takes place in the skin, liver, and kidneys but the site of Vitamin D activation to 1,25 dihydroxycholecalciferol takes place in the kidneys.', '["Kidney","Liver","Skin","Both A and B"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2027-09-07T08:09:43.375Z","interval":313,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":8}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:09:43.375Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:09:43.697Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756554374872-44', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Nutrient that promotes calcium-binding protein activity in the intestinal tract.', 'Vit D', 'Vitamin D facilitates calcium absorption.

Vitamin D (specifically its active form, calcitriol) acts as a hormone that upregulates the transcription and expression of calbindin, a crucial calcium-binding protein located in the intestinal epithelial cells. This protein physically binds and facilitates the active transport and absorption of calcium across the intestinal tract.

• Vitamins A, E, and K do not play a direct role in inducing intestinal calcium-binding protein synthesis or managing active dietary calcium absorption.', '["Vit D","Vit A","Vit K","Vit E"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:56:48.293Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:56:48.293Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:56:48.760Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756554432103-45', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'In metabolic reactions, vitamins usualy serves as __ while minerals as __.', 'coenzymes, cofactors', 'Water-soluble vitamins (coenzymes) and minerals (cofactors) are required by enzymes to catalyze a specific reaction and assist in converting a substrate to an end-product.', '["coenzymes, cofactors","catalyst, inhibitor","cofactors, coenzymes","inhibitor, catalyst"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:36:52.713Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:36:52.713Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:36:52.713Z"'::jsonb)
