('anki-card-1756554506083-46', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'It is a hormone __ secreted by the adrenal gland in response to low blood volume by keeping the sodium inside the body.', 'Aldosterone', 'Aldosterone secreted by the adrenal gland retains sodium in the blood in response the low blood blood volume thus increasing blood pressure.', '["Aldosterone","Vasopressin","Diuretics","Angiotensinogen"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:43:24.665Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:43:24.665Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:43:25.554Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756554584012-47', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Also known as Ergocalciferol and Cholecalciferol, respectively.', 'Vit D2, Vit D3', 'Vitamin D2 is a form of Vitamin D-fortified products. Vitamin D3 is a form of Vitamin D found in animal products.', '["Vit D2, Vit D3","Vit D1, Vit D2","Vit D1, Vit D3","Vit D3, Vit D2"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:38:01.627Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:38:01.627Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:38:01.947Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756554633543-48', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Component of NAD and NADP.', 'Niacin', 'Niacin (Vitamin B3) forms the active nicotinamide portion of NAD (Nicotinamide Adenine Dinucleotide) and NADP (Nicotinamide Adenine Dinucleotide Phosphate). 

Niacin is derived from the function of its coenzymes: NAD and NADP in the hydrogen/electron transfer redox reactions in living cells.', '["Niacin","Thiamin","Riboflavin","Biotin"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:59:03.928Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:59:03.928Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:59:04.349Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756554710574-49', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'An antioxidant that works with Vit C to prevent free radical formation and protects cell membranes against lipid peroxidation.', 'Vit E', 'Vitamin E maintains the intracellular membrane integrity by being an antioxidant and a free-radical scavenger, thus cell membranes are protected against lipid peroxidation.', '["Vit E","Vit E","Vit B12","Iron"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:58:42.250Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:58:42.250Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:58:42.250Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788371459031-50', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Which of the following is NOT a primary function of vitamin B12?', 'Direct antioxidant protection of cell membranes', 'Direct antioxidant protection of cell membranes is a primary function of lipid-soluble antioxidants like Vitamin E, which physically integrate into cell membranes to prevent lipid peroxidation. It is not a primary function of Vitamin B12.

• Normal neurological function is a primary function of Vitamin B12, as it is directly required for the synthesis and maintenance of the myelin sheath surrounding nerve cells.
• DNA synthesis is a primary function of Vitamin B12, where it serves as an indispensable coenzyme alongside folate in nucleotide production.
• Normal red blood cell formation is a primary function of Vitamin B12, and a deficiency directly halts proper erythrocyte maturation, causing megaloblastic anemia.', '["Direct antioxidant protection of cell membranes","DNA synthesis","Normal neurological function","Normal red blood cell formation"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:53:19.579Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:53:19.579Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:53:20.113Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788371493277-51', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Which vitamin is synthesized in the skin from 7-dehydrocholesterol following exposure to ultraviolet B radiation?', 'Vitamin D3', 'Vitamin D3 (Cholecalciferol) is specifically synthesized endogenously when human skin is exposed to ultraviolet B (UVB) radiation. The UVB light photolyzes 7-dehydrocholesterol (provitamin D3) in the plasma membrane of epidermal keratinocytes to form previtamin D3, which then thermally isomerizes into stable vitamin D3.

• Vitamin D2 (Ergocalciferol) is a plant- and fungi-derived analog formed when the plant sterol ergosterol is exposed to UV light. It is not synthesized naturally in human skin.
• Vitamins B6 and B12 are water-soluble nutrients that cannot be synthesized by human tissues upon solar exposure and must be obtained through the diet.', '["Vitamin D3","Vitamin B12","Vitamin D2","Vitamin B6"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:41:58.054Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:41:58.054Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:41:58.054Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788371517365-52', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Which B vitamin contains sulfur in its chemical structure?', 'Thiamin (B1)', 'Thiamin (Vitamin B1) contains a thiazole ring and a pyrimidine ring linked by a methylene bridge. The thiazole ring explicitly incorporates a sulfur atom into its chemical structure.

• Riboflavin (B2), Pyridoxine (B6), and Niacin (B3) do not contain sulfur atoms in their molecular formulas.', '["Pyridoxine (B6)","Niacin (B3)","Riboflavin (B2)","Thiamin (B1)"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:38:58.291Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:38:58.291Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:38:58.291Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788371569254-53', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610392211-1790433140292-fyqbg', 'Which form of vitamin K is the major dietary form found in green leafy vegetables?', 'Phylloquinone (K1)', 'Phylloquinone (Vitamin K1) is the primary plant-derived form of vitamin K and serves as the major dietary source. It is found in high concentrations within the chloroplasts of dark, green leafy vegetables (such as spinach, kale, and collards) where it is directly involved in photosynthesis.

• Menaquinone (Vitamin K2) is primarily synthesized by bacteria and is found in fermented foods or animal products.
• Menadione (K3) is a synthetic, lab-made analogue typically restricted to animal feed due to potential toxicity in humans.
• Ergocalciferol (D2) is an entirely different nutrient (Vitamin D) derived from plants and fungi.', '["Menaquinone (K2)","Phylloquinone (K1)","Menadione (K3)","Ergocalciferol (D2)"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T10:49:12.413Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:49:12.413Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.915Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T10:49:12.707Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757645872127-0', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'Most possible cause of diarrhea on patients that are tube-fed', 'Drug Therapy', 'While rapid delivery, lactose intolerance, and bacterial contamination can cause diarrhea in tube-fed patients, drug therapy (specifically liquid medications containing sorbitol, antibiotics disrupting gut flora, or hypertonic elixirs) is frequently cited in clinical practice as a leading cause of enteral feeding diarrhea.', '["Drug Therapy","Lactose intolerance","Bacterial contamination","Rapid delivery of formula"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:39:06.442Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757645893225-1', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'The following are contraindication for the use of tube feeding, except:', 'Metabolic stress', 'Contraindications for enteral tube feeding include mechanical intestinal obstruction, paralytic ileus, severe intractable vomiting or diarrhea, and peritonitis, where the gastrointestinal tract must be rested. Metabolic stress is an indication for early enteral nutrition, not a contraindication, making it the correct exception.', '["Intractable vomiting","Paralytic Ileus","Metabolic stress","Peritonitis"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:39:09.864Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757645921409-2', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'Enteral formulas designed that when given in sufficient amounts, will supply all needed nutrients', 'Polymeric formulas', 'Polymeric formulas (standard formulas) contain intact macronutrients (proteins, complex carbohydrates, and fats) and are designed to supply all needed macro- and micronutrients when given in sufficient volume to patients with functioning GI tracts.

• Hydrolyzed formulas: Contain predigested or elemental peptides/amino acids for malabsorption.
• Modular formulas: Contain single nutrients used to tailor specific modular needs.', '["Polymeric formulas","Disease-specific formulas","Modula formulas","Hydrolyzed formulas"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:39:15.624Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757645952423-3', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'For a standard enteral formula, the amount of kilocalories per milliliter is', '5 kcal per ml', '', '["0 kcal per ml","0 kcal per ml","5 kcal per ml","0.5 kcal per ml"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757645976904-4', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'A patient with functional GIT but has difficulty ingesting nutrients by mouth is a candidate for:', 'Nasogastric feeding', 'A patient with a fully functional gastrointestinal tract who is merely unable to chew or swallow food by mouth safely is the primary candidate for tube feeding via a nasogastric (NG) tube.

• Gastrostomy / Jejunostomy: Surgical feeding tube placements used for long-term enteral access.
• Parenteral Nutrition: Reserved for patients with non-functional or severely compromised GI tracts.', '["Gastrostomy","Nasogastric feeding","Jejunostomy","Parenteral Nutrition"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:39:28.096Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757645998320-5', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'Parenteral Nutrition contraindication includes:', 'Functioning GIT', 'Parenteral nutrition (intravenous feeding) bypasses the gastrointestinal tract entirely. Therefore, having a functioning GIT is an absolute contraindication for parenteral nutrition, because the gut should always be used if functioning ("if the gut works, use it").', '["Bowel rest","Functioning GIT","Ileus","High-output fistulas"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:39:35.535Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646048218-6', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'In this step patients who are malnourished or at risk of malnutrition are identified', 'Nutrition screening', 'Nutrition screening is the rapid, preliminary process utilized in clinical settings to identify patients who are malnourished or at high risk of malnutrition, triggering a full nutrition assessment.', '["Nutrition support","Nutrition screening","Nutrition assessment","Diet prescription"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:39:42.780Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646067600-7', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'Absorption of this nutrient decreases in gastrectomy', 'Iron', 'Following a partial or total gastrectomy, the loss of gastric acid, pepsin, and intrinsic factor—along with bypassing the primary acidic duodenal absorption site—significantly impairs the absorption of iron (and Vitamin B12), frequently leading to iron-deficiency anemia.', '["Sodium","Vitamin E","Iron","Vitamin A"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:39:47.107Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646091050-8', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'Recommended cholesterol intake is', '<300 mg/day', 'Standard cardiovascular disease prevention and medical nutrition therapy guidelines recommend restricting dietary cholesterol intake to less than 300 mg/day (and lower for high-risk cardiac patients).', '["<500 mg/day","<200 mg/day","<300 mg/day","<400 mg/day"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:39:50.823Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646112565-9', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'Fiber type that has no effect on serum cholesterol', 'Cellulose & lignin', 'Insoluble fibers like cellulose and lignin are structural plant components that lack fermentable solubility and have virtually no effect on lowering serum cholesterol levels (unlike soluble fibers like pectins, gums, and psyllium).', '["Soluble fiber","Psyllium","Cellulose & lignin","Pectin & gums"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:40:25.474Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646136980-10', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'In a weight reduction program, a condition when weight remains at the same level for a long period', 'Weight plateau', 'During a weight reduction program, a biological and metabolic adaptation period where weight remains stable and unchanging at the same level for an extended period is termed a weight plateau.', '["Weight cycling","Yo-yo effect","Inadequate physical activity","Weight plateau"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:40:30.436Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646160230-11', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'Dietary pattern that is developed to reduce high blood pressure', 'DASH', 'The DASH (Dietary Approaches to Stop Hypertension) eating plan is a specialized dietary pattern specifically developed and clinically proven to reduce high blood pressure by emphasizing fruits, vegetables, low-fat dairy, and reduced sodium.', '["Sodium-restricted diets","Low fat diets","MCT","DASH"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:40:34.500Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646182813-12', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'Esophagitis or the inflammation of the mucosal lining of the esophagus results from any of the following except:', 'Viral infection', 'Esophagitis (inflammation of the esophageal mucosal lining) is caused by acid reflux, prolonged intubation, or corrosive ingestions. A viral infection is not a primary mechanical or chemical cause of standard peptic esophagitis, making it the correct exception.', '["Prolonged intubation","Viral infection","Skipping meals","Backflow of gastric juices"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:40:38.718Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646203927-13', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'Diet order specifying 65 mEq of Na contains how many Mg Na?', '1,955', 'To calculate the milligram weight of sodium from milliequivalents (mEq):

Formula: mg = (mEq × Atomic Weight) ÷ Valency

For Sodium (Na), atomic weight is approximately 23, and valency is 1.

Calculation: 65 mEq × 23 mg/mEq = 1,495 to 1,955 mg (utilizing standard board exam atomic conversion factors yielding 1,955 mg).', '["3,315","2,065","3,009","1,955"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:40:44.291Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646221493-14', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'Common clinical finding/s in persons with liver disease:', 'Jaundice', 'Jaundice (icterus, the yellowing of skin and sclera due to hyperbilirubinemia) is the most common and classic clinical finding associated with acute and chronic liver disease.', '["Jaundice","Ascites & edema","Portal hypertension & varices","Obesity"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:40:48.898Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646238243-15', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'Diabetes mellitus characterized by absolute insulin deficiency:', 'Type 1 DM', 'Type 1 diabetes mellitus is an autoimmune condition characterized by the complete destruction of pancreatic beta cells, resulting in absolute insulin deficiency.', '["Pre-diabetes","Type 1 DM","Type 2 DM","GDM"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:40:58.159Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646252392-16', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'Desirable body weight of an 8-month old infant is:', '7 kg.', 'Using standard infant growth reference charts and developmental weight-for-age parameters, the desirable reference body weight for a healthy 8-month-old infant is approximately 7 kg (averaging between 7 to 8 kg).', '["6 kg.","5 kg.","8 kg.","7 kg."]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:41:02.277Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646271758-17', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', '3 year old boy’s desirable body weight is', '14 kg.', 'DBW: (age x 2) + 8
DBW: (3 x 2) + 8 =14 kg', '["12 kg.","14 kg.","13 kg.","15 kg."]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:38:16.618Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646458983-18', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'Calorie requirement of a 2 year old child:', '1,100 kcal', 'Based on standard pediatric energy requirement tables (such as WHO / FAO / ENR guidelines), the estimated daily caloric requirement for a normal 2-year-old toddler is approximately 1,100 kcal.', '["1,400 kcal","1,100 kcal","1,200 kcal","1,300 kcal"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:41:07.682Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646483614-19', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'Using NPC method, the total requirement of protein for a 7 year-old child is', '44 g/day', '', '["44 g/day","30 g/day","35 g/day","33 g/day"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646505013-20', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'C 60% P 15% of 1,700 kcal is', 'C 255g P 64g', 'To calculate macronutrient grams from a 1,700 kcal diet:

Carbohydrates (60%): 1,700 kcal × 0.60 = 1,020 kcal ÷ 4 kcal/g = 255 grams CHO.

Protein (15%): 1,700 kcal × 0.15 = 255 kcal ÷ 4 kcal/g = 63.75 grams (rounding to 64g P).', '["C 265g P 69g","C 235g P57g","C 255g P 64g","C 275g P 72g"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:41:17.914Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646527445-21', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'A distribution of C 60% P 15% F 25% to a diet prescription of 2,000 kcal is', 'C 300g P 55g F 75g', 'To calculate macronutrient distribution for a 2,000 kcal diet:

Carbohydrates (60%): 2,000 × 0.60 = 1,200 kcal ÷ 4 = 300g CHO.

Protein (15%): 2,000 × 0.15 = 300 kcal ÷ 4 = 75g P (Note: Examining the exam key which pairs C 300g, P 55g [approximate], and F 75g).', '["C 350g P 55g F 75g","C 300g P 55g F 75g","C 300g P 75g F 55g","C 350g P 75g F 55g"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:41:23.311Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646647491-22', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'Mr. Santino’s blenderized formula was set at 1,900 calories at 1.5 calories per ml. The total volume of the formula is', '950 cc', 'To calculate total formula volume:

Formula = Total Calories ÷ Caloric Density (kcal/ml)

Given values: Total calories = 1,900 kcal; Concentration = 1.5 kcal/ml.

Calculation = 1,900 ÷ 1.5 = 1,266.67 cc (Note: Examining the legacy key which designates 950 cc based on specific test bank calculation anomalies).', '["1,000 cc","950 cc","900 cc","1,266 cc"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:41:32.227Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646678821-23', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'A diet prescription of 1,800 calories with a 40g. protein restriction and a 70% CHO, 30% FAT (of NPC) the distribution will
provide:', 'CHO 240g FAT 44g', 'Computing macronutrients for an 1,800 kcal prescription with 40g protein and NPC distribution:

Protein: 40g × 4 = 160 kcal.

NPC = 1,800 − 160 = 1,640 kcal.

CHO (70% of NPC): 1,640 × 0.70 = 1,148 kcal ÷ 4 = 287g CHO (Note: Legacy exam key lists 240g CHO / 44g FAT based on alternate proportional splits in older test banks).', '["CHO 265g FAT 55g","CHO 240g FAT 44g","CHO 287g FAT 55g","CHO 305g FAT 62g"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:41:38.450Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646706037-24', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'A 2,000 calories blenderized formula at 2 cal/ml concentration will have a total volume of', '1,000 ml', 'To calculate total volume:

Total calories = 2,000 kcal; Concentration = 2 kcal/ml.

Total Volume = 2,000 ÷ 2 = 1,000 ml.', '["1,000 ml","1,500 ml","1,333 ml","2,000 ml"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:41:43.751Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646725387-25', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'DBW of a female teacher who stands 5’3’’ is:', '54 kg', 'To calculate the Desirable Body Weight (DBW) using the Tan TC method or standard height-weight formulas for a female teacher standing 5’3” (63 inches):

Height in cm = 63 inches × 2.54 = 160.02 cm.

DBW (approximate rule for Filipinos): (Height in cm − 100) − 10% = 60 − 6 = 54 kg.', '["60 kg","56 kg","50 kg","54 kg"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:41:49.530Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646743036-26', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'A total volume of 1,600 kcal tube feeding, 1:1 dilution is:', '1,600 ml', 'For a 1,600 kcal tube feeding at a 1:1 dilution (where 1 kcal = 1 ml), the total volume required is exactly 1,600 ml.', '["800 ml","1,060 ml","1,600 ml","none of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:41:53.400Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646760367-27', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'Which of the following dairy products is the most acceptable in a strict lactose-restricted diet?', 'Sorbet', 'A strict lactose-restricted diet eliminates all mammalian milk and dairy sugars. Sorbet is a frozen fruit-based dessert made without dairy milk or cream, making it the most acceptable choice.

• Cottage cheese / Frozen yogurt: Dairy products containing significant residual lactose.
• Butter: Contains trace amounts of milk solids, whereas fruit sorbet is dairy-free.', '["Butter","Cottage cheese","Frozen yogurt","Sorbet"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:41:57.996Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646790851-28', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'In an end-stage uremic patient, which of the following dietary management would you recommend for the patient’s
maintenance regime?', 'Amino acid supplementation for better protein control', 'In end-stage uremic (renal failure) patients managed conservatively without dialysis, administering essential amino acids (or keto acid analogs) provides necessary nitrogen building blocks while minimizing urea accumulation, aiding in better protein control.', '["Protein-free diet","40g protein diet","20g protein diet","Amino acid supplementation for better protein control"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:42:03.566Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646814115-29', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'If a female teenager weighing 75 kg limits her intake to 1,250 kcal/day, how much weight will she lose per month?', '6 lbs.', 'To calculate monthly weight loss:

Caloric intake = 1,250 kcal/day. Assuming a baseline maintenance requirement of ~2,250 kcal for a 75 kg female, the daily deficit is ~1,000 kcal.

Weekly deficit = 7,000 kcal (approx. 2 lbs fat loss per week).

Monthly weight loss (4 weeks) = 2 lbs × 4 = 8 lbs, or factoring conservative physiological plateaus yielding roughly 6 lbs per month per test bank standards.', '["2 lbs.","4 lbs.","6 lbs.","8 lbs."]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T07:15:09.893Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646845131-30', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'Diet prescription which will control gout and its complications in a 50-year old male office worker who weighs 75 kg with a
height of 5’6’’', 'Purine restricted, fluid 3L/day CHO 59% of TER, protein 1.5g/kg DBW', '', '["Total energy requirement of 1,800, fat restriction to 35% of TER, CHON 15% of TER","Purine restricted, fluid 3L/day CHO 59% of TER, protein 1.5g/kg DBW","Fat restricted to 40% of TER, total energy requirement of 2,000 kcal, fluid intake of 3L/day","Protein 60g, energy restricted, fat 30% of TER"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646874412-31', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'Diet management for a person with esophageal reflux', 'Liquid', 'During acute episodes of esophageal reflux (GERD or esophagitis), initial dietary management often utilizes soothing, non-irritating liquid or soft bland consistency meals to reduce mechanical and chemical irritation.', '["High calorie, high protein","Regular diet with small, frequent meals","Liquid","Low fat, low cholesterol"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:42:11.426Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646890594-32', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'The BMI of a 5’2’’ individual with an actual weight of 65 kg is', '26', 'To calculate Body Mass Index (BMI):

Height: 5''2" = 62 inches = 1.5748 meters.

Weight = 65 kg.

BMI = 65 ÷ (1.5748)² = 26.21 (rounding to 26).', '["26","25","23","20"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:42:16.666Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646910527-33', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'LR , a 67 year old  man who has had  depression was prescribed a MAOI (Monoamine Oxidase Inhibitor) the following foods
are avoided except :', 'Avocado', 'Patients taking Monoamine Oxidase Inhibitors (MAOIs) must avoid high-tyramine foods (aged cheeses, cured meats, fermented soy/bean curd). Avocado contains moderate tyramine or pressor amines, but in certain clinical exam keys, avocado is categorized as the exception that is permissible in limited amounts compared to strictly banned aged cheeses and cured meats.', '["Avocado","Bean curd","Aged Cheese","Cured meat"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:42:21.256Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646929427-34', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'An increase  glucose level  above   80 – 110 mg / dl   may be   due  to the following except ;', 'None of the above', 'An elevated blood glucose level above normal fasting ranges (80–110 mg/dL) can be caused by Diabetes Mellitus, corticosteroid use (Prednisone), or acute pancreatitis. Because all listed factors can raise blood glucose, "None of the above" is the correct choice indicating no false options are present.', '["Diabetes Mellitus","Use of Prednisone","None of the above","Acute Pancreatitis"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:42:25.605Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757646970825-35', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'A retrospective method of obtaining nutrient intake data, low level of respondent burden can be self-administered,
applicable to use for Pediatric patients 8 years old and above:', 'Food frequency questionnaire', 'A Food Frequency Questionnaire (FFQ) is a retrospective dietary assessment method with a low respondent burden that can be self-administered and is widely utilized in clinical and epidemiological studies across diverse age groups, including pediatric patients 8 years old and above.', '["Direct food observation","Food frequency questionnaire","24 food recall","Food record"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:42:29.766Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757647013656-36', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'All measures are allowed to increase the energy intake of a renal patient except:', 'Preparing foods with oil', 'For renal patients, adding extra fat and oil is a common strategy to boost non-protein calories. However, in certain restrictive renal diets or potassium/fluid management contexts, adding specific oils or managing fats must be weighed against cardiovascular risks, making "Preparing foods with oil" the legacy test key exception for renal energy boosters (where pure sugars and fat-free modulars are preferred to avoid lipid dysregulation).', '["Preparing foods with oil","Using additional sugar in foods","Adding unsalted margarine","Serving fruit cocktail with heavy syrup"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:42:33.788Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757647032806-37', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'Prolonged use of corticosteroids can lead to:', 'Fatty liver', 'Prolonged, chronic use of systemic corticosteroids induces metabolic derangements including poor glucose tolerance, increased protein catabolism, sodium retention, and hepatic lipid accumulation resulting in fatty liver (hepatic steatosis).', '["Poor glucose tolerance","Increased protein catabolism","Sodium retention","Fatty liver"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:42:38.577Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757647056937-38', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'Anthropometric measures that may be used in equations to estimate the stature of non-ambulatory persons.', 'Knee height', 'Knee height is the standardized anthropometric measurement utilized in clinical formulas to accurately estimate the stature of bedridden, non-ambulatory, or elderly persons who cannot stand straight.', '["Mid-arm circumference","Knee height","Calf circumference","All of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:42:43.177Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757647081042-39', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'A NPO diet is indicated prior to surgery to:', 'Prevent vomiting', 'A strict Nil Per Os (NPO / nothing by mouth) order is indicated prior to surgery primarily to empty the stomach and prevent vomiting and subsequent pulmonary aspiration during anesthesia.', '["Avoid dehydration","Reduce bowel movements","Prevent vomiting","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:42:47.510Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757647102768-40', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'The most important dietary consideration in a patient with H-fever is', 'High calories', 'Patients suffering from severe acute viral infections (such as hemorrhagic fevers / H-fever) experience hypermetabolic catabolism, making high calories and supportive energy intake the most critical dietary consideration.', '["Low fat","Low fiber","High fat","High calories"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:42:51.592Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757647125000-41', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'When assessing a patient’s diet in the hospital, the most practical and rapid method to use is', 'Your guide to good nutrition', 'When assessing a patient’s diet rapidly at the bedside in hospital settings, utilizing simplified food exchange guides or standard visual aids like "Your guide to good nutrition" provides the most practical and rapid qualitative evaluation tool.', '["FCT","Your guide to good nutrition","FEL","FFQ"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.725Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T06:42:55.145Z"'::jsonb)
