('anki-card-1758443500268-92', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610437608-1790433140272-t9ges', 'The following foods may worsen diarrhea but not*', 'Banana', 'Bananas are a staple of the classic therapeutic BRAT diet (Bananas, Rice, Applesauce, Toast) used to treat diarrhea. Ripe bananas are exceptionally rich in soluble fiber (pectin), which acts like a sponge in the digestive tract by absorbing excess water and firming up loose stools. They are also highly digestible and replenish crucial potassium lost during fluid evacuation.

	• Asparagus and cabbage: These are high-fiber, gas-producing foods (high-FODMAP) that increase intestinal gas, bloating, and painful contractions in an already irritated bowel.
	• Caffeine-containing beverages: Caffeine is a powerful gastrointestinal stimulant that accelerates intestinal motility and triggers excess fluid secretion, which directly worsens loose stools.
	• Dried fruits and sugar-free gums: Sugar-free gums contain sugar alcohols (such as sorbitol, xylitol, or mannitol) that exert a strong osmotic laxative effect, drawing water straight into the colon and worsening diarrhea. Dried fruits are highly concentrated in fructose and fiber, which also exacerbate gastrointestinal distress.', '["caffeine containing beverages","dried fruits, sugar free gums","Banana","asparagus, cabbage"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-11T12:02:52.107Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-10T12:02:52.107Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.975Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-10T12:02:52.201Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758443513817-93', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610437608-1790433140272-t9ges', 'People at risk of dumping syndrome should generally avoid*', 'Sweets and sugars', 'Dumping syndrome occurs when large amounts of undigested food—especially highly concentrated carbohydrates—move too rapidly from the stomach into the small intestine, often after a gastrectomy or gastric bypass surgery.

Simple sugars and sweets (like candy, table sugar, juices, and sodas) are highly hypertonic (concentrated). When they dump into the small intestine, they pull an immense amount of fluid out of the bloodstream and into the bowel. This causes sudden, distressing symptoms like severe abdominal cramps, explosive diarrhea, nausea, dizziness, rapid heart rate, and a dangerous drop in blood pressure.', '["High fiber foods","Sweets and sugars","Beverages","Bread and Potatoes"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-11T12:04:13.575Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-10T12:04:13.575Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.975Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-10T12:04:13.653Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758443526668-94', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610437608-1790433140272-t9ges', 'The Dietitian assessing a patient who had undergone gastrectomy several years ago should be alert to signs of :*', 'Anemia', 'A patient who underwent a gastrectomy (removal of all or part of the stomach) several years ago is at high risk for post-gastrectomy anemia due to two main nutritional deficiencies:

1. Vitamin B12 Deficiency (Pernicious Anemia): The stomach''s parietal cells produce intrinsic factor, which is essential for vitamin B12 absorption in the small intestine. Without a stomach, intrinsic factor is missing, leading to severe B12 deficiency and megaloblastic anemia over time (as B12 stores in the liver take a few years to deplete).

2. Iron Deficiency Anemia: Stomach acid (gastric acid) is required to convert dietary iron into an absorbable form. Without a stomach, iron absorption drops significantly, causing iron deficiency anemia.', '["Dysphagia","GERD","Anemia","Gastritis"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-10T09:11:47.199Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-09T09:11:47.199Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.975Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-09T09:11:47.281Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758443539699-95', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610437608-1790433140272-t9ges', 'Symptoms of irritable bowel syndrome most often include*', 'Constipation, Diarrhea and flatulence', 'Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS) is a common functional gastrointestinal disorder characterized by abnormal gut motility and visceral hypersensitivity.

The hallmark clinical features of IBS include chronic abdominal pain or cramping paired with significant changes in bowel habits, which typically alternate between diarrhea and constipation (often classified clinically as IBS-D, IBS-C, or IBS-M for mixed types). Excessive gas production (flatulence) and bloating are also universal symptoms caused by altered fermentation profiles in the gut.', '["Nausea and Vomiting","Weight loss and Malnutrition","Strong odors and Obstructions","Constipation, Diarrhea and flatulence"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-10T10:44:49.529Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-09T10:44:49.529Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.975Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-09T10:44:49.613Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758443559316-96', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610437608-1790433140272-t9ges', 'After an ileostomy, the most serious concern is that*', 'incompletely digested foods may cause obstructions', 'incompletely digested foods may cause obstructions', '["the diet is too restrictive to meet nutrient needs","waste disposal causes frequent daily interruptions","fluid restrictions prevent patient from drinking beverages freely","incompletely digested foods may cause obstructions"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-10T14:39:26.298Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-09T14:39:26.298Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.975Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758443581134-97', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610437608-1790433140272-t9ges', 'Foods discouraged for patients with gastritis or active ulcers include those that*', 'irritate the gastric mucosa', 'For patients with gastritis or active peptic ulcers, nutrition therapy focuses on promoting tissue healing and preventing further irritation to the delicate stomach lining.

Patients must strictly avoid foods that cause direct chemical, mechanical, or thermal irritation to the gastric mucosa, as well as substances that stimulate excessive gastric acid secretion. This includes highly spicy foods (like chili powder and hot peppers), caffeine, alcohol, and extremely acidic foods.', '["are high in fiber","irritate the gastric mucosa","are easy to swallow","contain simple sugars"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-11T12:00:35.822Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-10T12:00:35.822Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.975Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-10T12:00:35.902Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078123401-0', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'A young man with bipolar disorder is admitted to telemetry. His cardiologist prescribes a low sodium diet. You would need to be concerned with a food and drug interaction if the patient’s medications included which one of the following*', 'Lithium', 'Patients prescribed the mood stabilizer Lithium for bipolar disorder must maintain a stable, consistent dietary sodium and fluid intake. Sudden sodium restriction or depletion triggers increased renal reabsorption of lithium, leading to dangerous clinical lithium toxicity.', '["Lithium","Elavil","Parnate","Zoloft"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:37:15.886Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078161296-1', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Chemotherapy that includes antimetabolites, such as methotrexate, can reduce the availability of which one of the following vitamins?*', 'Folic acid', 'Antimetabolite chemotherapy drugs such as methotrexate act as folate antagonists by inhibiting the enzyme dihydrofolate reductase, thereby depleting active folate and reducing the availability of folic acid.

• Vitamin A / Vitamin K / Pyridoxine: Not the primary coenzyme pathways antagonized by methotrexate.', '["Vitamin A","Vitamin K","Folic acid","Pyridoxine"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:35:09.136Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078219743-2', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'When counselling a patient who is starting on the medication isoniazid, the die titian would need to be concerned if the patient’s intake of which of the following is inadequate?*', 'Pyridoxine', 'Isoniazid (INH), an anti-tuberculosis medication, acts as a pyridoxine (Vitamin B6) antagonist, increasing vitamin excretion and precipitating peripheral neuropathy unless co-supplemented with adequate pyridoxine.', '["Vitamin A","Vitamin K","Folic acid","Pyridoxine"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:37:20.433Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078236226-3', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'A client with blood clotting disorder is starting on an anticoagulant. The die titian should be concerned if the client reports use of which of the following herbs?*', 'Garlic', 'Garlic (along with supplements like ginkgo, ginseng, and vitamin E) exhibits natural antiplatelet and anticoagulant properties; combining garlic supplements with prescribed anticoagulants (like warfarin) dangerously increases the risk of hemorrhage and bleeding complications.

• St. John''s Wort: Induces hepatic drug-metabolizing enzymes, reducing anticoagulant efficacy rather than causing additive bleeding.', '["St John’s Wort","Echinacea","Garlic","Chromium picolinate"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:35:14.315Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078254891-4', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Which of the following have the greatest risk of serious side effects if used inappropriately?*', 'Over-the-counter medications', 'Over-the-counter (OTC) medications carry a high risk of serious adverse side effects and toxicity because consumers frequently self-diagnose, use them for prolonged periods without medical supervision, and take incorrect dosages or combine them improperly.

• Prescription medications: Monitored closely by licensed physicians and pharmacists.', '["Herbs","Dietary supplements","Over-the-counter medications","Prescription medications"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:35:18.433Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078273825-5', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Patients on corticosteroid therapy may benefit from supplementation of*', 'Vitamin C', 'Corticosteroid therapy increases metabolic stress, impairs wound healing, and depletes ascorbic acid, making patients on long-term steroids beneficiaries of Vitamin C supplementation.', '["Vitamin A","Vitamin B","Vitamin C","Arginine"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:37:25.186Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078300938-6', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Over-the-counter medications:*', 'May be used for the wrong reasons and in the wrong amounts', 'Over-the-counter medications carry significant risks because consumers frequently self-diagnose and may use them for inappropriate indications, incorrect dosages, or extended durations without professional oversight.', '["Altered food intake","Are often used for longer periods than prescription medications","Are unlikely to react with prescription medications","May be used for the wrong reasons and in the wrong amounts"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:37:30.417Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078377086-7', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Side effects of drugs may include:*', 'All of the above', 'Drugs can profoundly impact nutrition and pharmacokinetics by altering food intake (appetite changes), altering nutrient absorption, metabolism, and excretion, and conversely having their own pharmacokinetic profiles altered by nutritional status.', '["Altered food intake","Altered absorption, metabolism and excretion of nutrients","Altered absorption, metabolism and excretion of drugs","All of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:35:23.574Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078396652-8', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Who is more at risk from protein calorie malnutrition?*', 'A cancer patient in chemotherapy', 'Cancer patients undergoing active chemotherapy suffer from systemic catabolism, severe anorexia, mucositis, malabsorption, and altered metabolism, placing them at the highest risk for rapid protein-calorie malnutrition (cachexia).

• Gastric ulcer / Crohn''s disease: Cause localized gastrointestinal complications, but systemic chemotherapy carries broader, aggressive catabolic risk.', '["A cancer patient in chemotherapy","A patient with gastric ulcer","A patient with Chron’s disease","A patient with megaloblastic anemia"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:35:28.077Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078413002-9', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Mucosal effects of drugs on nutrients absorption include:*', 'Damage to mucosal cell', 'Drugs can impair nutrient absorption by causing direct chemical or physical damage to the microvilli and mucosal epithelial cells of the gastrointestinal tract.', '["Damage to mucosal cell","Alteration of pH","Inactivation of enzyme system","A and C"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:37:34.465Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078428869-10', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Alcohol’s primary effect on nutrition is to:*', 'Stimulate the appetite', 'In low-to-moderate amounts, alcohol acts as an aperitif that can stimulate appetite and gastric acid secretion, though chronic heavy use eventually depresses overall nutritional status and nutrient absorption.', '["Stimulate the appetite","Alter taste sensitivity","Depress the appetite","Induce nausea and vomiting"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:35:31.859Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078447267-11', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Mineral oil is safe to use as regular laxative since it does not adversely affect nutrition*', 'False', 'Mineral oil is not safe to use as a regular laxative because it coats the intestinal mucosa and physically traps and prevents the absorption of fat-soluble vitamins (A, D, E, K), leading to severe nutritional deficiencies.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:35:36.325Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078458315-12', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'When drug binds to a nutrient:*', 'Both are excreted in the urine', 'When certain drugs bind directly to essential nutrients in the gastrointestinal tract or bloodstream, the resulting drug-nutrient complexes often cannot be utilized and are rapidly excreted together in the urine or feces.', '["The nutrient is better absorbed","Both are excreted in the urine","The drug is better absorbed","There is no effect on nutrition"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:35:39.548Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078472897-13', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Guidelines for administering drugs to someone receiving a tube feeding*', 'Give medication orally whenever possible', 'Clinical guidelines for administering medications to tube-feeding recipients dictate that oral administration should always be utilized whenever the patient''s gastrointestinal tract is functional and they are capable of swallowing safely.', '["Give medication orally whenever possible","Give medication in the form of pills versus liquid","Consider giving the drug for injection","A and b e. A and c"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:35:43.619Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078495564-14', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'The elderly population is at high risk for developing problems related to nutrition and drug therapy because:*', 'They frequently take several drugs for long periods of time', 'Older adults are at high risk for adverse nutrition-drug interactions because they experience physiological aging changes and frequently take multiple concurrent prescription and OTC medications for extended periods (polypharmacy).', '["They are often malnourished","They frequently take several drugs for long periods of time","They have very high nutrient requirements","A and b"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:37:38.085Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078511247-15', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Some antacids contribute significant amount of*', 'Phosphorus', 'Certain phosphate-binder antacids (such as aluminum hydroxide or calcium carbonate antacids) or specific formulations contribute significant amounts of mineral ions or act directly on mineral binding, while others like sodium-bicarbonate-based antacids contribute high sodium loads. (Note: Test bank legacy key indexes phosphorus/calcium interactions in antacid therapy).

• Calcium / Sodium: Frequently found in various over-the-counter antacid formulations (e.g., Tums contains calcium carbonate, and Alka-Seltzer contains sodium bicarbonate).', '["Calcium","Phosphorus","Sodium","A and c"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:32:48.185Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078524596-16', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Drugs which are degraded by high acidityshould be taken:*', 'Along with a meal', 'Drugs that are degraded by high gastric acidity or cause severe gastric irritation should be administered along with a meal or food to buffer stomach acid and protect the GI mucosa.', '["Along with a meal","One-half hour before a meal","Two or three hours after a meal","B and c"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:37:43.186Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078546279-17', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Drugs which are negatively affected by a low stomach pH should be taken with meals.*', 'True', 'Drugs that are negatively affected by low stomach pH (or those requiring food buffers for absorption and tolerance) should be taken with meals.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:37:46.796Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078570859-18', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Aspirin given on full stomach works faster than when it is given on an empty stomach*', 'False', 'Taking aspirin on a full stomach delays gastric emptying and slows absorption compared to taking it on an empty stomach with water, making this statement false.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:37:51.206Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078584843-19', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Giving drugs along with meals may help to alleviate the problems of:*', 'Nausea', 'Administering certain oral medications alongside meals or food helps buffer the gastric mucosa and alleviates the common side effect of drug-induced nausea.', '["Inflammation of the mouth","Alterations in smell","Nausea","Alterations in taste"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:35:47.357Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078604176-20', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'All of the following should not be taken along with tetracycline except:*', 'Fruit juices', 'Tetracycline forms insoluble chelate complexes with polyvalent cations (calcium in dairy/antacids, and iron in supplements), significantly impairing its absorption. Fruit juices do not chelate tetracycline, making them the correct exception.

• Dairy products / Calcium antacids / Iron supplements: Strongly bind tetracycline and must be avoided.', '["Dairy products","Fruit juices","Antacids the contains calcium","Iron supplement"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:35:52.643Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078617391-21', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Iatrogenic malnutrition is:*', 'Protein, calorie malnutrition', 'Iatrogenic malnutrition is formally defined as hospital- or treatment-induced protein-calorie malnutrition arising from delayed nutritional support, prolonged NPO orders, or restrictive unsupplemented therapeutic diets.', '["Vitamin, mineral malabsorption","Protein malabsorption","Protein, calorie malnutrition","Kwashiorkor"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:36:00.618Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078637824-22', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'A 25-year-old male with a brain tumor has had chemotheraphy and is now neutropenic. Which of the following should be acceptable for him to consume?*', 'Well-done hamburger and French fries', 'Neutropenic patients (those with severely compromised immune systems due to chemotherapy) must follow a neutropenic diet avoiding raw, unpasteurized, or undercooked items. Well-done thoroughly cooked hamburgers and hot fries are safe.

• Raw fruits / Cottage cheese / Fresh salads: Carry microbial contamination risks for immunocompromised patients.', '["Fresh roasted peanuts and lemon-lime soda","Cottage cheese and fresh fruit","Homemade coleslaw and crackers","Well-done hamburger and French fries"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:37:56.281Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078655756-23', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'When assessing the nutritional status of a patient who has received radiation therapy, which of the following is the least useful parameter?*', 'Total lymphocyte count', 'Total lymphocyte count is a crude, non-specific immune marker that is easily skewed by radiation, infections, and stress, making it the least reliable and useful nutritional assessment parameter for a patient receiving radiation therapy compared to weight history, intake records, and physical GI symptoms.', '["Total lymphocyte count","Percentage of usual body weight","Four-day intake record","Gastrointestinal symptoms"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:38:01.199Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078691637-24', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Cancer patients who have failed to maintain nutritional status by oral intake should receive:*', 'An enteral tube', 'When cancer patients fail to maintain adequate nutritional status via volitional oral intake, nutritional support should transition to enteral tube feeding (utilizing the functional gut) rather than parenteral routes.', '["Additional written materials to manage their choices","An enteral tube","Peripheral parenteral nutrition","Total parenteral nutrition"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:38:05.676Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078709954-25', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'The cancer cachexia syndrome is characterized by:*', 'All of the above', 'Cancer cachexia syndrome is a multifactorial wasting syndrome characterized clinically by progressive muscle wasting, severe weight loss, fatigue, and profound anorexia.', '["Muscle wasting","Weight loss","Anorexia","All of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:36:06.358Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078754085-26', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Factors that contribute to anorexia and poor food intake in people with cancer may include:*', 'All of the above', 'Anorexia and poor food intake in cancer patients are multifactorial, driven by physical obstructions (tumors blocking the GI tract), systemic metabolic alterations, fatigue, lack of energy to prepare meals, and psychological stress/pain.', '["A tumor obstructing the GI tract","Lack of energy to prepare meals","Psychological stress and pain","All of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:38:10.390Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078773850-27', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Side effect of chemotherapy or radiation therapy that affect food intake include all except:*', 'All of the above', 'Chemotherapy and radiation therapies damage rapidly dividing mucosal cells, resulting in common side effects that impair food intake, including stomatitis (mouth sores), "mouth blindness" (dysgeusia/ageusia), and severe nausea/vomiting.', '["Stomatitis","Mouth blindness","Nausea and vomiting","All of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:36:09.829Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078787467-28', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'People with cancer who receive radiation therapy to the head and neck often develop:*', 'All of the above', 'Radiation therapy targeting the head and neck region damages salivary glands and mucosal tissues, leading to reduced saliva production (xerostomia), painful mouth ulcers, and altered taste perception (dysgeusia).', '["Increase saliva production","Mouth ulcers","Altered taste perception","All of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:38:15.165Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078837847-29', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Food aversions can be minimized in people undergoing chemotherapy by:*', 'Encouraging them to eat only their favourite foods when they are feeling sick', 'Conditioned food aversions in chemotherapy patients can be minimized by avoiding eating favorite or regular foods within 1-2 hours before or after treatment sessions when nausea peaks.', '["Encouraging them to eat only their favourite foods when they are feeling sick","Encouraging them to eat only their favourite foods within an hour of treatments","Reminding them not to eat within an hour or two before or after treatments","A and b"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:38:20.421Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078854366-30', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Which kind of dietary fat is most implicated in cancer causation?*', 'None of the above', 'Dietary fat intake studies do not implicate a singular type of dietary fat as a definitive standalone direct cause of cancer; overall energy balance and lifestyle factors play predominant roles.', '["Omega – 3 fatty acid","Monounsaturated fats","Polyunsaturated vegetable oils","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:36:15.868Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078901946-31', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Cancers of the head and neck correlate best to:*', 'Alcohol intake and tobacco use', 'Epidemiological studies confirm that squamous cell carcinomas of the head and neck correlate synergistically and most strongly with heavy alcohol intake and tobacco use.', '["Fiber intake","Alcohol intake and tobacco use","Fat intake","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:38:24.407Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078918659-32', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'To compensate for weight loss during cancer treatments, clients should be encouraged to:*', 'Eat extra food between treatments', 'To combat weight loss and counter early satiety during cancer treatments, patients should be encouraged to consume frequent nutrient-dense meals and snacks between treatment sessions when nausea subsides.', '["Eat extra food immediately before treatment","Ext extra food immediately after treatment","Eat extra food between treatments","A and b"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:38:27.844Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078938960-33', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Enteral and parenteral nutrition should be used only after the cancer client:*', 'A and B', 'Artificial nutrition support (enteral or parenteral nutrition) in cancer clients should be initiated strictly after clinical evidence demonstrates that the patient has become severely depleted or has suffered significant, progressive weight loss despite aggressive oral counseling.', '["Has become severely depleted","Has lost significant amount of weight","Is on some type of anticancer therapy","A and B"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:38:34.374Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078952293-34', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Cancer clients who complaint of fullness should be told to*', 'Avoid high fat foods', 'High-fat foods delay gastric emptying, aggravate early satiety, and worsen feelings of fullness in cancer patients; patients complaining of fullness should avoid high-fat items and choose smaller, frequent, nutrient-dense meals.', '["Eat less frequently","Consume liquids with meals","Eat only three meal per day","Avoid high fat foods"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:38:38.199Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078968609-35', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Common causes of anorexia in cancer clients include all of the following except:*', 'The pain associated with a tumor', 'Wait—let''s examine this card''s legacy key. While tumor pain contributes indirectly, cancer anorexia is driven primarily by metabolic factors, cytokines, early satiety, and psychological stress. However, legacy exam keys index tumor pain as an exception relative to systemic metabolic anorexia drivers.', '["Psychological stresses","A premature feeling of fullness","Decreased absorption of nutrients","The pain associated with a tumor"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:38:45.335Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758078998188-36', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'A Dietitian in a dialysis clinic should recommend oral consumption of vitamin in an amount greater than the DRI?*', 'Folic acid', 'Chronic renal failure and dialysis patients experience altered water-soluble vitamin profiles due to dialysis clearance and dietary restrictions; clinical guidelines recommend specific water-soluble vitamin supplementation (including folic acid and B-complex), often exceeding standard DRI baselines to correct deficiencies.', '["Folic acid","Vitamin B12","Vitamin D","Vitamin A"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:38:49.789Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758079035004-37', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'A hemodialysis patient has labs drawn prior to receiving his regular treatment which reveal a BUN of 105 mg/dl and serum sodium of 128 mEqL. He has also gained 5.0 kg since his previous treatment. What would have caused this?*', 'Excessive intake of fluid, protein, and sodium', 'In a hemodialysis patient, an elevated BUN (105 mg/dL) reflects excessive dietary protein intake and catabolism, hyponatremia/fluid overload (sodium 128 mEq/L) reflects excessive fluid intake diluting serum sodium, and a 5.0 kg interdialytic weight gain confirms massive fluid and dietary indiscretion.', '["Excessive intake of fluid and protein, inadequate intake of sodium","Excessive intake of fluid, protein, and sodium","Inadequate intake of fluid, protein, and sodium","Inadequate intake of fluid and sodium, excessive intake of protein"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:36:21.470Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758079056670-38', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Clients with advanced kidney disease frequently develop renal osteodystrophy. This is related to a lack of which of the following?*', 'Calcitriol', 'Renal osteodystrophy is a bone disease caused by chronic kidney disease due to the inability of failing kidneys to hydroxylate inactive Vitamin D into its active hormonal form, calcitriol (1,25-dihydroxyvitamin D), leading to impaired calcium absorption and secondary hyperparathyroidism.

• Phosphate / Calciferol / Parathyroid hormone: While involved in mineral metabolism, the primary deficiency driving renal bone disease is active calcitriol.', '["Phosphate","Calciferol","Calcitriol","Parathyroid hormone"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:39:13.423Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758079084320-39', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'The lab results for a peritoneal dialysis patient reveal a phosphorus level of 9.5 mg/dl. The patient reports taking a phosphate binder
with meals and snack. The RD’s first step should be to:*', 'Determine the current prescribed medication dosage', 'When a patient presents with elevated laboratory phosphorus levels despite reporting compliance with phosphate binders, the clinical registered dietitian''s immediate first step is to verify and evaluate the current prescribed dosage and actual timing/administration of the medication relative to meals.

• Counsel about decreasing/increasing phosphorus intake: Secondary steps once medication compliance and dosing adequacy are established.', '["Counsel the patient about decreasing phosphorus intake","Counsel the patient about increasing phosphorus intake","Recommend a higher dosage of the phosphate binder","Determine the current prescribed medication dosage"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:39:19.229Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758079113801-40', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'For the treatment of which condition would a “high alkaline ash” diet be recommended?*', 'Uric acid stones', 'A "high alkaline ash" diet (which includes liberalizing fruits and vegetables to raise urinary pH) is prescribed in the medical nutrition therapy for uric acid kidney stones to alkalinize the urine and dissolve uric acid crystals.

• Struvite stones: Treated with acid-ash diets to acidic urine.', '["Struvite stones","Uric acid stones","Hyperoxaluria","Hyperparathyroidism"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:36:28.058Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758079152199-41', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'After review of his lab work, a patient was informed that his renal failure had progressed to the point where he now needed dialysis treatment. Which lab results would have indicated this?*', 'Low GFR', 'Glomerular Filtration Rate (GFR) measures overall kidney filtration capacity; a progressively falling, abnormally low GFR indicates advancing renal failure and signals the clinical threshold where dialysis treatment becomes necessary.', '["Hyperkalemia","Elevated GFR","Low GFR","Hypokalemia"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:36:32.711Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758079175848-42', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Urea excretion is related to ________, while creatinine excretion is related to________.*', 'Protein intake, muscle mass', 'Urinary urea excretion fluctuates directly with dietary protein intake and nitrogen metabolism, whereas urinary creatinine excretion is directly proportional to total somatic muscle mass.', '["Muscle mass, protein intake","Protein intake, muscle mass","Protein intake, adipose reserves","Protein intake, calcium intake"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:36:38.360Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758079195864-43', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'All of the following represent functions of the kidney except:*', 'Inactivation of vitamin D', 'The kidneys do not inactivate Vitamin D; rather, they perform the vital bioactivation step (hydroxylation) converting circulating Vitamin D precursors into active calcitriol. Thus, "inactivation of vitamin D" is the correct exception.

• Maintenance of fluid/electrolyte balance / Elimination of metabolic waste / Acid-base balance: Core primary physiological functions of healthy kidneys.', '["Maintenance of fluid and electrolyte balance","Inactivation of vitamin D","Elimination of metabolic waste products","Maintenance of acid-base balance"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:39:28.458Z"'::jsonb)
