('anki-card-1758080355958-94', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Products labeled “very low sodium” must contain less than _____ milligrams of sodium per serving*', '35', 'According to FDA food labeling regulations, claims for "very low sodium" require that the food item contains less than 35 milligrams of sodium per standard serving.', '["20","35","50","65"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:42:46.609Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758080370092-95', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'The obese person is at increased risk of cardiovascular disease if the excess fat is concentrated in the:*', 'Abdominal area', 'Upper-body android obesity (visceral fat concentrated in the abdominal area) carries a significantly greater risk of cardiovascular disease, insulin resistance, and metabolic syndrome compared to gynecoid (hip/thigh) fat distribution.', '["Abdominal area","Hips and thighs","Extremities","Buttocks"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:42:51.017Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758080392440-96', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'A high sucrose intake is related to cardiovascular disease because:*', 'Sucrose stimulates triglyceride production by the body', 'High intakes of refined sucrose (fructose moiety) stimulate hepatic lipogenesis and VLDL synthesis, significantly elevating blood triglyceride production and cardiovascular risk.', '["Many cardiac patients have a genetic deficiency of sucrose","A high-sugar diet causes hyperactivity and hypertension","Excess sugar has to be excreted, causing premature aging of the kidney","Sucrose stimulates triglyceride production by the body"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:42:54.920Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758080406640-97', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Which of the following is not always a nutritional goal for a child with renal disease?*', 'Promote normal growth and development', 'Promoting normal growth and development is always a fundamental nutritional and clinical goal for pediatric patients with renal disease, making this statement the correct exception.', '["Promote normal growth and development","Maintain current hydration status","Minimize uremic toxicity","Stimulate patient well-being"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:42:58.357Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758080418589-98', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'The risk of heart disease is reduced in people who have high blood levels of*', 'high-density lipoproteins', 'High-density lipoproteins (HDLs) act as protective scavengers transporting cholesterol away from peripheral tissues back to the liver for excretion ("good cholesterol"), reducing heart disease risk.', '["Triglyceride","very low-density lipoprotein","low-density lipoproteins","high-density lipoproteins"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:43:02.073Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758080433339-99', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Fatty acids with a double bond at one part of the molecule are referred to as*', 'Monounsaturated', 'Fatty acids containing a single carbon-carbon double bond in their molecular structure are classified as monounsaturated fatty acids.', '["Monounsaturated","Hydrogenated","Saturated","essential"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:43:05.833Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758605365848-0', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Incidental additive is*', 'Al residue in the processed food product', 'An incidental (or indirect) additive is a substance that unintentionally migrates into food from packaging, processing equipment, or environmental contact during manufacturing (such as aluminum residue from equipment or cans).

• Hg in canned food / Nitrates and nitrites / Beta-carotene fortified food: Represents environmental/heavy-metal contamination, intentional chemical preservatives, or purposeful nutrient fortification rather than incidental processing residues.', '["Hg in the canned food product","Al residue in the processed food product","Nitrates and nitrites in the processed food product","Beta-carotene fortified food product"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T08:49:49.003Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T08:49:49.003Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:43:50.185Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758605379913-1', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'The more common microorganism that is involved in alcoholic fermentation is*', 'Sacccharomyces cerevisiae', 'Saccharomyces cerevisiae is the most common yeast strain utilized globally in alcoholic fermentation to convert sugars into ethanol and carbon dioxide.

• Acetobacter species: Produce acetic acid (vinegar), not alcohol.
• Saccharomyces carlsbergensis: Used specifically for bottom-fermenting lagers.', '["Acetobacter xylinum","Acetobacter aceti","Sacccharomyces cerevisiae","Saccharomyces carlsbergensis"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:08:45.273Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:08:45.273Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:43:55.617Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758605396944-2', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'The oxygen requirement in acetic fermentation is*', 'aerobic', 'Acetic acid fermentation (such as vinegar production via Acetobacter) is strictly an aerobic biological process requiring molecular oxygen to oxidize ethanol into acetic acid.

• Anaerobic / Facultative / Microaerophilic: Inappropriate oxygen requirements for active acetic acid conversion, which stalls or fails without abundant oxygen.', '["aerobic","anaerobic","Facultative","Microaerophilic"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T09:14:17.283Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T09:14:17.283Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:40:49.854Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758605414295-3', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Type of microorganism that will grow in strawberry jam*', 'osmophilic', 'Osmophilic yeasts and microorganisms thrive and grow successfully in high-sugar environments like high-sugar fruit preserves and strawberry jam.', '["halophilic","xerophilic","thermophilic","osmophilic"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T08:49:54.929Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T08:49:54.929Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:54:03.742Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758605429092-4', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Pasteurization is applied in processing*', 'high acid foods', 'Pasteurization is a mild thermal process applied primarily to high-acid foods (such as fruit juices, milk, and pickles) where the acidic environment inhibits surviving heat-resistant bacterial spores.

