❌ EHEC (Enterohemorrhagic E. coli): Causes severe bloody diarrhea (hemorrhagic colitis) and can lead to hemolytic uremic syndrome (HUS)
❌ EIEC (Enteroinvasive E. coli): Invades the intestinal lining to cause a dysentery-like illness with blood and mucus, similar to Shigella', '["EPEC","ETEC","EHEC","EIEC"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:16:16.102Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:16:16.102Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:47:25.975Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606229107-32', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'The major causative microbial agent of bloody diarrhea is*', 'EHEC', 'Enterohemorrhagic E. coli (EHEC, e.g., O157:H7) produces Shiga toxins and is the major causative microbial agent responsible for severe bloody diarrhea (hemorrhagic colitis) and HUS.

❌ ETEC (Enterotoxigenic E. coli): leading cause of Traveler''s diarrhea
❌ EPEC (Enteropathogenic E. coli): leading cause of infant water diarrhea
❌ EIEC (Enteroinvasive E. coli): Invades the intestinal lining to cause a dysentery-like illness with blood and mucus, similar to Shigella', '["EHEC","EPEC","ETEC","EIEC"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T08:48:32.988Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T08:48:32.988Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:47:43.373Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606249439-33', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Sentence A. Clostridium botulinum is a mesophilic soil bacteria that can grow in high acid foods.
Sentence B. Clostridium botulinum produces a fatal toxin called neurotoxin.*', 'Sentence B is correct.', 'Sentence A is incorrect because Clostridium botulinum is an anaerobic bacterium that cannot grow in high-acid foods (pH < 4.6). 

Sentence B is correct: it produces a fatal neurotoxin called botulinum toxin.', '["Sentence A is correct.","Sentence B is correct.","Both sentences are correct.","Both sentences are incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:15:37.423Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:15:37.423Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:48:03.171Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606270855-34', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Pus forming bacteria present on the surface of the skin, under the fingernails, in the nose, and throat that do not grow under refrigeration but can multiply if food is allowed to warm at room temperature.*', 'Staphylococcus aureus', 'Staphylococcus aureus is frequently found on human skin, under fingernails, and in the nasal passages/throat, producing heat-stable enterotoxins when food is left to warm in the temperature danger zone.', '["Salmonella","Clostridium botulinum","Staphylococcus aureus","Bacillus cereus"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:04:41.820Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:04:41.820Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:48:11.833Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606291322-35', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Sentence A. Molds produce mycotoxin with most potent carcinogenic activities.
Sentence B. Aspergillus flavus and Aspergillus ochraceous are species of molds that can produce carcinogenic mycotoxin.*', 'Both sentences are correct.', 'Sentence A is correct: molds produce secondary metabolites known as mycotoxins possessing potent carcinogenic properties. 

Sentence B is correct: Aspergillus flavus and Aspergillus ochraceus produce dangerous mycotoxins like aflatoxin and ochratoxin.', '["Sentence A is correct.","Sentence B is correct.","Both sentences are correct.","Both sentences are incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T08:44:39.866Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T08:44:39.866Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:48:21.364Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606304084-36', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'The mold that is used in the production or manufacture of sake, soy sauce and miso is*', 'Aspergillus oryzae', 'Aspergillus oryzae (koji mold) is the filamentous mold utilized traditionally to manufacture traditional Asian fermented products like sake, soy sauce, and miso.', '["Aspergillus flavus","Aspergillus ochraceous","Aspergillus oryzae","Aspergillus niger"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T09:17:03.677Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T09:17:03.677Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:53:33.925Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606322969-37', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Sentence A. Biological spoilage or deterioration is the result of the action of enzymes on chemical reactions in foods.
Sentence B. Soft rot in vegetables, oxidative browning reactions and overripe fruits are examples of biological spoilage/deterioration.*', 'Both sentences are correct.', 'Sentence A is correct: biological spoilage is driven by endogenous enzyme activity and chemical reactions within plant and animal tissues. 

Sentence B is correct: vegetable soft rot, enzymatic browning, and overripening are classic examples of biological deterioration.', '["Sentence A is correct.","Sentence B is correct.","Both sentences are correct.","Both sentences are incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T09:08:07.163Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T09:08:07.163Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:48:28.353Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606337468-38', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'The process of keeping microorganisms out by sanitary handling is*', 'asepsis', 'Asepsis is the sanitary practice of keeping microorganisms out of food or sterile environments entirely through strict hygienic handling.', '["sanitation","disinfection","asepsis","sterilization"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:10:49.853Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:10:49.853Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:48:33.852Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606362300-39', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'It is the preventive approach of ensuring food safety.*', 'HACCP', 'Hazard Analysis Critical Control Point (HACCP) is the internationally recognized preventive systematic approach to ensuring food safety.', '["GMP","HACCP","Codex Alimentarius","Republic Act 3720"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T08:53:00.567Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T08:53:00.567Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:48:37.487Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606376783-40', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'The Sanitation Code of the Philippines is*', 'Presidential Decree 856', 'Presidential Decree No. 856 is formally known as the Code on Sanitation of the Philippines.', '["Republic act 3720","Republic Act 10611","Food Code","Presidential Decree 856"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T09:58:35.078Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T09:58:35.078Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:48:43.266Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606391366-41', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Type of microorganisms that will grow in very low Aw is*', 'xerophilic', 'Xerophilic microorganisms are specialized organisms capable of growing and multiplying in environments with very low water activity (aw).

• Osmophilic: Grows in high sugar concentrations.
• Psychrophilic: Cold-loving.
• Thermophilic: Heat-loving.', '["osmophilic","psychrophilic","xerophilic","thermophilic"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T09:09:01.961Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T09:09:01.961Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:50:41.140Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606419065-42', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Sterilization is mostly applied to canning of fish and meats because*', 'more microorganisms both pathogenic and non-pathogenic and their spores that are needed to be destroyed', 'Sterilization is applied to low-acid canned meats and fish because they carry massive loads of diverse microorganisms, including highly heat-resistant bacterial spores and pathogens that require intense thermal lethality to eliminate.', '["there are more pathogenic microorganisms that are needed to be destroyed","more microorganisms both pathogenic and non-pathogenic and their spores that are needed to be destroyed","there are more non-pathogenic microorganisms that are needed to be destroyed","thermophilic and aerobic spoilage microorganisms are destroyed"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:11:36.058Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:11:36.058Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:50:48.805Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606440280-43', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'The drying rate is accelerated fastest when*', 'temperature is high, relative humidity is low', 'The drying rate of foods is accelerated fastest when the ambient drying temperature is high and relative humidity is low, creating a steep vapor pressure gradient that draws moisture out rapidly.', '["relative humidity is high, temperature is constant","relative humidity is low, temperature is constant","temperature is high, relative humidity is low","temperature is low, relative humidity is high"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:05:37.288Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:05:37.288Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:50:54.626Z"'::jsonb)
