('anki-card-1758606455494-44', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'These are treatments done to food immediately after drying to ensure longer preservation.*', 'sweating then packing', 'Sweating (equilibrating warm dried foods in closed bins so remaining internal moisture distributes evenly across pieces) should be done immediately after drying before final packing to prevent localized mold growth.', '["packing then storing","sweating then packing","packing then sweating","sweating then storing"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:09:48.382Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:09:48.382Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:50:59.626Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606467279-45', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Method of processing applicable to acid foods like tomatoes and fruit juices*', 'Hot-water bath', 'A boiling water bath canner is the standard thermal processing method applicable to high-acid foods such as tomatoes, fruit juices, jams, and pickled items.', '["Hot-water bath","Canner","Cold-pack method","Hot-packed method"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T08:51:10.996Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T08:51:10.996Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:47:17.771Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606535009-46', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'The best temperature for drying is*', '50-60°C', 'The optimal temperature range for conventional food dehydration generally spans 50°C to 60°C, balancing moisture removal efficiency while preventing thermal scorching or surface case hardening.

• 100-115°C / 90-95°C: Excessively high temperatures that cause surface cooking, scorching, and case hardening rather than uniform drying.', '["100-115°C","90-95°C","50-60°C","50-60 F"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:15:47.467Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:15:47.467Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:40:55.907Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606558325-47', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Sentence A. Cold point in cooking/canning food with liquid is at the bottom.
Sentence B. Cold point in cooking/canning solid food is at the center. *', 'Both sentences are correct.', '', '["Sentence A is correct.","Sentence B is correct.","Both sentences are correct.","Both sentences are incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T10:04:19.525Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T10:04:19.525Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T10:04:19.525Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606568757-48', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Two nutrients that are more easily destroyed during drying.*', 'Vitamins C and B', 'Water-soluble vitamins—specifically Vitamins C and B-complex—are highly sensitive to heat, oxygen, and moisture loss, making them the most easily degraded and destroyed nutrients during dehydration.

• Vitamins D, E, A, K: Fat-soluble vitamins with higher thermal stability during drying processes.', '["Vitamins C and B","Vitamins D and E","Vitamins A and K","Simple sugars and proteins"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T09:52:00.830Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T09:52:00.830Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:41:02.422Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606582674-49', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Case hardening during drying may be prevented by*', 'application of moderate temperature and relative humidity', 'Case hardening occurs when external moisture evaporates too rapidly under high heat and low humidity, forming a hardened outer crust that traps internal moisture. Applying moderate temperatures and controlled relative humidity allows steady, uniform moisture diffusion from the center outward, preventing case hardening.', '["wrapping food","application of moderate temperature and relative humidity","application of high temperature and low relative humidity","chilling before drying"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:10:10.165Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:10:10.165Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:41:07.321Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606594973-50', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Processing involving the removal of water from frozen foods under vacuum without passing the liquid state is called*', 'freeze drying', 'Freeze drying (lyophilization) involves freezing food and sublimating moisture directly from ice into water vapor under a vacuum without passing through an intermediate liquid state.

• Spray drying / Frying / Osmotic dehydration: Involve liquid phase transitions or standard evaporation.', '["spray drying","frying","osmotic dehydration","freeze drying"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:15:43.472Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:15:43.472Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:41:11.526Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606609971-51', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Type of bacteria that can grow with or without free oxygen*', 'facultative', 'Facultative microorganisms (such as facultative anaerobes) are versatile organisms capable of growing and surviving in either the presence or absence of free oxygen.', '["anaerobic","facultative","aerobic","microaerophilic"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:07:03.819Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:07:03.819Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:41:15.861Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606620888-52', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Microorganism used in making tempeh*', 'Rhizopus', 'Tempeh (a traditional Indonesian fermented soybean cake) is produced using filamentous molds belonging to the genus Rhizopus (specifically Rhizopus oligosporus).

• Saccharomyces cerevisiae: Brewer''s or baker''s yeast.
• Aspergillus niger: Mold used for citric acid or enzyme production.', '["Saccharomyces cereviceae","Lactobacillus brevis","Aspergillus niger","Rhizopus"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T09:17:07.140Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T09:17:07.140Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:41:20.076Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606635037-53', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Group of microorganisms that are more likely to grow on the surface of dried squid packed in polyethylene bags*', 'Mold', 'Dried squid has significantly reduced moisture content and available water. 

Most bacteria require a high water activity (typically above 0.91) to grow. 

Yeasts generally need an Aw 0.80 or above. 

Conversely, xerophilic (dry-loving) molds can actively grow in environments with a water activity as low as 0.60 to 0.70.', '["Bacteria","Algae","Mold","Yeasts"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T08:49:18.240Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T08:49:18.240Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:32:00.423Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606647787-54', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Used to limit the migration of moisture into the product*', 'packaging', 'The primary purpose of food packaging (specifically moisture-barrier films, vacuum packs, and sealed containers) is to separate the food product from the surrounding environment.

It acts as a physical shield that directly limits or blocks the migration of moisture—preventing dry foods (like crackers or chips) from absorbing damp air and becoming soggy, and preventing moist foods (like meat or bread) from drying out or developing freezer burn.

• Drying: A preservation method that removes moisture already inside the food to lower water activity, but it does not stop external moisture from migrating back into the product afterward.
• Heating: Used to cook food, destroy micro-organisms (pasteurization/sterilization), or drive off water vapor, but it offers no physical barrier protection once the heat source is removed.
• Freezing: Turns liquid water inside the food into ice crystals to halt microbial growth. Without proper packaging, freezing actually accelerates moisture loss to the dry freezer air through sublimation (freezer burn).', '["drying","packaging","heating","freezing"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T08:49:35.960Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T08:49:35.960Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:32:00.423Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606663102-55', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Which of the following preservation technique cannot achieve commercial sterility?*', 'Dehydration', 'Dehydration reduces water activity (aw) to levels that inhibit microbial multiplication, but it does not completely destroy all bacterial spores or achieve absolute commercial sterility (unlike thermal retorting, high-dose irradiation, or specialized high-pressure processing steps).', '["Heat Processing","irradiation","Dehydration","High pressure processing"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:07:32.500Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:07:32.500Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:42:53.784Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606674884-56', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'International symbol indicating food is irradiated*', 'Radura', 'The Radura is the international symbol used to indicate that a food product has been treated with ionizing radiation (irradiated). It features a distinctive green icon of a stylized plant inside a broken circle, which symbolizes a safe protective shield.

• Hurdle concept: A highly influential food preservation strategy that applies a combination of multiple sub-lethal preservative factors or barriers (like adjusting temperature, pH, water activity, and competitive flora simultaneously) to completely inhibit microbial growth instead of relying on a single intense sterilization method.
• Vacuum pack: A packaging method where air is entirely drawn out and evacuated from a non-permeable pouch before sealing. This creates an anaerobic interior that prevents the growth of standard spoilage-causing aerobic bacteria and molds.
• Modified atmosphere packaging (MAP): A food preservation technique that replaces the ambient air inside a package with a precise, pre-calculated gas blend (usually varying combinations of nitrogen, carbon dioxide, and oxygen) to drastically slow down chemical respiration and extend the product''s natural shelf-life.', '["CODEX","Radura","ISO 22000","HACCP"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:11:41.311Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:11:41.311Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:32:00.423Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606691369-57', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Which of the following is the overriding priority of food preservation?*', 'Minimize the potential for the occurrence and growth of microorganisms', 'The overriding priority and primary objective of all food preservation methods is to minimize or prevent the occurrence, survival, and multiplication of microorganisms.', '["Minimize the potential for the occurrence and growth of microorganisms","Slow down biochemical reactions","Preserve the nutritional quality of thefinished product","Prevent physical deterioration of product attributes"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T08:46:20.980Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T08:46:20.980Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:51:04.366Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758606703668-58', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Appropriate packaging material for liquid items which require high temperature processing*', 'Tetrapack', 'Tetrapack (Tetra Pak): This multi-layered carton packaging is specifically engineered for liquid items (such as milk, juices, and soups) that undergo aseptic or high-temperature processing (such as Ultra-High Temperature or UHT pasteurization and retort sterilization).

It provides a sterile environment, strong barrier protection against light and oxygen, and structural integrity under heat. 

• Saran: A plastic wrap (polyvinylidene chloride) mostly used for moisture/odor barriers or food covering, but not suitable for structural liquid packaging during high-temperature processing.
• Glassine: A smooth, translucent paper that is grease-resistant. It is used for dry goods, interleaving, or bakery items but cannot hold liquids or withstand extreme liquid processing temperatures. 
