Sentence B. Dry wine is when only part of the fermentable carbohydrates has been converted to ethyl alcohol.*', 'Sentence A is correct.', 'Sentence A is correct: alcoholic fermentation converts fermentable carbohydrates into ethyl alcohol and carbon dioxide gas.

Sentence B: Sweet wine is when only part of the fermentable carbohydrates has been converted to ethyl alcohol. Dry wine is produced when yeasts successfully convert all or nearly all of the fermentable carbohydrates into ethyl alcohol, leaving little to no residual sugar.', '["Sentence A is correct.","Sentence B is correct.","Both sentences are correct.","Both sentences are incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:09:26.328Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:09:26.328Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:55:55.005Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758607281741-88', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Sentence A. Whiskers are cottony growth on the surface of spoiled food caused by molds.
Sentence B. Ropinesss are slimy silk -like threads growing in the inside tissues of spoiled food caused by the molds.*', 'Sentence A is correct.', 'Sentence A is correct: "whiskers" describe cottony mold mycelium growth on spoiled food surfaces. 

Sentence B: ropiness is caused by spore-forming bacteria (Bacillus subtilis and Bacillus licheniformis), not molds', '["Sentence A is correct.","Sentence A is correct.","Both sentences are correct.","Both sentences are incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:08:58.351Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:08:58.351Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:54:46.663Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758607296857-89', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Sentence A. Sorbic acid and its salt are fungistatic agents.
Sentence B. They are bacterial growth inhibitor.*', 'Sentence A is correct.', 'Sentence A is correct: sorbic acid and sorbates act as fungistatic agents inhibiting mold and yeast growth. 

Sentence B is incorrect because they do not primarily target broad bacterial growth.', '["Sentence A is correct.","Sentence B is correct.","Both sentences are correct.","Both sentences are incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T10:01:21.869Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T10:01:21.869Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:54:36.495Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758607310788-90', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'It is a high heat method of food preservation that is also a method of drying.*', 'Smoking', 'Sentence A is correct: "whiskers" describe cottony mold mycelium growth on spoiled food surfaces. 

Sentence B is incorrect because ropiness is caused by spore-forming bacteria (Bacillus species), not molds.', '["Osmotic dehydration","Curing","Salting","Smoking"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:09:53.551Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:09:53.551Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:54:52.436Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758607332472-91', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Sentence A. Chemical food spoilage agents include light, heat, cold, moisture and rough handling.
Sentence B. Biological food spoilage agents include molds, yeasts, bacteria, parasites, insects and rodents.*', 'Sentence B is correct.', 'Sentence A is incorrect because light, heat, and moisture are physical/environmental agents rather than chemical spoilage agents. 

Sentence B is correct: biological spoilage is driven by living agents including molds, yeasts, bacteria, parasites, insects, and rodents.', '["Sentence A is correct.","Sentence B is correct.","Both sentences are correct.","Both sentences are incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T09:44:14.153Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T09:44:14.153Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:53:44.371Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758607349436-92', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Sentence A. The target microorganism in pasteurization is Mycobacterium tuberculosis.
Sentence B. The targetmicroorganisms in low temperature preservation is Lysteria monocytogenes.*', 'Both sentences are correct.', 'Sentence A is correct: Mycobacterium tuberculosis is the historical thermal resistance benchmark target for milk pasteurization. 

Sentence B is correct: Listeria monocytogenes is the primary pathogen of concern in low-temperature refrigerated storage.', '["Sentence A is correct.","Sentence B is correct.","Both sentences are correct.","Both sentences are incorrect."]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T14:16:06.045Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T14:16:06.045Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:53:50.975Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758607364204-93', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610451953-1790433140293-winqs', 'Exposure of food to an atmosphere below -60°C through direct contact with liquid nitrogen or liquid carbon dioxide or their vapor is called*', 'cryogenic freezing', 'Cryogenic freezing exposes food to extremely low temperatures below -60°C via direct contact with liquefied gases like liquid nitrogen or liquid carbon dioxide.', '["ripening","cryogenic freezing","aging","blast freezing"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-08T09:57:07.488Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-07T09:57:07.488Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.006Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T11:53:55.733Z"'::jsonb)
