False', 'False', 'Insulin is an anabolic hormone that promotes lipogenesis, glycogenesis, and protein synthesis while inhibiting lipolysis (the breakdown of stored triglycerides), making the statement that insulin favors lipolysis false.', '["False","Albumin","Propionate","Passive diffusion"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.690Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T03:05:01.294Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757927667442-70', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610525132-1790433140279-g2fd9', 'Ketogenesis results when there is abundance of NADH and scarcity of glucose.





