False', 'False', 'Ketogenesis is stimulated when there is a scarcity of carbohydrates (low glucose) coupled with high levels of fatty acid beta-oxidation (which generates acetyl-CoA), rather than an abundance of NADH. High NADH actually inhibits certain Krebs cycle steps and promotes fat synthesis, whereas ketogenesis occurs under low carbohydrate/high glucagon conditions.', '["False","manganese","All of above","Hexokinase"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.690Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T03:05:06.480Z"'::jsonb),
