False', 'True', 'Intermediate-Density Lipoproteins (IDLs) have a higher core lipid ratio (specifically cholesterol esters and triglycerides) relative to protein content compared to High-Density Lipoproteins (HDLs), which are densely packed with protective apolipoproteins and proteins.', '["True","glutelin","Glucose","lysozomes"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.690Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T02:58:28.786Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928083271-98', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610525132-1790433140279-g2fd9', '125 grams of protein equals 200 grams Nitrogen.





True




False', 'False', 'Nitrogen makes up approximately 16% of the weight of a typical protein molecule (meaning 1 gram of nitrogen corresponds to roughly 6.25 grams of protein). Therefore, 125 grams of protein does not equal 200 grams of nitrogen; it contains roughly 20 grams of nitrogen (125 / 6.25 = 20g N).', '["False","Skin, liver, kidney","PDCAAS","Elastin"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.690Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T02:58:34.251Z"'::jsonb),
