False', 'False', 'Glycolysis is initiated by the phosphorylation of free glucose into glucose-6-phosphate catalyzed by the enzyme hexokinase (or glucokinase in the liver), whereas enolase is an enzyme that catalyzes a much later step in glycolysis (converting 2-phosphoglycerate to phosphoenolpyruvate).', '["False","lysozomes","They are needed when we are young","Parietal cells"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.910Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T02:58:18.859Z"'::jsonb),
