False', 'False', 'The Krebs cycle (citric acid cycle) is a continuous cyclic pathway consisting of 8 enzymatic reactions (not 6) designed to oxidize acetyl groups and regenerate oxaloacetate.', '["False","Kreb Cycle","zein","Maltodextrin"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.910Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T03:06:25.600Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928133350-102', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610525132-1790433140279-g2fd9', 'Kreb Cycle forms 12 ATP per cycle.



True




False', 'False', 'A single turn of the Krebs cycle does not yield 12 ATP directly through substrate-level phosphorylation; it produces reduced coenzymes (NADH and FADH2) and one GTP, which subsequently yield approximately 10 to 12 ATP equivalents only after passing through oxidative phosphorylation in the electron transport chain (though modern stoichiometry revisions estimate around 10 ATP per cycle).', '["False","Glycogenesis","Gluconeogenesis","Protein, lipids, carbohydrates"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.910Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T02:58:23.374Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757928144336-103', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610525132-1790433140279-g2fd9', 'A transporter driven by membrane potential, The flow of ADP into the mitochondrial matrix is coupled to the exit of ATP is called ATP synthase.





True




