('anki-card-1756883089519-0', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610563139-1790433136793-gn4oo', 'It is the phase in the microbial growth curve where there is little or no apparent growth for a period following the contact between the microorganisms and the environment.', 'lag phase', 'The lag phase is the initial adaptation period in a microbial growth curve where microorganisms adjust to their new environment, showing little to no apparent cell division.

• Log phase: Rapid exponential growth.
• Stationary phase: Growth balances cell death.
• Death phase: Decline in viable cell numbers.', '["lag phase","log phase","stationary phase","death phase"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.526Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:18:10.454Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756883106734-1', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610563139-1790433136793-gn4oo', 'Microorganism associated with the production of soy sauce.', 'Aspergillus oryzae', 'Aspergillus oryzae (koji mold) is a filamentous fungus traditionally utilized in Asian food fermentations for breaking down starches and proteins in the commercial production of soy sauce, miso, and sake.

• Saccharomyces cerevisiae: Baker''s or brewer''s yeast.
• Propionibacterium sp.: Associated with Swiss cheese flavor.
• Penicillium roqueforti: Used for blue cheese ripening.', '["Saccharomyces cerevisiae","Propionibacterium sp.","Aspergillus oryzae","Penicillium roqueforti"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.526Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:18:20.186Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756883122783-2', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610563139-1790433136793-gn4oo', 'Trichinella spiralis is an example of a ________.', 'Helminth', 'Trichinella spiralis is a parasitic roundworm belonging to the animal kingdom group known as helminthes, typically transmitted via undercooked pork.', '["Helminth","Yeast","Mold","Protozoa"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.526Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:18:25.609Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756883137982-3', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610563139-1790433136793-gn4oo', 'Entamoeba hystolica is an example of a ________.', 'Protozoa', 'Entamoeba histolytica is a single-celled eukaryotic parasite classified under protozoa, responsible for amoebic dysentery.', '["Helminth","Yeast","Mold","Protozoa"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.526Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:18:30.213Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756883157416-4', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610563139-1790433136793-gn4oo', 'It is the phase in the growth curve where microorganisms grow at the maximal rate.', 'log phase', 'The log (logarithmic) phase is characterized by cells dividing exponentially at their maximum possible rate.', '["lag phase","log phase","stationary phase","death phase"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.526Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:18:35.088Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756883171998-5', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610563139-1790433136793-gn4oo', 'It is the phase in the growth curve where there is no net increase or decrease in cell number.', 'stationary phase', 'The stationary phase occurs when nutrient depletion and waste accumulation cause the overall growth rate to equal the death rate, resulting in no net increase or decrease in total living cell numbers.', '["lag phase","log phase","stationary phase","death phase"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.526Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:18:40.376Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756883188514-6', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610563139-1790433136793-gn4oo', 'It is the phase in the growth curve that is characterized by accumulation of waste that are toxic and nutrient depletion.', 'stationary phase', 'The accumulation of toxic metabolic waste products and the progressive exhaustion of available nutrients are the primary physiological drivers that force microbial populations into the stationary phase.', '["lag phase","log phase","stationary phase","death phase"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.526Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:18:44.313Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756883206331-7', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610563139-1790433136793-gn4oo', 'It is the phase in the growth curve where the rate of death exceeds the rate of growth.', 'death phase', 'The death (decline) phase occurs when adverse environmental conditions and severe nutrient depletion cause the rate of cell death to exceed the rate of cellular growth and division.', '["lag phase","log phase","stationary phase","death phase"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.526Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:18:48.083Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756883223613-8', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610563139-1790433136793-gn4oo', 'In food preservation, the goal is to lengthen the ______.', 'lag phase', 'The primary operational goal of food preservation techniques (such as refrigeration, drying, or adding preservatives) is to artificially extend the lag phase, delaying microbial multiplication and spoilage.', '["lag phase","log phase","stationary phase","death phase"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.526Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:18:52.655Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756883247461-9', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610563139-1790433136793-gn4oo', 'If the bacterial cells grow from 1000 cells to 64 000 cells in 3 hours, how many generations of microorganisms occurred?', '6', 'To calculate the number of generations (n): 
Formula: N = N₀ × 2ⁿ, where N = 64,000 and N₀ = 1,000. 
64,000 ÷ 1,000 = 2ⁿ ⇒ 64 = 2ⁿ ⇒ 6 generations (2⁶ = 64).', '["2","4","6","8"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.526Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:19:56.405Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756883262994-10', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610563139-1790433136793-gn4oo', 'If the bacterial cells grow from 1000 cells to 64 000 cells in 3 hours, what is the generation time?', '30 minutes', 'To calculate generation time (g): 
