('anki-card-1756883295193-12', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610563139-1790433136793-gn4oo', 'High acid foods with pH of ___.', 'less than 3.7', 'According to food microbiology and canning standards, high-acid foods possess an intrinsic pH of less than 3.7 (e.g., citrus juices, pickles).

• Less than 4.6: The critical regulatory boundary distinguishing low-acid foods from acid/high-acid foods regarding Clostridium botulinum safety.', '["less than 3.7","less than 4.6","less than 5.7","less than 7.0"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.526Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:20:35.054Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756883310992-13', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610563139-1790433136793-gn4oo', 'Foods with pH of 4.0 is considered as _____.', 'acid foods', 'Foods with a pH level ranging between 4.0 and 4.6 (or broadly 3.7 to 4.6) are classified under food safety guidelines as acid foods.', '["high acid foods","acid foods","medium acid foods","low acid foods"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.526Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T10:20:38.740Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756883328208-14', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610563139-1790433136793-gn4oo', 'It is referred to as the available water in food that can be utilized for the growth and development of microorganisms.', 'water activity', 'Water activity (aw) measures the ratio of water vapor pressure of a food to pure water, representing the unbound, free water available to support microbial growth.

