('anki-card-1756789570192-7', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610598974-1790433142628-tj9iq', 'Ob gene codes that suppresses appetite and increases energy expenditure.', 'Leptin', '', '["Leptin","Uncoupling proteins","Brown fat","White fat"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:46:17.323Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:46:17.323Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.801Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:46:17.323Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756789625925-8', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610598974-1790433142628-tj9iq', 'Permit only heat loss; no formation of adenosine, triphosphate; increase basal metabolic rate; resist weight gain.', 'Uncoupling proteins', 'In standard cellular respiration, the mitochondria create an electrochemical proton gradient across their inner membrane, which powers ATP synthase to generate adenosine triphosphate (ATP). Uncoupling proteins (UCPs) act as specialized proton channels that short-circuit this system. They allow protons to leak back across the membrane, completely uncoupling the proton motive force from ATP synthesis.

Because the energy gradient is bypassed, no ATP is formed. Instead, 100% of the energy from food oxidation is dissipated strictly as heat loss. This massive cellular energy drain forces the body to burn through excess calories, which drastically increases the basal metabolic rate and naturally helps the organism resist weight gain.

• Brown fat: Brown adipose tissue (BAT) is the specific tissue that contains a massive abundance of mitochondria packed with these uncoupling proteins. While brown fat is the site where this process happens, Uncoupling proteins are the exact molecular entities responsible for the chemical mechanism described in the prompt.
• White fat: The primary energy-storing adipose tissue. It stores excess calories as large single droplets of triglycerides for later use rather than burning them off as heat.
• Leptin: A hormone secreted by fat cells that signals the brain to suppress appetite and increase baseline metabolism, but it does not act as a mitochondrial membrane proton uncoupler.', '["Leptin","Uncoupling proteins","Brown fat","White fat"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 3, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-04T08:10:28.672Z","interval":6,"easeFactor":2.15,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:10:28.672Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.801Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:10:28.998Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756789838647-9', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610598974-1790433142628-tj9iq', 'Espouse exaggerated or false theories of weight loss and advise consumers to follow inadequate diets.', 'Fad diet', '', '["Fad diet","Weight cycling","Dangerous drugs","Surgery"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:47:09.238Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:47:09.238Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.801Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:47:09.238Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756789869844-10', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610598974-1790433142628-tj9iq', 'Lipoprotein lipase is activated causing more weight gain after weight loss.', 'Weight cycling', 'Lipoprotein lipase (LPL) is the rate-limiting enzyme responsible for the uptake and storage of triglycerides into fat cells.

When an individual loses weight, the body views the loss of fat tissue as a threat to survival. In response, it increases adipose tissue LPL activity to aggressively pull fat from the bloodstream back into storage.

Because LPL activity skyrockets and remains elevated after weight reduction, it actively drives the body to regain the lost weight. This metabolic pull leads directly to weight cycling (commonly known as "yo-yo dieting"), where an individual falls into a repetitive pattern of losing weight only to rapidly regain it.

• Dangerous drugs: Refers to hazardous chemical compounds or banned stimulants (like ephedra or PPA) used to abnormally accelerate metabolism, not the body''s natural enzymatic response to fat loss.
• Fad diet: Represents a short-term, unscientific dietary pattern (like the cabbage soup diet). While fad diets frequently trigger weight cycling because they are unsustainable, the actual physiological activation of LPL is an enzymatic survival mechanism rather than a diet type.
• Surgery: Refers to anatomical weight-loss interventions such as gastric bypass or sleeve gastrectomy.', '["Fad diet","Weight cycling","Dangerous drugs","Surgery"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-11T08:08:40.479Z","interval":13,"easeFactor":2.15,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:08:40.479Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.801Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:08:40.799Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756789913359-11', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610598974-1790433142628-tj9iq', 'Like phenylpropanolamine, ephedra, and triiodothyroacetic acid.', 'Dangerous drugs', 'In the context of regulatory laws and professional practice boards, substances like phenylpropanolamine (PPA), ephedra, and triiodothyroacetic acid (TRIAC) are explicitly categorized under Dangerous drugs or banned/restricted pharmaceutical agents due to their severe, life-threatening toxicities.

Rather than being treated as simple lifestyle components or mild dietary trends, health ministries and food and drug administrations classify these compounds strictly as high-hazard substances because of their devastating systemic impacts:

	• Phenylpropanolamine (PPA): Legally restricted and pulled from commercial availability globally due to its confirmed risk of causing hemorrhagic strokes and severe cardiovascular damage.
	• Ephedra: An unregulated herbal amphetamine-like stimulant explicitly banned by the FDA and international drug enforcement units following documented cases of arrhythmias, seizures, and sudden cardiac death.
	• Triiodothyroacetic acid (TRIAC): A highly potent thyroid hormone metabolite classified as a dangerous prescription-only or banned hormone derivative due to its risk of inducing thyrotoxicosis and metabolic shock.', '["Fad diet","Weight cycling","Dangerous drugs","Surgery"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-31T12:20:13.616Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.35,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T12:20:13.616Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.801Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T12:20:13.807Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756789951674-12', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610598974-1790433142628-tj9iq', 'An approach to weight loss to effectively limit food intake by reducing the size of the stomach.', 'Surgery', '', '["Fad diet","Weight cycling","Dangerous drugs","Surgery"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:48:11.711Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:48:11.711Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.801Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:48:11.711Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756790174796-13', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610598974-1790433142628-tj9iq', 'Refers to congenital deformities in the lip or palate that prevents adequate closure.', 'Cleft lip/cleft palate', 'Cleft lip/cleft palate', '["Cleft lip/cleft palate","Cheilosis","Angular stomatitis","Stomatitis"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:48:17.980Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:48:17.980Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.801Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756790192413-14', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610598974-1790433142628-tj9iq', 'Refers to the angular fissuring of mouth.', 'Cheilosis', '', '["Cleft lip/cleft palate","Cheilosis","Angular stomatitis","Stomatitis"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:48:24.219Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:48:24.219Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.801Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:48:24.219Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756790215412-15', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610598974-1790433142628-tj9iq', 'Pertains to lip lesion characterized by fissures of the corners of the lips.', 'Angular stomatitis', 'Angular stomatitis', '["Cleft lip/cleft palate","Cheilosis","Angular stomatitis","Stomatitis"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:48:35.671Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:48:35.671Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.801Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756790257593-16', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610598974-1790433142628-tj9iq', 'Refers to the inflammation of the oral mucosa due to niacin, tryptophan, folic acid, or vit B12 deficiency.', 'Stomatitis', 'Stomatitis is the broad medical term for any inflammation or swelling of the oral mucosa (the soft mucous membrane lining inside the mouth, including the cheeks, gums, inside of the lips, and palate).

Rapidly dividing epithelial cells lining the mouth depend heavily on continuous coenzyme energy networks to replicate. Deficiencies in vitamins like niacin (and its amino acid precursor tryptophan), folic acid, or vitamin B12 disrupt cellular synthesis, causing the protective lining to break down. This leads directly to generalized redness, painful open sores, and burning swelling inside the mouth.

• Angular stomatitis: This is a localized subcategory of inflammation that occurs strictly at the angles (corners) of the mouth, rather than representing a widespread inflammation of the entire oral mucosa. It is classically tied to riboflavin (B2) and iron deficits.
• Cheilosis: This refers specifically to the structural drying, cracking, and splitting of the skin of the lips themselves, rather than targeting the interior mucous membranes lining the oral cavity.
• Cleft lip/cleft palate: A congenital structural birth defect where the tissues of the lip or upper palate fail to fuse properly during embryonic development, unrelated to an acquired adult vitamin-deficiency inflammation.', '["Cleft lip/cleft palate","Cheilosis","Angular stomatitis","Stomatitis"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2028-06-27T13:49:33.306Z","interval":596,"easeFactor":2.15,"repetitions":9}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T13:49:33.306Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.801Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-09T13:49:33.306Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756790423519-17', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610598974-1790433142628-tj9iq', 'Refers to the increased vascularity of papillary epithelium manifested by soreness of the tongue, atrophy and flattening.', 'Glossitis', '', '["Glossitis","Gingivitis","Periodontitis","Tonsilitis"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:49:07.693Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:49:07.693Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.801Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:49:07.693Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756790464665-18', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610598974-1790433142628-tj9iq', 'Pertains to the inflammation of the gums caused by plaque, Vit C or niacin deficiency.', 'Gingivitis', '', '["Glossitis","Gingivitis","Periodontitis","Tonsilitis"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:49:13.093Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:49:13.093Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.801Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:49:13.093Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756790506396-19', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610598974-1790433142628-tj9iq', 'Refers to the inflammation of the supporting structure of the teeth with a resultant loss of alveolar bone.', 'Periodontitis', 'Periodontitis is a chronic inflammatory disease that directly affects the periodontium—the tissues, ligaments, and supporting structures that surround and anchor the teeth.

Unlike milder gum diseases, periodontitis involves the progressive destruction and loss of the alveolar bone surrounding the teeth. If left untreated, this structural breakdown causes the teeth to become loose and eventually fall out.

• Tonsillitis: Refers to inflammation of the tonsils at the back of the throat.
• Gingivitis: This is the early phase of gum inflammation. While the gums are red and swollen, the inflammation remains confined to the soft tissue and does not cause alveolar bone loss or attachment loss.
• Glossitis: Refers strictly to inflammation or swelling of the tongue.', '["Glossitis","Gingivitis","Periodontitis","Tonsilitis"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-31T16:56:05.850Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.35,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T16:56:05.850Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.801Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T16:56:06.029Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756790524329-20', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610598974-1790433142628-tj9iq', 'Refers to the inflammation of the throat.', 'Tonsilitis', '', '["Glossitis","Gingivitis","Periodontitis","Tonsilitis"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:49:42.140Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:49:42.140Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.801Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:49:42.140Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756790629573-21', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610598974-1790433142628-tj9iq', 'Refers to the acute or chronic inflammation of the esophageal wall.', 'Esophagitis', '', '["Esophagitis","Dysphagia","Achalasia","Esophageal obstruction"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:49:55.327Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:49:55.327Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.801Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:49:55.327Z"'::jsonb),
