('anki-card-1756633750812-43', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610619615-1790433142629-53sdx', 'Needed for the integrity of cellular and intracellular membranes; widely distributed in both plant foods and animal products; synthesized in many blood tissues from glucose.', 'Myoinositol', '', '["Lipoic acid","Choline","Myoinositol","Carnitine"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-27T20:00:00.000Z","interval":35,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.842Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756633853740-44', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610619615-1790433142629-53sdx', 'Not a dietary essential since it can be synthesized in the liver and kidneys from lysine and methionine; an essential substance needed to transport long chain fatty acid into the cell''s mitochondria where they are oxidized to provide energy.', 'Carnitine', '', '["Myoinositol","Carnitine","Coenzyme Q","Taurine"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-27T20:00:00.000Z","interval":5,"easeFactor":2.35,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.842Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756633924736-45', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610619615-1790433142629-53sdx', 'A generic name for lipid-like substance found in all cells; concentrated in mitochondria, where energy synthesis takes place. It plays an important role in the respiratory chain where energy from nutrients is trapped within ATP.', 'Coenzyme Q', '', '["Myoinositol","Carnitine","Coenzyme Q","Taurine"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-22T20:00:00.000Z","interval":30,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.842Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756634063296-46', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610619615-1790433142629-53sdx', 'A sulfur-containing amino acid derived from cysteine, which has an essential role in regulating the activity of the nervous system, particularly the retina of the eye; also involved in the absorption of fat. Its different chemical structure does not enable the compound to incorporate into protein molecule.', 'Taurine', '', '["Myoinositol","Carnitine","Coenzyme Q","Taurine"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-26T20:00:00.000Z","interval":34,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.842Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756634238888-47', NULL, 'anki-deck-1783610619615-1790433142629-53sdx', 'What are the macronutrients?', 'Calcium, Phosphorus, Potassium, Sulfur, Chlorine, Magnesium', 'Answer: Calcium, Phosphorus, Potassium, Sulfur, Chlorine, Magnesium', '["Calcium, Phosphorus, Potassium, Sulfur, Chlorine, Magnesium","Physiologic fuel value","Choline","Satiation"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-24T20:00:00.000Z","interval":2,"easeFactor":2.35,"repetitions":8}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.842Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-08T12:24:43.573Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788372752831-0', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788372725999-1790433136743-6obos', 'Which nutrient provides the greatest amount of energy per gram?', 'Fat', '', '["Carbohydrate","Protein","Fat","Alcohol"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-26T15:45:27.186Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":1.7,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-25T15:45:27.186Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.508Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-25T15:45:27.491Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788372772737-1', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788372725999-1790433136743-6obos', 'Which GI hormone primarily stimulates pancreatic bicarbonate secretion?', 'Secretin', '❌ Gastrin: Secreted by gastric G cells; primarily stimulates gastric acid (HCl) and intrinsic factor secretion by parietal cells.
❌ CCK: Cholecystokinin (CCK) stimulates gallbladder contraction and pancreatic enzyme secretion, not primary bicarbonate release.
❌ Motilin: Stimulates migrating motor complexes (MMCs) in the interdigestive state to promote GI motility and gastric emptying.', '["Secretin","Gastrin","Motilin","CCK"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-26T15:45:21.819Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":1.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-25T15:45:21.819Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.508Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-25T15:45:22.119Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788372794460-2', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788372725999-1790433136743-6obos', 'Where does glycolysis occur?', 'Cytoplasm', '❌ Mitochondrial matrix: Site of the Krebs (Citric Acid) cycle, pyruvate decarboxylation, and beta-oxidation.
❌ Inner mitochondrial membrane: Site of the electron transport chain (ETC) and ATP synthase for oxidative phosphorylation.
❌ Nucleus: Site of DNA replication and transcription into RNA; contains no glycolytic enzymes.', '["Cytoplasm","Mitochondrial matrix","Inner mitochondrial membrane","Nucleus"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-26T15:45:34.554Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":1.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-25T15:45:34.554Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.508Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-25T15:45:35.170Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788372819464-3', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788372725999-1790433136743-6obos', 'What is the primary significance of the Krebs cycle in energy metabolism?', 'It produces NADH and FADH₂ for oxidative phosphorylation', 'During one turn of the Krebs cycle, acetyl-CoA is condensed with oxaloacetate to form citrate, which undergoes a series of decarboxylation and oxidation-reduction reactions catalyzed by enzymes such as isocitrate dehydrogenase and alpha-ketoglutarate dehydrogenase. These reactions reduce NAD⁺ and FAD into NADH and FADH₂. These reduced coenzymes then donate their high-energy electrons to the mitochondrial electron transport chain, establishing a proton gradient that powers oxidative phosphorylation via ATP synthase to generate the vast majority of cellular ATP.', '["It produces the majority of ATP directly","It produces NADH and FADH₂ for oxidative phosphorylation","It converts glucose directly into lactate","It produces bile acids"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-26T15:46:53.580Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":1.7,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-25T15:46:53.580Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.508Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-25T15:46:54.260Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788372836388-4', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788372725999-1790433136743-6obos', 'Which transporter is primarily responsible for intestinal absorption of fructose?', 'GLUT5', '❌ SGLT1: Sodium-glucose cotransporter 1; actively transports glucose and galactose across the apical membrane, not fructose.
❌ GLUT2: Basolateral transporter that exports glucose, galactose, and fructose out of enterocytes into portal circulation (can translocate apically only during high-sugar surges).
❌ GLUT4: Insulin-dependent glucose transporter found primarily in skeletal muscle and adipose tissue; absent from the intestinal brush border.', '["GLUT5","SGLT1","GLUT2","GLUT4"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-26T15:46:09.325Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":1.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-25T15:46:09.325Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.508Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-25T15:46:09.673Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788372856294-5', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788372725999-1790433136743-6obos', 'Long-chain dietary fatty acids are primarily transported from the intestine initially through the:', 'Lymphatic system', '❌ Portal vein: Transports water-soluble nutrients and short- to medium-chain fatty acids (SCFAs and MCFAs) directly to the liver.
❌ Renal circulation: Directs blood flow to kidneys for filtration and waste excretion; plays no role in initial lipid absorption.
❌ Hepatic artery: Delivers oxygenated arterial blood from systemic circulation to the liver; not an initial transport route from the gut.', '["Lymphatic system","Portal vein","Renal circulation","Hepatic artery"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-26T15:46:26.704Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":1.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-25T15:46:26.704Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.508Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-25T15:46:26.983Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788372875718-6', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788372725999-1790433136743-6obos', 'A patient receiving long-term isoniazid develops peripheral neuropathy. Which nutrient deficiency should be suspected?', 'Vitamin B6', 'Isoniazid is a hydrazine derivative that is structurally similar to pyridoxine. It causes vitamin B6 deficiency through two primary mechanisms: (1) it chemically binds to pyridoxal and pyridoxal-5''-phosphate (PLP) to form inactive isoniazid-pyridoxal hydrazone complexes that are rapidly excreted in the urine, and (2) it competitively inhibits pyridoxal kinase, the enzyme responsible for phosphorylating pyridoxine into bioactive PLP. Because PLP is an obligate coenzyme for glutamic acid decarboxylase (which converts glutamate to GABA) and for enzymes involved in sphingolipid and myelin sheath synthesis, severe depletion produces peripheral axonal degeneration and neuropathy. Prophylactic administration of pyridoxine (25 to 50 mg daily) is routinely indicated for high-risk patients receiving INH.

Isoniazid forms an inactive hydrazone complex with pyridoxal phosphate (PLP) and accelerates its urinary excretion, leading to secondary pyridoxine deficiency and peripheral neuropathy.
❌ Vitamin B1: Thiamine deficiency causes beriberi (wet/dry) or Wernicke-Korsakoff syndrome, characteristically tied to alcohol use or poor intake.
❌ Vitamin B12: Cobalamin deficiency causes subacute combined degeneration of the spinal cord (SCD) and megaloblastic anemia, typically due to lack of intrinsic factor or ileal disease.
❌ Vitamin C: Ascorbic acid deficiency results in scurvy (petechiae, bleeding gums, impaired collagen synthesis).', '["Vitamin B6","Vitamin B1","Vitamin C","Vitamin B12"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-26T15:46:42.657Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":1.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-25T15:46:42.657Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.508Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-25T15:46:42.977Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788372902904-7', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788372725999-1790433136743-6obos', 'A patient taking warfarin asks whether they should completely avoid green leafy vegetables. What is the best nutrition advice?', 'Maintain a consistent vitamin K intake', 'Warfarin competitively inhibits the enzyme vitamin K epoxide reductase complex 1 (VKORC1), blocking the reduction of vitamin K epoxide to vitamin K hydroquinone. Vitamin K hydroquinone is an obligate cofactor for gamma-glutamyl carboxylase, the enzyme that adds carboxyl groups to glutamic acid residues on hepatic clotting factors II (prothrombin), VII, IX, and X, as well as regulatory proteins C and S. Dosing of warfarin is empirically titrated to achieve a therapeutic target INR (typically 2.0 to 3.0) based on the patient''s habitual dietary intake of phylloquinone (vitamin K1, predominantly found in green leafy vegetables). Maintaining consistent daily intake prevents fluctuations in hepatic substrate availability; drastic reductions increase INR to supratherapeutic levels (elevating bleeding risk), whereas sudden spikes bypass VKORC1 inhibition and precipitate subtherapeutic INR (elevating thromboembolic risk).', '["Avoid all vitamin K-containing foods","Increase vitamin K intake substantially","Maintain a consistent vitamin K intake","Eliminate all dietary fat"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-26T15:44:56.889Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":1.7,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-25T15:44:56.889Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.508Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-25T15:44:57.421Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788372923211-8', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788372725999-1790433136743-6obos', 'Which combination represents the essential fatty acids?', 'Linoleic acid and α-linolenic acid', '❌ EPA and DHA: Conditionally essential / semi-essential omega-3s that can be synthesized endogenously from α-linolenic acid (ALA), though conversion efficiency is limited.
❌ Arachidonic acid and EPA: Arachidonic acid is conditionally essential (synthesized from linoleic acid), and EPA is derived from ALA; neither are primary essential precursors.
❌ Oleic acid and palmitic acid: Oleic acid (omega-9 MUFA) and palmitic acid (SFA) are fully synthesized endogenously via acetyl-CoA and Δ9 desaturase.', '["Linoleic acid and α-linolenic acid","EPA and DHA","Oleic acid and palmitic acid","Arachidonic acid and EPA"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-26T15:45:07.664Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":1.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-25T15:45:07.664Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.508Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-25T15:45:08.059Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788372940368-9', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788372725999-1790433136743-6obos', 'During prolonged fasting, which metabolic process becomes increasingly important as insulin decreases and glucagon increases?', 'Ketogenesis', 'During prolonged fasting, your body''s stored liver glycogen is completely depleted (usually within 24 hours). As insulin levels fall dramatically and glucagon rises, adipose tissue breaks down fat into free fatty acids.

The liver takes up these fatty acids and undergoes a process called ketogenesis to produce ketone bodies (acetoacetate and beta-hydroxybutyrate). These ketone bodies cross the blood-brain barrier and serve as a vital alternative fuel source for the brain and muscles, effectively preserving muscle mass by minimizing the need for protein breakdown.

❌ Glycogenesis: Glycogen synthesis is an anabolic process stimulated by insulin in the well-fed state; inhibited during fasting.
❌ Lipogenesis: De novo fatty acid synthesis requires high insulin and excess energy; shut off when glucagon levels rise.
❌ Protein synthesis: Anabolic tissue building promoted by insulin and amino acid availability; replaced by proteolysis/autophagy in prolonged starvation.', '["Ketogenesis","Glycogenesis","Lipogenesis","Protein synthesis"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 3, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T08:08:47.387Z","interval":9,"easeFactor":1.3,"repetitions":6}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:08:47.387Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.508Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:08:47.718Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373017762-0', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788372990381-1790433139833-43li1', 'What is the main objective of DOH AO 2019-0033?', 'To establish uniform implementation of the Nutrition Care Process (NCP) in hospitals', 'The AO ensures standardized, evidence-based nutrition care through the NCP in all hospital settings.', '["To establish uniform implementation of the Nutrition Care Process (NCP) in hospitals","To standardize medical documentation across all hospitals","Option C","To replace the role of dietitians with nutrition nurses"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-29T10:46:16.516Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T10:46:16.516Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.026Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T10:46:16.841Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373038968-1', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788372990381-1790433139833-43li1', 'What are the four core steps of the NCP?', 'Assessment, diagnosis, intervention, and monitoring & evaluation', 'These four steps make up the standardized NCP model recognized by DOH and the Academy of Nutrition and Dietetics.', '["Assessment, diagnosis, intervention, and monitoring & evaluation","Screening, assessment, evaluation, and referral","Planning, implementation, documentation, and discharge","Option D"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-29T10:45:45.592Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T10:45:45.592Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.026Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T10:45:45.915Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373059775-2', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788372990381-1790433139833-43li1', 'Which of the following is a nutrition diagnosis domain in NCPT?', 'Clinical, Behavioral-Environmental, Intake', 'Nutrition diagnoses fall into three domains: Intake (NI), Clinical (NC), and Behavioral-Environmental (NB).', '["Clinical, Behavioral-Environmental, Intake","Food/Nutrition-Related History, Anthropometric Measurements, Nutrition-Focused Physical Findings","Assessment, Diagnosis, Intervention","Anthropometrics, Biochemical, Clinical"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-29T10:45:33.740Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T10:45:33.740Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.026Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T10:45:34.059Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373080763-3', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788372990381-1790433139833-43li1', 'Which of the following BEST describes Nutrition Assessment according to the Academy of Nutrition and Dietetics?', 'Collecting, analyzing, and interpreting data to determine a nutrition-related problem', 'Nutrition Assessment is the systematic process of obtaining and interpreting data to identify nutrition problems, forming the basis for the nutrition diagnosis.', '["Collecting, analyzing, and interpreting data to determine a nutrition-related problem","Option B","Planning and documenting diet prescriptions for the patient","Providing individualized counseling sessions"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-29T10:45:52.579Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T10:45:52.579Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.026Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T10:45:52.905Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373102252-4', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788372990381-1790433139833-43li1', 'During nutrition assessment, you observe muscle wasting, temporal wasting, and poor skin turgor. These findings fall under which category?', 'Nutrition-focused physical findings', 'A nutrition-focused physical exam identifies physical signs of malnutrition such as muscle loss, fat depletion, and micronutrient deficiencies.', '["Nutrition-focused physical findings","Food and nutrition-related history","Biochemical data","Anthropometrics"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-29T10:45:27.007Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T10:45:27.007Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.026Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T10:45:27.326Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373123708-5', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788372990381-1790433139833-43li1', 'A 28-year-old pregnant woman reports nausea and vomiting, with', 'At risk for malnutrition', 'Reduced intake plus physical findings of muscle wasting indicate she is at risk and needs close monitoring/intervention.', '["At risk for malnutrition","Adequate intake, no problem","Option C","Normal pregnancy symptoms only"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-29T10:45:39.857Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T10:45:39.857Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.026Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T10:45:40.175Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373146879-6', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788372990381-1790433139833-43li1', '"Unintentional weight loss related to hypermetabolism secondary to cancer as evidenced by 10% weight loss in 6 months". Which diagnosis domain is this?', 'Clinical', 'Clinical domain covers weight changes, biochemical values, physical findings influenced by disease or condition.', '["Clinical","Intake","None of the above","Behavioral-Environmental"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-29T10:46:10.942Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T10:46:10.942Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.026Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T10:46:11.249Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373171785-7', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788372990381-1790433139833-43li1', 'Which of the following is NOT a correct PES statement?', 'Hypertension related to age as evidenced by 160/100 mmHg', 'Age is not a modifiable nutrition-related etiology. PES statements must link to nutrition problems the dietitian can address.', '["Hypertension related to age as evidenced by 160/100 mmHg","Inadequate oral intake related to poor appetite as evidenced by","Altered nutrition-related laboratory values related to uncontrolled diabetes as evidenced by FBS 300 mg/dL","Impaired nutrient utilization related to pancreatic insufficiency as evidenced by steatorrhea"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-29T10:45:19.540Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T10:45:19.540Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.026Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T10:45:19.858Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373197171-8', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788372990381-1790433139833-43li1', 'What is the best nutrition diagnosis?', 'Impaired nutrient utilization related to liver dysfunction as evidenced by steatorrhea', 'Cirrhosis affects nutrient metabolism/absorption.', '["Impaired nutrient utilization related to liver dysfunction as evidenced by steatorrhea","Inadequate energy intake related to poor appetite as evidenced by weight loss","Inadequate oral intake related to ascites as evidenced by early satiety","Option D"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-29T10:46:06.229Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T10:46:06.229Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.026Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T10:46:06.552Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373220308-9', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788372990381-1790433139833-43li1', 'Which of the following is NOT a category of outcomes monitored in the NCP?', 'Nutrition diagnosis statement', 'The nutrition diagnosis is not an outcome—it is a problem statement.', '["Nutrition diagnosis statement","Food/nutrition-related history","Anthropometric measurements","Biochemical data & medical tests"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-29T10:46:01.522Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T10:46:01.522Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.026Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T10:46:01.856Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373375295-0', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788373344910-1790433142628-l4qb7', 'During a nutrition education session, a school-age child states, ''I don''t like vegetables, so I''ve never tried broccoli.'' When offered steamed broccoli once, she refused it immediately. Her parent conclude the child will never accept vegetables and stops offering them. From a developmental and behavioral nutrition perspective, what is the most significant error in the parent''s reasoning?', 'Research demonstrates that children typically require 8 - 10 exposures to new foods before acceptance; one exposure is insufficient to establish a lasting food preference, and repeated exposure with positive reinforcement is necessary', '', '["The child simply lacks motivation to try new foods; if she wanted to eat vegetables, she would accept them on first offering","Because children naturally prefer sweet and salty tastes, they are biologically incapable of developing preferences for bitter or mild-flavored vegetables","Research demonstrates that children typically require 8 - 10 exposures to new foods before acceptance; one exposure is insufficient to establish a lasting food preference, and repeated exposure with positive reinforcement is necessary","Children''s taste preferences are genetically determined at birth; environmental exposure has minimal influence on food acceptance"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:41:11.621Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:41:11.621Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.825Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:41:12.001Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373396201-1', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788373344910-1790433142628-l4qb7', 'A 9-year-old boy presents with poor appetite and frequent school absences. Upon assessment, you discover he participates in multiple after-school activities with minimal rest periods. His parents report he skips breakfast regularly and often trades his packed lunch with classmates. Based on nutritional assessment principles for school-age children, which intervention would most effectively address the root cause of his inadequate nutrient intake?', 'Educate the family on balancing academic, physical, and rest activities while establishing a structured meal schedule that includes breakfast and monitored lunch consumption', '', '["Educate the family on balancing academic, physical, and rest activities while establishing a structured meal schedule that includes breakfast and monitored lunch consumption","Increase the frequency and variety of sweets in packed lunches to make them more appealing and less likely to be traded","Restrict the child''s participation in after-school activities until appetite improves and weight gains are documented","Recommend high-calorie nutritional supplements to compensate for missed meals and increase overall energy intake"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:37:57.093Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:37:57.093Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.825Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:37:57.409Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373417625-2', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788373344910-1790433142628-l4qb7', 'You are counseling the parents of an 8-year-old girl who exhibits early signs of body image concerns and requests to begin dieting despite having a normal BMI for her age. Her mother mentions she had struggles with her own weight as a child. Considering the developmental context and evidence on feeding practices, what is the most appropriate nutrition counseling approach?', 'Counsel parents to avoid restrictive feeding practices, emphasize normal body changes during preadolescence, and model positive attitudes toward food and body image', '', '["Counsel parents to avoid restrictive feeding practices, emphasize normal body changes during preadolescence, and model positive attitudes toward food and body image","Suggest the family focus exclusively on increasing physical activity without addressing dietary or psychological concerns","Recommend comprehensive metabolic testing and micronutrient supplementation to address potential nutritional imbalances","Support the family''s dieting approach and implement calorie-restricted meal plans to prevent future obesity"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:30:00.669Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:30:00.669Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.825Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:30:01.209Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373443628-3', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788373344910-1790433142628-l4qb7', 'A school nutrition program is evaluating its canteen offerings. Currently, 60% of items sold fall into the RED category (high sodium, sugar, and saturated fat). The program director argues that removing these items will reduce canteen revenue and student satisfaction. Using principles of nutrition assessment and public health nutrition, which evidence-based argument best supports the need for menu revision?', 'The current menu contradicts the school''s nutrition education mission and contributes to rising childhood obesity and overweight trends documented in surveillance data, undermining long-term student health outcomes', '', '["Menu changes in a single school canteen will have negligible impact on regional obesity trends, so revision is not justified","Students who choose unhealthy foods are responsible for their own health outcomes; the school should not restrict their autonomy","The canteen''s financial sustainability is more important than menu composition; student preferences should determine food availability","The current menu contradicts the school''s nutrition education mission and contributes to rising childhood obesity and overweight trends documented in surveillance data, undermining long-term student health outcomes"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:23:41.752Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:23:41.752Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.825Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:23:42.280Z"'::jsonb)
