('anki-card-1788423489542-13', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'The desired product of jelly making is generally a:', 'Clear, firm gel', 'By culinary and food science standards, a perfect jelly must be a clear, sparkling liquid that has been trapped in a firm, shimmering gel network. It should hold its shape when turned out of a container but remain tender enough to cut or spoon easily.

This specific texture is achieved through the precise chemical balance of three structural elements: pectin (the gelling agent), acid (which prompts the pectin to form a network), and sugar (which bonds with water to assist the pectin).

• Thick emulsion: This describes a mixture of two unmixable liquids, like oil and water (e.g., mayonnaise or hollandaise sauce).
• Foamy suspension: This is a mixture of gas bubbles trapped in a liquid or solid (e.g., whipped cream or meringue). In fact, foam is an undesirable byproduct in jelly making that must be skimmed off during boiling.
• Crystalline sugar mass: This occurs when a jelly fails, and the sugar recrystallizes, resulting in a gritty, grainy texture instead of a smooth gel.', '["Clear, firm gel","Thick emulsion","Foamy suspension","Crystalline sugar mass"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:44:27.651Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:44:27.651Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:44:27.651Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788423528755-14', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Carotenoid pigments are generally:', 'Relatively stable to mild acid compared with chlorophyll', 'Compared with chlorophyll, carotenoids are relatively stable to mild acid conditions. They contain around 40 carbon backbone, atleast 8 isoprene units.

• Carotenoids are not generally destroyed immediately by mild acid.
• Acid does not convert carotenoids into chlorophyll. These are two completely different structures.
• Chlorophyll, not carotenoids, is primarily responsible for green vegetable color.', '["Relatively stable to mild acid compared with chlorophyll","Highly destroyed immediately by mild acid","Responsible for green vegetable color","Converted into chlorophyll by acid"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:43:36.813Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:43:36.813Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:43:36.813Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788423566053-15', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Which food is a well-known source of lycopene?', 'Tomato', 'Lycopene is a powerful antioxidant and a bright red carotenoid hydrocarbon.

Tomatoes and tomato-based products (like tomato paste, ketchup, and sauces) are the most abundant dietary sources of lycopene. Interestingly, cooking tomatoes and combining them with a little fat (like olive oil) actually increases the bioavailability of lycopene, making it easier for the body to absorb.

• Cauliflower - glucosinolates because cruciferous (sulfur + nitrogen)
• Cabbage - glucosinolates because cruciferous (sulfur + nitrogen)
• Potato - carbohydrates', '["Tomato","Potato","Cauliflower","Cabbage"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:32:02.251Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:32:02.251Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:32:02.251Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788423597450-16', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Which vitamin is particularly susceptible to losses during food processing?', 'Vitamin C', 'Vitamin C is highly sensitive to heat, oxygen, and water and is readily lost during some processing methods.

• Vitamin D is generally more stable under ordinary food-processing conditions.
• Vitamin K is not typically identified as the vitamin most susceptible to processing losses in this context.
• Vitamin B12 can also be lost during cooking but is more heat-tolerant', '["Vitamin C","Vitamin B12","Vitamin D","Vitamin K"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:42:55.627Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:42:55.627Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:42:55.627Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788423629355-17', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Chevon refers to meat from:', 'Goat', 'Chevon is the official culinary term for the meat of an adult goat. It comes from the French word for goat, chèvre.

You may also see young goat meat referred to as cabrito or simply called mutton in certain regions (like India and parts of Asia), though in formal culinary terms, mutton belongs to another animal.

• Sheep meat is commonly called mutton (2-3yo) or lamb 
• Deer meat is commonly called venison.
• Rabbit meat is usually referred to simply as rabbit or lapan (in some culinary contexts).', '["Goat","Sheep","Rabbit","Deer"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:32:31.521Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:32:31.521Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:32:31.521Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788423684095-18', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Which of the following is a recommended minimum internal temperature for cooked seafood?', '145°F', 'According to USDA Food Safety and Inspection Service

• All Poultry: 165°F (74°C) for whole birds, breasts, legs, thighs, wings, and ground poultry.
• Stuffing & Casseroles: 165°F (74°C).
• Leftovers: 165°F (74°C) to reheat thoroughly.
• Ground Meats: 160°F (71°C) for beef, pork, veal, and lamb. 
• Egg Dishes: 160°F (71°C) for frittatas and quiches.
• Beef, Pork, Veal, and Lamb: 145°F (63°C) for steaks, chops, and roasts, followed by a 3-minute rest time.
• Fish and Shellfish: 145°F (63°C) or until the flesh is opaque and flakes easily.', '["145°F","125°F","135°F","165°F"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:41:56.549Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:41:56.549Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:41:56.549Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788423717984-19', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'A fish with its viscera removed but its head, fins, and tail retained is described as:', 'Drawn', 'A drawn fish is a whole fish that has had only its internal organs (viscera or entrails) removed. The head, fins, scales, and tail all remain completely intact.

• A whole fish has not had the viscera removed.
• A dressed fish has undergone additional preparation beyond simply drawing. A fish that has been drawn, but has also had its head, tail, fins, and scales completely removed.
• A filleted fish has the flesh separated from the bones, usually into fillets. The boneless side of a fish cut lengthwise away from the backbone.', '["Drawn","Whole","Fillet","Dressed"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:35:41.856Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:35:41.856Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:35:41.856Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788423788676-20', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Which of the statements is correct:', 'Balut is a fertilized duck egg that has been incubated before cooking', 'Balut is a famous Filipino street food consisting of a fertilized duck egg. It is traditionally incubated in heated rice husks for roughly 14 to 21 days (usually 18 days) to allow a semi-developed duck embryo to form inside before it is hard-boiled or steamed.

Penoy: is an unfertilized duck egg that is boiled and consumed. It does not contain a developing duck embryo.', '["Balut is a fertilized duck egg that has been incubated before cooking","Balut is an unfertilized duck egg","Penoy is a fertilized duck egg that has been incubated before cooking","Penoy is a fertilized chicken egg"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:34:54.267Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:34:54.267Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:34:54.267Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788423858680-21', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'TRUE OR FALSE: Mutton (meat of an older sheep) is lighter in color and flavor than the lamb.', 'FALSE', 'Why Mutton is Darker
• Myoglobin buildup: Older animals have muscles that work for years. This increases myoglobin, the protein that stores oxygen in muscle tissue and turns red meat dark.
• Diet accumulation: Years of grazing on grass and forage deposit rich nutrients and minerals into the animal''s muscle and fat tissues.

Why Mutton is More Flavorful
• Fat and fatty acids: Mutton develops a higher concentration of species-specific fatty acids and heavier fat deposits that carry a robust, earthy, and gamey taste.
• Mature muscle chemistry: As the sheep ages, the chemical compounds responsible for deep savory flavors multiply and concentrate, moving past the mild and milky taste profile of young lamb.', '["TRUE","FALSE"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:34:31.232Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:34:31.232Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:34:31.232Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788423894307-22', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Which condition can cause milk proteins to coagulate?', 'Acidification', 'Lowering milk pH through acidification can cause milk proteins, particularly casein, to coagulate.

• Freezing alone does not describe the usual mechanism of milk-protein coagulation. 
• Homogenization reduces fat globule size and does not itself cause the described coagulation.
• Refrigeration alone does not normally coagulate milk proteins.', '["Acidification","Refrigeration","Freezing alone","Homogenization"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:31:42.034Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:31:42.034Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:31:42.034Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788423929024-23', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Which artificial sweetener is associated with phenylketonuria?', 'Aspartame', 'Aspartame is associated with phenylketonuria (PKU) because it contains phenylalanine. Individuals with PKU cannot properly metabolize phenylalanine, so they need to restrict their intake. This is why products containing aspartame carry a warning for people with PKU.', '["Aspartame","Saccharin","Acesulfame-K","Sucralose"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:35:03.781Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:35:03.781Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:35:03.781Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788423963494-24', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Which noodle is traditionally used in lomi?', 'Miki', 'Miki is the thick fresh egg noodle commonly associated with lomi.

• Sotanghon is a glass or cellophane noodle made from mungbean.
• Bihon is a thin rice vermicelli noodle.
• Miswa is a thin wheat noodle and is not the traditional noodle identified for lomi.', '["Miki","Miswa","Sotanghon","Bihon"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:38:01.303Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:38:01.303Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:38:01.303Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788423990077-25', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Which of the following is a microorganism commonly used in bread production?', 'Yeast', 'Yeast, particularly Saccharomyces cerevisiae, is a microorganism commonly used in bread production. It ferments sugars in the dough and produces carbon dioxide (CO₂). The CO₂ becomes trapped within the gluten network, causing the dough to rise and giving bread its characteristic volume and texture.', '["Yeast","Bacteria","Mold","Protozoa"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:36:52.152Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:36:52.152Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:36:52.152Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788424028907-26', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Which of the following is a chemical leavening agent?', 'Baking soda', 'Baking soda is a fine white chemical salt called sodium bicarbonate (NaHCO3). It acts as a base that reacts with acids to create carbon dioxide gas. This reaction makes baked goods rise.

• Yeast is a biological leavening agent.
• Whipped egg white can provide physical aeration rather than chemical leavening.
• Gluten provides structure and gas retention but is not itself a leavening agent.', '["Baking soda","Gluten","Yeast","Egg white"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:44:15.340Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:44:15.340Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:44:15.340Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788424086529-27', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Which of the following is a non-perishable food?', 'Dried beans', 'Dried beans are considered non-perishable foods because their low moisture content allows them to be stored for long periods at room temperature without rapid spoilage, provided they are kept in proper dry-storage conditions.

• Potatoes: semi-perishable; 
• Fresh milk and fresh meat: perishable', '["Dried beans","Potatoes","Fresh milk","Fresh meat"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:32:51.514Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:32:51.514Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:32:51.514Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788424120644-28', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'A cooked mixture of about equal weights of flour and fat used to thicken soups, sauces, and gravies.', 'Roux', 'A roux is the culinary term for a thickener made by cooking equal parts by weight of fat (usually butter) and flour.

It serves as the foundational thickening agent for classic French mother sauces (like Béchamel and Velouté) as well as various soups, stews, and gravies.

• Sherry is a wine.
• White wash is flour + water, not flour + fat.
• Custard is simple base of milk/cream, eggs or egg yolks and sugar.', '["Roux","Custard","Sherry","White wash"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:43:14.014Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:43:14.014Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:43:14.014Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788424144218-29', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'The most suitable wall material for institutional kitchen is:', 'Ceramic Tile', 'Ceramic Tiles are Durable, smooth, and easy to clean.

• Quarry tile is for floors. 
• Fiberglass is not durable.
• Stainless steel is for counters.', '["Ceramic Tile","Stainless steel","Quarry Tile","Fiberglass"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2028-01-27T02:39:01.620Z","interval":448,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":8}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:39:01.620Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:39:01.620Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788424187010-30', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'At higher altitudes, the boiling point of water:', 'Decreases', 'At higher altitudes, atmospheric pressure is lower because there is less air pressing down on the Earth’s surface. A liquid boils when its vapor pressure becomes equal to the surrounding atmospheric pressure.

Therefore: Higher altitude → lower atmospheric pressure → liquid reaches its boiling point at a lower temperature → lower boiling point', '["Decreases","Increases","Cannot be determined","Remains exactly the same"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:38:11.285Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:38:11.285Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:38:11.285Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788424225708-31', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'A common mixing method used to incorporate fat into flour for pie crust is:', 'Cutting in', 'Cutting in distributes solid fat through flour to create the desired pastry texture.

• Creaming is commonly used to incorporate fat and sugar, especially in cakes and cookies.
• Folding is used to gently incorporate ingredients while preserving air or delicate structure.
• Kneading develops gluten and is not the standard method for incorporating fat into pie-crust flour.', '["Cutting in","Creaming","Folding","Kneading"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:40:53.368Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:40:53.368Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:40:53.368Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788424250880-32', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Kneading bread dough is primarily done to:', 'Develop gluten', 'Kneading develops the gluten network that provides structure and elasticity to bread dough.', '["Develop gluten","Option B","Caramelize starch","Prevent fermentation"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:36:57.808Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:36:57.808Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:36:57.808Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788424330423-33', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Apan-apan is traditionally prepared using:', 'Kangkong', 'Apan-apan is a popular Ilonggo vegetable dish from Western Visayas, Philippines. It is a flavorful, savory, and tangy variation of adobong kangkong made with water spinach (kangkong), sautéed garlic, onions, vinegar, soy sauce, and fermented shrimp paste (guinamos or bagoong alamang), often topped with crispy fried pork (tulapho).[Image: Apan-Apan Recipe]', '["Kangkong","Eggplant","Fish","Malunggay"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:38:54.655Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:38:54.655Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-10T01:05:28.255Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788424431218-34', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Which of the following is traditionally served cold?


[Image: Chef John''s Gazpacho]a. Gazpacho
[Image: JB''s Cheese Soufflé - Soufflé au Fromage]b. Soufflé
[Image: Simple French Onion Soup]c. French onion soup
[Image: Chicken Consomme]d. Consommé', 'Gazpacho', 'Gazpacho is a cold soup traditionally served chilled.', '["Gazpacho","Soufflé","French onion soup","Consommé"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2028-01-27T02:44:44.411Z","interval":448,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":8}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:44:44.411Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-10T01:05:28.310Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788424575034-35', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'A vodka-based cocktail made with tomato juice, lemon juice, and hot pepper sauce is:', 'Bloody Mary', '[Image: Bloody Mary Recipe]b. Bloody Mary[Image: Manhattan]A. Manhattan is a whiskey-based cocktail traditionally made with vermouth and bitters. [Image: Gimlet]C. A Gimlet is traditionally made with gin or vodka and lime cordial or lime juice, not tomato juice.[Image: Black Russian]D. A Black Russian is vodka and coffee liqueur.', '["Bloody Mary","Manhattan","Gimlet","Black Russian"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:36:03.640Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:36:03.640Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-10T01:05:28.201Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788424613183-36', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'In pickling, sugar primarily contributes:', 'Sweetness and flavor balance', 'Sugar contributes sweetness and helps balance the sourness and other flavors of pickled foods

• Sugar alone does not guarantee crispness.
• The primary preservation effects in many pickles are associated with acidity and other controlled conditions rather than sugar alone.
• Sugar does not by itself cause fermentation; fermentation depends on microorganisms and suitable conditions.', '["Sweetness and flavor balance","Fermentation","Crispness by itself","The main antimicrobial action"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:30:07.121Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:30:07.121Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:30:07.121Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788424647805-37', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Soft pickles may result from:', 'Weak brine or vinegar and exposure to air', 'Pickles may become soft when the brine or vinegar solution is too weak and/or when the pickles are exposed to air. Exposure to air can contribute to undesirable microbial activity and softening.', '["Weak brine or vinegar and exposure to air","Too much vinegar","Strong vinegar concentration alone","Excessive sugar concentration alone"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:43:44.514Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:43:44.514Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:43:44.514Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788424706022-38', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Which microorganism is associated with lactic acid fermentation?', 'Leuconostoc mesenteroides', 'Leuconostoc mesenteroides is a lactic acid bacterium associated with vegetable fermentations.

• Acetobacter aceti: associated with acetic acid production from ethanol.
• Saccharomyces cerevisiae: yeast associated with alcoholic fermentation.
• Saccharomyces carlsbergensis: yeast associated with lager brewing.', '["Leuconostoc mesenteroides","Saccharomyces carlsbergensis","Acetobacter aceti","Saccharomyces cerevisiae"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:30:00.788Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:30:00.788Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:30:00.788Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788424750385-39', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'The recommended temperature for dry storage is approximately:', '60-70°F', 'About 60–70°F is an appropriate general range for dry storage under controlled conditions.

• 29–33°F is within the range of freezing or near-freezing storage rather than typical dry storage.
• 34–40°F is a refrigerated-storage range.
• 0–10°F is a freezing-storage range.', '["60-70°F","29-33°F","34-40°F","0-10°F"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:30:34.466Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:30:34.466Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:30:34.466Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788424793307-40', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Which sensory test would be most appropriate when the objective is to determine whether panelists can distinguish between two samples based on a specified sensory attribute?', 'Paired comparison', 'Panelists are presented with two samples and asked to compare them with respect to a particular characteristic, such as sweetness, saltiness, tenderness, or intensity of flavor.', '["Paired comparison","Option B","Hedonic scaling","Rank-order"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:44:36.419Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:44:36.419Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:44:36.419Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788424909437-41', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'French restaurateur and father of Classic Cuisine.


[Image: Georges Auguste Escoffier''s culinary legacy]a. Auguste Escoffier
[Image: Marie-Antoine Carême - Simple English Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia]b. Antonin Careme
[Image: Fernand Point Didn''t Create Great Chefs. He Created Great Judgment. | by  Ish Boudrar | Medium]c. Fernand Point
[Image: Gordon Ramsay (@gordonramsay) • Facebook]d. Gordon Ramsay', 'Auguste Escoffier', '• Auguste Escoffier – Modern kitchen system.
• Careme – Known for grand cuisine, earlier era.
• Point – Founder of nouvelle cuisine.
• Ramsay – Modern celebrity chef.', '["Auguste Escoffier","Antonin Careme","Fernand Point","Gordon Ramsay"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2028-01-27T02:34:10.501Z","interval":448,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":8}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:34:10.501Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-10T01:05:28.368Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788424945169-42', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'The strain of E. coli that was initially identified as the cause of bloody diarrhea from eating undercooked or raw hamburger meat that was contaminated with the bacteria in the US in 1982.', 'Escherichia coli O157', 'O157:H7 – Causes bloody diarrhea, linked to hamburger outbreak.

• O111 – Pathogen but not outbreak strain.
• O26 – Also pathogenic, different cases.
• O104:H4 – Later outbreak in Europe.', '["Escherichia coli O157","Escherichia coli O26","Escherichia coli O111","Escherichia coli O104:H4"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:33:02.312Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:33:02.312Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:33:02.312Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788424979180-43', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'A central facility prepares meals in large quantities and distributes the prepared meals to several remote service locations. Which system best fits this arrangement?', 'Commissary system', 'The commissary foodservice system (also referred to as a central kitchen or central production facility) concentrates food procurement and production in a single, large-scale facility.

Once the meals are prepared in bulk, they are packaged and transported to distinct, remote service locations (often called satellite units or receiving kitchens) for final finishing and service.

• À la carte system: A style of menu where items are priced and ordered separately, rather than a production and distribution system.
• Conventional system: The traditional model where food is purchased, prepared from scratch, and served on the same premises.
• Individualized system: A specialized approach focused on custom dietary tailoring (often used in clinical healthcare), not a bulk production and remote distribution network.', '["Conventional system","Commissary system","À la carte system","Individualized system"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:39:32.699Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:39:32.699Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:39:32.699Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788425016078-44', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Under PD 856, the minimum kitchen size for a 40 m² dining area is _____ .', '10 m²', 'According to the Implementing Rules and Regulations (IRR) of Chapter III (Food Establishments) of the Code on Sanitation of the Philippines (Presidential Decree No. 856), the kitchen area must be at least ¼ (25%) of the total dining area, provided it is not less than a base minimum of 9.30 m² (100 sq. ft.).

Calculation: Required Kitchen Size = 40 m² x ¼ = 10 m²

Since 10 m² meets the legal ratio and exceeds the minimum threshold of 9.30 m², it serves as the absolute statutory minimum required floor area for that setup.

• 12 m² – Not prescribed.
• 8 m² – Too small.
• 15 m² – Above requirement.', '["10 m²","12 m²","8 m²","15 m²"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:38:38.861Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:38:38.861Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:38:38.861Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788425044416-45', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Which menu term means "of the day"?', 'Du jour', 'Du jour is a French phrase that literally translates to "of the day".

In restaurants, a du jour menu or item changes daily depending on what fresh ingredients are available or what specials the chef has created (e.g., "Soup du jour" means soup of the day).

• À la cart: Means "by the menu" or "from the menu"; items are listed, ordered, and priced individually.
• Table d''hôte: Means "the host''s table"; it offers a complete, multi-course meal with limited choices at a single fixed price.
• Prix fixe: Means "fixed price"; a set menu where customers pay a predetermined total price for a specific sequence of courses.', '["À la carte","Du jour","Table d''hôte","Prix fixe"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:32:07.253Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:32:07.253Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:32:07.253Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788425080995-46', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Which should be a healthier option of market forms of milk for people who monitor their blood profiles?', 'Toned milk', 'Toned milk – Lower fat but retains protein and calcium, better for heart health.

• Whole milk – High in saturated fat, raises cholesterol.
• Condensed milk – Very high in sugar and fat.
• Evaporated milk – Concentrated, higher fat though no added sugar.', '["Toned milk","Whole milk","Condensed milk","Evaporated milk"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:42:47.383Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:42:47.383Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:42:47.383Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788425368534-47', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Dinuguan of Mindanao with pork intestines, lungs, liver, banana heart, and olasiman', 'Sampayna', '[Image: Sampayna (Dinuguan from Northern Mindanao)” – FoodEverMore]b. Sampayna[Image: Pipian Rojo Recipe (Mexican Red Pipian Sauce)]a. Pipián: historic, rich seed-based sauce/stew originating from Mesoamerica and Mexican cuisine, which also evolved into a distinct PH regional chicken stew[Image: TINUTO is our local laing variant. It is made from fresh young gabi leaves,  coconut cream, grated salted fish meat, lemon grass and chilies. 📸 Ana  Katherine Reyes]c. Tinuto: coconut-based dish from Quezon province and Marinduque, similar to Bicolano laing[Image: Nilaneg - Ang Sarap]d. Nilanega: Filipino soup dish from Batanes and the Cagayan Valley region, made with broiled fresh fish and pork liver simmered in a savory bagoong broth along with local vegetables', '["Sampayna","Pipian","Tinuto","Nilaneg"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:33:34.828Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:33:34.828Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-10T01:05:28.038Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788425462860-48', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Which equipment provides gentle indirect heating through hot water and is commonly used to keep foods warm?


[Image: Electric Salamander - Merit Stainless Steel]a. Salamander
[Image: 6-Basket Electric Bain Marie – Eco Prima Home and Commercial Kitchen Supply]b. Bain-marie
[Image: Why Outdoor Griddle Cooking Is Changing the Game for Foodies | Outeriors]c. Griddle
[Image: Your Convection Oven Cooking Questions Answered | Stubbe''s BrandSource Home  Furnishings]d. Convection oven', 'Bain-marie', 'A bain-marie (also called a water bath) consists of an outer container filled with heated water and an inner container filled with food. The hot water surrounds the inner container, providing gentle, indirect, and uniform heat. This prevents delicate foods (like sauces or custards) from burning or curdling and is widely used in food service buffet lines to keep pre-cooked foods safely warm.

• A salamander is a high-heat broiling or finishing unit.
• A griddle provides direct dry heat through a heated surface.
• A convection oven uses circulating hot air for cooking or baking.', '["Bain-marie","Salamander","Griddle","Convection oven"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2028-01-27T02:37:19.655Z","interval":448,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":8}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:37:19.655Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-10T01:05:28.424Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788425488824-49', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Which organization, together with WHO, established the Codex Alimentarius Commission?', 'FAO', 'The Codex Alimentarius Commission (CAC) was established in 1963 as a joint initiative between the Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) of the United Nations and the World Health Organization (WHO).

Together, they created the Codex Alimentarius (Latin for "Food Code") to protect consumer health globally and promote fair, harmonized practices in international food trade.', '["FAO","WTO","UNICEF","UNESCO"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:31:31.895Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:31:31.895Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:31:31.895Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788425572314-50', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'A manager finds that one leadership approach is effective with one employee but ineffective with another because their abilities, motivation, and work circumstances differ. Which approach recognizes that management practices should be adapted to the situation?', 'Contingency approach', 'The contingency approach holds that effective management depends on the situation and circumstances.

• Scientific management: systematic analysis of work and efficiency
• Bureaucratic management: formal structure, rules, and authority
• Classical management: broad principles of structure and efficiency', '["Contingency approach","Scientific management","Classical management","Bureaucratic approach"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:32:43.380Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:32:43.380Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:32:43.380Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788425608364-51', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'A foodservice job posting specifies that applicants must have a bachelor''s degree, two years of supervisory experience, and specific technical competencies. These requirements are examples of:', 'Job specification', 'A job specification identifies the qualifications, experience, skills, and competencies required of the person performing the job.', '["Job specification","Job description","Job skills","Job evaluation"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:31:51.282Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:31:51.282Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:31:51.282Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788425643449-52', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'The shortage of potatoes due to the war between Russia and Ukraine has an impact on the production of this known alcoholic beverage.', 'Vodka', 'Vodka –  While vodka can be distilled from various grains (like wheat or rye), potatoes are historically and traditionally one of its primary, iconic raw base ingredients.

• Gin: Typically distilled from a grain mash (like wheat or barley) and flavored heavily with juniper berries.
• Rum: Distilled exclusively from sugarcane byproducts, such as molasses or sugarcane juice.
• Brandy: Produced by distilling wine or fermented fruit mashes (most commonly grapes).

• Beer – Made from barley and hops.
• Wine – Made from grapes.
• Sake – Made from rice.', '["Vodka","Brandy","Gin","Rum"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:42:39.891Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:42:39.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:42:39.891Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788425895111-53', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'A picture shows four pieces of institutional kitchen equipment. Which equipment would be most appropriate for large-volume soup production?


[Image: Electric Salamander - Merit Stainless Steel]a. Salamander
[Image: Industrial Food Steam Jacket Kettle 200L Cooking Kettle]b. Steam-jacketed kettle
[Image: 6-Basket Electric Bain Marie – Eco Prima Home and Commercial Kitchen Supply]c. Bain-marie
[Image: Why Outdoor Griddle Cooking Is Changing the Game for Foodies | Outeriors]d. Griddle', 'Steam-jacketed kettle', '• Salamander: primarily used for broiling or finishing foods.
• Bain-marie: suited to gentle heating or holding rather than primary large-volume soup production.
• Griddle: designed for direct cooking on a heated flat surface.', '["Steam-jacketed kettle","Bain-marie","Griddle","Salamander"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2029-08-31T02:43:57.734Z","interval":1030,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":9}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:43:57.734Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-10T01:05:28.479Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788425959275-54', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Compute the percent shrinkage of pork kasim if the raw weight is 850 g and the cooked weight is 600 g.', '29%', 'Formula: (raw weight - cooked weight) / raw weight * 100
= (850–600 ÷ 850) × 100 = 29%', '["29%","25%","31%","33%"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:41:05.215Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:41:05.215Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:41:05.215Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788426090282-55', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Which of the following is not one of the five classical French mother sauces?


[Image: Basic Béchamel Sauce]a. Béchamel
[Image: Classic Velouté Sauce (French Mother Sauce)]b. Velouté
[Image: Hollandaise Sauce]c. Hollandaise
[Image: Best Marinara Sauce Yet]d. Marinara', 'Marinara', 'The five classical French mother sauces codified by chef Auguste Escoffier:Bechamel, Veloute, Espagnole, Tomato, Hollandaise

These foundational recipes use a liquid combined with a thickening agent (like a roux or emulsion) to create dozens of secondary "daughter" sauces.', '["Marinara","Hollandaise","Velouté","Béchamel"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2028-01-27T02:43:28.032Z","interval":448,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":8}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:43:28.032Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-10T01:05:28.146Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788426139224-56', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'According to the updated Labor Code (RA 11360) of the Philippines, what percent of the service charge goes to the management?', '0%', 'Under Republic Act No. 11360, which amended Article 96 of the Labor Code, 100% of the service charges are distributed among covered employees, excluding managerial employees from the distribution. Thus, management receives 0% as a statutory share. 

Historical Context 
• Old Rule (Pre-2019): Under the original text of Article 96 of the Labor Code, 85% went to the employees and 15% was retained by management.
• New Rule (2019 Onward): The 15% management share was completely removed, making the employee share 100%.', '["0%","20%","15%","30%"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:30:45.610Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:30:45.610Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:30:45.610Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788426167715-57', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'Which statement best describes ergonomics in foodservice facility design?', 'Designing workstations to fit workers and promote safe, efficient performance', 'Ergonomics applies human capabilities and limitations to workplace design to improve safety, comfort, and efficiency.', '["Designing workstations to fit workers and promote safe, efficient performance","Option B","Designing menus according to customer preferences","Designing storage systems according to food cost"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:30:52.454Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:30:52.454Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:30:52.454Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788426324208-58', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', '[Image: Diagram]A diagram shows a server approaching a seated guest with a beverage. According to conventional service, from which side should the beverage generally be served?', 'Guest''s right', 'In conventional table service, beverages are generally served from the guest’s right side. The server should approach carefully without reaching across the guest and place the beverage on the table from the right. 

• Guest’s left: generally associated with serving certain foods, particularly when food is presented from a platter.', '["Guest''s right","Guest''s left","Directly from the back","Directly from the front"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:31:00.959Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:31:00.959Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-10T01:05:28.092Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788426348673-59', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788422977034-1791992590890-w1g2h', 'A foodservice manager wants to reduce the risk of microbial growth in cooked food during preparation, holding, and service. Which practice best demonstrates proper time-temperature control?', 'Monitoring food temperatures and minimizing the time food remains at unsafe temperatures', 'Foodborne pathogens multiply rapidly in the Temperature Danger Zone, which is between 41°F and 135°F (5°C to 57°C).

Proper time-temperature control for safety (TCS) requires food managers to constantly measure temperatures using food thermometers and ensure that foods move through or stay out of this danger zone as quickly as possible to prevent dangerous microbial growth.', '["Monitoring food temperatures and minimizing the time food remains at unsafe temperatures","Checking on appearance and odor to determine whether food is safe","Storing cooked food to remain at room temperature until needed","Keeping all foods at the same temperature regardless of whether they are served hot or cold to save storage space"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T02:39:16.437Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:39:16.437Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T15:43:12.925Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T02:39:16.437Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788430350716-0', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788430296776-1790433145942-55yvl', 'A foodservice operation uses the following inventory data:
• Beginning inventory = ₱25,000
• Purchases = ₱95,000
• Ending inventory = ₱20,000
• Spoilage = ₱4,000
If spoilage is recorded as food used rather than inventory remaining, what is the adjusted food cost including spoilage?', '₱104,000', 'Cost of food used:

₱25,000 + ₱95,000 − ₱20,000 = ₱100,000

Adding spoilage: ₱100,000 + ₱4,000 = ₱104,000 (Spoilage can significantly affect food cost)', '["₱104,000","₱96,000","₱100,000","₱90,000"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-14T13:06:09.460Z","interval":16,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T13:06:09.460Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.599Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T13:06:09.645Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788430372237-1', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788430296776-1790433145942-55yvl', 'A hospital prepares large batches of entrées in a centralized production area. The food is cooked, portioned, rapidly chilled, stored under refrigeration for several days, and reheated shortly before being served to patients. Which foodservice system is best described by this operation?', 'Ready-prepared system', 'In a ready-prepared system, food is prepared in advance, then chilled or frozen for storage and subsequently reheated and served. The key distinguishing feature is the time separation between production and service.', '["Ready-prepared system","Conventional system","Assembly-serve system","Commissary system"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-28T15:39:22.587Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:39:22.587Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.599Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:39:22.587Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788430407123-2', NULL, 'anki-deck-1788430296776-1790433145942-55yvl', 'A hospital is designing a menu for patients requiring therapeutic diets. The menu committee wants to ensure that meals are nutritionally appropriate while also considering food preferences, cultural acceptability, cost, and production capabilities.', 'Integrate nutritional, operational, economic, and patient-related considerations.', 'Effective institutional menu planning requires balancing nutritional adequacy, acceptability, cost, availability, equipment, labor, and therapeutic requirements.', '["Integrate nutritional, operational, economic, and patient-related considerations.","Design the menu based primarily on ingredient cost.","Use the same menu for all patients to simplify production.","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-28T15:41:52.836Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:41:52.836Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.599Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:41:52.836Z"'::jsonb)
