('card-cphn-2019-197', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'Situation 7 - In a community Cee, the number of underfive children is 250.
About 100 children have weight - for - age Z score ≤-2SD; 50 have > 2 SD; 60 had +- SD; about 80 have height -for-age <2SD and 40 had > 2SD.

What is the prevalence of children with normal weight?', '20%', 'Situation 7 Question 2: In the problem vignette, the counts are: 100 (WFA <= -2 SD), 50 (WFA > 2 SD), and 60 (+- SD). On the exam key, option C (20%) is marked, which corresponds to (50 / 250) * 100 = 20%. Note: The examinee/exam key mapped 50 / 250 = 20% to normal weight and 60 / 250 = 24% to overweight in Item 198.', '["20%","A. 30%","B. 40%","C. 20%"]'::jsonb, '["Situation 7","Prevalence Calculation","Normal Weight","Nutritional Status"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, 'Exam paper circled C (20%). Notice how the exam options paired 20% (50/250) for this question and 24% (60/250) for Item 198.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T05:50:46.951Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:50:46.951Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:50:46.951Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-198', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'Situation 7 - In a community Cee, the number of underfive children is 250.
About 100 children have weight - for - age Z score ≤-2SD; 50 have > 2 SD; 60 had +- SD; about 80 have height -for-age <2SD and 40 had > 2SD.

What is the prevalence of overweight?', '24%', 'Situation 7 Question 3: In the question structure, the remaining weight category gives (60 / 250) * 100 = 24.0%. Option D (24%) is marked on the examination paper.', '["24%","A. 40%","B. 50 %","C. 30%"]'::jsonb, '["Situation 7","Prevalence Calculation","Overweight","Nutritional Assessment"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, 'Exam paper circled D (24%). Calculation: 60 / 250 = 24%. Margin note: ''overweight''.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T05:58:13.525Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:58:13.525Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:58:13.525Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-199', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'Situation 7 - In a community Cee, the number of underfive children is 250.
About 100 children have weight - for - age Z score ≤-2SD; 50 have > 2 SD; 60 had +- SD; about 80 have height -for-age <2SD and 40 had > 2SD.

What is the prevalence of stunting?', '32%', 'Situation 7 Question 4: Stunting is defined by height-for-age Z-score < -2 SD. The vignette indicates that 80 children have height-for-age < 2SD (stunted). Total population = 250. Prevalence of stunting = (80 / 250) * 100% = 32.0%.', '["32%","A. 28%","B. 30%","C. 45%"]'::jsonb, '["Situation 7","Prevalence Calculation","Stunting","Epidemiology"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled D (32%). Calculation: (80 / 250) * 100 = 32%. Margin note: ''stunting''.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T05:46:54.299Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:46:54.299Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:46:54.299Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-2', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'What is the step in program planning where it involves identifying approaches necessary for the implementation of the program?', 'defining strategies', 'Strategy formulation involves selecting the broad courses of action, methods, and intervention pathways (e.g., direct feeding, fortification, social behavioral change communication) necessary to achieve defined program goals and objectives.', '["A. defining the problem","B. field networking","C. evaluation","D. defining strategies"]'::jsonb, '["Program Planning","Strategy Formulation","Intervention Design"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled D. Defining strategies bridges problem analysis/objective setting with detailed tactical activities.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T05:33:18.634Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:33:18.634Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:33:18.634Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-20', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'The PPAN has ________ projects serving as a framework for actions that could be undertaken by member agencies of the National Nutrition Council and other agencies.', '46', 'The Philippine Plan of Action for Nutrition (PPAN 2017–2022) operational matrix encompasses 46 distinct projects structured across 12 strategic programs (8 nutrition-specific, 1 nutrition-sensitive, and 3 enabling support programs) executed by NNC member agencies and local government units.', '["A. 30","B. 46","C. 25","D. 36"]'::jsonb, '["PPAN","Nutrition Policy","NNC Programs"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, 'Exam paper circled B. Remember PPAN numbers: 12 Programs, 46 Projects. See also Item 143.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T06:07:42.918Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:07:42.918Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:07:42.918Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-200', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'Situation 7 - In a community Cee, the number of underfive children is 250.
About 100 children have weight - for - age Z score ≤-2SD; 50 have > 2 SD; 60 had +- SD; about 80 have height -for-age <2SD and 40 had > 2SD.

What is the prevalence of tallness?', '16%', 'Situation 7 Question 5: Tallness is defined by height-for-age Z-score > +2 SD. The vignette states that 40 children had height-for-age > 2SD. Total population = 250. Prevalence of tallness = (40 / 250) * 100% = 16.0%.', '["16%","A. 16%","B. 32%","C. 24%"]'::jsonb, '["Situation 7","Prevalence Calculation","Tallness","Height-for-Age"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled A (16%). Calculation: (40 / 250) * 100 = 16%. Margin note: ''tallness''.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T05:27:45.945Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:27:45.945Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:27:45.945Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-21', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'The nutrient that aids in the absorption of calcium in any stage of life is', 'Vitamin D', 'Vitamin D, converted to its biologically active hormonal form 1,25-dihydroxyvitamin D3 [calcitriol], stimulates the synthesis of calcium-binding proteins (calbindin-D9k) in the intestinal enterocytes, thereby facilitating active calcium and phosphorus absorption.', '["A. Riboflavin","B. Vitamin B12","C. Vitamin A","D. Vitamin D"]'::jsonb, '["Micronutrients","Vitamin D","Calcium Absorption","Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled D. Calcitriol (active Vitamin D) is indispensable for intestinal calcium and phosphorus absorption.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T05:37:16.760Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:37:16.760Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:37:16.760Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-22', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'The current body status of a person or population groups related to their state of consumption and utilization of foods is ________', 'Nutritional status', 'Nutritional Status is defined as the physiological condition of an individual or population resulting from the balance between nutrient intake, bioavailability, cellular utilization, and biological expenditure/losses.', '["A. Weight for age z - score","B. Weight for height z-score","C. Body mass index","D. Nutritional status"]'::jsonb, '["Nutrition Assessment","Nutritional Status","Public Health Principles"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled D. BMI and Z-scores are indices/metrics used to assess nutritional status, but the overarching physiological state is Nutritional Status.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T05:29:13.409Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:29:13.409Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:29:13.409Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-23', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'This pertains to the category of variables that can be measured using either the interval or ordinal scale of measurement.', 'Categorical', 'In research methodology and biostatistics, variables are classified into continuous/quantitative or categorical/qualitative scales. Ordinal variables represent ordered qualitative categories (e.g., mild, moderate, severe malnutrition). On the test paper, D is marked.', '["A. Hypothesis","B. Continuous","C. Research question","D. Categorical"]'::jsonb, '["Biostatistics","Research Methodology","Scales of Measurement"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, 'Exam paper circled D (Categorical). Note: Scales of measurement: Nominal (labels), Ordinal (ordered ranks), Interval (equal intervals without absolute zero), Ratio (true zero).', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T04:58:30.590Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T04:58:30.590Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T04:58:30.590Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-24', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'What is the term used to the monosaccharides and disaccharides added to foods and beverages by the manufacturer, cook or consumer, and these sugars naturally present in honey, syrups, fruit juices and fruit juice concentrates?', 'Free sugars', 'The World Health Organization (WHO 2015 Guideline) defines ''Free sugars'' as all monosaccharides and disaccharides added to foods and beverages by the manufacturer, cook, or consumer, plus sugars naturally present in honey, syrups, fruit juices, and fruit juice concentrates. WHO recommends free sugar intake be less than 10% (and ideally <5%) of total daily energy intake.', '["A. Free sugars","B. D-glucose","C. D-fructose","D. Sucrose and D-fructose"]'::jsonb, '["WHO Guidelines","Free Sugars","Dietary Guidelines","NCD Prevention"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, 'Exam paper circled A. Intrinsic sugars (in whole fresh fruits/vegetables) and milk sugars (lactose) are NOT free sugars.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T05:48:42.899Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:48:42.899Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:48:42.899Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-25', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'Children put to the breast within 1 hour after birth is called', 'early initiation of breastfeeding', 'WHO, UNICEF, and the Philippine Essential Intrapartum and Newborn Care (EINC / Unang Yakap) protocol define Early Initiation of Breastfeeding as putting the newborn to the mother''s breast within the first hour of delivery. This ensures colostrum intake and stimulates maternal oxytocin/prolactin.', '["A. continued breastfeeding","B. early initiation of breastfeeding","C. exclusive breastfeeding","D. delayed initiation of breastfeeding"]'::jsonb, '["Breastfeeding","IYCF","EINC","Early Initiation"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled B. Early initiation: within 1 hour; Exclusive breastfeeding: breast milk only for 6 months; Continued breastfeeding: up to 2 years or beyond.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T06:00:54.293Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:00:54.293Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:00:54.293Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-26', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'This refers to the skills, supporting knowledge and professional values necessary to begin independent professional practice?', 'Professional competence', 'Professional Competence refers to the integrated capability of applying foundational knowledge, clinical/technical skills, critical judgment, and ethical values required to perform health and nutrition services safely and independently.', '["A. Professional competence","B. Good attitude","C. Integrity","D. Knowledge based practice"]'::jsonb, '["Professional Practice","Competence","PRC Standards"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled A. Governed by PRC Professional Regulatory Board of Nutrition and Dietetics standards.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T04:58:09.529Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T04:58:09.529Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T04:58:09.529Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-27', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'The sustainable development goal considers ________ as an indicator of inadequate food intake and frequent attacks of illness.', 'underweight', 'Historically under the MDGs (Target 1.C) and continued in SDG tracking frameworks, Underweight (low weight-for-age) serves as a classic composite indicator reflecting both acute food deprivation and recurrent infectious illnesses. (Note: Stunting reflects chronic deprivation, wasting reflects acute wasting).', '["A. stunting","B. underweight","C. wasting","D. overweight"]'::jsonb, '["SDGs","Nutrition Indicators","Underweight","Global Goals"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, 'Exam paper circled B (underweight). Weight-for-age captures both chronic and acute insults.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T06:28:17.337Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:28:17.337Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:28:17.337Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-28', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'What is the measure that assess the benefits of interventions vis-a-vis cost?', 'Effectiveness', 'In health economics and program evaluation, cost-effectiveness analysis assesses the outcomes or benefits achieved relative to monetary costs expended. On the exam paper, option A is marked. In standard evaluation terminology, efficiency also assesses inputs/costs relative to outputs.', '["A. Effectiveness","B. Efforts","C. Efficiency","D. Relevance"]'::jsonb, '["Program Evaluation","Health Economics","Cost Effectiveness"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, 'Exam paper circled A. Margin handwritten note: ''-> Face to face''. Cost-effectiveness weighs cost per unit of health benefit gained.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T05:56:46.952Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:56:46.952Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:56:46.952Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-29', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'Which of the following aims to improve current dietary practices to prevent diet-related public health problems in line with current scientific knowledge?', 'Nutritional Guidelines for Filipinos', 'The Nutritional Guidelines for Filipinos (NGF), revised by an inter-agency technical working group led by FNRI-DOST, is a set of primary dietary recommendations designed to foster healthy lifestyles, ensure nutritional adequacy, and prevent non-communicable diseases and nutritional deficiencies.', '["A. Green Banner Award","B. FIVIMS","C. Nutritional Guidelines for Filipinos","D. Food Composition Table"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Guidelines for Filipinos","FNRI","Public Health Nutrition"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled C. NGF consists of 10 messages (10 Kumainments for popular advocacy).', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T05:34:19.933Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:34:19.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:34:19.933Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-3', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'The continual monitoring - in a community, region or country - of factors or conditions that indicate, relate to or impinge on the nutritional status of individuals or groups of people is called', 'nutrition surveillance', 'According to the WHO and the National Nutrition Council (NNC), Nutrition Surveillance is the continuous and systematic collection, analysis, interpretation, and dissemination of nutritional and related socio-economic data to guide ongoing policy, program planning, and resource management.', '["A. nutrition surveillance","B. anthropometry","C. height measurement","D. weight taking"]'::jsonb, '["Nutrition Surveillance","Public Health Monitoring","NNC Protocols"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled A. Note the distinction between surveillance (continuous tracking for policy/action) and periodic surveys (one-time snapshots).', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T05:47:38.818Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:47:38.818Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:47:38.818Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-30', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'What is the IBW (in grams) of a 8 month - old infant who has a birth-weight of 2 kgs?', '6000', 'Philippine pediatric nutrition formula for infant Ideal Body Weight (IBW): IBW (in g) = (Age in months * 500) + Birth Weight (in g). For an 8-month-old infant with birth weight 2000 g: IBW = (8 * 500) + 2000 = 4000 + 2000 = 6000 grams.', '["A. 8500","B. 6000","C. 6500","D. 7500"]'::jsonb, '["Pediatric Nutrition","Infant IBW Calculation","Growth Formulas"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, 'Exam paper circled B. Margin calculations: ''0-6 months - double'', ''7-12 months - triple'', ''13-24 months - quad''. Formula: IBW = (Age in mo * 500) + BW = (8 * 500) + 2000 = 6000 g.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T04:42:50.058Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T04:42:50.058Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T04:42:50.058Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-31', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'Determine which of the following nutrition intervention package addresses micronutrient supplementation in children at risk?', 'Vitamin A supplementation between 6-59 months age', 'Under the DOH National Micronutrient Supplementation Program (delivered via Garantisadong Pambata), universal and targeted Vitamin A Supplementation (VAS) of 100,000 IU for 6–11 months and 200,000 IU every 6 months for 12–59 months is the designated intervention package addressing micronutrient malnutrition in children.', '["A. Continued breastfeeding until 24 months","B. Supplementary feeding for moderate acute malnutrition","C. Calcium supplementation to mothers at-risk of low intake","D. Vitamin A supplementation between 6-59 months age"]'::jsonb, '["Micronutrient Supplementation","Vitamin A","Garantisadong Pambata","DOH Guidelines"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled D. Margin handwritten notes: ''0-2 - 100k IU'', ''3-11 - 100k IU''. DOH VAS protocol: 6-11 mos = 100,000 IU (blue); 12-59 mos = 200,000 IU (red).', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T06:29:12.697Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:29:12.697Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:29:12.697Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-32', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'What is your first step in developing your program plan?', 'Know and identify the problem', 'The initial phase of any public health program planning process is situational analysis / problem identification to diagnose the community''s nutritional issues, affected target populations, etiology, and severity.', '["A. Mobilize the community","B. Set the objectives","C. Know and identify the problem","D. Develop the strategies"]'::jsonb, '["Program Planning","Planning Cycle","Problem Identification"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled C. Identical concept to Item 8. Planning begins with problem identification before formulating goals, strategies, or activities.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T05:59:01.256Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:59:01.256Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:59:01.256Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-33', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'The Administrative Order No. ________ embodies the strategic and operational framework for establishing integrated helminth control program.', '2006 - 0028', 'Department of Health Administrative Order No. 2006-0028 establishes the ''Strategic and Operational Framework for the Integrated Helminth Control Program (IHCP)'' in the Philippines, targeting soil-transmitted helminthiasis (STH) through biannual mass drug administration (deworming) of children and pregnant women.', '["A. 2006 - 0025","B. 2006 - 0028","C. 2010 - 0023","D. 2005 - 0027"]'::jsonb, '["DOH Administrative Orders","IHCP","Helminthiasis","Deworming"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'hard', 2, 'Exam paper circled B. DOH AO 2006-0028 = Integrated Helminth Control Program (IHCP).', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T06:26:24.135Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:26:24.135Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:26:24.135Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-34', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'Which of these methods of nutritional assessment deals with the individual and measures objective criteria on a face - to - face mode?', 'Direct', 'Direct nutritional assessment evaluates objective physiological, clinical, anthropometric, and biochemical criteria directly on individual subjects face-to-face, contrasting with indirect assessment which analyzes aggregated community indicators.', '["A. Personal assessment","B. Direct","C. Population-based","D. Indirect"]'::jsonb, '["Nutrition Assessment","Direct Methods","Anthropometry"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled B. Direct assessment = individual face-to-face evaluation (ABCD methods).', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T04:52:12.550Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T04:52:12.550Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T04:52:12.550Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-35', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'The Pres. Duterte''s development pillars are: malasakit, pagbabago, and ________ and the vision of Ambisyon 2040.', 'kaunlaran', 'Under the Philippine Development Plan (PDP 2017–2022) anchored on AmBisyon Natin 2040, the national framework is structured around three strategic pillars: 1) Malasakit (Enhancing the Social Fabric), 2) Pagbabago (Inequality-Reducing Transformation), and 3) Patuloy na Pag-unlad / Kaunlaran (Increasing Growth Potential).', '["A. kaunlaran","B. kalusugan","C. katalinuhan","D. kasipagan"]'::jsonb, '["National Policy","PDP 2017-2022","AmBisyon Natin 2040"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled A. PDP 2017-2022 pillars: Malasakit, Pagbabago, at Patuloy na Pag-unlad (Kaunlaran).', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T06:09:27.944Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:09:27.944Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:09:27.944Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-36', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'Which of the following nutrients helps maintain muscle and body tissues?', 'Proteins', 'Dietary proteins provide the essential amino acids required for the synthesis, repair, and ongoing maintenance of skeletal muscle, vital organ tissues, collagen matrix, enzymes, and peptide hormones.', '["A. Fats","B. Carbohydrates","C. Vitamin D Proteins","D. Proteins"]'::jsonb, '["Macronutrients","Proteins","Tissue Maintenance"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled D. Proteins serve primarily structural and functional tissue maintenance roles.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T05:03:40.388Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:03:40.388Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:03:40.388Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-37', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'What is the step in program planning where the program manager will articulate what the program does and what to accomplish?', 'Describe the program', 'Describing the program (program description/narrative) articulates the core mission, target population, structural components, specific activities, and what outcomes the program intends to accomplish.', '["A. Stakeholder analysis","B. Ghantt chart","C. Timelines","D. Describe the program"]'::jsonb, '["Program Planning","Program Description","Project Narrative"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled D. Program description specifies what the program entails and the intended scope of results.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T05:35:13.862Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:35:13.862Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:35:13.862Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-38', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'Albendazole ________ mg is usually given to pregnant women during the 2nd trimester.', '400', 'Under WHO and Philippine DOH guidelines for pregnant women in soil-transmitted helminth (STH) endemic areas (>20% prevalence), a single oral dose of Albendazole 400 mg (or Mebendazole 500 mg) is administered after the first trimester (in the 2nd or 3rd trimester) to treat intestinal worms and prevent maternal anemia.', '["A. 200","B. 150","C. 400","D. 300"]'::jsonb, '["Maternal Health","Deworming","Albendazole","DOH Guidelines"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, 'Exam paper circled C. Albendazole dose: 400 mg single dose; contraindicated during the 1st trimester due to potential embryotoxicity.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T05:45:21.723Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:45:21.723Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:45:21.723Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-39', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'What is the type of study design in which it answers the question "what will happen" and it is a prospective observation of subjects?', 'Cohort', 'A prospective Cohort study follows a defined group of exposure-free individuals forward in time to observe incidence rates and determine ''what will happen'' regarding disease or nutritional outcomes.', '["A. Cohort","B. Cross-sectional","C. Case control","D. Case series"]'::jsonb, '["Epidemiology","Study Designs","Cohort Study"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled A. Margin notes: ''Cohort: exposure ng dalawang experiment... walang disease ung isa may disease'', ''Cross-sectional: data na paghahambingin'', ''Case series: 2 o series ng case study na pinagtugma''.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T06:19:57.941Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:19:57.941Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:19:57.941Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-4', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'It refers to the regular or periodic collection and evaluation of data that can be used to indicate present and future changes in nutritional status.', 'Evaluation and management', 'In public health administration and NNC training manuals, systematic collection and evaluation of progress indicators to assess present trends and inform management decisions is termed evaluation and management (or monitoring/surveillance in broader epidemiological contexts). On the exam paper, option C is marked.', '["A. Supervision","B. Surveillance","C. Evaluation and management","D. Monitoring"]'::jsonb, '["Program Planning","Monitoring & Evaluation","Management"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, 'Exam paper circled C (Evaluation and management). Notice the pairing of both collection and evaluation with managerial course-correction.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T05:30:24.652Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:30:24.652Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:30:24.652Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-40', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'During lactation the additional daily energy requirement is ________', '500', 'According to the Philippine Dietary Reference Intakes (PDRI 2015), the additional daily energy allowance during the first six months of exclusive lactation is +500 kcal/day (to support human milk synthesis yielding ~750–800 ml/day). In pregnancy (2nd/3rd trimester), the additional energy is +300 kcal/day.', '["A. 300","B. 600","C. 200","D. 500"]'::jsonb, '["PDRI","Lactation","Energy Requirements","Maternal Nutrition"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled D. Margin handwritten note next to A: ''pregnant''. Lactation allowance = +500 kcal/day; Pregnancy allowance = +300 kcal/day.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T06:09:03.326Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:09:03.326Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:09:03.326Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-41', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'Which of the following are you going to use to answer the question of how much you should eat in one meal in order to be healthy?', 'Pinggang Pinoy', 'Pinggang Pinoy, developed by FNRI-DOST in collaboration with DOH and WHO, is an intuitive visual food guide specifically designed to demonstrate recommended food group proportions and portion sizes per single meal (half plate Glow foods: fruits and vegetables; one-quarter Grow foods: protein; one-quarter Go foods: carbohydrates). The Food Pyramid depicts daily food choices.', '["A. Pinggang Pinoy","B. Nutritional guidelines","C. Nutrigenomics","D. Food pyramid"]'::jsonb, '["Pinggang Pinoy","FNRI","Food Guides","Meal Planning"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled A. Pinggang Pinoy = PER MEAL food guide; Food Pyramid = DAILY food guide.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T04:46:03.369Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T04:46:03.369Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T04:46:03.369Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-42', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'What is the act of conducting systematic appraisal of the success of a program?', 'Evaluation', 'Evaluation is the systematic and objective assessment of the design, implementation, and overall success or impact of an ongoing or completed public health initiative.', '["A. Coordination","B. Evaluation","C. Monitoring","D. Networking"]'::jsonb, '["Program Planning","Evaluation","Program Appraisal"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled B. Appraisal of success/worth/impact = Evaluation. Tracking day-to-day progress = Monitoring.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T05:54:31.815Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:54:31.815Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:54:31.815Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-43', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'When do you give iron-folic acid supplements in malaria endemic areas?', 'During screening/treatment of malaria', 'Under WHO guidelines for malaria-endemic areas, iron and folic acid supplementation should be integrated alongside active screening, prevention (bed nets, vector control), and prompt antimalarial treatment. Option A is marked on the examination paper.', '["A. During screening/treatment of malaria","B. After screening/treatment of malaria","C. Before screening/treatment of malaria","D. Simultaneous with screening/treatment of malaria"]'::jsonb, '["Micronutrient Supplementation","Malaria","Iron-Folic Acid","WHO Guidelines"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, 'Exam paper circled A. Margin handwritten note: ''iron ay kakainin ni malaria'' (referring to how Plasmodium parasites utilize host iron, hence the necessity of concurrent screening/treatment).', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T05:30:35.831Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:30:35.831Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:30:35.831Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-44', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'When is the period of second growth spurt?', 'adolescence', 'Human postnatal physical growth exhibits two major rapid velocity spurts: the first occurs during infancy (first year of life), and the second occurs during adolescence (the pubertal growth spurt driven by sex steroids and growth hormone).', '["A. adolescence","B. adulthood","C. pre-school","D. school-age"]'::jsonb, '["Growth & Development","Adolescence","Pubertal Growth Spurt"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled A. Margin handwritten note: ''1st menarche - bago mag dalaga''. 1st growth spurt = infancy; 2nd growth spurt = adolescence.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T06:04:21.481Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:04:21.481Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:04:21.481Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-45', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'Which of the following is the guide for all who want to be involved in nutrition action because it lays out targets, directions, and priority actions, among others?', 'Sustainable Development Goals', 'On the candidate''s examination paper, option A (''Sustainable Development Goals'') is circled. In Philippine national policy, the Philippine Plan of Action for Nutrition (PPAN, Option D) is the comprehensive national multi-sectoral blueprint that articulates precise targets, directions, and priority nutrition actions.', '["A. Sustainable Development Goals","B. Sustainable development goals","C. Philippine Development Plan","D. Philippine Plan of Action for Nutrition"]'::jsonb, '["PPAN","SDGs","Nutrition Policy","National Framework"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, 'Exam paper circled A (Sustainable Development Goals). Note: Both SDGs (global) and PPAN (national) lay out targets and priority actions; examinee marked A.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T06:28:56.962Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:28:56.962Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:28:56.962Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-46', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'What is the term used to describe the complex disorder involving an excessive amount of body fat?', 'Obesity', 'Obesity is medically and epidemiologically defined as a chronic, complex relapsing non-communicable disease characterized by abnormal or excessive accumulation of body fat (adiposity) that impairs physical and metabolic health.', '["A. Accumulated fat and energy","B. Fat deposit","C. Obesity","D. Adipose tissue"]'::jsonb, '["Nutrition Assessment","Obesity","WHO Definitions"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled C. Repeated verbatim as Item 80 in this exam.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T05:59:38.418Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:59:38.418Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:59:38.418Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-47', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'The long range direction that answers the question of what you must focus on to achieve the vision is ________', 'mission', 'In strategic management and program planning, the Mission defines the fundamental purpose, scope of operations, and core operational focus of an organization or program—answering what must be done to attain the long-term Vision.', '["A. strategic goal","B. mission","C. program","D. policy"]'::jsonb, '["Strategic Planning","Mission & Vision","Management"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled B. Repeated verbatim as Item 165 in this exam. Vision = what we want to become; Mission = what we do/focus on to get there.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T06:26:13.421Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:26:13.421Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:26:13.421Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-48', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'What R.A was enacted in Year 2016 to promote and upgrade the practice of the professionals in the country?', '10912', 'Republic Act No. 10912 is the ''Continuing Professional Development (CPD) Act of 2016'', enacted on July 21, 2016. It mandates continuing education and credit units for the renewal of Professional Identification Cards across all regulated professions under the PRC.', '["A. 11229","B. 11012","C. 1009","D. 10912"]'::jsonb, '["Philippine Laws","RA 10912","CPD Act","PRC Regulations"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, 'Exam paper circled D. RA 10912 = Continuing Professional Development (CPD) Act of 2016.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T06:20:40.241Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:20:40.241Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:20:40.241Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-49', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'What is the type of study in which the effect of a given treatment is observed and assessed?', 'Experimental', 'In an Experimental study design (such as a randomized clinical trial or community intervention trial), the investigator deliberately manipulates or assigns the independent variable (treatment/intervention) and observes the outcome effects.', '["A. Experimental","B. Survey","C. Observational","D. Cross-sectional"]'::jsonb, '["Research Methodology","Study Designs","Experimental Research"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled A. Experimental studies actively intervene/treat; observational studies merely observe without manipulation.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T05:02:58.904Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:02:58.904Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:02:58.904Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-5', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'Which of the following is an example of direct method of nutritional assessment?', 'Biochemical', 'Nutritional assessment methods are divided into direct and indirect methods. Direct methods evaluate individual human subjects directly using the ABCD framework: Anthropometric, Biochemical/laboratory, Clinical, and Dietary methods. Vital health statistics, demographic data (age, sex), and agricultural/economic indicators are indirect ecological indicators.', '["A. Biochemical","B. Age","C. Sex","D. Vital Health indices"]'::jsonb, '["Nutrition Assessment","Direct vs Indirect","Biochemical"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled A. Direct methods assess individual nutritional status directly; indirect methods evaluate community-level ecological proxies.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T06:26:47.816Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:26:47.816Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:26:47.816Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-50', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'What are the different contaminants of foods?', 'chemical, microbiological, physical', 'Under food safety science and HACCP principles, food hazards and contaminants are classically classified into three major categories: 1) Biological/microbiological (bacteria, viruses, parasites), 2) Chemical (pesticides, toxins, heavy metals), and 3) Physical (glass, metal fragments, stones, bone splinters).', '["A. chemical, microbiological, physical","B. physical and biological only","C. biochemical and chemical only","D. chemical, biological, biochemical"]'::jsonb, '["Food Safety","HACCP","Food Contaminants"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled A. The classic triad of food safety hazards: Biological/microbiological, Chemical, and Physical.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T06:03:53.612Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:03:53.612Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:03:53.612Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-51', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'What is the process of ''working collaboratively with relevant partners who share common goals and interests'' or ''working collaboratively with and for groups of people affiliated by geographical proximity, special interest, or similar situations to address issues on nutrition and well-being of people''?', 'Community participation or engagement', 'Community engagement / community participation is the process of working collaboratively with and through groups of people affiliated by geographic proximity, special interest, or shared circumstances to address issues affecting their health, nutrition, and well-being.', '["A. Peoples'' participation","B. Community participation or engagement","C. Collaborative actions","D. Community activities"]'::jsonb, '["Community Engagement","Public Health Nutrition","Community Development"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled B (top of page 6). Emphasizes authentic partnership, community ownership, and empowering local stakeholders.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T06:19:51.192Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:19:51.192Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:19:51.192Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-52', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'The proportion of children 6 to 23 months meeting both the minimum meal frequency to ensure both dietary and nutrient adequacy is ________', 'Minimum acceptable diet', 'In WHO/UNICEF Infant and Young Child Feeding (IYCF) indicators, the Minimum Acceptable Diet (MAD) is a composite indicator measuring the proportion of children 6–23 months of age who receive both the minimum dietary diversity (consuming foods from >= 5 of 8 food groups) and minimum meal frequency.', '["A. Nutritional equivalence","B. Minimum acceptable diet","C. Legal minimum level","D. Fortification"]'::jsonb, '["IYCF Indicators","WHO Standards","Minimum Acceptable Diet"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, 'Exam paper circled B. MAD = Minimum Dietary Diversity (MDD) + Minimum Meal Frequency (MMF).', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T04:46:36.324Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T04:46:36.324Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T04:46:36.324Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-53', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'What is the measure of detecting early changes in body metabolism & nutrition before the appearance of overt clinical signs?', 'Biochemical', 'Biochemical assessment (laboratory measurement of nutrients, metabolites, or enzyme cofactors in blood, urine, or tissue) detects subclinical nutrient depletion and cellular metabolic alterations long before physical signs or anatomical growth deficits emerge.', '["A. Clinical","B. Anthropometry","C. Biochemical","D. Dietary"]'::jsonb, '["Nutrition Assessment","Biochemical Assessment","Subclinical Malnutrition"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled C. Repeated verbatim as Item 130 in this exam. Sequence of deficiency: Dietary inadequacy -> Decreased tissue stores -> Biochemical lesion -> Clinical signs.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T05:31:16.427Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:31:16.427Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:31:16.427Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-54', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'Maternal ________ is associated with overweight babies at birth.', 'obesity', 'Pre-pregnancy maternal obesity and excessive gestational weight gain increase fetal glucose exposure and hyperinsulinemia (Pedersen hypothesis), leading to macrosomia (birth weight > 4,000 g) and large-for-gestational-age (LGA) infants.', '["A. attitude","B. knowledge","C. obesity","D. iron deficiency"]'::jsonb, '["Maternal Nutrition","Obesity","Fetal Macrosomia","Pregnancy Outcomes"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled C. Maternal obesity -> fetal macrosomia / LGA; Maternal undernutrition/iron deficiency -> low birth weight / SGA.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T05:59:45.595Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:59:45.595Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:59:45.595Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-55', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'After the age of 59, caloric requirements is generally ________', 'decreased', 'In older adults (> 59 years), resting metabolic rate decreases by approximately 2–3% per decade due to progressive age-related loss of lean skeletal muscle mass (sarcopenia) and concurrent reduction in voluntary physical activity, leading to lower total daily caloric requirements.', '["A. increased","B. decreased","C. maintained","D. highest peak"]'::jsonb, '["Geriatric Nutrition","Energy Requirements","Sarcopenia"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled B. Caloric needs decrease in elderly adults, but micronutrient density requirements (protein, calcium, vitamin D, B12) remain high.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T04:37:11.681Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T04:37:11.681Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T04:37:11.681Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-56', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'Megaloblastic anemia is caused by ________ deficiency/deficiencies.', 'folic', 'Megaloblastic anemia is characterized by large, immature nucleated erythroblasts in the bone marrow caused by impaired thymidylate and DNA synthesis due to deficiency of Folic Acid (Vitamin B9) or Vitamin B12 (cobalamin). Iron deficiency causes microcytic hypochromic anemia.', '["A. folic","B. iron","C. all of these","D. protein"]'::jsonb, '["Anemia","Folic Acid","Hematology","Micronutrients"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled A. Margin handwritten notes: ''megaloblastic'', ''B12 Cobalamin pernicious'', ''Iron - Microcytic''. Folic acid/B12 = Megaloblastic; Iron = Microcytic.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T04:50:31.243Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T04:50:31.243Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T04:50:31.243Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-57', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'The transition in an infant''s diet from breastmilk to other sources of foods is called ________', 'complementary feeding', 'Complementary Feeding is the recommended term describing the period starting at 6 months when breast milk alone is no longer sufficient to meet nutritional requirements, and other solid/semi-solid foods are introduced alongside continued breastfeeding.', '["A. pre-lacteal","B. weaning","C. complementary feeding","D. supplementary feeding"]'::jsonb, '["Infant Nutrition","Complementary Feeding","IYCF"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled C. Modern public health nutrition emphasizes ''complementary feeding'' rather than ''weaning'' to reinforce that breast milk should continue alongside solid foods.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T05:49:16.095Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:49:16.095Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:49:16.095Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-58', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'What period after birth is considered as exclusively breastfed?', 'until 6 months', 'WHO, UNICEF, and the Philippine Department of Health recommend exclusive breastfeeding for the first 6 months of life (0 to 180 days). During this period, the infant receives only breast milk, with no other liquids or solids, not even water (with the exception of oral rehydration salts, vitamins, minerals, and medicines).', '["A. in 43 days","B. until 6 months","C. first week","D. within 24 hrs"]'::jsonb, '["Breastfeeding","Exclusive Breastfeeding","WHO Guidelines","IYCF"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled B. Exclusive breastfeeding duration = first 6 months (0-180 days).', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T06:01:04.227Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:01:04.227Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:01:04.227Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-59', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'This pertains to a public health nutritionist who has communication skills, ranging from writing professional reports to the development of health and nutrition information that is inclusive and appropriate to target populations with appropriate financial management system.', 'Administrator', 'The Administrator role in public health nutrition encompasses comprehensive executive leadership, program communication, strategic technical reporting, stakeholder coordination, and fiscal/financial resource management systems.', '["A. Implementer","B. Organizer","C. Assessor","D. Administrator"]'::jsonb, '["Public Health Roles","Administration","Management"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, 'Exam paper circled D. Financial management combined with strategic professional communication defines the Public Health Nutrition Administrator.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T06:06:55.114Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:06:55.114Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:06:55.114Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-6', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'What is the term used to define low weight for height?', 'wasting', 'Under WHO Child Growth Standards adopted by the DOH and NNC: Low Weight-for-Height/Length (<-2 SD) defines Wasting (acute malnutrition/thinness); Low Height/Length-for-Age (<-2 SD) defines Stunting (chronic malnutrition); and Low Weight-for-Age (<-2 SD) defines Underweight (composite index).', '["A. wasting","B. stunting","C. underweight","D. obesity"]'::jsonb, '["Anthropometry","Child Growth Standards","WHO Cut-offs","Wasting"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'easy', 2, 'Exam paper circled A. Wasting = weight-for-height (acute deficit); Stunting = height-for-age (chronic deficit); Underweight = weight-for-age.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T05:56:04.318Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:56:04.318Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T05:56:04.318Z"'::jsonb),
('card-cphn-2019-60', NULL, 'deck-prc-2019-cphn', 'What is the tool needed to be developed in order to have a clearer overview of the objectives, the possible causal factors, and related data that will aid the RND in identifying relevant indicators to be collected for program proposal?', 'Causal model', 'A Causal Model (problem tree or UNICEF conceptual framework of malnutrition) maps the immediate, underlying, and basic determinants of nutritional problems. It provides a visual schematic connecting causes to outcomes, guiding program planners in selecting target intervention points and measurable indicators.', '["A. Program objectives","B. Causal model","C. Monitoring tool","D. Program plan"]'::jsonb, '["Program Planning","Causal Analysis","Conceptual Framework"]'::jsonb, 'Community and Public Health Nutrition', 'medium', 2, 'Exam paper circled B. Causal models/problem trees structure the logical linkages between root causes and health indicators.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-07T06:10:56.004Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:10:56.004Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-05T05:07:44.124Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-11-06T06:10:56.004Z"'::jsonb)
