('mc:a restaurant served 87 guests and made p 18, 705 sales. average check per guest was.:::p 215', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'a restaurant served 87 guests and made p 18, 705 sales. average check per guest was.', 'P 215', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"In foodservice management and financial accounting, the average check (also termed cover average) measures the mean spending per customer. The standard mathematical formula is: Average Check = Total Sales Revenue / Total Number of Guests (Covers). Substituting the problem''s values: P 18,705 / 87 guests = P 215. This financial control metric allows managers to evaluate menu pricing efficiency, sales performance, and guest spending patterns.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"P 215\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"In foodservice management and financial accounting, the average check (also termed cover average) measures the mean spending per customer. The standard mathematical formula is: Average Check = Total Sales Revenue / Total Number of Guests (Covers). Substituting the problem''s values: P 18,705 / 87 guests = P 215. This financial control metric allows managers to evaluate menu pricing efficiency, sales performance, and guest spending patterns.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: P 250, P 205, P 217"}'::jsonb),
