('mc:a function of management that involves developing in broad outline the activities required to accomplish the objectives of the organization and the most effective ways of doing so. it is a continuous process and requires that management be diligent in conducting periodic reviews of all plans to ensure that they are still appropriate as conditions change.:::planning', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'a function of management that involves developing in broad outline the activities required to accomplish the objectives of the organization and the most effective ways of doing so. it is a continuous process and requires that management be diligent in conducting periodic reviews of all plans to ensure that they are still appropriate as conditions change.', 'Planning', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"In management theory, planning is universally recognized as the foundational function that involves determining the organization''s goals and charting out a broad outline of activities and strategies to achieve them.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Planning\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"In management theory, planning is universally recognized as the foundational function that involves determining the organization''s goals and charting out a broad outline of activities and strategies to achieve them.\n\nBecause business and environmental conditions constantly shift, planning cannot be a one-time task. It requires an ongoing, continuous process where managers regularly review, adjust, and adapt their roadmaps to ensure the organization stays on track.\n\n• Marketing: The function focused on identifying, anticipating, and satisfying customer needs through product design, pricing, promotion, and distribution.\n• Finance: The function responsible for managing the organization''s monetary resources, budgeting, and capital allocations.\n• Operations: The function that deals with the daily execution, transformation of inputs into outputs, and physical manufacturing or service delivery processes.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Marketing, Finance, Operations"}'::jsonb),
