er needs through product design, pricing, promotion, and distribution.\n• Finance: The function responsible for managing the organization''s monetary resources, budgeting, and capital allocations.\n• Operations: The function that deals with the daily execution, transformation of inputs into outputs, and physical manufacturing or service delivery processes.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Marketing, Finance, Operations"}'::jsonb),
('mc:the main goal of staff orientation program::::communicate information and create response to the company and the job', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the main goal of staff orientation program:', 'communicate information and create response to the company and the job', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Staff orientation is done to help recently hired staff in adjusting to their new employer. It gives staff members the fundamental organizational knowledge and serves as a venue for the employees to solicit responses about their new team, division, and job within the firm.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"communicate information and create response to the company and the job\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Staff orientation is done to help recently hired staff in adjusting to their new employer. It gives staff members the fundamental organizational knowledge and serves as a venue for the employees to solicit responses about their new team, division, and job within the firm.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: establish a system of discipline and rewards for the staff, establish training plan and method for evaluation progress, assess the reaction of other workers to the new worker"}'::jsonb),
