('mc:a component of coenzyme a, a carrier of acetyl groups.:::pantothenic acid', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'a component of coenzyme a, a carrier of acetyl groups.', 'Pantothenic acid', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Pantothenate is vitamin B5 and is the key precursor for the biosynthesis of CoA, a universal and essential cofactor involved in a myriad of metabolic reactions, including the synthesis of phospholipids, the synthesis and degradation of fatty acids, and the operation of the TCA cycle.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Pantothenic acid\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Pantothenate is vitamin B5 and is the key precursor for the biosynthesis of CoA, a universal and essential cofactor involved in a myriad of metabolic reactions, including the synthesis of phospholipids, the synthesis and degradation of fatty acids, and the operation of the TCA cycle.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Biotin, Provitamin, Thiamin"}'::jsonb),
