('mc:involved in biosynthesis of collagen.:::vit c', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'involved in biosynthesis of collagen.', 'Vit C', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Vitamin C plays a critical role in the maintenance of a normal mature collagen network by preventing the auto-inactivation of lysyl and prolyl hydroxylase, two key enzymes in collagen biosynthesis.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Vit C\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Vitamin C plays a critical role in the maintenance of a normal mature collagen network by preventing the auto-inactivation of lysyl and prolyl hydroxylase, two key enzymes in collagen biosynthesis.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Vit A, Vit B, Vit D"}'::jsonb),
