('mc:is the form of vit k found in animal products while is the form of vit k in plants.:::menaquione, phylloquione', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'is the form of vit k found in animal products while is the form of vit k in plants.', 'Menaquione, Phylloquione', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Menaquinone (Vitamin K2) is primarily of bacterial origin and is the main form of Vitamin K found in animal products (such as meat, dairy, and eggs) and fermented foods.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Menaquione, Phylloquione\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Menaquinone (Vitamin K2) is primarily of bacterial origin and is the main form of Vitamin K found in animal products (such as meat, dairy, and eggs) and fermented foods.\n\nPhylloquinone (Vitamin K1) is synthesized directly by plants and is found abundantly in green leafy vegetables.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Phylloquione, Menaquione, Phylloquione, Phylloquione, Menaquione, Menaquione"}'::jsonb),
