nrolled in public schools).","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Young children 6-59 months old, School children, Pregnant women"}'::jsonb),
('mc:compute the calories provided by a 2-l dialysate solution containing 2.5% dextrose.:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'compute the calories provided by a 2-l dialysate solution containing 2.5% dextrose.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"A 2.5% dextrose solution contains 2.5 g of dextrose per 100 mL.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"170 kcal\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"A 2.5% dextrose solution contains 2.5 g of dextrose per 100 mL.\n\nFor 2 L (2,000 mL):\n2.5 g/100 mL × 2,000 mL = 50 g dextrose\n\nDextrose provides approximately 3.4 kcal/g\n50 g × 3.4 kcal/g = 170 kcal\n\nTherefore, the dialysate provides approximately 170 kcal.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: 108 kcal, 148 kcal, 200 kcal"}'::jsonb),
('mc:mobilization of lgus; policy development for food and nutrition; and strengthened management support are known as . these are necessary for the implementation of ppan.:::enabling programs', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'mobilization of lgus; policy development for food and nutrition; and strengthened management support are known as . these are necessary for the implementation of ppan.', 'Enabling programs', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Under the Philippine Plan of Action for Nutrition (PPAN) framework managed by the National Nutrition Council (NNC), these three components are specifically classified as enabling support programs:","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Enabling programs\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Under the Philippine Plan of Action for Nutrition (PPAN) framework managed by the National Nutrition Council (NNC), these three components are specifically classified as enabling support programs:\n\n1. Mobilization of LGUs for nutritional outcomes\n2. Policy development for food and nutrition\n3. Strengthened management support\n\nThese programs are designated to ensure that both nutrition-specific and nutrition-sensitive interventions are well-coordinated and effectively implemented across all local government levels.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Nutrition advocacy, Support services, Facilitating initiatives"}'::jsonb),
('mc:mobilization of lgus; policy development for food and nutrition; and strengthened management support are known as . these are necessary for the implementation of ppan.:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'mobilization of lgus; policy development for food and nutrition; and strengthened management support are known as . these are necessary for the implementation of ppan.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Under the Philippine Plan of Action for Nutrition (PPAN) framework managed by the National Nutrition Council (NNC), these three components are specifically classified as enabling support programs:","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Enabling programs\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Under the Philippine Plan of Action for Nutrition (PPAN) framework managed by the National Nutrition Council (NNC), these three components are specifically classified as enabling support programs:\n\n1. Mobilization of LGUs for nutritional outcomes\n2. Policy development for food and nutrition\n3. Strengthened management support\n\nThese programs are designated to ensure that both nutrition-specific and nutrition-sensitive interventions are well-coordinated and effectively implemented across all local government levels.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Nutrition advocacy, Support services, Facilitating initiatives"}'::jsonb),
('mc:it is known as participatory planning that involves local leaders, implementers and people themselves in planning the program.:::joint planning', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'it is known as participatory planning that involves local leaders, implementers and people themselves in planning the program.', 'Joint planning', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"In program planning and management (particularly within nutrition and public health frameworks), Joint planning is explicitly defined as a type of participatory planning. It acts as a hybrid approach that combines elements of both top-down and bottom-up planning strategies. This method ensures comprehensive collaboration by actively involving local leaders, the implementers, and the target beneficiaries (the people themselves) directly in the program design.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Joint planning\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"In program planning and management (particularly within nutrition and public health frameworks), Joint planning is explicitly defined as a type of participatory planning. It acts as a hybrid approach that combines elements of both top-down and bottom-up planning strategies. This method ensures comprehensive collaboration by actively involving local leaders, the implementers, and the target beneficiaries (the people themselves) directly in the program design.\n\n• Microlevel planning: This refers strictly to planning conducted at the localized, community, or grass-roots level (such as creating a specific barangay or municipal nutrition plan).\n• Strategic planning: This is a systematic process of mapping out a long-term vision, transforming that vision into broadly-defined strategic goals, and determining the sequential steps needed to achieve them.\n• Food and nutrition planning: This is the overarching thematic discipline focused on formulating national policies, interventions, and guidelines to combat malnutrition and ensure food security.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Food and nutrition planning, Strategic planning, Microlevel planning"}'::jsonb),
('mc:it is known as participatory planning that involves local leaders, implementers and people themselves in planning the program.:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'it is known as participatory planning that involves local leaders, implementers and people themselves in planning the program.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"In program planning and management (particularly within nutrition and public health frameworks), Joint planning is explicitly defined as a type of participatory planning. It acts as a hybrid approach that combines elements of both top-down and bottom-up planning strategies. This method ensures comprehensive collaboration by actively involving local leaders, the implementers, and the target beneficiaries (the people themselves) directly in the program design.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Joint planning\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"In program planning and management (particularly within nutrition and public health frameworks), Joint planning is explicitly defined as a type of participatory planning. It acts as a hybrid approach that combines elements of both top-down and bottom-up planning strategies. This method ensures comprehensive collaboration by actively involving local leaders, the implementers, and the target beneficiaries (the people themselves) directly in the program design.\n\n• Microlevel planning: This refers strictly to planning conducted at the localized, community, or grass-roots level (such as creating a specific barangay or municipal nutrition plan).\n• Strategic planning: This is a systematic process of mapping out a long-term vision, transforming that vision into broadly-defined strategic goals, and determining the sequential steps needed to achieve them.\n• Food and nutrition planning: This is the overarching thematic discipline focused on formulating national policies, interventions, and guidelines to combat malnutrition and ensure food security.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Food and nutrition planning, Strategic planning, Microlevel planning"}'::jsonb),
('mc:the effortless expulsion of gastric contents caused by gi reflux in babies:::regurgitation', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the effortless expulsion of gastric contents caused by gi reflux in babies', 'Regurgitation', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Regurgitation is clinically defined as the effortless, passive expulsion of swallowed food or gastric contents from the stomach back into the esophagus and mouth. In infants, this is primarily driven by an immature lower esophageal sphincter—a common, normal condition known as gastroesophageal reflux (GER) that usually resolves on its own as the baby grows.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Regurgitation\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Regurgitation is clinically defined as the effortless, passive expulsion of swallowed food or gastric contents from the stomach back into the esophagus and mouth. In infants, this is primarily driven by an immature lower esophageal sphincter—a common, normal condition known as gastroesophageal reflux (GER) that usually resolves on its own as the baby grows.\n\n• Colic: This refers to periods of intense, frequent, and unexplained crying in an otherwise healthy infant, often thought to be linked to gas or abdominal discomfort, rather than the physical ejection of stomach contents.\n• Diarrhea: This describes loose, watery stools passing through the lower gastrointestinal tract, not an upward reflux into the mouth.\n• Spitting-up-food: While this is the casual, everyday term parents use for this exact behavior, Regurgitation is the primary scientific and medical terminology used in public health exams to describe the involuntary mechanism itself.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Colic, Spitting-up-food, Diarrhea"}'::jsonb),
('mc:a principle in planning that refers to desired breadth and depth of the nutrition program.:::comprehensiveness', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'a principle in planning that refers to desired breadth and depth of the nutrition program.', 'Comprehensiveness', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Comprehensiveness is a core principle in nutrition program planning and management. It explicitly dictates that the desired breadth and depth of whatever has been selected as the overall scope of the program or project must be thoroughly and accurately reflected in the actual plan.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Comprehensiveness\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Comprehensiveness is a core principle in nutrition program planning and management. It explicitly dictates that the desired breadth and depth of whatever has been selected as the overall scope of the program or project must be thoroughly and accurately reflected in the actual plan.\n\n• Balance: Emphasizes that all specific activities, tasks, and resource allocations are properly distributed so that they directly contribute to the achievement of the program''s objectives.\n• Workability: Mandates that the plan must be operationally practical, meaning the objectives are completely realistic and achievable within the set timeframe and available resources.\n• Appropriateness: Refers to how well the designed program fits the localized cultural, environmental, and socio-economic context of the target community.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Balance, Workability, Appropriateness"}'::jsonb),
('mc:a principle in planning that refers to desired breadth and depth of the nutrition program.:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'a principle in planning that refers to desired breadth and depth of the nutrition program.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Comprehensiveness is a core principle in nutrition program planning and management. It explicitly dictates that the desired breadth and depth of whatever has been selected as the overall scope of the program or project must be thoroughly and accurately reflected in the actual plan.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Comprehensiveness\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Comprehensiveness is a core principle in nutrition program planning and management. It explicitly dictates that the desired breadth and depth of whatever has been selected as the overall scope of the program or project must be thoroughly and accurately reflected in the actual plan.\n\n• Balance: Emphasizes that all specific activities, tasks, and resource allocations are properly distributed so that they directly contribute to the achievement of the program''s objectives.\n• Workability: Mandates that the plan must be operationally practical, meaning the objectives are completely realistic and achievable within the set timeframe and available resources.\n• Appropriateness: Refers to how well the designed program fits the localized cultural, environmental, and socio-economic context of the target community.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Balance, Workability, Appropriateness"}'::jsonb),
('mc:the following is/are true for problem matrix, causal model, or problem tree except::::formulated by the bns and presented to lce as an advocacy tool', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the following is/are true for problem matrix, causal model, or problem tree except:', 'Formulated by the BNS and presented to LCE as an advocacy tool', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Formulating a problem tree, causal model, or problem matrix is not a task done individually by the Barangay Nutrition Scholar (BNS). According to local nutrition planning guidelines, it requires collective brainstorming and data analysis from the entire members of the Local Nutrition Committee (LNC) during their strategic planning meetings. The entire plan (not just the tree) is what is eventually packaged and presented to the Local Chief Executive (LCE) for adoption and funding.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Formulated by the BNS and presented to LCE as an advocacy tool\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Formulating a problem tree, causal model, or problem matrix is not a task done individually by the Barangay Nutrition Scholar (BNS). According to local nutrition planning guidelines, it requires collective brainstorming and data analysis from the entire members of the Local Nutrition Committee (LNC) during their strategic planning meetings. The entire plan (not just the tree) is what is eventually packaged and presented to the Local Chief Executive (LCE) for adoption and funding.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Trace the chain of factors that can affect nutrition situation, Constructed by asking and answering a series of \"whys\" to understand better the factors, Being updated every year as a result of new data on nutrition situation"}'::jsonb),
('mc:it refers to the anabolic formation of triacyglycerol from glycerol and fatty acids.:::lipogenesis', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'it refers to the anabolic formation of triacyglycerol from glycerol and fatty acids.', 'Lipogenesis', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Lipogenesis refers broadly to the formation and storage of fat, including the synthesis of triacylglycerol (TAG) from glycerol-derived molecules and fatty acids. It occurs primarily when energy intake exceeds immediate energy needs, allowing excess energy to be stored as body fat.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Lipogenesis\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Lipogenesis refers broadly to the formation and storage of fat, including the synthesis of triacylglycerol (TAG) from glycerol-derived molecules and fatty acids. It occurs primarily when energy intake exceeds immediate energy needs, allowing excess energy to be stored as body fat.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Fatty acid synthesis, Cholesterol synthesis, Gluconeogenesis"}'::jsonb),
('mc:taters refer to::::potatoes', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'taters refer to:', 'Potatoes', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"\"Taters\" is a casual, colloquial slang term derived from the word \"potatoes\" (commonly used in phrases like tater tots or mashed taters).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Potatoes\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"\"Taters\" is a casual, colloquial slang term derived from the word \"potatoes\" (commonly used in phrases like tater tots or mashed taters).","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Chips, Popcorn, Shrimp"}'::jsonb),
