('mc:the following are dietary management for wernicke-korsakoff syndrome except::::high energy and protein tube feedings', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the following are dietary management for wernicke-korsakoff syndrome except:', 'High energy and protein tube feedings', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Wernicke-Korsakoff syndrome is associated with severe thiamine (vitamin B1) deficiency, commonly in the setting of chronic alcohol use and malnutrition. Management includes prompt thiamine replacement, adequate hydration and nutritional rehabilitation, and alcohol avoidance. However, high-energy/high-protein tube feeding is not a routine specific dietary management measure; enteral feeding is used when oral intake is inadequate or unsafe, and nutrition should be advanced appropriately rather than automatically prescribing high-energy, high-protein tube feeding.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"High energy and protein tube feedings\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Wernicke-Korsakoff syndrome is associated with severe thiamine (vitamin B1) deficiency, commonly in the setting of chronic alcohol use and malnutrition. Management includes prompt thiamine replacement, adequate hydration and nutritional rehabilitation, and alcohol avoidance. However, high-energy/high-protein tube feeding is not a routine specific dietary management measure; enteral feeding is used when oral intake is inadequate or unsafe, and nutrition should be advanced appropriately rather than automatically prescribing high-energy, high-protein tube feeding.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Thiamine supplementation, Adequate hydration, Avoidance of alcohol"}'::jsonb),
