('mc:what is the main objective of doh ao 2019-0033?:::to establish uniform implementation of the nutrition care process (ncp) in hospitals', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'what is the main objective of doh ao 2019-0033?', 'To establish uniform implementation of the Nutrition Care Process (NCP) in hospitals', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The AO ensures standardized, evidence-based nutrition care through the NCP in all hospital settings.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"To establish uniform implementation of the Nutrition Care Process (NCP) in hospitals\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The AO ensures standardized, evidence-based nutrition care through the NCP in all hospital settings.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: To standardize medical documentation across all hospitals, Option C, To replace the role of dietitians with nutrition nurses"}'::jsonb),
