('mc:what are the four core steps of the ncp?:::assessment, diagnosis, intervention, and monitoring & evaluation', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'what are the four core steps of the ncp?', 'Assessment, diagnosis, intervention, and monitoring & evaluation', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"These four steps make up the standardized NCP model recognized by DOH and the Academy of Nutrition and Dietetics.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Assessment, diagnosis, intervention, and monitoring & evaluation\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"These four steps make up the standardized NCP model recognized by DOH and the Academy of Nutrition and Dietetics.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Screening, assessment, evaluation, and referral, Planning, implementation, documentation, and discharge, Option D"}'::jsonb),
