ry for a competitive combat sport athlete undergoing strenuous training cycles.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: 66g to 85g Protein, 55 g to 75g Protein, 75g to 120g Protein"}'::jsonb),
('mc:what is the choice of fuel to sustain a high intensity exercise that lasts between 3 to 20 minutes?:::carbohydrate and some fat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'what is the choice of fuel to sustain a high intensity exercise that lasts between 3 to 20 minutes?', 'Carbohydrate and some fat', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"During high-intensity exercise sustained from 3 to 20 minutes, the predominant energy system transitions from immediate phosphagen pathways to rapid glycogenolysis and glycolysis, which generate ATP rapidly via carbohydrate oxidation. Because this duration exceeds immediate ATP-PCr capacity yet allows sufficient oxygen delivery for mixed-substrate metabolism, aerobic and anaerobic pathways operate simultaneously. Fat oxidation contributes a measurable percentage of total energy expenditure, particularly as the exercise duration extends past 5 minutes and reliance shifts partially toward oxidative phosphorylation.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Carbohydrate and some fat\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"During high-intensity exercise sustained from 3 to 20 minutes, the predominant energy system transitions from immediate phosphagen pathways to rapid glycogenolysis and glycolysis, which generate ATP rapidly via carbohydrate oxidation. Because this duration exceeds immediate ATP-PCr capacity yet allows sufficient oxygen delivery for mixed-substrate metabolism, aerobic and anaerobic pathways operate simultaneously. Fat oxidation contributes a measurable percentage of total energy expenditure, particularly as the exercise duration extends past 5 minutes and reliance shifts partially toward oxidative phosphorylation.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Protein and BCAA, Carbohydrate only, Carbohydrate and protein"}'::jsonb),
