('mc:tequila-based cocktail with lime juice and triple sec.:::margarita', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'tequila-based cocktail with lime juice and triple sec.', 'Margarita', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Margarita typically consists of tequila, lime juice (often freshly squeezed), and triple sec (an orange-flavored liqueur). It is usually served in a glass with a salted rim. The combination of tequila’s agave flavor, tart lime juice, and sweet triple sec creates a balanced and refreshing cocktail.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Margarita\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Margarita typically consists of tequila, lime juice (often freshly squeezed), and triple sec (an orange-flavored liqueur). It is usually served in a glass with a salted rim. The combination of tequila’s agave flavor, tart lime juice, and sweet triple sec creates a balanced and refreshing cocktail.\n\n• Martini: Typically made with gin and vermouth, garnished with an olive or a lemon twist.\n• Tequila Sunrise: Made with tequila, orange juice, and grenadine syrup, creating a layered sunrise effect.\n• Daiquiri: A classic cocktail made with rum, lime juice, and simple syrup, served straight up or on the rocks.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Martini, Tequila sunrise, Daiquiri"}'::jsonb),
('mc:tequila-based cocktail with lime juice and triple sec.:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'tequila-based cocktail with lime juice and triple sec.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Margarita typically consists of tequila, lime juice (often freshly squeezed), and triple sec (an orange-flavored liqueur). It is usually served in a glass with a salted rim. The combination of tequila’s agave flavor, tart lime juice, and sweet triple sec creates a balanced and refreshing cocktail.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Margarita\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Margarita typically consists of tequila, lime juice (often freshly squeezed), and triple sec (an orange-flavored liqueur). It is usually served in a glass with a salted rim. The combination of tequila’s agave flavor, tart lime juice, and sweet triple sec creates a balanced and refreshing cocktail.\n\n• Martini: Typically made with gin and vermouth, garnished with an olive or a lemon twist.\n• Tequila Sunrise: Made with tequila, orange juice, and grenadine syrup, creating a layered sunrise effect.\n• Daiquiri: A classic cocktail made with rum, lime juice, and simple syrup, served straight up or on the rocks.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Martini, Tequila sunrise, Daiquiri"}'::jsonb),
('mc:head of the kitchen brigade system.:::executive chef', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'head of the kitchen brigade system.', 'Executive Chef', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"In the traditional kitchen brigade system, which was developed by Georges Auguste Escoffier, the Executive Chef holds the highest authority and responsibility in the kitchen. This role involves overseeing all aspects of the kitchen operations, including menu planning, food preparation, kitchen staff management, and ensuring culinary standards and quality control.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Executive Chef\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"In the traditional kitchen brigade system, which was developed by Georges Auguste Escoffier, the Executive Chef holds the highest authority and responsibility in the kitchen. This role involves overseeing all aspects of the kitchen operations, including menu planning, food preparation, kitchen staff management, and ensuring culinary standards and quality control.\n\n• Garde Manger: The Garde Manger, also known as the pantry chef, is responsible for cold food preparation, such as salads, appetizers, and sometimes desserts.\n• Sommelier: A wine steward or wine expert responsible for selecting and serving wines in a restaurant.\n• Sous Chef: The second-in-command in the kitchen, assisting the Executive Chef in managing kitchen staff, overseeing food production, and ensuring kitchen operations run smoothly.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Garde manger, Sommelier, Sous Chef"}'::jsonb),
('mc:typically refers to dishes originating from or in the style of nice, france. it can include various salads, seafood dishes, or other regional specialties.:::nicoise', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'typically refers to dishes originating from or in the style of nice, france. it can include various salads, seafood dishes, or other regional specialties.', 'Nicoise', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"• Hors d’oeuvres: Refers to small dishes served before a main meal to stimulate the appetite. It can include a variety of items such as finger foods, dips, spreads, or small hot and cold dishes.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Nicoise\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"• Hors d’oeuvres: Refers to small dishes served before a main meal to stimulate the appetite. It can include a variety of items such as finger foods, dips, spreads, or small hot and cold dishes.\n• Canapés: Small pieces of bread or pastry topped with savory garnishes, often served as appetizers.\n• Macedoine: A culinary term that typically refers to a mixture or salad containing small diced vegetables or fruits.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Canapes, Hors d''oeuvres, Macedoine"}'::jsonb),
