('mc:an appetizer made of fried or toasted bread spread with anchovies or other small savory foods is called::::canape', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'an appetizer made of fried or toasted bread spread with anchovies or other small savory foods is called:', 'Canape', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Canapés are small pieces of bread or pastry topped with savory garnishes, often served as appetizers.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Canape\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Canapés are small pieces of bread or pastry topped with savory garnishes, often served as appetizers.\n\n• Capelletti: Small, stuffed pasta shapes similar to tortellini. They are typically filled with meat or cheese and served in broth or with a sauce.\n• Cassata: Traditional Italian dessert made with sponge cake, ricotta cheese, candied fruit, and a layer of marzipan. It is often associated with Sicily.\n• Cannelloni: Large pasta tubes that are typically stuffed with a filling such as ricotta cheese and spinach or ground meat. They are then covered in sauce and baked.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Capelleti, Cassata, Cannelloni"}'::jsonb),
