('mc:vitamin c, vitamin e, bht, and bht and sulfites are all::::antioxidants', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'vitamin c, vitamin e, bht, and bht and sulfites are all:', 'antioxidants', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Antioxidants are substances that inhibit oxidation processes, which can lead to the deterioration of food products. They help prevent or slow down the oxidation of fats and oils, thus extending the shelf life of foods. Examples include vitamin C (ascorbic acid), vitamin E (tocopherol), BHA (butylated hydroxyanisole), BHT (butylated hydroxytoluene), and sulfites.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"antioxidants\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Antioxidants are substances that inhibit oxidation processes, which can lead to the deterioration of food products. They help prevent or slow down the oxidation of fats and oils, thus extending the shelf life of foods. Examples include vitamin C (ascorbic acid), vitamin E (tocopherol), BHA (butylated hydroxyanisole), BHT (butylated hydroxytoluene), and sulfites.\n\n• Flavor enhancers: These substances are added to food to enhance or modify its taste and flavor.\n• Antimicrobial agents: These are substances that inhibit or kill microorganisms, helping to preserve food by preventing microbial spoilage or contamination.\n• Incidental food additives: These are substances that may be present in food as a result of manufacturing, processing, packaging, or storing, but are not intentionally added.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: flavor enhancers, antimicrobial agents, incidental food additives"}'::jsonb),
('mc:vitamin c, vitamin e, bht, and bht and sulfites are all::::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'vitamin c, vitamin e, bht, and bht and sulfites are all:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Antioxidants are substances that inhibit oxidation processes, which can lead to the deterioration of food products. They help prevent or slow down the oxidation of fats and oils, thus extending the shelf life of foods. Examples include vitamin C (ascorbic acid), vitamin E (tocopherol), BHA (butylated hydroxyanisole), BHT (butylated hydroxytoluene), and sulfites.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"antioxidants\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Antioxidants are substances that inhibit oxidation processes, which can lead to the deterioration of food products. They help prevent or slow down the oxidation of fats and oils, thus extending the shelf life of foods. Examples include vitamin C (ascorbic acid), vitamin E (tocopherol), BHA (butylated hydroxyanisole), BHT (butylated hydroxytoluene), and sulfites.\n\n• Flavor enhancers: These substances are added to food to enhance or modify its taste and flavor.\n• Antimicrobial agents: These are substances that inhibit or kill microorganisms, helping to preserve food by preventing microbial spoilage or contamination.\n• Incidental food additives: These are substances that may be present in food as a result of manufacturing, processing, packaging, or storing, but are not intentionally added.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: flavor enhancers, antimicrobial agents, incidental food additives"}'::jsonb),
('mc:the philippines'' abundant use of rice is reflected on its wide selection of rice-based desserts. example of rice-based delicacies include the following except::::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the philippines'' abundant use of rice is reflected on its wide selection of rice-based desserts. example of rice-based delicacies include the following except:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Etag is a type of preserved meat, specifically salted and smoked pork, not a rice-based dessert.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Etag\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Etag is a type of preserved meat, specifically salted and smoked pork, not a rice-based dessert.\n\n• Tibok-Tibok: A Filipino dessert made from carabao’s milk and rice flour, often flavored with latik (coconut caramel).\n• Kalamay: A sticky sweet delicacy made from glutinous rice, coconut milk, and sugar.\n• Puto Calasiao: A type of steamed rice cake that originates from Calasiao, Pangasinan, made from fermented rice batter.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Tibok-tibok, Kalamay, Puto Calasiao"}'::jsonb),
('mc:an example of aseptic packaging::::tetra pack drinking boxes', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'an example of aseptic packaging:', 'tetra pack drinking boxes', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Aseptic packaging refers to a method of packaging food and beverages in a sterile environment to maintain freshness without the need for refrigeration or additives. Tetra Pak is a well-known brand that produces aseptic packaging solutions, such as drinking boxes for juices, milk, and other beverages. These packages are designed to keep the contents safe from contamination and maintain their quality over an extended period without the need for preservatives or refrigeration until opened.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"tetra pack drinking boxes\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Aseptic packaging refers to a method of packaging food and beverages in a sterile environment to maintain freshness without the need for refrigeration or additives. Tetra Pak is a well-known brand that produces aseptic packaging solutions, such as drinking boxes for juices, milk, and other beverages. These packages are designed to keep the contents safe from contamination and maintain their quality over an extended period without the need for preservatives or refrigeration until opened.\n\n• Paper bag: Generally used for dry goods and not aseptically packaged.\n• Milk carton: While milk cartons can be sealed aseptically, Tetra Pak specifically refers to the brand of aseptic packaging.\n• Plastic bread bag: Used for packaging bread and typically not aseptic.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: paper bag, milk carton, plastic bread bag"}'::jsonb),
('mc:an example of aseptic packaging::::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'an example of aseptic packaging:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Aseptic packaging refers to a method of packaging food and beverages in a sterile environment to maintain freshness without the need for refrigeration or additives. Tetra Pak is a well-known brand that produces aseptic packaging solutions, such as drinking boxes for juices, milk, and other beverages. These packages are designed to keep the contents safe from contamination and maintain their quality over an extended period without the need for preservatives or refrigeration until opened.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"tetra pack drinking boxes\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Aseptic packaging refers to a method of packaging food and beverages in a sterile environment to maintain freshness without the need for refrigeration or additives. Tetra Pak is a well-known brand that produces aseptic packaging solutions, such as drinking boxes for juices, milk, and other beverages. These packages are designed to keep the contents safe from contamination and maintain their quality over an extended period without the need for preservatives or refrigeration until opened.\n\n• Paper bag: Generally used for dry goods and not aseptically packaged.\n• Milk carton: While milk cartons can be sealed aseptically, Tetra Pak specifically refers to the brand of aseptic packaging.\n• Plastic bread bag: Used for packaging bread and typically not aseptic.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: paper bag, milk carton, plastic bread bag"}'::jsonb),
('mc:of the pork cuts, the most tender is::::loin', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'of the pork cuts, the most tender is:', 'loin', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The loin is known for being the most tender cut of pork. It comes from the area along the back of the pig and includes cuts such as pork chops and pork tenderloin. This area of the pig does less work, resulting in more tender meat.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"loin\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The loin is known for being the most tender cut of pork. It comes from the area along the back of the pig and includes cuts such as pork chops and pork tenderloin. This area of the pig does less work, resulting in more tender meat.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: pork chop, shank, pigue"}'::jsonb),
