('mc:the similarities in food culture between the southern philippines, malaysia, and indonesia are attributed to common religion. the similarity in food culture between the philippines and latin america is the history of colonization.:::both sentences are correct', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the similarities in food culture between the southern philippines, malaysia, and indonesia are attributed to common religion. the similarity in food culture between the philippines and latin america is the history of colonization.', 'Both sentences are correct', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Sentence A is correct. The southern Philippines, Malaysia, and Indonesia share a significant Muslim population, and their food cultures reflect Islamic dietary laws, including the use of halal ingredients and specific cooking practices.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Both sentences are correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Sentence A is correct. The southern Philippines, Malaysia, and Indonesia share a significant Muslim population, and their food cultures reflect Islamic dietary laws, including the use of halal ingredients and specific cooking practices.\n\nSentence B is also correct. The Philippines was colonized by Spain for over 300 years, which influenced Filipino cuisine with techniques and dishes similar to those found in Latin America, which were also Spanish colonies. Examples include the use of ingredients like tomatoes, garlic, and onions, as well as dishes like adobo and empanadas.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Only the first sentence is correct, Only the second sentence is correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb),
('mc:the similarities in food culture between the southern philippines, malaysia, and indonesia are attributed to common religion. the similarity in food culture between the philippines and latin america is the history of colonization.:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the similarities in food culture between the southern philippines, malaysia, and indonesia are attributed to common religion. the similarity in food culture between the philippines and latin america is the history of colonization.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Sentence A is correct. The southern Philippines, Malaysia, and Indonesia share a significant Muslim population, and their food cultures reflect Islamic dietary laws, including the use of halal ingredients and specific cooking practices.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Both sentences are correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Sentence A is correct. The southern Philippines, Malaysia, and Indonesia share a significant Muslim population, and their food cultures reflect Islamic dietary laws, including the use of halal ingredients and specific cooking practices.\n\nSentence B is also correct. The Philippines was colonized by Spain for over 300 years, which influenced Filipino cuisine with techniques and dishes similar to those found in Latin America, which were also Spanish colonies. Examples include the use of ingredients like tomatoes, garlic, and onions, as well as dishes like adobo and empanadas.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Only the first sentence is correct, Only the second sentence is correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb),
('mc:considered as the healthiest among cuisines of southeast asia because of the use of a profusion of green leafy vegetables, bean sprouts, nuts, fresh herbs and lean meat.:::vietnamese', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'considered as the healthiest among cuisines of southeast asia because of the use of a profusion of green leafy vegetables, bean sprouts, nuts, fresh herbs and lean meat.', 'Vietnamese', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Vietnamese cuisine is renowned for its fresh ingredients, balanced flavors, and minimal use of oil. Dishes often incorporate a variety of vegetables and herbs, lean proteins, and rice, creating a light and nutritious meal profile. Popular dishes like pho, fresh spring rolls (goi cuon), and various salads (goi) highlight these healthy components.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Vietnamese\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Vietnamese cuisine is renowned for its fresh ingredients, balanced flavors, and minimal use of oil. Dishes often incorporate a variety of vegetables and herbs, lean proteins, and rice, creating a light and nutritious meal profile. Popular dishes like pho, fresh spring rolls (goi cuon), and various salads (goi) highlight these healthy components.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Myanmar, Thai, Lao"}'::jsonb),
('mc:a food or group of foods served at one time or intended to be eaten at the same time is called::::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'a food or group of foods served at one time or intended to be eaten at the same time is called:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"A course is a food or group of foods served or intended to be eaten at one time;","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Course\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"A course is a food or group of foods served or intended to be eaten at one time;\n\nA menu is the list of offerings. \n\nA meal is an occasion when food is eaten.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Menu, Meal, none of the above"}'::jsonb),
('mc:considered as the healthiest among cuisines of southeast asia because of the use of a profusion of green leafy vegetables, bean sprouts, nuts, fresh herbs and lean meat.:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'considered as the healthiest among cuisines of southeast asia because of the use of a profusion of green leafy vegetables, bean sprouts, nuts, fresh herbs and lean meat.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Vietnamese cuisine is renowned for its fresh ingredients, balanced flavors, and minimal use of oil. Dishes often incorporate a variety of vegetables and herbs, lean proteins, and rice, creating a light and nutritious meal profile. Popular dishes like pho, fresh spring rolls (goi cuon), and various salads (goi) highlight these healthy components.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Vietnamese\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Vietnamese cuisine is renowned for its fresh ingredients, balanced flavors, and minimal use of oil. Dishes often incorporate a variety of vegetables and herbs, lean proteins, and rice, creating a light and nutritious meal profile. Popular dishes like pho, fresh spring rolls (goi cuon), and various salads (goi) highlight these healthy components.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Myanmar, Thai, Lao"}'::jsonb),
('mc:a known tausug dish. it is also called the black soup: because of its color. it is served hot and spicy, made from beef or chicken, flavored with ginder, tumeric, and burned coconut meat.:::tiula itum', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'a known tausug dish. it is also called the black soup: because of its color. it is served hot and spicy, made from beef or chicken, flavored with ginder, tumeric, and burned coconut meat.', 'Tiula Itum', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Tiula Itum is a traditional Tausug dish from the Sulu Archipelago in the southern Philippines. Its distinctive black color comes from the use of burned or charred coconut meat, which is combined with spices such as ginger and turmeric to create a flavorful and aromatic soup.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Tiula Itum\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Tiula Itum is a traditional Tausug dish from the Sulu Archipelago in the southern Philippines. Its distinctive black color comes from the use of burned or charred coconut meat, which is combined with spices such as ginger and turmeric to create a flavorful and aromatic soup.\n\n• Linat-an: A Visayan soup dish made with pork or chicken, vegetables like gabi (taro), corn, and green leafy vegetables, seasoned with ginger and other spices. It is comforting and mildly flavored.\n• Batchoy: A hearty noodle soup originating from Iloilo, Batchoy is made with a flavorful pork and beef broth, round noodles, and topped with pork offal, crushed pork cracklings, garlic, and an egg. It’s savory, rich, and often served hot.\n• Piarun: Also known as “Piyanggang,” this is a dish from the Tausug people of Mindanao, made with chicken or fish marinated in spices and burnt coconut, then grilled or stewed. It has a rich, smoky flavor with a complex blend of spices.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Linat-an, Batchoy, Piarun"}'::jsonb),
