('mc:gas that cause the fruit to ripen::::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'gas that cause the fruit to ripen:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Ethylene is a natural plant hormone that plays a key role in the ripening process of fruits. It is produced by fruits themselves as they ripen and can also be released by other fruits nearby, leading to a chain reaction of ripening in a group of fruits.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"ethylene\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Ethylene is a natural plant hormone that plays a key role in the ripening process of fruits. It is produced by fruits themselves as they ripen and can also be released by other fruits nearby, leading to a chain reaction of ripening in a group of fruits.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: carbon monoxide, propane, nitrogen"}'::jsonb),
('mc:the following are functional subsystems of a traditional food service operation, except::::packaging', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the following are functional subsystems of a traditional food service operation, except:', 'Packaging', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Packaging is not typically considered a functional subsystem within a traditional food service operation. While food packaging is essential in certain contexts (such as retail food products or take-out services), traditional food service operations primarily focus on preparing and serving food rather than packaging it for distribution or sale.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Packaging\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Packaging is not typically considered a functional subsystem within a traditional food service operation. While food packaging is essential in certain contexts (such as retail food products or take-out services), traditional food service operations primarily focus on preparing and serving food rather than packaging it for distribution or sale.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Production, Storage and Inventory, Sanitation and Maintenance"}'::jsonb),
