('mc:the transformation of raw or processed foods into an acceptable finished product.:::food production', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the transformation of raw or processed foods into an acceptable finished product.', 'Food Production', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Food production involves the actual preparation and assembly of ingredients and materials to create finished dishes or food items that are ready to be served to customers. It encompasses all activities related to cooking, baking, assembling, and garnishing food according to recipes and standards.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Food Production\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Food production involves the actual preparation and assembly of ingredients and materials to create finished dishes or food items that are ready to be served to customers. It encompasses all activities related to cooking, baking, assembling, and garnishing food according to recipes and standards.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Standardized recipe, Kitchen brigade, Forecasting"}'::jsonb),
('mc:the transformation of raw or processed foods into an acceptable finished product.:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the transformation of raw or processed foods into an acceptable finished product.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Food production involves the actual preparation and assembly of ingredients and materials to create finished dishes or food items that are ready to be served to customers. It encompasses all activities related to cooking, baking, assembling, and garnishing food according to recipes and standards.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Food Production\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Food production involves the actual preparation and assembly of ingredients and materials to create finished dishes or food items that are ready to be served to customers. It encompasses all activities related to cooking, baking, assembling, and garnishing food according to recipes and standards.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Standardized recipe, Kitchen brigade, Forecasting"}'::jsonb),
('mc:what do you call it when fruits continue to ripen after harvesting (such as bananas)::::climacteric', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'what do you call it when fruits continue to ripen after harvesting (such as bananas):', 'Climacteric', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Climacteric fruits are capable of undergoing a ripening process even after being harvested. Bananas are a classic example of climacteric fruits; they are typically harvested while still green and then ripen further during storage due to the production of ethylene gas.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Climacteric\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Climacteric fruits are capable of undergoing a ripening process even after being harvested. Bananas are a classic example of climacteric fruits; they are typically harvested while still green and then ripen further during storage due to the production of ethylene gas.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Unripe, Artificial ripening process, Degree of maturity"}'::jsonb),
('mc:the following are dietary management for morning sickness during pregnancy except::::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the following are dietary management for morning sickness during pregnancy except:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Citrus juice (high acidity), water (trigger the gag reflex), milk (aggravates nausea), coffee, or tea (can stimulate stomach acid secretion) if experiencing nausea.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Citrus juice, water, milk coffee or tea if experiencing nausea\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Citrus juice (high acidity), water (trigger the gag reflex), milk (aggravates nausea), coffee, or tea (can stimulate stomach acid secretion) if experiencing nausea.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Frequent small meals, Dry toast or crackers, Avoidance of foods with offensive odors"}'::jsonb),
('mc:what do you call it when fruits continue to ripen after harvesting (such as bananas)::::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'what do you call it when fruits continue to ripen after harvesting (such as bananas):', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Climacteric fruits are capable of undergoing a ripening process even after being harvested. Bananas are a classic example of climacteric fruits; they are typically harvested while still green and then ripen further during storage due to the production of ethylene gas.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Climacteric\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Climacteric fruits are capable of undergoing a ripening process even after being harvested. Bananas are a classic example of climacteric fruits; they are typically harvested while still green and then ripen further during storage due to the production of ethylene gas.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Unripe, Artificial ripening process, Degree of maturity"}'::jsonb),
('mc:desirable characteristic of fish::::crystal clear eyes; bright colored gills; whole fins; resilient flesh', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'desirable characteristic of fish:', 'Crystal clear eyes; bright colored gills; whole fins; resilient flesh', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The desirable characteristics of fresh fish are typically indicated by:","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Crystal clear eyes; bright colored gills; whole fins; resilient flesh\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The desirable characteristics of fresh fish are typically indicated by:\n\n• Crystal clear eyes\n• Bright colored (red) gills\n• Whole and intact fins\n• Resilient and firm flesh","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sunken eyes; fishy smell; slimy gills; dry fins, Moist eyes; dark colored gills; fresh smell; remains indented when poked, all of the above"}'::jsonb),
('mc:desirable characteristic of fish::::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'desirable characteristic of fish:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The desirable characteristics of fresh fish are typically indicated by:","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Crystal clear eyes; bright colored gills; whole fins; resilient flesh\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The desirable characteristics of fresh fish are typically indicated by:\n\n• Crystal clear eyes\n• Bright colored (red) gills\n• Whole and intact fins\n• Resilient and firm flesh","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sunken eyes; fishy smell; slimy gills; dry fins, Moist eyes; dark colored gills; fresh smell; remains indented when poked, all of the above"}'::jsonb),
('mc:the last date on which the product should be used::::expiration', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the last date on which the product should be used:', 'Expiration', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Expiration date is the last date on which the product should be used or consumed. It is often used for products where safety is a concern, indicating that after this date, the product may no longer be safe to consume.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Expiration\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Expiration date is the last date on which the product should be used or consumed. It is often used for products where safety is a concern, indicating that after this date, the product may no longer be safe to consume.\n\n• Best used by: This date indicates the last date recommended for the use of the product at its peak quality. It does not refer to safety but rather optimal quality.\n• Packed on: This date indicates the date on which the product was packed or processed. It helps in tracking the freshness or age of the product.\n• Sell by: This date is the date by which the product should be sold to the consumer. It indicates to the retailer how long to display the product for sale.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Best used by, Packed on, Sell by"}'::jsonb),
('mc:the last date on which the product should be used::::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the last date on which the product should be used:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Expiration date is the last date on which the product should be used or consumed. It is often used for products where safety is a concern, indicating that after this date, the product may no longer be safe to consume.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Expiration\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Expiration date is the last date on which the product should be used or consumed. It is often used for products where safety is a concern, indicating that after this date, the product may no longer be safe to consume.\n\n• Best used by: This date indicates the last date recommended for the use of the product at its peak quality. It does not refer to safety but rather optimal quality.\n• Packed on: This date indicates the date on which the product was packed or processed. It helps in tracking the freshness or age of the product.\n• Sell by: This date is the date by which the product should be sold to the consumer. It indicates to the retailer how long to display the product for sale.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Best used by, Packed on, Sell by"}'::jsonb),
('mc:which of the following is true about basal metabolic rate?:::fever increases bmr', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'which of the following is true about basal metabolic rate?', 'Fever increases BMR', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"When the body develops a fever, its internal temperature rises, which accelerates enzymatic and cellular activities to help fight off infection. As a general clinical rule, BMR increases by approximately 7% for every 1°F rise in body temperature.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Fever increases BMR\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"When the body develops a fever, its internal temperature rises, which accelerates enzymatic and cellular activities to help fight off infection. As a general clinical rule, BMR increases by approximately 7% for every 1°F rise in body temperature.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Pregnancy decreases BMR, Fasting increases BMR, Females have higher BMR than males"}'::jsonb),
('mc:you have only dried ground herb available, but the recipe call for 1 tbsp fresh herb. how will you substitute dried for fresh?:::use less - 1 tsp dried', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'you have only dried ground herb available, but the recipe call for 1 tbsp fresh herb. how will you substitute dried for fresh?', 'Use less - 1 tsp dried', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"When substituting dried herbs for fresh herbs in a recipe, the general rule of thumb is to use less dried herb than the amount of fresh herb called for. This is because dried herbs are more concentrated in flavor than fresh herbs due to the drying process.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Use less - 1 tsp dried\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"When substituting dried herbs for fresh herbs in a recipe, the general rule of thumb is to use less dried herb than the amount of fresh herb called for. This is because dried herbs are more concentrated in flavor than fresh herbs due to the drying process.\n\nThe typical substitution ratio is 1 part dried herb for 3 parts fresh herb.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Use the same amount, Use more - 2 tbsp, Use less – ½ tbsp"}'::jsonb),
('mc:you have only dried ground herb available, but the recipe call for 1 tbsp fresh herb. how will you substitute dried for fresh?:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'you have only dried ground herb available, but the recipe call for 1 tbsp fresh herb. how will you substitute dried for fresh?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"When substituting dried herbs for fresh herbs in a recipe, the general rule of thumb is to use less dried herb than the amount of fresh herb called for. This is because dried herbs are more concentrated in flavor than fresh herbs due to the drying process.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Use less - 1 tsp dried\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"When substituting dried herbs for fresh herbs in a recipe, the general rule of thumb is to use less dried herb than the amount of fresh herb called for. This is because dried herbs are more concentrated in flavor than fresh herbs due to the drying process.\n\nThe typical substitution ratio is 1 part dried herb for 3 parts fresh herb.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Use the same amount, Use more - 2 tbsp, Use less – ½ tbsp"}'::jsonb),
('mc:a prediction of food needs for a day or other specific period of time.:::forecasting', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'a prediction of food needs for a day or other specific period of time.', 'Forecasting', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Forecasting in the context of food service involves estimating the quantity of food that will be required to meet customer demand over a certain period. This helps in planning and preparing the right amount of food to minimize waste while ensuring that enough food is available to meet customer orders.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Forecasting\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Forecasting in the context of food service involves estimating the quantity of food that will be required to meet customer demand over a certain period. This helps in planning and preparing the right amount of food to minimize waste while ensuring that enough food is available to meet customer orders.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Purchasing, Production, Recipe writing"}'::jsonb),
