('mc:which one of the following statements is incorrect?:::according to pinggang pinoy, meat, fish, and alternatives should comprise one-third of the plate', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'which one of the following statements is incorrect?', 'According to Pinggang Pinoy, meat, fish, and alternatives should comprise one-third of the plate', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Answer should be 1/6 ~ 17%.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"According to Pinggang Pinoy, meat, fish, and alternatives should comprise one-third of the plate\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Answer should be 1/6 ~ 17%.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: According to Pinggang Pinoy, half of our plate should be include fruits and vegetable, The statement \"Eat lots of fruits and vegetables\" is a food-based dietary guideline, The statement \"Eat less sodium-no more than 2g/day\" is not food-based dietary guideline"}'::jsonb),
('mc:which of the following conditions accounts for the most non-communicable disease worldwide?:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'which of the following conditions accounts for the most non-communicable disease worldwide?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"According to official global statistics from the World Health Organization (WHO), Non-Communicable Diseases (NCDs) are responsible for approximately 74% of all deaths worldwide.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Cardiovascular disease\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"According to official global statistics from the World Health Organization (WHO), Non-Communicable Diseases (NCDs) are responsible for approximately 74% of all deaths worldwide.\n\nAmong these conditions, cardiovascular diseases (CVDs) are the absolute leading cause of mortality and morbidity globally:\n• Cardiovascular Diseases (CVDs): Account for the vast majority of NCD deaths, causing roughly 17.9 to 19 million deaths annually (primarily driven by ischemic heart disease and strokes).\n• Cancers: Follow as the second largest group, accounting for around 9 to 10 million deaths each year.\n• Chronic Respiratory Diseases: Account for approximately 3.9 to 4 million annual deaths.\n• Diabetes: Accounts for roughly 1.6 to 2 million deaths annually.\n\nTogether, these four groups make up over 80% of all premature NCD-related mortality worldwide.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Breast cancer, Diabetes, Respiratory disease"}'::jsonb),
('mc:the nutriskwela community radio network partners named their stations with words starting with this letter.:::k', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the nutriskwela community radio network partners named their stations with words starting with this letter.', 'K', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The correct answer is the letter K, reflecting the “ka-“ branding convention used across Nutriskwela community radio stations established by the NNC.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"K\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The correct answer is the letter K, reflecting the “ka-“ branding convention used across Nutriskwela community radio stations established by the NNC.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: C, N, M"}'::jsonb),
