('mc:in nutritional assessment, causes of malnutrition must be classified into immediate, underlying and basic causes. food insecurity and poor child care are classified as::::underlying causes', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'in nutritional assessment, causes of malnutrition must be classified into immediate, underlying and basic causes. food insecurity and poor child care are classified as:', 'Underlying causes', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Underlying causes – contributing causes; food security, health services, practices","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Underlying causes\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Underlying causes – contributing causes; food security, health services, practices\n\n• Immediate causes – direct causes; food and care (individual level)\n• Basic causes – societal; political, economic, education etc.\n• Cross-cutting causes","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Immediate causes, Basic cause, Cross-cutting causes"}'::jsonb),
