('mc:it is the practice of analyzing describing a complex phenomenon in terms of phenomena that are held to represent a single or more fundamental level, especially when this is a said to provide a sufficient explanation:::reductionism in research', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'it is the practice of analyzing describing a complex phenomenon in terms of phenomena that are held to represent a single or more fundamental level, especially when this is a said to provide a sufficient explanation', 'Reductionism in research', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Reductionism is a philosophical and scientific approach that breaks down complex systems or phenomena into their smaller, simpler, or more fundamental components. In research (especially in fields like nutritional biochemistry or physiology), it assumes that understanding these isolated, individual parts provides a sufficient explanation for the behavior of the entire system.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Reductionism in research\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Reductionism is a philosophical and scientific approach that breaks down complex systems or phenomena into their smaller, simpler, or more fundamental components. In research (especially in fields like nutritional biochemistry or physiology), it assumes that understanding these isolated, individual parts provides a sufficient explanation for the behavior of the entire system.\n\n• Scientific Method: The systematic, step-by-step process of observing, forming a hypothesis, experimenting, and drawing conclusions to gather knowledge.\n• Research Method: The specific tools, techniques, or procedures used to collect and analyze data (e.g., surveys, randomized controlled trials, or double-blind studies).\n• Research Design: The overall structural blueprint or strategy chosen to integrate the different components of a study in a coherent and logical way (e.g., cross-sectional, cohort, or experimental design).","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Research method, Scientific method, Research design"}'::jsonb),
