('mc:it refers to the person''s unique pattern of living::::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'it refers to the person''s unique pattern of living:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Lifestyle - Total way of living","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Lifestyle\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Lifestyle - Total way of living\n\n• Health - state of complete physical, mental, and social well-being\n• Wellness - Active pursuit of optimal health through conscious choice\n• Behavior - Individual actions or reactions","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Health, Wellness, Behavior"}'::jsonb),
('mc:an approach to health and well-being which focuses on identiying risk factors and prevention to minimize risk.:::preventive approach', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'an approach to health and well-being which focuses on identiying risk factors and prevention to minimize risk.', 'Preventive approach', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Preventive approach: This specific model focuses directly on screening populations, identifying underlying risk factors (such as high blood pressure, genetics, or poor diet), and introducing interventions to minimize those risks before a clinical disease develops.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Preventive approach\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Preventive approach: This specific model focuses directly on screening populations, identifying underlying risk factors (such as high blood pressure, genetics, or poor diet), and introducing interventions to minimize those risks before a clinical disease develops.\n\n• Traditional approach: Often referred to as the pathogenic or biomedical model, this approach is reactive. It focuses primarily on diagnosing and treating a disease after symptoms have already manifested.\n• Wellness approach: This is a holistic approach that goes beyond risk minimization. It focuses on actively optimizing positive health, well-being, and lifestyle factors (such as self-actualization, fitness, and stress management) to help an individual thrive, rather than just preventing illness.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Traditional approach, Wellness approach, Avoidance approach"}'::jsonb),
('mc:in conducting mental feeding to daycare students, which nutrition education material is best to use?:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'in conducting mental feeding to daycare students, which nutrition education material is best to use?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Cartoons are colorful and engaging, appropriate for children.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Cartoons\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Cartoons are colorful and engaging, appropriate for children.\n\n• Diorama - formal\n• Comics - individual\n• Caricature - satirical or comic effect.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Diorama, Comics, Caricature"}'::jsonb),
('mc:an approach to health and well-being which focuses on identiying risk factors and prevention to minimize risk.:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'an approach to health and well-being which focuses on identiying risk factors and prevention to minimize risk.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Preventive approach: This specific model focuses directly on screening populations, identifying underlying risk factors (such as high blood pressure, genetics, or poor diet), and introducing interventions to minimize those risks before a clinical disease develops.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Preventive approach\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Preventive approach: This specific model focuses directly on screening populations, identifying underlying risk factors (such as high blood pressure, genetics, or poor diet), and introducing interventions to minimize those risks before a clinical disease develops.\n\n• Traditional approach: Often referred to as the pathogenic or biomedical model, this approach is reactive. It focuses primarily on diagnosing and treating a disease after symptoms have already manifested.\n• Wellness approach: This is a holistic approach that goes beyond risk minimization. It focuses on actively optimizing positive health, well-being, and lifestyle factors (such as self-actualization, fitness, and stress management) to help an individual thrive, rather than just preventing illness.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Traditional approach, Wellness approach, Avoidance approach"}'::jsonb),
('mc:a branch of science dealing with psychological, social, economical, physiological, and medical aspects of aging.:::gerontology', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'a branch of science dealing with psychological, social, economical, physiological, and medical aspects of aging.', 'Gerontology', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Gerontology is the broad, multidisciplinary study of the aging process. It encompasses the biological, psychological, social, economic, physiological, and even political aspects of growing old.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Gerontology\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Gerontology is the broad, multidisciplinary study of the aging process. It encompasses the biological, psychological, social, economic, physiological, and even political aspects of growing old.\n\n• Geriatrics - Medical care of elderly people and their diseases\n• Healthy ageing - Maintaining functional ability and well-being throughout later life.\n• Nutrigenomics - How nutrients affect genes and gene expression","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Geriatrics, Healthy ageing, Nutrigenomics"}'::jsonb),
