('mc:it is a process by which a community identifies its needs or objectives, gives priority to them, develops confidence and will work at them, find resources to deal with them and extends and develops cooperative and collaborative attitude and practices in the community.:::community organizing', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'it is a process by which a community identifies its needs or objectives, gives priority to them, develops confidence and will work at them, find resources to deal with them and extends and develops cooperative and collaborative attitude and practices in the community.', 'Community organizing', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Community organizing is building permanent, local power structures to solve problems.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Community organizing\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Community organizing is building permanent, local power structures to solve problems.\n\n• Community mobilization - Rallying all existing resources to achieve a specific goal.\n• Community participation - Involvement of members in planning and implementation of a project.\n• Community empowerment - Gaining control by community members over the factors affecting their lives.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Community mobilization, Community participation, Community empowerment"}'::jsonb),
