('mc:adoption of local nutrition action plan by the lgu requires::::all of the above', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'adoption of local nutrition action plan by the lgu requires:', 'All of the above', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Formal LNAP adoption by a local government unit requires multiple coordinated steps together: acceptance, approval, and endorsement by the local chief executive to the Sanggunian; sponsorship by a member of the local legislative body; and a resolution filed for adoption and funding.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"All of the above\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Formal LNAP adoption by a local government unit requires multiple coordinated steps together: acceptance, approval, and endorsement by the local chief executive to the Sanggunian; sponsorship by a member of the local legislative body; and a resolution filed for adoption and funding.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Acceptance, approval and endorsement of LCE to Sangguniang Bayan/Panlalawigan, Sponsorship by a member of the local legislative body, Resolution filed for adoption and funding of the LNAP"}'::jsonb),
