of recognition awarded at the regional level to municipalities, cities, or provinces that excel in their annual nutrition performance benchmarks.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Green Banner Award, Consistent Regional Outstanding Winner in Nutrition, National Outstanding Nutrition Award"}'::jsonb),
('mc:in 2014, the national nutrition council governing board approved and adopted the guidelines on local nutrition planning that direct lgus to come up with a local nutrition action plan.:::3 year', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'in 2014, the national nutrition council governing board approved and adopted the guidelines on local nutrition planning that direct lgus to come up with a local nutrition action plan.', '3 year', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The 2014 NNC guidelines for LGU-level Local Nutrition Action Plans, aligning with the local government''s typical elected term of office. Aligning the LNAP''s three-year cycle with local elected officials'' terms helps ensure political ownership and continuity of nutrition planning across the term of local leadership.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"3 year\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The 2014 NNC guidelines for LGU-level Local Nutrition Action Plans, aligning with the local government''s typical elected term of office. Aligning the LNAP''s three-year cycle with local elected officials'' terms helps ensure political ownership and continuity of nutrition planning across the term of local leadership.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: 1 year, 2 year, 4 year"}'::jsonb),
('mc:in 2014, the national nutrition council governing board approved and adopted the guidelines on local nutrition planning that direct lgus to come up with a local nutrition action plan.:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'in 2014, the national nutrition council governing board approved and adopted the guidelines on local nutrition planning that direct lgus to come up with a local nutrition action plan.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The 2014 NNC guidelines for LGU-level Local Nutrition Action Plans, aligning with the local government''s typical elected term of office. Aligning the LNAP''s three-year cycle with local elected officials'' terms helps ensure political ownership and continuity of nutrition planning across the term of local leadership.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"3 year\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The 2014 NNC guidelines for LGU-level Local Nutrition Action Plans, aligning with the local government''s typical elected term of office. Aligning the LNAP''s three-year cycle with local elected officials'' terms helps ensure political ownership and continuity of nutrition planning across the term of local leadership.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: 1 year, 2 year, 4 year"}'::jsonb),
('mc:the lnap is best prepared on the first semester of an election year to ensure that the nutrition agenda is integrated in the executive legislative agenda which becomes the bases for local development plan and in-turn the annual investment plan. this is essential for::::local budgeting', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the lnap is best prepared on the first semester of an election year to ensure that the nutrition agenda is integrated in the executive legislative agenda which becomes the bases for local development plan and in-turn the annual investment plan. this is essential for:', 'Local Budgeting', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Local budgeting because timely integration of the nutrition agenda into the Executive Legislative Agenda ensures that nutrition programs are properly reflected and funded in the subsequent Annual Investment Plan and local budget allocations. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Local Budgeting\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Local budgeting because timely integration of the nutrition agenda into the Executive Legislative Agenda ensures that nutrition programs are properly reflected and funded in the subsequent Annual Investment Plan and local budget allocations. \n\nWhile local planning, implementation, and monitoring/evaluation are all eventually affected by this timing, the question mentioning ELA and AIP points most directly to securing adequate budgeting for nutrition programs.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Local Planning, Local Implementation, Local Monitoring and evaluation"}'::jsonb),
('mc:a bns is trained volunteer community worker with the following qualifications except::::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'a bns is trained volunteer community worker with the following qualifications except:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"At least high school graduate - the law states ‘elementary’ or ‘primary school’ (see PD 1569)","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"At least high school graduate\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"At least high school graduate - the law states ‘elementary’ or ‘primary school’ (see PD 1569)","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Bonadife resident of the barangay, Willingness to serve, part-time or full-time, More than 18 years old, but younger than 60 years old"}'::jsonb),
('mc:the lnap is best prepared on the first semester of an election year to ensure that the nutrition agenda is integrated in the executive legislative agenda which becomes the bases for local development plan and in-turn the annual investment plan. this is essential for::::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the lnap is best prepared on the first semester of an election year to ensure that the nutrition agenda is integrated in the executive legislative agenda which becomes the bases for local development plan and in-turn the annual investment plan. this is essential for:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Local budgeting because timely integration of the nutrition agenda into the Executive Legislative Agenda ensures that nutrition programs are properly reflected and funded in the subsequent Annual Investment Plan and local budget allocations. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Local Budgeting\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Local budgeting because timely integration of the nutrition agenda into the Executive Legislative Agenda ensures that nutrition programs are properly reflected and funded in the subsequent Annual Investment Plan and local budget allocations. \n\nWhile local planning, implementation, and monitoring/evaluation are all eventually affected by this timing, the question mentioning ELA and AIP points most directly to securing adequate budgeting for nutrition programs.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Local Planning, Local Implementation, Local Monitoring and evaluation"}'::jsonb),
