('mc:in planning for a food for work intervention, the following key decision points must be considered, except::::will the assistance be in cash or kind?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'in planning for a food for work intervention, the following key decision points must be considered, except:', 'Will the assistance be in cash or kind?', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"By definition, food-for-work is already established as a food (in-kind) assistance modality, so this cash-versus-kind question does not apply as a decision point within a program already defined as food-based.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Will the assistance be in cash or kind?\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"By definition, food-for-work is already established as a food (in-kind) assistance modality, so this cash-versus-kind question does not apply as a decision point within a program already defined as food-based.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: What food commodities will be used?, What volume of food will be given for each unit of work?, What complementary services will be provided?"}'::jsonb),
