('mc:a decision-making process of identifying potential nutrition problems and needs of a specific population group, analyzing possible ways of preventing and controlling malnutrition, allocating resources based on needs and expectations, and taking deliberate action to address nutritional problems, including those related to monitoring and evaluation.:::nutrition program management', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'a decision-making process of identifying potential nutrition problems and needs of a specific population group, analyzing possible ways of preventing and controlling malnutrition, allocating resources based on needs and expectations, and taking deliberate action to address nutritional problems, including those related to monitoring and evaluation.', 'Nutrition Program Management', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Nutrition Program Management is executing, supervising, and coordinating all activities to achieve program goals.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Nutrition Program Management\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Nutrition Program Management is executing, supervising, and coordinating all activities to achieve program goals.\n\n• Nutrition Program Planning - designing the specific program: defining objectives, strategies, resources, and implementation steps.\n• Nutrition Intervention - specific action designed to directly improve nutritional status (e.g., supplementation, education).\n• Food and Nutrition Planning - macro-level process to set national/regional policies and strategies for food supply and consumption.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Nutrition Program Planning, Nutrition Intervention, Food and Nutrition Planning"}'::jsonb),
