('mc:a researcher wants to conduct a study wherein men with coronary artery disease and a comparable group of men without coronary artery disease were asked about their prior use of aspirin. this is an example of which type of study?:::case control', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'a researcher wants to conduct a study wherein men with coronary artery disease and a comparable group of men without coronary artery disease were asked about their prior use of aspirin. this is an example of which type of study?', 'Case control', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"This scenario perfectly illustrates the design of a case-control study based on two defining factors:","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Case control\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"This scenario perfectly illustrates the design of a case-control study based on two defining factors:\n\n• Selection by Outcome (Disease Status): The researcher selects participants based on whether they already have the condition of interest. The \"cases\" are the men with coronary artery disease, and the \"controls\" are the comparable group of men without the disease.\n• Retrospective Assessment: The researcher then looks backward in time (\"asked about their prior use of aspirin\") to compare how frequently each group was exposed to the factor being studied.\n\n• Ecological study - Comparing the average per capita salt intake across ten different countries to the average national hypertension rate in those same countries.\n• Randomized clinical trial - Dividing 500 patients with a specific disease into two groups: one receiving a new drug and one receiving a placebo (or standard treatment), and then following both groups for a year to see which group has a better outcome.\n• Case series - A doctor publishing a report detailing the clinical presentation, diagnosis, treatment, and outcomes for three unusual patients presenting with the same rare cluster of symptoms at their clinic over a six-month period.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Ecological study, Randomized clinial trial, Case series"}'::jsonb),
