both groups for a year to see which group has a better outcome.\n• Case series - A doctor publishing a report detailing the clinical presentation, diagnosis, treatment, and outcomes for three unusual patients presenting with the same rare cluster of symptoms at their clinic over a six-month period.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Ecological study, Randomized clinial trial, Case series"}'::jsonb),
('mc:it refers to the epidemiological approach which explains the occurence, nature, and extent of a disease::::man-agent-environment triad', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'it refers to the epidemiological approach which explains the occurence, nature, and extent of a disease:', 'Man-Agent-Environment Triad', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Man-Agent-Environment triad - epidemiological model; analyzing disease causation via host, pathogen, and surroundings.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Man-Agent-Environment Triad\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Man-Agent-Environment triad - epidemiological model; analyzing disease causation via host, pathogen, and surroundings.\n\n• Triple A approach - cycle for planning: assessment, analysis, action\n• UNICEF framework - three-level causes of malnutrition: basic, underlying, and immediate (food/health).\n• Undernutrition infection cycle - vicious spiral where poor nutrition weakens immunity, increasing infection risk, which worsens nutrition.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Triple A approach, UNICEF framework, Undernutrition infection cycle"}'::jsonb),
