('mc:a community health center provides comprehensive services including primary care, dental care, and a public health nutritionist. a patient with recently diagnosed pre-diabetes is referred by their primary care physician to the nutritionist for a consultation. in the scenario, what type of healthcare delivery model does this best represent, and what is the primary benefit for the patient?:::model: integrated healthcare system. benefit: coordinated care and communication between the physician and nutritionist are streamlined.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'a community health center provides comprehensive services including primary care, dental care, and a public health nutritionist. a patient with recently diagnosed pre-diabetes is referred by their primary care physician to the nutritionist for a consultation. in the scenario, what type of healthcare delivery model does this best represent, and what is the primary benefit for the patient?', 'Model: Integrated Healthcare System. Benefit: Coordinated care and communication between the physician and nutritionist are streamlined.', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The correct answer is that this represents an Integrated Healthcare System, whose primary benefit is coordinated care and streamlined communication between the physician and nutritionist within the same facility/system. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Model: Integrated Healthcare System. Benefit: Coordinated care and communication between the physician and nutritionist are streamlined.\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The correct answer is that this represents an Integrated Healthcare System, whose primary benefit is coordinated care and streamlined communication between the physician and nutritionist within the same facility/system. \n\n• Fee-for-service describes a payment model emphasizing provider choice, unrelated to the coordinated, in-house referral pathway described. \n• Specialized healthcare system would emphasize focused expert care in one narrow area, not the coordinated, multi-service nature of the scenario. \n• Direct primary care describes a flat-fee payment model for physician access, unrelated to the multidisciplinary, coordinated referral pattern described.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Model: Fee-for-Service. Benefit: The patient has a wide choice of providers., Model: Specialized Healthcare System. Benefit: The patient receives highly focused care from an expert in one specific area., Model: Direct Primary Care. Benefit: The patient pays a flat monthly fee for unlimited access to the physician."}'::jsonb),
