('mc:which of the following is an example of a secondary data source in nutrition research?:::data collected from a nutrition surveillance system', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'which of the following is an example of a secondary data source in nutrition research?', 'Data collected from a nutrition surveillance system', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Primary (newly collected)","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Data collected from a nutrition surveillance system\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Primary (newly collected)\nSecondary (previously collected, reused)\n\n• A newly conducted survey – primary\n• Published research articles – secondary in a broader sense\n• Results from a clinical trial – primary\n• Data collected from a nutrition surveillance system – secondary from previously collected surveillance data with an ongoing, general monitoring purpose and later reused/reanalyzed by researchers","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: A newly conducted survey, Published research articles, Results from a clinical trial"}'::jsonb),
('mc:which of the following is an example of a secondary data source in nutrition research?:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'which of the following is an example of a secondary data source in nutrition research?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Primary (newly collected)","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Data collected from a nutrition surveillance system\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Primary (newly collected)\nSecondary (previously collected, reused)\n\n• A newly conducted survey – primary\n• Published research articles – secondary in a broader sense\n• Results from a clinical trial – primary\n• Data collected from a nutrition surveillance system – secondary from previously collected surveillance data with an ongoing, general monitoring purpose and later reused/reanalyzed by researchers","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: A newly conducted survey, Published research articles, Results from a clinical trial"}'::jsonb),
('mc:what is the main difference between a cohort study and a case-control study in nutrition research?:::a cohort study follows a group over time, while a case-control study looks back at past exposure', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'what is the main difference between a cohort study and a case-control study in nutrition research?', 'A cohort study follows a group over time, while a case-control study looks back at past exposure', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"A cohort study follows a group forward over time (from exposure toward outcome), while a case-control study looks backward from an already-occurred outcome to past exposures.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"A cohort study follows a group over time, while a case-control study looks back at past exposure\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"A cohort study follows a group forward over time (from exposure toward outcome), while a case-control study looks backward from an already-occurred outcome to past exposures.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: A cohort study involves intervention, while a case-control study does not, A cohort study is more expensive than a case-control study, A cohort study uses randomization, while a case-control study does not"}'::jsonb),
('mc:what is the main difference between a cohort study and a case-control study in nutrition research?:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'what is the main difference between a cohort study and a case-control study in nutrition research?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"A cohort study follows a group forward over time (from exposure toward outcome), while a case-control study looks backward from an already-occurred outcome to past exposures.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"A cohort study follows a group over time, while a case-control study looks back at past exposure\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"A cohort study follows a group forward over time (from exposure toward outcome), while a case-control study looks backward from an already-occurred outcome to past exposures.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: A cohort study involves intervention, while a case-control study does not, A cohort study is more expensive than a case-control study, A cohort study uses randomization, while a case-control study does not"}'::jsonb),
('mc:a key aspect of designing a nutrition surveillance system is to determine::::the specific population group to be monitored', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'a key aspect of designing a nutrition surveillance system is to determine:', 'The specific population group to be monitored', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The specific population group to be monitored is correct because defining the target population is a foundational design decision that shapes every other aspect of a surveillance system, including what indicators to collect and how. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"The specific population group to be monitored\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The specific population group to be monitored is correct because defining the target population is a foundational design decision that shapes every other aspect of a surveillance system, including what indicators to collect and how. \n\n• The exact number of individuals to include is more of a sampling/statistical detail; \n• The optimal time of day for data collection and ideal food sample storage temperature are narrow, operational/logistical details.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: The exact number of individuals to be included in the study, The optimal time of day for data collection, The ideal temperature for storing food samples"}'::jsonb),
('mc:a key aspect of designing a nutrition surveillance system is to determine::::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'a key aspect of designing a nutrition surveillance system is to determine:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The specific population group to be monitored is correct because defining the target population is a foundational design decision that shapes every other aspect of a surveillance system, including what indicators to collect and how. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"The specific population group to be monitored\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The specific population group to be monitored is correct because defining the target population is a foundational design decision that shapes every other aspect of a surveillance system, including what indicators to collect and how. \n\n• The exact number of individuals to include is more of a sampling/statistical detail; \n• The optimal time of day for data collection and ideal food sample storage temperature are narrow, operational/logistical details.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: The exact number of individuals to be included in the study, The optimal time of day for data collection, The ideal temperature for storing food samples"}'::jsonb),
('mc:a community nutritionist is tasked with designing an intervention to reduce childhood obesity in a low-income urban neighborhood. a preliminary needs assessment revealed that the primary barriers are limited access to affordable, fresh produce and a lack of safe, accessible recreational spaces. according to the socio-ecological model and the principles of community nutrition, which of the following interventions would be most effective and sustainable?:::advocating for a city policy that provides incentives for mobile vendores to sell fresh produce in the neighborhood, while also collaborating with the parks and recreation department to improve a local playground', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'a community nutritionist is tasked with designing an intervention to reduce childhood obesity in a low-income urban neighborhood. a preliminary needs assessment revealed that the primary barriers are limited access to affordable, fresh produce and a lack of safe, accessible recreational spaces. according to the socio-ecological model and the principles of community nutrition, which of the following interventions would be most effective and sustainable?', 'Advocating for a city policy that provides incentives for mobile vendores to sell fresh produce in the neighborhood, while also collaborating with the parks and recreation department to improve a local playground', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Advocating for a city policy incentivizing mobile produce vendors while also improving a local playground addresses multiple levels of the socio-ecological model (SEM) simultaneously: policy/environmental level (vendor incentives) and physical/community environment level (playground improvement), matching both identified barriers (limited produce access and lack of safe recreational space). ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Advocating for a city policy that provides incentives for mobile vendores to sell fresh produce in the neighborhood, while also collaborating with the parks and recreation department to improve a local playground\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Advocating for a city policy incentivizing mobile produce vendors while also improving a local playground addresses multiple levels of the socio-ecological model (SEM) simultaneously: policy/environmental level (vendor incentives) and physical/community environment level (playground improvement), matching both identified barriers (limited produce access and lack of safe recreational space). \n\n• A nutrition education class alone addresses only the individual/interpersonal level, ignoring the structural access barriers identified in the assessment. \n• Partnering with a grocery store addresses food access but does not address the recreational space barrier. \n• A school-based program addresses only the school setting and misses the broader community-level access and environment barriers identified. \n\nThe SEM framework explains how multiple levels of influence: from individual factors to broad social structures interact to determine a health outcome, such as malnutrition.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Implementing a weekly nutrition education for parents at a local community center., Partnering with a local grocery store to create a \"healthy eating\" ailse and offering discount coupons for fruits and vegetables, Developing a school-based program that offers free healthy snacks and incorporates a daily physical activity period"}'::jsonb),
('mc:a community nutritionist is tasked with designing an intervention to reduce childhood obesity in a low-income urban neighborhood. a preliminary needs assessment revealed that the primary barriers are limited access to affordable, fresh produce and a lack of safe, accessible recreational spaces. according to the socio-ecological model and the principles of community nutrition, which of the following interventions would be most effective and sustainable?:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'a community nutritionist is tasked with designing an intervention to reduce childhood obesity in a low-income urban neighborhood. a preliminary needs assessment revealed that the primary barriers are limited access to affordable, fresh produce and a lack of safe, accessible recreational spaces. according to the socio-ecological model and the principles of community nutrition, which of the following interventions would be most effective and sustainable?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Advocating for a city policy incentivizing mobile produce vendors while also improving a local playground addresses multiple levels of the socio-ecological model (SEM) simultaneously: policy/environmental level (vendor incentives) and physical/community environment level (playground improvement), matching both identified barriers (limited produce access and lack of safe recreational space). ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Advocating for a city policy that provides incentives for mobile vendores to sell fresh produce in the neighborhood, while also collaborating with the parks and recreation department to improve a local playground\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Advocating for a city policy incentivizing mobile produce vendors while also improving a local playground addresses multiple levels of the socio-ecological model (SEM) simultaneously: policy/environmental level (vendor incentives) and physical/community environment level (playground improvement), matching both identified barriers (limited produce access and lack of safe recreational space). \n\n• A nutrition education class alone addresses only the individual/interpersonal level, ignoring the structural access barriers identified in the assessment. \n• Partnering with a grocery store addresses food access but does not address the recreational space barrier. \n• A school-based program addresses only the school setting and misses the broader community-level access and environment barriers identified. \n\nThe SEM framework explains how multiple levels of influence: from individual factors to broad social structures interact to determine a health outcome, such as malnutrition.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Implementing a weekly nutrition education for parents at a local community center., Partnering with a local grocery store to create a \"healthy eating\" ailse and offering discount coupons for fruits and vegetables, Developing a school-based program that offers free healthy snacks and incorporates a daily physical activity period"}'::jsonb),
('mc:according to the philippine nutrition and dietetics act of 2016 (ra 10862), which of the following is a specific function that a public health nutritionist-dietitian is mandated to perform in collaboration with other professionals?:::conducting nutrition program planning, implementation, and evaluation at a community or institutional level', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'according to the philippine nutrition and dietetics act of 2016 (ra 10862), which of the following is a specific function that a public health nutritionist-dietitian is mandated to perform in collaboration with other professionals?', 'Conducting nutrition program planning, implementation, and evaluation at a community or institutional level', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The correct answer is conducting nutrition program planning, implementation, and evaluation at a community or institutional level, which falls within the legally mandated scope of practice for public health nutritionist-dietitians under the Philippine Nutrition and Dietetics Act of 2016 (RA 10862).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Conducting nutrition program planning, implementation, and evaluation at a community or institutional level\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The correct answer is conducting nutrition program planning, implementation, and evaluation at a community or institutional level, which falls within the legally mandated scope of practice for public health nutritionist-dietitians under the Philippine Nutrition and Dietetics Act of 2016 (RA 10862).","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Prescribing specific drug medications for nutritional deficiencies, Leading a multidisciplinary team in a surgical ward, Owning and operating a food manufacturing company that produces fortified products"}'::jsonb),
('mc:according to the philippine nutrition and dietetics act of 2016 (ra 10862), which of the following is a specific function that a public health nutritionist-dietitian is mandated to perform in collaboration with other professionals?:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'according to the philippine nutrition and dietetics act of 2016 (ra 10862), which of the following is a specific function that a public health nutritionist-dietitian is mandated to perform in collaboration with other professionals?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The correct answer is conducting nutrition program planning, implementation, and evaluation at a community or institutional level, which falls within the legally mandated scope of practice for public health nutritionist-dietitians under the Philippine Nutrition and Dietetics Act of 2016 (RA 10862).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Conducting nutrition program planning, implementation, and evaluation at a community or institutional level\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The correct answer is conducting nutrition program planning, implementation, and evaluation at a community or institutional level, which falls within the legally mandated scope of practice for public health nutritionist-dietitians under the Philippine Nutrition and Dietetics Act of 2016 (RA 10862).","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Prescribing specific drug medications for nutritional deficiencies, Leading a multidisciplinary team in a surgical ward, Owning and operating a food manufacturing company that produces fortified products"}'::jsonb),
('mc:a public health nutritionist is evaluating a long-standing food assistance program for pregnant women. the program has high participation rates, but a recent health survey shows that participants'' fruit and vegetable intake remains well below recommended levels. which of the following principles of community nutrition is most likely being neglected, and what is the most appropriate next step?:::principle neglected: cultural competency. next step: conduct focus groups with participants to understand their food preferences and dietary habits, and adjust the food packages accordingly.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'a public health nutritionist is evaluating a long-standing food assistance program for pregnant women. the program has high participation rates, but a recent health survey shows that participants'' fruit and vegetable intake remains well below recommended levels. which of the following principles of community nutrition is most likely being neglected, and what is the most appropriate next step?', 'Principle Neglected: Cultural competency. Next Step: Conduct focus groups with participants to understand their food preferences and dietary habits, and adjust the food packages accordingly.', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The correct answer is that the principle neglected is cultural competency, and the appropriate next step is conducting focus groups to understand participants'' food preferences and dietary habits and adjusting food packages accordingly. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Principle Neglected: Cultural competency. Next Step: Conduct focus groups with participants to understand their food preferences and dietary habits, and adjust the food packages accordingly.\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The correct answer is that the principle neglected is cultural competency, and the appropriate next step is conducting focus groups to understand participants'' food preferences and dietary habits and adjusting food packages accordingly. \n\nHigh participation with persistently poor dietary outcomes suggests the food assistance being provided may not align with what participants actually want or will consistently consume, pointing to a cultural/preference mismatch rather than a participation or awareness problem.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Principle Neglected: Outcome-based evaluation. Next Step: Implement a more rigorous evaluation protocol to measure changes in health indicators like blood pressure and BMI., Principle Neglected: Community empowerment. Next Step: Train participants to become peer-educators and advocates for healthy eating within their own social networks., Principle Neglected: The ecological perspective. Next Step: Broaden the program to include a walking club and cooking demonstrations to address multiple factors influencing food choices."}'::jsonb),
