ly poor dietary outcomes suggests the food assistance being provided may not align with what participants actually want or will consistently consume, pointing to a cultural/preference mismatch rather than a participation or awareness problem.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Principle Neglected: Outcome-based evaluation. Next Step: Implement a more rigorous evaluation protocol to measure changes in health indicators like blood pressure and BMI., Principle Neglected: Community empowerment. Next Step: Train participants to become peer-educators and advocates for healthy eating within their own social networks., Principle Neglected: The ecological perspective. Next Step: Broaden the program to include a walking club and cooking demonstrations to address multiple factors influencing food choices."}'::jsonb)
