('mc:rh, a 70year old female, admitted with a diagnosis of cvd infarct left frontal lobe, weight: 65 kg. height 5’4 “ gsc glasgow coma scale 8 the attending physician gave a diet prescription tf ensure 6 scoops in 230 ml water divided into 6 feedings ensure 9 grams per scoop = 38.5 calories 5.16 grams carbohydrates 1.43 grams protein fats 1.26 grams per scoop what is the bmi of mr. rh?:::24.6', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'rh, a 70year old female, admitted with a diagnosis of cvd infarct left frontal lobe, weight: 65 kg. height 5’4 “ gsc glasgow coma scale 8 the attending physician gave a diet prescription tf ensure 6 scoops in 230 ml water divided into 6 feedings ensure 9 grams per scoop = 38.5 calories 5.16 grams carbohydrates 1.43 grams protein fats 1.26 grams per scoop what is the bmi of mr. rh?', '24.6', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"To calculate the Body Mass Index (BMI), use the standard formula: BMI = Weight (kg) / Height (m²).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"24.6\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"To calculate the Body Mass Index (BMI), use the standard formula: BMI = Weight (kg) / Height (m²).\n1. Convert Height to Inches:\n\t• 5 feet 4 inches = 64 inches\n2. Standard Metric Conversion Steps:\n\t• Precise Conversion: 64 inches × 0.0254 = 1.6256 meters\n\t• Height Squared = 1.6256 meters x 1.6256 meters = 2.6426\n• BMI = 65 kg / 2.6426 = 24.59 ~ 24.6","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: 23.4, 25.0, 25.1"}'::jsonb),
