('mc:for atonic constipation, the following are the medical nutrition therapy required except::::low fiber, agar – agar', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'for atonic constipation, the following are the medical nutrition therapy required except:', 'Low Fiber, agar – agar', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"A low-fiber diet reduces stool bulk and slows down intestinal transit, which would severely worsen atonic constipation. Agar-agar, while a thickening agent, is a hydrocolloid that acts as a structural soluble fiber; pairing it with \"Low Fiber\" forms a contradictory and clinically incorrect dietary prescription.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Low Fiber, agar – agar\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"A low-fiber diet reduces stool bulk and slows down intestinal transit, which would severely worsen atonic constipation. Agar-agar, while a thickening agent, is a hydrocolloid that acts as a structural soluble fiber; pairing it with \"Low Fiber\" forms a contradictory and clinically incorrect dietary prescription.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Probiotics, High Fiber, agar – agar, High Fiber, Liberal Fruits"}'::jsonb),
('mc:to avoid conflict in authority, all workers should::::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'to avoid conflict in authority, all workers should:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Unity of command requires each worker to know the person to whom they are directly responsible, helping avoid conflicting authority.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Know to whom they are directly responsible\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Unity of command requires each worker to know the person to whom they are directly responsible, helping avoid conflicting authority.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Be directly responsible to the head of the department, Cooperate with each other, Be rotated in different sections"}'::jsonb),
