('mc:the following foods have moderate to low in tyramine except::::beer and ale', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the following foods have moderate to low in tyramine except:', 'Beer and Ale', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"In standard clinical dietetic manuals, beer and ale (especially tap, draft, unpasteurized, or micro-brewed varieties) are classified under the Strictly Avoid / High-Tyramine category. Fermented alcohol contains high concentrations of yeast byproducts that trigger severe monoamine accumulation. Because they belong to the high-risk category, they are the absolute exception to the \"moderate-to-low\" group listed in the question.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Beer and Ale\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"In standard clinical dietetic manuals, beer and ale (especially tap, draft, unpasteurized, or micro-brewed varieties) are classified under the Strictly Avoid / High-Tyramine category. Fermented alcohol contains high concentrations of yeast byproducts that trigger severe monoamine accumulation. Because they belong to the high-risk category, they are the absolute exception to the \"moderate-to-low\" group listed in the question.\n\n\t• Peanuts & Buttermilk: Fresh nuts, commercial peanut butter, and cultured dairy products like buttermilk or sour cream contain small, manageable amounts of tyramine, making them safe to consume in moderate or restricted amounts.\n\t• Soy sauce: While commercial soy sauce is traditionally high in tyramine, standard commercial food tables allow it in very tiny, limited amounts (such as 1 teaspoon) or classify it beneath the danger threshold compared to unfiltered yeast beverages. Therefore, the examiner isolated Beer and Ale as the primary high-risk danger substance.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Soy sauce, Buttermilk, Peanuts"}'::jsonb),
('mc:the following foods have moderate to low in tyramine except::::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the following foods have moderate to low in tyramine except:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"In standard clinical dietetic manuals, beer and ale (especially tap, draft, unpasteurized, or micro-brewed varieties) are classified under the Strictly Avoid / High-Tyramine category. Fermented alcohol contains high concentrations of yeast byproducts that trigger severe monoamine accumulation. Because they belong to the high-risk category, they are the absolute exception to the \"moderate-to-low\" group listed in the question.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Beer and Ale\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"In standard clinical dietetic manuals, beer and ale (especially tap, draft, unpasteurized, or micro-brewed varieties) are classified under the Strictly Avoid / High-Tyramine category. Fermented alcohol contains high concentrations of yeast byproducts that trigger severe monoamine accumulation. Because they belong to the high-risk category, they are the absolute exception to the \"moderate-to-low\" group listed in the question.\n\n\t• Peanuts & Buttermilk: Fresh nuts, commercial peanut butter, and cultured dairy products like buttermilk or sour cream contain small, manageable amounts of tyramine, making them safe to consume in moderate or restricted amounts.\n\t• Soy sauce: While commercial soy sauce is traditionally high in tyramine, standard commercial food tables allow it in very tiny, limited amounts (such as 1 teaspoon) or classify it beneath the danger threshold compared to unfiltered yeast beverages. Therefore, the examiner isolated Beer and Ale as the primary high-risk danger substance.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Soy sauce, Buttermilk, Peanuts"}'::jsonb),
('mc:pl is a 35-year-old male who drinks occasionally (5 bottles of beer two to three times a week) and recently had an executive check-up. his uric acid level showed 6.5 mg/dl, and he has complained of pain in the lower knees. which medical condition could this be?:::gout', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'pl is a 35-year-old male who drinks occasionally (5 bottles of beer two to three times a week) and recently had an executive check-up. his uric acid level showed 6.5 mg/dl, and he has complained of pain in the lower knees. which medical condition could this be?', 'Gout', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Gout is a type of inflammatory arthritis triggered by the accumulation of monosodium urate crystals in the joints. While PL''s uric acid level of 6.5 mg/dL sits at the upper end of the normal range (often defined as up to 7.0 mg/dL for men), a patient can experience acute gout flare-ups even with normal serum values during an attack. His significant lifestyle risk factor—drinking 5 bottles of beer multiple times a week—is a primary trigger. Beer is exceptionally rich in purines and contains alcohol, both of which accelerate purine breakdown into uric acid while simultaneously blocking the kidneys from flushing it out, leading to localized joint pain like his knee complaints.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Gout\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Gout is a type of inflammatory arthritis triggered by the accumulation of monosodium urate crystals in the joints. While PL''s uric acid level of 6.5 mg/dL sits at the upper end of the normal range (often defined as up to 7.0 mg/dL for men), a patient can experience acute gout flare-ups even with normal serum values during an attack. His significant lifestyle risk factor—drinking 5 bottles of beer multiple times a week—is a primary trigger. Beer is exceptionally rich in purines and contains alcohol, both of which accelerate purine breakdown into uric acid while simultaneously blocking the kidneys from flushing it out, leading to localized joint pain like his knee complaints.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Rheumatoid Arthritis, Osteoarthritis, Leukemia"}'::jsonb),
('mc:pl is a 35-year-old male who drinks occasionally (5 bottles of beer two to three times a week) and recently had an executive check-up. his uric acid level showed 6.5 mg/dl, and he has complained of pain in the lower knees. which medical condition could this be?:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'pl is a 35-year-old male who drinks occasionally (5 bottles of beer two to three times a week) and recently had an executive check-up. his uric acid level showed 6.5 mg/dl, and he has complained of pain in the lower knees. which medical condition could this be?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Gout is a type of inflammatory arthritis triggered by the accumulation of monosodium urate crystals in the joints. While PL''s uric acid level of 6.5 mg/dL sits at the upper end of the normal range (often defined as up to 7.0 mg/dL for men), a patient can experience acute gout flare-ups even with normal serum values during an attack. His significant lifestyle risk factor—drinking 5 bottles of beer multiple times a week—is a primary trigger. Beer is exceptionally rich in purines and contains alcohol, both of which accelerate purine breakdown into uric acid while simultaneously blocking the kidneys from flushing it out, leading to localized joint pain like his knee complaints.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Gout\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Gout is a type of inflammatory arthritis triggered by the accumulation of monosodium urate crystals in the joints. While PL''s uric acid level of 6.5 mg/dL sits at the upper end of the normal range (often defined as up to 7.0 mg/dL for men), a patient can experience acute gout flare-ups even with normal serum values during an attack. His significant lifestyle risk factor—drinking 5 bottles of beer multiple times a week—is a primary trigger. Beer is exceptionally rich in purines and contains alcohol, both of which accelerate purine breakdown into uric acid while simultaneously blocking the kidneys from flushing it out, leading to localized joint pain like his knee complaints.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Rheumatoid Arthritis, Osteoarthritis, Leukemia"}'::jsonb),
('mc:fodmaps is indicated for nutrition management of ibd, the following examples of fod maps except::::inulin', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'fodmaps is indicated for nutrition management of ibd, the following examples of fod maps except:', 'Inulin', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Inulin is a polymer of fructose molecules linked by beta-(2,1) bonds with a terminal glucose molecule. Human small intestinal enterocytes lack the brush border hydrolase (inulase) required to cleave these beta-linkages, allowing inulin to pass intact into the colon where it undergoes rapid and excessive osmotic fermentation by resident microbiota, producing hydrogen, methane, and carbon dioxide gases that trigger irritable bowel symptoms.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Inulin\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Inulin is a polymer of fructose molecules linked by beta-(2,1) bonds with a terminal glucose molecule. Human small intestinal enterocytes lack the brush border hydrolase (inulase) required to cleave these beta-linkages, allowing inulin to pass intact into the colon where it undergoes rapid and excessive osmotic fermentation by resident microbiota, producing hydrogen, methane, and carbon dioxide gases that trigger irritable bowel symptoms.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Corn syrup, Ice cream, Avocado"}'::jsonb),
('mc:fodmaps is indicated for nutrition management of ibd, the following examples of fod maps except::::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'fodmaps is indicated for nutrition management of ibd, the following examples of fod maps except:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Inulin is a polymer of fructose molecules linked by beta-(2,1) bonds with a terminal glucose molecule. Human small intestinal enterocytes lack the brush border hydrolase (inulase) required to cleave these beta-linkages, allowing inulin to pass intact into the colon where it undergoes rapid and excessive osmotic fermentation by resident microbiota, producing hydrogen, methane, and carbon dioxide gases that trigger irritable bowel symptoms.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Inulin\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Inulin is a polymer of fructose molecules linked by beta-(2,1) bonds with a terminal glucose molecule. Human small intestinal enterocytes lack the brush border hydrolase (inulase) required to cleave these beta-linkages, allowing inulin to pass intact into the colon where it undergoes rapid and excessive osmotic fermentation by resident microbiota, producing hydrogen, methane, and carbon dioxide gases that trigger irritable bowel symptoms.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Corn syrup, Ice cream, Avocado"}'::jsonb),
('mc:which of the following is a disease specific formula which may contains hmb ( beta hydroxy beta methylbutyrate ):::juvenaid', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'which of the following is a disease specific formula which may contains hmb ( beta hydroxy beta methylbutyrate )', 'Juvenaid', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Juvenaid is a disease-specific medical nutrition therapeutic powder manufactured by Abbott. It is specifically formulated to promote wound healing and support lean muscle tissue building in patients experiencing muscle wasting from chronic illnesses (such as HIV/AIDS or cancer cachexia) or recovering from surgery and severe wounds.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Juvenaid\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Juvenaid is a disease-specific medical nutrition therapeutic powder manufactured by Abbott. It is specifically formulated to promote wound healing and support lean muscle tissue building in patients experiencing muscle wasting from chronic illnesses (such as HIV/AIDS or cancer cachexia) or recovering from surgery and severe wounds.\n\nIts targeted clinical formula contains HMB (Beta-Hydroxy-Beta-Methylbutyrate), an active metabolite of the branched-chain amino acid leucine that stops muscle protein breakdown and accelerates tissue synthesis, combined with Arginine and Glutamine.\n\n\t• Diabetasol: A diabetes-specific formula designed to manage blood sugar levels using slow-release carbohydrates and fiber.\n\t• Peptamen: A peptide-based elemental formula designed for patients with severely impaired gastrointestinal function and malabsorption.\n\t• Nutren Optimum: A general, premium nutritional formula containing whey protein, probiotics, and fiber aimed at overall immune support and recovery for the elderly or weak.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Nutren Optimum, Peptamen, Diabetasol"}'::jsonb),
('mc:which of the following parameters are indicators of a patient’s nutritional status, except::::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'which of the following parameters are indicators of a patient’s nutritional status, except:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"A food diary is a prospective, self-reported tool filled out by the patient. In clinical nutrition, self-reported food diaries are notoriously prone to severe under-reporting, recall bias, and subjective estimation errors. Therefore, it is classified as a dietary assessment tool rather than a verified, objective indicator of true physical nutritional status.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Food Diary\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"A food diary is a prospective, self-reported tool filled out by the patient. In clinical nutrition, self-reported food diaries are notoriously prone to severe under-reporting, recall bias, and subjective estimation errors. Therefore, it is classified as a dietary assessment tool rather than a verified, objective indicator of true physical nutritional status.\n\n\t• 3-day actual food intake: Unlike a casual food diary, a 3-day actual intake measurement (such as a weighed food record or a hospital-monitored calorie count overseen by medical staff) is a validated, precise indicator of exact energy and macronutrient delivery.\n\t• CBC and Serum Electrolytes: These are objective, laboratory-verified biochemical markers. A Complete Blood Count directly tracks cellular parameters that signal long-term nutrient deficiencies (like iron or B12 anemia), while serum electrolytes reflect acute fluid-metabolic balances inside the body.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: CBC (Complete Blood Count), Serum Electrolytes, 3 day actual food intake"}'::jsonb),
('mc:which of the following is a disease specific formula which may contains hmb ( beta hydroxy beta methylbutyrate ):::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'which of the following is a disease specific formula which may contains hmb ( beta hydroxy beta methylbutyrate )', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Juvenaid is a disease-specific medical nutrition therapeutic powder manufactured by Abbott. It is specifically formulated to promote wound healing and support lean muscle tissue building in patients experiencing muscle wasting from chronic illnesses (such as HIV/AIDS or cancer cachexia) or recovering from surgery and severe wounds.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Juvenaid\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Juvenaid is a disease-specific medical nutrition therapeutic powder manufactured by Abbott. It is specifically formulated to promote wound healing and support lean muscle tissue building in patients experiencing muscle wasting from chronic illnesses (such as HIV/AIDS or cancer cachexia) or recovering from surgery and severe wounds.\n\nIts targeted clinical formula contains HMB (Beta-Hydroxy-Beta-Methylbutyrate), an active metabolite of the branched-chain amino acid leucine that stops muscle protein breakdown and accelerates tissue synthesis, combined with Arginine and Glutamine.\n\n\t• Diabetasol: A diabetes-specific formula designed to manage blood sugar levels using slow-release carbohydrates and fiber.\n\t• Peptamen: A peptide-based elemental formula designed for patients with severely impaired gastrointestinal function and malabsorption.\n\t• Nutren Optimum: A general, premium nutritional formula containing whey protein, probiotics, and fiber aimed at overall immune support and recovery for the elderly or weak.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Nutren Optimum, Peptamen, Diabetasol"}'::jsonb),
('mc:dietary modification for diverticulitis is a low residue diet for the acute phase. which of the following set of foods can be given to the patient?:::papaya and siopao', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'dietary modification for diverticulitis is a low residue diet for the acute phase. which of the following set of foods can be given to the patient?', 'Papaya and Siopao', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Even though papaya is a fruit, ripe papaya contains predominantly soluble fiber and has an incredibly soft, buttery texture that completely breaks down into a smooth liquid in the stomach. In local dietetics, ripe papaya is highly favored in acute GI recovery phases because it is exceptionally easy on the digestive tract and contains papain, a natural enzyme that aids in protein breakdown.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Papaya and Siopao\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Even though papaya is a fruit, ripe papaya contains predominantly soluble fiber and has an incredibly soft, buttery texture that completely breaks down into a smooth liquid in the stomach. In local dietetics, ripe papaya is highly favored in acute GI recovery phases because it is exceptionally easy on the digestive tract and contains papain, a natural enzyme that aids in protein breakdown.\n\nThe white bun of a Siopao is made from highly refined bleached wheat flour with its fiber-rich outer bran layers completely milled away. The filling is typically heavily stewed, shredded, and tenderized meat without coarse roughage. This matches the mechanical requirements of a soft, low-residue diet.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Evaporated Milk and fita biscuit, Ensure Gold and Fita Biscuit, Avocado Shake and Fita Biscuit"}'::jsonb),
('mc:dietary modification for diverticulitis is a low residue diet for the acute phase. which of the following set of foods can be given to the patient?:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'dietary modification for diverticulitis is a low residue diet for the acute phase. which of the following set of foods can be given to the patient?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Even though papaya is a fruit, ripe papaya contains predominantly soluble fiber and has an incredibly soft, buttery texture that completely breaks down into a smooth liquid in the stomach. In local dietetics, ripe papaya is highly favored in acute GI recovery phases because it is exceptionally easy on the digestive tract and contains papain, a natural enzyme that aids in protein breakdown.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Papaya and Siopao\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Even though papaya is a fruit, ripe papaya contains predominantly soluble fiber and has an incredibly soft, buttery texture that completely breaks down into a smooth liquid in the stomach. In local dietetics, ripe papaya is highly favored in acute GI recovery phases because it is exceptionally easy on the digestive tract and contains papain, a natural enzyme that aids in protein breakdown.\n\nThe white bun of a Siopao is made from highly refined bleached wheat flour with its fiber-rich outer bran layers completely milled away. The filling is typically heavily stewed, shredded, and tenderized meat without coarse roughage. This matches the mechanical requirements of a soft, low-residue diet.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Evaporated Milk and fita biscuit, Ensure Gold and Fita Biscuit, Avocado Shake and Fita Biscuit"}'::jsonb),
('mc:documentation is an important aspect of the nutrition care process. when writing in the patient’s chart about the patient’s actual intake, the acceptable ink color should be:::black ink', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'documentation is an important aspect of the nutrition care process. when writing in the patient’s chart about the patient’s actual intake, the acceptable ink color should be', 'Black ink', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Black ink provides the highest level of visual contrast, making it easy to read. More importantly, when physical medical charts are scanned, photocopied, or microfilmed for insurance, legal, or archiving purposes, black ink reproduces perfectly without fading or blurring.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Black ink\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Black ink provides the highest level of visual contrast, making it easy to read. More importantly, when physical medical charts are scanned, photocopied, or microfilmed for insurance, legal, or archiving purposes, black ink reproduces perfectly without fading or blurring.\n\nWhile a sign pen may use black ink, standard \"sign pens\" often use water-based gel or liquid inks that easily smear, bleed through thin charting paper, or run if they accidentally come into contact with fluids (like water or alcohol rubs at a nursing station), which can compromise the integrity of legal medical documents.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Blue ink, Green Ink, Sign pen with black ink"}'::jsonb),
('mc:total lymphocyte count (tlc) is obtained from the results of a cbc and calculated using the formula: (wbc x lymphocytes %) divided by 100. if the wbc is 9.00 x 10^9/l (9,000 cells/µl) and lymphocytes are 7%, compute for the total lymphocyte count (tlc).:::630', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'total lymphocyte count (tlc) is obtained from the results of a cbc and calculated using the formula: (wbc x lymphocytes %) divided by 100. if the wbc is 9.00 x 10^9/l (9,000 cells/µl) and lymphocytes are 7%, compute for the total lymphocyte count (tlc).', '630', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"To compute the Total Lymphocyte Count (TLC) using the specific laboratory math parameters provided in the problem:","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"630\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"To compute the Total Lymphocyte Count (TLC) using the specific laboratory math parameters provided in the problem:\n\n1. Express the WBC count in standard units: A WBC reading of 9.00 represents 9,000 cells/µL.\n2. Apply the given percentage: The lymphocyte differential is 7%.\n3. Run the calculation:\nTLC = (9,000 x 7) / 100 = 630 cells/μL","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: 6.3, 6300, 63.333"}'::jsonb),
('mc:a coddled egg is one which has been::::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'a coddled egg is one which has been:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"A coddled egg is gently cooked by residual heat after the water has been brought to a boil, producing a softly set egg. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"cooked in water after it has stopped boiling\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"A coddled egg is gently cooked by residual heat after the water has been brought to a boil, producing a softly set egg. \n\nProlonged boiling produces a harder-cooked egg rather than a coddled egg.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: cooked in boiling water for 10-12 minutes, cooked slowly in boiling water for 20 minutes, boiled for 5 minutes in a covered pot"}'::jsonb),
