('mc:the soap format is needed when writing the progress notes of dietitians. the following data can be written in the o format except:::subjective global assessment rating = severely malnourished', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the soap format is needed when writing the progress notes of dietitians. the following data can be written in the o format except', 'Subjective Global Assessment rating = Severely Malnourished', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The SOAP (Subjective, Objective, Assessment, Plan) formatting structure used by clinical dietitians separates physical data metrics from clinical diagnoses and analytical tools.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Subjective Global Assessment rating = Severely Malnourished\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The SOAP (Subjective, Objective, Assessment, Plan) formatting structure used by clinical dietitians separates physical data metrics from clinical diagnoses and analytical tools.\n\nThe Subjective Global Assessment (SGA) is a formal clinical evaluation tool that requires a dietitian to synthesize multiple variables (such as historical data, physical wasting signs, and clinical symptoms) into a final diagnostic judgment. Because a final classification like \"Severely Malnourished\" represents an overall clinical interpretation, it must strictly be placed under the Assessment (A) section of the progress notes, not the Objective section.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Height, weight, BMI, Hemoglobin, Hematocrit, Total Lymphocyte Count, Actual Caloric Intake / Actual Protein Intake"}'::jsonb),
('mc:the soap format is needed when writing the progress notes of dietitians. the following data can be written in the o format except:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the soap format is needed when writing the progress notes of dietitians. the following data can be written in the o format except', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The SOAP (Subjective, Objective, Assessment, Plan) formatting structure used by clinical dietitians separates physical data metrics from clinical diagnoses and analytical tools.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Subjective Global Assessment rating = Severely Malnourished\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The SOAP (Subjective, Objective, Assessment, Plan) formatting structure used by clinical dietitians separates physical data metrics from clinical diagnoses and analytical tools.\n\nThe Subjective Global Assessment (SGA) is a formal clinical evaluation tool that requires a dietitian to synthesize multiple variables (such as historical data, physical wasting signs, and clinical symptoms) into a final diagnostic judgment. Because a final classification like \"Severely Malnourished\" represents an overall clinical interpretation, it must strictly be placed under the Assessment (A) section of the progress notes, not the Objective section.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Height, weight, BMI, Hemoglobin, Hematocrit, Total Lymphocyte Count, Actual Caloric Intake / Actual Protein Intake"}'::jsonb),
