('mc:all are types of nonprobability sampling except::::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'all are types of nonprobability sampling except:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Convenience, purposive, and quota sampling are nonprobability methods, meaning population units do not have a known or equal chance of selection, and selection is instead guided by accessibility, judgment, or predetermined quotas. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"cluster sampling\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Convenience, purposive, and quota sampling are nonprobability methods, meaning population units do not have a known or equal chance of selection, and selection is instead guided by accessibility, judgment, or predetermined quotas. \n\nCluster sampling, in contrast, is a probability sampling technique in which naturally occurring groups (clusters) are randomly selected, giving every unit in the population a calculable chance of inclusion.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: convenience sampling, purposive sampling, quota sampling"}'::jsonb),
('mc:the recommended amount of fish and alternatives based on the pinggang pinoy is .:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the recommended amount of fish and alternatives based on the pinggang pinoy is .', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Under the Pinggang Pinoy food exchange guide developed by the DOST Food and Nutrition Research Institute, one serving from the fish and alternatives (\"Grow\") food group, such as a small piece of fish, a matchbox-sized portion of meat, or an equivalent like shrimp or legumes, corresponds to approximately half a cup, consistent with the food guide''s exchange list of household measures (DOST-FNRI, n.d.).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"½ cup\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Under the Pinggang Pinoy food exchange guide developed by the DOST Food and Nutrition Research Institute, one serving from the fish and alternatives (\"Grow\") food group, such as a small piece of fish, a matchbox-sized portion of meat, or an equivalent like shrimp or legumes, corresponds to approximately half a cup, consistent with the food guide''s exchange list of household measures (DOST-FNRI, n.d.).","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: ¼ cup, ⅓ cup, ¾ cup"}'::jsonb),
('mc:which of the following dishes is not included in the three sets of vegetables provided by the may gulay project at affordable prices?:::dinengdeng', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'which of the following dishes is not included in the three sets of vegetables provided by the may gulay project at affordable prices?', 'Dinengdeng', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The Department of Agriculture''s \"May Gulay Project\" was launched to ensure a continuous and stable supply of vegetables at affordable prices (traditionally packed and retailed as pre-cut, hygienic half-kilo sets).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Dinengdeng\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The Department of Agriculture''s \"May Gulay Project\" was launched to ensure a continuous and stable supply of vegetables at affordable prices (traditionally packed and retailed as pre-cut, hygienic half-kilo sets).\n\nThe program officially provides three specific sets of pre-packaged vegetable combinations tailored for classic Filipino dishes:\n1. Pinakbet\n2. Sinigang\n3. Chopsuey","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Pinakbet, Sinigang, Chopsuey"}'::jsonb),
('mc:which of the following dishes is not included in the three sets of vegetables provided by the may gulay project at affordable prices?:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'which of the following dishes is not included in the three sets of vegetables provided by the may gulay project at affordable prices?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The Department of Agriculture''s \"May Gulay Project\" was launched to ensure a continuous and stable supply of vegetables at affordable prices (traditionally packed and retailed as pre-cut, hygienic half-kilo sets).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Dinengdeng\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The Department of Agriculture''s \"May Gulay Project\" was launched to ensure a continuous and stable supply of vegetables at affordable prices (traditionally packed and retailed as pre-cut, hygienic half-kilo sets).\n\nThe program officially provides three specific sets of pre-packaged vegetable combinations tailored for classic Filipino dishes:\n1. Pinakbet\n2. Sinigang\n3. Chopsuey","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Pinakbet, Sinigang, Chopsuey"}'::jsonb),
('mc:in this type of planning approach, the programs are dictated by the mandate, thrusts, and concerns of the sector where the program is lodged.:::sectoral planning', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'in this type of planning approach, the programs are dictated by the mandate, thrusts, and concerns of the sector where the program is lodged.', 'Sectoral planning', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Sectoral planning is an approach in which programs and priorities are determined primarily by the specific mandate and thrust of the government sector or agency implementing them (e.g., health, agriculture, or education) rather than by a shared, cross-sectoral nutrition goal.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Sectoral planning\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Sectoral planning is an approach in which programs and priorities are determined primarily by the specific mandate and thrust of the government sector or agency implementing them (e.g., health, agriculture, or education) rather than by a shared, cross-sectoral nutrition goal.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Nutrition-based development planning, Option C, Community nutrition planning"}'::jsonb),
