('mc:sentence a. illness caused by ingestion of the toxin present in food is called food poisoning. sentence b. botulism is an example of food intoxication.:::both sentences are correct', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'sentence a. illness caused by ingestion of the toxin present in food is called food poisoning. sentence b. botulism is an example of food intoxication.', 'Both sentences are correct', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Food intoxication results from ingesting toxins already present in food. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Both sentences are correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Food intoxication results from ingesting toxins already present in food. \n\nBotulism is a classic example because illness results from ingestion of botulinum toxin.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence A is correct, Sentence B is correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb),
('mc:semolina flour is made from:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'semolina flour is made from', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Semolina is a coarse flour made from durum wheat and is commonly used for pasta and some other wheat products.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Durum wheat\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Semolina is a coarse flour made from durum wheat and is commonly used for pasta and some other wheat products.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Cassava starch, Rootcrop starch, Millet"}'::jsonb),
('mc:sentence a. cream of tartar in corn syrup causes the inversion of lactose. sentence b. acids are responsible for the tiny crystals in fondants.:::sentence b is correct', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'sentence a. cream of tartar in corn syrup causes the inversion of lactose. sentence b. acids are responsible for the tiny crystals in fondants.', 'Sentence B is correct', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Acid can invert sucrose, not lactose. Acids are responsible for preventing or controlling the size of crystals in fondant, rather than creating them.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Sentence B is correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Acid can invert sucrose, not lactose. Acids are responsible for preventing or controlling the size of crystals in fondant, rather than creating them.\n\nIn confectionery, adding an acid—such as cream of tartar, lemon juice, or citric acid—breaks down sucrose into simpler sugars (glucose and fructose) through a process called inversion.\n\nThese simpler sugars physically get in the way of sucrose molecules, which prevents large, crunchy sugar crystals from binding together. This ensures the fondant stays smooth, creamy, and microscopic in texture.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence A is correct, Both sentences are correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb),
('mc:sentence a. cream of tartar in corn syrup causes the inversion of lactose. sentence b. acids are responsible for the tiny crystals in fondants.:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'sentence a. cream of tartar in corn syrup causes the inversion of lactose. sentence b. acids are responsible for the tiny crystals in fondants.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Acid can invert sucrose, not lactose. Acids are responsible for preventing or controlling the size of crystals in fondant, rather than creating them.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Sentence B is correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Acid can invert sucrose, not lactose. Acids are responsible for preventing or controlling the size of crystals in fondant, rather than creating them.\n\nIn confectionery, adding an acid—such as cream of tartar, lemon juice, or citric acid—breaks down sucrose into simpler sugars (glucose and fructose) through a process called inversion.\n\nThese simpler sugars physically get in the way of sucrose molecules, which prevents large, crunchy sugar crystals from binding together. This ensures the fondant stays smooth, creamy, and microscopic in texture.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence A is correct, Both sentences are correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb),
('mc:sentence a. hydrolytic rancidity is brought about by the enzyme lactase. sentence b. hydrolytic rancidity produces free fatty acids.:::sentence b is correct', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'sentence a. hydrolytic rancidity is brought about by the enzyme lactase. sentence b. hydrolytic rancidity produces free fatty acids.', 'Sentence B is correct', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Sentence A is incorrect because hydrolytic rancidity is mainly caused by lipase, not lactase. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Sentence B is correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Sentence A is incorrect because hydrolytic rancidity is mainly caused by lipase, not lactase. \n\nSentence B is correct because hydrolysis of triglycerides releases free fatty acids, which may produce rancid odors and flavors.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence A is correct, Both sentences are correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb),
