('mc:sentence a. broken mayonnaise may be reformed by adding egg yolks. sentence b. the separation of mayonnaise may be caused by too much addition of oil.:::both sentences are correct', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'sentence a. broken mayonnaise may be reformed by adding egg yolks. sentence b. the separation of mayonnaise may be caused by too much addition of oil.', 'Both sentences are correct', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"A broken mayonnaise can often be re-emulsified by starting with an emulsifier such as egg yolk (has lecithin) and slowly incorporating the broken mixture. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Both sentences are correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"A broken mayonnaise can often be re-emulsified by starting with an emulsifier such as egg yolk (has lecithin) and slowly incorporating the broken mixture. \n\nAdding oil too rapidly or in excessive amounts can overwhelm the emulsion and cause separation.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence A is correct, Sentence B is correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb),
