('mc:sentence a. fish has less extractives than red meats. sentence b. fish is commonly eaten with salt, seasoning, and sauces.:::both sentences are correct', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'sentence a. fish has less extractives than red meats. sentence b. fish is commonly eaten with salt, seasoning, and sauces.', 'Both sentences are correct', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Fish generally contains fewer extractives than red meat, contributing to its milder flavor. Salt, seasonings, and sauces are therefore commonly used to enhance fish dishes.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Both sentences are correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Fish generally contains fewer extractives than red meat, contributing to its milder flavor. Salt, seasonings, and sauces are therefore commonly used to enhance fish dishes.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence A is correct, Sentence B is correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb),
