('mc:sentence a. barbeque from loin is less tender and less flavourful than belly. sentence b. belly is more exercise than loin.:::both sentences are correct', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'sentence a. barbeque from loin is less tender and less flavourful than belly. sentence b. belly is more exercise than loin.', 'Both sentences are correct', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Barbeque made from pork loin is naturally more tender in initial structure than pork belly, but it has less flavor and a much higher risk of drying out. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Both sentences are correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Barbeque made from pork loin is naturally more tender in initial structure than pork belly, but it has less flavor and a much higher risk of drying out. \n\nPork belly is usually more flavorful and succulent than loin because it contains more fat and connective tissue. \n\nThe belly muscles are generally subjected to more activity than the relatively tender loin muscles.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence A is correct, Sentence B is correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb),
('mc:sentence a. barbeque from loin is less tender and less flavourful than belly. sentence b. belly is more exercise than loin.:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'sentence a. barbeque from loin is less tender and less flavourful than belly. sentence b. belly is more exercise than loin.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Barbeque made from pork loin is naturally more tender in initial structure than pork belly, but it has less flavor and a much higher risk of drying out. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Both sentences are correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Barbeque made from pork loin is naturally more tender in initial structure than pork belly, but it has less flavor and a much higher risk of drying out. \n\nPork belly is usually more flavorful and succulent than loin because it contains more fat and connective tissue. \n\nThe belly muscles are generally subjected to more activity than the relatively tender loin muscles.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence A is correct, Sentence B is correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb),
('mc:sentence a. during rigor mortis, actomyosin dissociates due to lack of energy. sentence b. rigor mortis is the stiffening of muscle.:::sentence b is correct', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'sentence a. during rigor mortis, actomyosin dissociates due to lack of energy. sentence b. rigor mortis is the stiffening of muscle.', 'Sentence B is correct', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Sentence A is incorrect because rigor mortis involves the formation and persistence of actomyosin cross-bridges when ATP is depleted. Actomyosin does not dissociate because of lack of energy. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Sentence B is correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Sentence A is incorrect because rigor mortis involves the formation and persistence of actomyosin cross-bridges when ATP is depleted. Actomyosin does not dissociate because of lack of energy. \n\nSentence B is correct because rigor mortis is the postmortem stiffening of muscle.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence A is correct, Both sentences are correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb),
('mc:sentence a. during rigor mortis, actomyosin dissociates due to lack of energy. sentence b. rigor mortis is the stiffening of muscle.:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'sentence a. during rigor mortis, actomyosin dissociates due to lack of energy. sentence b. rigor mortis is the stiffening of muscle.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Sentence A is incorrect because rigor mortis involves the formation and persistence of actomyosin cross-bridges when ATP is depleted. Actomyosin does not dissociate because of lack of energy. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Sentence B is correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Sentence A is incorrect because rigor mortis involves the formation and persistence of actomyosin cross-bridges when ATP is depleted. Actomyosin does not dissociate because of lack of energy. \n\nSentence B is correct because rigor mortis is the postmortem stiffening of muscle.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence A is correct, Both sentences are correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb),
('mc:sentence a. papain is a proteolytic enzyme found in papaya. sentence b. papain tenderizes meat by changing gelatin to collagen:::sentence a is correct', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'sentence a. papain is a proteolytic enzyme found in papaya. sentence b. papain tenderizes meat by changing gelatin to collagen', 'Sentence A is correct', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Sentence A is correct because papain is a proteolytic enzyme from papaya. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Sentence A is correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Sentence A is correct because papain is a proteolytic enzyme from papaya. \n\nSentence B is incorrect because papain tenderizes meat by hydrolyzing proteins and elastin at high temperatures. It does not change gelatin into collagen.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence B is correct, Both sentences are correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb),
('mc:sentence a. papain is a proteolytic enzyme found in papaya. sentence b. papain tenderizes meat by changing gelatin to collagen:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'sentence a. papain is a proteolytic enzyme found in papaya. sentence b. papain tenderizes meat by changing gelatin to collagen', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Sentence A is correct because papain is a proteolytic enzyme from papaya. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Sentence A is correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Sentence A is correct because papain is a proteolytic enzyme from papaya. \n\nSentence B is incorrect because papain tenderizes meat by hydrolyzing proteins and elastin at high temperatures. It does not change gelatin into collagen.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence B is correct, Both sentences are correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb),
('mc:sentence a. fish cooks faster than meat. sentence b. this is because fish has less glycogen than meat thus making the muscle less tough.:::sentence a is correct', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'sentence a. fish cooks faster than meat. sentence b. this is because fish has less glycogen than meat thus making the muscle less tough.', 'Sentence A is correct', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Sentence A is correct because fish generally cooks faster than red meat due to its delicate muscle structure and lower connective tissue content. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Sentence A is correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Sentence A is correct because fish generally cooks faster than red meat due to its delicate muscle structure and lower connective tissue content. \n\nSentence B is incorrect because the main reason is not lower glycogen content but the structure and composition of fish muscle. Fish has less connective tissues.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence B is correct, Both sentences are correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb),
('mc:sentence a. fish cooks faster than meat. sentence b. this is because fish has less glycogen than meat thus making the muscle less tough.:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'sentence a. fish cooks faster than meat. sentence b. this is because fish has less glycogen than meat thus making the muscle less tough.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Sentence A is correct because fish generally cooks faster than red meat due to its delicate muscle structure and lower connective tissue content. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Sentence A is correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Sentence A is correct because fish generally cooks faster than red meat due to its delicate muscle structure and lower connective tissue content. \n\nSentence B is incorrect because the main reason is not lower glycogen content but the structure and composition of fish muscle. Fish has less connective tissues.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence B is correct, Both sentences are correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb),
('mc:sentence a. less tender cuts of meat usually contain more connective tissue. sentence b. elastin hydrolyzes during moist heat cooking.:::sentence a is correct', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'sentence a. less tender cuts of meat usually contain more connective tissue. sentence b. elastin hydrolyzes during moist heat cooking.', 'Sentence A is correct', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Sentence A is correct because less tender cuts usually contain more connective tissue. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Sentence A is correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Sentence A is correct because less tender cuts usually contain more connective tissue. \n\nSentence B is incorrect because collagen can be converted to gelatin during moist heating, whereas elastin is much more heat resistant and does not readily tenderize.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence B is correct, Both sentences are correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb),
('mc:sentence a. starch high in amylose will gel while starch high in amylopectin does not gel. sentence b. taro flour, which has a considerable amount of amylopectin, can be used in noodle making.:::both sentences are correct', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'sentence a. starch high in amylose will gel while starch high in amylopectin does not gel. sentence b. taro flour, which has a considerable amount of amylopectin, can be used in noodle making.', 'Both sentences are correct', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Sentence A is correct because amylose has a linear structure that forms strong hydrogen bonds upon cooling, creating a firm gel network.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Both sentences are correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Sentence A is correct because amylose has a linear structure that forms strong hydrogen bonds upon cooling, creating a firm gel network.\n\nAmylopectin has a heavily branched structure that provides high viscosity when hot, but it does not form a strong gel on its own. \n\nSentence B is correct because taro flour contains high levels of amylopectin and provides the necessary cohesive, viscous paste properties useful in certain food applications, including specific types of noodles and binding.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence A is correct, Sentence B is correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb),
('mc:sentence a. starch high in amylose will gel while starch high in amylopectin does not gel. sentence b. taro flour, which has a considerable amount of amylopectin, can be used in noodle making.:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'sentence a. starch high in amylose will gel while starch high in amylopectin does not gel. sentence b. taro flour, which has a considerable amount of amylopectin, can be used in noodle making.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Sentence A is correct because amylose has a linear structure that forms strong hydrogen bonds upon cooling, creating a firm gel network.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Both sentences are correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Sentence A is correct because amylose has a linear structure that forms strong hydrogen bonds upon cooling, creating a firm gel network.\n\nAmylopectin has a heavily branched structure that provides high viscosity when hot, but it does not form a strong gel on its own. \n\nSentence B is correct because taro flour contains high levels of amylopectin and provides the necessary cohesive, viscous paste properties useful in certain food applications, including specific types of noodles and binding.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence A is correct, Sentence B is correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb),
('mc:sentence a. baking soda may be substituted for baking powder. sentence b. baking soda also contains an acid ingredient.:::both sentences are incorrect', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'sentence a. baking soda may be substituted for baking powder. sentence b. baking soda also contains an acid ingredient.', 'Both sentences are incorrect', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Sentence A is incorrect because baking soda can replace baking powder if sufficient acid is also supplied. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Both sentences are incorrect\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Sentence A is incorrect because baking soda can replace baking powder if sufficient acid is also supplied. \n\nSentence B is incorrect because baking soda is alkaline and does not itself contain an acid ingredient.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence A is correct, Sentence B is correct, Both sentences are correct"}'::jsonb),
