('mc:flat yellow noodles made from wheat flour, lye, salt, and water:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'flat yellow noodles made from wheat flour, lye, salt, and water', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Miki is a flat yellow noodle made from wheat flour, water, salt, and alkaline ingredients such as lye water. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Miki\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Miki is a flat yellow noodle made from wheat flour, water, salt, and alkaline ingredients such as lye water. \n\nBihon is rice vermicelli, sotanghon is usually mung-bean starch vermicelli, and canton refers to another style of wheat noodle.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Bihon, Sotanghon, Canton"}'::jsonb),
('mc:raw starch flavor is caused by::::lumping', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'raw starch flavor is caused by:', 'Lumping', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"A raw starch flavor results when a starch mixture form lumps that could be due to inadequate stirring or cooking. Formation of lumps can cause uneven hydration and gelatinization.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Lumping\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"A raw starch flavor results when a starch mixture form lumps that could be due to inadequate stirring or cooking. Formation of lumps can cause uneven hydration and gelatinization.\n\nWhen starch hits hot liquid without proper separation, the outside of a clump gelatinizes instantly.\n\nThis outer sticky layer blocks liquid from reaching the inner starch. The trapped center remains ungelatinized, leaving a distinct raw flour or starch taste in the final dish.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: incorrect measurements of ingredients, vigorous stirring, inadequate stirring"}'::jsonb)
