('mc:which should you start planning for first?:::entrée', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'which should you start planning for first?', 'Entrée', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Meal planning generally starts with the entrée because it is usually the focal point around which the remaining meal components are selected.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Entrée\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Meal planning generally starts with the entrée because it is usually the focal point around which the remaining meal components are selected.\n\nThe main dish dictates the overall flavor profile of the meal. Once the entrée is selected, you can curate appetizers, soups, and salads that complement, cleanse the palate for, or contrast its flavor notes instead of competing with them.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Salads, Appetizer, None of the above"}'::jsonb),
