('mc:basis for recruiting personnel:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'basis for recruiting personnel', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Job description – an organized list of duties, skills and responsibilities required in a specific position. This should be written for every position and should be reviewed and updated periodically.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Job description\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Job description – an organized list of duties, skills and responsibilities required in a specific position. This should be written for every position and should be reviewed and updated periodically.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Performance rating scale, Procedure manual, Organizational chart"}'::jsonb),
('mc:café au lait is similar to which italian coffee concoction:::caffe latte', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'café au lait is similar to which italian coffee concoction', 'Caffe Latte', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Café au lait is coffee served with hot milk and is most similar to caffè latte in the Italian coffee family. It is made by mixing equal parts of strongly brewed coffee (often from a French press or drip filter) and steamed milk.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Caffe Latte\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Café au lait is coffee served with hot milk and is most similar to caffè latte in the Italian coffee family. It is made by mixing equal parts of strongly brewed coffee (often from a French press or drip filter) and steamed milk.\n\n• Macchiato: An espresso shot \"stained\" or marked with just a tiny dollop of frothed milk or foam on top, making it significantly stronger and less milky than a latte.\n• Ristretto: A short, highly concentrated shot of espresso extracted with half the amount of water but using the same amount of coffee grounds, resulting in a sweeter, richer flavor.\n• Espresso: A concentrated, full-bodied coffee shot brewed by forcing hot water under high pressure through finely-ground coffee beans. It contains no milk at all.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Espresso, Macchiato, Ristretto"}'::jsonb),
('mc:café au lait is similar to which italian coffee concoction:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'café au lait is similar to which italian coffee concoction', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Café au lait is coffee served with hot milk and is most similar to caffè latte in the Italian coffee family. It is made by mixing equal parts of strongly brewed coffee (often from a French press or drip filter) and steamed milk.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Caffe Latte\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Café au lait is coffee served with hot milk and is most similar to caffè latte in the Italian coffee family. It is made by mixing equal parts of strongly brewed coffee (often from a French press or drip filter) and steamed milk.\n\n• Macchiato: An espresso shot \"stained\" or marked with just a tiny dollop of frothed milk or foam on top, making it significantly stronger and less milky than a latte.\n• Ristretto: A short, highly concentrated shot of espresso extracted with half the amount of water but using the same amount of coffee grounds, resulting in a sweeter, richer flavor.\n• Espresso: A concentrated, full-bodied coffee shot brewed by forcing hot water under high pressure through finely-ground coffee beans. It contains no milk at all.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Espresso, Macchiato, Ristretto"}'::jsonb),
