('mc:concrete floors in a food service facility are::::both of the above', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'concrete floors in a food service facility are:', 'Both of the above', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Concrete floors are durable and suitable for areas such as storerooms and receiving areas, but they are hard and non-resilient, which can fatigue workers. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Both of the above\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Concrete floors are durable and suitable for areas such as storerooms and receiving areas, but they are hard and non-resilient, which can fatigue workers. \n\nTherefore both statements are correct.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Suitable for storerooms and receiving area, Not resilient and therefore fatiguing to workers, None of the above"}'::jsonb),
