('mc:promotes team spirit of unity and harmony among employees:::principle of esprit de corps', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'promotes team spirit of unity and harmony among employees', 'Principle of esprit de corps', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"According to Henri Fayol''s 14 Principles of Management, Esprit de Corps literally translates to \"group spirit\" or \"team spirit\". This principle dictates that organizations should actively strive to promote team spirit, mutual trust, unity, and harmony among employees to build a cooperative and highly productive work environment.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Principle of esprit de corps\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"According to Henri Fayol''s 14 Principles of Management, Esprit de Corps literally translates to \"group spirit\" or \"team spirit\". This principle dictates that organizations should actively strive to promote team spirit, mutual trust, unity, and harmony among employees to build a cooperative and highly productive work environment.\n\n• Principle of unity of command: States that each employee should receive orders from, and report to, only one direct supervisor to prevent confusion and conflicting instructions.\n• Principle of centralization: Refers to the degree to which decision-making authority is concentrated at the top levels of management versus being dispersed throughout the organization.\n• Principle of unity of direction: States that organizational activities sharing the same objective must be directed by a single manager using a single, unified plan to ensure proper coordination.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Principle of unity of direction, Principle of unity of command, Principle of centralization"}'::jsonb),
('mc:promotes team spirit of unity and harmony among employees:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'promotes team spirit of unity and harmony among employees', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"According to Henri Fayol''s 14 Principles of Management, Esprit de Corps literally translates to \"group spirit\" or \"team spirit\". This principle dictates that organizations should actively strive to promote team spirit, mutual trust, unity, and harmony among employees to build a cooperative and highly productive work environment.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Principle of esprit de corps\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"According to Henri Fayol''s 14 Principles of Management, Esprit de Corps literally translates to \"group spirit\" or \"team spirit\". This principle dictates that organizations should actively strive to promote team spirit, mutual trust, unity, and harmony among employees to build a cooperative and highly productive work environment.\n\n• Principle of unity of command: States that each employee should receive orders from, and report to, only one direct supervisor to prevent confusion and conflicting instructions.\n• Principle of centralization: Refers to the degree to which decision-making authority is concentrated at the top levels of management versus being dispersed throughout the organization.\n• Principle of unity of direction: States that organizational activities sharing the same objective must be directed by a single manager using a single, unified plan to ensure proper coordination.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Principle of unity of direction, Principle of unity of command, Principle of centralization"}'::jsonb),
('mc:the architectural plan of spaces on a floor of a building is called the::::floor plan', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the architectural plan of spaces on a floor of a building is called the:', 'Floor plan', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"A floor plan is a scaled, top-down diagram showing the arrangement of rooms, spaces, and structural features on a specific floor of a building.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Floor plan\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"A floor plan is a scaled, top-down diagram showing the arrangement of rooms, spaces, and structural features on a specific floor of a building.\n\nA blueprint is a general reproduction or copy of any technical drawing.\n\nA lay-out is a broader term for the overall arrangement of elements, not strictly the architectural drawing of a building floor.\n\nFoodservice design refers specifically to commercial kitchen and dining facility planning.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Blueprint, Lay-out, Foodservice design"}'::jsonb),
('mc:the optimum working tº is between::::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the optimum working tº is between:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The optimum working temperature for productivity and human comfort in an office environment is typically between 65–73ºF (18–23ºC).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"65-73ºF\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The optimum working temperature for productivity and human comfort in an office environment is typically between 65–73ºF (18–23ºC).","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: 60-71ºF, 3-72ºF, 67-74ºF"}'::jsonb),
('mc:the architectural plan of spaces on a floor of a building is called the::::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the architectural plan of spaces on a floor of a building is called the:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"A floor plan is a scaled, top-down diagram showing the arrangement of rooms, spaces, and structural features on a specific floor of a building.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Floor plan\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"A floor plan is a scaled, top-down diagram showing the arrangement of rooms, spaces, and structural features on a specific floor of a building.\n\nA blueprint is a general reproduction or copy of any technical drawing.\n\nA lay-out is a broader term for the overall arrangement of elements, not strictly the architectural drawing of a building floor.\n\nFoodservice design refers specifically to commercial kitchen and dining facility planning.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Blueprint, Lay-out, Foodservice design"}'::jsonb),
('mc:the principle that refers to the number of subordinates who report directly to a higher executive:::span of control', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the principle that refers to the number of subordinates who report directly to a higher executive', 'Span of control', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Span of control is the number of subordinates who report directly to a manager or higher executive.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Span of control\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Span of control is the number of subordinates who report directly to a manager or higher executive.\n\n• Departmentalization: The process of dividing an organization into distinct sections or departments based on functions, products, or geographic areas (e.g., separating a facility into a Kitchen Department, Purchasing Department, and Accounting Department).\n• Unity of command: The management principle stating that each subordinate should receive orders from, and be accountable to, only one direct supervisor to prevent conflicting instructions.\n• Delegation: The act of assigning authority, responsibility, and specific tasks from a higher-level manager down to a subordinate.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Departmentalization, Unity of command, Delegation"}'::jsonb),
('mc:the principle that refers to the number of subordinates who report directly to a higher executive:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the principle that refers to the number of subordinates who report directly to a higher executive', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Span of control is the number of subordinates who report directly to a manager or higher executive.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Span of control\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Span of control is the number of subordinates who report directly to a manager or higher executive.\n\n• Departmentalization: The process of dividing an organization into distinct sections or departments based on functions, products, or geographic areas (e.g., separating a facility into a Kitchen Department, Purchasing Department, and Accounting Department).\n• Unity of command: The management principle stating that each subordinate should receive orders from, and be accountable to, only one direct supervisor to prevent conflicting instructions.\n• Delegation: The act of assigning authority, responsibility, and specific tasks from a higher-level manager down to a subordinate.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Departmentalization, Unity of command, Delegation"}'::jsonb),
('mc:budget that is used to determine if funds will be available when needed::::cash', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'budget that is used to determine if funds will be available when needed:', 'Cash', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Cash Budget tracks expected cash inflows and outflows. Its primary purpose is to manage liquidity, allowing managers to forecast cash positions and ensure that enough cash is available when needed to meet immediate obligations like payroll or supplier bills. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Cash\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Cash Budget tracks expected cash inflows and outflows. Its primary purpose is to manage liquidity, allowing managers to forecast cash positions and ensure that enough cash is available when needed to meet immediate obligations like payroll or supplier bills. \n\n• Master Budget: This is a comprehensive, overarching financial plan that consolidates all individual functional budgets (including operating, capital, and financial budgets). \n• Operating Budget: This focuses on day-to-day revenue-generating activities, such as projected sales, production, and routine operating expenses. It does not measure actual cash timing.\n• Capital Budget: This is a long-term plan dedicated to major asset investments, such as buying property, new machinery, or technology","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Master, Operating, Capital"}'::jsonb),
('mc:budget that is used to determine if funds will be available when needed::::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'budget that is used to determine if funds will be available when needed:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Cash Budget tracks expected cash inflows and outflows. Its primary purpose is to manage liquidity, allowing managers to forecast cash positions and ensure that enough cash is available when needed to meet immediate obligations like payroll or supplier bills. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Cash\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Cash Budget tracks expected cash inflows and outflows. Its primary purpose is to manage liquidity, allowing managers to forecast cash positions and ensure that enough cash is available when needed to meet immediate obligations like payroll or supplier bills. \n\n• Master Budget: This is a comprehensive, overarching financial plan that consolidates all individual functional budgets (including operating, capital, and financial budgets). \n• Operating Budget: This focuses on day-to-day revenue-generating activities, such as projected sales, production, and routine operating expenses. It does not measure actual cash timing.\n• Capital Budget: This is a long-term plan dedicated to major asset investments, such as buying property, new machinery, or technology","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Master, Operating, Capital"}'::jsonb),
('mc:information which is/are useful for time and motion studies::::all of the above', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'information which is/are useful for time and motion studies:', 'all of the above', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Job breakdowns, process charts, and flow charts can all provide information useful in time-and-motion studies.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"all of the above\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Job breakdowns, process charts, and flow charts can all provide information useful in time-and-motion studies.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: job breakdown, process chart, flow chart"}'::jsonb),
('mc:broiler is a term used to refer to:::chicken', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'broiler is a term used to refer to', 'Chicken', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Broiler is a market term for a young chicken suitable for broiling or similar dry-heat cooking.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Chicken\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Broiler is a market term for a young chicken suitable for broiling or similar dry-heat cooking.\n\n• Young or middle-aged pork: Swine or pigs are categorized into culinary and market classes such as suckling pig (lechon de leche), boar, sow, or gilt. The term \"broiler\" is never applied to pork or any mammalian livestock.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Young pork, Middle-aged pork, All of the above"}'::jsonb),
('mc:broiler is a term used to refer to:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'broiler is a term used to refer to', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Broiler is a market term for a young chicken suitable for broiling or similar dry-heat cooking.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Chicken\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Broiler is a market term for a young chicken suitable for broiling or similar dry-heat cooking.\n\n• Young or middle-aged pork: Swine or pigs are categorized into culinary and market classes such as suckling pig (lechon de leche), boar, sow, or gilt. The term \"broiler\" is never applied to pork or any mammalian livestock.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Young pork, Middle-aged pork, All of the above"}'::jsonb),
('mc:it is a special type of broiler used in foodservice that makes use of overhead infrared heating.:::salamander', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'it is a special type of broiler used in foodservice that makes use of overhead infrared heating.', 'Salamander', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"A salamander is a specialized broiler that applies intense overhead infrared or radiant heat for browning, finishing, or broiling.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Salamander\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"A salamander is a specialized broiler that applies intense overhead infrared or radiant heat for browning, finishing, or broiling.\n\nIn professional kitchens and food service operations, it is primarily used for rapid top-browning, melting cheese (such as on French onion soup or lasagna), crisping meat fat, or lightly caramelizing sugar coatings without cooking the interior of the dish further.\n\n• Rotisserie: A cooking appliance or attachment where meat (often whole chickens) is skewered on a spit and slowly rotated over or next to a heat source for even roasting.\n• Bain-marie: A hot water bath system used in commercial food lines to hold cooked food at safe, warm serving temperatures. It does not cook, broil, or emit infrared heat.\n• Microwave: An appliance that cooks food by using electromagnetic radiation waves to excite water molecules within the food, generating friction and volumetric heat rather than overhead radiant grilling.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Baine Marie, Rotisserie, Microwave"}'::jsonb),
('mc:it is a special type of broiler used in foodservice that makes use of overhead infrared heating.:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'it is a special type of broiler used in foodservice that makes use of overhead infrared heating.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"A salamander is a specialized broiler that applies intense overhead infrared or radiant heat for browning, finishing, or broiling.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Salamander\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"A salamander is a specialized broiler that applies intense overhead infrared or radiant heat for browning, finishing, or broiling.\n\nIn professional kitchens and food service operations, it is primarily used for rapid top-browning, melting cheese (such as on French onion soup or lasagna), crisping meat fat, or lightly caramelizing sugar coatings without cooking the interior of the dish further.\n\n• Rotisserie: A cooking appliance or attachment where meat (often whole chickens) is skewered on a spit and slowly rotated over or next to a heat source for even roasting.\n• Bain-marie: A hot water bath system used in commercial food lines to hold cooked food at safe, warm serving temperatures. It does not cook, broil, or emit infrared heat.\n• Microwave: An appliance that cooks food by using electromagnetic radiation waves to excite water molecules within the food, generating friction and volumetric heat rather than overhead radiant grilling.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Baine Marie, Rotisserie, Microwave"}'::jsonb),
('mc:roasted suckling pig:::lechon de leche', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'roasted suckling pig', 'Lechon de leche', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"In culinary terms and Spanish-Filipino food culture, a suckling pig is a young piglet that has fed exclusively on its mother''s milk (hence the word leche, meaning milk). When this young, tender piglet is slowly roasted whole over charcoal, it is specifically designated as Lechon de leche.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Lechon de leche\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"In culinary terms and Spanish-Filipino food culture, a suckling pig is a young piglet that has fed exclusively on its mother''s milk (hence the word leche, meaning milk). When this young, tender piglet is slowly roasted whole over charcoal, it is specifically designated as Lechon de leche.\n\n• Pritchon: A portmanteau of the words prito (fried) and lechon. It refers to a whole or chopped piglet that is deep-fried in oil rather than roasted over charcoal, often carved and wrapped in pita or mandarin pancakes.\n• Lechon: A broad, generic term for any whole roasted pig. A standard lechon usually involves a fully matured, adult market hog rather than a young suckling piglet.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Pritchon, Lechon, None of the above"}'::jsonb),
('mc:roasted suckling pig:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'roasted suckling pig', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"In culinary terms and Spanish-Filipino food culture, a suckling pig is a young piglet that has fed exclusively on its mother''s milk (hence the word leche, meaning milk). When this young, tender piglet is slowly roasted whole over charcoal, it is specifically designated as Lechon de leche.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Lechon de leche\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"In culinary terms and Spanish-Filipino food culture, a suckling pig is a young piglet that has fed exclusively on its mother''s milk (hence the word leche, meaning milk). When this young, tender piglet is slowly roasted whole over charcoal, it is specifically designated as Lechon de leche.\n\n• Pritchon: A portmanteau of the words prito (fried) and lechon. It refers to a whole or chopped piglet that is deep-fried in oil rather than roasted over charcoal, often carved and wrapped in pita or mandarin pancakes.\n• Lechon: A broad, generic term for any whole roasted pig. A standard lechon usually involves a fully matured, adult market hog rather than a young suckling piglet.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Pritchon, Lechon, None of the above"}'::jsonb),
('mc:the place calasiao is associated with what food.:::puto', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the place calasiao is associated with what food.', 'Puto', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Calasiao, a municipality in Pangasinan, is widely celebrated as the \"Puto Capital of the Philippines\".","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Puto\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Calasiao, a municipality in Pangasinan, is widely celebrated as the \"Puto Capital of the Philippines\".\n\nPuto Calasiao is a bite-sized, semi-sweet steamed rice cake. It stands out because it is traditionally made using fermented short-grain glutinous rice (galapong), giving it a distinctively soft, chewy, and slightly springy texture.\n\nWhile the classic white version is the most iconic, it is also sold in variations like ube (purple yam), pandan, cheese, mango, and strawberry.\n\n• Buro: A fermented rice dish (often mixed with fish or shrimp) that is a famous condiment in neighboring Pampanga and other parts of Central/Northern Luzon.\n• Patupat: A sweet Ilocano delicacy made of glutinous rice cooked in sugarcane juice and wrapped in a woven pouch of coconut or palm leaves. While found in Pangasinan, it is not uniquely synonymous with Calasiao the way puto is.\n• Tocino: A sweet, cured pork breakfast meat most famously associated with Pampanga (the culinary capital of the Philippines).","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Buro, Tocino, Patupat"}'::jsonb)
ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.ai_explanation_cache (id, question_hash, front_text, back_text, options, explanation, breakdown, created_at, question_text, user_answer, is_correct, ai_explanation) VALUES
('mc:the place calasiao is associated with what food.:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'the place calasiao is associated with what food.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Calasiao, a municipality in Pangasinan, is widely celebrated as the \"Puto Capital of the Philippines\".","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Puto\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Calasiao, a municipality in Pangasinan, is widely celebrated as the \"Puto Capital of the Philippines\".\n\nPuto Calasiao is a bite-sized, semi-sweet steamed rice cake. It stands out because it is traditionally made using fermented short-grain glutinous rice (galapong), giving it a distinctively soft, chewy, and slightly springy texture.\n\nWhile the classic white version is the most iconic, it is also sold in variations like ube (purple yam), pandan, cheese, mango, and strawberry.\n\n• Buro: A fermented rice dish (often mixed with fish or shrimp) that is a famous condiment in neighboring Pampanga and other parts of Central/Northern Luzon.\n• Patupat: A sweet Ilocano delicacy made of glutinous rice cooked in sugarcane juice and wrapped in a woven pouch of coconut or palm leaves. While found in Pangasinan, it is not uniquely synonymous with Calasiao the way puto is.\n• Tocino: A sweet, cured pork breakfast meat most famously associated with Pampanga (the culinary capital of the Philippines).","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Buro, Tocino, Patupat"}'::jsonb),
('mc:intrinsic factors that have the capacity to either stimulate or retard the growth of microorganisms in food:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'intrinsic factors that have the capacity to either stimulate or retard the growth of microorganisms in food', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Intrinsic factors are properties inherent in the food itself.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"pH, redox potential, water activity and antimicrobial substances\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Intrinsic factors are properties inherent in the food itself.\n\nThese are:\n• pH\n• Moisture\n• Redox potential\n• Nutrient Content\n• Antimicrobial constituents\n• Biological structures","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Temperature, relative humidity, pH and water activity, Redox potential, atmosphere, relative humidity and antimicrobial substances, Relative humidity, atmosphere and temperature"}'::jsonb),
('mc:linat-an is closest to the dish::::nilaga', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'linat-an is closest to the dish:', 'Nilaga', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Linat-an is a traditional boiled pork soup dish native to the Visayas and Mindanao regions. Structurally and visually, it is almost identical to the Tagalog Nilaga. Both dishes involve simmering tough cuts of meat (usually pork ribs or beef) with an abundance of clear broth, paired with vegetables like cabbage, potatoes, leafy greens, and green beans.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Nilaga\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Linat-an is a traditional boiled pork soup dish native to the Visayas and Mindanao regions. Structurally and visually, it is almost identical to the Tagalog Nilaga. Both dishes involve simmering tough cuts of meat (usually pork ribs or beef) with an abundance of clear broth, paired with vegetables like cabbage, potatoes, leafy greens, and green beans.\n\nThe primary difference lies in the flavor aromatics: while Nilaga relies heavily on onions and whole black peppercorns, Linat-an incorporates distinct regional ingredients like lemongrass (tanglad), ginger, and sometimes red bell peppers or taro (gabi) to give the clear broth a more fragrant, refreshing, and slightly sweet flavor profile.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Kare-kare, Pochero, Cardillo"}'::jsonb),
('mc:linat-an is closest to the dish::::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'linat-an is closest to the dish:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Linat-an is a traditional boiled pork soup dish native to the Visayas and Mindanao regions. Structurally and visually, it is almost identical to the Tagalog Nilaga. Both dishes involve simmering tough cuts of meat (usually pork ribs or beef) with an abundance of clear broth, paired with vegetables like cabbage, potatoes, leafy greens, and green beans.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Nilaga\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Linat-an is a traditional boiled pork soup dish native to the Visayas and Mindanao regions. Structurally and visually, it is almost identical to the Tagalog Nilaga. Both dishes involve simmering tough cuts of meat (usually pork ribs or beef) with an abundance of clear broth, paired with vegetables like cabbage, potatoes, leafy greens, and green beans.\n\nThe primary difference lies in the flavor aromatics: while Nilaga relies heavily on onions and whole black peppercorns, Linat-an incorporates distinct regional ingredients like lemongrass (tanglad), ginger, and sometimes red bell peppers or taro (gabi) to give the clear broth a more fragrant, refreshing, and slightly sweet flavor profile.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Kare-kare, Pochero, Cardillo"}'::jsonb),
('mc:sentence a. fruits become more brilliant in color during ripening. sentence b. this is due to the breakdown of chlorophyll and exposes the underlying pigments.:::both sentences are correct', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'sentence a. fruits become more brilliant in color during ripening. sentence b. this is due to the breakdown of chlorophyll and exposes the underlying pigments.', 'Both sentences are correct', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"During ripening, chlorophyll breaks down and green color diminishes, revealing or allowing the development of pigments such as carotenoids and anthocyanins, which make many fruits appear brighter or more intensely colored.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Both sentences are correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"During ripening, chlorophyll breaks down and green color diminishes, revealing or allowing the development of pigments such as carotenoids and anthocyanins, which make many fruits appear brighter or more intensely colored.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence A is correct, Sentence B is correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb),
