('mc:sentence a. basi is fermented sugar cane. sentence b. lambanog is distilled basi.:::sentence a is correct', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'sentence a. basi is fermented sugar cane. sentence b. lambanog is distilled basi.', 'Sentence A is correct', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Basi – fermented drink from sugar cane. Very popular among the lIocanos in Northern regions.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Sentence A is correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Basi – fermented drink from sugar cane. Very popular among the lIocanos in Northern regions.\na) Basing babae – sweet wine\nb) Basing lalake – dry wine\n\nLambanog – distilled drink from tuba; alcohol content is higher than tuba; common in Southern Luzon\n\nOther Philippine Alcoholic Beverages:\n• Tuba – sweet, fermented coconut sap obtained by tapping the young, flowering spathe of the coconut palm\n• Tapuy – rice wine common in the Cordillera region","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence B is correct, Both sentences are correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb),
