('mc:which menu term means "of the day"?:::du jour', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'which menu term means "of the day"?', 'Du jour', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Du jour is a French phrase that literally translates to \"of the day\".","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Du jour\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Du jour is a French phrase that literally translates to \"of the day\".\n\nIn restaurants, a du jour menu or item changes daily depending on what fresh ingredients are available or what specials the chef has created (e.g., \"Soup du jour\" means soup of the day).\n\n• À la cart: Means \"by the menu\" or \"from the menu\"; items are listed, ordered, and priced individually.\n• Table d''hôte: Means \"the host''s table\"; it offers a complete, multi-course meal with limited choices at a single fixed price.\n• Prix fixe: Means \"fixed price\"; a set menu where customers pay a predetermined total price for a specific sequence of courses.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: À la carte, Table d''hôte, Prix fixe"}'::jsonb),
('mc:which menu term means "of the day"?:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'which menu term means "of the day"?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Du jour is a French phrase that literally translates to \"of the day\".","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Du jour\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Du jour is a French phrase that literally translates to \"of the day\".\n\nIn restaurants, a du jour menu or item changes daily depending on what fresh ingredients are available or what specials the chef has created (e.g., \"Soup du jour\" means soup of the day).\n\n• À la cart: Means \"by the menu\" or \"from the menu\"; items are listed, ordered, and priced individually.\n• Table d''hôte: Means \"the host''s table\"; it offers a complete, multi-course meal with limited choices at a single fixed price.\n• Prix fixe: Means \"fixed price\"; a set menu where customers pay a predetermined total price for a specific sequence of courses.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: À la carte, Table d''hôte, Prix fixe"}'::jsonb),
('mc:which should be a healthier option of market forms of milk for people who monitor their blood profiles?:::toned milk', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'which should be a healthier option of market forms of milk for people who monitor their blood profiles?', 'Toned milk', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Toned milk – Lower fat but retains protein and calcium, better for heart health.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Toned milk\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Toned milk – Lower fat but retains protein and calcium, better for heart health.\n\n• Whole milk – High in saturated fat, raises cholesterol.\n• Condensed milk – Very high in sugar and fat.\n• Evaporated milk – Concentrated, higher fat though no added sugar.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Whole milk, Condensed milk, Evaporated milk"}'::jsonb),
