('mc:dinuguan of mindanao with pork intestines, lungs, liver, banana heart, and olasiman:::sampayna', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'dinuguan of mindanao with pork intestines, lungs, liver, banana heart, and olasiman', 'Sampayna', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"<img alt=\"Sampayna (Dinuguan from Northern Mindanao)” – FoodEverMore\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" width=\"203\">b. Sampayna<img alt=\"Pipian Rojo Recipe (Mexican Red Pipian Sauce)\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" width=\"200\">a. Pipián: historic, rich seed-based sauce/stew originating from Mesoamerica and Mexican cuisine, which also evolved into a distinct PH regional chicken stew<img alt=\"TINUTO is our local laing variant. It is made from fresh young gabi leaves,  coconut cream, grated salted fish meat, lemon grass and chilies. 📸 Ana  Katherine Reyes\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" width=\"200\">c. Tinuto: coconut-based dish from Quezon province and Marinduque, similar to Bicolano laing<img alt=\"Nilaneg - Ang Sarap\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" width=\"202\">d. Nilanega: Filipino soup dish from Batanes and the Cagayan Valley region, made with broiled fresh fish and pork liver simmered in a savory bagoong broth along with local vegetables","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Sampayna\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"<img alt=\"Sampayna (Dinuguan from Northern Mindanao)” – FoodEverMore\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" width=\"203\">b. Sampayna<img alt=\"Pipian Rojo Recipe (Mexican Red Pipian Sauce)\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" width=\"200\">a. Pipián: historic, rich seed-based sauce/stew originating from Mesoamerica and Mexican cuisine, which also evolved into a distinct PH regional chicken stew<img alt=\"TINUTO is our local laing variant. It is made from fresh young gabi leaves,  coconut cream, grated salted fish meat, lemon grass and chilies. 📸 Ana  Katherine Reyes\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" width=\"200\">c. Tinuto: coconut-based dish from Quezon province and Marinduque, similar to Bicolano laing<img alt=\"Nilaneg - Ang Sarap\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" width=\"202\">d. Nilanega: Filipino soup dish from Batanes and the Cagayan Valley region, made with broiled fresh fish and pork liver simmered in a savory bagoong broth along with local vegetables","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Pipian, Tinuto, Nilaneg"}'::jsonb),
