('mc:which equipment provides gentle indirect heating through hot water and is commonly used to keep foods warm?:::bain-marie', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'which equipment provides gentle indirect heating through hot water and is commonly used to keep foods warm?', 'Bain-marie', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"A bain-marie (also called a water bath) consists of an outer container filled with heated water and an inner container filled with food. The hot water surrounds the inner container, providing gentle, indirect, and uniform heat. This prevents delicate foods (like sauces or custards) from burning or curdling and is widely used in food service buffet lines to keep pre-cooked foods safely warm.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Bain-marie\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"A bain-marie (also called a water bath) consists of an outer container filled with heated water and an inner container filled with food. The hot water surrounds the inner container, providing gentle, indirect, and uniform heat. This prevents delicate foods (like sauces or custards) from burning or curdling and is widely used in food service buffet lines to keep pre-cooked foods safely warm.\n\n• A salamander is a high-heat broiling or finishing unit.\n• A griddle provides direct dry heat through a heated surface.\n• A convection oven uses circulating hot air for cooking or baking.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Salamander, Griddle, Convection oven"}'::jsonb),
('mc:which equipment provides gentle indirect heating through hot water and is commonly used to keep foods warm?:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'which equipment provides gentle indirect heating through hot water and is commonly used to keep foods warm?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"A bain-marie (also called a water bath) consists of an outer container filled with heated water and an inner container filled with food. The hot water surrounds the inner container, providing gentle, indirect, and uniform heat. This prevents delicate foods (like sauces or custards) from burning or curdling and is widely used in food service buffet lines to keep pre-cooked foods safely warm.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Bain-marie\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"A bain-marie (also called a water bath) consists of an outer container filled with heated water and an inner container filled with food. The hot water surrounds the inner container, providing gentle, indirect, and uniform heat. This prevents delicate foods (like sauces or custards) from burning or curdling and is widely used in food service buffet lines to keep pre-cooked foods safely warm.\n\n• A salamander is a high-heat broiling or finishing unit.\n• A griddle provides direct dry heat through a heated surface.\n• A convection oven uses circulating hot air for cooking or baking.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Salamander, Griddle, Convection oven"}'::jsonb),
('mc:which organization, together with who, established the codex alimentarius commission?:::fao', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'which organization, together with who, established the codex alimentarius commission?', 'FAO', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The Codex Alimentarius Commission (CAC) was established in 1963 as a joint initiative between the Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) of the United Nations and the World Health Organization (WHO).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"FAO\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The Codex Alimentarius Commission (CAC) was established in 1963 as a joint initiative between the Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) of the United Nations and the World Health Organization (WHO).\n\nTogether, they created the Codex Alimentarius (Latin for \"Food Code\") to protect consumer health globally and promote fair, harmonized practices in international food trade.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: WTO, UNICEF, UNESCO"}'::jsonb),
('mc:which organization, together with who, established the codex alimentarius commission?:::', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'which organization, together with who, established the codex alimentarius commission?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The Codex Alimentarius Commission (CAC) was established in 1963 as a joint initiative between the Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) of the United Nations and the World Health Organization (WHO).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"FAO\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The Codex Alimentarius Commission (CAC) was established in 1963 as a joint initiative between the Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) of the United Nations and the World Health Organization (WHO).\n\nTogether, they created the Codex Alimentarius (Latin for \"Food Code\") to protect consumer health globally and promote fair, harmonized practices in international food trade.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: WTO, UNICEF, UNESCO"}'::jsonb),
('mc:a manager finds that one leadership approach is effective with one employee but ineffective with another because their abilities, motivation, and work circumstances differ. which approach recognizes that management practices should be adapted to the situation?:::contingency approach', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb, 'a manager finds that one leadership approach is effective with one employee but ineffective with another because their abilities, motivation, and work circumstances differ. which approach recognizes that management practices should be adapted to the situation?', 'Contingency approach', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The contingency approach holds that effective management depends on the situation and circumstances.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Contingency approach\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The contingency approach holds that effective management depends on the situation and circumstances.\n\n• Scientific management: systematic analysis of work and efficiency\n• Bureaucratic management: formal structure, rules, and authority\n• Classical management: broad principles of structure and efficiency","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Scientific management, Classical management, Bureaucratic approach"}'::jsonb),
